-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[13] = {
[6535]={"'If I stood here as crowned liege and not in hooded stealth, that herb-master, Galathir, would know something of my displeasure! He has decided, I cannot fathom how, that Draught of Everworth is what wounded soldiers most need - when that is farthest from the case. At best, it will add to their suffering and at worse... but let us not speak of that. \
\
'Alas, cloaked diplomacy is the thing of the day, so I must enlist your help, friend. I have had Galathir shooed from this hall, but I cannot keep him from the others. Will you follow Galathir and his herbalists, and gather up the infusions wherever he has placed them?'","Galathir is giving patients Draught of Everworth, which Aragorn believes may be harmful.","Aragorn has asked you to remove any of Galathir's Draught of Everworth infusions that have been left near patients in the House of Rest and the House of Remedies in the Houses of Healing.","You hand Aragorn the infusions you gathered.\
\
'This many? If that man does not let up... but now is not the time. I thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will see these dealt with swiftly.'","Removed a Draught of Everworth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ill-advised Infusions","Aragorn can be found in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should bring the harmful Draughts of Everworth to Aragorn, as he asked.","Remove Draughts of Everworth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring Aragorn the Draughts of Everworth"},
[6536]={"Gondren can be found in central Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Harnion has asked you to rescue Gondren from the forces in Tarlang's Crown.","'Come back to taunt me, have you? I'm already a dead man, I hardly see the point....\
\
'You... you're not a Corsair! If Harnion sent you, I'm afraid you are too late to save me... but I learned many things of their plans here before I was captured. They seem to take a great deal of joy in bleeding me out, so much so that they have even kept the hounds from me.\
\
'Come close, my friend, I must speak while I still can....'","Ill-fated Deception","'${PLAYER}, there is another matter that has me worried.\
\
'You see, my friend Gondren devised a plan to discover more of our enemies' plans. He thought to disguise himself as a Corsair to sneak behind their lines... and the man cannot even grow a beard! It was a truly foolish plan, but I believe he went ahead with it anyway.\
\
'Gather your allies and search for him near their camps. If he spoke true, he will be dressed like one of them, so take care not to rough him up too badly!'","Harnion fears for the life of his friend, Gondren, who disguised himself in an attempt to discover more of the Heirs of Castamir and their vile plans.","Talk to Gondren in Tarlang's Crown","DNT"},
[6537]={"'Bring me those ill-gotten good, ${PLAYER}!'","Innoth is at his camp, to the west and south of the Dunlending supply-line.\
\
You should return to Innoth with the supplies that you recovered from the Dunlendings.","'${PLAYER}, the supplies once being ferried beneath the Isendale to Wulf's Cleft are now being delivered to many Dunlending outposts, including Brôntrig.\
\
'The Dunlendings hauling these supplies have been spotted along the hill to the east of here. If you would, follow the switchback to the north and look for the Dunlendings... they must be stopped!'","Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ill-gotten Goods","The supplies that were being ferried beneath the Isendale to Cuvnerth are now being brought to several outposts, including Brôntrig. Stop any Dunlendings from ferrying supplies.","Talk to Innoth near the Isen","'These supplies will be sent to Forthbrond, where they will benefit our men.'","The Dunlending transporting the supplies can be found along the hill east of Innoth's camp, reached by travelling the switchback to the north.\
\
Innoth has asked you to stop the Dunlendings from delivering their Orc-provided supplies to their various outposts.","Collected supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6538]={"Urge leering Zhélruka to depart Hammerstead (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Much to Grámi Hornhelm's dismay, a newly-arrived company of Zhélruka has taken an uncomfortable interest in the works of Hammerstead.","Ill-meaning Glances","Talk to Grámi Hornhelm","Leering Zhélruka can be found throughout Hammerstead.\
\
Concerned that ill-meaning glances shall soon turn to theft, Grámi Hornhelm has asked you to politely urge the visiting Zhélruka to depart Hammerstead.","Grámi Hornhelm can be found at Hammerstead.\
\
Although not all of them took your words to heart, you have urged many of the visiting Zhélruka to depart Hammerstead. You should now speak to Grámi Hornhelm.","'I do not mind the occasional guest, but it seemed to me those Zhélruka had hidden intentions. I shall keep a watchful eye on those that still remain, but that should not prove a difficult task.\
\
'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps you can help me with another matter....'\
\
Grámi Hornhelm pauses and glances around.\
\
'You have seen them, haven't you? A company of Zhélruka has come to Hammerstead, and I do not know how long they intend to remain. All I know is that I am not fond of the gazes of some of these Zhélruka lingering upon the works of my kinsfolk. These are not glances of admiration or curiosity, I think. These seem to me the leers of thieves laying in wait!\
\
'There are already more than enough matters that demand my attention in Hammerstead, and I would not burden myself further by keeping watch on the works of my smiths. Would you politely urge the Zhélruka to continue on their journey?'","Urged leering Zhélruka to depart Hammerstead (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[6539]={"'For as long as I can remember, our buildings were always draped in black. The Church did not allow any other colours to be displayed. A silly thing to concern themselves with, perhaps, but hasn't it always been about control?\
\
'That is why the scholars and I continue to do our research. With every colour we return to the city, we spit in the faces of tyrants who tried to control us... and come what may, the people of Umbar will endure.'","'I cannot surmise much else from this ink bottle without dedicated study. Unfortunately, having more questions than answers is only natural in my vein of research. History is always fragmented and difficult to piece together -- the Church's burning of our archives only exacerbated our restoration attempts.\
\
'But I did not come to the Tor-gardens to sulk about research! I have a wrecked shrine to further deface.\
\
'Why not join me there? Should you spot a blight of black among the buildings to the south, you will know you have found the shrine.'","You have hung up the banners.\
\
You should talk to Rimâti.","Banners hung (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Despite those who would try to destroy it, Umbar's past survives.","Talk to Rimâti at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-All","Rimâti has invited you to join her at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-All.\
\
You can find the shrine at the southern end of the Tor-gardens.","Talk to Rimâti","Rimâti has given you dyed banners to hang up at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-All.","'There you are. Behold!'\
\
Rimâti reaches into a sack and pulls out a banner. At first glance, the banner is simply pink. But then the cloth shifts, and you realize at certain angles, the colour transforms -- blue, then purple, then pink again.\
\
'The scholars and I spent months researching this pigment. Bidulêkh, it is called -- Dawn-sheen. When Kamîr Kateb burned down, the recipe burned with it. The scribes and scholars who would have held that knowledge met their ends at the Church's hands.\
\
'I came to the shrine to hang up the banners, but...' She gestures to the flag-poles before you and grins. 'Would you like to do the honours instead?'","Hang banners on flag-poles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Illumination"},
[6541]={"Complete quests of Imlad Morgul: The Reclamation.","The White Company must face many challenges in reclaiming Minas Ithil from the grasp of darkness.","Complete quests of Imlad Morgul: The Reclamation, weekly.","Imlad Morgul: La Reclamación","Complete quests of Imlad Morgul: The Reclamation (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6544]={"'El norte está asegurado, y podemos decir honestamente que ahora hemos hecho nuestra parte. Sin embargo, aún no hemos terminado. Los años de penurias crearon otro problema, que por fin es hora de abordar.'","Hay varias amenazas que deben abordarse para que Ost Forod cumpla su parte del pacto.","Ayuda a Clark Cercapiedra de nuevo","Ayuda a Ballard Wilmer de nuevo","'Ya va siendo hora de que empecemos a trabajar con los Montaraces en lugar de contra ellos.'","Por el pacto con los Montaraces de Tinnudir, Ost Forod acordó ocuparse de amenazas en el norte. Es hora de encargarse de ellas.","'Has demostrado que los Montaraces van en serio en cuanto a restaurar el pacto entre nosotros. Ahora es el momento de que demos un paso al frente y honremos nuestra parte del acuerdo.\
\
'Dijimos que vigilaríamos Evendim desde el norte, protegeríamos las rutas comerciales con Forochel y nos aseguraríamos de que los enemigos de los Montaraces no entraran por esas tierras. Han entrado y ya están aquí, eso no podemos cambiarlo, pero podemos expulsarlos.\
\
'Habla con mis asociados por el pueblo, los mismos a los que ayudaste a prepararse para el invierno. A cada uno se le ha asignado la tarea de explorar una amenaza. Sabrán más sobre lo que hacer a continuación.'","Amenazas inmediatas","Habla con Basilio Resinas en Ost Forod","Ayuda a Poppy Silleras de nuevo","Ayuda a Rowena Guardacotos de nuevo","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod.\
\
Basilio se alegrará de saber que Ost Forod ha cumplido su parte del pacto con Tinnudir."},
[6546]={"Imping: Awls Forgotten","'I see that you have found some of the heirlooms used by the Men of Imping. These tools have been passed down through generations of woodworkers. \
\
'Were these all you were able to find?'","Collect heirloom tools","Collect heirloom tools within Imping.","While exploring Imping, you notice a number of tool-packs containing various collections of ancient-looking woodworking tools. \
\
You take it upon yourself to collect these packs so that they can be returned to their proper owners.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Imping: The Miller's Foe to be underway in order to access Imping. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter Imping in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","'This is very kind of you, ${PLAYER}. Losing such precious heirlooms would surely devastate the millers. I will see that each is returned to its owner.'","Collect heirloom tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected heirloom tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the tools to Ethelbryt","You should collect the heirloom tools left behind in the lumber-yard and bring them to Ethelbryt."},
[6547]={"Defeat invaders in Imping (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated invaders in Imping (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat enemies in Imping","You should return to Ethelbryt and inform him of your deeds within Imping.","Talk to Ethelbryt","To weaken the resolve of the invaders within Imping, you take it upon yourself to thin their numbers.","'You have done well, friend ${RACE}. Your efforts make our reclaimation of Imping even easier!'","Imping: Cut Against the Grain","The invaders of Imping are numerous. Driving off even a fraction of their number will better position the Rohirrim to take back the village after you complete your mission within it.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Imping: The Miller's Foe to be underway in order to access Imping. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter Imping in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Defeat enemies within Imping."},
[6548]={"'You look the sort who is up for some danger. To the south, our milling-camp fell under attack. Most of my men were able to escape but we were forced to abandon Imping. Imping is one of our most important mills and one of the last timber caches on the Entwash. Should we lose it for good, we will also lose the resources it provides us.\
\
'With our forces busied elsewhere, we are hard pressed to muster a response to these invaders, but perhaps a smaller effort will do. Travel to Imping and see about the demise of whatever creature leads our enemies there.\
\
'Gangfinda knows the way and will lead you to the shores directly across from Imping. From there, you will need to take a boat across to the docks, I am certain there remains one of ours upon that shore.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting this quest.</rgb>","You hear Ethelbryt shout from across the yard, 'Gangfinda will take you to the milling-settlement of Imping, if you still have unresolved matters there.'","You ran out of time...","you should return to Ethelbryt and apprise him of your efforts.","Talk to Ethelbryt","Ethelbryt has asked you investigate the village and find a way to discourage the invaders from remaining there.","Defeat the leader of the enemies within Imping","Defeated the leader of the enemies within Imping","Enemies of the Rohirrim have invaded the small lumber-milling settlement of Imping along the southern banks of the Entwash.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time-limit. The timer will begin upon accepting this quest.</rgb>","You hear Ethelbryt shout from across the yard, 'Gangfinda will see you to the shores across Imping. Hurry! The longer the enemy commands Imping, the greater the risk to the lumber and trees we keep there.'","'Gangfinda will see you to the shores across Imping. \
\
'Hurry! The longer the enemy commands Imping, the greater the risk to the lumber and trees we keep there.'","'You have succeeded have you? Nothing disquiets the enemy quite so much as the loss of their leader!'","Imping: The Miller's Foe"},
[6549]={"'Te saludo en la victoria, ${PLAYER}, y mi corazón está más alegre que en mucho tiempo, al saber que Barashal está muerto. Duerman tranquilos, mis parientes — estáis vengados.\
\
'Es un honor y un privilegio conocerte, ${PLAYER}, pues verdaderamente eres grande entre los guardianes.\
\
'Te entrego esta arma con la esperanza de que la uses bien y para el bien de todos los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media.'","Garras de huargo encorvadas reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta garras macabras de murciélago (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Si puedes derrotar a Barashal y recuperar de él su cuerno carmesí, ambos nos beneficiaremos, ${PLAYER}. Y agradecería que le dijeras esto a Barashal cuando caiga: \\q¡Así son vengados los parientes de Wáli!\\q\
\
'En algún lugar de Urugarth, el comandante uruk Gruglok vigila su arena. Si puedes quitarle un Sello de Guerra, el arma que forje para ti será más poderosa.'","Wáli está en el puesto de avanzada de Noglond, al sur de la Mansión de Thorin y al oeste de la ciudad enana de Gondamon, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wáli está esperando que regreses con el primer conjunto de componentes que necesita.","Reúne cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog","'¿No tienes el primer conjunto de componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}? Debo preguntarte, ¿por qué?'","Maza cruel de Shataz reunida","Reúne Sello de Guerra","Wáli está en el puesto de avanzada de Noglond, al sur de la Mansión de Thorin y al oeste de la ciudad enana de Gondamon, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wáli está esperando que regreses con el segundo conjunto de componentes que necesita.","'${PLAYER}, puedes encontrar arañas, huargos y murciélagos en Angmar y otros lugares igualmente terribles.'","Instrumentos de Batalla","Barashal puede encontrarse en Carn Dûm, en Angmar. Gruglok está en Urugarth, en Angmar.\
\
Wáli te pidió que le trajeras un cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog y un Sello de Guerra.","'¿No tienes los componentes que buscaba, ${PLAYER}? ¿Por qué es eso?'","'Puedo hacerte un arma que esté a la altura de tu tremendo poder como ${PLAYERNAME:guardián[m]|guardiana[f]}, , ¡y me complace hacerlo! Como todo lo que vale la pena, sin embargo, debo decirte que algo de tal valor requerirá mucho esfuerzo y dificultad. ¡El arma — y tú — serán más fuertes por ello!\
\
'Primero necesitaré la maza cruel del Troll de las nieves Shataz y las lanzas impregnadas de azufre de los trasgos Tarkrîp. Shataz habita ahora en los alrededores de la tierra de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas. Los Tarkrîp que buscas están acampados entre los campamentos de orcos de Malenhad, en Angmar.'","Reúne lanzas impregnadas de azufre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wáli está en el puesto de avanzada de Noglond, al sur de la Mansión de Thorin y al oeste de la ciudad enana de Gondamon, en Ered Luin.\
\
Wáli está esperando que regreses con el conjunto final de componentes que necesita.","'Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}, ¡y con tanta rapidez también! Tu arma se volverá mucho más poderosa cuando el recuerdo de estos enemigos forme parte de ella.\
\
'Solo necesito un conjunto más de componentes, y estos serán los más difíciles de obtener. Barashal el Gorthorog y Gruglok de Urugarth son oponentes temibles. De Barashal, recoge un cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog. Puedes encontrarlo en Carn Dûm. De Gruglok en Urugarth puedes obtener un Sello de Guerra.'","Mandíbulas moteadas de araña recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Puedes encontrar al Troll de las nieves Shataz cerca de las tierras de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas. Los trasgos Tarkrîp sirven en los campamentos de orcos en Malenhad.'","Recoge las mandíbulas moteadas de araña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reúne la maza cruel de Shataz","'Has hecho bien en derrotar a Shataz, ${PLAYER}, y me alegra que su historia haya terminado al fin, pues trajo mucha pena a mis parientes en su tiempo.\
\
'Te agradezco también por estas lanzas. Observa la pobre manufactura... ¡me asombra que las armas hechas por trasgos no se deshagan al blandirse! Destruiré estas armas y esparciré el polvo sobre el arma que forje para ti, para recordarle la fragilidad de sus enemigos.\
\
'Estoy listo para el siguiente conjunto de componentes. Ahora parte y tráeme garras de murciélago macabras, garras de huargo encorvadas y mandíbulas de araña de criaturas que habitan en Angmar y otros lugares igualmente terribles.'","Shataz puede encontrarse en los alrededores de la tierra de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas. Los trasgos Tarkrîp pueden encontrarse entre los campamentos de orcos de Malenhad, en Angmar.\
\
Wáli te pidió que le trajeras la maza cruel de Shataz y las lanzas impregnadas de azufre de los Tarkrîp.","Reúne garras de huargo encorvadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog reunido","Wáli ha aceptado ayudarte a forjar un arma digna de tu poder como ${PLAYERNAME:guardián[m]|guardiana[f]}. Te ha asegurado que del gran esfuerzo nace la fuerza.","Lleva el último conjunto de componentes a Wáli","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Wáli","Lanzas impregnadas de azufre reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes las cosas que te pedí, ? ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro de que eres un guardián[m]|segura de que eres una guardiana[f]}?'","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Wáli","Sello de Guerra reunido","Arañas, huargos y murciélagos pueden encontrarse en Angmar y otros lugares peligrosos.\
\
Wáli te pidió que le trajeras garras macabras de murciélago, mandíbulas moteadas de araña y garras encorvadas de huargo."},
[6550]={"Recoge colas de barghest con púas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Garras astilladas de huargo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Gwesgylliel","Recoge espadas de Ongbúrz con muescas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gwesgylliel está en Lin Giliath en Meluinen, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Gwesgylliel está esperando a que regreses con el último conjunto de componentes que necesita.","'Me alegra verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}, y que traigas contigo algunas de las espadas de Ongbúrz. Ya no sumarán muescas por cada uno de nuestros amigos caídos.\
\
'También me alegra que hayas privado a Tramug de su hacha de mano. ¡Su historia termina contigo, al parecer!\
\
'Ve ahora y tráeme garras de los huargos que merodean por el este de Angmar y otros lugares peligrosos, como Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. También necesito las colas barghest con púas de esas criaturas que rondan Imlad Balchorth.'","'Puedes encontrar huargos en lugares como Angmar, Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. Los barghests que busco pueden encontrarse en Imlad Balchorth en Angmar.'","Sello de Guerra recogido","Lleva el conjunto final de componentes a Gwesgylliel","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Los orcos Ongbúrz pueden encontrarse en Fasach-falroid en Angmar. Tramug acecha los pantanos de Malenhad en Angmar.\
\
Gwesgylliel te pidió que le trajeras espadas melladas de Ongbúrz y el hacha de mano de Tramug.","'¿No tienes los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}?'","'Puedes encontrar a los Ongbúrz acampados en Fasach-Falroid en Angmar. En las regiones orientales de Angmar, en Malenhad, puedes encontrar a Tramug.'","Recoge una escama impecable de Lhugrien","Recoge garras de huargo astilladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Escama impecable de Lhugrien recogida","'Me alegra verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. Estos componentes mejorarán mucho el arma que estoy fabricando para ti.\
\
'Busca a la vil dragonzuelo Lhugrien y obtén de ella una escama impecable. Consígueme también un Sello de Guerra del malvado Gruglok. Ambos pueden encontrarse en Urugarth.'","Instrumentos de Osadía","Lhugrien y Gruglok se pueden encontrar en Urugarth en Angmar.\
\
Gwesgylliel te pidió que le trajeras una escama impecable de Lhugrien y un Sello de Guerra.","'¡Regresas victorioso, ! Me inclino ante tu habilidad, pues sé que Lhugrien y Gruglok son rivales temibles.\
\
'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un campeón digno, mi amigo[m]|una campeona digna, mi amiga[f]}, y es un honor conocerte. Te entrego esta arma con la sincera esperanza de que te sirva mucho y bien.'","'¿Dónde están los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Gwesgylliel","Colas barghest con púas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gwesgylliel está en Lin Giliath en Meluinen, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Gwesgylliel está esperando a que regreses con el primer conjunto de componentes que necesita.","'La ciudad fortaleza de Urugarth es un lugar malvado, ${PLAYER}, pero también guarda los componentes restantes que necesito para tu arma.'","Gwesgylliel está en Lin Giliath en Meluinen, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Gwesgylliel está esperando a que regreses con el segundo conjunto de componentes que necesita.","Recoge el hacha de mano de Tramug","Espadas de Ongbúrz melladas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Puedo hacerte un arma que llevarás con orgullo, , pues aquellos que la contemplen sabrán que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un poderoso campeón[m]|una poderosa campeona[f]}. ¡Más poderosos aún son los actos realizados con honor, y tú has realizado muchos!\
\
'Pero procede con precaución, . Los componentes que necesitaré para esta arma no serán fáciles de conseguir.\
\
'Primero, necesito que recojas espadas de los Orcos Ongbúrz de Fasach-falroid en Angmar, luego viaja hacia el este a Malenhad y obtén el hacha de mano del trasgo Tramug.'","Gwesgylliel ha accedido a ayudarte a crear un arma digna de tu reputación como campeón de los Pueblos Libres.","Se pueden encontrar huargos en Angmar y en otros lugares peligrosos, como Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. Los barghests se pueden encontrar en Imlad Balchorth en Angmar.\
\
Gwesgylliel te pidió que le trajeras garras de huargo astilladas y colas de barghest con púas.","Recoge un Sello de Guerra"},
[6552]={"Implementos de ferocidad","Recoge colas de barghest con púas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra el cuerno de gorthorog carmesí y el Sello de Guerra y llévaselos a Sterkist","'¡Gracias por estos componentes! Mi amigo estaba tan encantado de que partieras a derrotar a Barashal y Gruglok que se adelantó y ya te forjó el arma. No te enfades, pero no necesitó usar estos componentes para su fabricación. Aun así, hiciste algo bueno al eliminar a estos crueles enemigos.\
\
'¡Ahora el arma es tuya! Úsala en nombre de Beorn y trae honor a nuestra familia, como desea Grimbeorn.'","Cuerno de gorthorog carmesí recogida","Shataz puede encontrarse en las afueras de la tierra de los gigantes, en las Montañas Nubladas. Los trasgos Tarkrîp se encuentran entre los campamentos de orcos de Malenhad, en Angmar.\
\
Sterkist te pidió que le llevaras la cruel maza de Shataz y lanzas Tarkrîp teñidas de azufre.","Sterkist tiene un plan para conseguirte un arma de gran calidad, pero necesita que recojas varios componentes difíciles de obtener.","Garras astilladas de huargo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sterkist se encuentra en la Torre del Encuentro, en Rivendel.\
\
Has reunido el conjunto final de componentes para Sterkist y deberías llevárselos de regreso a Rivendel.","Reúne cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog","Sterkist se encuentra en la Torre del Encuentro, en Rivendel.\
\
Has reunido el primer conjunto de componentes que Sterkist dice necesitar para que su amigo te forje un arma excelente, y deberías llevárselos.","Maza cruel de Shataz reunida","'Mi amigo puede forjarte un arma digna de nuestra estirpe, , pero necesitará varias cosas que pueden ser difíciles de obtener.\
\
'Dice que necesitará la cruel maza del Troll de las nieves Shataz y lanzas teñidas de azufre de los trasgos Tarkrîp. Shataz mora ahora en las afueras de la tierra de los gigantes, en las Montañas Nubladas. Los Tarkrîp que necesitas están acampados entre los campamentos de orcos de Malenhad, en Angmar.\
\
'¡Buena suerte, ${PLAYERNAME:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}! Obtener estas cosas no será fácil y requerirá un largo viaje!'","Entrega el segundo conjunto de componentes a Sterkist","Entrega el primer conjunto de componentes a Sterkist","Reúne lanzas impregnadas de azufre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar huargos en Angmar y otros lugares peligrosos, como Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. Los barghests se encuentran en Imlad Balchorth, en Angmar.\
\
Sterkist dice que necesita garras de huargo astilladas y colas de barghest con púas para su amigo.","'Mientras estabas fuera, mi amigo me contó historias sobre Shataz y su gran maldad. ¡Me alegra mucho que hayas puesto fin a él! Y gracias también por las lanzas.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para oír cuál es el siguiente conjunto de componentes? Necesitaremos garras de huargo de los que acechan el este de Angmar y otros lugares peligrosos, como Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. También necesitaremos colas de barghest con púas de esas criaturas que rondan Imlad Balchorth.'","Reúne la maza cruel de Shataz","'Barashal el gorthorog y Gruglok de Urugarth son adversarios temibles, si siquiera la mitad de las historias que he oído sobre ellos es cierta. De Barashal, recoge una cuerno de gorthorog carmesí. Puedes encontrarlo en Carn Dûm. De Gruglok, en Urugarth, puedes obtener un Sello de Guerra. Ambos lugares son aterradores y peligrosos, ¡así que ten cuidado cuando vayas!'","Sterkist se encuentra en la Torre del Encuentro, en Rivendel.\
\
Has reunido el segundo conjunto de componentes que Sterkist dice necesitar para que su amigo te forje un arma excelente.","Recolecta garras astilladas de huargo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Mi amigo dice que tu arma se volverá mucho más fuerte cuando el recuerdo de estos enemigos pase a formar parte de ella. Suena cierto, aunque no soy armero. Es una idea agradable, ¿no?\
\
'Solo necesita un último conjunto de componentes, y será el más difícil de obtener. Barashal el gorthorog y Gruglok de Urugarth son adversarios temibles, si siquiera la mitad de las historias que he oído es cierta. De Barashal, recoge una corne de gorthorog carmesí; puedes encontrarlo en Carn Dûm. De Gruglok, en Urugarth, obtén un Sello de Guerra. Ambos lugares son aterradores y peligrosos, así que procede con cautela.'","Colas con púas de barghest recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lanzas impregnadas de azufre reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sello de Guerra reunido"},
[6553]={"Se recogieron bastones escarchados de los Corcur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Isdi","Se recogió el diente desgarrador de Zarpahelada","Recolecta el Emblema de Ritual","'Los espectros pueden encontrarse entre las tumbas de Imlad Balchorth, en Angmar, mientras que las sierpes vagan por Forochel, Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas.'","Se recogieron ojos de sierpes odiosas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Corcur pueden encontrarse cerca de Helegrod en las Montañas Nubladas. Zarpahelada puede encontrarse en la tierra de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
Isdi te ha pedido que le traigas bastones escarchados de los Corcur y el diente desgarrador de Zarpahelada.","'Estos servirán muy bien, ${PLAYER}, y mejorarán el filo del arma que estoy creando para ti.\
\
'Queda un conjunto de componentes, y estos se encuentran en el corazón mismo de la tierra de Angmar. Mantén la mente alerta, como sé que harás, y alcanzarás la victoria.\
\
'Necesito que busques al uruk Morthrâng de Carn Dûm y obtengas de él un Emblema de Ritual. También en Carn Dûm, deberías buscar al Hombre de Angmar conocido como Sálvakh y arrebatarle su Runa de Presencia Maligna.'","Recoge bastones escarchados de los Corcur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se recogieron uñas pútridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Recoge uñas pútridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge la Runa de Presencia Maligna","'Te agradezco por estos componentes, ${PLAYER}, y estoy seguro de que no tendrás dificultad en regresar con el segundo conjunto.\
\
'A continuación, necesitaré los ojos de las sierpes que pueden encontrarse en Forochel, Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas. También necesitaré las uñas pútridas de los tumularios que vagan por Imlad Balchorth en Angmar.'","'Ahora llegamos al momento, ${PLAYER}. Puedes encontrar tanto a Morthrâng como a Sálvakh en Carn Dûm, en Angmar.'","'¿Aún no has reunido los materiales que necesito, ${PLAYER}?'","'No me sorprende que hayas regresado ${PLAYERNAME:victorioso[m]|victoriosa[f]}, , pues sé que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un Sabio[m]|una Sabia[f]} de habilidad y conocimiento insuperables.\
\
'Me inclino ante tu sabiduría y te entrego esta arma. ¡Que te sirva bien!'","Emblema de Ritual recogido","Isdi está en las ruinas de Edhelion, cerca de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Isdi está esperando que regreses con el primer conjunto de componentes.","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Isdi","Instrumentos de conocimiento","Se recogió la Runa de Presencia Maligna","'Los Corcur pueden encontrarse cerca de Helegrod, ${PLAYER}, mientras que el oso Zarpahelada vaga por la tierra de los gigantes, ambos en las Montañas Nubladas.'","'Puedo confeccionarte un arma digna de la sabiduría de un Sabio consumado como tú, . Seguramente no necesito decirte que el camino hacia su creación no será fácil —eres lo suficientemente ${PLAYERNAME:sabio[m]|sabia[f]} como para saberlo.\
\
'Sin embargo, debo pedirte que me traigas los componentes que necesitaré para fabricarla. No temas al camino difícil, pues en él se encuentra la verdadera satisfacción.\
\
'Primero, necesitaré los bastones de los Corcur, que están acampados cerca de Helegrod en las Montañas Nubladas, y la garra desgarradora del gran oso Zarpahelada, que vaga por la tierra de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas.'","Los espectros pueden encontrarse en Imlad Balchorth en Angmar. Las sierpes pueden encontrarse en Forochel, Eregion y las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
Isdi te ha pedido que le traigas ojos de sierpes odiosas y uñas pútridas.","Isdi está en las ruinas de Edhelion, cerca de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Isdi está esperando que regreses con el segundo conjunto de componentes.","Recolecta ojos de sierpes odiosas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Isdi ha aceptado ayudarte a confeccionar un arma que refleje la sabiduría de un Sabio consumado.","Recoge el diente desgarrador de Zarpahelada","Lleva el último conjunto de componentes a Isdi","Morthrâng está dentro de Urugarth y Sálvakh puede encontrarse en Carn Dûm.\
\
Isdi te ha pedido que le traigas un Emblema de Ritual y una Runa de Presencia Maligna.","Isdi está en las ruinas de Edhelion, cerca de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Isdi está esperando que regreses con el último conjunto de componentes."},
[6554]={"'Me pregunto, ${PLAYER}. ¿No es acaso un arma otra herramienta de navegación? Es cierto que puede guiarte al final de un conflicto... o de una conversación.\
\
'Puedo forjarte un arma excelente, digna de alguien de tu talento, pero antes necesitaré que me traigas una serie de materiales. Debo advertirte, sin embargo, que no será una tarea sencilla.\
\
'Para tu primera tarea en esta prueba, necesitaré dos materiales. Primero, necesito un tonel del repugnante aceite ígneo que porta el orco Throghásh, quien merodea cerca de las ruinas de Eitheldir. Y segundo, necesito varias cantimploras de acero que llevan los semiorcos y bandidos del Ángulo del Mitheithel. A pesar de nuestros esfuerzos, han mantenido un campamento en las ruinas de Thelgarth, así que no será difícil encontrarlos.\
\
'Una vez me hayas traído esos materiales, te pediré otros que deben obtenerse más lejos, en tierras mucho menos hospitalarias.'","'Para los últimos materiales que necesito, deberás viajar nuevamente a Angmar. Dafrim, Gríshakrum y Kughûrz son temibles orcos de Urugarth. La fama de su crueldad y de su ferocidad en combate es bien conocida entre los Dúnedain, y se dice que disfrutan contabilizando a los que han matado tallando muescas en palos toscos. Si logras vencer a uno de ellos en combate, recoge uno de estos palos ensangrentados y tráemelo a Tornhad.\
\
'En cuanto al segundo material, la tarea es sumamente peligrosa. Se dice que Helchgam se encuentra en las alcantarillas bajo la temible ciudad de Carn Dûm, pero temo que solo hay un modo de obtener la baba pútrida de Helchgam: poniendo fin a su existencia.'","Recolecta gotas corrosivas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge picos venenosos de tortuga aterradora (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge el tonel de aceite ígneo de Throghásh","Recoge cantimploras de acero (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge un palo de cuentas ensangrentado","Recoge la baba pútrida de Helchgam","Aelindil se encuentra en Tornhad, en el Ángulo del Mitheithel.","Entrega el conjunto final de materiales a Aelindil en Tornhad","'Para los siguientes materiales, deberás viajar a las tierras de Angmar. Necesito que recojas varios picos de las tortugas aterradoras venenosas de Malenhad, y también gotas corrosivas de las sanguijuelas de azufre que habitan entre las aguas mancilladas de Duvuinen.'","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Estos servirán perfectamente, ¡pero aún queda trabajo por hacer!\
\
'Para los siguientes materiales, tendrás que viajar a las tierras de Angmar. Necesito que reúnas varios picos de las tortugas aterradoras venenosas de Malenhad, y también que me traigas un conjunto de gotas corrosivas de las sanguijuelas de azufre que habitan en las aguas contaminadas de Duvuinen.'","Tonel de aceite ígneo de Throghásh recogido","Picos venenosos de tortuga aterradora recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Para tu primera tarea en esta prueba, necesitaré dos materiales. Primero, necesito un tonel del repugnante aceite ígneo que porta el orco Throghásh, quien merodea cerca de las ruinas de Eitheldir. Y segundo, necesito varias cantimploras de acero que llevan los semiorcos y bandidos del Ángulo del Mitheithel. A pesar de nuestros esfuerzos, mantienen un campamento en las ruinas de Thelgarth, así que no será difícil encontrarlos.\
\
'Una vez me hayas traído esos materiales, te pediré otros que deben obtenerse más lejos, en tierras mucho menos hospitalarias.'","Gotas corrosivas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Palo de cuentas ensangrentado recogido","'¡Regresas triunfante, !\
\
'Me inclino ante tu habilidad, pues nadie salvo un Marinero experimentado podría haber completado todas las tareas que te encomendé, y mucho menos derrotar a la terrible bestia Helchgam en su abominable cisterna.\
\
'Has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un Marinero verdaderamente digno, amigo mío[m]|una Marinera verdaderamente digna, amiga mía[f]}, y es un honor para mí entregarte esta arma. ¡Que te sirva bien en tus viajes!'","Aelindil en Tornhad ha aceptado ayudarte a forjar un arma digna de alguien de tu habilidad.","Helchgam puede encontrarse en Carn Dûm, en Angmar. Dafrim, Gríshakrum y Kughûrz están todos en Urugarth, en Angmar.\
\
Aelindil te ha pedido que le traigas un palo de cuentas ensangrentado y la baba pútrida de Helchgam.","Entrega el segundo conjunto de materiales a Aelindil en Tornhad","Instrumentos de navegación","Entrega el primer conjunto de materiales a Aelindil en Tornhad","Puedes encontrar sanguijuelas de azufre hinchadas en el este de Malenhad y en Duvuinen, en Angmar. Las tortugas aterradoras pueden hallarse en Malenhad, en Angmar.\
\
Aelindil te ha pedido que le traigas picos de tortuga aterradora venenosa y gotas corrosivas.","Aelindil te ha pedido recoger el tonel de aceite ígneo de Throghásh en Eitheldir y también varias cantimploras de acero que portan los semiorcos y bandidos del Ángulo del Mitheithel.","Cantimploras de acero recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baba pútrida de Helchgam recogida","'¡Bien hecho! Ahora solo necesito dos objetos más, y estos serán los más difíciles de todos.\
\
'Para estos materiales finales, deberás viajar nuevamente a Angmar: a Urugarth y a Carn Dûm. Primero, debes buscar a los temibles orcos llamados Dafrim, Gríshakrum y Kughûrz en Urugarth. La fama de su crueldad y destreza en combate se ha extendido entre los Dúnedain, y se dice que disfrutan llevando la cuenta de sus víctimas tallando muescas en palos toscos. Si puedes derrotar a cualquiera de ellos, recoge uno de sus palos de cuentas ensangrentados y tráemelo a Tornhad.\
\
'En cuanto al segundo material, es una tarea sumamente peligrosa. Se dice que la bestia Helchgam puede encontrarse en las alcantarillas bajo la temible ciudad de Carn Dûm, pero temo que solo hay una forma de obtener la baba pútrida de Helchgam: acabando con ella.'"},
[6555]={"'El camino del juglar no está libre de peligro, ${PLAYER}, una verdad que sin duda ya habrás llegado a comprender. Para enfrentar ese peligro, necesitas un arma en la que puedas confiar. Puedo forjarte un arma así.\
\
'Como en todos los relatos dignos de ser escuchados, la historia de esta arma estará colmada de dificultades y fatiga. Mirarás atrás, al camino que has recorrido cuando todo haya terminado, y sabrás que valió la pena el viaje, ${PLAYER}. De esto estoy segura.\
\
'Debo pedirte que reúnas los objetos que necesitaré para crear esta arma y darle la fuerza para contrarrestar a nuestros odiados enemigos. El primer conjunto de componentes que necesitaré incluye el diente mellado del huargo Narglup, que ronda Fasach-larran en Angmar, y los colmillos de las sierpes de las rocas de las Montañas Nubladas.'","'Me alegra verte regresar, ${PLAYER}, y con los componentes que necesito si he de hacer tu arma tan fuerte como merece serlo. Te lo agradezco.\
\
'¡Tu tarea final será la más desafiante y digna de ser cantada! Necesito que obtengas para mí un Emblema de Ritual de los uruk Morthrâng en Urugarth y una Runa de Dominio Alado de las merrevail Mormoz y Azgoth en Carn Dûm.'","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Baillindiel","Recolecta gotas corrosivas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los babosos azufrosos pueden encontrarse en Angmar. Los huargos pueden encontrarse en Angmar y en Eregion. Los murciélagos pueden encontrarse en Angmar y en Moria.\
\
Baillindiel te pidió que le trajeras gotas corrosivas, garras astilladas de huargo y garras macabras de murciélago.","Recolecta el Emblema de Ritual","Recolecta garras macabras de murciélago (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Creo que encontrarás todo lo que necesito en Angmar, aunque también podrás hallar garras de huargo en Eregion y garras de murciélago en Moria.'","Baillindiel está en el puerto élfico de Celondim, en Ered Luin.\
\
Baillindiel espera que regreses con el segundo conjunto de componentes.","Diente mellado de Narglup recogido","Garras astilladas de huargo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Has tenido un éxito admirable hasta este punto, ${PLAYER}. Haré uso de estos componentes en la forja de esta arma.\
\
'También necesito las gotas corrosivas de las babosas de azufre de Angmar, garras de huargos, como los que se encuentran en Angmar y Eregion, y garras de los murciélagos que infestan Angmar y Moria.'","Baillindiel ha aceptado ayudarte a forjar un arma que te ayude a cumplir tus deberes como ${PLAYERNAME:un Juglar[m]|una Juglaresa[f]} de gran renombre.","Baillindiel está en el puerto élfico de Celondim, en Ered Luin.\
\
Baillindiel espera que regreses con el primer conjunto de componentes.","Garras macabras de murciélago recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","'Busca al huargo Narglup en Angmar, ${PLAYER}, y a las sierpes de las rocas en las Montañas Nubladas.'","'¿No tienes los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}?'","Runa de Dominio Alado recogida","Recolecta colmillos astillados de sierpe de las rocas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baillindiel está en el puerto élfico de Celondim, en Ered Luin.\
\
Baillindiel espera que regreses con el último conjunto de componentes.","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí? ¿Por qué es esto, ${PLAYER}?'","Gotas corrosivas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'El uruk Morthrâng habita dentro de los muros de Urugarth, y las merrevail Mormoz y Azgoth pueden encontrarse en Carn Dûm.'","Emblema de Ritual recogido","Instrumentos de Canción","Recolecta garras astilladas de huargo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el último conjunto de componentes a Baillindiel","Recolecta el diente mellado de Narglup","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Baillindiel","Colmillos astillados de sierpe de las rocas recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Morthrâng puede encontrarse en Urugarth. Mormoz y Azgoth habitan en Carn Dûm.\
\
Baillindiel te pidió que regresaras con un Emblema de Ritual y una Runa de Dominio Alado.","Recolecta la Runa de Dominio Alado","Narglup merodea por Fasach-larran en Angmar. Las sierpes de las rocas habitan en las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
Baillindiel te pidió que le trajeras colmillos astillados de sierpe de las rocas y el diente mellado del huargo Narglup.","'¡Estoy encantada de tu regreso, ${PLAYER}! Sé que la historia de tu valentía y coraje en la obtención de estos objetos debe de ser una realmente emocionante. Permíteme usarlos en la forja de esta arma para ti... y está hecho.\
\
'Te entrego esta arma con la certeza de que te servirá bien y fielmente mientras lleves esperanza a los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media. Te cuento entre mis amigos, ${PLAYER}, y espero que tú hagas lo mismo.'"},
[6556]={"Entrega el último lote de materiales a Hunward en el Muelle de los Comerciantes","'Te estás perdiendo algo.'","Recoge picos venenosos de tortuga aterradora (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge corteza de ucorno endurecida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reúne cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog","'¡Esto servirá perfectamente! Los próximos materiales que necesito que consigas te llevarán más lejos, a lugares de mayor peligro. Hablo de las extensiones nevadas de Forochel y de la temida tierra llamada Angmar.\
\
'Tráeme los ojos nublados de sierpes como las que habitan en Forochel y Angmar. También necesitaré los picos de las tortugas aterradoras que solo se arrastran por Angmar. ¡Cuidado con sus caparazones duros y procura que tus golpes alcancen solo la carne blanda del interior!'","'Muchos son quienes subestiman el poder de un buen Luchador. \\q¿Dónde está tu espada o tu lanza?\\q preguntan, solo para descubrir, para su pesar, que no necesitamos tales armas.\
\
'Forjaré para ti un magnífico par de guanteletes de batalla, pero necesitaré que me traigas varios materiales. Debes saber que no será fácil. Usaré algunos de estos objetos para fabricar tus armas, pero otros servirán para demostrar que eres digno de tal equipo. Así fue conmigo, y así será contigo.\
\
'Primero necesitaré corteza de ucorno endurecida de los ucornos que acechan el Bosque Salvaje, y cuchillos de orco del Bosque Salvaje. Tráemelos y luego te encomendaré buscar materiales que deberán obtenerse más lejos, en lugares más peligrosos.'","'Barashal el gorthorog y Gruglok de Urugarth son adversarios temibles. De Barashal, recoge un cuerno de gorthorog carmesí. Se lo puede encontrar en la siniestra ciudad de Carn Dûm. De Gruglok, en Urugarth, obtendrás un Sello de Guerra, si eres capaz de derrotarlo en combate.'","Recoge ojos de sierpe nublados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Picos venenosos de tortuga aterradora recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega el primer lote de materiales a Hunward en el Muelle de los Comerciantes","Se pueden encontrar sierpes en Forochel y Angmar. Las tortugas aterradoras se encuentran en Malenhad, en Angmar.\
\
Hunward te pidió que le llevaras ojos de sierpe nublados y picos venenosos de tortuga aterradora.","'¡Bien hecho! Estos materiales son justo lo que buscaba. Pero aún necesitaré dos objetos más, ¡y puede que recolectarlos te resulte la tarea más exigente!\
\
'Barashal el gorthorog y Gruglok de Urugarth son adversarios temibles. De Barashal, recoge un cuerno de gorthorog carmesí. Se lo puede encontrar en la siniestra ciudad de Carn Dûm. De Gruglok, en Urugarth, obtendrás un Sello de Guerra, si eres capaz de derrotarlo en combate.'","Corteza de ucorno endurecida recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hunward te ha pedido que consigas corteza de ucorno endurecida y cuchillos de orco del Bosque Salvaje a partir de criaturas del Bosque Salvaje.","Cuchillos de orco del Bosque Salvaje recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hunward se encuentra en el Muelle de los Comerciantes, en el Bosque Salvaje.","'¡Nunca dudé de ti ni por un instante, ${PLAYER}! Muy bien hecho, y como recompensa por tus grandes esfuerzos te entrego estos guanteletes de batalla. ¡Que te sirvan bien allá donde te lleven tus aventuras!\
\
'Tus adversarios llegarán a temer cada uno de tus golpes, pues serán más mortíferos que nunca.'","Cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog reunido","'Primero necesitaré corteza de ucorno endurecida de los ucornos que acechan el Bosque Salvaje, y cuchillos de orco del Bosque Salvaje. Tráemelos y luego te encomendaré buscar materiales que deberán obtenerse más lejos, en lugares más peligrosos.'","Implementos para golpear","Barashal se encuentra en Carn Dûm, en Angmar. Gruglok está en Urugarth, en Angmar.\
\
Hunward te ha pedido que le lleves un cuerno de gorthorog carmesí y un Sello de Guerra.","Ojos de sierpe nublados recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega el segundo lote de materiales a Hunward en el Muelle de los Comerciantes","Hunward, en el Muelle de los Comerciantes del Bosque Salvaje, ha aceptado forjarte un excelente conjunto de armas para tus puños.","'Tráeme los ojos nublados de sierpes como las que habitan en Forochel y Angmar. También necesitaré los picos de las tortugas aterradoras que solo se arrastran por Angmar. ¡Cuidado con sus caparazones duros y procura que tus golpes alcancen solo la carne blanda del interior!'","Sello de Guerra reunido","Recoge cuchillos de orco del Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6557]={"Las arañas pueden encontrarse en Angmar y Helegrod, en las Montañas Nubladas. Las sierpes pueden encontrarse en lugares como Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas, Sarnur en Ered Luin y Eregion. Los barghests pueden encontrarse en Fornost, en las Quebradas del Norte, en la Tumba de Maenadar en las Quebradas de los Túmulos de Bree-land, y en Angmar.\
\
Dawn Stockard te pidió que le trajeras hileras enroscadas de araña, ojos de sierpes odiosas y patas podridas de barghest.","Recolecta la hoja dentada de Fakhthal","Dawn Stockard ha accedido a ayudarte a forjar un arma digna de tu estatus como gran capitán","Has recolectado patas podridas de barghest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has reunido asquerosos cuchillos de Quitanieves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recolectado Medallón de Paso","Lleva el último conjunto de componentes a Dawn Stockard","'Los Trasgos Quitanieves habitan en las Montañas Nubladas, mientras que Fakhthal comanda a los orcos de Fasach-falroid en Angmar.'","'Dushkâl, Brízrip y Thordragh pueden encontrarse en Urugarth, en Angmar, y los uruks pueden hallarse en Carn Dûm, también en Angmar.'","Recolecta cuchillos nocivos de Quitanieves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta patas podridas de barghest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Dawn Stockard","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","'¿No tienes los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}?'","Implementos de Guerra","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Dawn Stockard","Dawn Stockard está en el pueblo de Archet, al norte de Bree.\
\
Dawn Stockard espera que regreses con el primer conjunto de componentes que necesita.","Dawn Stockard está en el pueblo de Archet, al norte de Bree.\
\
Dawn Stockard espera que regreses con el segundo conjunto de componentes.","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí?'","Gertheryg Dushkâl, Brízrip y Thordragh pueden encontrarse en Urugarth, en Angmar. Los uruks pueden hallarse en Carn Dûm, también en Angmar.\
\
Dawn Stockard te pidió que regresaras con los dientes del Gorthorog y un Medallón de Paso.","'Busca arañas en Angmar y en Helegrod en las Montañas Nubladas, sierpes en lugares como Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas, Sarnur en Ered Luin y Eregion, y barghests en Fornost y Haudh Iarchith.'","'Puedo forjarte un arma que corresponda a tu imponente caracter como ${PLAYERNAME:Capitán[m]|Capitana[f]}, , pero te advierto que su fabricación estará llena de peligros. Como con todas las cosas de valor, el camino hacia ella será duro y largo, pero sin duda mirarás atrás con satisfacción.\
\
'Necesito que te aventures y me traigas los materiales necesarios para forjar tu arma. Los primeros objetos son algunos cuchillos de los Trasgos Quitanieves que habitan en las Montañas Nubladas y la hoja dentada del orco Fakhthal, que manda a los orcos de Fasach-falroid en Angmar.\
\
'Tráeme estos objetos, y comenzaré mi trabajo.'","Has reunido la hoja dentada de Fakhthal.","Recolecta dientes de un Gorthorog","Recolecta Medallón de Paso","Los Trasgos Quitanieves se encuentran en las Montañas Nubladas. Fakhthal lidera a los orcos de Fasach-falroid en Angmar.\
\
Dawn Stockard te pidió que le llevaras asquerosos cuchillos Quitanieves y la hoja dentada de Fakhthal.","'Regresas de entre la oscuridad, , ¡y te saludo por ello! Toma esta arma con mis más altos respetos, porque eres verdaderamente ${PLAYERNAME:un Capitán poderoso[m]|una Capitana poderosa[f]} entre los Hombres.'","Has recolectado dientes de un Gorthorog","Recolecta hileras enroscadas de araña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta ojos de sierpes odiosas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has reunido hileras enroscadas de araña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dawn Stockard está en el pueblo de Archet, al norte de Bree.\
\
nDawn Stockard espera que regreses con el último conjunto de componentes que necesita para el arma que hará para ti.","'¡Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo, ${PLAYER}! Me alegra mucho verte regresar a Archet y con los componentes que te pedí.\
\
'Queda un conjunto de componentes, y estos serán los más peligrosos de conseguir. Necesito los dientes de un Gorthorog, que se pueden conseguir de Dushkâl, Brízrip o Thordragh en Urugarth, y un Medallón de Paso de los uruks que guardan Carn Dûm.'","'Mi corazón se alegra de verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}, y de ver que has acabado con Fakhthal. Su deuda conmigo está saldada.\
\
'Los cuchillos de los Quitanieves son también un valioso botín, y prestarán su filo al arma que forjaré para ti.\
\
'Sin embargo, estos son solo los primeros componentes que necesito. Ahora deberías buscar para mí ojos de sierpes como las que se encuentran en Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas, Sarnur en Ered Luin o Eregion; hileras de araña de las arañas de Angmar y Helegrod en las Montañas Nubladas; y patas de los barghests de Fornost y Haudh Iarchith.'"},
[6558]={"'Puedo forjarte un arma que esté a la altura de tu gran habilidad como ${PLAYERNAME:cazador[m]|cazadora[f]}, , pero debes prepararte para la adversidad, pues su historia no será fácilmente ganada.\
\
'Necesitaré tiempo entre cada etapa del proceso, así que no me traigas todo de una vez. Primero necesitaré bastones corroídos de la Corona de Hierro, que pueden encontrarse en Angmar, y una garra afilada de Zarpahelada, un gran oso de las Montañas Nubladas, que habita en la tierra de los gigantes.\
\
'¡Que la fortuna te sonría durante tu cacería, ! Lo ha hecho hasta ahora, y sé que seguirá haciéndolo.'","'¡Me alegra tu regreso, , pues Zarpahelada fue antaño un oponente temible! ¡Su garra ahora me servirá para forjar un arma digna de ${PLAYERNAME:un cazador[m]|una cazadora[f]} como tú!\
\
'Puede que te sorprenda saber que los bastones que has traído no son lo que busco. No, lo valioso es la corrosión de su superficie. Eso le dará filo a tu arma.\
\
'Hay más componentes que deben reunirse. Ahora debes encontrar los ojos de las sierpes que habitan en Forochel y Angmar. También necesitaré los picos de las tortugas temibles de Angmar y las uñas pútridas de los muertos vivientes en Imlad Balchorth.'","'No te envidio esta tarea, ${PLAYER}, pero estos componentes finales me permitirán forjarte un arma verdaderamente extraordinaria. Carn Dûm alberga un gran mal, pero recuperar estos objetos dará a tu arma una fuerza increíble.'","Recolectado baba pútrida de Helchgam","Has recolectado Medallón de Paso","Fenton Marshley está en el Refugio de Cazadores, al este de Archet y al norte de Bree, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Has recolectado el segundo conjunto de componentes que Fenton Marshley te pidió.","'¿No tienes el primer conjunto de componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? ¿Por qué?'","Fenton Marshley está en el Refugio de Cazadores, al este de Archet y al norte de Bree, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Has recolectado el último conjunto de componentes que Fenton Marshley te pidió.","Recolecta bastones corroídos de la Corona de Hierro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recolectado los picos venenosos de las tortugas temibles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Puedes encontrar todas las criaturas que buscas en Angmar, aunque se dice que una variedad similar de sierpe vive en Forochel.'","Lleva el último conjunto de componentes a Fenton Marshley","Fenton Marshley está en el Refugio de Cazadores, al este de Archet y al norte de Bree, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Has recolectado el primer conjunto de componentes que Fenton Marshley te pidió.","Se recogieron uñas pútridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Hombres de Angmar pueden encontrarse en Fasach-falroid y cerca de Malenhad, en Angmar. Zarpahelada puede hallarse en las Montañas Nubladas, donde habitan los gigantes.\
\
Fenton Marshley te pidió que le trajeras una de las garras afiladas de Zarpahelada y los bastones corroídos de la Corona de Hierro, llevados por los malvados Hombres de Angmar.","Has recolectado la garra afilada de Zarpahelada","Recolectados ojos de sierpe nublados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge uñas pútridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el segundo conjunto de componentes a Fenton Marshley","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? ¿No deseas esta arma?'","Has recolectado bastones corroídos de la Corona de Hierro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instrumentos de la Caza","'Puedes encontrar Hombres de Angmar en Angmar. Zarpahelada, según entiendo, merodea por la tierra de los gigantes en las Montañas Nubladas.'","Lleva el primer conjunto de componentes a Fenton Marshley","Recolecta picos venenosos de tortuga temible (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta la garra afilada de Zarpahelada","Fenton Marshley ha aceptado ayudarte a forjar un arma digna de tu gran habilidad como cazador. La historia de esta arma será una de peligro y maldad, pero de estas dificultades surgirá la fuerza.","Recolecta ojos de sierpe nublados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Has regresado, y con los componentes que te pedí! ¡Extraordinario!\
\
'Has hecho un gran trabajo hasta ahora, , y has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un cazador digno[m]|una cazadora digna[f]}, pero tu mayor desafío aún está por venir.\
\
'Los componentes finales que necesito para forjarte un arma digna se encuentran en la oscura ciudad de Carn Dûm. Es un lugar malvado, y dentro de sus muros enfrentarás grandes peligros si decides continuar. Necesito un Medallón de Paso, llevado por los uruks que custodian la ciudad, y la baba pútrida de Helchgam, que habita bajo la ciudad.'","Las sierpes pueden encontrarse en Forochel y Angmar. Las tortugas temibles habitan en Malenhad, en Angmar. Los muertos vivientes rondan Imlad Balchorth, en Angmar.\
\
Fenton te pidió que le trajeras ojos de sierpe nublados, picos venenosos de tortuga temible y uñas pútridas.","Recolecta Medallón de Paso","Los uruks custodian la ciudad de Carn Dûm, en Angmar, mientras que el vil Helchgam habita en sus profundidades.\
\
Fenton te pidió que le trajeras un Medallón de Paso y la baba pútrida de Helchgam.","Recolecta baba pútrida de Helchgam","'¿No tienes los componentes que te pedí? ¿Por qué?'","'Has regresado, ${PLAYER}, ¡y con los componentes finales que necesito!\
\
'La historia de esta arma será verdaderamente notable, pues has cazado criaturas de tal malicia que pocos antes que tú se habrían atrevido a enfrentarlas.\
\
'Me honra conocerte, ${PLAYER}, y estoy a tu servicio. Te entrego un arma que espero esté a la altura de tu gran habilidad.'"},
[6559]={"El cuidador de huargos Athpukh se puede encontrar en Urugarth en Angmar. La reina morroval Azgoth se puede encontrar en Carn Dûm en Angmar.\
\
Sterling Ganapié te pidió que le trajeras un símbolo de cuidador de huargos y una garra cruel de Azgoth.","'¡Perfecto, perfecto! ¡Estos servirán muy bien!\
\
'Me pondré a trabajar usando estos en la construcción de tu arma, pero tendrás que salir de nuevo y buscar el segundo grupo de cosas que necesito.\
\
'Necesito que recojas ojos de sierpes odiosas de lugares como Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas y Eregion. También necesito picos de las tortugas temibles de Malenhad en el este de Angmar.'","Recoge la garra partida de Narglup","Las sanguijuelas de azufre se pueden encontrar por las regiones orientales de Malenhad en Angmar. Narglup se puede encontrar cerca de Tór Gailvin en las regiones occidentales de Angmar.\
\
Sterling Ganapié te pidió que regresaras con colmillos de sanguijuela de azufre huecos y la garra partida del Huargo Narglup.","Lleva el último grupo de componentes a Sterling Ganapié","'Todavía estoy esperando el primer grupo de componentes, ${PLAYER}.'","Has recogido el símbolo del cuidador de huargos","Recoge colmillos de sanguijuela de azufre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No me has traído los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}? ¿No quieres esta arma?'","'No tienes los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}.'","Has recogido una garra cruel de Azgoth","Recoge ojos de sierpes odiosas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el segundo grupo de componentes a Sterling Ganapié","Has recogido colmillos de sanguijuela de azufre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recogido la garra partida de Narglup","Has recogido picos venenos de tortuga temible (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el primer grupo de componentes a Sterling Ganapié","'Athpukh se puede encontrar en Urugarth, y Azgoth se puede encontrar en Carn Dûm, ambos en Angmar.'","'¡Otro trabajo bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Déjame incorporar estos objetos y... ¡ay! Esta garra es afilada -- ¡espero no encontrarme nunca con una morroval, si esta garra es una indicación!\
\
'Te doy esta arma, saqueador ${PLAYER}. ¡Úsala bien!\
\
'No fue tan difícil, ¿verdad?'","Utensilios de la noche","Sterling Ganapié está en Los Gamos, al oeste de Bree y al este del río Brandivino.\
\
Sterling Ganapié está esperando a que regreses con el último grupo de componentes.","Recoge la garra cruel de Azgoth","'Las sanguijuelas de azufre y el huargo Narglup se pueden encontrar en Angmar; las sanguijuelas al este y Narglup al oeste.'","Sterling Ganapié está en Los Gamos, al oeste de Bree y al este del río Brandivino.\
\
Sterling Ganapié está esperando a que regreses con el primer grupo de componentes.","Ojos de sierpes odiosas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sterling Ganapié ha accedido a ayudarte a fabricar un arma que complemente tu gran habilidad como saqueador.","'Las sierpes que necesitas cazar se pueden encontrar en lugares como Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas y Eregion.'","Las sierpes con los ojos que nos interesan habitan en lugares como Forochel, las Montañas Nubladas y Eregion. Las tortugas temibles habitan en Malenhad, en las regiones orientales de Angmar.\
\
Sterling Ganapié te pidió que le trajeras ojos de sierpes odiosas y picos venenosos de tortuga temible.","Sterling Ganapié está en Los Gamos, al oeste de Bree y al este del río Brandivino.\
\
Sterling Ganapié está esperando a que regreses con el segundo grupo de componentes.","Recoge el símbolo del cuidador de huargos","Recoge picos venenos de tortuga temible (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Si eres algo ${PLAYERNAME:parecido[m]|parecida[f]} a mí, , querrás un arma que sea justo lo que necesitan aquellos que han elegido seguir esa noble profesión convirtiéndose en saqueadores. ¡Y no cualquier ${PLAYERNAME:saqueador[m]|saqueadora[f]}, sino uno hábil! ¡No cualquier arma servirá, y yo puedo hacer una así para ti!\
\
'No será fácil, sin embargo. Necesitaré una serie de cosas de lugares de difícil acceso. ¿Qué estoy diciendo? ¡Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un excelente saqueador[m]|una excelente saqueadora[f]}! ¡Estoy seguro de que podrás hacerlo!\
\
'Las primeras cosas que necesitaré son colmillos de las sanguijuelas de azufre del este de Angmar y la garra del Huargo Narglup, que también se puede encontrar en Angmar, aunque al oeste cerca de Tór Gailvin.'","'¡Trabajo espléndido, ! ¡Sabía que eras ${PLAYERNAME:un saqueador[m]|una saqueadora[f]} de primera!\
\
'Hay un último grupo de cosas que necesitaré. Ten en cuenta que tendrás que buscar en lugares bastante desagradables, pero ese es el trabajo, ¿no?\
\
'Necesito un símbolo de cuidador de huargos del trasgo Athpukh, que custodia los corrales de huargos de Urugarth en Angmar. También necesito la garra cruel de la reina morroval Azgoth, que habita en la ciudad malvada de Carn Dûm en Angmar.'"},
[6560]={"Dirígete bajo el puente del Cruce de las Cenizas","Has defendido a Regin","Has llegado bajo el puente del Cruce de las Cenizas","Habla con Regin bajo el puente sur a la salida del Cruce de las Cenizas","Conocimiento impuro","'Ve a hablar con Regin. Cuanto más tardes, mayores serán las posibilidades de que los orcos utilicen la antigua forja contra nosotros.'","Gúthi está en el Cruce de las Cenizas, en la parte occidental de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Deberías regresar con Gúthi.","'La antigua forja de Hurmulkezer es responsable de toda esa armadura llameante que vemos en los Ghâsh-hai, y parece que también la están usando para forjar grandes armas.\
\
'Ve a hablar con Regin, el antiguo encargado de la forja, para descubrir cómo impedir que los orcos la utilicen.\
\
'Lo encontrarás en la zona inferior, justo al sur del Cruce de las Cenizas; está trabajando en reforzar los puentes.'","Nuevas informaciones han salido a la luz: los orcos buscan una forja en particular, la antigua forja de Hurmulkezer. La han estado usando para forjar armaduras llameantes y también planean crear una nueva arma mortal...","'¿Los orcos controlan la antigua forja? ¡Esto no puede ser! No es de extrañar que sean tan fuertes y peligrosos en estas profundidades olvidadas.\
\
'Por suerte, hay una forma de detenerlos. Procedo de una larga estirpe de enanos que han transmitido el conocimiento de la forja, y resulta que existe un sistema de seguridad para una situación así. Toma este diapasón de mithril y hazlo sonar cerca de la forja para desactivarla.\
\
'Mantente alerta, ${PLAYER}: ¡los atacantes están cerca!'","Habla con Gúthi en el Cruce de las Cenizas","'¿Hay una forma de desactivar la forja? ¡Debemos hacerlo de inmediato! No podemos permitir que los orcos sigan utilizándola contra nosotros.'","'Vigila a Regin. Cuanto más tardes, mayor será el peligro en el que se encuentra.'","Regin se encuentra en la esquina suroeste de las Profundidades Llameantes, en la zona inferior al sur del Cruce de las Cenizas.\
\
Deberías ir a hablar con Regin bajando por las escaleras desde el Cruce de las Cenizas.","Regin se encuentra en la esquina suroeste de las Profundidades Llameantes, en la zona inferior al sur del Cruce de las Cenizas.\
\
Deberías encontrarlo y hablar con él."},
[6561]={"Has encontrado el estanque en la segunda terraza","Encuentra el estanque de la tercera terraza","Aguas impuras","La entrada a Glinghant se encuentra en la plaza de Clorhir, en Annúminas. Glinghant se compone de varias terrazas, y en cada terraza hay un estanque.\
\
Debes verter agua del vial de agua limpia que te han proporcionado en cada uno de los estanques de las terrazas de Glinghant.","Has encontrado el estanque en la tercera terraza","Los aguaoscuras que han ocupado Glinghant son criaturas viles y corruptas enviadas por Amarthiel con el propósito de profanar la belleza de sus estanques y jardines. La belleza que tenía antaño está perdida, y el agua emponzoñada ahora se extiende a la ciudad. ¡Temo que la corrupción pronto llegue al lago Nenuial si no hacemos algo!\
\
No es algo fácil, pero hablé con Gwindeth, la Dama Azul de Nenuial y adquirí un vial de agua limpia con la que deberíamos ser capaces de purificar los estanques de Glinghant. El vial no contiene mucha, así que no debemos malgastarla, pero si se vierte en los estanques en cada una de las tres terrazas de Glinghant deberían purificar las aguas y con ello disminuir la corrupción de los aguaosucras.\
\
La entrada de Glinghant está aquí en la plaza de Clorhir. Vierte algo de agua de este vial en los estanque sde cada terraza de Glinghant y vuelve cuando lo hayas hecho. ¡Quizá todavía podamos purgar algo de este mal, ${PLAYER}! Si no estoy disponible cuando vuelva, habla con el capitán general Daerdan en Echad Garthadir, aquí en la ciudad.","Encuentra el estanque de la segunda terraza"},
[6562]={"Faeleth se encuentra en Minas Tirith (Solsticio de Verano).\
\
Faeleth te da las gracias por participar en la celebración del Solsticio de Verano.","'¡Muy bien! ¡Espero que estés disfrutando de los festejos del Solsticio de Verano!\
\
'¡Como muestra de agradecimiento por acompañarnos en la celebración, permíteme ofrecerte este regalo!\
\
'¿Volverás mañana también?'","Habla con Faeleth en Minas Tirith (Solsticio de Verano)","Habla con el capitán Khâtaphos en Isla Remota, en las Islas Escudo","Las celebraciones del solsticio de verano tienen lugar en Minas Tirith (Solsticio de Verano), así como en la Mansión de Thorin, Duillond, Bree, el Árbol de la Fiesta en la Comarca e Isla Remota en las Islas Escudo.\
\
A medida que se acerca el día del solsticio de verano, los pueblos de la Tierra Media se reúnen para celebrar el gran Festival del Solsticio. ¡Disfruta del baile, la alegría y el amor con tu familia y amigos!","Celebrando el Solsticio de Verano","'Tanto si te unes a la fiesta aquí, en Isla Remota, como en tierras distantes, ¡sin duda te encontrarás en alegre compañía!\
\
'¡Solo te pedimos que celebres con el espíritu del Solsticio de Verano!'","'Tanto si te unes a la fiesta aquí, en Minas Tirith, como en tierras distantes, ¡sin duda te encontrarás en alegre compañía!\
\
'¡Solo te pedimos que celebres con el espíritu del Solsticio de Verano!'","Participaste en la celebración del Solsticio de Verano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A medida que se acerca el día del solsticio de verano, los pueblos de la Tierra Media se reúnen para celebrar el gran Festival del Solsticio. ¡Disfruta del baile, la alegría y el amor con tu familia y amigos!"},
[6563]={"The Middle Stores are in south part of the Third Circle.\
\
They have some Old Calembel deep at the back of the Middle Stores. You should gather some for Forlong's table.","Find a hat","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Listen to Forlong continue his tale.","'Hm... Is this claim to be the wine... or the cheese?'","In Days of Youth","Listen to Hirluin","Forlong claims the mark can be found in the Third Circle, just north of the Pier.\
\
Look for a mark on the column where the old Master of the Burg swung at Forlong's head. Forlong claims it can still be seen but Hirluin disbelieves him.","'Well, what did you see? I was right, wasn't I?'","Look for the mark on the column","Bring the cheese to Neldir","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Forlong, Hirluin, and Neldir have tasted the Old Calembel. See how they liked it.","'And there we were, stumbling down the darkened street, all that wine and what-have-you stuffed under our coats! Now what was it called, that wine? The name escapes me! And to think I drank so very much of it in those years!\
\
'Ah, hold your tongue, Hirluin! I hear the dart of wit upon it before you ever moved your lips. Forgetting comes of drinking, you will say, and so that wine was its own undoing. I guess correctly, do I not? Ha ha! But let me think one moment... was it? ... yes! Beren's Blood, it was named. How I should like a taste of that wine now!\
\
'You there, my good ${RACE}. Since you are standing right at hand, be so good as to go ask old Imadan if he has got any.'","'And look, we have drained this bottle of Beren's Blood. Why, friend, I know what you should do. You should run and place it on that stone he loved, as a tribute to his memory. Yes, that is just the thing!'","'Hold! Hold! This is too much. Confess, Forlong, for NOW you have embellished! Ah, I know that set of the jaw. You stand by your story, do you? So be it.\
\
'Friend ${CLASS}, as you have not wandered off, I wonder if you will settle another quibble. Can you find such things as these and bring them here? Surely they can all be found somewhere in this Circle. What did you say, Forlong? It was a hat, some bread, some flowers, and a small rug?'","Listen to Neldir","'If you are looking for Authlin, you have missed him by ten years. Though, for what it's worth, I have heard he died with a glass of wine in his hand and a song on his lips.'","Go up to the Fourth Circle and see if anyone knows what became of the minstrel Authlin.","'The mark can be seen? And you swear to it? Well! I cannot shout at the sun that it is night, can I? Ha ha!\
\
'But we interrupted ourselves mid-tale. Please, carry on!'","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Hear what Hirluin has to say.","The three friends raise their glasses and drink","'Why, what have we here? It is a memory in the round, my friends! I thank you, good ${CLASS}. Hirluin, hand me that bread. Forlong, the knife. Let us put fond memory to our lips.'","Ask for Old Calembel in the Middle Stores","'How marvelous! You have brought the things. Now we will put it to the test. Can you walk from here to there and carry these? I do not even ask you to run.'","'What? Old Calembel? Aye, I think we might well have some, farther in. I'm not going back there. If you want some, you'll need to go yourself.'","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Return to the Merry Swan and tell Forlong the bottle has been placed at Authlin's favourite stone.","Search for these things in the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Look for a hat, some bread, some flowers, and a small rug to help prove Neldir's point.","'I will confess, this is not how I remembered it. Ha ha! No, it is quite... different.'","'It is tart - or perhaps merely bitter - and yet mellow. Or perhaps not so mellow as bland.'","Found some flowers","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Hear to what Neldir has to say.","Take some Beren's Blood wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If we've got any Old Calembel, it's far at the back. Take any you find in there. Nobody else seems to want it.'","Find some flowers","'Lord Forlong here must not be indulged or allowed such extravagant tales. Do see if you can find those things somewhere nearby.'","Return with the wine","Return to Neldir","Place the bottle at Authlin's stone","Find a small rug","Raise a glass","Take some Old Calembel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Bring the cheese back to the Merry Swan.","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Lord Forlong has recalled an old wine they used to drink, named Beren's Blood, and has asked you to bring him some.","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Find some of the Old Calembel cheese that Forlong and his friends used to eat with their favourite wine. Start by asking Imadan, the barkeep of the Merry Swan.","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Try to carry the pile of things across the room.","Took a bottle of wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Forlong","'Old Calembel? Ah, well. I don't know what to say, but that some things linger and some things fade away. I haven't had any of that cheese for a good many years. Though now that I think of it, you might try the back of the Middle Stores, just up the way. You'll find all kinds of things back there, you will.'","'Is this truly the companion to our youthful wine? My eyes tell me so, but my tongue calls them liars!'","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
You have learned what became of Authlin, Master Minstrel. Now you should return to Forlong and company in the Merry Swan.","Return to Hirluin","'Why, to woo the heart of my Vanyalos! Oh, do not give such frowns, you goats. None of us have forgotten the procession of maids swooning over you, Hirluin. Nor that tale of climbing the circle-wall, with... what was her name, that one maid with the dark hair?'","Talk to Neldir","Ask after Authlin (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Imadan has some of the Beren's Blood wine Forlong wants. You should gather some yourself from the storage area.","Talk to Hirluin","'You will see, Neldir. It can be done and I did it!'","Forlong and his friends are in the Merry Swan, in the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Drink with Forlong and company.","Found some bread","'The bottle is placed? That is good. We did well to honour old Authlin.'\
\
Forlong closes his eyes and for a moment, the garrulous conversation comes to a rest.","Ask Imadan for Old Calembel","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Return to the Merry Swan and tell Hirluin the mark can, in fact, be seen.","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Bring the wine back over to Forlong's table.","The things tumble from your hands!","'Be a good ${RACE} and ask old Imadan if he's got any Beren's Blood wine, would you?'","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Listen to Forlong's reply.","The three solemnly partake of bread and cheese","Hirluin catches your arm as you come up.\
\
'Give that wine here, friend. Should you place it before Forlong, we others might never have a taste.'\
\
This is met with hearty laughter, not least by Forlong himself.\
\
'Here friends - a glass for you Neldir, a glass for me, yes, and one for you, Forlong, old friend. To our days of youth!'","You place the bottle reverently at the stone's base","Found a hat","'Beren's Blood?'\
\
Imadan lets out a low whistle.\
\
'You might say that old stuff's a bit beneath lords such as they. But I know what they're at. It's what they drank when they were young men and went free about the City. I suppose recollecting old times can recollect old thirsts, eh?\
\
'There's some over there, among my stores. You may help yourself.'","'That old Beren's Blood wine is over yonder, among the storage. Take what you please.'","'That was an invention of the minstrel Authlin, and what is more, I think you know it. Though I hold that she spread the tale with as much relish as the minstrel ever did.'","'I haven't had any Old Calembel in years. But you might find some in the Middle Stores.'","Carry the pile of things","'Well done. That was quite amusing.'","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Hear what Forlong has to say.","Found a small rug","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Bring the things you have gathered back to Neldir, in the Merry Swan.","Here was Authlin's favourite place to sing","'But now we have our wine and our regrettable cheese. Finish your tale, Forlong. You had so many bottles of Beren's Blood under your coats... and what then?'","'That wasn't how it went at all. You haven't the grasp, and besides, your heart wasn't in it!'","Find some bread","Listen to Forlong","'How many times have I heard Authlin the Minstrel's name spoken? There are many tales told of that man. Why that patch of green, across the way over there, was his favourite place to perform. They say the night air filled with his harp as he stood there and played sweet melodies to the stars.'","'Ah, now you go too far! I will not allow such a wanton claim to stand. Someone must be sent. You, ${RACE}, will you go out on the street and show this for a braggart's lie? It was just north of the Pier, Forlong, was it not? Against an alley-column? Yes. Will you go and see?'","'And with one sip, a flood of memories! How we sat at this very table, night upon night. Our glasses full of Beren's Blood and Old Calembel cheese upon our plates.\
\
'${CLASS}, you have kindly furnished us with the wine. Can you find us the cheese, as well? Do some old men a kindness!'","'Ho ho! This is a mess! I am sorry, friend. Forlong, we see through your plans now. You fed us one truth in hopes we would swallow a lie!\
\
'But tell me, even if you could bear all that in your arms, why in Isildur's name WOULD you?'","Authlin's favourite spot was across from the Artists' Fellow-hall in the Fourth Circle.\
\
Place the empty bottle of Beren's Blood at Authlin's favourite spot, to commemorate the old minstrel.","Ask Imadan for Beren's Blood wine","'If you could settle this question of whether the old Master's cane-mark has lasted to this day, or not, we should be ever so grateful.'","Took Old Calembel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Authlin's favourite spot","Lord Forlong sits in the Merry Swan Tavern, drinking with his old friends Lord Hirluin and one Neldir of Minas Tirith, making the most of the calm before the storm.","'Authlin? Why I knew him well, perhaps better than most, though I have not seen him in many a year. I will tell you something I remember of him. Sometimes, after a night of drink and merriment and song, he would confess to me that though his heart burned bright, there was a well of sorrow in it, too, and they ever wrestled. Sorrow for what, he would never tell. And then, sometimes, he would tell me he meant to fight the sorrow and love all the world until he knew his time had come, and then how sweet his rest would be. That is what he told me.'","You can clearly make out the mark Forlong spoke of","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Hear what Neldir has to say.","'Why, old Minastúr, the last Master of the Burg stumbled across us! It was blind luck, and very bad at that. He knew at once we were the ones who'd done it, and he set to chasing us, waving that iron cane he went about with at us most menacingly!\
\
'In fact, he swung at my head and nearly took it off. To this day, there is a mark against the stone that he hit instead!'","'Well! As I was saying, there we were with some bottles of wine tucked in our arms, but I, for one, had also a hat, bread, some flowers, and a small rolled up rug.'","'Well, my dear friends. If we've learned something tonight, it is that in drink old friends stay true. In taste, they may differ. Ha ha! Ha ha ha!\
\
'Let us wash away that unfortunate taste with another drink of Beren's Blood!'","'Do us a kindness and see if Imadan's got some Old Calembel cheese lying around.'","'I doubt it not, Hirluin. The maids ever fell under your cold spell.\
\
'Old Authlin, though. Now there was a minstrel of uncommon gifts! And a bit of a mischief-maker, too, wasn't he? But who would not forgive words so sweetly sung, or deftly penned! Of war he sang and kings of old, of flowery vales and shepherd's pipes, and of fair-eyed maids.\
\
'You, Neldir, you have lived in Minas Tirith all this time. Does he live and play still? You know not? I must learn his fate. My good ${RACE}, may we lean upon your goodness once again? Will you go up into the Fourth Circle and learn what became of Authlin, Master Minstrel?'","The Middle Stores are in south part of the Third Circle.\
\
Imadan has no Old Calembel cheese, but thinks the back reaches of the Middle Stores might have some.","The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.\
\
Listen to Neldir's interjection.","Neldir combines the items into a rough pile","Talk to Forlong","'So Authlin lived a good life and died a willing death? Truly, that is the wisdom of old Westernesse!\
\
'Let us honour him and raise a glass. You, too, friend ${CLASS}! You have earned your place, I think!'"},
[6564]={"Collect athelas in Gurz-shâpol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected athelas in Gurz-shâpol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect athelas in Gurz-shâpol","You have discovered patches of athelas growing in Gurz-shâpol and should recover it for the good of the Rohirrim.","You have gathered much athelas from Gurz-shâpol, and stowed it away for the coming journey to Dunharrow. The warriors of Rohan will benefit greatly from your bravery as the darkest days of war draw ever nearer.","Athelas can be found throughout Gurz-shâpol.\
\
You have discovered athelas growing in the dark of Gurz-shâpol that has gone unnoticed by the Orcs. You should gather it for the warriors of Rohan.","You have gathered much athelas for the warriors of Rohan, and should now store it for the coming journey to Dunharrow.","You have not gathered enough athelas for the Rohirrim and should continue to search for more.","Completado","Amid the dim glow of Gurz-shâpol, you have discovered blooms of athelas bursting from the earth near the Orcs' filth and destruction. The healing plant has gone unnoticed by the untrained eyes of the Orcs, but through your dealings with the Rangers, you are well-acquainted with its appearance. You should gather as much as possible before returning to the Rohirrim for they will have great use of it in the coming days of the war.","Blooming in the darkness of Gurz-shâpol, patches of athelas grow unnoticed by the Orcs of the White Mountains.","In Death's Shadow"},
[6565]={"Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Ingbert regarding the battle at Maustazg.","'Alas for Ingmar's foolishness! He went against my commands and now lies dying in the infirmary. It is only to be hoped that the healers may ease his wounds and save his life.'\
\
His face becomes grim as he continues.\
\
'However, not all will be well even then. From what Ingmar managed to tell me and what you yourself report, there is indeed a traitor in our midst, and I am loath to pursue her.'","'You will ride to my son's aid? My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>","Talk to Ingbert","Ingbert stands near Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Góda, disgusted with you, suggested that if you wish to redeem yourself for your errors in judgement, you should speak with Ingbert.","Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Speak with Ingbert when you are ready to ride to Maustazg.","You have won victory at Maustazg","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'Despite your defiance of Théoden King's laws, our defences are set, but we may still lose everything!\
\
'My grandson has taken a force to Maustazg, intent on destroying the Orcs, against the commands of his King and of his father. If he lives, he will most certainly be branded a traitor and face exile or death. If he dies in battle, he will earn no glory.\
\
'I am through with you, ${PLAYER}. If you wish to redeem yourself, speak with Ingbert.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>","The preparations for the defence of Eaworth have been completed, but all is not well....\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>","Talk to Ingbert to ride to Ingmar's aid","In Defence of Eaworth","'It is as I feared, ${PLAYER}. My son could not bear the shame of waging a war from the walls of Eaworth. He took a force out this morning to lay siege to Maustazg.\
\
'I beg you, ${PLAYER}, go to him and lend him your arm... I would see my son return safely, though I fear it may not change his fate.\
\
'Let me know if you will do so, and I will lend you a steed.'"},
[6566]={"You have attained glory against the Orcs","'Ha! To battle then, and may the Orcs feel the wrath of the Mark!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Ingbert to accompany Ingmar to Maustazg","Preparations for the assault on Maustazg are now complete, which Ingmar has decided to lead himself, against his father's wishes.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>","Reeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Ingbert if you are ready to join Ingmar for the assault on Maustazg.","'Alas that I could not join in the fray. Perhaps if I had, my son would not lie abed in the infirmary.\
\
'Nevertheless, victory belongs to the house of Léotharn, and my son has earned the glory he so desired. His wounds will mend, and we will be the stronger for it!'\
\
Ingbert looks grim as he continues.\
\
'But all is not well. From what Ingmar reports and what you have told me, there is indeed a traitor in our midst with whom I am loath to pursue justice.'","Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Ingbert regarding the assault on Maustazg.","In Defence of Eaworth","'The preparations for the attack on Maustazg are now complete, but alas... Ingmar has defied my commands and has taken command of the assault. Go to him at once and see that he does not do anything rash.\
\
'I wish that I were joining you in this battle, but I cannot. My duty is first to my people, and I cannot leave them undefended, even to protect my son.\
\
'You have my thanks for the assistance you have provided thus far, ${PLAYER}. May you win glory as well!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance can only be completed Solo.</rgb>"},
[6567]={"'Mae govannen. ¿Laenin te hizo enfrentar a las moscas guadaña? Bien. Se ha vuelto necesario expulsarlas del bosque, no sea que maten los árboles.\
\
'Tu ayuda será bienvenida aquí, ${PLAYER}, pues hay mucho por hacer.'","'Nuestro tiempo en esta tierra se está acabando. Pronto no seremos mas que leyenda y memoria para los mortales que permanecerán en estas costas. Sin embargo, mientras aún estemos aquí, debemos hacer lo que podamos para asegurar que estas tierras sigan siendo seguras y hermosas.\
\
'La preservación de la tierra es la razón por la cual he venido al puerto de Celondim. Mis hermanos y yo hemos estado investigando acontecimientos recientes en un claro al norte. Estoy aquí para reclutar a quienes estén dispuestos a ir allí y ayudarnos a descubrir la causa de una infestación de moscas guadaña entre los árboles al oeste y suroeste del puerto.\
\
'Si estás dispuesto, elimina la amenaza de las moscas guadaña de los árboles y reporta a Ovorlas en Nen Hilith hacia el suroeste.'","Derrota moscas del valle alrededor de Celondim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En Defensa del Bosque","Las moscas guadaña pueden encontrarse en los bosques al oeste y suroeste de Celondim.\
\
Laenin, el Guardián del Claro, te informó que está reclutando a quienes deseen ayudar a salvar la naturaleza circundante de una infestación de moscas guadaña.","Ovorlas está en el campamento élfico en Nen Hilith, al suroeste de Celondim.\
\
Has derrotado muchas moscas guadaña, como pidió Laenin, y ahora deberías buscar a Ovorlas.","Laenin, el Guardián del Claro, planea dejar la Tierra Media, pero desea ver preservada la santidad y la belleza de los bosques que rodean Celondim. Acontecimientos recientes han llevado a un gran número de insectos viles a internarse en el bosque, y Laenin teme que los árboles puedan enfermar como resultado.","'Encontrarás a Ovorlas hacia el suroeste, en el área que llamamos Nen Hilith. Habla con él y ayúdalo en lo que puedas, después de haber eliminado la amenaza que las moscas guadaña representan para el bosque circundante.'","Moscas del valle derrotadas alrededor de Celondim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Ovorlas en Nen Hilith"},
[6568]={"Defend the north-west entrance leading to Calembel","Candúr can be found patrolling the village of Ethring.\
\
You should speak with Candúr.","Defend the west entrance leading to Eilendoth","Ethring west entrance","Defend the south entrance leading to Dor-en-Ernil","You have defended the north-east entrance of Ethring","Ethring north-east entrance","Arvaethor has asked you to accompany him back to Ethring and help strengthen their defences.","Speak with Candúr","'Quickly, Orcs have been spotted around Ethring! We must protect the village. To arms!'","Ethring north-west entrance","You have defended the north-west entrance of Ethring","'I wonder how long these Orcs have been waiting in the mountains so that they may once again prey upon the hard-working folk of the Vale.\
\
'Come, let us return to Ethring. This news of the Orc camp is worrying. We must help strengthen Ethring's defences before returning to the Orkish threat in the woods.'","'I am Laerind, wife of Arvaethor. My husband has returned and I am glad that he is safe. I thank you for aiding him.\
\
'Arvaethor should not worry of Ethring. In Borhador's reclusiveness, I have taken it upon myself to organize the village defences with what little resources we have. I have men upon the beacon of Eilendoth, on look-out for attacking Orcs. Our woodworkers have been tasked with making barricades and placing them at the town's four entrances.'","Ethring south entrance","In Ethring's Defence","'Not just Orcs in these mountains but cave trolls as well! I fear the worst is yet to come. Let us bring the fight to the Orcs instead of waiting here for them to attack Ethring.'","Speak with Arvaethor","Defend the four entrances of Ethring.","Speak with Arvaethor.","Defend the north-east entrance near the lumber mill","You have defended the south entrance of Ethring","Speak with Laerind","The entrances of Ethring need defending!","Laerind can be found in the village of Ethring.\
\
You should speak with Laerind.","You have defended the west entrance of Ethring","You hear a call to arms from Candúr"},
[6569]={"Garnyd te saluda.\
\
'Has obrado bien, ${PLAYER}. Tus hazañas han inspirado a los guerreros en el campo de batalla y seguirán inspirando a hombres, mujeres y niños durante muchos años.\
\
'Has demostrado tu valía, y me atrevo a decir que es mayor incluso que la del mithril que antaño hizo famosa a Moria.'","Garnyd se encuentra en Anazârmekhem, al norte de Fil-gashan.\
\
Deberías regresar con Garnyd para informarle de tu victoria.","Orcos derrotados en Fil-gashan","Fil-gashan se halla en los confines suroccidentales de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Garnyd te ha indicado que uses el cuerno de guerra de Nanlug para desafiar a los orcos en Fil-gashan.","En el corazón del peligro (opcional)","Desafía a los orcos dentro de Fil-gashan, cerca de su estandarte de batalla","El sonido del cuerno de guerra de Nanulg sería una afrenta tal para los orcos de Fil-gashan que no se atreverían a ignorar su llamada.","Habla con Garnyd en Anazârmekhem","'¿Está hecho, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Recuerda que, en esta lucha, tu cometido como capitán es inspirar a tus compañeros para que continúen la batalla.'","'Para tu última tarea, ${PLAYER}, llevarás este cuerno de guerra hasta Fil-gashan y buscarás el estandarte de batalla de los orcos que se encuentra allí. Cuando lo encuentres, haz uso de él y derrota a los orcos que acudan a tu llamada… y acudirán, sin duda. No hay forma de que ignoren el insulto de que se use el cuerno de guerra de su antiguo líder para desafiarlos.\
\
'Comienza tu búsqueda en un lugar donde se reúnan muchos orcos. Es probable que su estandarte de batalla se encuentre allí, y más probable aún que los orcos respondan a la llamada del cuerno de guerra de su líder caído.\
\
'Recuerda que, en esta lucha, tu cometido como capitán es inspirar a tus compañeros para que continúen combatiendo.\
\
'Cuando hayas ganado la batalla, regresa conmigo.'"},
[6570]={"'¡Por Nykr! ¡En recuerdo a Nykr, el portador del medallón!'","'No le conocías desde hacía tanto tiempo como nosotros, pero has probado que tu amistad con Nykr es férrea, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'¡Será a través de acciones nobles de gente como tú, dispuesta a luchar por el futuro y respetar las tradiciones del pasado, que se cantarán de nuevo canciones sobre la gloria de Khazad-dûm por todo el mundo!'","'Ah, recuerdo bien a Nykr. Se le echará de menos. Cuando éramos niños, recuerdo que una vez escondió una gema que había extraído yo mismo con mi pequeño pico, que valoraba más que el todas mis otras posesiones, hasta que me disculpé con otro niño al que había insultado. Me llevó años perdonarle del todo...'","'La muerte de Nykr será llorada durante mucho tiempo, y la historia de su vida será cantada hasta que yo también muera, o así me corten la barba.'","'¡Oh, que día más aciago! Estoy conmovido... ¡escribiré una oda épica a la memoria del Portador del Medallón!'","Kúli quiere que la muerte de Nykr sea anunciada y celebrada a la verdadera manera de los enanos.","'Me apena escuchar esta noticia, ${PLAYER}. ¡Qué trágica noticia para difundir!'","En su memoria","Deberías visitar, sin un orden particular: el Refugio Sombrío, Jazârgund, el Descenso Profundo, Anazârmekhem, el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, la Cámara de la Encrucijada, la Guardia Orca, la Sala Vigesimoprimera, el Umbral de Durin y la Bodega Putrefacta.\
\
Kúlli quiere que hablas con los amigos de Nykr el Portador del Medallón en cada uno de los puestos avanzados enanos de Moria, para llevarles la noticia de su muerte y brindar en su memoria con cada uno de ellos.","'${PLAYER}, la muerte de Nykr ha causado una gran pena. Solo se me ocurre una manera de celebrar apropiadamente su vida y muerte, de acuerdo a nuestras más antiguas y venerables tradiciones enanas.\
\
'Nykr tenía muchos amigos entre los miembros de la expedición, que están repartidos desde la Puerta de Acebeda hasta las ruinas del Puente de Khazad-dûm. ¿Honrarás la memoria de Nykr con ellos, compartiendo una buena jarra de cerveza con cada uno de ellos donde se encuentren en los diez principales campamentos de mi gente en las ruinas?'","Habla con Kúli en el Agujero Chirriante","Kúli se encuentral al norte del Agujero Chirriante, en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Tras localizar a todos los amigos de Nykr el Portador de Medallón por todo Moria, deberías volver a ver a Kúli, su pariente.","'Nykr murió como vivió, valiente y fiel a Finna. ¡Ojalá todos encontremos la felicidad que ellos tenían en nuestra vida!'","'¿Qué? ¿Nykr, muerto? Esta noticia me pesa en el corazón. Parece que cada día recibimos malas noticias... ¡me hace desear nunca haber oído el nombre de Khazad-dûm!'","'¡Pobre Finna! Compadezco al mensajero que le haga llegar esta noticia. Supongo que no te dirigirás a la Montaña Solitaria, ¿no? No, eso hubiera demasiado fácil, supongo. Ah, bien. ¡Por Nykr! ¡Brindemos a su memoria!'","'Coincidí con él varias veces. Un buen artesano, y podía ganarnos bebiendo a cualquiera de nosotros.'","'¿Nykr está muerto? ¡Qué desgracia! Es una noticia ralmente triste. ¡Nunca podremos disfrutar de nuevo juntos la buena cerveza de mi hijo!'","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! ¡Brindemos en recuerdo a mi amigo caído!'","Has celebrado la vida y muerte de Nykr el Portador del Medallón con sus amigos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Bebe en memoria de Nykr con sus amigos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6571]={"Brinda en memoria de Kafli en Anazârmekhem","Encuentra la jarra que hay en la Cámara de la Encrucijada y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","Habla con Kúli, que acampa cerca de la colmena de gredbyg","'${PLAYER}, la muerte de Kafli es motivo de gran dolor. Solo se me ocurre una forma de celebrar como es debido su vida y su muerte, de acuerdo con nuestras tradiciones enanas más antiguas y venerables.\
\
'Kafli era amigo de muchos de los que participan en esta expedición, y que se encuentran desde la Puerta de Acebeda hasta las ruinas del Puente de Khazad-dûm. ¿Honrarás la memoria de Kafli junto a ellos, empinando una buena cerveza en los principales campamentos de mi pueblo que están a lo largo de las Minas?'","Encuentra la jarra que hay en el Refugio Sombrío y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","Kúli se encuentra al norte de la colmena de gredbyg, en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Tras haber empinado el codo con los amigos de Kafli por todo Moria, deberías volver con Kúli, su pariente.","'Kafli murió tal y como vivió, valiente y fiel a la encantadora Finna. ¡Ojalá todos podamos encontrar en nuestras vidas la felicidad que ellos tuvieron!'","'La muerte de Kafli será lamentada por mucho tiempo, y la historia de su vida se cantará hasta que yo también muera, o que me corten la barba.'","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en el Refugio Sombrío","En su memoria","'¡Ay, qué día tan triste! Estoy conmovido... ¡Escribiré una oda épica en memoria de Kafli!'","'¡Pobre Finna! Compadezco al mensajero que le dé la noticia. Supongo que no irás a la Montaña Solitaria, ¿no? No, eso habría sido demasiado fácil, supongo. En fin. ¡Por Kafli! ¡Levantemos una jarra en su nombre!'","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en la Bodega Putrefacta","Encuentra la jarra que hay en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","Encuentra la jarra que hay en la Bodega Putrefacta y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","'No lo conocías tanto como nosotros, pero has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} incondicional de Kafli.\
\
'¡Será gracias a las nobles acciones de personas como tú, dispuestas tanto a luchar por el futuro como a respetar las tradiciones del pasado, que la gloria de Khazad-dûm volverá a cantarse por todo el mundo!'","Encuentra la jarra que hay en el Descenso Profundo y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","Encuentra la jarra que hay en la Sala Vigesimoprimera y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","Kúli quiere que la muerte de Kafli se dé a conocer y se celebre a la auténtica manera enana.","'Ah, recuerdo bien a Kafli. Lo echaremos de menos... Cuando éramos unos enanitos, recuerdo que una vez me escondió una gema que yo mismo había extraído con mi pequeño pico, y que valoraba más que todas mis posesiones, hasta que me disculpé con otro niño al que había ofendido. Me llevó años perdonarlo por completo...'","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! ¡Brindemos por mi primo caído!'","Encuentra la jarra que hay en Anazârmekhem y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria.","'¡Saludemos todos a Kafli! ¡En memoria del enano más valiente que he conocido!'","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en el campamento de Kúli","'Me lo crucé varias veces. Era un buen artesano... y podía beberse una jarra de cerveza mejor que cualquiera de nosotros.'","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en el Descenso Profundo","Brinda en memoria de Kafli en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Encuentra la jarra que hay en el campamento de Kúli y bebe de ella.\
\
Kúli quiere que hables con los amigos de Kafli en cada uno de los puestos avanzados que hay por todo Moria, para informarles de su muerte y brindar con ellos en su memoria."},
[6572]={"Tuilinn te ha invitado a meditar solemnemente en Cerin Amroth.","Te encuentras en el lugar donde Elessar y Undómiel se juraron fidelidad","En honor del amor pospuesto","El lugar del que habló Tuilinn se encuentra en el lado sur de Cerin Amroth.\
\
Tuilinn quiere que vayas al punto de la colina de Cerin Amroth donde Aragorn y Arwen se juraron fidelidad y <rgb=#FF0000>medites</rgb> en honor de su amor, tal como ella hace.","<rgb=#FF0000>Medita</rgb> en Cerin Amroth","'Ahora que conoces la hermosa historia de Elessar y su amada Undómiel, quizá comprendas la solemnidad de su unión y de su separación. \
\
El tiempo más feliz que compartieron fue la estación que pasaron en Lórien, especialmente aquí, en Cerin Amroth. Es costumbre entre muchos de nosotros que los hemos conocido pasar tiempo en la colina bajo la luz del sol, reflexionando sobre los sacrificios que han hecho el uno por el otro. Es una buena forma de poner los problemas propios en perspectiva, entre otras cosas.\
\
¿Te gustaría hacerlo también? Debe ser durante el día: como dijo Aragorn cuando pronunciaron sus promesas, ni la Sombra, que siempre rechaza, ni el Crepúsculo son para él, por ser mortal. Ve al lado sur de la colina y <rgb=#FF0000>medita</rgb> sobre estas cuestiones durante un tiempo.'","'Tienes el aspecto sereno de quien ha meditado, ${PLAYER}: solemne y tranquilo.'","Habla con Tuilinn en Cerin Amroth","'Deberías sentarte en la vertiente sur de Cerin Amroth y meditar sobre la historia de Arwen y Elessar.'","Tuilinn se encuentra en lo alto del flet en Cerin Amroth.\
\
Deberías decirle a Tuilinn que has hecho lo que te indicó."},
[6573]={"'Podría haber salido mejor, pero sin duda también podría haber salido peor.'","Habla con Eluna","Eluna ha concertado una reunión con los Draig-lûth.\
\
Deberías hablar con ella cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}.","Eluna desea que actúes como su escolta para una reunión crucial.","'Logré concertar una reunión con uno de los Draig-lûth. Con suerte podremos resolver esto sin más violencia, pero si las cosas toman un giro desafortunado, tu brazo armado será más que bienvenido.'","'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}, deberíamos partir ahora.'","Has regresado a Lhan Garan con Eluna y los demás.\
\
Habla con Eluna","Con Esperanza de Paz"},
[6574]={"'¿No me has traído nada?'","'¿Cómo está el dolor de Núrelleth? ¿La has visitado hoy?'","En Memoria de los Perdidos","'Núrelleth puede que no desee usar la flecha contra los Orcos, pero yo vengaré a Faengris.'","'Mi esposo fue asesinado por los Orcos de Moria, pero nunca me dejará realmente.'","Lleva la flecha de la venganza a Núrelleth","'Faengris siempre fue rápido para reír. Incluso ahora, puedo ver sus ojos brillantes.'","'Vengo aquí todos los días... para mirar a lo lejos y pensar en Faengris.'","'¿Tienes un momento, ${PLAYER}? Soy un fabricante de flechas, y es mi deber elaborar flechas para los carcajes de los Galadhrim. He hecho esto durante muchos años, y mis flechas han sido la perdición de muchos Orcos. Pero recientemente terminé una flecha diferente a todas las demás.\
\
'Mi amigo Faengris, con quien aprendí el arte de fabricar arcos y flechas, fue asesinado recientemente por una compañía de Orcos que descendió de las Montañas Nubladas. Cuando el dolor agudo del duelo disminuyó un poco, me puse a fabricar una flecha con tal poder que podría matar a una línea de Orcos con un solo disparo si se lanzaba desde un arco de calidad.\
\
'Esta flecha en memoria de Faengris puede ser un pequeño consuelo para su viuda, Núrelleth. Llévasela para que vea que los Orcos pagarán por su muerte. A menudo se la puede encontrar en Telain Glorelloth, donde los flets se extienden sobre la cerca que rodea Caras Galadhon.'","Cúbenn ha fabricado una flecha en memoria del esposo de Núrelleth, Faengris, asesinado por los Orcos.","'Hay poco que pueda hacer para aliviar la tristeza de Núrelleth, o la mía, pero espero que el conocimiento de que esta flecha que he fabricado matará a muchos Orcos le brinde algo de consuelo. Búscala en Telain Glorelloth, donde los flets se extienden sobre la cerca que rodea Caras Galadhon.'","Núrelleth te mira en silencio por un momento antes de tomar la flecha de tus manos y examinarla con tristeza.\
\
'Es muy amable de parte de Cúbenn haber trabajado tanto en esta flecha en memoria de mi esposo, ${PLAYER}. Su amistad era muy importante para Faengris, y hablaba a menudo de la habilidad de Cúbenn en la fabricación de arcos y flechas. Faengris...'\
\
Sus dedos recorren el patrón en la flecha, y ya no parece consciente de tu presencia. Después de un momento, Núrelleth vuelve a levantar la vista.\
\
'Esta es una flecha realmente fina, ${PLAYER}, pero Faengris no querría que se desperdiciara en los Orcos.'","'¿Estuvo Núrelleth complacida con la flecha que hice en memoria de Faengris?'","Núrelleth se encuentra en Telain Glorelloth, donde los flets se extienden sobre la cerca que rodea Caras Galadhon.\
\
Cúbenn te ha dado la flecha que fabricó en memoria del esposo asesinado de Núrelleth, Faengris."},
[6575]={"'Oh! I will get it next time! Watch this, my boys!'","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! My brother and I have been teaching the folk here where to shoot at a Mûmak in order to bring it down. This crafted fellow is not as large as one of the actual beasts, but it still serves as good practice for letting fly our arrows.\
\
'If you retrieve the arrows I have already fired and give them to my brother, he will be able to practice. He has been asking for his turn for awhile now.'","Collected Blackroot swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect Blackroot bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected Blackroot bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale went to the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith to reprimand his sons.","Retrieve arrows from the makeshift Mûmak","Talk to Duinhir atop the wall in the Second Circle","Duinhir stares at the makeshift Mûmak, seeming to see it for the first time","In Need of Discipline","'Find our father in the city for us, ${PLAYER}. And perhaps you could plead on our behalf for leniency? He will be stern, I do not doubt it, but perhaps you can convince him that we need not be reprimanded for this adventure of ours? It ended happily, did it not?'","Derufin is inside the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of the city.","Collect Blackroot swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Lord Duinhir once again, in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern","'Give him a moment, ${PLAYER}. I have a feeling about this, and I am rarely wrong about such things!'","Duilin and Derufin have been firing arrows at the makeshift Mûmak in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern, in the Second Circle of the city.\
\
Duilin has asked you to recover the arrows he has already fired at the Mûmak, and give them to Derufin for his turn.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Have you seen our father around the city anywhere? I ask only because we have not yet seen him since we returned, and I am afraid he might be rather cross with us.\
\
'You see, he commanded us not to leave the city... but we left anyway. You understand, I am sure. There were Mûmakil to hunt! And furthermore, we learned how best to bring down the mighty beasts. That must be worth something, even to our stern and disapproving father!\
\
'Find him in the city for us, ${PLAYER}. He will be atop the wall somewhere in the Second Circle, probably with a view of the gate to the city. And perhaps you could plead on our behalf for leniency? He will be stern, I do not doubt it, but perhaps you can convince him that we need not be reprimanded for this adventure of ours? It ended happily, did it not?'","Lord Duinhir stares at the sight of the arrows flying toward the makeshift Mûmak, and is silent for a moment. Suddenly he erupts once again, but with quite a different exclamation.\
\
'Ha! A palpable hit, Derufin! That is the way!\
\
'Why did you not tell me about this, ${PLAYER}? This exercise seems to me quite a useful one. Can I have a try, my son? I will show you how this is done, I warrant! You will see your sire get it on his first try, Duilin!\
\
'I cannot stay mad at my boys. They get their skill at archery from me, you know!'","'Give those arrows to my brother and he will be able to practice these shots. He has been asking for his turn for awhile now.'","Collect Blackroot shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have arrived to find Lord Duinhir mid-shout.\
\
'...and as my sons, you are responsible for upholding my good name! If you do not do as I command, folk will look at your example and say, \\qDuinhir cannot even control his own sons! What sort of a man is that?\\q And furthermore... furthermore!'\
\
Duinhir splutters into silence.","Duilin is in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith.","Talk to Duilin in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern","Bring the Blackroot equipment to Lord Duinhir in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern","Duilin and Derufin left Minas Tirith without their father's permission, and now that they have returned they want to make amends.","Duinhir is somewhere within the city of Minas Tirith.\
\
Derufin asked you to find his father Duinhir and put in a good word for he and his brother's forbidden adventure in Ithilien.","Bring the Blackroot arrows to Derufin inside the Mûmak and Keep Tavern","'I know you, ${PLAYER}. You are the ${RACE} that brought my boys back to the city. You have my thanks for that. I will have some words for them when I catch them, I don't mind telling you! I am the Lord of the Blackroot Vale, and within those boundaries my command is the law. Outside of them, I am given authority over others by the grant of the Council and the Steward. But in affairs of my own house, and over the actions of my sons, I have complete authority no matter where I am!'\
\
Duinhir thunders his displeasure, and some of the men nearby shrink away involuntarily.\
\
'I commanded them to stay within the city for their own safety. What would I tell their mother if they ran afoul of some evil in Ithilien? Rosfin would never let me hear the end of it! Tell me where they are, ${PLAYER}, and I will teach them obedience!'\
\
You tell him that they learned something valuable about fighting Mûmakil, and that he can find them in the tavern in Minas Tirith named for the beasts.\
\
'I know the place. If you help my men finish gathering up these bows, swords, and shields, I will meet you there. My sons must learn to obey my words, or they will be no sons of mine!'","Collected Blackroot shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lord Duinhir asked you to help his men gather up the equipment he had been inspecting.","'Do you see, ${PLAYER}? There is nothing to worry about after all! He has never been able to stay mad at Derufin or me for very long. Our mother thinks we remind him of himself when he was young. Or perhaps old! He insists he has not changed, after all.\
\
'Thank you once again, my friend! We will be here, practicing our technique! If the battle comes, we will be ready!'"},
[6576]={"Gathered jackal pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather jackal pelts for Munsubur from the nearby jackal dens of Urgudag or Khazâda.","Return to Munsubur with the pelts","'Adventurer, might I trouble you for your help?\
\
'I must gather pelts for the people in need here in Urash Dâr. Many are fleeing from these Orcs pouring from the demon-pits. I have given them what I could, but it has not been enough. I am in need of more pelts from the jackals, but it is now a task too dangerous for a trader such as myself to accomplish alone.\
\
'I ask of you to bring me any pelts you manage to gather. The jackals can be found to the west, in Urgudag, and to the east, in Khazâda.'","Bring the jackal pelts back to Munsubur in Ub Nishir near Maurûsh.","Munsubur has asked you to help him to gather pelts from jackals in Urash Dâr.","Gather jackal pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","In Need of Pelts","'You have returned and with the pelts in hand!'\
\
You give Munsubur the jackal pelts.\
\
'I can not thank you enough, adventurer. These pelts will help many during the cold nights as long as get them to those in need. The other traders here are unhappy with me for not making any coin with these pelts.'"},
[6577]={"¡Dokhára derrotado!","Rescata a los prisioneros (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Prisioneros rescatados (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","En necesidad de rescate","Liberen a los prisioneros detenidos en Eshadûr y sáquenlos de Dokhára, el torturador ordâkhai.","Has rescatado a los prisioneros detenidos en Eshadûr. Ahora debes enfrentarte a Dokhára, el torturador ordâkhai.","Derrota a Dokhára en el camino hacia la Entrada","'¡Me alegra que hayas podido ayudar a Mushendu! Me han enviado para llevarte de regreso a Urmâkh, hay otros asuntos allí que requieren tu atención.'","Dokhára, el torturador ordâkhai, retiene a varias personas de Ambarûl prisioneras en Eshadûr."},
[6578]={"Quickbeam can be found in Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest.\
\
You have delivered the lost Huorns to safety at Quickbeam's side in Derndingle. You should speak to Quickbeam.","Young Huorns have become lost in Fangorn Forest and must be tended by Quickbeam if they are to survive.","Bring the lost Huorns to Derndingle","Derndingle can be found in south-eastern Fangorn Forest.\
\
You have gathered as many young Huorns as you could find, and should now return to Derndingle.","Find lost Huorns in Fangorn Forest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hoom. You have done well to bring these young ones to me, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'I shall look after them, for such a role is not new to me... hum, or any Ent for that matter.\
\
'Thank you, little one.'","Talk to Quickbeam","Found lost Huorns in Fangorn Forest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","In Need of Tending","Lost Huorns can be found throughout southern Fangorn Forest.\
\
Quickbeam's Huorn wants you to help search for young Huorns in Fangorn Forest.","You have encountered a young Huorn, and your companion swiftly shuffles to its side, as if to defend it. You cannot quite tell, but Quickbeam's Huorn appears upset that it has been left to fend for itself in this empty, dangerous forest.\
\
You should continue your search for other lost Huorns and then bring them to safety in Derndingle.","DNT -- Players will not see"},
[6579]={"A crevasse can be found on the south-western side of the Orc-roadway through the Balewood.\
\
Strongroot wants you to search for more evidence of Núrzum's assault in the Balewood, so the Ents may better understand the foe they face.","Núrzum's destruction can be found off the sides of the Orc-roadway through northern Balewood.\
\
Strongroot wants you to search for more evidence of Núrzum's assault in the Balewood so that the Ents may better understand the foe they face.","'Hoom. Perhaps there is more to this monster than we thought....\
\
'Such strength is uncommon, even for a giant of stone. And that foul roots sprang from the earth amid his havoc... this is odd, indeed. Hom. Odd and gravely unsettling....\
\
'${PLAYER}, we must speak of what is to be done to learn more of this monster lest any hasty action be taken....'","'Barallas is a wise Ent, and he is my elder. However, many are elders to us, for us young Ents are all that remain here. My bark looks old and weathered, you say? Old, my small friend... may still be young to us.\
\
'The monster, Núrzum, has been a cause of great destruction to my friends in this forest. The cries of the trees as he pulled them from the earth is not something I long to hear again. His assault on this forest was swift and brutal, and many of his damages remain still.\
\
'Along the side of that twisted path through the forest that the Orcs defile with their crude machinery, you will find his handiwork smashed into the earth.\
\
'If you search for signs of his destruction, I would ask that you examine them... for strange things have been cropping up in this forest as of late, and none of them good.'","Examine the nearby crevasse in the Balewood","The Orc-roadway can be found to the south and west of Strongroot in northern Balewood.\
\
Strongroot has sent you to explore further down the Orc-roadway in hopes of finding evidence of Núrzum's destruction, so that he and the Ents might better understand their foe.","You have encountered a shard of ice upon which Núrzum has impaled several wood-trolls","Talk to Strongroot","Strongroot wants you to explore around the Orc-roadway and discover evidence of Núrzum's corruption of the Balewood.","Search for a boulder thrown by Núrzum","You have discovered a jagged crack in the Balewood's earth, surely caused by Núrzum's stomping","Search for more signs of Núrzum's destruction in the Balewood","You have found an icy boulder that has impacted the ground deeply... such strength goes beyond even that of a giant","Strongroot can be found in northern Balewood.\
\
You have discovered much of Núrzum's destruction and should now return to Strongroot to discuss what you have found.","In Núrzum's Wake"},
[6580]={"Flík está en el campamento de los trasgos donde lo encontraste.\
\
Deberías llevar a Flík a un lugar seguro.","En problemas","'Odio este sitio... ¡Llévame de vuelta al Descenso Profundo!'","Has encontrado a un enano de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata retenido como prisionero en un campamento de trasgos.","'¿Así que encontraste a Flík? ¿Y estaba bien? ¿No estaba muy malherido? Es una noticia muy tranquilizadora.\
\
'¡Gracias! Te estoy en deuda. Tanto el hijo del capitán como mi barba están a salvo, al menos por otra noche.'","Styrr se encuentra en el campamento de Descenso Profundo.\
\
Deberías volver inmediatamente con Styrr e informarle de que han encontrado y rescatado a Flík.","'¡Date prisa y sácame de aquí! Ojalá nunca hubiera querido venir aquí. Lo único que quería era que mi padre se sintiera orgulloso de mí, ¡y ahora estoy a punto de acabar en un guiso de trasgos! ¡Deja de perder el tiempo y vámonos!'","Informa a Styrr de que Flík ha sido rescatado","Dile a Flík que ya estáis listos para salir","Flík está a salvo"},
[6581]={"Esta hacha es de fabricación enana y parece haber sido abandonada recientemente. Quizá uno de los expedicionarios enanos haya tenido problemas en el camino.\
\
Deberías buscar por los alrededores al dueño de esta hacha.","Túbi Puñogrueso se encuentra en lo alto de las escaleras del Umbral de Durin.\
\
Kambi te habló de los desvaríos del jefe trasgo acerca de su tribu y la voz que teme. Te pidió que informaras a Túbi Puñogrueso lo antes posible.","En persecución","'He sido un viejo tonto por precipitarme aquí sin ayuda, pero pensaba que ese trasgo loco estaba solo. No sabía que fuera tan hábil en combate.\
\
'Desde entonces ha estado balbuceando locuras sobre una tribu que acecha en la oscuridad, cerca de aquí, liderada por una misteriosa voz surgida de las sombras. Es algo que teme profundamente.\
\
'No te preocupes por mí... esta pierna no está tan mal como parece. Ve y haz saber a Túbi lo de los trasgos y la voz. Eso es mucho más preocupante que este rasguño en la pierna.'","Habla con Túbi Puñogrueso","El dueño del hacha probablemente se encuentre en algún punto de los túneles cercanos al Umbral de Durin, hacia el oeste de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Deberías buscar al propietario del hacha.","'Date prisa. Haz saber a Túbi lo de la tribu de trasgos y esa voz misteriosa. No van a desaparecer sin más ni a dejarnos en paz.'","'Lo que dice Kambi es preocupante. Una tribu de trasgos tan cerca de la entrada me inquieta. No podemos recuperar Moria con seguridad con una amenaza tan inminente.\
\
'También tengo curiosidad por la naturaleza de esa voz. Debemos hacer todo lo posible por localizar su campamento, pues aunque Moria alberga muchas cosas que no duermen y se deslizan en la oscuridad, los trasgos no son una de ellas.'","Encuentra al dueño del hacha abandonada","Has encontrado un hacha enana abandonada en el camino y ahora estás buscando al enano que la empuñaba."},
[6582]={"Return to Uda at her camp and let her know you have reduced the number of Orcs in the area.","Defeat Orcs in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Uda at her camp near Utug-bûr","Defeated Orcs in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Uda has asked you to slay Orcs in Urash Dâr to help her thin their numbers.","In Pursuit of Orcs","Uda is unhappy with the number of Orcs in the area and has asked that you help her to reduce it.","'Adventurer, you seem worthy enough to join our efforts.\
\
'The opening of the demon-pits nearby has unleashed hordes of Orcs into these lands, and we mean to push them back. I ask of you to help thin their numbers.\
\
'They can be found throughout the area of Urash Dâr, though you may find a concentration of them in the camps to the north and east of here.'","'You have returned. I trust that means you have completed your task?\
\
'Thank you, my friend. These lands are still dangerous, but I am glad to see people such as yourself helping our cause.\
\
'I ask of you to continue to reduce their numbers, should you encounter any more.'"},
[6583]={"In Search of Quellwort","Collect daewath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The three plants can be found in central Clovengap.\
\
Golodhrim has asked you to collect samples of three plants.","Collected daewath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Clovengap plants with special properties are written of in ancient tales.","'You come bearing plants? Lovely! Let us see what we have.'","Collected fingloth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect elialas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Golodhril","Collect fingloth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected elialas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should bring the flowers you collected to Golodhril.","'You have my gratitude for your assistance with the fountains. I wonder if I might ask you for further help. I have read about three rare plants that grew here in Clovengap. One of them is said to cure stomach ailments, and I believe it could be useful for our eventual sailing trip to the West.'\
\
She lowers her voice, glancing to be sure her sister is not listening.\
\
'Sadorwen does not do so well with the rocking of boats, which is no doubt why she agreed to put off going for as long as we have. Sadly, my book is unclear on which plant has this property. The three plants are called daewath, fingloth, and elialas in Sindarin.'\
\
She shows you a page with the image of three flowers, with illegible writing next to them.\
\
'Gather some of each for me and bring them back here… ah, please.'"},
[6584]={"Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.\
\
You should speak with Thandor.","The eastern river-gate can be found on the east side of the city.\
\
You should investigate the river-gate.","Spoke with Thandor","In Search of Truth","Take the note","Took the note","DNT - Not Used","A stray note on the ground catches your attention","Speak with Thandor","Investigate the area near the river-gate","'I've heard rumours which are unsettling. It is believed that the Corsairs were let into the city by someone from within. I do not know who would have done this, though I've heard the name of every captain and noble thrown around, including myself.\
\
'I want this dealt with, ${PLAYER}. You and Thandor are the only two I can trust with this matter, so I would ask that you seek counsel with him.'","'It is most perplexing, ${PLAYER}. Despite the havoc they wrought, the Corsairs seemed able to take the city without much resistance.\
\
'My men were not able to find anything of note at the eastern river-gate, but I suspect that we may find something at one of the other gates. Certainly if the gates were opened, then it probably would have happened with more than just the one.\
\
'I would ask that you start with the eastern river-gate, and make sure to not overlook anything too small.'","The stray note can be found near the eastern river-gate of Pelargir.\
\
You should bring the note to Thandor.","Suspicious of recent events, Thandor has asked you to inspect the eastern river-gate for any clues about what caused Pelargir to fall.","Talk to Thandor","Thandor carefully reads the note.\
\
'These orders bear the seal of Sirgon? This cannot be. It would mean that the lordship itself is responsible for the fall of the city! I know Faltharan too well to think that he would have a hand in this, but I'm almost too afraid to ask.\
\
'Those men who tried to attack you are part of a larger group. They've made the east-garth their own personal haven. Why they would want these orders has me concerned.'"},
[6586]={"'I was in the grove and someone shot me with an arrow! I did not think anyone else was here. Of the living, anyway. Thankfully the arrow hit nothing vital and I can dress the wound myself.\
\
'I expect you are the capable sort, else you would not have come to these woods. Please, if you desire to help me, seek out who did this. Tread carefully friend, as those who say these woods are haunted speak true. I neither saw nor heard anything before I was struck, so be vigilant.'","In Search of the Culprit","'Tell me, who treads upon this sacred grove of my people?'\
\
The Elf has an ethereal quality about him and you find him unsettling, though you cannot determine exactly why. He is not like any other Elf you have met.","Look for the person responsible","Agalûnu was stuck by an arrow, shot by an unseen foe in Arwáth.","Agalûnu has asked you to help her by finding who is responsible for wounding her. You should explore Arwáth in northern Ambarûl and seek out the culprit.","Talk to the strange Elf","'I was in the grove and someone shot me with an arrow! Please, seek out who did this.'","You spot a strange Elf","While searching Arwáth for who might have struck Agalûnu with an arrow, you spotted a strange Elf.  You should talk to him."},
[6587]={"Search Sirthanc for the source of the moans","Haradrim have overrun the road leading up to the beacon!","Faltharan can be found at Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have spoken to Lord Sirgon and should now speak to Faltharan.","Faltharan can be found just inside the western entrance to Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.\
\
Arvellon has heard of Faltharan's arrival in Glaniath. You should now reunite with him and aid in his search.","Talk to Lord Sirgon","'Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I was beginning to worry that you had set off without me. The folk of Glaniath have told me the Haradrim passed by along the roads to the west and south, and did not halt their advance to attack. These folk have also spoken of hearing weakened cries of a man among their ranks... I hope my father yet lives, but I fear the tortures the Haradrim might inflict upon him if he is indeed their prisoner.\
\
'The roadway to the west passes to the north and leads up a great hill to one of the south-beacons of Lebennin. Let us follow it and see if we can discover where the Haradrim have gone!'","Haradrim guards can be found along the pathway leading to the beacon Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have discovered Haradrim near the base of the beacon-hill, and should defeat them.","Follow the road north towards the beacon Sirthanc","'My father needs the care of a healer, and Pelargir is no place for the wounded.\
\
'There is a fortified haven nestled in the mountains to the east known as Tumladen. It is a shelter to my people during times of war, and indeed, many of the folk of Lebennin and Lossarnach have already sought refuge within its walls.\
\
'It is there I must bring my father, and with haste.'","Sirthanc can be found to the north-west of Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.\
\
Faltharan has asked you to accompany him to the beacon Sirthanc where he believes his father may have been taken.","Talk to Faltharan","As the Haradrim slaver falls defeated, you can hear the laboured breaths of a man nearby...","Defeated Haradrim guarding the beacon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sirthanc can be found in north-western Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have defeated the leader of the Haradrim and should now search the beacon for Lord Sirgon.","Too weakened to support himself, Lord Sirgon falls to the ground","Faltharan can be found at your side or can be called with your horn while you are in Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have freed Lord Sirgon from his bonds and should speak to Faltharan about what is to be done next.","Free Lord Sirgon from his bonds","After reuniting with Faltharan, the time has come to seek Lord Sirgon in Upper Lebennin.","'I had begun to lose hope, my friend, but I fear our journey is not yet over. My father's condition is greatly concerning... he looks starved to the bone and his wounds risk infection!\
\
'I wish to look over his wounds, but I do not wish him to see the worry in my eyes. Speak to him, and draw his attention for a moment.'","Call forth and defeat the leader of the Haradrim","Sirgon gazes into the distance at the ruin of Pelargir, his eyes heavy and laden with tears. He musters a weak smile as you approach him.\
\
'I believed none yet lived to search for me... but you have proven me wrong, ${CLASS}. You have renewed the hope that the Men of Harad stole from me as they forced me to watch my city burn.\
\
'I may be but a lord of ruins, but my family lives yet and there is still a dawn waiting to pierce these skies.'","Talk to Faltharan at Sirthanc","You have discovered Lord Sirgon of Pelargir, bound and barely standing","The binding pole can be found on Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have discovered Lord Sirgon bound to a pole on Sirthanc, and should now free him.","'Ah! My friend, the lord regent has arrived in Glaniath. I heard a great commotion by the western road as he rode in, and he has made it known that he seeks his father who was lost in the conflict at Pelargir.\
\
'Our folk have heard many strange things of late, but I am not certain of his whereabouts. Perhaps he has already spoken to the others of such matters...\
\
'You have been a great help to me and my folk, ${PLAYER}. I hope your charge bears fruit, for the sake of all in Lebennin.'","Defeat Haradrim guarding the beacon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","In Search of the Lost Lord","Lord Sirgon can be found at Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.\
\
Faltharan has asked you to speak to his father while he examines the Lord's injuries.","A watch-horn can be found somewhere near the beacon Sirthanc.\
\
You have defeated many of the Haradrim and should now confront their leader.","Talk to Faltharan in Glaniath"},
[6588]={"Travel into Lhingris and join Legolas in his search for Ungwetári","In Search of the Spider-queen","Legolas has ventured into Lhingris after becoming suspicious that an old foe of his father, Thranduil, still dwells in the Ephel Dúath.","'I am glad you have come, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'Be this the work of Ungwetári herself or that of her terrible children, the spiders of Lhingris are born of some terrible evil.'","Legolas can be found somewhere near the road leading to Durthang in Lhingris.\
\
Legolas has asked you to join him in his search for an old foe known to his father as the spider-queen, Ungwetári.","'${PLAYER}, I have seen something terrible along the road to Durthang. A few spiders scuttled too near the ruins from Lhingris, and I was reminded at once of Mirkwood and the tales of my father, Thranduil!\
\
'In an Age now past, he battled against a terrible spider -- itself only a child of one even greater. The great spider-queen: Ungwetári!\
\
'It has been over three thousand years since my father heard her terrible name spoken by one of the Nazgûl, but I fear a creature so terrible and so near to the lands of the Enemy had strength enough to persist long beyond the years of Men!\
\
'I must go into Lhingris and seek the source of the evil within the Ephel Dúath! If you wish to join me, I shall wait for a time near the road to Durthang -- but do not tarry overlong!'","You have found Legolas amid a ruined encampment...","Talk to Legolas in the ruined encampment","Legolas is standing in the remains of small encampment beside the road to Durthang in Lhingris.\
\
You have found Legolas in a ruined Orkish encampment and should now speak to him."},
[6589]={"'You... you slew them, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Let us hope they remain dead this time, my... friend... at least for Gondor's sake... for I fear I do not have long.'","Fell spirit tormentors can be found inhabiting fell-trolls in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
You have discovered foul fell spirits inhabiting trolls in Tarlang's Crown and should defeat them before they can be used against Gondor.","A fell spirit leaps from the troll's remains","Fell trolls can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially along the main pathway.\
\
Gondren has asked you to defeat fell trolls and quell the fell spirits he believes is inhabiting their bodies.","Talk to Gondren","Inhabited by foul fell spirits, hulking fell trolls now lurk Tarlang's Crown and are among Azruthor's most powerful allies.","Defeat fell spirits inhabiting trolls in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","DNT -- will not be seen","In Service of the Heirs","Defeat a fell troll in Tarlang's Crown","Gondren can be found near the main encampment in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
You have quelled several fell spirits and trolls, severely weakening Azruthor's forces in Tarlang's Crown.","'The things I have seen here, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'When first the Corsairs began to set up their tents, they killed the trolls that came down from Tarlang's Peaks. All of them were to rot where they fell... when suddenly this wave of terror came over me. When I awoke, the trolls walked the Crown once more... but they were dead, I tell you! I know what I saw!\
\
'What manner of foul power could bring forth such a thing, ${PLAYER}? You must see them slain, I beg you!'","Defeated fell spirits inhabiting trolls in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6590]={"Talk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving","'${PLAYER}? You must be the wise ${RACE} I have heard so much about. I simply must thank you... I could not be more pleased with the results of the investigation.\
\
'To think that a coward would threaten my life with poisons rather than face me with their grievances in person... it sickens me. We must put these matters behind us, for further turmoil yet lies ahead for me and my people.\
\
'Receive this reward, and please consider helping us further.'","'You have been a tremendous help, both to me and to the people of Cliving. We all owe you a debt of gratitude for your fine service.\
\
'Reeve Athelward has sent word that he would personally like to thank you for your assistance in these matters. Go with haste! The Reeve's time is precious, and it is rare for him to pay heed to visitors of your stature.'","Reeve Athelward has heard of your endeavours to help Walnoth investigate the crimes in Cliving.","In Service to Reeve Athelward","Reeve Athelward resides at the Mead Hall at the north-east end of Cliving.\
\
Reeve Athelward has summoned you before him to discuss matters that concern him and his people."},
[6592]={"'You have become an asset to the Avanc-lûth and Lhan Rhos, ${RACE}. Thank you for all that you have done. Our work, however, is never done.\
\
'Living in a wet environment allows for many diseases among the people. We do our part to allay such illnesses, but it always seems like there are more and more every day.\
\
'I believe that some of this sickness is coming from Lhan Colvarn, the village of the Abominations, to the north. We have seen a rise in rats and the diseased swamp-gas. Please, do something to dispose of these, then speak with Anurin.'","Rats and clouds of swamp gas can be found to the north of Lhan Rhos.\
\
Elder Kedivor has asked you to reduce the number of diseased rats and clouds of swamp-gas.","In Sickness and in Plague","Anurin is at the northern lines of the Avanc-lûth.\
\
You should report to Anurin now that you have disposed of the rats and scattered the swamp-gas.","Defeated diseased rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Anurin in the Dunbog","Elder Kedivor is worried about the sickness and disease that are spreading from the camp in the north.","Scatter clouds of swamp-gas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scattered clouds of swamp-gas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Avanc-lûth are very grateful and just a bit healthier now. And this is good, for the Abominations are becoming more and more difficult, just as rumours of ill tidings from Isengard are on the rise.\
\
'I do not know if there is any connexion, but Saruman seems to have increased his studies in the Dunbog.'","'Please, rid us of as many rats as you can and disperse the swamp-gas. We need to cut down on disease as quickly as possible.\
\
'Go north, and you will not be able to miss them.'","Defeat diseased rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6593]={"Los enanos Sigrun y Greip fueron enviados al norte del campamento de Glóin en el nacimiento oeste del Bruinen para explorar Helegrod y se supone que han establecido un pequeño campamento en los árboles a la vista de la Escalera Amarga.\
\
Glóin te ha enviado a hablar con los exploradores que ha enviado para vigilar la Escalera Amarga que sube a las puertas de Helegrod, lejos al norte de su campamento en la Fuente occidental del Bruinen.","Completa Viejas Amistades","'Debes ser un mensajero del Señor Glóin, porque nadie en sus cabales subiría hasta tan cerca de Helegrod sin un motivo como ese. ¡Es cierto que el mal vive de nuevo aquí! ¡Greip y yo tenemos todas las pruebas que necesitamos para asegurarlo!\
\
'¿El Señor Glóin quiere que te cuente la historia de Durin, el quinto de su nombre? No puedo negarme, aunque es una historia dolorosa. Si te habló de la llegada de Thorog, entonces te diré lo que pasó cuando Durin supo que el dragón había tomado la ciudad.\
\
'¿Un dragón durmiendo sobre tesoros en Helegrod? ¡Durin no toleraría tal insulto! Se ciñó a la espalda a Mírdanant, un regalo de Eregion a sus antepasados, transmitido de padres a hijos a lo largo de los años, y marchó con una pequeña compañía de enanos a las puertas de Helegrod. Durin desafió a Thorog, ¡quien respondió! ¡La batalla comenzó! ¡Tan fiera fue la lucha entre el dragón y el enano que hasta las puertas de Helegrod se hicieron añicos!\
\
'Después de días y noches agotadores, Durin empezó a estar extenuado; todos los de su compañía yacían muertos o moribundos, salvo Bruni quien fue llamado Barbamarilla años después, cuyas heridas eran demasiado graves para que pudiera continuar. Todavía luchaba el poderoso Thorog, negando rendir los tesoros de Helegrod a sus legítimos dueños. Thorog preparó su aliento de llamas incandescentes con el que calcinar a Durin, a quien creía cercano a la muerte, pero se dio cuenta de su error demasiado tarde. ¡Demasiado tarde! ¡Y he aquí que Durin esgrimió a Mírdanant con todas las fuerzas que le quedaban, y terminó con el cruel reinado de Thorog!\
\
'Pero Durin no sobreviviría para ver la victoria, ya que la última llamarada de Thorog había resultado ser demasiado fuerte para el resistente escudo de Durin, y ese fue su fin. Mírdanant se perdió con Durin, todavía enterrada en el cuello del cadáver de Thorog.\
\
'¡Ay de los enanos! Los elfos de Eregion habían pronunciado palabras de protección al forjar el hacha: \\qLa oscuridad no caerá sobre Hadhodrond mientras la estirpe de Durin porte a Mírdanant en amistad con los Gwaith-i-Mírdain,\\q ¡pero esas palabras resultaron ser falsas, con la muerte de Durin!\
\
'Investigué mi linaje muy atrás hasta Bruni, quien era Barbamarilla, el único superviviente de la batalla de Helegrod. El no morir en la batalla como un héroe ante las puertas fue la vergüenza de toda su vida, y es una marca en todos sus descendientes. Yo también la porto, y me he impuesto el deber de hacer que la historia no sea olvidada: ni la tradición de los Gwaith-i-Mírdain, ni la crueldad de Thorog y por supuesto ninguna de las valerosas hazañas del quinto Durin en defensa de su pueblo.\
\
'El mal ha reptado de vuelta a Helegrod, ${PLAYER}, y necesitaremos la ayuda de mucha gente si queremos combatirlo. ¡Habla con Greip y conmigo para saber qué ha de hacerse!'","'Tras la derrota de Thorog, los enanos repararon las puertas y grabaron en ellas un registro de la batalla.'","Completa El Lamento del Cazador de sierpes","'Sigrun te contará el relato del quinto Durin, pues lo afecta de manera directa, aunque ocurriera hace tanto tiempo. Lo encontrarás a él y a su hermano Greip entre los árboles, a la vista de la Escalera Amarga, muy al norte, cerca de Helegrod.'","'La historia de Durin es triste, pues termina tanto en victoria como en derrota.'","Encuentra la entrada a Helegrod","La antigua fortaleza se alza ante ti. Será mejor buscar compañeros antes de aventurarte más adelante.","Helegrod está al noreste de Sigrun y el campamento de Greip.\
\
Es la hora de que veas esta antigua fortaleza con tus propios ojos.","Completa La Magnitud de la Amenaza","'Te encargo que busques a los exploradores que mandé hacia Helegrod. Escucha lo que hayan descubierto, ${PLAYER}, y sabremos mejor cómo enfrentarnos a la nueva amenaza que acecha en el interior de ese oscuro lugar.\
\
'Se habrán refugiado en algún lugar al norte, a la vista de la Escalera Amarga que sube a los muros de la fortaleza. Pide a Sigrun que te cuente el resto de la triste historia de Durin cuando le encuentres, pues a él le concierne más directamente y la relatará para ti si deseas oírla.\
\
'Ten cuidado en las laderas nevadas y busca los árboles a la vista de la Escalera Amarga para encontrar a Sigrun y a Greip, mis exploradores. Tienen autoridad para tratar cualquier asunto sobre Helegrod.'","Glóin te contó solo una pequeña parte de la historia de Helegrod y te pidió que hablases con los exploradores que envió para vigilar la Escalera Amarga en busca de signos de la amenaza creciente tras los muros de Helegrod.'","'Sigrun ha llevado durante largo tiempo la marca de la cobardía de Bruni Barbamarilla en Helegrod.'","Completa Enemigos Antiguos de Matarañas","'Los enanos intentaron recuperar Helegrod tras la muerte de Thorog, pero no estaba destinado a ser.'","'Hemos visto cosas malignas tras los muros de Helegrod. La ciudad está ocupada nuevamente, aunque no por enanos.\
\
'Sigrun te contará la historia de aquel lugar, y entonces deberemos decidir qué puede hacerse ante los nuevos males que acechan en Helegrod.'","Los enanos Sigrun y Greip deben consultar y enviar información a varios de sus amigos antes de aventurarse nuevamente en Helegrod.","A la Vista de la Escalera Amarga"},
[6594]={"'What brings you to Northcotton Farm, ${PLAYER}? Something's not quite right here, and I'm glad to have your help! This is the last place Gladiola Farmer was seen before her disappearance. We'll get to the bottom of it!'","In Their Absence, Chapter 1","Fenric Banks is in Oatbarton, the hobbit-town in the southern reaches of Evendim. It is one of the most northerly villages of the Shire.\
\
Barliman Butterbur has asked you to investigate the worries of the hobbit Fenric Banks, in Oatbarton.","Talk to Fenric Banks in Oatbarton","Shadows are lengthening throughout Eriador now that many of the Rangers have left for the south-lands, and trouble is brewing in their absence.","'Things have been a mite worrisome about my fire for the past few evenings, ${PLAYER}. Talk of the surrounding lands has been grim, with little good cheer to be had, even in the common room of the Pony! That's a sure sign of trouble, isn't it?\
\
'Why, just recently one of the good hobbits of Bree gave to me a letter he received from one of his relations out Shire way, and he talks of trouble as plain as the nose on your face, or on mine! Mysterious relics appearing out of the blue, promising crops suddenly failing, and good solid hobbits vanishing, with no reasons given!\
\
'I was never over-fond of Rangers, but they seem to be gone now. No one has seen that Strider for weeks, and few other grim-faced Men of his stripe have been seen since either. Is it possible the Rangers really did protect the peace of the countryside? In their absence, things seem to be getting worse, that's for certain.\
\
'If you're of a mind to, you should travel to the town of Oatbarton, in the southern reaches of Evendim but within the Shire-bounds, to speak to Fenric Banks. His cousin Henric, who showed me his letter, is worried and wants to make sure that everything is all right. You are just the ${RACE} to see it done, that is clear to me!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This Quest Arc begins with 3-Man Small Fellowship content, progresses through 6-Man Fellowship instances, and finally culminates in a 12-Man Raid. It is recommended that you complete Volume III Books 1 and 2 beforehand, but is not required.</rgb>","'Henric,\
\
Strange things are afoot these days in and around Oatbarton. First there was that mysterious relic that appeared in Bungo Grubb's pipe-weed fields; killed the crop dead, it did, and left everyone else worried for their own!\
\
But now things are even worse. Hobbits have been disappearing left and right. And these aren't Tooks I'm talking about, neither! No, these are good, honest Bolgers and Boffins, as solid and dependable gentlehobbits as you could hope to meet! Not a flaw among them, save being over-fond of their food and drink, and that's not a flaw at all in my estimation!\
\
I don't know for sure what could have caused this recent spate of disappearances, though I have my guesses. I have not seen as many of the grim-faced Rangers lurking about in recent days; is it the same in Bree? In any event, if you know of a stalwart adventurer, be sure to send him or her to me at once. I am worried for my friends here in Oartbarton! We're within the bounds of the Shire, of course, but the rest of Evendim is a dangerous place, just to our north, and even Oatbarton has been frightful of late.\
\
Wishing you the best, your devoted cousin,\
\
Fenric'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This Quest Arc begins with 3-Man Small Fellowship content, progresses through 6-Man Fellowship instances, and finally culminates in a 12-Man Raid. It is recommended that you complete Volume III Books 1 and 2 beforehand, but is not required.</rgb>","Talk to Bounder Boffin inside Northcotton Farm","'Ah, hello there, ${PLAYER}, it is a pleasure to meet you. I wish we met under happier circumstances, because things have not been going well here in Oatbarton, as you must know if you saw my letter to cousin Henric!\
\
'The Bounders have been kept busy in recent weeks, but now things are happening within the Bounds: strange relics appearing in pipe-weed fields overnight, crops dying out suddenly; it's the worst I've ever seen it!\
\
'But now hobbits are disappearing: first that thing appeared in Bungo Grubb's field, and not long after, Isenbard Bolger's up and gone. Then Crystal Bolger vanished, and afterwards Andy Boffin and Gladiola Farmer. A couple Bounders went off to Northcotton Farm, west of here and up the hill, where Gladiola Farmer was last seen. You should gather a couple friends and go investigate. I'm worried!'","The Northcotton Farm is located west of Oatbarton's town centre and up the steep hill.\
\
Fenric Banks has told you of the hobbit disappearances and wants you to gather a couple friends and investigate the Northcotton Farm, where one of the hobbits was last seen.","'The letter Henric Banks showed me from his cousin Fenric is worrying, ${PLAYER}, wouldn't you say? It seems to me that troubles are increasing everywhere these days, and even the cheery common room of the Pony is not safe from these worries!\
\
'I haven't seen hide nor hair from those Rangers recently, and if you'd asked me a couple weeks ago, I'd have been delighted! But now I'm not so sure. In their absence, the shadows seem to be lengthening and the troubles increasing! It's bad for business!\
\
'You should travel to Oatbarton and see about helping Fenric Banks. The village is in the southern reaches of Evendim, but is within the bounds of the Shire. It is one of the most northerly of the hobbit-villages.'","'A couple Bounders went off to Northcotton Farm, west of here and up the hill, to look for the missing hobbits. You should gather a couple friends and go investigate. I'm worried!'"},
[6595]={"'You have brought no tablet to me. What madness has taken you?'","Drugoth the Deathmonger has been commanded to raise an army of wights on Sâri-surma, in Forochel.\
\
Elrond has translated the broken tablet he found within the Lost Temple and now knows the location of another Gaunt-lord.","You are not alone. A Lossoth hunter watches you closely","Talk to Pirita in the fortress on Sâri-surma","'Sâri-surma is located in Forochel, within the Icebay. You must go there and find Drugoth the Death-monger.'","Pirita of the Lossoth is inside the fortress on Sâri-surma.\
\
Pirita wishes to speak with you.","Travel to Sâri-surma and make your way through the fortress","'I found this broken tablet within the crypts of the Lost Temple, ${PLAYER}, and it reveals more commands of the gaunt-lord Gortheron. The missing section seems to be addressed to Ferndúr, for I see several mentions of the Red Cloud, but most of the directives for Drugoth are intact.\
\
'Drugoth is commanded to go to Forochel, and to assemble an army of wights from Sâri-surma, the Isle of Death, with which to sweep south into the populated lands of Eriador. Gortheron's displeasure is clear: it seems that his servant Ivar was given the task of raising an army of wights, but failed to do so, and now it falls to Drugoth.\
\
'It was Drugoth that sought to threaten Rivendell with the terror of the dragon Thorog, and though he was cast out of the dragon, somehow Drugoth has returned. He has gone to Sâri-surma in Forochel, and you must find him and end this scheme of his master.'","'I found this broken tablet here within the crypts of the Lost Temple, ${PLAYER}, and it reveals more commands of the Gaunt-lord Gortheron. The missing section seems to be addressed to Ferndúr, for I see several mentions of the Red Cloud, but most of the directives for Drugoth are intact.\
\
'Drugoth is commanded to go to Forochel and to assemble an army of wights from Sâri-surma, the Isle of Death, with which to sweep south into the populated lands of Eriador. Gortheron's displeasure is clear: it seems that his servant Ivar was given the task of raising an army of wights, but failed to do so, and now it falls to Drugoth.\
\
'It was Drugoth that sought to threaten Rivendell with the terror of the dragon Thorog, and though he was cast out of the dragon, somehow Drugoth has returned. He has gone to Sâri-surma in Forochel, and you must find him and end this scheme of his master.'","'Things go ill with my people. Great storms descended upon our homes. The bay of ice heaved in the tumult. The words were not spoken for many days, but they could not remain unsaid forever: had the Witch-king returned to cast his deathly winter upon us again?\
\
'It is not so. But still the land is angry. Someone has disturbed it, bends its will against my people. I do not come to this Isle of Death lightly, but Yrjänä has commanded it.'","'Sâri-surma is in Forochel, within the Icebay. You must hinder Drugoth's plans there!'","In Their Absence, Chapter 10","Elrond's examination of the tablet he found in the Lost Temple has revealed the objective of another of the Gaunt-lords."},
[6596]={"'The creature within this fortress is a being of great evil. Yrjänä seems to know the name of this creature and has gone further into the fortress to confront it.\
\
'Find Yrjänä! He cannot fight this foe by himself! We cannot lose our chieftain. You and your allies must oppose the evil here and fight in his stead.'","In Their Absence, Chapter 11","'${PLAYER}! For what reason have you come to the Isle of Death?'\
\
Yrjänä listens to your tale, and he nods in understanding.\
\
'Yes, this creature that has come to Sâri-surma is the gaunt-lord Drugoth. He brings fear in his train, but there is something else: I think madness has taken him.'","Talk to Yrjänä in Sâri-surma","'The Lossoth cannot lose Yrjänä. We would be lost without our chieftain. You must find him and keep him from fighting the evil creature that lives now on this Isle of Death!'","Yrjänä is somewhere within the fortress on Sâri-surma.\
\
Pirita has asked you to find the Lossoth chieftain, Yrjänä, within the depths of the fortress.","In the depths of the fortress on Sâri-surma, the Lossoth are trying to end the threat of Drugoth the Death-monger."},
[6597]={"In the depths of the fortress on Sâri-surma, Drugoth the Death-monger threatens the safety of Forochel and the lands beyond.","Defeat Drugoth the Death-monger in the fortress on Sâri-surma","'My people have never faced a Gaunt-lord who acts as...strangely...as this Drugoth. He pits his servants against each other; little thought seems to go into his actions beyond the sowing of discord.\
\
'If you speak truly of his errand, his master cannot be pleased with Drugoth. His actions are almost...animal-like...and if he is raising an army, he is then turning it against itself. There is no reason there!\
\
'Do not underestimate this creature. If he is more beast than thinking being now, he is an animal uncaged, and will fight with ferocity.'","'You must defeat Drugoth the Death-monger, ${PLAYER}. He is just ahead!'","Drugoth the Death-monger waits in the depths of his fortress on Sâri-surma.\
\
Yrjänä has told you that Drugoth acts impulsively, more like an animal than a thinking being.","Defeated Drugoth the Death-monger","Habla con Yrjänä","'Drugoth has been defeated, and you have the thanks and praise of my people. Even as he succumbed to his madness, he still had teeth with which to rip and tear, and a cruel mind with which he could do harm.\
\
'It is good he be no more.'","Yrjänä wants to speak with you now that you have defeated Drugoth in the fortress on Sâri-surma.","In Their Absence, Chapter 12"},
[6598]={"'Pirita found this tablet cast aside in a corner of the fortress. She showed it to me, sure of its significance but not its meaning.\
\
'If I read this illustration rightly, it is a map of the southern lands spoken of by our friend Lothrandir; the lands he once lived in, and now to which he has returned. See these four lines? They all come from one point, and travel across the map in many directions; this one at the northern edge of the map arrives at an island. It must be Sâri-surma. Four lines, four gaunt-lords.\
\
'If you follow this line southward, to where all the points meet, you will find the one who commanded Drugoth to come here. The line goes to the land called Enedwaith. In its south-western reaches, among the Lich Bluffs, stands the ruin of a mighty stronghold. It is in this place that the lines meet.'","'See where the lines on the tablet begin? That is where you will find the leader of the Gaunt-lords. Travel to Enedwaith and find the stronghold in the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs.'","'Pirita found this tablet cast aside in a corner of the fortress. She showed it to me, sure of its significance but not its meaning.\
\
'If I read this illustration rightly, it is a map of the southern lands spoken of by our friend Lothrandir; the lands he once lived in and now to which he has returned. See these four lines? They all come from one point and travel across the map in many directions; this one at the northern edge of the map arrives at an island. It must be Sâri-surma. Four lines, four Gaunt-lords.\
\
'If you follow this line southward, to where all the points meet, you will find the one who commanded Drugoth to come to Sâri-surma. The line goes to the land called Enedwaith. In its south-western reaches, among the Lich Bluffs, stands the ruin of a mighty stronghold. It is in this place that the lines meet.'","Find Gortheron's lair in the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs, in Enedwaith","'It is a pleasure to meet you at last, ${PLAYER}. Yes, I know your name. The presence of my kinsmen was known to me when first they stepped into this land, and I sought out Halbarad some days ago.\
\
'I have advised him not to bring the Grey Company too near this place; danger has been growing here recently, and I believe that Gortheron, the leader of the Gaunt-lords, is to blame. He revived his fallen allies and sent them north into Eriador on errands unknown to me.'\
\
Túgonn listens to your account of the other Gaunt-lords you encountered.\
\
'Impressive feats all, ${PLAYER}. But Gortheron is the greatest of the gaunt-lords, and your victories over his lesser allies will avail you nothing if you underestimate his powers.'","Yrjänä picked up a tablet that seems to contain directions to the stronghold of Gortheron the Doom-caller, leader of the Gaunt-lords.","In Their Absence, Chapter 13","'See where the lines on the tablet begin? That is where you will find the leader of the Gaunt-lords. Travel to Enedwaith, to the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs.'","The stronghold of Gortheron the Doom-caller is located in Enedwaith, in the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs.\
\
Yrjänä found a tablet in the depths of the fortress on Sâri-surma that reveals the location of the leader of the Gaunt-lords.","'¡Nada de cháchara!'"},
[6599]={"Túgonn is in the entrance of Ost Dunhoth.\
\
You have conquered two wings of Ost Dunhoth and should return now to Túgonn.","Talk to Túgonn","In Their Absence, Chapter 14","'The door to the central area is open, ${PLAYER}. You will find Gortheron within.'","Ost Dunhoth has two wings that must be explored before the central area can be unsealed.","'Explore the two side wings of Ost Dunhoth, and we can work to unseal the central area.'","Survive the spread of plague and poison in the west wing","The Ranger Túgonn has told you that the door into the central area of Ost Dunhoth is locked and can only be opened by exploring the side wings.","'Each of the Gaunt-lords you defeated held mastery over a particular facet of the offensive planned by Gortheron: Thadúr the Ravager, master of poison; Ferndúr the Virulent, master of plague; Drugoth the Death-monger, master of fear. You did not encounter Ivar the Blood-hand, but he is the master of war.\
\
'Together, with Gortheron, they are five. Five Gaunt-lords made in mockery of the five Wizards. Gortheron has corrupted these sprawling ruins, making of them a home for the servants of the Gaunt-lords.\
\
'The door into the central area is sealed; if you are able to defeat the minions of Gortheron in each of the side wings, we may be able to open the central area and challenge Gortheron directly.'","Survive the wages of war and conquer your fear in the east wing"},
[6601]={"'Look for the missing hobbits inside Northcotton Farm, ${PLAYER}! Once you've found them, find my assistant, Tulip. She's gone ahead to investigate.'","Rescued hobbits inside Northcotton Farm (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Bounder Boffin's assistant Tulip is somewhere further inside the Northcotton Farm, and it could be the missing hobbits are as well.\
\
Bounder Boffin has asked you to search for the missing hobbits inside the Northcotton Farm.","In Their Absence, Chapter 2","Bounder Boffin is concerned about the disappearances happening in and around the Northcotton Farm and wants you to investigate.","'There are hobbits to be rescued, ${PLAYER}! Find them throughout the Northcotton Farm and save them if you can! I found several of them, but it was beyond my abilities to free them from their predicaments. But you may be able to help them, and I hope that you will!'","'My assistant, Tulip Grubb, has gone further into the farm in search of the four missing hobbits. If you do see any sign of them, be sure to tell Tulip. Keep your eyes open for any clues! Were those good folk hobbitnapped?\
\
'There's something very strange going on here in the Northcotton Farm, that's for sure!'","'${PLAYER}! You've saved the hobbits! I did not believe I could free them myself, but I was able to stealthily speak with each of them before you came to their rescue, and the stories they whispered to me were very familiar! Crystal Bolger, up in her tree, spoke of a delicious smell that drew her to the farm, and Gladiola said something similar. Andy Boffin said the smell began so deliciously, but turned so foul when he started eating that it knocked him out with the power of its stench.\
\
'I held my nose shut with one hand, and though my eyes watered furiously, I investigated the main farmhouse. There's an evil-looking creature back there, ${PLAYER}, and I think it was he who brewed that terrible poison! I think he was using it to lure hobbits into his trap, and Isenbard Bolger is still missing! That creature must still have him captive.\
\
'He muttered to himself almost constantly. It seems that his name is Thadúr, and his poison is called Darkthorn. You've got to stop this evil creature, ${PLAYER}, you and your friends! You've just got to!'","Rescue hobbits inside Northcotton Farm (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Tulip Grubb is somewhere within the Northcotton Farm.\
\
You have rescued the missing hobbits and should now find Bounder Boffin's assistant, Tulip Grubb, who came into the farm to investigate the disappearances.","Talk to Tulip Grubb within the Northcotton Farm"},
[6602]={"Defeat Thadúr the Ravager on the Northcotton Farm","In Their Absence, Chapter 3","'Good job, ${PLAYER}! You have rescued Isenbard, and that Thadúr fellow won't be bothering us anymore!\
\
'I do wonder about his last words, though. What did he mean by battle, shadow, and plague returning? And where is Tirith dan Forduath? I've never heard of it and can barely even say it!'","'You've got to stop this Thadúr and his deadly Darkthorn poison, ${PLAYER}! He seems to be back by the main farmhouse here on the Northcotton Farm! Just go through these doors and follow the path around!'","Thadúr el Devastador derrotado","Tulip Grubb told you about an evil-looking creature named Thadúr at the end of the path through the doors behind Tulip. He seems to be the creature responsible for the deadly Darkthorn poison.\
\
You and your allies need to defeat Thadúr before he can bring any more trouble to the Shire.","You have rescued some of the hobbitnapped hobbits from the Northcotton Farm, and now Tulip Grubb believes she knows what caused the disappearances.","'This Thadúr seems to be a pretty terrible creature, ${PLAYER}, and he has a band of goblins to do his bidding! He seems to have given them phials of the Darkthorn poison, so it will be no easy task to make your way into the rear of the farm. Go through these doors and follow the path to Thadúr...and good luck!\
\
'It's up to you, ${PLAYER}! Teach this ghastly fellow a lesson!'","Talk to Bounder Boffin on the Northcotton Farm","Bounder Boffin is inside the Northcotton Farm.\
\
You have defeated Thadúr the Ravager, and Bounder Boffin is eager to speak with you about your victory on the Northcotton Farm."},
[6603]={"'A friendly face? At last! Oh, my friend, it is terrible! War and death have come to Stoneheight! This place is lost!'","'Yes? You have a philological question for me? Wonderful, wonderful! It is my favourite study of all: the study of words!'\
\
Ronald Dwale listens eagerly as you recount the final threatening words of Thadúr the Ravager.\
\
'Ah, very interesting, yes. Tirith dan Forduath. A bit on the easy side, but it does have a few points of note. \\qTirith\\q is \\qguard\\q, and \\qdan\\q gives us \\qagainst.\\q So this is a location that guards against something, some threat. But what threat?\
\
'Words, as you have certainly observed by now, sometimes behave differently together than they do apart, and such is the case here. Forduath is a construction composed of two words joined for the purpose of linguistics: in this case \\qforn,\\q \\qnorthern,\\q and \\qdúath,\\q \\qshadow.\\q You are looking for a place once known as \\qGuard against the Northern Shadow,\\q and I think I know the place!\
\
'It is not called that anymore, of course, and in my studies I have learned that it was also once called Orod Elon, the \\qMountain of the Stars and Stones.\\q But now it is called Stoneheight, and it is on the North Downs, north-east of Amon Raith. A road leads north of a deserted farm-house, climbing up to the heights.'","'Look for Ronald Dwale at his home north-east of Oatbarton, just outside the village of Dwaling. He'll know the meaning of that Thadúr fellow's final words, if anyone does.'","In Their Absence, Chapter 4","Stoneheight is located on the North Downs, north-east of Amon Raith. The town of Stoneheight is located atop a sloping rise north of a deserted farm-house.\
\
Ronald Dwale has teased apart the meaning of Thadúr's final words and has told you that Tirith dan Forduath was the ancient name for a place now called Stoneheight, on the North Downs.","Talk to Benedric Jacklin in the town of Stoneheight","Talk to Ronald Dwale about Thadúr's final words","'You are looking for a place now called Stoneheight on the North Downs, ${PLAYER}, north-east of Amon Raith. The town of Stoneheight is located atop a sloping rise north of a deserted farm-house.'","Ronald Dwale lives north-east of Oatbarton, just outside the village of Dwaling.\
\
Bounder Boffin has sent you to speak with Ronald Dwale about Thadúr's final words. If anyone knows what Tirith dan Forduath is, he will.","'I get the impression that this Thadúr was an ancient fellow, which means that the mystery of his final words may be ancient as well. It could be that Tirith dan Forduath is an old name for a place that goes now by a new name! In fact, I am almost certain this is the case!\
\
'If so, then you're not very far from solving this mystery, because a hobbit lives nearby who just loves the history and makeup of old words. If anyone knows what \\qTirith dan Forduath\\q describes, it'll be Ronald Dwale. He is an expert at languages and words.\
\
'Ronald lives north-east of Oatbarton, just outside the village of Dwaling. If you would solve this mystery of words, you should talk to him at once!'","Before his defeat, Thadúr the Ravager spoke some mysterious words. You must get to the bottom of them before great evil comes to pass."},
[6604]={"'It was terrible, friend! A tall, menacing figure stalked through the streets of town while his cruel allies slew anyone that moved! I do not know what he wanted, but he moved with a single-minded purpose; I think he was looking for something.\
\
'But why would he visit this destruction upon Stoneheight? Ours was just a town of peaceful folk whose other homes had been lost in the fighting with Orcs out of Angmar! We have done nothing wrong! We were just trying to get a fresh start!'\
\
Benedric is on the very edge of tears.\
\
'There may be others who were able to hide from that terrible figure. You have to search Stoneheight to see if anyone survived! But be careful... the allies of that frightful apparition may still be here!'","You have come to the town of Stoneheight, but it seems to have been recently attacked.","In Their Absence, Chapter 5","'Who is it...? Are you... a friend...?'\
\
The man is near death; his wounds seem most severe. He coughs weakly and his face contorts painfully. He gathers the little strength he has left, determined to tell you something.\
\
'I... I think I... did this.... I think I drew the horror... to Stoneheight....'","Benedric Jacklin has asked you to search further within Stoneheight for survivors of the attack.\
\
The town of Stoneheight was attacked by a merciless figure who moved with a single-minded purpose, and now you must search for survivors.","You catch a glimpse of movement out of the corner of your eye.","Talk to Seward Pearse before he succumbs to his injuries","'You have to search the streets of Stoneheight for survivors of the attack, you just have to! We have done nothing to deserve this!'","'Have you found any survivors of the attack? You have to keep looking!'","Search Stoneheight for survivors of the attack","You have found a survivor of the attack on Stoneheight, but his wounds seem very severe."},
[6605]={"'It feels strange to say that we have been fortunate in such circumstances, ${PLAYER}, but still it is so: for Ivar the Blood-hand has left our town behind. He must have found what he came to find and was content to leave his servants behind. They have now been dealt with!\
\
'But now the real work -- the work of rebuilding -- must begin...if anyone will even want to rebuild this town, that is!'","Seward Pearse's home is further within the town of Stoneheight, and he wants you to see if the helm is still there.\
\
Ivar the Blood-hand stalked through the town of Stoneheight, and Seward Pearse believes he came looking for the helm Seward purchased from a merchant.","'We came here...for a new life. I met a merchant...he had a helm, said it had passed through the hands of...many adventurers. Inlaid with gems, it was.... \
\
'He offered a fair...a fair price...and I thought I could pry the gems loose.'\
\
Seward coughs again, and his body shakes with the pain of the effort.\
\
'I could not...loose the gems. Woe betide me! I think...I think the helm's true owner...came to claim it! Ivar! Ivar the Blood-hand! He stalked through the town....\
\
'My home...is further in. See if the helm...is still there. But beware the Blood-hand!'","Defeated Dale Truitt","'Ivar's followers...do not get along...it seems, but do not...underestimate...them!'","The helm is gone. Ivar found what he was seeking","While in the wreckage of the town of Stoneheight, you saw in-fighting between two of the enemies left by Ivar to finish the job.\
\
Dale Truitt slew Búbhosh-grat and now must be defeated if the people of Stoneheight are to rebuild.","Benedric Jacklin wishes to speak with you about what happened to the town of Stoneheight.","In Their Absence, Chapter 6","Search further within Stoneheight for sign of the helm","'Did I...cause this...to happen...? Did the helm...draw the Blood-hand...to this place? Go to my home, further in, and...see if anything...remains....'","Defeat Dale Truitt in Stoneheight","Talk to Benedric Jacklin in Stoneheight","The attack on Stoneheight must be avenged, and quickly: allies of the terrible figure that led the attack still remain within its walls."},
[6606]={"'If you are here to explore this Lost Temple, I must warn you, friends! The Gaunt-lord Ferndúr has come to this place, but to what purpose I cannot guess. There is something else, too, something that I cannot explain.'","Bring the broken tablet to Elrond in Rivendell","'I found this tablet on the ground on the way here, ${PLAYER}. It is covered in evil runes, and I cannot read it, but I believe it was dropped by the Gaunt-lord as he passed through Stoneheight. Perhaps if you can uncover its meaning, you will be able to make some sense of this attack.\
\
'You know Elrond of Rivendell? It is rumoured that he is a master of lore, and he might be able to read the markings on this tablet. Perhaps he can tell us what it says.'","'These are evil runes, ${PLAYER}. I can read them, though it is not pleasing to do so. The tablet contains directives for Ivar, as you supposed, from the Gaunt-lord named Gortheron. He is instructed to raise an army of wights with which to crush the Free Peoples.\
\
'It is curious, ${PLAYER}, that Ivar's actions in the town of Stoneheight do not seem to have been in line with these orders. Why did the Blood-hand destroy the town as he did, and then leave it? Would not following his orders be more important?\
\
'There is more here: he is told to keep a close eye on Ferndúr, for though he was the Master of Imlad Balchorth for many years, Gortheron has not forgotten what happened to Ferndúr's people in the depths of his temple.\
\
'I do not know what this is in reference to, ${PLAYER}, but I do know where this temple, this Lost Temple, is located, because a scout of Rivendell has observed worrisome activity there of late. Assemble a fellowship of allies and find her at Ost Chall, in the northern reaches of Nan Tornaeth.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'The mention of the Lost Temple on the tablet from Stoneheight has me concerned, ${PLAYER}. Gather a fellowship of allies and join my scout Ithriel at the Lost Temple, beyond Ost Chall in the northern reaches of Nan Tornaeth.'","Elrond Half-elven is in his library in Rivendell.\
\
You have been given a mysterious tablet that was found in the town of Stoneheight. The tablet is covered in mysterious runes; perhaps Elrond can read them.","'It is said that Elrond Half-elven is most learned in the ways of lore; he may be able to read the runes on this tablet. Was it really dropped by Ivar the Blood-hand? Might it tell us where Ivar plans to go next?'","In Their Absence, Chapter 7","The Elf-scout Ithriel is scouting the Lost Temple, located at Ost Chall in the northern reaches of Nan Tornaeth.\
\
Elrond has read the runes on the tablet found in Stoneheight, and a mention of the Lost Temple has drawn his notice.","Benedric Jacklin found a tablet with curious markings on it in the wreckage of Stoneheight.","Find Ithriel at the Lost Temple"},
[6607]={"The mercenary Scristan is seriously injured just within the entrance to the crypts of the Lost Temple.\
\
You have found an injured mercenary, but he makes no hostile sign.","Cross the temple-grounds and enter the crypts","'Make your way to the crypts, beyond the temple-grounds, fighting the mercenary band hired by Ferndúr as you go.'","The crypts of the Lost Temple are beyond the grounds of the temple.\
\
Ithriel has asked you to fight the mercenary band hired by Ferndúr as you make your way across the temple-grounds.","In Their Absence, Chapter 8","'I don't have the will to fight you, ${RACE}. Just leave me be. We were given good coin to come to this forsaken place, but once we descended into this crypt, something didn't feel right to me.\
\
'I told them I would go no further. Coward, they called me, and left me here with a knife in my side to keep me company. Some payment! Didn't know Colfrith before yesterday, but me and Rimbald had done lots of jobs before this one. I guess that's what friendship is good for...these days....\
\
'But they'll get theirs! If the screams I heard not long ago are any indication, they already have! Ha ha ha ha!'","Ithriel has told you that the Gaunt-lord Ferndúr the Virulent has come to the Lost Temple for some unknown purpose.","Talk to Scristan","An injured mercenary nods weakly at you, but makes no sign to attack","'Ferndúr the Virulent would be worrisome enough, ${PLAYER}, but he has hired a mercenary band, and they have been prowling about the grounds of the Lost Temple. It is highly unusual, and I do not know why Ferndúr would deign to work with such Men. It is my understanding that the desires of Men are beneath the notice of such creatures as the Gaunt-lords.\
\
'But this mercenary band is certainly in the employ of the Gaunt-lord. Make your way through the grounds, and you will see it is so; enter the crypts and look for signs of what Ferndúr is planning.'","'You found an injured mercenary within the crypts, but he made no sign of attacking? You should see what he has to say, if he does not appear to be hostile. Perhaps he can illuminate Ferndúr's interest in this place.'"},
[6608]={"The mercenary Scristan has been left for dead by his former allies, but he wants you to avenge himself upon his employer, the Gaunt-lord Ferndúr.","'You and your allies have done well to dispatch Ferndúr, ${PLAYER}. He was as cruel to his allies as he was to his enemies, and my investigation of the crypts has confirmed what previously I only suspected. But now the story is clear to me.\
\
'Long ago, the Men of Rhudaur waged battle against the other remnants of the North Kingdom. They worshipped Ferndúr, believing he could grant them the victory...and indeed, the plague he harnessed would be so great a weapon that Arthedain and Cardolan could not hope to stand against its threat.\
\
'He gave to them the plague, the Red Cloud, but they could not control it. The Men of Rhudaur who lived and worshipped at the Lost Temple were laid low by the weapon they sought to wield. It was their undoing, but Ferndúr did not weep for them, though it cost him many servants. He merely laughed as the Red Cloud claimed its victims.\
\
'I am glad you have ended his threat.'","Elrond wishes to speak with you about your defeat of Ferndúr the Virulent.\
\
You have defeated the Gaunt-lord Ferndúr in the depths of the Lost Temple, and now Elrond wishes to speak with you.","'I'm glad you showed that gaunt fellow not to trifle with us. Serves him right.'","Ferndúr the Virulent is further within the crypts of the Lost Temple.\
\
The mercenary Scristan believes that the Gaunt-lord intended to throw away the lives of the mercenary band he hired, and Scristan wants him to pay for it.","In Their Absence, Chapter 9","'I have no love for my old mates now, but Ferndúr should pay for bringing us here without telling us the risks. I don't like it. He's further within. I suspect he never intended us to leave this place alive!'","'It's all over now; I care not a whit for them! Let 'em suffer, I say. They should have listened to me and saved their own lives; could be they're wanting for the blade they stuck me with, eh? Ha ha ha!'\
\
Scristan's laughter seems to cause him pain, and he wheezes with the effort of it.\
\
'But I don't like being deceived, ${RACE}, and that gaunt fellow's coin wasn't good enough to get me to go further into this place without explanation. I want you to make him pay for tryin' to use us. His coin'd need to be better to get Scristan to throw his life away!\
\
Scristan laughs again, painfully.\
\
'My life's been thrown away, without my consent! That's a good deal cheaper, it seems. Find this gaunt fellow, this Ferndúr, further in and make him remember me.'","Defeat Ferndúr the Virulent within the Lost Temple","Talk to Elrond in the depths of the Lost Temple","Defeated Ferndúr the Virulent"},
[6609]={"Thane Edric can be found in the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.\
\
You have aided Thane Edric's men greatly in preparing the town and eliminating the Enemy's nearest forces.","Thane Edric's men can be found inside Entwade, as well as along the road west to Middlemead and among the fields outside southern Entwade.\
\
Thane Edric has asked that you aid his men in identifying and minimizing the threats that lurk outside Entwade, as well as helping the men of the settlement bolster its defences before the White Hand returns to siege the town.","'Few could deny the effort you have put forth, ${PLAYER}. My men and I are grateful for what you have done to aid us in preparing for the White Hand's next assault. Without the King's aid, we were ill-prepared for such a task, but should the Wade hold, he and I shall have words upon his return.\
\
'Come then, we must talk of what is to be done with this man you have found.'","Aid Thane Edric's men in securing Entwade (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Thane Edric","'Hail, ${PLAYER}.  Léoflad and my people have set off to Aldburg, and my hope is that they shall arrive having encountered nary a trouble.\
\
'Their safety weighs heavily upon me, friend. I have held the Wade for years, and I would not have sent them away, if I saw not the danger approaching from all sides. Yet, I wish Théoden had done more to aid us....he could have secured Kingstead before leaving us to fend for ourselves among so many foes. As it stands, he has left his niece to handle his affairs here, but I think her no more likely to lead than him, even spared the venomous whisperings of Wormtongue.\
\
'This, of course, brings me to you. You have come into our lands and aided my people well. There are many matters to attend to in Entwade, and all of them of dire importance. Without a concerted effort, there can be no way to address them all before time runs out.'","Thane Edric and his men struggle to make ready for the coming siege of Entwade amid the numerous threats already surrounding the town.","In Too Deep","DNT -- Players will not see"},
[6610]={"In a Spot of Trouble","Marigold Winterdown is at the hobbit-village of Hoarhallow, found on the western edge of the Grimwood Forest in Hithlad. The village is found on the shores of the Hoarwell River.\
\
Alf is free, but before he left you, he asked that you inform Marigold Winterdown that he would be returning to work at the bakery in Hoarhallow shortly.","'Alf was captured by the goblins! We had all thought him lost for good.\
\
'You saved him, ${PLAYER}! We should have a party in your honour. Mayhaps we will, once we get to see the sun shining in these parts again. \
\
'One day it will happen, I know this in earnest. For the moment, I feel it fitting to part with a couple of these tokens the Big Folk from Glân Vraig gave us. Thank you for saving my baker!'","Alf Earthenway is at Grothum.\
\
Alf Earthenway asked you to help him escape from the goblins.","Alf is free","'Please, no more beatings.\
\
'Y-you're no goblin. Merry me! I have never been so pleased to see someone in all my days.\
\
'As you see, I am in a spot of trouble and need a fair bit of rescuing, if you wouldn't mind. Can you help me get clear of these accursed goblins?'","Talk to Alf","Alf Earthenway was out for a leisurely stroll when goblins found him and dragged him to the north. He has spent the time since his capture cooking for the goblins as they think he makes the tastiest food. It was the only thing that he could do to prevent the goblins from eating him."},
[6611]={"Cyneberg painstakingly buried the townsfolk and decorated their graves","Tell Cyneberg what you saw","You gently tell Cyneberg that you saw the brave, heroic work she did when she came to this town, and the view of her fallen home. She looks at you with tear-filled eyes.\
\
'I did what I could for them, but I was too late. Luckily the Orcs were not many, and they were scattered. But my heart broke when I saw Scylfig down below....'","Discover what Cyneberg saw to make her despair (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Cyneberg has moved mountains in Grimnesberg as her grief caught up with her at last.","Scylfig, Cyneberg's own ice-encased home from the Writhendowns, can be seen from this peak...","'I should have done Gárwig's bidding and helped at Byre Tor, but I was blinded by my desire to find Thrymm alive.\
\
'I came here and found... horrible things, and that's when I understood. I understood that Núrzum has won. My family is dead, all of them. Thrymm is dead. The enemy has taken Wildermore, and there is nothing left.\
\
'When I came here, my eyes were opened at last.'","Cyneberg can be found in the centre of Grimnesberg.\
\
You should speak with Cyneberg.","In the Clutches of Despair","Cyneberg did a great deal of work in Grimnesberg as her grief overwhelmed her.\
\
You should have a look around and see where Cyneberg's mind was while she captured this town."},
[6612]={"En las grietas sombrías","'Hace algunos días nuestro más valiente explorador se marchó para espiar a los orcos que cruzaban el paso.\
\
'Envió un mensaje que decía que había encontrado algo peor: una grieta sombría llena de malvadas criaturas-murciélago que no había visto antes... pero esto es lo último que sabemos de él.\
\
'¿Puedes encontrar a nuestro explorador y ver si está a salvo? Tenía un pequeño campamento en lo alto de la pared del valle al este. Si vive, le encontrarás allí.'","'El jefe Tuokki te envía a ayudarme? Podría haber enviado a alguien más grande, creo... ¡pero estoy herido y aceptaré tu ayuda de buen grado!\
\
'Seres malvados se reúnen aquí en Ram Dúath. Más malvadas que los orcos, más malvadas que los Hombres que sirven a los señores oscuros. ¡Te hablaré de ellos!'","El jefe Tuokki te ha pedido que busques a uno de los Hijos de la Tierra, un explorador que fue enviado al siguiente valle para espiar a un grupo de mujeres-murciélago que habían hecho su guardia en algún lugar de las grietas ocultas de Ram Dúath. El Jefe te ha informado de que un explorador tenía un campamento escondido en lo alto de la pared del valle hacia el este."},
[6613]={"Talk to Dori and Nori in the Keep of Tharrazhâr","Dori and Nori can be found in the Keep of Tharrazhâr.\
\
You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu, but many mysteries linger about the fate of the Steel Keep. You should talk to Dori and Nori.","'This cannot be!'\
\
Dori stares at Nori's axe in disbelief.\
\
'Has my brother gone into Thikil-gundu without the aid of his own expedition? Has Karazgar devised some cruel purpose for him?\
\
'But what if... what if he has been taken like the others? No! I will not believe such things!\
\
'We will enter Thikil-gundu together, ${PLAYER}, and we will find my brother!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete the instance 'Thikil-gundu' on its solo difficulty to advance this quest.</rgb>","Fearing that Nori has met with a terrible end at the hands of Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights within Thikil-gundu, Dori and Company must muster the courage to enter the Steel Keep.","'Our journey is over, ${PLAYER}... at least for the moment!\
\
'Nori thinks himself a disgraced dwarf, but these hurts will heal in time! He has adventured as few dwarves have in their lives! Was I disappointed in my brother? Was I fearful that he had led himself to certain doom? Of course I was! But... he is my brother! Even if the King under the Mountain will not forgive Nori as I have, this will not be the end of our adventures!\
\
'There is a fire in the hearts of Durin's Folk! An unquenchable flame! And you have proven yourself among us, my friend. \
\
'We have forced Karazgar out of Thikil-gundu, and that is enough! Even so, there is some unseen evil lurking in our delving of old... and many questions linger in my mind.\
\
'But this day, we honour the lost here among the halls of Tharrazhâr!'","In the Halls of Thikil-gundu","Dori can be found atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall.\
\
You have found evidence that Nori has gone into Thikil-gundu, and Dori now seeks to find his brother before Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights can bring any harm to him.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete the instance 'Thikil-gundu' on its solo difficulty to advance this quest.</rgb>","'I will not allow my brother to meet with such a fate, ${PLAYER}. I swear it!'","'I cannot atone for what I have done, ${PLAYER}. I have disobeyed the King under the Mountain, I have deceived my brother... and for what? Naught, I say!\
\
'Even the gold we found is no boon to my people! There is a curse upon Thikil-gundu... and nothing in the halls of the Steel Keep has gone untouched by it!\
\
'Once I was renowned among Durin's Folk... a hero of the Lonely Mountain! Am I now to be known as the foolish, old dwarf who dreamt of treasures lost?\
\
'No... I will not let this be the end of it!'","Talk to Dori and travel into Thikil-gundu"},
[6614]={"DNT - Company and Nori","'Let us search for Nori in Afhân-binnîn! If my brother is not here, we will be able to follow other passages into the deepest chambers of Thikil-gundu!'","Talk to Dori in Afhân-binnîn","Defeat Athramóth","Find the northern hall that leads into Afhân-binnîn from Kall-khebâb","Appearing to anticipate your arrival, Karazgar stands beneath a great crack in the Wrathhorn!","In the Halls of Thikil-gundu","To your horror, a great cold-drake rests among her brood at Thikil-nesad!","Karazgar can be found in the western reaches of Zashar-tûmun.\
\
You have found Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and you should now attempt to defeat him.","After sealing the western passage into Thikil-nesad, Nori suddenly notices Dori and Company!","The old forges of Thikil-gundu are rife with Orcs!","You feel a cold wind blowing from the rimed ruin-dwellings of Thikil-gundu...","Talk to Dori at the ruined hall to Afhân-binnîn in Kall-khebâb","The hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt can be found in the centre of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces.\
\
Dori has directed you and the rest of the company to search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt for signs of Nori.","'It has been frozen solid!\
\
'Is this some final insult by Vethúg Wintermind? If this is how the great cold-drake has chosen to guard his stolen gold, there will be no recovering it... not until all the halls of the Steel Keep are reclaimed. And many still lie ahead of us, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Many of these old gears are frozen or ruined, but we must find a way to travel deeper into Thikil-gundu. Unless my eyes deceive me, it looks like the gears to some of the eastern halls are intact. If we can reach the old lore-trove of Afhân-binnîn by some path, it would allow us to reach many of the deepest chambers of Thikil-gundu. We must find a way there!\
\
'According to the notes Nori left behind, Afhân-binnîn can be reached through a small hall at the northern end of the smithies of Kall-khebâb.\
\
'Let us find a way into Kall-khebâb, and then we will see if we can find the way into Afhân-binnîn. Besides, it would do us all well to warm ourselves by the forges, I think!\
\
'But... we would be wise to remain on guard. Such silence brings me no comfort.'","Athramóth and her brood can be found in Thikil-nesad.\
\
You have discovered a great cold-drake resting among her brood. You should defeat Athramóth and make safe the old throne of the Steel Keep.","Recover the crown of Dáin","Slain long ago by Vethúg Wintermind, Frór, son of Dáin I, has been raised from death...","'Dori! I cannot believe my eyes!'\
\
Nori rushes forward and embraces his brother.\
\
'It has gone all wrong, brother. I am the last of my expedition. The Weeping Warrior ambushed us before the gates of Thikil-gundu, and he slew the few of my company that survived the Wrack.\
\
'In vengeance, I faced Karazgar in battle. Though I landed many blows, he managed to wrest my axe from my hand! It is a coward's way out of a fight, I think! All I have now is this torch. It has kept me warm, but it is no weapon!'\
\
Dori hands Nori the axe you found before Thikil-gundu.\
\
'My axe! Karazgar will know its bite once more!\
\
'You have found me, brother, and for that I am grateful... but I cannot let Karazgar escape Thikil-gundu! Let us seek our vengeance against Karazgar together!'","'What a terrible cold-drake! We must slay it before it can lay more of its eggs in Thikil-gundu!\
\
'What has become of my brother?'","Find and confront Karazgar in Zashar-tûmun","Frór the Lost can be found in the heights of Afhân-binnîn.\
\
You have discovered the remains of Frór, son of Dáin I, brought to life by a fell spirit in Afhân-binnîn. You should defeat him and let him at last be laid to rest.","Find a way into the smithies of Kall-khebâb","Defeat Karkasht Crow-feeder and the Orcs of Gundabad in Kall-khebâb","Dori can be found in Thikil-gundu.\
\
You have reunited with Nori. You should now speak to Dori and learn what is to be done.","'Listen well, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'If these old maps are to be believed, Durûz-mazal should lie beyond these doors. It was a great chamber wrought in honour of the Seven Dwarf-kings and in its centre, a great hoarding-vault was delved. It became known as Immêsh-khalt, and it held the whole of the wealth of Grárik in its depths.\
\
'If my brother came in search of the treasures of Thikil-gundu, he and his expedition would not have had to look any further than Immêsh-khalt. And so, it is there we will begin our search!\
\
'Let us hope these old gears still turn!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Dori and Company, you can summon them to your side using the Horn of Erebor. In addition, you can access the map of Thikil-gundu by pressing 'M'.</rgb>","'Come, ${PLAYER}. Let us see what has become of Immêsh-khalt!'","Talk to Nori at Thikil-nesad","Find a way through Amrâg-zahar to Zashar-tûmun","Search for Nori at Thikil-nesad, the Steel Seat","Defeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior","'${PLAYER}....\
\
'What Karazgar has done cannot go unanswered. He has slain our kinsfolk, he has set the Dragons of the North upon the Lonely Mountain, and he has stolen and defiled the halls of Thikil-gundu! We seven must stand against him!'\
\
Dori turns to Nori.\
\
'Where has he gone, brother?'\
\
Nori explains that Karazgar travelled into Zashar-tûmun, but he warns you that many Dragon-kind now lurk in the ruin-dwellings of Thikil-gundu.\
\
'Karazgar must answer for the evil he has worked against Durin's Folk! Baruk Khazâd!'","Nori can be found at Thikil-nesad.\
\
Nori has fled into Thikil-nesad and unwittingly reunited with Dori. You should talk to Nori.","Zashar-tûmun, the ruin-dwellings of Thikil-gundu, can be found to the west of the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar.\
\
Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find a way to Zashar-tûmun and confront Karazgar.","Defeat Frór the Lost and banish the fell spirit inhabiting his remains","The smithies of Kall-khebâb can be found in the eastern halls of Thikil-gundu.\
\
Determined to delve deeper into Thikil-gundu, Dori has asked you to find the smithies of Kall-khebâb so that you might gain passage into the other halls of the Steel Keep.","Search for Nori in Afhân-binnîn","'Karazgar must pay for the evil he has wrought!'","Set in gold and adorned with precious mithril, the crown of Dáin has not faded in beauty...","Find a way to Afhân-binnîn through the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar","'The hall to Afhân-binnîn must lie at the northern end of the smithies. Let us see if the path is clear!'","Amid the ruined remains of Amrâg-zahar, a passage leading into Afhân-binnîn lies open...","Athramóth falls defeated, but you hear a great commotion in the distance!","The remains of Frór, son of Dáin I, fall lifeless to the ground...","Nori might be found somewhere within Afhân-binnîn. Afhân-binnîn can be found through Amrâg-zahar.\
\
You have discovered a passage into Afhân-binnîn, and you should now search for Nori within the lore-troves of Thikil-gundu.","Thikil-nesad, the Steel Seat, can be found deep within Thikil-gundu.\
\
Fearing that Nori has been discovered by the inhabitants of the Steel Keep, Dori now hopes to find him before the old throne of Thikil-gundu.","A hall to Afhân-binnîn can be found at the northern end of the smithies of Kall-khebâb.\
\
With the smithies clear of foes, you should now search the smithies for a way into the lore-trove of Afhân-binnîn.","Fearing that Nori has met with a terrible end at the hands of Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights within Thikil-gundu, Dori and Company must muster the courage to enter the Steel Keep.","Talk to Dori","'It is worse than I feared.... \
\
'The Dead walk the halls of Thikil-gundu, and through some vile means, Karazgar has mastered the will of Vethúg Wintermind!\
\
'There is little to celebrate this day, ${PLAYER}, but we have found my brother... and that is enough!\
\
'Let us return to Tharrazhâr, and leave this sorrowful place behind.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: When you complete this quest, you will swiftly travel to the Keep of Tharrazhâr in Skarháld. If you have not finished exploring or seeking treasures in Thikil-gundu, it is advised that you wait to talk to Dori.</rgb>","'How could so many vile spirits be drawn to this place?\
\
'Dwalin once told me of the fate of Skorgrím Dourhand. Have you heard the tale?\
\
'He spoke much of spirits, Gaunt-lords, bloody hands, and other things of which I knew little, but perhaps that was for the best! What a terrible fate for a dwarf... even for one as villainous as Skorgrím!\
\
'What has happened? Has a curse fallen upon Thikil-gundu? So many dwarves have been roused from their rest to serve whatever evil now lurks here....'\
\
Dori pauses and looks at the company of dwarves staring at a great geode in Afhân-binnîn.\
\
'Wait a moment, ${PLAYER}. There is something familiar about that dwarf....\
\
'No... it cannot be! That is Frór, the lost son of Dáin I. After Dáin fell to Vethúg Wintermind, Frór sacrificed himself so that his brothers and kinsfolk could escape from Thikil-gundu. It can be no other... the crown of Dáin I rests upon his head!\
\
'We must banish whatever evil has taken hold of him!'","Dori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn.\
\
You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu. You should now speak to Dori.","Karazgar can be found somewhere within Zashar-tûmun.\
\
Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find and confront Karazgar.","Dori can be found in Thikil-gundu.\
\
You have defeated the fell spirit inhabiting the remains of Frór and recovered the long-lost crown of Dáin. You should offer the crown to Dori and learn what is to be done.","'It is with great regret that we cannot bear Frór's remains from the Steel Keep. Thikil-gundu itself will have to serve as his tomb!\
\
'The King under the Mountain demanded that we return bearing a bone of Vethúg Wintermind, but to instead return with the crown of Dáin might speak better of our deeds in the ruins of Grárik!'\
\
Dori places the crown in a pack, and begins to study his map of Thikil-gundu again.\
\
'We should descend into the lore-trove and continue to the northern halls. If we follow that path, we will come to Thikil-nesad! It was once the seat of all of Grárik, and it was there that King Dáin I ruled before he fell.\
\
'Perhaps Nori has hidden himself away before the old throne of Thikil-gundu, but I fear many more foes lurk in these halls.\
\
'Even so, we must press on!'","Search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt","An enormous hoard of gold lies encased in ice beneath your feet...","Talk to Dori in Thikil-gundu","Dori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn.\
\
You have come to Thikil-gundu in search of Nori. You should now speak to Dori in Thikil-gundu.","The hall into Afhân-binnîn is sealed by rubble and debris...","Karkasht Crow-feeder can be found in the smithies of Kall-khebâb.\
\
You have discovered a massive hobgoblin leading the Orcs in the smithies of Kall-khebâb. You must defeat him if you are to continue deeper into Thikil-gundu.","The feast-house of Amrâg-zahar can be found through the northernmost doors of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces.\
\
With the heat of the smithies now spreading through Thikil-gundu, Dori hopes to find another way to reach Afhân-binnîn and continue the search for Nori.","'Bah! Orcs? Hobgoblins? This was supposed to be the swiftest path to Afhân-binnîn!'\
\
Dori studies his map of Thikil-gundu and turns it about a few times.\
\
'It seems that there is another way to the lore-trove, but to reach it, we must pass through the old feast-house of Amrâg-zahar! The gears outside its doors appeared to be frozen when I stood atop the hoarding-vault, but perhaps the heat of the smithies might loosen them.\
\
'We have been lucky to find only a few Orcs so far, but I fear that Karazgar and the Dragon-kind dwelling in Thikil-gundu may soon be aware of us. It is some consolation that those dwarf-wights are not fond of the dragons, but they are no friends of ours either!\
\
'The swifter we find my brother, the swifter we can leave this place. Let us go!'","Karkasht Crow-feeder falls defeated, and the heat of the smithies begins to spread through Thikil-gundu...","Deliver the crown of Dáin to Dori in Thikil-gundu","'According to my map, there is a way to Afhân-binnîn through the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar. Let us search for it!'"},
