[6616]={"Amid growing dangers in Kingstead, Thane Edric and Léoflad struggle to prepare their people to journey to the Eastfold.","Thane Edric and his wife, Léoflad, can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade.\
\
Thane Edric has asked you to aid Léoflad and his people as they make ready to travel. You should speak to Edric and Léoflad.","Talk to Thane Edric","'Well then, welcome to Entwade, traveller. I have little time to spend chatting with one so ill-acquainted with the troubles of Rohan. The King has ridden west and left me many problems and not enough men to handle them. Be him renewed or not, my people have still been forgotten.\
\
'Look to my side, traveller. My wife, Léoflad, struggles to make ready to evacuate my people to Aldburg. Such a task would be difficult even if the Uruks were not riding our plains, but such things are commonplace under Théoden King.\
\
'Let me speak no more of him, for my wife thinks such things bode ill for my temper. If you would help us prepare, we would be grateful for your aid, though I know not how much I can repay you in these dire times.'","DNT -- Will not be seen","In the King's Wake","Aid Thane Edric and Léoflad in their preparations (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. With these threats identified, and my people prepared for the journey, they can set off.\
\
'You have saved me a great deal of time, and provided my people the safe passage they so dearly needed. Their journey will take some time, but they will find the surest of safety within Aldburg.\
\
'As for those threats to the north and south, I have much more to ask of you before I say my farewells to my wife and people, so do not wander yet, friend.'","Aided Thane Edric and Léoflad in their preparations (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Thane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade near the waggons.\
\
You have aided the people of Entwade greatly, and should now speak to Thane Edric of what is to be done next."},
[6618]={"Lianas resistentes del Bosque Viejo recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega las lianas resistentes a Buckley Sheppard","Recolecta lianas resistentes del Bosque Viejo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las raíces pueden encontrarse por todo el Bosque Viejo, en los tramos orientales al norte y al sur del campamento de Adso. Buckley Sheppard está en el campamento de Adso, junto al Gran Camino del Este.\
\
Buckley Sheppard te ha ofrecido pagarte por encontrar lianas resistentes de las raíces en el Bosque Viejo. Las lianas se usarán para fabricar ataduras resistentes en lugar de clavos.","'¡Buen trabajo! Estas servirán exactamente como esperaba. Podemos usarlas para amarrar las vigas que necesitamos mientras este lugar se mantenga en pie.\
\
'Gracias por tu esfuerzo.'","A la sombra de gigantes","Buckley Sheppard cree que las raíces de los árboles en el Bosque Viejo son lo bastante fuertes como para atar grandes secciones de madera.","'Fortalece tu corazón y enfrenta tus temores. Hay monedas que ganar si regresas con el tesoro que busco en el Bosque Viejo.'","'Los clavos escasean... sí, ¡los bandidos incluso se llevaron nuestros clavos! ¿Puedes imaginarlo? Ladrones de una clase distinta a la que haya visto jamás. No debemos preocuparnos por los clavos, sin embargo, y con el precio del hierro como está, he ideado una mejor solución para el problema de construir la posada de Adso. El único inconveniente es que la solución se encuentra al sur, dentro del Bosque Viejo.\
\
'A la sombra de los árboles gigantes, allí encontrarás raíces. Enormes zarcillos que emergen de la tierra con la fuerza de los siglos. Si conseguimos lianas resistentes de esas raíces, podremos fabricar ataduras para unir nuestras vigas y reservar los clavos restantes para todo lo demás que necesitamos construir.\
\
'¿Qué dices? ¿Tienes el valor para enfrentar ese lugar oscuro y sombrío y recoger algunas lianas para hacer las ataduras?'"},
[6619]={"'Despite my efforts to rout them after the War, Orcs hide yet in the vales of the Emyn-nu-Fuin.\
\
'We must defeat them and drive them from Eryn Lasgalen if the taint of Mirkwood is ever to heal.'","Defeat Orc-kind in Eryn Lasgalen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated many Orcs in Eryn Lasgalen and have assisted the Elves in their efforts to restore the forest.","Defeated Orc-kind in Eryn Lasgalen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated many Orc-kind in Eryn Lasgalen.","The Orcs who escaped the Battle Under the Trees now hide in the vicinity of the Emyn-nu-Fuin.","Completado","In the Shadow of the Emyn-nu-Fuin","Orcs can be found scattered throughout Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
King Thranduil has bade you defeat any Orc-kind you come across."},
[6620]={"Andreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp.\
\
Andreg has asked you to help him face the evils at the Slade of Shadows.","Complete Baa, Baa, Black Sheep","Complete Spirits of Dunland","'I thank you again for coming, ${PLAYER}. When I found the Slade of Shadows, I did not expect it to be so utterly inhabited by evils from the ancient world. I avoided detection for a short time, but I did not wish to risk betraying our presence here to the Enemy.\
\
'It may be, though, that one such as yourself, with no true tie to the Dúnedain, might be able to confront the foe without breaking the secrecy of the Grey Company.\
\
'Will you lend me your aid?'","Complete Dimming the Lights","The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.","Andreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp.\
\
You should return to Andreg with news of your successes.","Talk to Andreg near the Slade of Shadows","Complete Mystery of the Trees","'With what you discovered in the Slade of Shadows, I think I know how to ensnare Gwyllion. We shall be revealed, but I think the risk is worth the gain.'","In the Shadow of the Mountain"},
[6621]={"'Greetings. You are looking for Frithstan, friend? Then you are not alone.\
\
'Penda is my name, and Frithstan is my sergeant. This is where last I saw him, at his camp in the shadows of the Cuthstan.'","A camp of Rohirrim located north of the Cuthstan has missed delivering a report to the soldiers of Stangard. Byrnstan wishes to check on the camp's leader and ensure that all is well.","The camp appears deserted, except for one man","Penda may be found in the Rohirrim-camp along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard.\
\
Penda seems to be the only man left at Frithstan's camp.","In the Shadow of the Stone","'Frithstan's camp is west of Stangard. When you see the fork, bear north and keep the Cuthstan to your left.\
\
'Frithstan and his men should be stationed on guard along the road.'","Visit the Rohirrim-camp along the northern base of the Cuthstan","The Rohirrim-camp may be found along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard.\
\
Byrnstan has asked you to visit Frithstan and ask about the delay in his report to Stangard.","'Early is the hour in which you return to Stangard. I welcome your presence here, as does Gadda, but there are further matters which need attention in the Wailing Hills. North of the Cuthstan, along the road to the west, lies a small camp of riders led by a man named Frithstan. Their position in the shadow of the Stone allows them to keep watch over the western roads out of Stangard, while remaining secluded from the eyes of Hill-orcs.\
\
'On occasion, Frithstan sends a patrol to Stangard with reports of any enemy activity in the west. A message was expected days ago, yet still we have received no word. After your most recent discovery, I take this as a cause for concern.\
\
'Head west out of Stangard and take the road north as it forks. Seek out Frithstan at his camp and discover the cause for the absence of tidings.'","Talk to Penda about Frithstan's location"},
[6622]={"Complete 'The Scourge's Captains'","Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
You have done much to rout the remnants of the Heirs of Castamir in the Sail-haven. You should talk to Eshmun.","'When I was made Captain of the Haven, Tumúldo said it had to be me—Kindred of the Coins or not, he knew I could keep watch on the Sail-haven. Like it was with poor Râmax, I have known Tumúldo since he was a boy, and though our friendship has been a complicated one at times, we have grown to trust each other without question.\
\
'Before Tumúldo departed on his voyage, he told me to do whatever I must to protect Umbar Baharbêl and its people from those who still put their faith in Balakhôr the Scourge. While these Heirsworn may not fly the black sails of old, they are still at war—only instead of with Gondor, who was too mighty for them to overcome, they have turned their hatred upon their own. I have seen Umbar changed again and again through turmoil in the course of my life, but we have never been so close to true freedom. The Heirsworn cling to the past, and their grip loosens with each passing day, but how many more must be injured—or killed—before they are finally only a memory? I say none! We shall pry each of their fingers loose until their grip is broken, and when that is done, Umbar Baharbêl shall truly be a Free City!\
\
'You are a hale adventurer, and though I do not know your journey, I know that you share my hatred of those who call themselves the Heirs of Castamir. Let us work together and put an end to them, once and for all!'","In the Shadows of Black Sails","'You have done very well, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'When Tumúldo returns from his voyage, I ought to introduce him to the ${CLASS} who drove out the last of the Scourge's Men in the Sail-haven!'","Complete 'Stealing From Their Own'","In the wake of a brazen murder committed by the Heirsworn, Eshmun, the Captain of the Haven, intends to deliver swift and terrible retribution upon those still loyal to the Heirs of Castamir in Umbar Baharbêl.","Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, has asked for your aid in ridding Umbar Baharbêl of those still loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir.","Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower","Complete 'Heirs To Naught'"},
[6623]={"Habla con Mara Arenales","'¡Bienvenido a Risco Nevado, amigo mío!\
\
'Si has venido por el Festival de Yule, te recomiendo que te contagies del espíritu de la estación y participes en muchas de nuestras divertidas actividades de Yule. Y si no has venido por el Festival de Yule… ¡quizá deberías hacerlo!\
\
'Para quienes participen en muchas de nuestras actividades festivas, puede que haya preparada alguna que otra recompensa de Yule, ¡así que anímate!\
\
'Hace un poco de frío, pero estoy seguro de que encontrarás cálida compañía por todas partes!'","Mara Arenales está emocionada de dar la bienvenida a los visitantes a Rivegel y los anima a participar en todas las actividades del festival.","'¡Vaya, eres una persona festiva! ¡Espero que te estés divirtiendo en el Festival de Yule!\
\
'Parece apropiado en esta temporada de dar que deberías tener un regalo, ¡así que aquí lo tienes!'\
\
'¡Vuelve mañana y tendré más regalos para ti!'","'Cada día hay algo que hacer en Barranca Escarchada. ¡Cada día es Yule! ¡Ven y únete a todos en Barranca Escarchada y participa en muchas actividades del Festival de Yule!'","Participaste en actividades del Festival de Yule en Barranca Escarchada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En el espíritu de Yule","Mara Arenales desea agradecerte por tu participación en el Festival de Yule hoy.","Participa en actividades del Festival de Yule en Barranca Escarchada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6624]={"Habla con Mara Arenales","Mara Arenales está emocionada de dar la bienvenida a los visitantes a Barranca Escarchada y los anima a participar en todo tipo de actividades durante el festival.'","'Cada día hay algo que hacer en Barranca Escarchada. ¡Cada día es Yule! ¡Ven y únete a todos en Barranca Escarchada y participa en muchas actividades del Festival de Yule!'","'¡Vaya, eres una persona festiva! ¡Espero que te estés divirtiendo en el Festival de Yule!\
\
'Parece apropiado en esta temporada de dar que deberías tener un regalo, ¡así que aquí lo tienes!'\
\
'¡Vuelve mañana y tendré más regalos para ti!'","'¡Hay mucho que hacer en Barranca Escarchada! Explora la ciudad y muestra tu espíritu navideño!\
\
'¡Hace un poco de frío, pero estoy seguro de que encontrarás buena compañía por todas partes!'","Participaste en actividades del Festival de Yule en Barranca Escarchada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En el espíritu de Yule","Mara Arenales desea agradecerte por tu participación en el Festival de Yule hoy.","Participa en actividades del Festival de Yule en Barranca Escarchada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6625]={"'The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.'","You found nothing of note here","The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angened, leading eastwards. The first patrol point lies to the north-west of Amon Angened, upon the road.\
\
Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.","Dannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.\
\
You should report back to Dannaswen at once.","You have found nothing of note here","In the Wake of the Golden Host","You have discovered an enemy patrol","You have found the enemy encampment at the Gostannon","'Then the scouts reports were accurate? This will make our task much easier.'","Patrol the road to the Gostannon","The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.\
\
Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.","'As you know, Falasgon sent word of another Orc-encampment near the Gostannon to the north. From what the scouts reported, the presence of the Enemy has been nearly wiped out at that camp, but we must be certain before devoting resources to destroy it.\
\
'I would ask you a favour, ${PLAYER}: patrol the lands to the north, especially along the road leading to the Gostannon, to determine the strength of the foe.\
\
'When you have completed your patrol, return here.'","The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continued presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.","Talk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened"},
[6626]={"'Do you have it? The dragon-stone?'\
\
You produce a small fragment of dragon-stone and show it to Zádokh Flint-eye. His eyes widen in awe.\
\
'I did not even believe it to be true! It is beautiful!'\
\
Zádokh Flint-eye pockets the dragon-stone fragment and appears to collect himself.\
\
'You have done as I asked, and I am nothing if not a dwarf of my word. The Longbeards have gone to Brúgrad, but they do not name it as we do. It is known to them as Tharrazhâr, and to those who speak in the Common Tongue: Skarháld.\
\
'If they have remained there, they will not be as welcome as they may think. The great warriors of my people have travelled for many miles, and they are not eager to share in the lost wealth of the Grey Mountains.\
\
'That is all I have to tell. Leave me to my gold!'","Dôm Goru can be found somewhere to the north-west of Furuk-mekhem, the Southgate.\
\
After learning that the Zhélruka have a small encampment named Dôm Goru in the eastern hills of the Ered Mithrin, Dori has asked you to ride ahead of the Company and learn if they know anything of Nori's expedition.","Bags of gold coins can be purchased at a Vault-keeper.\
\
In exchange for information, Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to give him ten gold coins.","'Ah, what brings a ${RACE} like you so far into the Grey Mountains?'\
\
You explain to Zádokh Flint-eye that you seek a company of Longbeards that passed through the Grey Mountains and that you have also come in search of the remains of the cold-drake, Vethúg Wintermind.\
\
'Zádokh Flint-eye is my name, and if you are in search of something, I will know where to find it. Indeed, the fates of those Longbeards and the cold-drake are known to me, but information of that sort is valuable... very valuable.\
\
'I will offer it to you... for a price. The worms, drakes, and Dragons of the Grey Mountains have slowed my journey. If you were to remove some of them from my path, I could be convinced to share what I know.\
\
'Do we have a deal?'","In the Way of Dwarves","Defeated drakes and worms in the Grey Mountains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You discover a small deposit of black rock...","Collect a fragment of dragon-stone","You discover a small encampment of Zhélruka just off the road into the Ered Mithrin...","'Drakes and worms? I think you misheard me, ${RACE}.\
\
'I asked you to defeat dragons... not their feeble offspring! Do you expect me to part with any worthwhile information, and information about Longbeards no less, for such a pittance?\
\
'You would have saved the both of us time if you had just handed me a bag of gold. In fact, why don't you do that?\
\
'Ten gold coins, and I'll tell you what I know. It is a fair price for such knowledge!'","Find a deposit of dragon-stone in the Bitter Scar","Find Dôm Goru","Zádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru.\
\
You have collected a small fragment of dragon-stone as Zádokh Flint-eye asked, and you should now deliver it to him at Dôm Goru and learn what else he knows of recent happenings in the Grey Mountains.","Learn if the Zhélruka at Dôm Goru encountered Nori's expedition","Deliver the bag of gold coins to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru","Talk to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru","You place a share of your gold into a small pouch and it jingles softly...","Desperate to learn more of Nori's passage into the Ered Mithrin, Dori hopes to parley with the Zhélruka that have come seeking their ancestral home of Dómekh.","Deliver the fragment of dragon-stone to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru","Defeat drakes and worms in the Grey Mountains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dragon-stone could once be found in the depths of the Ered Mithrin and near to the lairs of dragons, but it might also be found among the Bitter Scar.\
\
Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to find a deposit of dragon-stone in the Bitter Scar and bring a fragment of it to him.","Dori can be found at Dôm Goru.\
\
After returning to Zádokh Flint-eye with the dragon-stone you discovered, he informed you that Dori and Company have come to Dôm Goru. You should speak to Dori and tell him what you have learned.","A small deposit of dragon-stone can be found in the southernmost reaches of the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have discovered a deposit of dragon-stone and should now mine it for Zádokh Flint-eye.","Talk to Dori at Dôm Goru","Obtain a bag of gold coins","The dragon-stone appears to be a sort of hardened, shimmering coal...","Zádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru in the Ered Mithrin.\
\
You have defeated many drakes and worms as Zádokh Flint-eye asked and should now return to him.","'Very good. \
\
'Listen well, ${RACE}. You'll have to scrounge around for ten more gold coins if you want me to repeat myself.\
\
'You spoke of the cold-drake known to the Longbeards as Vethúg Wintermind. I know where he has gone! Such was the weight of his fall into the Grey Mountains that the ground was torn asunder. He fell broken into the foothills of Winterstith and left the Bitter Scar in his wake. Neither the Zhélruka nor the Longbeards knew such a ruin in the earlier years of the Grey Mountains, but it is here now, I assure you.\
\
'Ah, and if you wish to learn the destination of your Longbeard friends, you'll see it soon enough.\
\
'Have you heard of dragon-stone? It is normally found deep beneath the earth, but the creation of that black cleft by the Longbeards' cold-drake might have revealed some long-hidden deposits.\
\
'If you find even the smallest fragment of dragon-stone in the Bitter Scar, give it to me and I will tell you where the Longbeards have gone.'","Zádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru in the Ered Mithrin.\
\
You have collected ten gold coins for Zádokh Flint-eye as he asked and should now speak to him.","Dôm Goru can be found to the north-west of Furuk-mekhem, the Southgate in the Ered Mithrin.\
\
You have arrived at Dôm Goru and should now speak to the Zhélruka at the encampment and learn if they encountered Nori's expedition.","Drakes and worms can be found throughout the Ered Mithrin.\
\
In exchange for information, Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to defeat many of the drakes and worms of the Ered Mithrin.","'I had begun to think you continued to Thikil-gundu without us, ${PLAYER}! Did you learn anything of my brother or Vethúg Wintermind?'\
\
You explain that Vethúg Wintermind crashed onto the foothills of the mountain, Winterstith, and left the Bitter Scar in his wake. You also mention that Nori's expedition passed through the old dwarf-hold of Skarháld in the Ered Mithrin.\
\
'Skarháld lies upon the Men Angrún, but the matter of Vethúg Wintermind cannot be put off any longer.'","''There is another matter to discuss, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'While we waited on your return, a small company of Zhélruka passed through the Southgate. They spoke in hushed tones, but I heard enough. It seems they make for a small encampment named Dôm Goru in the foothills of the Ered Mithrin.\
\
'The Zhélruka are not the most cooperative of dwarves, but I have known them to be keen observers. Either this company or their kinsfolk might know of Nori's passage into the Ered Mithrin... or perhaps where Vethúg Wintermind has fallen. Ask what you must, but do not speak of Thikil-gundu. The rightful claim to the Steel Keep is still a matter of contention between our peoples, and it would be unwise to provoke them needlessly.\
\
'It seemed from their tone that they did not intend to remain there long, and so, I must ask you to ride ahead of our company.\
\
'Once we have readied ourselves, we will join you at Dôm Goru.'"},
[6627]={"Collect Múta's weapons at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Collect orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
After being discovered by Dourhands at the Witch-gate, Múta was captured and the rest of her scouts were scattered. You should find Múta.","Múta's weapons can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
Múta has asked you to return her weapons to her before attempting an escape. You should collect Múta's weapons.","Originally intending to join the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach, Múta and her scouts quickly became separated after being ambushed by Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.","Dourhands can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
In preparation for her escape, Múta has asked you to collect orders from the Dourhands at the Witch-gate. You should defeat the Dourhands and collect their orders.","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have recovered Múta's weapons. You should deliver them to Múta.","You discover Múta locked in a cage within the Dourhands' encampment at the Witch-gate","Deliver the orders to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","Talk to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","'${PLAYER}! What are you doing here?!'\
\
Múta's voice shrinks to a gruff whisper.\
\
'I didn't expect for help to be sent so soon, but given the circumstances, I'm more than happy to be wrong! When the Dourhands ambushed us, I saw Kársa and Uzvát escape to the east. But have you seen Gárjan?'\
\
You tell Múta that Gárjan escaped and that he now intends to warn Ausma and Lord Glóin of the danger beyond the Witch-gate.\
\
'It seems our efforts to foil the Iron Crown in Elderslade did not go as unnoticed as we hoped. After the Dourhands threw me in this cage, I overheard them mumbling about new orders from Brathar. Unfortunately, they were wise enough to continue their conversations where I couldn't eavesdrop on them.\
\
'Why don't you see if some of them have been foolish enough to keep their orders on hand? I'll keep trying to free myself in the meantime!'","'Before we set out, Múta warned us that some new purpose has kindled the spirits of the Dourhands and that they serve one of their own sworn to the Iron Crown: Brathar Crack-helm. We made every preparation... or so we thought.\
\
'No sooner had we passed through the Witch-gate than we were caught in a trap! Múta was captured by the Dourhands, but I do not know what has become of Kársa or Uzvát. Alas, ${PLAYER}, I'm in no condition to mount a rescue.'\
\
'I'm afraid you will have to manage that, my friend.'\
\
As Gárjan braces his leg, you notice a lengthy gash in the armour covering his thigh.\
\
'Bah, it looks worse than it is! At the very least, I can make it back to Bárgstad on my own to tell Ausma what has happened.\
\
'Do not let these Dourhands get the last laugh, ${PLAYER}. Múta must be freed before it is too late!'","Deliver the weapons to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have collected orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should deliver them to Múta.","Collected orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Did you find anything?'\
\
You hand the orders to Múta. As she reads them, her eyebrows raise and lower a few times. After a moment, she scoffs.\
\
'Bah! If these orders are to be believed, we and the Zhélruka have our work cut out for us. From what I can tell, the Iron Crown, as well as their Dourhand and Hill-men allies, now serve one named High Priestess Ásachal. I cannot be certain of it, but I would not doubt she is a descendant of the corrupt Men of Westernesse! It seems the Iron Crown has laid claim to that fortress across the valley—the Drearspire, they call it. It is said they seek something called \\qCrûn Nasgadh\\q, but I cannot glean anything else about it from these orders. Is it some sort of artifact? A spell of old Angmar? Whatever it is, I'm certain it won't be good for us or the Gabil'akkâ if they find it!\
\
'Things are more urgent than they seemed, ${PLAYER}. Will you fetch me my weapons? The Dourhands took them and set them on a table over there—just out of my reach. I've an idea on how to escape from this cage, but I'd feel a lot better about it if I wasn't unarmed.'","Múta's dagger is stained black, perhaps from a crude dye or Orkish blood","'You have them? Give them here, my friend!'\
\
As Múta examines her axe and dagger, a smile forms at the corner of her mouth.\
\
'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. It'll be time to put them to use soon enough!'","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
Múta has been captured and imprisoned by the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should talk to Múta.","Múta's axe is of a simple design, but it has clearly seen much use","Find Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","In the Wind"},
[6628]={"'Muchas gracias. Tengo claro que esto ayudará a que los pobres espíritus puedan descansar.'","Nan Mabli te ha pedido que quemes incienso en las los túmulos en las Quebradas del Sur.\
\
Los túmulos se encuentran en Gond Orchal, en las Quebradas del Sur.","Incienso quemado en los túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vuelve con Nan Mabli","Deberías informar a Nan Mabli de que has quemado incienso en los túmulos.\
\\Nan Mabli está en las Quebradas del Sur.","Incienso para los atormentados","Quema incienso en los túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Algo ha removido los huesos de los muertos en los túmulos de las Quebradas del Sur.","'Saludos, joven ${CLASS}. Soy Mabli, aunque la gente me llama Nan Mabli. Me pregunto si puedes ayudarme. Cada año, por estas fechas, tenemos la tradición en mi familia de venir y quemar incienso en las tumbas para calmar a los espíritus. Sin embargo, ¡este año los espíritus están furiosos!\
\
'No soy rival para su ira, pero quizá alguien con tus habilidades puede llegar donde una anciana no puede. ¿Podrías quemar el incienso por mí en sus tumbas?''","'Nunca he visto a los espíritus tan inquietos. Espero que podamos ayudarles a descansar en paz.'"},
[6629]={"You have defeated the Orcs in the hills of Duskenvale.\
\
You should return to Lúfred at the Beorning Watchpost to inform him.","Talk to Lúfred","Orcs have been troubling the road between the Gladden Fields and Duskenvale, preventing trade and travel. The trader Lúfred has asked you to take care of the issue.","Defeated Orcs in Brafulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lúfred has asked you to stop the Orc activity in Duskenvale so trade can resume.\
\
You should find the Orc camp in the hills in Duskenvale.","This appears to be the source of the Orc ambushers","You inform Lúfred that the Orcs have been defeated.\
\
'Wonderful! I cannot thank you enough, ${PLAYER}. A trader is nothing if he cannot freely trade!\
\
'Now I have to convince these stubborn Beornings that the road can be opened again!'","Defeated Captain Ugúrz","Find the Orc camp of Brafulug","Inconvenient Orcs","Defeat Orcs in Brafulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have discovered a camp of Orcs in northern Duskenvale.\
\
You should defeat the Orcs and their leader in Brafulug.","'The Beornings tell me that I can't deliver these goods because of Orc activity, but they also will not do anything about it! Why? Because then the post would be undermanned! You look to be skilled in combat, ${CLASS}. Would you please do something about these Orcs? I will pay you, of course!'","Defeat Captain Ugúrz"},
[6630]={"Al entrar en las Profundidades Llameantes desde las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, escuchaste un ruido que provenía de la esquina de la derecha.","¡El calor proviene de las profundidades llameantes! Espera, ¿qué es ese ruido que viene de detrás de la esquina de la derecha?","Los gredbyg solían estar confinados en los límites de esta caverna, pero la colmena ha crecido enormemente hasta alcanzar el impresionante tamaño que ves hoy en día. Debe de haber una fuente de calor cerca que ayude a los gredbyg a desarrollar sus larvas y capullos tan rápido.","¿Es un enano herido el que está ahí delante?","Encuentra la fuente de calor que sustenta a la colmena de gredbyg","Incubación en las Profundidades Llameantes","Has encontrado la fuente de calor que sustenta a la colmena de gredbyg y, por desgracia, no hay nada que se pueda hacer para detenerla. La colmena se ha construido en el lugar perfecto de Moria para aprovechar el calor natural que generan las minas.","El calor proviene de los charcos de aceite hirviendo y de los pozos de lava de las Profundidades Llameantes. No hay nada que se pueda hacer para impedir que sustente a la colonia de gredbyg a incubar sus larvas...\
\
Pero parece que hay un enano herido escondido entre las rocas. Deberías ver si necesita ayuda.","'¡Las formaciones de colmenas de esta caverna nunca habían sido tan grandes, y deben de estar incubando una inmensa población de gredbyg! Siempre han vivido en los recovecos de aquí, pero últimamente su crecimiento se ha disparado. ¡Desde aquí se puede ver que el techo y las paredes están cubiertos de capullos y larvas! Debe de haber una fuente de calor que ayude a incubar todos esos huevos tan rápidamente.\
\
'¿Quizás podrías buscar esa fuente de calor? Si averiguamos de dónde viene, tal vez podamos hacer algo al respecto.'","Comprueba el ruido que hay a la vuelta de la esquina a la derecha","Buscas la fuente de calor que ayuda a la colmena de gredbyg a incubar sus larvas tan rápidamente. Es probable que se encuentre en el extremo más alejado de la colmena."},
[6631]={"Glóin examinó el conjunto de órdenes recuperadas de los uruks en la Ciudad de los Trasgos y descubrió que también estaban escritas en la Lengua Negra.","Indescifrable","'Rápido, muestra esas órdenes al maestro Elrond en Rivendel. ¡No tenemos mucho tiempo!'","'Nunca deberías ver esto.'","Elrond está en la Última Morada en Rivendel, al suroeste del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Glóin se dio cuenta de que otro conjunto de órdenes escritas en Lengua Negra tardaría demasiado en traducirse y te envió a Rivendel para hablar directamente con Elrond.","'No tenemos tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}. Lleva esto directamente al maestro Elrond en Rivendel y ruégale que lo traduzca. Ya hemos tardado demasiado.\
\
'Es vital que sepamos qué están tramando los uruks. Si logran reunir a los trasgos de las Montañas Nubladas, ¿quién sabe qué fuerza podríamos tener enfrente?\
\
'Rápido. Rivendel queda al suroeste, por si aún no lo sabías.'","Muestra las órdenes a Elrond en Rivendel","'Nunca deberías ver este texto.'","'Regresa con Glóin rápidamente. Debe ser advertido de inmediato.'","'El maestro Glóin hizo bien en enviarte a mí. Parece que sus temores respecto a los trasgos eran ciertos. Debo admitir que me apena decirlo, pero parece que un nuevo líder trasgo ha surgido en los recovecos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos. Este nuevo Gran Trasgo ha unido a los trasgos allí dentro y ya desafía al emisario enviado desde el norte.\
\
'Hay que informar a Glóin de que el emisario del norte tiene órdenes de obligar a los trasgos a atender el llamado de Angmar. Adviértele y dile que sea cauteloso.\
\
'Devuélvele estas órdenes y pídele que lea mis palabras.'","'¿El Gran Trasgo? ¡Pero esto no puede ser! Gandalf abatió al Gran Trasgo con Glamdring. Otro trasgo ha debido ocupar su lugar, estoy seguro. Esta noticia es sumamente inquietante.'","Glóin está en su campamento, justo fuera de la Ciudad de los Trasgos, al noreste de Rivendel.\
\
Elrond Medio-Elfo hizo anotaciones en las órdenes y te advirtió de que los trasgos tenían un nuevo líder, un Gran Trasgo que desafiaba la intromisión de los uruks en la Ciudad de los Trasgos. Te envió de vuelta con Glóin junto con las órdenes traducidas.","Entrega las órdenes a Glóin en su campamento en las Montañas Nubladas","Elrond te ha devuelto las órdenes"},
[6632]={"Much of Lossarnach's farmland is burned and the first planting has been missed. Indir fears that if the Haradrim discover Arnach's grain supplies, no victory will forestall thin crops and starvation in seasons to come.","'Though Dagor might care little, I for one will sleep easier knowing we might eat in nine months' time, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping us in these dire times. I know we are one among many needing help from heroes like you.'","Lossarnach's seed stores can be found in the farms north-east of Arnach.\
\
You should travel to the remaining farms to the north-east and do what you can to hide and protect the seed stores there.","Defeated a Haradrim Raider (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hide the seed stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'These times of war have thwarted spring planting, ${CLASS}. The Haradrim have put some of our farmland to the torch, and in the rest our seed stores lie exposed and vulnerable.\
\
'Even if Dagor's grand war-plans defend us from the Haradrim here, we may yet starve in the coming winter. Already we have missed first planting. We face hard times at our most fortunate!\
\
'Good ${CLASS}, will you visit the farms to Arnach's north-east and defend its stores of seed?'","Indir: Close Their Eyes","Defeat Haradrim Raiders near the farms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Indir can be found in Arnach, near the keep.\
\
You should return to Indir and tell him that the remaining seed stores have been safely hidden from the foe.","Talk to Indir","Concealed seed store  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6633]={"War-horns can be found in the Haradrim camps south and east of Arnach.\
\
Indir's men have seen great warhorns in the Haradrim camps. He believes that if you sabotaged the horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized.","Indir: Cover Their Ears","Sabotaged a war-horn  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Indir seeks to further disorganize the Haradrim by sabotaging their war-horns.","Indir can be found in Arnach, near the keep.\
\
Indir believes that if you sabotaged the Haradrim's war-horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized. You should return to him and tell him this has been done.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have brought peace to my troubled heart by shattering those war-horns. Let us hope my dream of them saw true.'","'There is no doubt in my heart: the Haradrim will launch an assault on Arnach. I lay awake at night, imagining how it will go, and last night I dreamt they came with a great blowing of horns. Imagine my surprise when one of my most keen-eyed men told me he had seen great war-horns among the Southron camps!\
\
'Would you humour my whim, ${RACE}? You seem intrepid enough to do the deed. I believe they intend to use these war-horns to call the attack. If the horns were sabotaged, they may be unable to assail us in one overwhelming force. And perhaps, just perhaps, we might withstand them!'","War-horns sabotaged (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Indir"},
[6635]={"Lleva las muestras a Glorelloth en el Refugio Sombrío.","Muestras de kergrim infectadas","Piel espinosa recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Skûmfil no es más que un vertedero, un lugar donde se arrojan a los orcos muertos de Moria cuando empiezan a apestar. Es allí donde dos enemigos se han reunido, cada uno con la intención de usar los cadáveres para sus propios fines. Los kergrim y otros carroñeros los utilizan como fuente de alimento, y los insectos, como lugar para poner sus huevos y engendrar futuras generaciones.","'Llevará algún tiempo examinar estas muestras y determinar si la plaga es la misma o diferente a la que portan los kergrim. Le diré a Throstur que has hecho lo que te pedí.\
\
'Gracias, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'","'Los kergrim están repletos de enfermedades, eso es cierto, pero no estoy seguro de que sean los responsables de la plaga que afecta a los orcos. Sin embargo, es posible que lo sean, por lo que te pido que recojas muestras de los kergrim y sus congéneres en Skûmfil.\
\
'Encontrarás el lugar al sureste del Refugio Sombrío. Toma pequeñas tiras de su piel y tráemelas para que pueda determinar mejor si los kergrim están infectados con el mismo tipo de enfermedad que azota a los orcos.'","Skûmfil se encuentra al sureste del Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Glorelloth quiere asegurarse de que los kergrim no son los responsables de la enfermedad que afecta a los orcos de la oscuridad sombría, por lo que te ha enviado a recoger muestras de la piel de los kergrim.","Recolecta piel espinosa (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Recoge tiras de la piel de los kergrim y tráemelas. Encontrarás a los kergrim en Skûmfil, al sureste del Refugio Sombrío. El lugar está lleno de cadáveres de orcos muertos, pero si la enfermedad sigue presente en los kergrim, quizá los orcos la estén contrayendo cuando llevan los cuerpos a la fosa.'"},
[6637]={"'Espero poder evaluar la enfermedad que se extiende entre los orcos de la Sala Decimosexta, pero no me atrevo a entrar yo solo, pues no soy un guerrero.\
\
'Si estás dispuesto, solicito tu ayuda. Reúne numerosas muestras de tejido de los orcos para determinar cuán potente es la enfermedad y si puede transmitirse a otros.\
\
'No será una tarea fácil; debes procurar no permitir que los orcos infectados entren en contacto cercano contigo, pues podrían ser contagiosos. Encontrarás la Sala Decimosexta al noreste del Refugio Sombrío. Recoge las muestras y tráemelas cuando hayas terminado.'","Fragmentos de carne infectada recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge fragmentos de carne infectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Devuelve las muestras a Pentlenn en el Refugio Sombrío","Muestras infectadas","La Sala Decimosexta es una zona infestada de orcos, muchos de los cuales padecen una terrible enfermedad que provoca crecimientos similares a hongos en sus cuerpos.\
\
Mallas, un elfo aliado de los enanos, cree que hay algo oculto bajo la Sala Decimosexta y desea descubrir el verdadero propósito y el origen de la plaga.","La Sala Decimosexta se encuentra al noreste del Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Deberías recoger muestras de los orcos derrotados en la Sala Decimosexta para permitir que Pentlenn observe el comportamiento de esta enfermedad. Te ha aconsejado que hagas todo lo posible por evitar infectarte tú ${PLAYERNAME:mismo[m]|misma[f]}.","'Necesitaré tiempo para estudiar estas muestras, pero hasta ahora me has servido bien. Me aseguraré de contarle a Mallas lo que has hecho por mí.\
\
'Te doy las gracias, ${RACE}, y me alegra verte sano y salvo tras una empresa tan arriesgada.'","'Encontrarás las muestras que necesito en la Sala Decimosexta, al noreste del Refugio Sombrío.'"},
[6639]={"Kúli se encuentra en un campamento lejos hacia el sureste de Guardia Orca, en un pasadizo cavernoso entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo y las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Kúli se alegrará de saber que los chirridos de los gredbyg han sido acallados.","Gredbyg derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Esos incesantes chirridos nunca parecen detenerse. No puedo dormir, no importa cuántas almohadas apile sobre mi cabeza. Por favor, por mi cordura, haz que paren.\
\
'Los gredbyg son muy prolíficos hacia el suroeste de aquí. ¡Destrúyelos! ¡No puedo soportar más ese ruido!'","Los gredbyg pueden encontrarse al suroeste de Guardia Orca.\
\
Kúli te ha pedido que derrotes a los gredbyg que están volviéndolo loco con sus incesantes chirridos.","Los gredbyg del exterior del campamento de Guardia Orca sisean y chasquean durante la noche, impidiendo que los enanos duerman.","'Bendito sea Durin, han sido silenciados. Gracias, esta noche por fin dormiré en paz.'","Habla con Kúli","Derrota a los gredbyg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ese ruido infernal es tan intenso que no puedes ni pensar.'","Chirridos infernales"},
[6640]={"Derrota gredbyg guerreros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El zumbido de miles de gredbyg es suficiente para volver loco a cualquiera. Ese chirrido incesante parece no tener fin. Hay que silenciar todo ese ruido. Los gredbyg más grandes, los guerreros, son los responsables de los chillidos más fuertes.","Gredbyg derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La imponente colmena de gredbyg ocupa todo el pasillo cavernoso que une las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo y las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
El zumbido sigue siendo insoportablemente fuerte en toda la colmena, pero se nota mucho más silencioso en otras partes de Moria.","Los gredbyg de la colmena, situada en el túnel sur de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, chirrían y chillan. El alboroto que hacen se oye a kilómetros de distancia, y es sorprendente que Moria no retumbe con todo ese ruido.","Los gredbyg guerreros se encuentran por toda la colmena, que ocupa el pasillo cavernoso entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo y las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
El zumbido de miles de gredbyg se oye en casi todo Moria, pero es tan constante que la mayoría ni se da cuenta.","Completado","La colmena de gredbyg está más silenciosa, por ahora, y el zumbido que queda es casi... tolerable.","Chirridos infernales"},
[6641]={"Collect fire-pots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected fire-pots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The foolish goblins have left their fire-oil stores out where they can be tampered with...I trust that you will do what needs to be done....'","Thyrnir noticed that the Orcs of Gathbúrz have left their fire-oil supplies haphazardly piled about in the chaos of the Elven assault.","'Hello there, ${PLAYER}. Have you had a look down there in the Orc-camps yet? It's a real mess. Orcs and goblins aren't too good at staying organized when you put a good fright into them, from what I've seen.\
\
'Anyhow, I noticed that they have got the oil for their siege-engines piled up in great heaps of boxes and crates, just lying about. That's dangerous...you never know when it might catch fire!\
\
'If you were to steal a few of their fire-pots and use them to set the rest ablaze, I imagine it would help add a warm glow to these dreary slopes for the evening.'","'Ha! I could see the blazes from here, ${PLAYER}! That will teach the fool goblins to leave dangerous toys lying about! Good work, my friend.'","Burn oil-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Thyrnir at Thangúlhad","Thyrnir at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should report your success to Thyrnir.","YOU SHOULD NOT SEE THIS","Infernal Stores","Fire-pots and supply crates can be found in the Orc-forts throughout northern Gathbúrz.\
\
Thyrnir has asked you to destroy the goblins' stockpiles of fire-oil by igniting them with the goblins' own fire-pots.","Burned oil-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6642]={"'¡Esta situación es repugnante! Es bueno que hayas eliminado a algunos de esos orcos, ${PLAYER}, pero nuestro trabajo está lejos de terminar.'","'¿Has visto a los orcos por aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} ? Repugnantes, ¿verdad?\
\
'Dudo que tales horrores hayan poblado las peores pesadillas de Durin. En su nombre, deshazte de esta infestación.\
\
'Encontrarás muchos de estos orcos infectados al sur, alrededor del campamento que llaman Dalgum-ru.'","Tyki quiere que mates algunos de los orcos infectados de hongos que ha visto por la zona.","Los orcos de la tribu de los Globsnaga se encuentran en Dalgum-ru, al sur del Refugio de las Sombras.\
\
Tyki quiere que mates a los orcos de la tribu de los Globsnaga que hay por la zona.","'¡Están por todas partes! Si tienes problemas para encontrar algunos -- y no sé cómo podrías tenerlos -- puedes mirar hacia el sur, alrededor de Dalgum-ru.'","Tyki se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío, al norte de Dalgum-ru.\
\
Debes regresar a Tyki y informarle que Dalgum-ru está efectivamente infestada de orcos, y que has matado a muchos.","Habla con Tyki en el Refugio Sombrío","Infestation","Orcos Globsnaga derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota orcos Globsnaga (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6644]={"'Hmm... good enough, I think! Just keep your face covered, and let me do the talking. Let us travel to Er Shamol. And watch you do not get too close to the Jangovar outside the village. They are cruel, even to us.'","Tuhâl has fashioned you a disguise!\
\
You should talk to Tuhâl.","'The time has come. I must explain to Lord Náin what is happening in Er Shamol. I know you have no reason to help us, but will you stand by my side, ${PLAYER}? Forgive me for assuming, but you seem to have a kind heart.'","Now that you have a disguise, you need to infiltrate Er Shamol.\
\
You should travel to Utterby with Tuhâl.","Find and free Tuhâl's family","'I told you we are working as fast as we can! Wait... you are not one of them. And who is that with you? Tuhâl? Is that truly you?'","Tuhâl is waiting to speak to Lord Náin on behalf of his people.\
\
Speak with Tuhâl to enter the instance 'Lord of Iron'.","Speak with Tuhâl and enter Instance: The Lord of Iron","Talk to Tuhâl","Kunchat, who oversees the Jangovar's forces, would like to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to Kunchat.","Many Easterlings are occupying this Dalish village, now called Er Shamol","Kunchat, who oversees the Jangovar's operations, will put you to work.\
\
You should talk to Kunchat.","Tuhâl's family is somewhere in Utterby.\
\
You should find and free Tuhâl's family.","'Good work, Chayasír. You have proven yourself a skilled warrior and worthy of our attention. Perhaps one day we will make you a proper Jangovar!'","'Here we are: Er Shamol. It means \\qWindy-home\\q in your tongue. If only it were really a home, and not the work camp it has become.\
\
'We must do as Lord Náin asked, and find a way to undermine the Jangovar from within. I see no other way than to offer ourselves to Kunchat for work, and see what opportunities present themselves. Perhaps if we do well, we can meet their leader, Akh-gulûkh, and discover more of their plans.\
\
'My family is also here somewhere, being forced to work. I must find them and warn them of the dwarf attack, before it is too late.'","Tuhâl has convinced Lord Náin to give him time to evacuate the innocent Easterlings from Utterby.\
\
You should talk to Tuhâl.","Talk to Kunchat","'Tuhâl! We assumed you fell at Hammerstead when you did not return with the rest. Akh-gulûkh will be pleased to hear you survived your first taste of combat. And who is this with you? Fresh meat?'\
\
The man smirks and looks you up and down\
\
'Take ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} to Kúlkhur. He will put ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} to work.'","Tuhâl's family will escape Utterby when they are able","Tuhâl is ready to infiltrate Er Shamol.\
\
You should talk to Tuhâl.","You put on the Easterling clothing with Tuhâl's help","Undermine the Jangovar by completing quests in Utterby","The Dalish village of Utterby is currently under control of the Easterlings, who call it Er Shamol. Soon, the dwarves will be pushed to reclaim this territory for their allies.","Utterby is currently occupied by Jangovar forces.\
\
You should complete quests in Utterby to undermine the Jangovar.","Tuhâl's family will escape Er Shamol when they are able","Travel to Utterby","Infiltrating Er Shamol","'I must do this for my people.'","'How my heart beats within me! Lord Náin truly lives up to his reputation.\
\
'We are going to have to come up with a plan. Many lives weigh on our shoulders now. If you are going to pass as one of my people, you will need a disguise. I have some extra clothes; let us see what I can do.'"},
[6646]={"'Esteldín está oculta en las montañas al norte y al este de Lin Giliath, cerca de la frontera de la Dehesa del Rey y Nan Amlug. Hay que informar a Dagoras del paso de los Nazgûl.'","'Los Dúnedain de Esteldín tienen muchas preocupaciones y son pocos, pero la noticia sobre los Nazgûl es algo que deben saber.'","Informa a Esteldín","'Nos traes noticias funestas, ${PLAYER}, pues ahora sabemos que el Enemigo se mueve tanto en el sur como en el norte.'","Has ayudado a Aglardir a reabastecer Lin Giliath, pero sus preocupaciones aún no se han disipado. La misión original de la compañía de Gildor Inglorion sigue sin cumplirse.","Esteldín está al noreste de Lin Giliath, oculta en las montañas orientales entre la Dehesa del Rey y Nan Amlug.\
\
Aglardir te ha enviado con Dagoras, el capitán de la guardia de Esteldín, para informarle del paso de los Nazgûl.","'Lejos al norte y al este, los Dúnedain del Norte han establecido un campamento oculto al que llaman Esteldín. Estos hombres hacen lo posible por combatir las amenazas en las Quebradas del Norte, pero ahora son muy pocos y los peligros demasiado grandes.\
\
Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ir, quisiera que completes la misión original de nuestra compañía. Ve a Esteldín y habla con el capitán de la guardia, Dagoras. Dile que los Nueve están en movimiento y han cruzado el río. El Enemigo se mueve.\
\
Esteldín está oculta en las montañas, en la frontera de la Dehesa del Rey y Nan Amlug. Este mensaje no debe retrasarse.'","'Los Montaraces de Esteldín tienen mucho que considerar. Gracias por tu rapidez, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Los Nueve están en movimiento, después de todo este tiempo? Son malas noticias, pues solo pueden significar una cosa: se ha encontrado el Anillo del Enemigo.\
\
Solo podemos esperar que el Enemigo no lo haya recuperado ya, o el mundo tal como lo conocemos llegará a su fin. Creo que, si fuera así, nuestro líder, Aragorn, o Elrond el Medio Elfo nos habrían avisado.\
\
Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Entregaré esta noticia a Halbarad, nuestro intendente en ausencia de Aragorn.'","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Nuestra misión era demasiado importante para abandonarla por completo.'"},
[6647]={"'¡No cambiaré una amenaza por un grupo de señores salvajes! ¡Al diablo con los Montaraces!'","Habla con el Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar","'Regresa con Grimbriar a su puesto en la cabaña de piedra, al norte por el Camino Verde, fuera de la Puerta Oeste de Bree, y cuéntale lo que hemos aprendido aquí en Andrath.'","'Hojafrágil y Robledales no son cobardes, pero no puedo seguir su consejo. Los Montaraces son un grupo peligroso e indomable y causan más daño que bien en estas tierras.\
\
'No los invitaré a las Tierras de Bree para que se instalen como nuestros señores en cuanto termine esta crisis. No, debe de haber otra manera.\
\
'He recibido otras noticias desde dentro de los límites de las Tierras de Bree: hay otros ciudadanos que necesitan protección frente a esta amenaza de bandidos. Quiero que los ayudes antes de buscar el yugo de los Montaraces.'","El Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar se encuentra en su puesto fuera de Bree.\
\
Los Vigilantes Hojafrágil y Robledales creen que no se puede contener la marea a punto de estrellarse contra los muros de Andrath. Te han pedido que convenzas al Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar de que debe buscar la ayuda de los Montaraces del Norte.","Informar a Grimbriar","'Mi determinación no flaqueará, pero la razón me pide actuar con rapidez, y así lo haré. Necesito que regreses de inmediato con el Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar. Dile lo que has visto aquí y ruégale que deje de lado su odio hacia los Montaraces. Puede que sean el único aliado en el que las Tierras de Bree puedan apoyarse en estos tiempos oscuros.\
\
'Esta fortaleza está perdida para nosotros, pero Robledales y yo haremos lo que esté a nuestro alcance para evitar que la marea se desborde sobre las Tierras de Bree antes de que los ciudadanos estén preparados. Ve ahora, antes de que estos miserables descubran nuestra posición y provoquen el fin de nuestra resistencia antes incluso de que comience.'","Andrath ha sido invadida y los Vigilantes enviados para evaluar la amenaza creen que no puede recuperarse, a pesar de tus esfuerzos más recientes. De mala gana, has sido enviado de vuelta con el Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar con estas sombrías noticias."},
[6648]={"Deliver the letter to Porókho","'${PLAYER}, have I told you yet that I am grateful to have you as an ally? It means a lot that though you are a newcomer to this city, you take actions that are for the good of the common folk of Umbar. As you well know, I was a newcomer here once as well. It did not take me long to fall in love with the Umbari culture. The resiliency of the people, the bright colours, flavourful food, favourable winds, the blue seas... and of course, my beloved Mêshka, whom I can finally call my wife.\
\
'Whether or not you love this city as I do, I still appreciate what you have been doing for its people, and feel ashamed to have once called you my enemy. You are a good person, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Belondor takes a deep breath as his posture changes and his demeanour returns to that of the Kinsman of the Fleet-fast and Captain of Fleets of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
'Speaking of your quality, I have another thing to ask of you, if you are willing. I am unsure if the kinsmen of Tumúldo Fierce-water are aware of his fate. Tumúldo was the leader of a clan, Morutágya. Smuggling has been the family business for generations. When Nakási returned to the city with a hostage instead of her husband, I don't think she took the time to inform their clan of his murder. Rumours abound, of course, but they are family and deserve to know the truth.\
\
'If you would not mind delivering it, I have written a letter detailing everything I know about Tumúldo's death.'\
\
You confess to Belondor that you were present in Linhir when Tumúldo Fierce-water was murdered. He raises his eyebrows in surprise.\
\
'Is that so? I wouldn't tell them what you have just told me, or you may not walk away from the encounter without bloodshed. I've been told that they have a base of operations in the southern part of the Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven.'","Deliver Belondor's letter to the Morutágya clan, informing them of the demise of their leader, Tumúldo Fierce-water.","'What is this, then? Who are you?'\
\
You inform Porókho that you bring a letter from Belondor, Kinsman of the Fleet-fast, addressed to the Morutágya clan.\
\
He takes the letter from you, reads it, and sighs, handing the letter over to Eshéra.\
\
'So it is true. Tumúldo is dead, and Nakási has fled the city with the Sea-shadow, unlikely to return. Alive, anyway. We had our suspicions.'\
\
The man's attitude quickly changes from sadness to anger.\
\
'Curse all Men of Gondor, including this Belondor! They are as low as the wretched filth in these sewers.'\
\
He spits on the floor to make his point.","Belondor has asked you to deliver a letter to Morutágya, the clan of smugglers that Tumúldo Fierce-water was the leader of, informing them of his death. Morutágya maintains a hideout in the southern part of Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.","Informing the Kin"},
[6651]={"Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Tankho","Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Karishah in Rakhatâb","Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Beliash in Rakhatâb","Karishah did not enjoy the new recipe","'The workers of Rakhatâb are honest and forthright. I will get an honest opinion of this new dish from them. Please take it to them with haste.'","Karishah tears the bready creation in half and takes a large bite.\
\
'This bread is awful! It is bland. No spice, no taste. This is terrible.'\
\
He spits the mouthful on the ground.\
\
'I would not pay for this. Nor would I put in my body for free.'","Keteph wants discerning and brutally honest feedback from the workers of Rakhatâb. He asks that you deliver these free meals to the worker leaders there.","Beliash did not like the new recipe","Hûzo looks at you and cautiously accepts the sack.\
\
'I am wary of those bearing free gifts. Alas, I am hungry, as are many in Rakhatâb. I will indulge you.'\
\
He takes a bite of Keteph's new dish.\
\
'Dry. Drier and drabber than a day along the shore with no water. I will eat it begrudgingly because the crab is delicious.'","Tankho did not like the new recipe","Beliash opens the sack and looks the bready gift over.\
\
'Smells good.'\
\
He takes a bite.\
\
'Oh.'\
\
His face contorts.\
\
'This bread is the worst thing I have ever tasted. It mars the delicious crab and saffron in the dish. This is, perhaps, the worst thing I have eaten in a moon.'","Infusion from the North: A Worker's Honesty","Keteph listens to you explain the harsh reactions of the workers in Rakhatâb. He then nods his head.\
\
'I thought the same when I took a bite after you left. How you northerners use this bread as a means of sustenance is a wonder. It has no taste. Still, I think that I can make a marriage of northern heartiness and the delicacies of Umbar work well together.'","Taphis did not enjoy the meal","Hûzo was not impressed with the recipe","Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Taphis","'To be fair, my friend, I cannot determine if this is good. I need opinions I can trust before I present this to the aristocrats who so desire my dishes.\
\
'The workers of Rakhatâb are honest to a fault. They will not hold back on telling you how bad or good the new dish is. Please bring this new recipe to them, gather their opinions, and then return to me with their feedback.'","'You come bearing a gift, and I will gladly accept.'\
\
He takes a bite of Keteph's recipe.\
\
He chews for a few seconds and swallows.\
\
'Terrible, friend. Truly awful. This is not a gift. It is a curse.'","Keteph desires to hear fair criticism of his new dish. He enlists you to deliver sacks containing his new dish to the expedition leaders outside of Umbar to get their discerning opinions.","You gathered the responses and critiques from the worker leaders in Rakhatâb. Return this information to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.","Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Hûzo","'I will never forgo an offer of a free meal. Especially on the pay that the kindred see fit to offer us here.'\
\
She bites into the bread.\
\
'It is a bit dry. I can taste a hint of saffron. This bread is too porous and flavourless. Still, a free meal is a free meal.'\
\
She bites again.\
\
'I am sorry, I cannot. This is awful.'"},
[6655]={"'Were you able to procure the barley bread from a cook or through trade?'","Collect five loaves of <rgb=#00FF00>Barley Bread</rgb> (${NUMBER}/5)","'Tastes in Umbar are fickle. The aristocracy constantly strives to find something new to tempt their stomachs and tantalize their desires.\
\
'The source of the new flavour typically does not matter. My crab dishes, for example, were a mere play on traditional fare long-served in my hometown of Jax Phanâl.\
\
'I have been thinking. In the north, you have leavened bread. Leavened bread is a treat we do not often see. Yet, I desire to use a taste of the northlands and the standard fare of my home to create a delicacy that will sate the desires of the epicurean elite in Umbar.\
\
'I require bread from the north. I am told there is a grain growing wild and on farms those from the north call barley. We shall begin there. I will require five loaves of barley bread.\
\
'Will you assist me?'","Acquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake barley bread.","Acquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake <rgb=#00FF00>Barley Bread</rgb>.","Keteph asks for your assistance in creating a dish that satisfies the desires of the Epicurean elite in Umbar. He desires a sturdy bread to support his latest creation.","Return the loaves of <rgb=#00FF00>Barley Bread</rgb> to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall","Infusion from the North: The Proper Outer Layer","Collected a loaf of Barley Bread (${NUMBER}/5)","'Most excellent, my friend.'\
\
He sniffs the bread and makes a face.\
\
'Hmm, I expected something... more. This has almost no discernable scent. No matter, it is a taste of the north. Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.'\
\
He beams brightly."},
[6656]={"Collected Keteph's family cruet","Collect Keteph's family cruet","Deliver the cruet to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall","'Oh-ho! You are a dear associate, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'This cruet has been in my family for generations. My grandmother claims it was hers. My father told me it was in our family long before. Losing this would have been a tragedy I could not endure.\
\
'Let me have a moment, yes?'","'The raiding goblins have an encampment far to the south and east of Jax Phanâl in the shadow of the mountains. You will likely find the cruet on one of the tougher goblins in that encampment.'","Collect Keteph's family cruet from Phâredar in Jax Phanâl","'Keteph's cruet, you say?'\
\
She looks uncomfortable for a moment.\
\
'That will be an issue. When Keteph went silent those weeks ago, I thought this would not matter. Now, it seems it does.\
\
'As you know, Jax Phânal endures harassment by the goblins in the south-east. When their leader Shakfût was imprisoned, they raided the outpost under cover of night and stole many treasures.'\
\
She sighs.\
\
'Keteph's cruet was amongst the stolen items. You will need to visit their encampment and collect the cruet from whichever goblin carries it now.'","Return to Jax Phânal and speak with Phâredar to retrieve Keteph's family cruet.","Infusion from the North: The Right Tool","'Return to Jax Phanâl and collect my family's cruet from Phâredar. She will know where to find it. When you have it, return it to me here.'","You recovered Keteph's family cruet from the goblins. Return the cruet to him at Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.","Keteph asked you to further assist him in crafting a special new dish. He needs you to return to Jax Phanâl to retrieve his cruet.","'I am very close to presenting this new recipe to the aristocracy, my friend. However, I require a reminder from home to ensure that the recipe ends with the desired result.\
\
'I left Jax Phânal in such a hurry I forgot to take my grandmother's cruet. It is a precious family heirloom. While I have the one I crafted here, I would prefer to pay homage to my grandmother and use the family cruet for this recipe.\
\
'Return to Phâredar in Jax Phânal. She will know where it is.'","Phâredar told you that Keteph's family cruet was stolen in a raid by goblins. She suggested that you go to the encampment in the south-east to acquire the cruet from the goblins."},
[6658]={"Bebe una cerveza más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Has comenzado la séptima etapa de la iniciación de la Liga de las Posadas","'La siguiente es El Pájaro y el Bebé... ¡vamos!'","¡Se acabó el tiempo!","Bebe tres cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Bebe cervezas (5/6)","'Me alegra verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}.'","Bebe cervezas (0/6)","'¿Demasiado fuerte para ti?'","La posada El Pájaro y el Bebé está al otro lado del camino, al oeste de la Alcaldía.\
\
Ve a la posada El Pájaro y el Bebé en Cavada Grande y habla con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas que se encuentra allí.","Termina antes de que se acabe el tiempo.","'No puedo hablar... solo beber... que alguien pare los giros... duele.'","Bebe cervezas (1/6)","Bebe cervezas (2/6)","'¡Bebe, bebe, bebe por la Liga de las Posadas!'","'Veo que has superado nuestra pequeña prueba, ¿eh?'","Cervezas bebidas (3/6)","'Invítame a una pinta, ¿quieres, ${PLAYER}?'","Bebe cuatro cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Cervezas bebidas (1/6)","Habla con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas en la posada El Pájaro y el Bebé","Liga de las Posadas -- Prueba del Pájaro y el Bebé","'Oh, ¿tienes... problemas... eh? ¿No puedes con tu... cerveza?'","'¡Lo lograste! Has... demostrado ser... ${PLAYERNAME:un valioso[m]|una valiosa[f]} miembro... de la Liga... de Posadas. ¡Disfruta... y diviértete...!'","Cervezas bebidas (6/6)","'¡Bebe, bebe, bebe... por el... festival!'","'Tan cerca, y a la vez... tan lejos...'","Bebe seis cervezas en el tiempo asignado.","Bebe dos cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","${PLAYERNAME:Lleno[m]|Llena[f]} y con náuseas por la bebida, deberías hablar con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas que tienes delante.","Como miembro de la Liga de las Posadas, puedes poner a prueba tu temple periódicamente completando una vez más la prueba de iniciación.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu bitácora de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual. </rgb>","Cervezas bebidas (5/6)","Bebe cervezas (3/6)","Bebe cervezas (4/6)","Bebe cinco cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Cervezas bebidas (2/6)","'Un estómago fuerte y piernas firmes, ¿eh, ${PLAYER}?'","'¿Ya estás ${PLAYERNAME:borracho[m]|borracha[f]}? ¡Ja!'","Cervezas bebidas (4/6)"},
[6659]={"Has comenzado la cuarta etapa de la iniciación de la Liga de las Posadas.","Liga de las Posadas -- Prueba del Tronco Flotante","Bebe una cerveza más dentro del tiempo asignado.","¡Se acabó el tiempo!","Bebe tres cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Bebe cervezas (5/6)","El Tronco Flotante está en Los Ranales, a orillas del Pantano de la Rana, al norte del Camino.\
\
Dirígete al Tronco Flotante en Los Ranales y habla con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas que se encuentra allí.","Bebe cervezas (0/6)","'¡Por fin has llegado! ¡Date prisa! Tienes que beber seis cervezas más antes de que se acabe el tiempo. ¡No hay tiempo que perder, solo tiempo para beber!'","'Oh, vaya, te ves un poco ${PLAYERNAME:acalorado[m]|acalorada[f]}. ¿Te sientes mal?'","'¡Esto es bastante perturbador de ver, te lo aseguro!'","Termina antes de que se acabe el tiempo.","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Todavía te queda bastante camino por recorrer.\
\
'Has completado la cuarta etapa. ¡Solo te quedan tres más si deseas terminar la prueba de la Liga de las Posadas de nuevo! El Dragón Verde está a la vuelta de la esquina, en Delagua. ¡Adelante!'","'¿Ya estás ${PLAYERNAME:borracho[m]|borracha[f]}? ¡Apenas has empezado!'","Bebe cervezas (1/6)","Bebe cervezas (2/6)","'Bien, bien..... casi a mitad de camino.'","Cervezas bebidas (3/6)","Bebe cuatro cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Cervezas bebidas (1/6)","'¡Ya casi terminas! ¡No te molestes en respirar, solo termínala!'","'¡Date prisa y ve a la posada del Tronco Flotante en Los Ranales! Habla con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas que se encuentra allí. ¡Date prisa! El tiempo apremia.'","Habla con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas en El Tronco Flotante","Cervezas bebidas (6/6)","Bebe dos cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Bebe seis cervezas en el tiempo asignado.","${PLAYERNAME:Lleno[m]|Llena[f]} y con náuseas por la bebida, deberías hablar con el miembro de la Liga de las Posadas que tienes delante.","Como miembro de la Liga de las Posadas, puedes poner a prueba tu temple periódicamente completando una vez más la prueba de iniciación.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu bitácora de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual. </rgb>","Cervezas bebidas (5/6)","Bebe cervezas (3/6)","Bebe cervezas (4/6)","Bebe cinco cervezas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Cervezas bebidas (2/6)","Cervezas bebidas (4/6)"},
[6660]={"Bebe una cerveza más dentro del tiempo asignado.","La Perca Dorada está en el centro de Cepeda, en el extremo este del camino de Cepeda.\
