[6673]={"Habla con Umín","Te encuentras dentro de La Posada Abandonada a medianoche. El posadero te ha pedido que investigues el origen de los ruidos que provienen del sótano.","Los clientes ya han empezado a quejarse de los ruidos que se oyen en el sótano. Explora la zona y trata de descubrir el origen de los ruidos.","Explora las profundidades bajo La Posada Abandonada.","La estantería se abre deslizándose para revelar una escalera que desciende hacia la oscuridad.","Has encontrado a un hombre sospechoso leyendo un libro y mirando la puerta decorada con una runa brillante frente a él. ¿Quién es este hombre y qué hace aquí? Será mejor que se lo preguntes.","Habla con el hombre sospechoso","Derrota a Umín","Has descubierto lo que parece ser una cripta. Quizás Umin pueda desvelar este misterio.","La trampa giratoria ha arrancado el collar del cuello de Umín, y ahora yace brillando en el suelo. El propio Umín yace desplomado en el suelo. ¿Por qué te ha atacado?\
\
Habla con él y déjale que te lo explique...","Continúa explorando las cavernas.","Has liberado a Umín del poder del collar","Umín, el hombre que conociste en las cuevas, ha aceptado ayudarte en tu investigación. Debes aprovechar sus conocimientos para explorar las cuevas más a fondo.","Has descubierto la cripta del capitán Rabghul.","Umin ha quedado atrapado en un derrumbe. Debes continuar sin él. Ahora estás ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}, así que mantente siempre alerta.","'Me controlaba... mis pensamientos, mis acciones. Podía ver su propósito. No quiere nada menos que nuestra destrucción total.\
\
'¡Rápido! Debes abandonar este lugar antes de que vuelva. ¡Aún no ha terminado con nosotros! Déjame aquí... Yo fui quien más deseaba el collar, ¡y seré yo quien lo destruya!\
\
'¡No hay tiempo que perder! ¡Cruza hacia el otro lado  y sal por esa cueva!'","Investiga el origen de los ruidos","Los clientes han empezado a quejarse de ruidos en el sótano. Investiga la zona y descubre el origen de los ruidos.","Es Umin. Vivo y en forma... quizá demasiado. Parece que ha adquirido una fuerza casi sobrenatural durante su ausencia. Lleva un collar rojo brillante alrededor del cuello. También está enfadado contigo... Tendrás que derrotarlo si quieres sobrevivir.","Lleva a Umín a la cripta","Un hombre de aspecto sospechoso se encuentra frente a ti.","Sigue adelante a través de las cavernas","La Posada Abandonada: Acertijos en la oscuridad"},
[6674]={"Habla con Umín","Explora las profundidades bajo La Posada Abandonada","Te encuentras dentro de La Posada Abandonada a medianoche. El posadero te ha pedido que investigues el origen de los ruidos que provienen del sótano.","No era Umín quien intentaba matarte. Era el espíritu que habitaba en el collar. Lo controlaba, haciéndole cumplir sus órdenes. Debes destruir al espíritu, no sea que escape de ese lugar y cause estragos en la Tierra Media.","La estantería se abre deslizándose para revelar una escalera que desciende hacia la oscuridad.","Continúa explorando las cavernas","Has encontrado a un hombre sospechoso leyendo un libro y mirando la puerta decorada con una runa brillante frente a él. ¿Quién es este hombre y qué hace aquí? Será mejor que se lo preguntes.","Habla con el hombre sospechoso","Derrota a Umín","Has descubierto lo que parece ser una cripta. Quizás Umin pueda desvelar este misterio.","La trampa giratoria ha arrancado el collar del cuello de Umín, y ahora yace brillando en el suelo. El propio Umín yace desplomado en el suelo. ¿Por qué te ha atacado?\
\
Habla con él y déjale que te lo explique...","La Posada Abandonada: Acertijos en la oscuridad (Nivel 2)","Umin ha quedado atrapado en un derrumbe. Debes continuar sin él. Ahora estás ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}, así que mantente siempre alerta.","Se acabó. El espíritu ha sido derrotado. Habla con Umín y explícale tu victoria.","Has liberado a Umin del poder del collar","Un hombre de aspecto sospechoso se encuentra frente a una puerta brillante marcada con runas.","Investiga el origen de los ruidos","Los clientes han empezado a quejarse de ruidos en el sótano. Investiga la zona y descubre el origen de los ruidos.","Es Umin. Vivo y en forma... quizá demasiado. Parece que ha adquirido una fuerza casi sobrenatural durante su ausencia. Lleva un collar rojo brillante alrededor del cuello. También está enfadado contigo... Tendrás que derrotarlo si quieres sobrevivir.","La estantería ocultaba un pasadizo secreto que conducía bajo la posada. Deberías registrar esa cueva e intentar encontrar el origen de esos ruidos.","Lleva a Umín a la cripta","Has descubierto la cripta del capitán Rabghul","'¿De verdad se ha acabado? Siento todo el dolor que he causado. El collar me cegó incluso antes de verlo... Consumía mis pensamientos y mi vida. Es la razón por la que me embarqué en esta aventura. Ahora que el espíritu ha sido destruido, ya no tiene sentido para mí. ¿Qué voy a hacer ahora?\
\
'Déjame aquí solo con mis pensamientos...'","Destruye el espíritu del collar","'Él... controlaba... mis pensamientos, mis acciones. Podía ver sus intenciones. Solo quería una cosa: aniquilarnos a todos hasta el último.\
\
'¡Rápido! Debes abandonar este lugar antes de que él regrese. ¡No ha terminado con nosotros! Déjame aquí... ¡Yo quería este collar, yo debo destruirlo!\
\
'¡No hay tiempo que perder! ¡Ve al otro lado y sal de esta cueva!'","Sigue adelante a través de las cavernas","Umin, el hombre que conociste en las cuevas, ha aceptado ayudarte en tu investigación. Debes aprovechar sus conocimientos para explorar las cuevas más a fondo.","Abandona el barco"},
[6675]={"'¡Excelente! ¿Me ayudarás? Bien, bien... ah, claro, ¿la cerveza gratis? Una vez que empiece a servirla, el tiempo pasará volando y, antes de que te des cuenta, ¡será medianoche! Solo siéntate y disfruta...'","La Posada Abandonada: Golpe de medianoche","Habla con Anlaf sobre la cerveza gratis","Necesitarás estar lleno de cerveza si quieres pasar el rato.","'Ah, bien... ¡pareces ser de los que les gusta la aventura! Tengo un problema y esperaba que pudieras ayudarme. Parece que algunos clientes se han quejado de unos terribles ruidos que provienen de las paredes y el suelo del sótano. Estoy seguro de que no es nada, pero el negocio no ha ido muy bien últimamente con los rumores de que la posada está embrujada. Ahora bien, yo estoy demasiado ocupado para perder el tiempo con tonterías como esa, pero quizá tú estés interesado en echar un vistazo. Como mínimo, podrías confirmar que se trata solo de un rumor y nada más...\
\
'Sin embargo, debo advertirte que los clientes no suelen empezar a quejarse de los ruidos hasta medianoche, así que probablemente tendrás que quedarte por aquí hasta entonces. ¡Te invitaré a toda la cerveza que puedas beber para ayudarte a pasar el rato!'","Los clientes de La Posada Abandonada se han quejado de unos terribles ruidos que provienen del suelo y las paredes del sótano. El propietario de la posada te ha pedido que esperes hasta medianoche, cuando suelen comenzar las quejas por los ruidos."},
[6676]={"Ivorel, the leader of a scout expedition into the Scuttledells, is concerned about the fate of Hal Tiller, an adventuresome young hobbit who asked to be allowed to aid the Elves on their expedition into Mirkwood. Ivorel fears that the inexperienced hobbit may have been slain by the horrors lurking in the clefts of the Scuttledells.","Search the southern Scuttledells for signs of Hal Tiller.\
\
Ivorel suggested a few places where he might most likely be found as part of the mission he was assigned, but she believes that he is most likely dead.","You can find no sign of Hal Tiller","Search east of the Pool of Tranquility","Search the paths north of the Pool of Tranquility","Innocence in Peril","'I saw several halflings accompanying the band of strangers who came into Lórien these past weeks, and they were taken into the Lady's presence and set, or so I am told, to tasks most dire.\
\
'I had thought that perhaps they held some hidden strength, not apparent to the eye, and so I allowed young Hal to join us when he offered his services.\
\
'Now though I feel sick, as if I had sent a child into battle ahead of me. He must be alive, or I shall never forgive myself.'","Search the barrows north of the Pool of Tranquility","There is no sign that Hal Tiller was ever here","You found a torn and bloodied hobbit-pack","Habla con Ivorel en su campamento","'Greetings, traveller. My name is Ivorel, and I serve at Celeborn's request as the scout-leader for the Malledhrim expedition into Mirkwood. Alas! His trust in me was misplaced, for we have come to ruin here in this twisted place! Few of my scouts have returned at all, but worst of all is the loss of poor Hal Tiller!\
\
'Hal was a young hobbit of an unusually adventurous strain who begged to join us in this expedition. He was also a burglar with an unusually light step -- even for his kind -- and of such earnest heart that I accepted... and in so doing I surely signed the warrant for his death. My fellow scouts were all of fine mettle and experience, and the risks they knew well, but poor Hal was but a child compared to them, and I should never have allowed it.\
\
'I cannot abandon my watch for my duty to the Malledhrim is clear and should any of my scouts yet live they shall come here. Yet you are clearly an adventurer of great mettle to have come this far yourself -- would you help me discover the fate of poor Hal? There must be some trace of him in the Scuttledells....'","Ivorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.\
\
You should return to Ivorel and show her the pack you found.","'What a cruel fate for such a young innocent! These look to be the claw-marks of a Black Dog on the pack -- there is only a spark of hope left, for we have not yet found his body.\
\
'Most likely because he was torn to pieces by the Black Dogs....'"},
[6677]={"Derrota a las moscas-guadaña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar por toda la ciénaga de Meluinen, al sur de Lin Giliath.\
\
Debes reducir la amenaza de las moscas-guadaña de Meluinen, que han sido agitadas por los Trolls de Piedra.","Amenaza Insecto","Las moscas-guadaña en las ciénagas de Meluinen han sido perturbadas por la reciente agresión de los Trolls de Piedra.","Las moscas-guadaña en las ciénagas de Meluinen han sido perturbadas por la reciente agresión de los Trolls de Piedra, creando una amenaza para los Elfos de Lin Giliath.\
\
Debes derrotar moscas-guadaña en Meluinen.","Moscas-guadaña derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Has derrotado varias moscas-guadaña enfurecidas en Meluinen, lo que debería dar a los Elfos de Lin Giliath un pequeño respiro frente a estas criaturas hostiles en el claro."},
[6678]={"Encontraste esta quitina y muchas otras cosas en los insectos que habitan en Skûmfil. Deberías llevársela a alguien que pueda saber más sobre los insectos.","Recogiste este trozo de quitina de Brumbereth, la reina de los gredbyg de Skûmfil.","Entrega la quitina a Mallas en el Refugio Sombrío","Mallas se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Llévale la quitina a Mallas. Quizás él pueda darte alguna explicación sobre por qué hay insectos cerca de los orcos infectados.","'Estos insectos son como los que se han encontrado en otros lugares, según me cuentan los enanos. Es poco probable que sean los portadores de esta enfermedad, pero sin duda utilizan los cuerpos de los muertos como alimento para sus larvas.'","Insectos entre los moribundos"},
[6679]={"The boar's worried eyes are fixed on the baby bear","Ezôti has revealed where he keeps his captive animals. Share this information with Gûshida.\
\
Gûshida is in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Ezôti smiles at you for a little too long, an already uncomfortable pause becoming longer and more awkward with each passing second. Finally he says 'I think I can trust you with a most important task. I have many animals in my care.'\
\
He leans closer to you. His breath smells of good fish and bad milk.\
\
'...Or should I say \\qour\\q care? That is right! I am entrusting you with the care of my animals. Go to where I house my precious friends in the Upper Quarter. Feed and water them.'","Ezôti's captive animals are in poor condition. Gûshida has asked you to help check on them.\
\
Ezôti's hiding place is inside the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Gûshida across the way from Ezôti","Check on the boar","The goat leans into your touch. You sense it has been a long time since it has been treated with compassion","Inside Ezôti's Den","The creature's breathing is laboured","Check on the cave-claw","Meet with Gûshida inside Ezôti's Flat","The bear issues a plaintive cry, causing your companion to wince","Gûshida told you to meet her at Ezôti's hiding place.\
\
Ezôti's hiding place is inside an unassuming flat in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl, to the north-east.","Talk to Gûshida inside Ezôti's Flat","You have inspected the animals and should report back to Gûshida.\
\
Gûshida can be found in Ezôti's hiding place in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","The air is thick with an amalgam of stenches. Gûshida pinches her nose with a thick cloth.\
\
'Quickly! Help me check on them!'","Check on the bear","A strange man puts on a 'show' in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Check on the goat","'This is no natural exhaustion. I suspect Ezôti has given them something to make them sluggish, and less capable of escape. The fiend!'","You share the animals' location with Gûshida.\
\
'Good work! I will tell my associates we are on our way to rescue the animals. I will meet you inside Ezôti's Flat in the Upper Ward, north-east of here.'"},
[6680]={"'This is not good. Look at the gills. They are very different. None of the fungus here is like this. The ground here is too moist. This fungus is from the north.'","The Kintai of Sul Madásh welcome the assistance of you and the others against their ancient enemy, Sívigush. Irsinith directs you to enlist Viznak's further assistance.","Insight into Action","Collect a peculiar-looking mushroom from south-east Adagím","'Viznak's counsel shall be of great value.\
\
'Seek him out, and ask by what signs we might discern whether the 'Blight Lady' has come to this place, drawn to a hidden wellspring of the Earth-terror.'","Deliver the peculiar mushroom to Viznak at Sul Madásh","Speak with Viznak at the Sul Madásh in Adagím","'We must hurry. Go to the place on the dwarf map. Look for Uruks, look for trolls, and look for morvul! If you see blighted fungi different from others, collect one for me.'","Viznak directs you to scour the area in the south-east section of Adagím in search for something out of the ordinary. He believes that you will find a fungal growth very different from the others near the location not on the maps.","You discovered a mushroom at the foot of the mountains in south-eastern Adagím. The mushroom was certainly different and out of place from the rest. Return the mushroom to Viznak at the Mother's Hill.","Collected a peculiar-looking mushroom","Irsinith enlists you to gain Viznak's aid in learning more about the missing section of the map. Return to him at Sul Madásh."},
[6682]={"A merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.\
\
His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.","Pick up the bag of bad rice","You hear good sound quality and feel the firmness of the bag","Smack the bags of rice (3/5)","Smack the bags of rice (4/5)","You have delivered the bag of bad rice","Uh oh! That neither sounded nor felt right","You have inspected all the rice and should report back to the injured merchant.\
\
The injured merchant is outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Smack the bags of rice (2/5)","Smack the bags of rice (1/5)","'Only one sack of bad rice so far? I hope the others are good.\
\
'You will return there to check the rest of them?'","You have found a bag of rice that does not pass muster. Pick it up and drop it next to the injured merchant.\
\
The injured merchant can be found outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward.","A quality bag of rice if ever you smacked one","Inspecting the Goods","Sounds good!","Talk to the injured merchant outside the Monger's Guild-hall","'Ugh, I hurt my back recently, and now I cannot lift the sacks of rice I ordered. I need to check them in case I need to send any of them back to my supplier, but I can't easily move from this spot. Could you do it for me? No, you don't need to open the sacks. Just give them a whack. You'll know by the feel and the sound if the bag is good or not.\
\
'The sacks were unloaded by the Wharf-gate between the Sail-haven and the Upper Ward. There is an alley on the Sail-haven side of the gate where my men leave them. I need them to bring the sacks all the way here next time, if my back is not better, but I know they will not want to do that unless I pay them more... and that would be very difficult to do unless my fortunes change!'","A merchant needs help evaluating the quality of his goods.","Smack the bags of rice (0/5)","No problems here, just delicious rice","'Oh good! So there was only the one bag that did not pass the smack test? Good. I will return it and ask that my coin be returned to me... when I am able to, of course. For now, I will sit here and enjoy the breeze.'"},
[6683]={"Took down notes in Rhovendol's journal -- but the stone detail of a nearby building catches your eye","Bring your notes to Rhovendol","The great fountain of Dol Amroth is in the Court of the Fount.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> at the fountain, and think of how it reminds you of Barían.","Rhovendol is in the Scholar's Quarter in Dol Amroth.\
\
You should return to Rhovendol.","'Let us see what you wrote there.'\
\
You hand Rhovendol your thoughts on Barían.\
\
'All stone and strength! Creative, yes, but these are not words to describe a lady. You have much to learn about love, ${PLAYER}. Hold a moment; I will compose a poem, and when you deliver it to Barían, you will see how to properly woo with the written word.'","Perhaps it was because Barían stood amongst the stone-masons, but the fair stonework reminds you of her style of beauty","Rhovendol mentioned that Barían could often be found in the Mason's Quarter in Dol Amroth.\
\
You should see if you can catch a glimpse of Barían before you run off to take notes on things that resemble her.","Examine the blue canopy for resemblance to Barían","Write about the fair stonework's resemblance to Barían","Write about how the stream of water is strong and bold","This is a good place to meditate","The building whose stone detail caught your eye is south-east of the fountain in the Court of the Fount -- the one with the golden statue atop it.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> at the detail on this fine building.","Your journal is in your inventory.\
\
You should use the journal to write down your observations.","Inspiration for a Love Poem","<rgb=#FF0000>Meditate</rgb> at the fountain","This is a good place to look","Rhovendol, a poet of Dol Amroth, has asked you to take notes for him so that he may compose a poem to his love, Barían.","Blue canopies can be found in the Court of the Fount.\
\
You should examine the canopies for resemblance to Barían.","The colour is little like Barían's hardy presence, but the fabric's strength against the breeze impresses you","Took down notes in Rhovendol's journal","Barían stares boldly and expectantly at the master stone-mason, standing out amongst the workmen","Write about the fabric's strength against the wind","Try to catch a glimpse of Barían","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> at the stonework detail on the fine building","'Hm? I am sorry, I was lost in thought. I am a poet, you see, and my mind often wanders amongst my yet unwritten verses.\
\
'Today I think of Barían, the lady I love. She is oft in the Mason's Quarter, and fair as any maiden I've seen.\
\
'They say that meditation upon certain lovely objects will help the words flow, and come to think of it, I do wish to write a poem for fair Barían. Here, have a spare journal. Go take notes for me, if you would, on lovely things in the Court of the Fount. The clear water so like her voice, or the blue canopies so like her eyes. Your notes will help me profess my admiration.'"},
[6684]={"'You should speak with the Elders of Lhan Bach.'","'I should have known that my father was doing this, but he kept his plans from me. I am glad that the elders from Lhan Bach will stand with me against the monster my father has become.'","Lhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach.\
\
You should return to Lhucu with the answers from Nia and Parru.","Talk to Parru at Lhan Bach","Talk to Nia at Lhan Bach","'In the past, Trehéarn Brenin was able to rally our people to retake what was our birthright, but then the warriors abandoned us. I fear what has happened to our once-great leader.'","'In the past, we had always served Trehéarn Brenin without fail. His rule was difficult, but just.\
\
'However, he now views our people as cattle and presses us into service with these evil men. We cannot openly fight against his might, but would assist those who would depose him.'","Talk to Lhucu at her hut in the Bonevales","'In the village below, Lhan Bach, there are two influential elders that guide the people. These folk have been pressed into assisting my father and his men against their will.\
\
'Will you speak with the elders, Nia and Parru, and see if they would be willing to put aside the fouling of our ancestors?\
\
'Travel south along the path and you will eventually come to the gate of Lhan Bach.'","Nia and Parru are elders of Lhan Bach, found along the path south of Lhucu's hut.\
\
Lhucu asked you to speak with Nia and Parru and convince them to turn away from the service of Trehéarn Brenin.","Lhucu confirmed Naeglanc's suspicions regarding the urn-shards you discovered.","Inspire Hope"},
[6685]={"'¡El Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido volverá a hacer honor a su nombre si seguimos a este ritmo, ${PLAYER}! Hay algo con lo que puedes ayudarme, y quizá eso...\
\
'¡Oh, no te acerques todavía a las talegas de correo! De hecho estoy al día con las entregas de hoy y no necesito que lleves ninguna de estas a ningún lado. No, lo que quiero que hagas es llevar la noticia al cartero Raropié en los Ranales sobre nuestros esfuerzos para mejorar la rapidez con la que entregamos el correo. Ha estado bastante decaído últimamente: los hobbits en los Ranales no se cortan a la hora de expresar sus quejas, y Raropié siempre ha sido de los que se lo toman muy a pecho.\
\
Los Ranales está al este de Delagua. Dile a Raropié que estamos reparando la reputación del Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido y ofrécele cualquier ayuda que puedas.'","'Hola. Soy el cartero de los Ranales. Siento cualquier inconveniente que el Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido te haya podido causar....\
\
¿Qué? ¿No has venido a quejarte? Oh. Oh, ya veo. Eso es bueno. Sí, me alegra que hoy no hayamos defraudado a nadie. Recibo tantas quejas, ya sabes. Al cabo del tiempo eso agota a un hobbit.\
\
¿Dices que el cartero Coto está intentando revitalizar el Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido y devolverle su antigua fama? ¿Incluso con todas las cartas que se envían hoy en día? ¡Eso es una noticia increíble! Si recuperamos nuestra antigua reputación, quizá ya no tengamos que dedicar tanto tiempo a responder quejas.'","'Los Ranales está al este de Delagua, y encontrarás al cartero Raropié cerca del centro del pueblo. Por lo que cuenta, parece que solo tienes que seguir la fila de hobbits que van a quejarse. Anímalo y ayúdalo con las entregas que tenga que hacer, si tienes tiempo.'","El cartero Raropié está en los Ranales, al este de Delagua.\
\
El cartero Coto está preocupado por su amigo Raropié y quiere que le lleves noticias de tus esfuerzos por revitalizar el Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido con la esperanza de que eso le levante el ánimo.","Animar al cartero Raropié","El cartero Coto está encantado de que estés ayudando al Servicio de Correo Postal Rápido a recuperar su reputación de rapidez en la entrega del correo y quiere que lleves noticias de tus esfuerzos al cartero Raropié de los Ranales, que ha estado bastante decaído últimamente."},
[6686]={"Instancia: Un mal cumpleaños","'It is strange to me that after so many years spent in siege, tomorrow the sun may dawn upon the Great Alliance for the last time. The council was most clear: if the Bright Company fails to break Sauron's control over the Oath-stone, all hope of our victory is fled.\
\
'No! Banish the thought, banish it! We will think of something.'","The sons of Isildur are at Díngarth, waiting for you to sit by their camp-fire.","Listen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur","Meldaran is at Díngarth.","Talk to Vëamacil","Talk to Meldaran","Tárandil is at Díngarth.","<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire","'I have seen brighter birthdays, but if we do survive, let us look back upon this one more fondly! Tárandil, I am certain father will grant you the boon you seek; did he not rage for a week and a day at the betrayal of the Men of the Mountain? If you desire the death of Rioc, father is certain to grant it.\
\
'But let us speak of lighter matters! Among the Thíuda recently come through Ram Raedas, I saw a woman of such loveliness she could melt even your own sturdy armour, Tárandil! The blade she carried was sharp, even deadlier than your own, and with words of love you might win her heart. Why, she might join her weapon to yours, and let Rioc pay double for his treachery!'","Vëamacil is at Díngarth.","Vëamacil and his brothers are at Díngarth.","The sons of Isildur are at Díngarth.","'I will not lie to you, friend. Your mission tomorrow will not be easy, for you go to the most dangerous of all places in this Black Land. I envy you not the chance; I am no fool! But in this one thing I am envious: tomorrow you will be given the chance to do something, stand or fall, and you need not wait for fate to arrive; you will go to meet it! Not every man gets the opportunity for that.\
\
'The Elves of the Bright Company are renowned for their courage. If I had any advice to give you, it would be this: stay near to Glorfindel! Some measure of inspiration will serve you in good stead, and I warrant he will provide any you might require! Who can tell what we might say on the morrow? The glory of the Bright Company may be joined with yours, and Men may speak in reverent tones of your own contribution. Victory might not be yours, but at the least none will speak of cowardice!'","The sons of Isildur are spending a final night by the fire before the day dawns upon the Bright Company's desperate mission to rob Sauron of his domination over the Ghâzab Bôron.","'If we do survive... if the Bright Company does complete its mission, and Sauron's hold over the Ghâzab Bôron is broken, I wish to ask my foster-father for a boon. I do not seek treasure, or reward, or glory. I want only one thing.'\
\
Tárandil clenches his hands into fists.\
\
'I want Isildur to send me to Morthond. I want to find Rioc of the Mountain, in whatever hole he hides, and make him pay for his oath-breaking. I want to slay him myself. If we survive the days to come, I will take no rest until I have paid Rioc for his treachery.'","Talk to Tárandil"},
[6687]={"Instancia: Una tradición Beorninghús","You collect some fruit for the table from Violet","<rgb=#FF0000>Sit</rgb> down for a meal.","You collect some bread for the table from Lady","This is a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>sit</rgb> down","How kind of Clover! You should give this dinnerware to Rose","<rgb=#FF0000>Sit</rgb> down for a meal","'A Beorninghús feast is one of my favourite things! It is kind of you to volunteer to help us prepare for the feast.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I must finish preparing the food. If you would please help set the table, we will be ready for the guests. Do not worry about the time! Rose, Star, Bud, Sprout, Lily, Violet, Cream, Lady, Clover, Honey-bun, Honey-pie, and Leaf will help you out! Thank you kindly, ${RACE}.\
\
'Oh and some of the food will be out shortly to put on the table.'","Star is helping to set the table","Habla con Grimbeorn.","Help set the table.","'${PLAYER}, I am glad that you have visited my home. You have been a great help and voice of reason. You are always welcome here, my friend.'","You place the fruit on the table","Enjoy a meal.","How kind of Honey-bun! You should give this dinnerware to Star","You collect some honey for the table from Cream","'Eat, eat. There is food enough for all of us.'","Rose is helping to set the table","Talk to Gírta","Now that the guests have arrived, dinner can begin","How kind of Leaf! You should give this dinnerware to Sprout","Talk to Gírta.","Enjoy a meal","Sprout is helping to set the table","You collect some nuts for the table from Lily","You place the honey on the table","Grimbeorn invites many family members and guests to a feast.","Habla con Grimbeorn","Help set the table","How kind of Honey-pie! You should give this dinnerware to Bud","You place the bread on the table","Enjoy a moment's rest","You place the nuts on the table","Bud is helping to set the table","Enjoy a moment's rest."},
[6688]={"Speak with Mizâdi in the tower","Okhíso and Mizâdi draw their swords","Instancia: Una cuchilla de llamas y furia, parte 2","Listen to Mizâdi and Okhíso","Finish your ascent and enter the tower room to confront Okhiso.","Speak with Mizâdi to continue your ascent through the tower","Defeat Okhíso and his guards","Assist Mizâdi with her confrontation with Okhíso","Speak with Mizâdi in the tower.","Listen to Okhíso's dying words.","Go with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.","'Our ascent will not be without conflict. Stay close and we will reach Okhíso and bring the dog low.'","Mizâdi stops to allow you to rest","Defeat Okhíso's guards and archers.","Mizâdi stops to regroup with you","'We draw close to apex of the tower. Prepare yourself, ${PLAYER}, this scorpion will sting if we allow him the opportunity.'","You must quickly ascend the tower of Kûr Anzar. Okhíso must not escape what justice demands.","Listen to Okhíso's dying words","Listen to Mizâdi and Okhíso.","Alert Mizâdi you are prepared to continue","'Come, ${PLAYER}, let us press our advantage and bring the fight to Okhíso!'","'Gird yourself, ${PLAYER}, Okhíso will now pay by my hand.'","'There will be time for talk later. We must get outside, and quickly. We must save Kûr Anzar and her people!'","Tell Mizâdi you are prepared to move forward","Mizâdi arrives at the throne ready to treat with Okhíso"},
[6689]={"Put out straw fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tend to wounded Kûr Anzar citizens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meet Mizâdi back at the tower of Kûr Anzar.","Sectarios del que Todo lo Ve derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: Una cuchilla de llamas y furia, parte 3","Derrota a los sectarios del que Todo lo Ve (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Put out straw fires and rescue trapped citizens in Kûr Anzar.","Meet Mizâdi back at the tower of Kûr Anzar","Okhíso, seeking to divert your attention, has set Kûr Anzar aflame. That was not enough to stay Mizâdi's blade but now the city needs to be saved. You must put out the fires and rescue trapped citizens in Kûr Anzar.","Straw fires extinguished (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tended to wounded Kûr Anzar citizens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6690]={"Habla con Fastrith Halcomida en Zul-mazal","Bored by the discussion, Imák has called for you to speak with him. He believes danger is near.","Talk to Imák in Zul-mazal","Listen to the dwarves discuss the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal","Remain alert for any further threats to the dwarves","'That was well-fought, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps these Longbeards can take care of themselves after all... so long as there is a Stout-axe nearby to lend a hand!'","Fastrith and the other dwarves stand in Zul-mazal, discussing the broken mosaic on the wall.","Bori and the other dwarves prepare to defend Zul-mazal from the hobgoblin hunting-pack.","Imák calls for you from the other side of the chamber","You and the dwarves have defended Zul-mazal from the hobgoblin hunting-party.","A hobgoblin prey-catcher has found the entrance to Zul-mazal, and before he was slain he alerted his band to your position. You and the dwarves must ready your defence!","Return to Zul-mazal with Imák and ready the defence","Bori has suggested that you bring Fastrith to inspect the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal in order to see if her master Stáli the Hewer would be interested in it.","Imák has been defeated!","Instancia: Un mosaico roto","'Something smells foul, ${PLAYER}. Let them study that mosaic... we should look around for the source of this unsettling odour.\
\
'I think danger is near.'","'This mosaic must have been quite lovely, once! I have only been apprenticed to Stáli the Hewer for a short time, but I am certain he will want to see this!'","'These hobgoblins do not know who they have chosen for dancing partners!\
\
'Let us show them the mistake they have made!'","Talk to Bori in Zul-mazal","Fastrith has come to Zul-mazal."},
[6691]={"Palma Rizopardo te ha convencido de recuperar la espada Medhrod, robada por medio-orcos en Naerost, en las Tierras Solitarias.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ? Si eres ${PLAYERNAME:un saqueador[m]|una saqueadora[f]} que vale lo que pesa en sal, no tendrás dificultad en infiltrarte en Naerost y volver aquí con Medhrod. Vales lo que pesas en sal, ¿verdad, ? ¡Vamos, haz que me sienta orgullosa!\
\
'Yo lo haría, pero creo que te vendría bien practicar. ¡De nada!'","Palma Rizopardo está esperando para hablar contigo en las colinas fuera de Naerost.\
\
De alguna manera, Palma te ha convencido de infiltrarte en las ruinas de Naerost para recuperar la espada Medhrod.","'Medhrod probablemente esté guardado en algún lugar profundo dentro de las ruinas, ${PLAYER}. ¡Intenta no ser visto, o tendrás una pelea difícil entre manos!'","'¡Lo lograste! Bueno, eso es un alivio, ¿no es así, ? ¡Seguro que no tuviste ningún problema!\
\
'Ahora volvamos a la posada y compartamos las buenas noticias: los medio-orcos ya no tienen en su poder a Medhrod, ¡y bien merecido lo tienen!\
\
'Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'","'¡Estoy lista para partir si tú lo estás! ¡La posada nos espera!'","Palma Rizopardo está en la ladera, fuera de las ruinas de Naerost.\
\
Palma espera con entusiasmo tu regreso con Medhrod.","La espada Medhrod está en algún lugar dentro de las ruinas de Naerost.\
\
Los medio-orcos que la robaron seguramente la tienen bien vigilada dentro de las ruinas.","Recuperar Medhrod","Instancia: El encargo de un saqueador"},
[6692]={"¡Escucha a Angélica y entretenla para que no os descubra!","¡Dinodas tiene que quedarse callado!","Habla con Prisca Boffin","¡Tienes que esconder el regalo en algún sitio antes de que te encuentren con él!","Instancia: Un enredo en la calle Aguamiel","¡Rápido! ¡Debes pensar en algo para enmascarar los vítores de Dinodas!","Escapa del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel","Espera que Prisca vuelva al salón","<rgb=#00FF00>Anima</rgb> para evitar que Angélica encuentre a Dinodas","¡Alguien viene! ¡Será mejor que te escondas detrás de la mesa!","Angélica tiene algo más que decirte.","Habla con Angélica Boffin","'Ven conmigo al salón, ${PLAYER}. Quiero hablar contigo.'","¡Listo!","¡Ahora o nunca!","Prisca quiere hablar contigo.","¡Escóndete detrás de la mesa antes de que te vean!","Con el regalo seguro en tus manos, debes escapar del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel","'Esperaré a mi fiesta... ¡pero más vale que sea buena!'","Angélica quiere hablar contigo.","Esconde el regalo en algún sitio... ¡y rápido!","¡Oh no! ¡Tienes que ocultar el regalo en algún sitio, y rápido!","Dinodas cree que el regalo está guardado en la habitación de atrás, al final de la Sala de Entrada.","Para prevenir una situación embarazosa, Dinodas te ha encargado que lleves a cabo un plan mediante el cual espera recuperar el regalo de inauguración antes de que su hermana Angélica lo abra.","'Oh, no sé. ¡Parece una lástima celebrar la fiesta sin todos los hermanos y hermanas de Angélica! ¿Tú qué crees, ${PLAYER}?\
\
Le dices a Frisca que una verdadera fiesta de inauguración debería tener tanta gente como fuera posible, y que la verdadera lástima sería empezar la fiesta sin todos los hermanos de Angélica presentes para la celebración. Ella considera tu argumento.\
\
'Quizás, quizás...'","Debes esperar hasta que sea seguro moverse sin ser visto.","¡Dinodas ha conseguido salir del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel con el regalo envuelto!","<rgb=#00FF00>Desmáyate</rgb> o <rgb=#00FF00>túmbate</rgb> para esconderte de la vista","Alguien se está acercando a tu habitación. ¡Será mejor que te escondas detrás de la mesa!","Angélica te está buscando.","¡Justo a tiempo!","Escucha lo que Angélica tiene que decir","'Solo necesitaba desahogarme, creo. Esperaré hasta que todos mis hermanos y hermanas hayan vuelto.\
\
'Y entonces comenzará mi fiesta.'","Una fechoría bien ejecutada... más o menos.","Encuentra el regalo envuelto en el almacén oeste","'Te comprendo, ${PLAYER}, de verdad. ¡Pero no entiendes CÓMO DE A MENUDO pasa esto! Mis hermanos y hermanas siempre se van en el momento más inoportuno.'"},
[6693]={"Jarl Brazodecobre te espera fuera de Ost Galumar.\
\
Jarl Brazodecobre desea hablar contigo.","El estandarte ahora se muestra con orgullo","'¡Míralos, ! La vista de esos estandartes ondeando de nuevo sobre Ost Galumar es verdaderamente alegre. ¡Y eres ${PLAYERNAME:un capitán[m]|una capitana[f]} de gran valía por haber logrado esto!\
\
'Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar a Othrikar, , y daremos estas felices noticias a su gente.'","'Ost Galumar se encuentra adelante, ${PLAYER}, y encontrarás postes de estandarte en varios lugares a lo largo de los muros. Los Duramano deben tener alguna forma de trepar a los muros, pues retiraron los estandartes que antes ondeaban sobre esta fortaleza.\
\
'Izad tres de los estandartes que te he dado sobre Ost Galumar... ¡y cuidado con los Duramano que se esconden dentro!'","Tres postes de estandarte están colocados en los muros de Ost Galumar.\
\
Jarl Brazodecobre te ha pedido izar tres de los estandartes de los Pueblos Libres sobre Ost Galumar.","Jarl Brazodecobre se encuentra fuera de Ost Galumar.\
\
Jarl Brazodecobre espera hablar contigo sobre tu tarea exitosa.","Habla con Jarl Brazodecobre","Instancia: El estandarte de un capitán","'¿Estás listo para regresar a Othrikar, ${PLAYER}? ¡Debemos viajar con rapidez y decirle a la gente allí que los estandartes de los Pueblos Libres ondean nuevamente sobre Ost Galumar!'","Has viajado a Ost Galumar con Jarl Brazodecobre para izar los estandartes de los Pueblos Libres sobre las ruinas ocupadas por los Duramano.","Cuelga los estandartes de los Pueblos Libres en los postes de estandarte (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6694]={"Applaud Khûldim Umûn for his decision","Talk to Girhâzi","'Remember, just go along along with whatever I am saying.'","Listen to the conversation","Show Khûldim Umûn that you are powerful","<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> at Khûldim Umûn","Instancia: Un público cautivo","Greet Khûldim Umûn","Girhâzi has an idea for how to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of the lost archive, and she needs your help.","Listen to Khûldim Umûn","<rgb=#00FF00>Challenge</rgb> Khûldim Umûn to trial by combat","Girhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.","<rgb=#00FF00>Pose</rgb> for Khûldim Umûn","<rgb=#00FF00>Clap</rgb> for Khûldim Umûn's decision","Show Khûldim Umûn how courageous you are","Girhâzi signals that she wants to talk to you, but makes no effort to keep her words unheard by Khûldim Umûn.\
\
'I was planning on ransoming him and sending him back to his family once we learned where the archive is, but if he is not going to tell us, what do you think of giving the people of Ambarûl what they want? Public executions are so distasteful though. We could even make it a fair fight, you against him. It would end the same.'","Girhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh. You should talk to her.","Challenge Khûldim Umûn to single combat","<rgb=#00FF00>Flex</rgb> at Khûldim Umûn","Girhâzi grins at you.\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}, we are done here for now.'"},
[6695]={"'¡Lo que logramos hoy es digno de leyenda -- \\qLa Canción de Slade y  en Ost Cyrn,\\q si lo prefieres!\
\
'¿Estás  ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar a Ost Guruth? ¡Quizá encuentre un juglar a quien pueda contar esta historia!'","'¡Hemos salido victoriosos, , verdaderos campeones de las Tierras Solitarias! ¡Mosal-ruk ya no amenazará a los habitantes que intentan ganarse la vida en estas duras tierras, y hemos enviado un mensaje a sus amos en este día: nos mantendremos firmes contra ustedes, ¡sin importar las probabilidades!\
\
'Dime cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, y regresaremos a Ost Guruth con esta feliz noticia!'","Instancia: El Valor de un Campeón","Mosal-ruk se planta desafiante ante ti.\
\
Has luchado en lo profundo de Ost Cyrn junto a Slade Ransford, y ha llegado el momento de enfrentar a Mosal-ruk, el líder de la partida de guerra que ocupa las ruinas.","Slade Ransford está en Ost Cyrn, en las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Slade está descansando rápidamente en lo alto de uno de los edificios en ruinas de Ost Cyrn, y espera hablar contigo sobre avanzar más en las ruinas en busca de Mosal-ruk.","Slade Ransford está en Ost Cyrn, en las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Slade espera hablar contigo sobre luchar en lo profundo de Ost Cyrn en busca de Mosal-ruk, el vil orco que lidera esta partida de guerra.","'Continuemos, ${PLAYER} -- la parte más peligrosa de nuestro viaje está por delante, pues Mosal-ruk seguramente ya sabe que venimos. ¡Le mostraremos que él y los suyos no son bienvenidos en estas tierras!'","Has venido a Ost Cyrn con Slade Ransford para expulsar a los orcos que se han instalado en las ruinas.","'Ost Cyrn está adelante, ${PLAYER}, y si somos valientes de corazón y fuertes de brazo, ¡los orcos dentro no permanecerán allí para mañana!\
\
'Tomemos una ruta indirecta hacia las ruinas y eliminemos a tantos orcos como encontremos en nuestro camino. Mosal-ruk pondrá a prueba nuestro valor incluso solo, y cuantos menos de su banda queden cuando lo enfrentemos, más seguro estaré de nuestra victoria!'","Habla con Slade Ransford","Desafía a Mosal-ruk","Slade Ransford está triunfante en Ost Cyrn.\
\
Juntos, tú y Slade recorristeis las ruinas de Ost Cyrn y pusisteis fin a Mosal-ruk y su vil partida de guerra."},
[6697]={"Viaja a Lothlórien con Haldir y Bingo","Habla con Bingo en el camino","'Me avergüenza admitir que nunca pensé en el propio viaje de Willem Bigotes, ¡y ahora tengo la cara tan roja como un tomate! ¿Qué crees que está buscando? Si está en mi mano ayudarlo a encontrarlo, ¡haré todo lo que pueda!\
\
'¡Tendrías que haberme lo dicho antes, Willem!'","Habla con Bingo dentro de Caras Galadhon","Has venido con Bingo a través del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío y te has encontrado con un pequeño grupo de elfos enviados desde Lothlórien para recibiros.","Haldir ha pedido que tú y Bingo lo acompañéis a Lothlórien.","Haldir y varios Elfos han llegado en un momento oportuno, y parece que estaban esperándoos.","'¡Es un buen día para caminar! El aire fresco y limpio casi me recuerda a un paseo tranquilo por los senderos de la Comarca. ¡Y aun así estamos tan lejos de Cuaderna del Oeste... de hecho, tan al este de la Cuaderna del Este que he perdido la cuenta de la distancia!\
\
'Puedo ver el tono dorado de los bosques por esta pendiente, ${PLAYER}. ¡Caminemos y veamos qué nos espera bajo el dosel!'","Tú, Bingo y Willem Bigotes habéis salido de la vasta oscuridad de Moria y ahora os acercáis al Bosque de Oro.","'Mi espejo me muestra muchas cosas, y no todas llegarán a suceder. Conozco tu viaje, y conozco también el de nuestro joven Bingo. ¿De verdad le sorprende que su compañero felino tenga su propio camino? Quizá le convenga recordar que todos tenemos nuestras sendas en este mundo y, aunque puedan entrelazarse un tiempo, no lo harán para siempre.\
\
'Mi propio tiempo en esta tierra que amo está llegando a su fin, y mi viaje me llevará a otros lugares. Por ahora, es un placer daros la bienvenida a Caras Galadhon. Si deseáis aprender más, buscad a Pennasseth, nuestra Guardiana de Historias, en Cerin Nauth.'","'¡Ah, hemos encontrado un comité de bienvenida, ${PLAYER}, y parece que nos estaban esperando! ¡Qué giro tan agradable!\
\
'Será un placer acompañar a estos buenos Elfos. ¡Adelante, hacia el Bosque de Oro!'","Tú y Bingo os habéis encontrado con Celeborn y Galadriel, y están muy interesados en oír hablar de vuestros viajes.","'¡Apenas puedo creer que hayamos sido invitados al Bosque de Oro, ${PLAYER}, y que nos estén dando un recorrido personal por Caras Galadhon!\
\
'Tengo tantas preguntas para los Elfos de este lugar. ¿Qué les llevó a asentarse aquí, y desde cuándo viven en Lothlórien? ¿Llevan vidas solitarias o viajan? ¡Ver un Elfo es algo muy raro en la Comarca!\
\
'Espero que no consideren groseras mis preguntas, pero necesito aprender cuanto pueda sobre su pueblo, ¡o mi libro sufrirá por tal falta de conocimiento!'","'Esos orcos querían arruinar nuestro paseo relajante, ¡pero diría que frustraste sus planes con gran eficacia!\
\
'No pensemos más en las sombras que oscurecieron nuestro camino, y centrémonos en el brillante porvenir que nos aguarda bajo el sol dorado y los árboles que se alzan delante. ¡Continuemos, quizá a un paso más ligero!'","Instancia: Un capítulo sobre elfos","Habla con Galadriel","Bingo está dentro de Caras Galadhon, esperando hablar contigo.","Has defendido a Bingo de un ataque de un grupo de orcos, y ahora el hobbit está listo para continuar su tranquilo paseo por el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.","El Señor y la Dama de Lórien esperan hablar contigo en Caras Galadhon.","'¡Espero que tu amigo no se haya ofendido! Nuestra bienvenida a este bosque es sincera, y espero que lo considere un lugar de paz y descanso antes de continuar su viaje.\
\
'Hablaré con las centinelas de la puerta de Caras Galadhon. Desde ahora, los tres seréis bienvenidos dentro de la ciudad.'","Habla con Haldir en el camino","Habla con Bingo en el camino a través del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío","Habla con Bingo en Caras Galadhon","Habla con Celeborn","Escucha las palabras de Celeborn y Galadriel","'${PLAYER}, os estábamos esperando a ti y a tus amigos. La Dama de Lórien me dio instrucciones precisas de partir desde el Bosque de Oro en vuestra búsqueda. Me alegra ver que no habéis sufrido daño alguno.\
\
'Y si tu amigo está dispuesto, será un placer llevaros más allá de los límites y ante el Señor y la Dama.'","'Bueno, desde luego me han dado mucho en qué pensar!'","Tú y Bingo habéis sido escoltados hasta Lothlórien, y ahora el hobbit está muy emocionado por aprender todo lo que pueda sobre los Elfos.","Has avanzado con Bingo un buen trecho dentro del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío, y un sendero conduce hacia el este en dirección al Bosque de Oro."},
[6698]={"Talk to Kyrstig","Instancia: Una reunión clandestina","Listen to the conversation","'A little while ago, I was looking around the Thing-fold, admiring the grand and ancient structures, when I heard someone talking whose voice I did not recognize.'","Scout Kyrstig has an important report to share: a secret meeting between Loknashra and the leader of the Cult of Drugoth hints at their true motives in the region....","Kyrstig is describing what she saw transpire between the Angmarim cultist and Loknashra.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","'A secret ritual? This sounds like something we should try and prevent!'","Kyrstig is ready to describe what she saw earlier.\
\
You should talk to Kyrstig."},
[6699]={"Leave Borhador and face whatever is pounding upon the walls of the Crossing-hall.","The sound gets louder, rattling the doors","Instancia: Un Golpe Imponente","Borhador heard sounds coming from outside the hall.\
\
You should speak with Borhador.","'I saw strength in my people today and the strength of this Vale. How did I not see it before?'","Let the events transpire.","Speak with Borhador","Borhador stands outside the Crossing-hall.\
\
You should speak with Borhador.","'You hear it, too. The sounds grow with each passing minute. I fear the town is under siege! My time has come. This is surely the end of days!' \
\
Borhador begins to weep.\
\
'Leave my hall. It is to be my tomb!'","Let the events transpire","Borhador hears a loud noise outside and want you to investigate as he fears the a cave troll has come for him.","Leave Borhador and face whatever is pounding upon the walls of the Crossing-hall","'This day has given me strength.'","The townspeople of Ethring band together to overthrow a rampaging cave troll"},
[6700]={"Habla con Miluimil para salir de las oscuras cavernas.","Derrota a los orcos que persiguen a Gollum","Habla con Miluimil","El explorador elfo Miluimil ha recibido el encargo de capturar a la criatura llamada Gollum para impedir que caiga en manos de los orcos.","Instancia: Un enemigo acorralado","Habla con Miluimil y adéntrate en las cavernas para impedir que los orcos que persiguen a Gollum lo capturen.","'¡Rápido! ¡Debemos marcharnos de este lugar!'","Gollum ha escapado"},
[6701]={"Radagast te ha pedido que hables con Saeradan afuera","Instancia: Una Cabaña en el Bosque","Como veterano ${CLASS}, has visto tu parte de batallas. Ahora el Concilio Blanco y los Dúnedain buscan tu ayuda en la Guerra del Anillo. Lucha por ellos y protege los caminos de la Tierra Media.","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Te hemos estado esperando. Las tierras de la Tierra Media están cambiando. A tu alrededor puedes sentirlo. Anoche mismo vi relámpagos sobre la Cima de los Vientos. Debes apresurarte y descubrir más. Las tierras se agitan con el mal.\
\
'Habla con Saeradan afuera, y él te guiará en tu camino.\
\
<rgb=#ff0000>Completar esta misión te teletransportará fuera de esta cabaña y no podrás regresar.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00ff00>Como veterano, se te han concedido todas las habilidades de tu nivel. Sin embargo, solo unas pocas han sido asignadas. Si deseas asignar más, abre tu Panel de Habilidades presionando K.</rgb>\
\
'Estoy seguro de que volveré a verte antes del final.'","Frente a ti se sienta Radagast el Pardo, un Mago del orden de Gandalf. Busca tu ayuda en la Guerra del Anillo.\
\
Debes hablar con Radagast y ver cómo puedes ayudar.\
\
<rgb=#00ff00>Haz clic derecho en los personajes para interactuar</rgb>.","Habla con Radagast el Pardo"},
[6702]={"Bandrauth Adder-fang can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Bandrauth Adder-fang intends to slay you to atone for his failures in Elderslade. You should defend yourself and defeat Bandrauth Adder-fang.","Brathar Crack-helm is departing the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You should remain alert while Brathar and his Dourhands depart.","Talk to Múta","With the defeat of Bandrauth Adder-fang and the Dourhands, a sudden silence falls in Tûr Ágal","As the last of the other Angmarim leave the chamber, Bandrauth Adder-fang smirks at you","Brathar, the Dourhands, and the servants of the Iron Crown can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have found Brathar, the Dourhands, and the servants of the Iron Crown gathered in Tûr Ágal. You should observe this meeting and try to remain unseen.","'Dost thou not seest? All has come to pass as I foretold.\
\
'When first I met thee, I was fated to fail. But the mercy of Lord Brathar has granted me mine vengeance upon thee!\
\
'Thy fate is sealed!'","Follow Múta and fight your way through Tûr Ágal","'Swiftly now! We must leave this tower before the others discover what has happened!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Múta has been defeated!</rgb>","After reaching the door to the upper chamber, Múta pauses and beckons you over","Instancia: Una grieta en la Corona de Hierro","Observe Brathar's departure from Tûr Ágal","Talk to Bandrauth Adder-fang","Múta can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Múta is ready to search for Brathar in Tûr Ágal. You should speak to her when you are prepared.","Talk to Brathar Crack-helm","Brathar, the Dourhands, and servants of the Iron Crown have gathered in Tûr Ágal!","It seems your presence did not go unnoticed by Brathar","Múta can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have found Brathar, the Dourhands, and the servants of the Iron Crown gathered in Tûr Ágal. You should talk to Múta.","Bandrauth Adder-fang can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Sensing that Bandrauth Adder-fang may fail in his task yet again, the Dourhands have entered the fight to ensure that you do not leave Tûr Ágal.","Observe the meeting between Brathar and the Iron Crown","Defeat Bandrauth Adder-fang","Múta can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Múta has paused beside a door in the heights of Tûr Ágal. You should talk to Múta.","'Yes, this is it. It is exactly as I remember!\
\
'The stairs to the upper chamber lie just beyond these doors, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us find Brathar and put an end to this, my friend. For the Gabil'akkâ!'","'Have the Longbeards grown so cowardly that they send mercenaries like you? Disappointing, but I am not surprised.\
\
'Let me have a look at you, ${RACE}...'\
\
As Brathar Crack-helm inspects you, his eyes suddenly betray some sort of cruel amusement.\
\
'Ah, ${PLAYER}, what a curious twist of fate! Yes, I know your name, but how could you know mine? I am just a Dourhand, after all.\
\
'I was at Gabilazan! I saw what the Longbeards did to Skorgrím—what they did to every one of us Dourhands! That old coward Glóin would not deign to sully his hands with the blood of my brethren, and so he sent you and his own son to do what he could not. And I shall have my vengeance yet!\
\
'But that is not your fate, ${PLAYER}. Your blood is not fit to adorn the hammer of Skorgrím Dourhand!'","Brathar Crack-helm can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have been discovered by Brathar Crack-helm. You should approach Brathar and talk to him.","Word has spread that a mysterious enemy has arrived at Caivád Sâr, threatening to turn the tide of the War of Three Peaks.","Múta can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You should follow Múta into the heights of Tûr Ágal.","'I know the way, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'If we become separated, I do not think things will go well for either of us.\
\
'Follow me as closely as you can, and do not lose sight of me!'","Múta can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
With Múta's aid, you have overcome Bandrauth Adder-fang and the Dourhands at Tûr Ágal. You should talk to Múta.","Defeat Bandrauth Adder-fang and the Dourhands","'Oh, I don't like this at all...'\
\
Múta's voice sinks to a whisper.\
\
'There are too many of them to make our move, ${PLAYER}. If we keep quiet and remain unseen, we may at least overhear something of value to the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'Find some way to blend into this gathering, and I will do the same.'","Bandrauth Adder-fang can be found in the upper chamber of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have been offered to Bandrauth Adder-fang that he might atone for his failure. You should talk to Bandrauth Adder-fang.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. You didn't think I'd actually abandon you, did you?'\
\
Múta smirks slightly.\
\
'It was not the victory we sought, but it could have gone far worse for the both of us. These are ill tidings... even if Brathar is truly gone from Elderslade!\
\
'Our only good fortune is that we might still warn Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ of what is to come!'"},
[6703]={"'La cosa se ha complicado, ¿no? Bueno, estoy seguro de que es un simple malentendido y lo arreglaré todo con estos Duramano.\
\
'Deberías decir lo que dicen, ${PLAYER}. No quiero que te hagan daño por mi culpa. Arreglaré todo esto y me reuniré contigo en el campamento de Glóin.\
\
'¡Qué aventura! ¡Este va a ser un capítulo muy emocionante!'","Instancia: Un Desvío Peligroso","Habla con Spalvi en la pendiente por encima de Helegrod","Un grupo de Duramanos ha llegado a Helegrod, y su líder desea hablar contigo.","'Tienes toda la pinta de que te gusta la aventura. ¿Tenías algo que ver con esta escoria Corcur? Ya hemos pueesto fin a sus fechorías. La Piedra de Roth, la Estrella de Skorgrím, es nuestra de nuevo.'\
\
El Duramano mira más allá de ti, y su cara se ilumina al reconocerte.","Bingo está dispuesto a ayudar a su nuevo amigo Spalvi a recuperar el tesoro robado por los nómadas Corcur y llevarlo a la fortaleza enana de Helegrod.","'Esto no me gusta, ${PLAYER}, pero la situación es delicada y esta es la única manera de que todo el mundo esté a salvo. Te llevaré a la salida, y te imploro que no intentes nada.'","Bingo espera fuera de la gran puerta de Helegrod, esperando para hablar contigo.","Bingo está poco a poco subiendo las escaleras a la puerta de Helegrod, y deberías seguirle.","Habla con Bingo en lo alto de las escaleras","Bingo está en la pendiente nevada que lleva hasta la fortaleza enana de Helegrod.","Spalvi está en la pendiente nevada por encima de Helegrod.","Spalvi ha llegado a lo alto de los escalones, frente a la gran puerta de Helegrod.","Sobrevive al enfrentamiento con los Duramano","Bingo está siendo retenido por los Duramano a cambio de vuestro buen comportamiento.","Habla con el líder del grupo de los Duramano","'Ya basta de hablar. ¡Oigo a los Corcur aproximándose! ¡Sorprendámosles antes de que nos vean!'","Habla con Spalvi en lo alto de las escaleras","'¿Así que el plan es reunirse con Spalvi en la escalera principal? Creo que será mejor que vayas primero, ${PLAYER}. Estaré justo detrás de ti. Bueno... quizá no justo detrás de ti, pero a una distancia prudencial. Pero detrás de ti, ¡cuenta con ello! ¡Espero que tengamos buena suerte!'","Sube las escaleras hacia Helegrod con Bingo","Spalvi te ha revelado que es un Duramano, y ahora estás en una situación complicada.","Dirígete a las escaleras que conducen a la puerta de Helegrod","La gran puerta de Helegrod se alza ante ti","Habla con Spalvi","'Cubriremos más terreno si nos separamos,${PLAYER}. Yo daré un rodeo y veré si puedo encontrar a los nómadas Corcur que me atacaron. Tú deberías continuar junto con nuestro amigo Bingo a la escalera de la entrada. Yo me reuniré con vosotros en ese punto, y si ninguno de nosotros ha recuperado mi tesoro consideraremos subir a la puerta principal.\
\
'¡Que la suerte nos acompañe, ${CLASS}!'","Has derrotado un puñado de nómadas Corcur, pero Spalvi te ha dicho que entre ellos no reconoce a ninguno de los que le emboscaron.","Habla con Bingo","Habla con Bingo en la pendiente que conduce a Helegrod","'No encontré a los Corcur que me atacaron. Deben estar tras esta puerta, y cuando la crucemos les haré pagar por sus crímenes contra mí y mis hermanos, ¡y recuperaré el tesoro que robaron!'","Bingo sonríe de oreja a oreja, y te preguntas si hay algo que pueda disgustarle","'Si pudieras... darme un momento... para recuperar el aliento...'\
\
Bingo respira profundamente y se frota sus piernas doloridas.\
\
'¡Nunca había subido tantos escalones en mi vida, ${PLAYER}! Espero que Spalvi sepa cómo abrir la puerta, o tendremos que darnos la vuelta y volver, y estoy menos preparado para BAJAR estos escalones de lo que estaba para SUBIRLOS hace un rato!'","Un campamento nómada de los Corcur se interpone entre vosotros y las enormes puertas de Helegrod.\
\
Spalvi y Bingo se reunirán contigo una vez llegues a la escalera principal.","'¡Qué emocionante, ${PLAYER}! Este valle es tán recóndito... ¿cuántos hobbits crees que habrán visto alguna vez esta inmensidad nevada? ¡No muchos, diría yo!\
\
'Tenemos que encontrar a estos nómadas Corcur y hacer que devuelvan a Spalvi su tesoro. ¡Es una injusticia!'"},
[6704]={"Runald and his familly have prepared their waggon, said their farewells, and are ready to begin their dangerous journey south to Edoras.","'May we meet again someday, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Feel free to introduce yourself to the traders and thank them for their service. They have remained to provide aid when our King and Reeve have turned away from us.'","The waggon has been destroyed!","Escort the waggon along the road","Do not allow Runald's waggon to be destroyed","'We have arrived! We would not have survived the journey without your aid, ${PLAYER}. We owe you much.\
\
'I must purchase some supplies for my family, and then we will depart the camp at once. We should find safety as we head south into Elfhelm's lands and beyond to Edoras. Farewell, and may fortune find you, friend.'","Instancia: Un camino peligroso","Runald and his family have arrived safely at the trader's outpost along the road.\
\
Runald wishes to thank you for aiding his departure.","'Stay close, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs could come upon us at any moment. We must stay upon the road and seek protection at the trader's outpost to the west.'","Talk to Runald","The waggon has arrived safely at the trader's outpost","Runald and his family await you at the southern entrance to the village of Elthengels."},
[6705]={"'There is nothing left for you to help with! You have freed us from Sithric's mad corruption at last.'","'You did it, ${PLAYER}! Sithric will be locked up, for his proper place is in a prison. Stangard will be made right at last... and it is all thanks to you!'","'Free at last! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I cannot believe the gall of Sithric, nor how deep corruption runs in his veins.\
\
'It is time to take back my city!'","Stanric wants you to rally the men of Stangard while he makes his way to the Mead Hall","Help Stanric out of his cell","Defend Stanric and defeat Sithric.","Stanric is alive, defying the lies of Sithric. It is clear that Stanric must be freed at once, so that justice may be done for this betrayal.","Instance: A Daring Escape","Stanric is in the lock-house of Stangard.","Athulf is in the tavern of Stangard with some equally suspicious men.","'Go rally the men, and I will make my way to the Mead Hall to confront Sithric. The men are often in the inn at this time of night.\
\
'Meet me at the Mead Hall when you can -- I don't have the strength to fight Sithric alone now. I have not eaten or slept since I was locked up down here.'","Stanric is now in the Mead Hall of Stangard.","'${PLAYER}, I must ask to borrow your strength this night. It looks to me like Sithric does not intend to go down without a fight.'","Stanric is in the prison of Stangard.","Listen to Stanric's plan","Free Stanric from his bonds","Stanric is in the Mead Hall.","Stanric is in the lock-house.","Tell Athulf of Sithric's deception","'But -- ${PLAYER}! What are you doing here? Sithric has men looking for you at this very moment! You should run.\
\
'Why have you returned, friend? It must be urgent, if you are risking so much.'","Talk to Stanric","Rally the men in the inn","Help Stanric take down Sithric once and for all","The inn in Stangard is full of suspicious Rohirrim.","Stanric is free -- and now Sithric must pay for his crimes"},
[6706]={"Defeat the Barkhûshim!","You hear a cry behind you, and a voice calls out in challenge","Go with Razâl up the tower stairs to find Numûru and defeat All-seeing cultists.","Speak with Numûru in the Angar Aragín","Defeat Karâshna Zíri.","'My thanks. The Barkhûshim seem to have an unhealthy appreciation for my blood. It does wonders for me. I think it would not work nearly so well for their dark lord, but they would hear none of it.\
\
'They stuck me several times. It's fortunate you came when you did, or there would be precious little left of me to collect.\
\
'I can manage my way out of here - there are others trapped above us. Please help them escape as well.'","Find the other prisoners.","Speak with Razâl inside the Angar Aragín.","'There's no telling what we may find here. I believe they bring the sacrifices upstairs to one of their dark altars. That is likely where we'll find Numûru and any other unfortunates they've gathered.'","Free Numûru from his bonds.","<rgb=#ff0000>Razâl must not falter</rgb>","Speak with Razâl inside the Angar Aragín","Ascend the stairs and defeat the Barkhûshim guarding the other prisoners.","Free the third prisoner","'He is wounded. I will get him out of Kûr Anzar, leave it to me. Free those poor souls above us, they need your aid most now. Then meet us back in Urmâkh.'","Folllow Razâl and defeat All-seeing cultists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Go with Razâl up the tower stairs to find Numûru","Find the other prisoners","You must move quickly into Angar Aragín to save Numûru!","Defeat Karâshna Zíri","Free Numûru from his bonds","Sectarios del que Todo lo Ve derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Razâl","Speak with Razâl in the Angar Aragín.","Instancia: Un regalo oscuro","Free the prisoners.","Defeated Barkhûshim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Numûru in the Angar Aragín.","Free the second prisoner","Free the first prisoner","Razâl has faltered!","Ascend the stairs and defeat the Barkhûshim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6707]={"Azruthor and the Dead rush from the vale!","Gúrion is standing near the base of the Hill of Erech.\
\
You have arrived at the Hill of Erech and should now speak to Gúrion.","Gúrion is climbing the Hill of Erech.\
\
You should follow Gúrion toward the summit of the Hill of Erech.","'Honour or not, I am still not certain if I regret joining you here, ${PLAYER}. I suppose I shall soon find out....\
\
'We should advance as quietly as possible, for I do not wish to alert this man to our presence until the time comes.\
\
'Let us begin our ascent, ${PLAYER}. I hope the Dead are kind enough to leave us be....'","Nerzus is standing at the Stone of Erech.\
\
You have followed Gúrion to the Hill's peak, and should now attempt to convince Nerzus and the Ruthless Dead of the invader's deception.","Steward Malthellam seeks to expose and oust the strange invader from Tarlang's Crown before he can rally the Dead to his cause.","DNT -- will not be seen","Gúrion is climbing the Hill of Erech.\
\
You have defeated the Dead again, but should now sprint to the Hill's peak in hopes of avoiding continued attacks by the Dead.","Talk to Nerzus","Follow Gúrion up the Hill of Erech","Talk to Gúrion","'You speak of deception, ${RACE}... yet you know nothing of our plight. Azruthor has given us a means of escape!\
\
'The curse that binds us shall be lifted at this war's end and the line of Isildur shall finally be broken! We shall have no one left to answer to save for the Dark Lord, as it always should have been!\
\
'You are too late, ${PLAYER}... we will overwhelm these lands and the Heirs of Castamir shall lead us all to freedom!'","Gúrion is hiding near the peak of the Hill of Erech.\
\
You have reached a point close to the summit, and should now speak to Gúrion.","Observe the meeting of the Dead and Azruthor","Gúrion is at the peak of the Hill of Erech.\
\
You have defeated Nerzus once more, but many of the Dead have rallied to Azruthor's side in Tarlang's Crown.","Azruthor and Nerzus are at the Stone of Erech.\
\
You should watch the meeting between the invader and the Dead.","Follow Gúrion to the Hill's peak","Follow Gúrion further up the Hill of Erech","Defeat Nerzus","Gúrion is climbing the Hill of Erech.\
\
You have defeated the Dead that attacked you, and should continue up the hill.","<rgb=#FF0000>Gúrion has fallen!</rgb>","Instancia: Un Pacto Oscuro","<rgb=#FF0000>Gúrion must not be defeated</rgb>","Nerzus is at the Stone of Erech.\
\
You should defeat him before warning the people of Blackroot Vale of Azruthor's summoning of the Dead to Tarlang's Crown.","'Partamos ahora, ${PLAYER}.'","'Look ahead, ${PLAYER}! Is that the same Oathbreaker you spoke to once before? Nerzus, was it?\
\
'I do not see the invader yet, so this may be our last chance! You should speak to the Oathbreaker, and try to convince him of his folly!'","'We have kept our lives, ${PLAYER}, but I fear we won little else.\
\
'This Heir of Castamir, Azruthor, threatens the whole of Gondor and we may only count ourselves lucky that all of the Dead did not heed his call. He has fled to Tarlang's Crown, but he may not stay long there before waging war to the south... or even the West for the Anfalas is all but empty.\
\
'You must warn Malthellam and Lady Rosfin at once so the people of Dol Amroth might ready themselves for war in time!'"},
[6708]={"Habla con Andyri","Un Elfo ha caído en batalla. Has fallado como Vigilante.","Andyri está en la cueva de los trolls de piedra.\
\
Has protegido a los Elfos de Andyri mientras se recuperaban y ahora debes hablar con ella.","No permitas que ningún Elfo muera","Debes impedir que los Elfos sean derrotados mientras descansan tras sus batallas.","'Estoy lista para dejar este lugar, ${PLAYER}. Fuimos victoriosos hoy gracias a tu hábil defensa, aunque por poco. Tienes mi agradecimiento y el de mis amigos.'","Defiende a los Elfos hasta que recuperen sus fuerzas","Has llegado a las cuevas de los trolls de piedra, cerca de Lin Giliath, para defender a los Elfos de Andyri mientras se recuperan de su dura batalla.","'Gracias infinitas, ${PLAYER}. Si no hubieras estado aquí... bueno, no tiene sentido recorrer ese triste camino.\
\
'Has salvado a los Elfos de mi compañía, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} Vigilante, y te lo agradezco.'","Instancia: Una Defensa en la Oscuridad","'Por fin, ${PLAYER}. Debemos apresurarnos hacia los Elfos de mi compañía, pues están débiles por la batalla y no podrán defenderse por mucho tiempo.'","Andyri está esperando para hablar contigo dentro de las cuevas de los trolls de piedra."},
[6709]={"'We have always had to defend our lands from the creatures of the wild, and from bands of roaming Orcs. But things have never been this bad in Wildermore.'","Assist Gárwig in Forlaw","Speak with Gárwig at the gate.","Speak with Gárwig","'I... I cannot believe this. What do we do?'\
\
Cyneberg recovers a little when she sees her Reeve lying still in the snow.\
\
'We must get the Reeve indoors at once. He is too frail to be out in the snow!'","Help Gárwig","Gárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw.\
\
You should speak with Gárwig.","Gárwig is pale and breathless, his eyes wide in his shock at the cruel death of his remaining sons.\
\
'Why did it not take me instead? What does the creature want with us?\
\
'How can it be stopped?'","A disturbance at the west gate has come to the attention of the Reeve.","'Well, at least we have defeated them, from the looks of it. You there -- tell me what happened here.'","Assist Gárwig in Forlaw.","Follow Gárwig and speak with him","Instance: A Disturbance at the Gate"},
[6710]={"'I suppose this must be a taste of the mortals' Doom, to know that all we hold dear must slip from us. It is a wisdom that has been largely held from me until now.\
\
'I will not flinch from acting, though the price be heavy. Come, ${PLAYER}, let us go back to the Court and our waiting council of war.'","'Does it seem a riddle to you, what we have seen this night? The one light was Lothlórien; or rather it was myself; or rather it was this ring I bear upon my finger.'\
\
Suddenly, you are able to see a ring upon her finger, bright as a distant star.\
\
'And the darkness it vied with was Dol Guldur. In the Mirror we saw two possibilities of what might come. We may abandon our strife against these foes, and their power will grow and grow. Or we may snuff them out... but be ourselves ever -- diminished. I cannot say, precisely. I could not see as clearly as I have been used.\
\
'For in truth, some of my powers are failing whether we war against Dol Guldur or not. This ring that I revealed to you just now was forged in the same days the Dark Lord forged his One. Though it was ever hidden from him and its own power kept safe, still the rings were tied. Celebrimbor, for all he did, could not sever that bond, I am afraid. Now that the One is no more, all the others fade and falter. I doubt I shall ever see clearly within my Mirror again, and much else shall be lost to me.\
\
'Still, I would pay the price again, in a heart beat.'","Galadriel has stepped up to her Mirror and looks ready to gaze into it.","'Stand beside me. Gaze into the Mirror with me. In truth, I do not know what I will see here, though there is a great deal I would know if I could. I feel certain, however, that now is the time and that we should not wait.\
\
'Are you ready, friend?'","Hear what the Mirror shows","You have found a grave-faced Galadriel in her garden, by her Mirror, awaiting you.","Habla con Galadriel","You should approach Galadriel.","Galadriel seems to have seen all that she will see in the Mirror, tonight, and is ready to talk with you.","Galadriel is gazing into her Mirror. Stand by her and she will relate all that she sees.","Instancia: Un Reflejo Vacilante","Approach Galadriel"},
[6711]={"Asiste al Concilio final","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir?'","Habla con Glorfindel","Glorfindel te ha convocado a un último Concilio, que decidirá el destino de Narmeleth.'","Instancia: Un Consejo Final","Asistir al Concilio final.","Hablar con Glorfindel para volver a Rivendel.","'Debemos regresar a Rivendel, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[6712]={"After a moment, the eyes of all of the dwarves turn to Dáin","The Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After Dáin revealed that he encountered Durin's Bane, the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ have grown uneasy. You should calm them down.","As dawn breaks, you discover a great gathering of survivors at Durin's Stone","Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have paid your respects to the other dwarf-kings. You should talk to Thorin at the central pyre at Durin's Stone.","Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After finding King Thráin lost in thought beside Kheled-zâram, he told you to return to Thorin and let his son know that he would soon return. You should talk to Thorin.","It appears Nár has quietly followed you to the gates of Khazad-dûm","As the dwarves again fall silent, King Thráin turns to Thorin","At first, King Thráin says nothing.\
\
After a moment, he straightens his beard and turns to the other survivors.","It appears King Thráin has returned to the pyres at last","Pay your respects to King Onúr and the Landorrim","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After the lighting of the final pyres, the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs has come to an end. You should talk to Dáin.","Talk to Thorin","The Kings of the Seven Houses have gathered at Durin's Stone.\
\
On the morn after the Battle of Azanulbizar, the Kings of the Seven Houses have again gathered to council. You should listen to the council of the Kings of the Seven Houses.","Nár can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Urge the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ to remain <rgb=#FF00FF>calm</rgb>","Talk to Dáin","Talk to King Thráin","'Ah, Hermáth, I think we are ready to light the final pyres.\
\
'Although I am not certain as to his reasons, I believe my father has gone down to Kheled-zâram. We all mourn in our own ways, I suppose, so perhaps he seeks the wisdom of the First Crafter. Alas, this duty is his alone!\
\
'Would you go find him and tell him that we are prepared?'","As smoke rises into the night sky above the dale, Dáin looks to you","<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to the council of the Kings of the Seven Houses","'Oh, Hermáth, let us hope the burned are never forgotten. They mustn't be!'","'It is time we honoured our fallen as best we can.\
\
'We have stripped them of their mail, taken their weapons, and now we give their bodies to the flame. Bolg and the Orcs will never make trophies of them.\
\
'To burn the dead is not the way of any of our peoples, but it must be done, and we must hold those we lost dear to our hearts and memory.\
\
'Let us honour them together.'","'At last our work is done, but it rings hollow, my friend.\
\
'Many were lost in the fighting, but now even the dale itself lies barren and lifeless. I weep for my father, Náin. I wish he knew how soon victory would come after he fell. Along with the rest of our kin, he too will be burned, but he will remain in my mind as the proud dwarf he was!\
\
'Our friends and cousins mourn their losses, and I would not leave them to grieve alone. I have paid my respects to each of them. I am certain they would welcome any words of comfort from you as well, Hermáth.\
\
'Once that is done, you ought to talk to Thorin. I believe we need only await King Thráin before this grim task is finished.'","'I crossed the threshold, and the First Hall laid before me....'","Surviving Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ have gathered at Durin's Stone.\
\
After a night of fitful rest, you have awoken to find the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ gathered at Durin's Stone. You should join the gathering of survivors there.","'Nár is right.\
\
'All among my Haban'akkâ have earned a night's rest, but far too many of our kin and cousins shall not wake again. Let Khazad-dûm bear witness to their deeds, both great and small.\
\
'And so, we shall not return to Amdân tonight. Durin himself shall watch over us!'","King Thráin might be found by the banks of Kheled-zâram.\
\
After preparing the final pyres at Azanulbizar, Thorin has asked you to find King Thráin.","Rest at Durin's Stone","King Thráin can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After Azog's defeat and the routing of the Orcs at Azanulbizar, King Thráin has returned to the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to King Thráin.","Dáin can be found in the First Hall of Khazad-dûm.\
\
Dáin is recounting his tale of entering the First Hall of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.","Wait for King Thráin","Pay your respects to King Drógar and the Narfanghoth","As King Thráin prepares to order the lighting of the pyres, he calls to you","King Thráin and Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
King Thráin has asked Thorin what he believes should be done at Azanulbizar. You should listen to King Thráin and Thorin.","The pyres can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
King Thráin has asked you to join him in lighting the final pyres at Durin's Stone.","The pyres can be found at Durin's Stone.","King Thráin can be found by the banks of Kheled-zâram near Durin's Stone.\
\
You have found King Thráin at the banks of Kheled-zâram. Speak with him.","Witness as Nár inspects the head of Azog","Follow King Thráin","The Battle of Azanulbizar has ended, but at unimaginable cost.","King Thráin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You should talk to King Thráin.","King Thráin gazes into Kheled-zâram...","Pay your respects to King Ugún and the Kámbrada","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
Dáin has been forced to rebuke King Thráin with a tale of the aftermath of Azog's slaying. You should listen to Dáin.","Pay your respects to King Vékun and the Zhélruka","Without another word, Nár leaves","Listen to the council of the Kings of the Seven Houses","Pay your respects to King Shâlim and the Abnúzhu","As murmurs among the survivors fall silent, King Thráin begins to speak","King Thráin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
King Thráin has returned to Durin's Stone. You should wait for King Thráin to give the order to light the final pyres.","'My heart is heavy, friend. I wish it hadn't come to this....'","King Thráin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After Thorin gave his counsel, King Thráin and the other Kings of the Seven Houses have agreed to the war's ending. You should talk to King Thráin.","The Kings of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, Temámir, Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
Before the final pyres are lit at Durin's Stone, Dáin has suggested that you pay your respects to the Kings of the Seven Houses. Afterward, Dáin has asked you to talk to Thorin.","'It is time, Hermáth.'","Listen to Dáin's tale","As the other Kings of the Seven Houses nod in agreement, King Thráin falls silent","You should rest with King Thráin and the surviving Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ at Durin's Stone.","King Thráin can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.\
\
With the head of Azog prepared, King Thráin intends to send a warning to the Orcs of Moria. You should talk to King Thráin.","Nár says nothing.\
\
His face is stern, but it does little to mask the tears dried upon his cheeks.","Witness the lighting of the pyres at Durin's Stone","Among the survivors, you discover the Kings of the Seven Houses gathered in council","Nár can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After King Thráin set Azog's head upon a stake, Nár has arrived at the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Nár.","Instancia: Un ajuste de cuentas final","Talk to Nár","Join the gathering of survivors at Durin's Stone","King Thráin can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After witnessing Nár return the coin-purse to Azog, King Thráin has beckoned you over. You should talk to King Thráin.","Listen to King Thráin and Thorin","'Oh, Hermáth... I wish I did not have to speak of it.\
\
'But I will say what I must.'","'Ah, you return. But where is my father, Hermáth?'\
\
You explain that King Thráin sent you to inform Thorin that he would arrive shortly, despite his leg-wound.\
\
'He is stubborn as ever, I see. We will wait, then.'\
\
You and Thorin wait for a time, until finally King Thráin begins to shuffle up the ramp to the central pyre.\
\
'There he is!'","'Azog sealed his fate the moment he slew my father, Thrór. This shall be a fitting end for him, I think.'","Aid King Thráin and light the pyres at Durin's Stone","King Thráin can be found at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After the felling of trees and the raising of great pyres at Azanulbizar, the time has come to burn the fallen Kings and their guards at Durin's Stone.","King Thráin has set the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ on a grim task. You should aid the Haban'akkâ.","'Yes?'\
\
King Thráin appears lost in thought, his gaze fixed upon the dark waters of Kheled-zâram. You tell him the final pyres are prepared, and that Thorin has sent for him.\
\
'So be it.'","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After the other lords and Kings of the Seven Houses have expressed apprehension about continuing the war, King Thráin and the other dwarves have looked to Dáin. You should speak with him now.","Dáin and Thorin stand beside a newly-set stake at the gates of Khazad-dûm","Aid the Haban'akkâ","Witness as King Thráin places Azog's head upon a stake at Khazad-dûm","As Dain finishes his tale, King Thráin sighs and murmurs rise among the survivors","Find King Thráin at Kheled-zâram","Pay your respects to King Jegín and the Temámir","Listen to Dáin","Dáin is recounting the tale of what he saw in the First Hall of Khazad-dûm."},
[6713]={"Golodir felled the mighty Thrúgrath, but his body is broken and he will not survive.","Golodir has gone ahead. Can you find him before it is too late?","Habla con Corunir","'We... we cannot stay here, ${PLAYER}.'","'I am satisfied... ${PLAYER}. If the Gondorians... know of what they speak... then my death... will see Mordirith defeated....\
\
'Corunir... my friend... when this war is over... I ask that you ensure... safety for Wenda....'\
\
Golodir is quiet for a long moment. When he finally speaks again, it is for the last time.\
\
'It is enough... for me... to die thinking of Lorniel... as I always...'","Find Golodir","Despite his broken body, Golodir smiles at you","'Amegil did not repent of the words he spoke to Golodir, but he did tell me which way he seemed to go: here, to this encampment of Orcs. We may yet find Golodir, if we hurry!'","Corunir mourns the loss of his friend on the Pelennor.","Corunir hopes that you will be able to find Golodir before he comes to harm.","You have come with Corunir to an outpost on the Pelennor where the fighting has been thick.","<rgb=#FF0000>Corunir must not be defeated</rgb>","Instancia: Una venganza final","Habla con Golodir","'He is gone. I... I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[6714]={"Debes ahuyentar a la bandada de dragonzuelos que han descendido sobre las ruinas élficas de Pembar desde la cima de Zirakzigil. Si lo consigues, los elfos te permitirán usar la antigua forja de las ruinas y así potenciar el granate imbuido que llevas contigo.","Derrotado Dragonzuelo alado recién nacido","¡Has creado un granate potenciado!","Derrotada Rimlúg la Madre Alada","'Me atrevo a decir que los pocos dragonzuelos que quedan de este grupo no se alejarán mucho de las cumbres de Zirakzigil por un tiempo tras esta dolorosa derrota.'","Derrota Dragonzuelos alados jóvenes (${VALUE}/10)","Derrota a Rimlúg la Madre Alada","Derrotado Dragonzuelo alado joven","'¿Quieres regresar a Echad Dúnann?'","Instancia: Un Vuelo de Dragonzuelos","La enfurecida Madre Alada ha descendido al patio en el centro de las ruinas. Enfréntate a ella y derrótala para expulsar a los dragonzuelos de las ruinas para siempre.","Usa el yunque antiguo","Habla con Perimbant para volver a Echad Dúnann.","Caza a los dragonzuelos más jóvenes evitando a sus hermanos mayores.","Derrota Dragonzuelos alados recién nacidos (${VALUE}/20)","Usa la antigua forja para potenciar tu granate imbuido.","Habla con Perimbant"},
[6717]={"Defeat the roc huntress","You have joined Gôbezhir to present the axe he made to Mêshaget. You should talk to Gôbezhir.","The roc huntress is defeated","Watch Gôbezhir present the weapon to Mêshaget","'Hah! That cursed bird wanted to taste dwarf, and got a taste of my axe instead!\
\
'This axe is a true marvel indeed. A weapon such as this needs a name, don't you think? I shall call it... Semakéfë! That means Sky-splitter in Temîk. Perhaps you should see if old Gôbezhir is all right. I am relieved that he doesn't seem to need new trousers.'\
\
Mêshaget, flush with excitement from the battle, laughs as he admires his new weapon.","As you watched Gôbezhir give the weapon to Mêshaget, your company was attacked by a roc huntress. You should defeat the roc attacking you.","You have joined Gôbezhir to present the axe he made to Mêshaget. You watch Gôbezhir give the weapon to its recipient.","'By the Fathers, that was close! Those awful birds grow more aggressive by the day! It was my wish that the axe serve Mêshaget well, but I did not expect it to be so soon, or to be present to witness it!\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}, walk me back to the forges, where I belong.'","'It is beautiful, is it not, ${PLAYER}? The blade is razor-sharp and will hold its edge longer than any other before it needs to be sharpened! A lifetime of crafting experience and knowledge went into this weapon. It was also made from the kindness of a new friend who helped an old dwarf when he needed it.'\
\
Gôbezhir playfully winks at you.\
\
'And here comes Mêshaget!'","You're under attack!","Gôbezhir Firmhand, master smith of Jiret-menêsh, has decided to give his life's masterwork as a gift to Mêshaget.","Instancia: Un regalo para el futuro","As you watched Gôbezhir give the weapon to Mêshaget, your company was attacked by a roc huntress. Together, you and Mêshaget defeated the aggressive avian. You should talk to Mêshaget.","Talk to Mêshaget","Talk to Gôbezhir"},
[6718]={"'Tienes que avanzar y matar a ese troll de piedra. Si lo han capturado, estará en algún lugar más profundo del campamento.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir?'","Has viajado con Ulfar hasta las afueras del campamento de los enanos en el Pantano de los Juncos. Allí esperas poner fin al plan del enano Olwir de capturar un troll de piedra y dárselo como regalo al enano Skorgrím en el norte.","Ulfar te ha dicho que continúes, más adentro en el campamento de los enanos, sin él, y que mates al troll de piedra si encuentras uno.\
\
Ulfar fue herido en la lucha y no pudo seguir contigo. Sin embargo, te dijo que el troll de piedra debe ser eliminado y que estés atento a Olwir, ya que seguramente intentará impedir que mates a la bestia.","'Sí, supongo que he estado alejado de la batalla demasiado tiempo. La herida es dolorosa, pero no mortal. Sin embargo, me impedirá ser de mucha ayuda.\
\
Debes continuar sin mí y matar al troll de piedra, si han capturado uno. Y no olvides estar atento a Olwir, hará todo lo posible por detenerte.\
\
Me quedaré atrás y me aseguraré de que ninguno de estos escape.'","'¡Bien hecho! Me impacienté esperando, así que tuve que ver cómo te iba, pero parece que te las arreglaste bien sin mí. Ese troll de piedra ha caído, y parece que Olwir también. Pagó un alto precio por su crimen, robarle la vaca a Filibert, ¿verdad? Con él fuera, estos enanos no deberían causar más problemas en el Pantano de los Juncos.\
\
En cuanto a Filibert, no te preocupes por él, me aseguraré de que reciba dinero para comprar una nueva vaca.\
\
Has hecho un gran trabajo hoy, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Te lo agradezco.'","Habla con Ulfar","Habla con Ulfar y luego defiéndelo mientras se adentra más en el campamento de los enanos.","Ulfar ha sido herido en la batalla. Habla con él para ver qué quiere que hagas.","Con el troll de piedra y Olwir muertos, regresa con el herido Ulfar y cuéntale lo que ha pasado.","'Muy bien, ahora ten cuidado. Tenemos que entrar en este campamento y matar al troll de piedra que pueden haber capturado.\
\
Además, cuando entremos en el campamento, mantente atento a Olwir. No le agradará vernos intentando matar a su \\qregalo.\\q'","Instancia: Un regalo para el norte","Mata al troll de piedra"},
[6719]={"'I meant what I said. I will see these people restored to their homes. I will see them made whole.'\
\
Mizâdi pauses, and her breath becomes hushed.\
\
'I swear it.'","Give the bottle of Khôrob for Gúrumkir","'Oho, you've come to help us, have you? Aid us in our time of need? Well I have great need of you then, friend. Great need.\
\
'The Umûn says I can't have any Khôrob. I know, it is a tragedy. Usually I'd just swipe it as soon as her back was turned, but with this bum leg, it makes any petty thievery a terrible bother. She thinks it makes for bad soldiers. I say it makes for the best soldiers. Or at least the happiest.\
\
'What do you say? Can you make a bottle of Khôrob appear in these old hands?'","Let Mizâdi know you have helped the wounded.","You've found an unattended, mostly full bottle of Khôrob","Listen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversation","Speak with several of the wounded soldiers in Amalíbi's camp and ask if they require aid.","Comfort Jínsa in Amalíbi's encampment","Speak with Mizâdi in Amalíbi's camp","Instancia: Un atisbo de luz diurna","'It is nice of you to ask. Very well, I will tell you of the attack that caused all this.'","Gather fresh bandages for Zagêli","Help Amalíbi's wounded with their various needs.","'Oho, you really did it! Yes, that's the stuff. Don't worry, the Khôrob belongs to all of us in the company, there's no actual thievery. I'd say you've done a great job here. This soldier will be very happy for the rest of the afternoon.'","Give the fresh bandages to Zagêli","'Thank you. I can dress the wound myself. It's the little things that make the days a bit more manageable, don't you think?'","Enter Amalíbi's encampment near Iridír","This crate is filled with fresh cloth, wraps, and bandages","'Ah, it's good of you to ask. It's not much, but these bandages have frayed, and they are more dirt than cloth at the moment.\
\
'Would you see if there are any fresh ones among the quartermaster's things? Nothing worse for the spirit than soggy dressings.'","Listen to Jínsa's story","A small moment of peace has given Mizâdi time to speak with Amalíbi, to see the consequences of her decisions.","'You're helping those in the camp? That is very nice of you. I don't need much, I have a warm bedroll and enough bread to get by.\
\
'Maybe I could tell you my story? These words in my head seem to weigh heavily on me, pressing me down. Unless you don't want to hear it?'","Speak with Jínsa in Amalíbi's camp","Let Mizâdi know you have helped the wounded","Speak with Zagêli in Amalíbi's camp","Listen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversation.","Give the fresh bandages to Zagêli and the Khôrob to Gúrumkir in Amalíbi's camp.","Enter Amalíbi's encampment near Iridír.","Speak with Mizâdi in Amalíbi's camp.","Comfort Jínsa in Amalíbi's encampment.","Ask to hear Jínsa's story","Find a bottle of Khôrob for Gúrumkir","'Thank you for hearing my story, friend. It helps.'","Speak with Gúrumkir in Amalíbi's camp"},
[6720]={"Remain on guard during the confrontation with Azagath","Talk to Khôltekh","'We have found our quarry, ${PLAYER}. The journey that brought us from Umbar Baharbêl as allies is at its end. We have found Azagath.\
\
'But it seems someone else found him first.'","Khôltekh glances at you briefly but says nothing. All of his attention is fastened upon Azagath.","'Steel your resolve, ${PLAYER}. We know not the precise nature of the evil we go to face... but we will face it all the same.'","Servants of the Thardúth await you at Utug-bûr.","Mithrandir and your companions prepare to confront the Thardúth.","Talk to Rothog","Azagath Sea-shadow has suggested that his former allies among the Kindred of the Coins join his new cause.","Your companions stand opposed to Azagath Sea-shadow and the Thardúth he now serves.","The time has come for you and your companions to confront the Thardúth at Utug-bûr.","Confront Azagath in front of Utug-bûr","Talk to Mithrandir in front of the waterfall","Instancia: Un poder mayor"},
[6721]={"Instancia: El deber del guardián","Severin Rodador está junto al Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Severin Rodador está esperando asignarte tu posición en la defensa del pueblo.","Has defendido Puente de Caballetes de los orcos saqueadores.","'Recibí noticias de que algunos granjeros en las Quebradas del Norte se han refugiado en una pequeña cueva y están pidiendo ayuda desde Puente de Caballetes. Antes de tu llegada, temía que estuvieran perdidos, pues no podía abandonar el pueblo con tan pocos defensores — pero con tu llegada oportuna, ahora veo una oportunidad para salvar a esos granjeros.\
\
'Cabalgaré en su defensa, ${PLAYER}, y te confío la seguridad de Puente de Caballetes. Si los orcos atacan mientras estoy fuera, ¡debes mantenerlos alejados del puente a toda costa! Si el puente es tomado, perdemos la pequeña ventaja que tenemos. ¡No dejes que lleguen al puente!\
\
'Unos pocos hombres han prometido ayudar en la defensa. Habla con estos valientes y asígnales sus posiciones. ¡Te veré de nuevo, si nuestras tareas nos llevan a la victoria!'","'Lo hemos logrado, , y Puente de Caballetes está a salvo, por el momento. No creo que los orcos lancen otro ataque por un tiempo — a veces es difícil recordar que ellos también necesitan descansar. Aunque sus amos los empujen con látigos y amenazas, incluso un orco puede sucumbir al agotamiento si se lo presiona demasiado en servicio de la guerra.\
\
'Dime cuándo estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar al pueblo, y podremos esperar el regreso de Severin Rodador. Espero que su tarea haya salido bien, y que los granjeros que fue a salvar hayan sobrevivido a sus peligros.\
\
'Algunos de nosotros fuimos heridos hoy, pero aún nos mantenemos firmes contra los orcos, ¡y lo seguiremos haciendo mientras sea necesario!'","'Puede que no me recuerdes, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero yo sí te recuerdo! Ayudaste a mi papá y a mí a rechazar a los Montebruno en nuestra granja no hace mucho. Cole Culvert ya estaría comiendo de nuestros platos y disfrutando de los frutos de nuestro trabajo si no fuera por ti... ¡y no creas que no lo valoramos!\
\
'Mi papá se puso a pensar, y un día simplemente me preguntó si quería ir con él a luchar contra los orcos. Como yo lo veo, prefiero luchar contra orcos en el norte, por Puente de Caballetes, si eso significa que podemos evitar luchar contra ellos en las calles de Bree, o en nuestros propios campos. Cada uno tiene que hacer su parte.\
\
'He estado practicando con este arco desde que era un niño, y creo que puedo derribar a unos cuantos orcos antes de que se acerquen demasiado. Gritaré sus posiciones desde esa elevación de allá, si son tan audaces como para atacar el pueblo mientras estamos aquí.'","'Nos encontramos una vez más, ${PLAYER}, ¡y debo decirte que tu presencia eleva mi ánimo! Después de que me ayudaste a rechazar a los bandidos de los Montebruno que amenazaban mi granja, me puse a pensar. No está bien que la gente buena viva con miedo. Era hora de devolver el favor que me hiciste.\
\
'Los viajeros que pasaban por Bree hablaban de los ataques de orcos contra Puente de Caballetes, y me di cuenta de que aquí era donde se me necesitaba. Si los orcos se atreven a mostrar sus feas caras otra vez, los rechazaremos y los enviaremos aullando de regreso por las Quebradas, ¡no lo dudo!\
\
'Mi hijo también está aquí. Tiene buen ojo y es hábil con el arco, si lo recuerdas. Me quedaré a la sombra de esa torre y mantendré mi arma lista.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar al pueblo? Esperaremos el regreso de Severin Rodador y le contaremos las grandes hazañas que se realizaron hoy.'","Severin Rodador ha solicitado tu ayuda en la defensa de Puente de Caballetes. El pueblo está muy presionado por los orcos, y se necesitan guardianes para evitar que crucen hacia las Tierras de Bree.","'Hemos repelido a los orcos, por ahora, ¡y los repeliremos de nuevo si es necesario! Espero que no sea por un buen tiempo — ¡necesito una buena noche de sueño!\
\
'Mi papá puede luchar incansablemente, pero yo aún no tengo su resistencia, aunque espero poder decir que tengo su coraje.'","Habla con los defensores de Puente de Caballetes.","'Un guardián como tu también ha venido a ayudar en la defensa. Se llama Hilton Harper, y lo vi revisando la estructura del puente no hace mucho. Deberías hablar con él sobre el plan para defender este lugar, en caso de que los orcos ataquen.'","Hilton Harper está fuera de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Hilton Harper está esperando hablar contigo sobre tu defensa del pueblo.","Severin Rodador te dijo que varios hombres han venido a ayudar en la defensa de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Antes de partir para ayudar a un grupo de granjeros atrapados en las Quebradas del Norte, Severin Rodador te encargó mantener alejados del puente a cualquier orco saqueador. Deberías hablar con los hombres cercanos para asignarles sus posiciones.","'El pueblo está a salvo, por el momento, así que lo considero una victoria, ${PLAYER}. Los orcos atacarán de nuevo, y cuando lo hagan, ¡estaremos listos!'","'Es un placer conocer otros guardianes, ${PLAYER}, ¡y las defensas serán más fuertes con tu presencia aquí!\
\
'Me avergüenza admitir que no hace mucho había perdido la esperanza — la oscuridad que nos rodea parecía demasiado grande, y estaba lleno de desesperación. Pero un joven capitán me mostró que la esperanza siempre permanece, incluso en las situaciones más desesperadas.\
\
'Así que tomé mi espada una vez más y juré luchar en defensa de la gente buena, incluso cuando todos los demás hayan fallado. He venido a Puente de Caballetes, último baluarte entre las Tierras de Bree y los orcos saqueadores del norte; defenderé este lugar hasta que ya no pueda defenderlo más. Prevaleceremos, ${PLAYER}, pero debemos mantenernos alerta. Los orcos podrían atacar en cualquier momento, y si alguno llega al puente, estará perdido. ¡Mantenlos alejados del puente a toda costa!'","Hilton Harper está frente al Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Hilton Harper está esperando hablar contigo sobre la organización de la defensa de Puente de Caballetes.","'Mi papá estaba hablando con otro guardián hace un rato — Harper, se llama. Probablemente esté por aquí cerca. Deberías hablar con él sobre el plan para defender el pueblo, en caso de que los orcos decidan atacar mientras Severin Rodador está ausente.'","Habla con Hilton Harper"},
[6722]={"Gather dishes from the hutch","Fuirion's blood begins to form a pool on the floor, and it is clear that he has sustained a deep slash-wound in his belly","Fuirion is at Gladion's doorstep.\
\
You should examine Fuirion.","'Please hurry, ${PLAYER}, and fetch the healer! She can be found on the other end of the village. Hurry!'","Examine Fuirion","Set the table for six (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find out what the commotion is all about","The table is in Gladion and Limril's home.\
\
You should gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.","'Thank you for the help, ${PLAYER}. But where are Gladion and Fuirion? Really, now they are dreadfully late.'","Limril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should see what else Limril needs.","You should set the table for Limril","'You wish to help with dinner? That is very kind of you, ${PLAYER}! I do not wish to be an ungracious host, for you earned a rest after today.'\
\
You insist that you are up to the task, and ask what can be done to help.\
\
'If you insist, I will not refuse a generous offer. The hutch in the corner -- would you set the table, if you please?'","Instancia: Una Comida Ganada con Esfuerzo","'He stumbled to our doorstep from across the farm, limping. Help us! Someone help my brother!\
\
'Fuirion, what is wrong? Where are you hurt?'","Offer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Fuirion to arrive","Limril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should offer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Fuirion.","The peace is broken by the sound of the door banging open","The hutch is in the corner.\
\
You should gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.","Gladion kneels at the door with his brother in his arms.\
\
You should ask Gladion what happened to his brother Fuirion.","Talk to Limril","You should help by setting the table","While waiting for Fuirion to arrive, Limril has asked you to help with dinner."},
[6723]={"'So Zôreth thinks she can steal Manthríf from my people?'\
\
King Váskmun grasps the mithril-key tightly.\
\
'No! It belongs to my family -- it belongs to me!\
\
'Spakorth still lives, but I cannot know where his will ended and the will of the spirit began.\
\
'We have no time for such things now. Zôreth has betrayed my folk to serve herself! Our time in her service ends today!'","Talk to King Greytooth","Tell King Greytooth the <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb> of the Ring-bearer's quest","King Greytooth is standing in Lûghash. You should tell him of your many tales of valour, especially those you shared with Gimli.","Follow Gimli and join King Greytooth among the Stout-axes of Lûghash","King Greytooth is eager to hear tales of valour from you and Gimli. You should not keep him waiting.","Instancia: Una casa forjada de nuevo","'A tale of valour....\
\
'We have won many battles and many great victories together, my friend. It is hard to think of just one! Which among them speaks most of our trials and of the victories won by our peoples?\
\
'King Greytooth awaits us, so I suppose I'll have to decide soon enough!'","'No! Manthríf is gone... lost... stolen! The death of this wretched woman means nothing!'\
\
King Greytooth swings Dolgráth the Battle-hungry into Zôreth's lifeless body, and spits upon her corpse.\
\
'What right had she to speak of my imprisonment? Zôreth knew of the tortures Sauron visited upon me in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. How could she know such things?! To spread such lies about me—to sow the belief that I could not resist the Dark Lord's tortures and fell prey to the weakness of my forebears... it is unthinkable! And you believe it, don't you?\
\
'For how long have you and Gimli conspired against me? Durin's Folk damned my people! How do I know you did not find it in the Dark Tower when I asked you to search for it? Manthríf is mine—it is mine by right!\
\
'None shall stand against me in my quest to reclaim it! Not Zôreth, not Spakorth, not even you and Gimli!'","Tell King Greytooth the <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb> of the battles of the Hornburg and of the Pelennor Fields","Gimli is addressing King Greytooth in Lûghash. You should listen to his tale.","You have come to Zôreth's chamber with King Greytooth and the Stout-axes. You should now speak to him and confront the Mistress of Lûghash.","King Greytooth is standing in Zôreth's chamber in Lûghash.\
\
Despite freeing his people from the Mistress of Lûghash, King Greytooth appears more troubled than ever. You should speak to him.","Spakorth has noticed a peculiar key upon a necklace worn by King Greytooth. King Greytooth is willing to speak of it, but wishes to do so privately.","As he stands above Spakorth, a grim fury washes across King Váskmun's face","Defeat the fell spirit that was inhabiting Spakorth","Zôreth is standing in her chamber. You should join King Greytooth and the Stout-axes in confronting her and putting an end to her treachery.","With a fateful swing of Dolgráth the Battle-hungry, King Váskmun Greytooth slays Zôreth...","Sversting, the master-smith of Lûghash, has crafted a keen axe for King Greytooth and now wishes to present it to him.","King Greytooth is standing above the defeated Spakorth. You should speak to him and learn what is to be done.","'Time to go, ${PLAYER}.'","Listen to Gimli tell the tale of Smaug and the Battle of Five Armies","Spakorth attempted to steal the key from King Greytooth, and after being thwarted, a fell spirit has risen from him. Spakorth lies wounded, but the fell spirit appears unharmed.","'There she is, ${PLAYER}... the Mistress of Lûghash! \\qSaviour\\q of the Stout-axes! Bah!'\
\
King Váskmun spits in anger and grips Dolgráth the Battle-hungry tightly.\
\
'I think it is time we learned where Manthríf was taken!\
\
'Let us go!'","Confront Zôreth","Overjoyed by the return of their King, Váskmun Greytooth, the Stout-axes of Lûghash have asked you and Gimli to share your tales of valour among the Free Peoples that they might learn more of the world beyond Mordor.","Follow King Greytooth and learn of his secret","Witness Sversting present his tribute to King Greytooth","Habla con Gimli","Gimli is standing in Lûghash.\
\
King Greytooth has asked you and Gimli to share your tales of valour with him and his folk that he might learn of the path that led you to Mordor.","Tell King Greytooth the <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb> of Skorgrím and of the lost Dwarf-kingdom of Khazad-dûm"},
[6724]={"'¿Huargos? Si esas criaturas son algo parecido al gran oso negro que me ha causado tantos problemas, ¡seguro que son feroces!\
\
'No quiero líos con ninguno de esos Huargos. ¡Me voy adentro, sin hacer preguntas!'","Gytha Lainey está en el camino fuera de Sobrecolina.\
\
Has venido a Sobrecolina con Gytha Lainey para proteger a su gente del peligro que los amenaza. Gytha está esperando para hablar contigo sobre cómo proceder.","'Bueno, traes noticias inquietantes, ${PLAYER}, ¿no es así? ¡Y justo ahora mi carreta se ha averiado! Estoy seguro de que esos Huargos que mencionaste no se acercarían jamás a mi hogar en la Colina de Bree.\
\
'Me quedaré con mi amigo Everard hasta que esto pase. ¡Gracias por avisarme!'","'Bien, lo has hecho muy bien, ${PLAYER} — ahora, al menos, los hobbits de aquí deberían estar a salvo por un tiempo, en caso de que no logremos detener a los Huargos.\
\
'Según la dirección de sus huellas antes de que perdiera el rastro, los Huargos deben estar ya en el Bosque del Fardo. Mira hacia el norte e intenta detenerlos antes de que lleguen a la aldea. Para este momento ya se habrán separado, y seguramente merodean con cautela hacia el sur.\
\
'Intentaré detener a cualquiera que llegue a la aldea, ${PLAYER}, pero cuento contigo para derrotar a tantos como puedas mientras se acercan — si demasiadas criaturas llegan a Sobrecolina al mismo tiempo, sin duda seré sobrepasada, y toda esperanza de detenerlas se perderá.'","'No entiendo qué está pasando últimamente en la Comarca.'","Gytha Lainey está en Sobrecolina.\
\
Has derrotado con éxito a la partida de caza de Huargos que se adentró en el Bosque del Fardo y ahora deberías hablar de tu victoria con Gytha Lainey.","'¡Lo has logrado, , y no puedo agradecerte lo suficiente! Los habitantes de Sobrecolina habrían estado indefensos sin nuestra advertencia y ayuda posterior, y aunque quizás no comprendieron del todo el peligro, me reconforta saber que este lugar está a salvo una vez más de los estragos de la guerra.\
\
'No creo que los Huargos vuelvan a estas tierras, al menos por un tiempo. Me pregunto qué fue lo que los trajo aquí.\
\
'Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, y podremos regresar al campamento de Adso.'","Has viajado con Gytha Lainey a la aldea de Sobrecolina, en la Comarca, para defender a su gente de los estragos de un grupo de Huargos que merodea desde el norte.","Gytha Lainey está en la aldea de Sobrecolina.\
\
Ahora que has advertido a los habitantes de Sobrecolina que entren en sus casas, tú y Gytha deben detener a los Huargos invasores.","'¿Ya está todo a salvo?'","'¿Hola? ¿El peligro ha pasado, entonces? Me alegra oírlo. Tú y tu compañera tienen mi agradecimiento, por supuesto.'","'¿Huargos? ¿Qué podría haber traído criaturas tan aterradoras a la Comarca?\
\
'¡Voy a entrar de inmediato — no necesitas decírmelo dos veces, no a este hobbit!'","'Estoy listo para regresar al campamento de Adso, si tú también lo estás. La gente de aquí siempre es amable, aunque no siempre aprecian la presencia de \\qGente Grande\\q como yo. Hoy, sin embargo, creo que sí. Eso me alegra.'","Los habitantes de Sobrecolina siguen con sus quehaceres, ajenos al peligro que acecha en algún lugar al norte de su aldea.\
\
Gytha te ha dicho que adviertas a los habitantes de Sobrecolina que permanezcan dentro de sus casas hasta que el peligro haya pasado.","'¡Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}!'","'Parece que te encargaste de todo. ¡Gracias por eso!'","'¿Qué dijiste? ¿Huargos? ¡Oh cielos, qué clase de criatura es esa? Bueno, sean lo que sean, no tienen nada que hacer en Sobrecolina, ¡y no me importa decirlo!\
\
'Es tarde, y ya pensaba entrar pronto de todos modos. Me iré a dormir, y espero que por la mañana esas criaturas hayan recapacitado y dejen en paz a Sobrecolina.'","Habla con Gytha Lainey","'Parece que no hemos llegado tarde, ${PLAYER} — hemos llegado antes que los Huargos, pero no sé cuánto tiempo pasará antes de que alcancen la aldea.\
\
'Rápido, corre a la aldea y dile a todos los que veas que entren en sus casas y no salgan hasta que digamos que el peligro ha pasado. No aceptes un \\qno\\q como respuesta, ${PLAYER} — sus vidas pueden depender de que hagan lo que decimos.\
\
'Intentaré averiguar cuán lejos pueden estar las criaturas desde que perdí su rastro.'","'¿Así que los Huargos se han ido? Bien, bien. Yo habría salido también, claro, solo para ver de qué se trataba todo esto, pero tenía el té listo y no pude irme.\
\
'¡Buen trabajo, sin duda!'","Habla con los habitantes de Sobrecolina","Instancia: Encargo de Cazadora"},
[6725]={"'Was Shurug-nîn's own adventure like this, ${PLAYER}? The songs and tales record only her deeds of daring and of courage. Much was made of her contests of strength against the dragons, but little is said of the days and weeks between such battles, though they must have existed.\
\
'Will our own song speak of this waggon-ride? I suppose that depends upon what awaits us at the end of it: triumphant victory or crushing defeat.'","If the driver moves away, it should be safe to depart the waggon.","Rahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.","You hear the crunching of footsteps beside the waggon","Talk to Rahâzi inside the waggon","<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for anyone who might approach","Stand near the back of the waggon","You should stand near the back of the waggon and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for anyone to approach too near.","The driver has returned to the side of the waggon","Instancia: Un viaje hacia el peligro","Wait for the driver to leave before departing the waggon","Do not move, and make no noise!","'Now we wait. You might as well make yourself comfortable.'","It will be some time before the waggon arrives. Now you can only wait.","Pass the time while the waggon rumbles to its destination","Together, you and Rahâzi have snuck aboard a waggon carrying supplies and must remain hidden from the Temámir who drives it.","Try not to move or make any noise","'Look at the cargo this waggon transports, ${PLAYER}: these are not the ropes and timbers I expected necessary to finish construction of a fleet of ships. Much of these supplies are wealthy goods and valuables.\
\
'For what purpose does the Temámir waggon-driver bring these items to Sûg Nidar?'"},
[6726]={"Listen to Horn tell his story of King Fengel.","'We will leave at first light. For now you should get some rest.\
\
'In the morning we will continue our journey down the Anduin.'","Corudan is waiting to speak with you beside the river where you have stopped for the night.","Horn is sitting by the fire.","'I think that is enough tale-spinning for one night, ${PLAYER}. I will take the first watch, and I will wake you when it is your turn.\
\
'We will set out again at first light.'","Corudan is sitting by the camp-fire.","'Do you have a story to share?'","Talk to Horn by the camp-fire","'You are fortunate to have friends among the Elves, ${PLAYER}. I would not want to make this journey without a guide, and Corudan appears to know what he is doing.\
\
'But it is not seemly for a Man of Rohan to mingle with Elves, as you saw in Stangard. Of his kind my people have little to say but this: \\qlong-lived and dangerous.\\q\
\
'They have more to say of the folk of Dunland, but none of it is kind and I will not disturb the girl's ears with any of it. I regret Nona's ill welcome at Stangard when she had need of aid, though I understand its root. Her people and mine have a long and unhappy history. I have no quarrel with her personally, but our shared friends and duties make us allies, nothing more than that.'","'This is what she carved into the stone:\
\
'Feckless Fengel, fool I name thee,\
Grief shall be the get of thy greed.\
No lord of your line shall long live,\
Upon thy seat no son shall settle.\
Kin and kingdom your craving hath killed,\
Until the might of the Mark is mended.\
Wyrgende.'\
\
Horn sighs heavily and continues.\
\
'King Fengel was furious, and he ordered Wyrgende's body burned and the stone destroyed, but no man of his company could move her, and every hammer and mattock they set to the stone shattered on contact.'","'I do not have the flowery words or turns of phrase that Corudan and this man Horn have, ${PLAYER}. I write my tale in the hide of my enemies, with Wadu's sword as my quill!'","'We have some time before we should begin the night-watches, ${PLAYER}. Would you find some tale-telling agreeable? I find that the weaving of a good story among companions around a fire can be a pleasant way to pass the time.\
\
'Have a seat and listen, ${PLAYER}. I will begin, and perhaps our companions will have a tale to share as well.'","Instancia: Un viaje en barco","Horn and Nona are sitting on opposite sides of the camp-fire by the Anduin.","Nona is sitting by the camp-fire, waiting to tell her story.","You have travelled by boat down the Anduin in the company of Nona, Horn, and Corudan, but must camp for the night before you proceed further.","Nona is telling a story by the camp-fire.","'That is far enough for today, ${PLAYER}. Horn has already seen to the fire, so now we may sup and take some rest before the night-watches begin.\
\
'We will leave in the morning, at first light. It is not good to travel further south on Anduin at night, unless the need is considerable. The waters become treacherous the nearer you get to Sarn Gebir.'","Talk to Corudan and decide upon a tale to share","'The Elf-queen was right to send this guide with us, ${PLAYER}. He knows the waters and how to keep a boat afloat, which is more than the daughter of Suvulch knows. Were it up to me, I would lead us south on dry land, with springy turf underfoot and no fear of foundering.'\
\
Nona lowers her voice, a rare event for the Dunlending woman.\
\
'The boat is not large enough to keep us from speaking, ${PLAYER}, but as you saw, this horse-lord managed to avoid addressing me in any way once we were on the river. If he has a grievance with me, tell him to air it so I may respond appropriately: with words or with Wadu's sword! I have become tired of his ability to look all around him but not in my direction, whatever direction that happens to be!'","Talk to Corudan","Talk to Nona by the camp-fire","Listen to Nona's story","'I shall go next. My tale concerns King Fengel of Rohan, the grandfather of Théoden King. It is a sad tale, given the happenings of late, but you may find it interesting.'","Talk to Corudan by the camp-fire","Listen to Horn's story","Corudan is by the camp-fire, waiting to speak with you.","Horn is waiting to finish the story of King Fengel and Wyrgende the crone."},
[6727]={"Speak with Herion","<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> before the brave warriors to pay your respects","You kneel in silence at the loss of this brave Gondorian warrior","Erchar is saddened by his decisions","Erchar is at the battleground.\
\
You should speak with Erchar.","'We have returned but not without great loss.'","Instancia: Un Entierro Justo","Listen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion.","'Erchar does not see the greatness that we have accomplished, only the loss. Do not mistake my words, for I too am saddened by the difficulty of our enemy and the lives they have taken. What I ask for is hope from my brothers to get through this dawn-less day.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> before this brave warrior and pay your respects","Erchar and Herion return to the site of the battle that drove them apart and pay their respects before the returning journey to Linhir.","Herion is at the battleground.\
\
You should speak with Herion.","<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> before the brave warrior to pay your respects","The bodies of Gondorian warriors slain by the Corsair forces can be found at the battleground.\
\
You should cover the bodies with soil and pay your respects.","Covered fallen warriors in soil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Covered fallen warrior in soil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Herion is stubborn and cannot see that I have made a mistake in riding west into the enemy. This is not a decision I wish to make again be it rash or wise.\
\
'Come. Let us return to Linhir where I shall apologize to Garvir for my absence and for Herion's.'","'You have made your way to this place of grief with Herion and I thank you for reuniting us for the return to Linhir.'","Herion grows restless and wants to return to Linhir","Speak with Erchar","Erchar and Herion meet at the battleground.\
\
You should speak to Erchar.","Erchar and Herion meet at the battleground.\
\
You should listen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion."},
[6728]={"'You will do as my Queen requests? I think it will prove unnecessary, but I do not want my bride to worry if it might be prevented! Nor do I want my people to wait for any help I might have offered.\
\
'It is not an easy riddle to solve, ${PLAYER}, but I think I have the answer. The three of you will go ahead of me to visit the towns and cities of my kingdom, keeping watch for any sign of the Heirs of Castamir or their supporters, as Arwen requests, but you will go not only in search of danger. You will also go as my emissaries, and to begin my own mission of aid, doing what you can to help the people with their concerns.\
\
'When you have determined the Heirs of Castamir are of no real danger to myself or the kingdom, you will return to me and I will depart with my own travelling companions to further your work. If this will satisfy my Queen and my Council, then I suppose I must be content with the delay. It will be a balm to my spirit to know that you three, at least, will have begun my mission to heal the kingdom of its hurt.'","'Another adventure begins, ${PLAYER}, of a sort. It will not take long to learn if the Heirs of Castamir are truly gone, and when we have done so Elessar can tour his kingdom.\
\
'Let us start by journeying to the Harlond, my friends. The south-harbour is nearest to the city, and from there we can proceed west in search of news.'","Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion","Glindor has brought you to the Tower of Ecthelion, where King Elessar and Queen Arwen await you.","King Elessar and his advisors discuss his plan to tour the kingdom and heal the hurts caused by the war.","Instancia: Un rey debe ver su reino","King Elessar is ready to speak with you about his plans.","Talk to Thalhír in the Tower of Ecthelion","Listen to the discussion of the Heirs of Castamir","'I hesitate to mention it, my King, for I understand the majority of your people are overwhelmed with happiness at both the successful conclusion of the war and with your marriage to the Queen. I do not wish to spoil the broth of positive sentiment by dwelling upon the inclusion of one or two poor ingredients, and those in such tiny quantities.'\
\
Thalhír clears his throat and looks uncomfortable.\
\
'But there have been whispers of discontent in the city following your happy marriage, my King. Few perhaps, but some. I am sure they will disappear in time, as did those of the supporters of the Withered Tree, but as of yet they remain. I have heard tell from other members of the Council that people in the lower circles of the city speak wishfully of the Heirs of Castamir, praying for their return and believing they soon will.'","Talk to Glindor in the Tower of Ecthelion","Thalhír, the Warden of Laws, is in the Tower of Ecthelion and has been called to answer whether the Heirs of Castamir remain a threat to the peace of Gondor.","'We accomplished much good in the fight against Mordor and the forces of Sauron, ${PLAYER}, and prevented the triumph of terrible evil! The War of the Ring, for so I have heard it called in the days since its ending, has left its mark upon us and upon our lands. Our victory came at great cost, and the losses suffered in its achievement still wound those of us who remain. Perhaps they always will. And yet, if I can ease the hurts of my kingdom, I would do it. Can I count upon you to help me with this aim?'\
\
You assure Elessar that you are with him, and he smiles.\
\
'I knew our minds would be alike in this. This, then, is my purpose: I wish to travel my kingdom, from town to town, speaking with the people. I wish to hear what it is they lack, and to provide it; I wish to know how the war has injured them, and do what I can to repair those injuries. I want my people to know that their King is with them, not a distant figure in the Tower of Ecthelion, but a man who knows them and will strive every day of his life to prove he is worthy of Gondor.\
\
'I want to tour the kingdom, and see what I can do to heal the hurts of the war.'","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Tower of Ecthelion","Listen to the discussion of King Elessar's plans","Queen Arwen is in the Tower of Ecthelion and wishes to speak with you about a special task.","'King Elessar and Queen Arwen will see you now.'","'My husband so greatly desires to speak with his people and mend the pain of the hurts they suffered that I fear he will give no thought to his own protection, ${PLAYER}. I turn then to you, and to those others who hold him dear!\
\
'I ask this of you, ${PLAYER}, and of my husband's boon companions: Legolas of Eryn Lasgalen and Gimli the Dwarf, of Erebor. Where Elessar wishes to venture, I ask that you three travel first, with your ears listening and your eyes sharpened. Look for any sign that the Heirs of Castamir remain a danger to the kingdom or to the King, and make the path he plans to travel as secure as you may.\
\
'Only this will ease the burden of my heart.'","King Elessar has summoned you to the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith, where he wishes to discuss his plans with you.","King Elessar is in the Tower of Ecthelion, waiting to hear if you will agree to this new plan."},
[6729]={"Defend yourself against the attacking Corsairs.","Gladion is at the Corsair encampment in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should speak with Gladion.","Gladion's anguish is severe. It is best that you return to Dínadab....","Speak with Gladion","Instancia: Una Vida Pende de un Hilo","Fuirion's life hangs on a thread, and Hebil, a cruel Corsair captain, stands in the way of his rescue.","'No, no, Fuirion, my brother.... His wounds were too much, he was too weak!'","Defend yourself against the attacking Corsairs","Speak with Hebil","'Can't you see this fool has a death wish? I will see that his wish is granted. Every so often he murmurs about some woman, some great love, I am sure. \\qLimril, Limril,\\q he calls. Is he a spurned lover? It does not matter to me. It is a death sentence to walk into this camp, as you will both soon find out.'","Hebil stands over Fuirion in the middle of the corsairs' encampment.\
\
You should speak with Hebil.","Fuirion has collapsed!","Hebil stands over Fuirion in the middle of the corsairs' encampment.","Try to reason with Hebil"},
[6730]={"'Nay, do not interrupt, ${PLAYER}. I am waiting for Gadda to finish his thought.\
\
'You were saying, Gadda? Things are worse now -- since what? What has changed, in your view of things?'","Wait until Sithric is gone, then speak with Stanric","Stanric listens calmly as you share your impressions of the stagnant, malnourished state of things in Stangard.\
\
'Yes, ${PLAYER}... everything you say is true. Perhaps there is something that can be done. Let us all speak our minds!'","'Come, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps hearing of our unnecessary hardships from a stranger will make them realize that something must be done.'","Now that you have assessed the hardships of Stangard, it is time to make an appeal to the leaders for change.","Sithric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.","Watch the discussion in the Mead Hall.","See what Gadda plans to do","'It is well that Stanric sent that fool back to his post. Any more insolence, and I would have seen to it that he was imprisoned for his treasonous words.\
\
'Keep out of this, ${CLASS}. You are not of the Rohirrim, and Stangard's affairs are no concern of yours.'","Sithric has warned you to keep out of Stangard's affairs","Instancia: Una apelación lógica","Gadda stands with you in the Mead Hall of Stangard.\
\
You should speak with Gadda.","Watch the discussion","'That is all I can say for now. I thank you for your interest in our hardships, ${PLAYER}. Your concern is deeply felt.'","Stanric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.","Address your observations to Stanric when he is ready to hear you","Sithric is in the Mead Hall of Stangard.","Observe the leaders' discussion","You should observe the discussion between the leaders of Stangard.","'Our hands are tied here, ${PLAYER}. The king... is not the man he once was. To defy him, even for good reason, would not end well for me or my men.\
\
'But I have an idea. You are not truly bound by our laws. If you can think of anything you could do that would help us, you have my blessing.\
\
'That... that is all I will say on this matter. Sithric cannot imprison you, a guest, for any of your deeds in Eorlsmead, as long as no crime is committed.'","Talk to Sithric","Talk to Stanric","Stanric is in the Mead Hall.\
\
You should speak with Stanric about what you saw in Stangard.","Sithric is out of earshot -- you should speak with Stanric again"},
[6731]={"'Habiendo cumplido mi obligación de presentarme ante Théoden lo mejor que se pudo, dejé Edoras y continué mi viaje. Pasaría por el Paso de Rohan y luego giraría hacia el norte, a tierras que nunca había visto.'","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre el viaje","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre su viaje","Instancia: Muy Lejos de Gondor","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre la misión","Considera a Háma, Portero de Théoden","Denethor, el Senescal de Gondor, lucha con muchas dificultades.","'Pero al acercarme a los Vados del Isen, para mi sorpresa encontré a alguien que no esperaba ver.\
\
'Me desmonté para hablar con él.'","Escucha el relato de Boromir sobre su viaje","Escucha el relato de Boromir","'Antes de partir, mi padre me insistió en la necesidad del secreto. \\qLos enemigos podrían acechar en cualquier parte, hijo mío\\q, me dijo. \\qRecuerda que Gondor te necesita. Regresa con el conocimiento que el Medio Elfo pueda proveer, tan pronto como puedas. ¡Más pronto aún, si crees que la misión es una locura!\\q\
\
'Le aseguré que no abandonaría la misión, y partí al amanecer, tomando el camino del oeste hacia Rohan.'","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre el resto del viaje","'Mi padre es sabio en maneras en las que yo nunca podré serlo, pues soy en mis propios huesos un hombre de armas; las historias con las que crecí me moldearon para ser así. Pero el Senescal de Gondor debe ser un hombre instruido si ha de guiar a Gondor a través de tiempos tan turbios como estos. Qué significaba el nombre \\qImladris\\q para mi padre no quiso decir, solo que era un lugar muy al norte donde vivía Elrond, el Medio Elfo, de quien se decía que era el más grande de los sabios de la Tierra Media, astuto y peligroso. \\qPocos o ninguno en Gondor saben dónde se halla este lugar\\q, nos dijo mi padre.\
\
'Mi hermano Faramir se ofreció de inmediato para buscar ese lugar y preguntar a Elrond el Medio Elfo si conocía el significado de los... numerosos presagios extraños... que habíamos visto en días recientes. Yo sabía que el camino estaría lleno de peligro, y tomé la misión para mí mismo. Mi padre se encolerizó por mi decisión y discutió contra ella, pero al fin me dio permiso para partir. Debió ver que yo podía encontrar el valle secreto donde yace Imladris y traer de vuelta conocimientos para ayudar a Gondor.'","Considera a Éomer, Mariscal de la Marca","En junio, Boromir y su hermano Faramir fueron convocados por su padre, el Senescal de Gondor, a la Torre Blanca.","Considera a Gríma Lengua de Serpiente","Alguien inesperado dejó su hogar para hablar con Boromir cerca del Paso de Rohan.","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre Rohan","Aunque se le negó una audiencia con Théoden, Boromir habló con varios miembros de su corte.","Considera a Éowyn, Dama de Rohan","Considera a Théodred, heredero de Théoden","Boromir continúa el relato de su viaje.","Boromir ha aceptado contarte el relato de su viaje desde Gondor.","'Temí haberlo ofendido, pero intenté no mortificarme con ello. No había ido a visitarlo a su hogar, después de todo. Si debía dejar su torre y el valle de Isengard para interrumpir mi misión, que cargara él con el peso de mi lengua inexperta. Soy un hombre de armas, como he dicho antes, y no estoy habituado a las costumbres de los Magos.\
\
'Reanudé mi viaje. Ya estaba muy lejos de Gondor, pero aún quedaba un camino más largo por recorrer.'","Habla con Boromir y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre Gondor","'Durante mucho tiempo mi padre vigiló la Tierra Negra de Mordor, y a su orden los soldados de Minas Tirith nunca relajaron su guardia. Las órdenes del Senescal se respetan, como es debido, pero ¿qué hombre desde los altos muros de Minas Tirith no podía ver el humo alzándose del Monte del Destino, lejano y aun así demasiado cercano? En las tabernas de la ciudad lo llamaban un funesto presagio, y en las cámaras altas del consejo mi padre coincidía con su gente, aunque ellos no lo supieran.\
\
'Pero nadie podría haber previsto el ataque que surgió desde Mordor. Una gran fuerza avanzó por Ithilien, expulsando a nuestros soldados, y en Osgiliath detuvimos su avance cuanto tiempo pudimos, y destruimos el puente tras nosotros.\
\
'Hubo algo extraño en aquella batalla, amigos míos. Hubo... presagios extraños... antes y durante el combate, pero ni mi hermano Faramir ni yo pudimos comprender su significado. Hablamos de ellos con nuestro padre.'"},
[6732]={"Instancia: La Voluntad de un Sabio","Observa a Isferon abrir las cajas y descubrir sus secretos.","Isferon está de pie dentro de la cueva.\
\
Isferon está abriendo las cajas que le dejó Berenin.","'Regresemos a Duillond, ${PLAYER}. Tengo mucho en qué pensar.'","Isferon está de pie dentro de la cueva.\
\
Isferon ha abierto las tres cajas que le dejó su amigo Berenin cuando zarpó hacia el Oeste.","Has llegado a la cueva donde Isferon ha estado guardando las cajas que le dejó Berenin.","'Tengo las tres llaves listas. ¡Veamos qué secretos me dejó Berenin cuando zarpó hacia el Oeste!'","Isferon está de pie dentro de la cueva.\
\
Isferon está esperando para hablar contigo antes de abrir las tres cajas y descubrir qué secretos le dejó su amigo Berenin cuando zarpó hacia el Oeste.","'Te lo agradezco, . He aprendido más de lo que esperaba, y siento que eso me ha enriquecido más que cualquier otra cosa. Avísame si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, y podemos regresar a Duillond.'"},
[6733]={"You study some of the scrolls in this pile, but it avails you little","'It may come to nothing, ${PLAYER}. There are few in the city who would believe that a man might return from the darkest depths of evil. Though he was once Eärnur, he has worn many guises since he was King of Gondor. He cannot be the man he was, and despite the rules of succession he has been corrupted by Angmar, and by Mordor.\
\
'But we must remain alert. If Gothmog does seek to seize the throne of Gondor, we must oppose him... no matter the cost.'","'You had better fortune than I did, ${PLAYER}, for I have yet to find anything. Let me see this scroll.'\
\
Mithrandir takes it from you and quickly reads the yellowed parchment. After a moment he looks up at you again.\
\
'There are matters of interest in this scroll. It speaks of not one challenge but two, a detail of which I was not aware. It appears that the Witch-king challenged Eärnur to ride forth, and the King was dissuaded from that foolishness by his Steward, a wise man named Mardil. That name I do know, for he would become the first of the Ruling Stewards when Eärnur disappeared into Minas Morgul. It is from his line that Denethor draws his authority.'","'These names are not familiar to me, but I do have a dim recollection that a man named Orolang may have committed some heroic deed at the Battle of Fornost. It is the barest hint of a memory, but I have not even that for these others. Macilnis is a common name among the women of Gondor; none of the histories I have seen include any women in the retinue of Eärnur's knights, but this scroll appears genuine to me and I have no reason to doubt it.\
\
'Some of Eärnur's knights have returned to trouble Middle-earth as Cargûl, but the power he wielded as Mordirith seems more deadly than theirs. We should expect he will be more powerful still in his guise as Gothmog.\
\
'And yet, somewhere behind these masks, does any of Eärnur remain? He was bold but foolish. Can it be that Gothmog will be the same?'","Mithrandir is in the Old Archives.","'We should leave this place. It is no longer as comfortable or as familiar as it once was.'","None of these books mention Eärnur's name, as far as you can tell","Mithrandir is in the Old Archives, and he bears a worried expression.","You study many of the rolled scrolls, but find nothing relevant","You have found a book detailing the lineage of the Kings and the Stewards of Gondor, and should show it to Mithrandir.","You have come with Mithrandir to the Old Archives of Minas Tirith, in order to help the Wizard piece together something that has troubled him.","You have found a scroll bearing Eärnur's name in many locations, and should show it to Mithrandir.","The books are falling apart, and you handle them gingerly but find little of note","You unroll a number of the old scrolls, but nothing catches your eye","Talk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives","'You found something else? Ah, yes, this book contains diagrams describing the passage of succession through the line of Kings, and then through the line of the Ruling Stewards.\
\
'Do you see? Here is Mardil, the first of the Stewards, who ruled Gondor after Eärnur was taken into the darkness of Minas Morgul. Mardil swore an oath to rule only until the King returned, and each Ruling Steward has made the same vow.'\
\
Mithrandir looks around, furtively, ensuring that you are alone. When he is satisfied that you are alone in the Archives, he continues.\
\
'Perhaps at one time the Stewards believed the line of Kings would return, but that possibility must now seem quite unlikely. We should not speak of it, even here, but there is one on his way to Minas Tirith who will remind Denethor of his vow. The King may very well return to Gondor, and the rule of the Stewards will no longer be necessary.'","You find a dusty tome containing records of the Kings and Stewards","'Welcome to the Old Archives, ${PLAYER}. They were carved into the pier-rock in the centre of the Sages' Neath when the city was still called the Tower of the Sun. This was the original library and store-house of the city, and it remains a trove of ancient knowledge and secrets.\
\
'There is much to discover in the scrolls and books that are here kept, but few in these days give much thought to these dusty shelves. There is no semblance of order to be found. It was in these dark chambers that I found the Scroll of Isildur, and learned much that I needed to know.'","This pile of scrolls does not contain the information you seek","You pull many of the books at random, but do not find anything useful","Listen to Mithrandir in the Old Archives","Mithrandir has asked you to search one of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.","Mithrandir is inside the Old Archives.","Mithrandir is in the Old Archives of Minas Tirith.","Show the book you found to Mithrandir in the Old Archives","Search the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur","Instancia: Cuestión de linaje","You find a yellowed scroll that bears Eärnur's name many times throughout","Mithrandir has asked you to search another of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.","Show the Eärnur scroll to Mithrandir in the Old Archives","'Eärnur was mighty, and he did not lack for courage, but he possessed none of the caution that could have saved him from doom. He had great victory at Fornost, when he defeated the Witch-king of Angmar, but that victory stirred his pride to great heights. The Witch-king fled; Prince Eärnur believed he had nearly rid Middle-earth of that terrible foe, and cursed his failure to end it there.\
\
'Years later, the Witch-king issued a challenge to Eärnur, now the King of Gondor, and summoned him to Minas Morgul. Eärnur went to that dark city to face his hated foe, and was lost.\
\
'We know now that his will was mastered, and he became the loyal servant of his former enemy. He took a new name, Mordirith, and was given the rule of Angmar while the Witch-king managed the interests of Mordor elsewhere in Middle-earth. Through your own efforts and those of the Rangers and the Champion of Angmar, he was defeated, but it seems that victory was not to last. He maintains some bond to his former life, and it allowed his dark master to draw him back before he was lost for good.'","The pages of these books are very faded, and tell you nothing of interest"},
[6734]={"'Ah, you do see into our hearts, Frodo, as only a hobbit and an old friend could ever do. Well, you have my word then. Yours too, Merry? Good. Neither of us shall go back into Mordor during our stay in Gondor.\
\
'But if the riddle of those squinty fellows drives me to jibbering, it will be on your conscience!'","Listen to Frodo's answer to the complaint.","Approach the table","Habla con Merry","Eat or drink some more (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should approach the table, where the four hobbits have already begun.","Habla con Frodo","Habla con Sam","Eat or drink","Habla con Pippin","Pippin wishes to speak to you.","You should join in the meal and partake of the food and drink laid out on the table.","You should help yourself to some more food and drink while the four friends talk.","'No, and much has come of it, as I will tell you if you will stop frowning so sternly at me for a moment and listen. I confess, when first we set our hearts on seeing Mordor it was a foolhardy lark. We were thinking only of the treasure chest Bilbo was said to have returned with, and seeing what we had not yet seen. But that is not at all what we found.'\
\
Merry goes on to describe the two encounters with the half-orcs, the riddles they let drop, and all that followed in the hopes of unravelling them.\
\
'And so, you see Frodo, we have had a proper adventure of our own, in the end.'","You should hear what Sam says for himself.","You should hear what Pippin says to Frodo.","'They weren't so lavish as all that, as you put it, and besides, less than half were mine, truly, but only gifts Mr. Frodo refused. He has taken not a one gift, has he, though ever so many have been laid at his feet these last days. \
\
'But tell us, Mr. Merry, about this hidden house they have built for us, and what a palace it is, or so I've heard tell.'","You have gone down with Pippin and Merry to Cormallen, to share a meal with Sam and Frodo, who have been spending their days there.","'Don't worry, ${PLAYER}, we didn't wait to start eating. Or making merry. Still, I am awfully glad you are here to join us. I don't think we are in any danger of running short on food or drink, for that matter.\
\
'Sit down and have some, please!'","'No, Pippin, I am being quite serious. Those clever arguments might work on Aragorn or Gandalf, who do not see things quite at our level, as it were -- but it is me to whom you are talking. The time of hobbits going into Mordor should be done, I think. In fact, I have been thinking a great deal about how the time of our adventuring is coming to an end.'","Instancia: Una comida en Cormallen","Enjoy the hobbits' company","Hear Merry's reply to Frodo."},
[6735]={"Sigileth wipes the tears from her eyes.\
\
'I have said my part. I believe Silirtas heard my words... but I cannot know for certain.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Hail</rgb> the spirit, if spirit it be","Learn the severity of Corudan's injuries","The wound Nakási gave to my brother was deep; it worsened with travel, soaking through our makeshift bandages.","Hear what Cúridwan had to say of the unnatural chill","'That is... a curious sight...\
\
'In what direction do these animals travel?'","Listen to Sigileth's account","Ask Sigileth what she believes happened","'I urged you to come with us, Silirtas, to face a great and unknown evil. I thought despite every danger that lay ahead of us, if any need perish, it would be Sigileth of Lórien. I thought I could keep you safe! I am so sorry!\
\
'When you were slain by Azagath before the door of Utug-bûr, I fell into despair. I thought I too must die to atone for that terrible deed, for robbing you of the life you might have had; only the voice of  drew me out of that darkness.\
\
'${PLAYER:Her[f]|His} words made me realize something, dear Silirtas. Every moment of every day, for every person in this Middle-earth, is a gift: not of treasure, but of choice. Every point in time gives you the opportunity to decide how you choose to use that moment. You chose to fight the fading of your people. You chose to venture with an Elf and a  you had known for less than a day to combat an evil of the Elder Days. Those choices were yours, Silirtas, and I am inspired by them! I celebrate them!\
\
'But I have learned there is one more choice you might make, dear one!'","Follow Sigileth's account of her return from the Fearwater","Hear what Cúridwan had to say about Corudan's injuries","Sigileth wishes to tell you about her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.","Hear what Corudan had to say","Hear what Sigileth believed of the spirit","'Corudan lost a great deal of blood at Kasukhín before we could stem its flow, and that would explain a chill of the body.\
\
'But for you to feel it as well makes me think there may be another cause, an outward cause. This cold is not natural.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Shiver</rgb> at the thought of the unnatural cold","Hear the remainder of Sigileth's account","'Hers may not... but mine do. You say this may not be Silirtas... but if it is, I have to speak to her! I have to tell her I am sorry!'","Sigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.","Instancia: Una reparación"},
[6736]={"Talk to Prince Ingór","'${PLAYER}... you have to protect the prince... he is in great danger!'\
\
Thettmárr leans back and closes his eyes, seeking relief from the pain.\
\
'Tell Líkmund... I forgive his debt... it was never about the...'","'There is no time to mourn, ${PLAYER}. We must press on!'","Habla con Stóthkell","Instancia: Un mensaje en Mithril","'${PLAYER}! The Orcs launched this attack upon the Gabil'akkâ while you were away, but I have not yet seen Gorgar among his warriors. He must be here somewhere!\
\
'Let your companions remain here to fortify our defences! I need you to come with me in search of the Orc leader!'","Hear Thettmárr's dying words","Talk to Imák","Thettmárr has suffered grievous injury at the hands of the attacking Orcs, and will not long survive.","'We must reach Prince Ingór and Prince Durin! This way, my friends!'","It is too late. Stóthkell is dead.","On your return to Máttugard with Imák and Venko, you discover that the dwarves at Maergrind are under attack by the forces of Gorgar!","Venko and Imák are ready to join the fight!","Imák knows there is no time to spend on grief.","Talk to Venko","Mantente en guardia","Gorgar has emerged from the ranks of the Orcs to challenge the dwarves for control of Gundabad!","Prince Ingór requests your help in the middle of the battle.","Stóthkell has been grievously wounded by the mithril hammer wielded by Gorgar the Ruthless, and will not long survive."},
[6737]={"Leigh Putnam está dentro de la cueva de los refugiados.\
\
Has ayudado en la defensa de los refugiados, y ahora Leigh desea hablar contigo.","Habla con Severin Rodador","Habla con Leigh Putnam","Has viajado a una cueva cercana con Leigh Putnam para ayudar a levantar el ánimo de los refugiados que buscan refugio allí y convencerlos de que Puente de Caballete sería un lugar más seguro para esconderse.","'${PLAYER}, es demasiado tarde — ¡una partida de Orcos se dirige aquí! Bríndanos la ayuda que puedas, ¡pues estarán aquí en unos instantes! Si Edward y yo caemos, tú y Leigh serán la única defensa para la gente aquí — ¡no dejes que los Orcos los alcancen!'","'¿No hay ningún lugar seguro de estas criaturas viles? ¡¿Por qué no pueden dejarnos en paz?!'","'Esta es la cueva, ${PLAYER}. Vamos rápido — quiero convencer a esta gente de que venga a Puente de Caballete. La ciudad puede no estar segura, pero tiene que ser más segura que esta cueva.\
\
'Apurémonos — mi hermano nos avisará si algún Orco se acerca demasiado.'","'Regresemos a Puente de Caballete, ${PLAYER}. Esta cueva ya no es segura, si alguna vez lo fue.'","Severin Rodador ha llegado a la cueva con malas noticias.\
\
Has intentado convencer a los refugiados de que vayan a la relativa seguridad de Puente de Caballete, pero se negaron.","'Los Orcos saben de esta cueva ahora. No tenemos otra opción que ir a Puente de Caballete. Te agradezco tu ayuda, pero desearía que no fuera necesario. ¿Cuándo volverá a ser seguro este territorio para que la gente buena viva en paz?'","Los refugiados se esconden en el fondo de la cueva.\
\
Leigh Putnam te ha pedido que intentes levantar el ánimo de los refugiados que se esconden en la cueva y que los convenzas de ir a Puente de Caballete.","'No creo que sea una buena idea ir a Puente de Caballete, y Ford está de acuerdo. Estamos más seguros aquí.\
\
'Gracias por tu preocupación, pero creo que nos vamos a quedar donde estamos.'","Instancia: La esperanza de un juglar","'Se pensaba que esta banda de Orcos no tendría problemas para encontrarnos, pero el Capitán Rodador, Edward Putnam y tú les mostraron su error. ¡Te aplaudo, amigo juglar!'","'Eso estuvo demasiado cerca, . Hemos brindado la ayuda que pudimos, y ya es hora de que regresemos a Puente de Caballete. Quizá ahora esta gente escuchará la razón.\
\
'Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar a la ciudad, y nos iremos.'","Leigh Putnam está justo dentro de la entrada de la cueva.\
\
Has viajado con Leigh a la cueva donde los refugiados buscan refugio de los ataques de Orcos.","Habla con los refugiados escondidos en la cueva","'Los Orcos no te vieron, ¿verdad? ¡Si nos has puesto en peligro al venir aquí, me aseguraré de que lo lamentes!\
\
'¿Puente de Caballete? No, no vamos allí — ¡es la muerte! Al menos aquí podríamos permanecer ocultos a los Orcos. Puente de Caballete es el objetivo principal de las partidas de saqueo, ¡y seríamos unos tontos si intentáramos escondernos allí!'","'Los Orcos están buscando supervivientes de su incursión inicial, ${PLAYER}, pero si permanecemos escondidos un rato, deberíamos estar a salvo. Espero que no te hayan seguido hasta aquí.'"},
[6738]={"Aragorn stands atop the wall, ready to speak to the worried defenders.","Help Aragorn to bolster the spirits of the defenders on the wall","Aragorn is atop the Deeping Wall, and wishes to speak with you.","The Men of Rohan stand ready to defend the Deeping Wall, but Aragorn fears the vast extent of Saruman's forces will cause them to despair.","Gather worried defenders and send them to Aragorn atop the wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We have done what we can, ${PLAYER}. I hope it will be enough.'","Instancia: Una Necesidad de Palabras","'Thank you for sending them to me, friend Captain. Now we must fill them with hope and with the fire of battle!\
\
'What should I say to them, ${PLAYER}?'","Thurketel stands atop the wall. Did Aragorn's words help him recover his hope?","Talk to Aragorn atop the wall","Worried defenders can be found atop the wall, and Aragorn has asked you to send them to him for encouraging words.","'You choose your friends well, ${PLAYER}. This Dúnadan has me believing we might survive this night, after all!\
\
'I am ready for Saruman's armies! Indeed, I feel like I could teach the Wizard himself a lesson with my blade, a lesson so sharp he would soon regret waging this war!\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. My heart stirs for battle!'","'I see now the extent of Saruman's forces, and it is vast. How will the Men of Rohan keep their courage in face of such an army? I wait still for allies from afar, but none come. Where is Erkenbrand? Where are the men who fought at the Ford? We wait, but still no allies come to our aid.\
\
'You are a Captain, ${PLAYER}, and know well how to inspire a man's heart. We need words to raise the hopes of these defenders and give them strength to fight. Gather the defenders on the wall and send them here, and we will do what we can to inspire them.'","'Thank you for sending them to me, my friend. Now to fill them with hope and with the fire of battle!'","Talk to Thurketel atop the wall","The men of Rohan need inspiring words if they are to stand against Saruman's forces.","'I see now the extent of Saruman's forces, and it is vast. How will the Men of Rohan keep their courage in face of such an army?\
\
'We need words of inspiration to raise the hopes of these defenders and give them the strength to fight. Gather the defenders on the wall and send them here, and I will do what I can to inspire them.'"},
[6740]={"'Sí, le di permiso a Bingo y Esmeralda para que llevaran a cabo su broma con Dinodas. No estará contento cuando le digan que era una broma, pero todos nos reímos mucho, y él también se reirá. Eventualmente.'","'Oh, no conozco muchas historias de miedo, pero estoy seguro de que uno de mis hijos estará encantado de contar la primera'","'La historia que voy a contarles es más antigua que todas las demás que hemos escuchado esta noche, ya que data de los primeros días de la Comarca y está registrada en muy pocos lugares. La encontré en un libro que ${PLAYER} recuperó de la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials, pero me parece que se hicieron pocas copias de ese libro. Una vez que les cuente esta historia, vivirá para siempre, y todos deberían recordarla.\
\
'Incluso en los primeros días de la Comarca, los festivales ya eran importantes para nuestros lejanos antepasados. ¿Había Boffin incluso entonces? Me gustaría pensar que sí, aunque no he visto un árbol genealógico que se extienda tan atrás. Ciertamente, algunas ramas de nuestros árboles genealógicos llevan nombres similares a los de los primeros habitantes de la Comarca, y he visto relatos de Esmeraldas, Caléndulas, Griffos y Foscos. ¡Pero me estoy distrayendo!\
\
'Una joven llamada Menegilda deseaba ganar una competencia de baile, pero su principal rival, una tal Peony, era excelente en el arte y la superaba en todas las oportunidades. Menegilda estaba obsesionada con ganar el gran premio, y se convenció de que Peony debía su éxito a los zapatos violetas que siempre usaba. Menegilda ideó un plan para robar los zapatos.\
\
'Sorprendió a Peony en las orillas del Brandivino y le exigió que le entregara los zapatos. Peony se negó y dijo que había un hechizo en los zapatos; solo funcionarían bajo su comando, y no le harían ningún bien a Menegilda. Menegilda no se dejó disuadir. De hecho, la revelación de que los zapatos estaban encantados la llenó de felicidad. ¡Al fin, una explicación para su continua incapacidad para vencer a Peony en el baile!\
\
'Peony se quitó los zapatos y se los lanzó a su rival. \\q¡Muy bien!\\q gritó, \\q¡Tómalos! Le diré a mi padre lo que has hecho, ¡y no se te permitirá bailar en absoluto!\\q Esto fue un error, pero Peony no entendía la rabia que hervía dentro del corazón de Menegilda. Menegilda se lanzó hacia ella con los brazos levantados, y empujó a Peony al río. Ella nunca volvió a salir a la superficie.\
\
'Menegilda se puso sus zapatos robados y regresó a la ciudad. Hubo susurros, pero nadie había visto su encuentro con Peony, y se creía que Peony podría haberse escapado, buscando su fortuna más allá de las fronteras de la Comarca. A Menegilda no le importaba; todos sus pensamientos estaban centrados en ganar el próximo concurso de baile.\
\
'Unas semanas más tarde, Menegilda se puso sus nuevos zapatos y bailó en el escenario ante todos los hobbits reunidos. Todos vitorearon y aplaudieron, porque nunca habían visto un baile así antes, ni siquiera cuando Peony había participado. Menegilda fue la clara ganadora.\
\
'Y sin embargo, algo estaba mal. Alguien intentó presentar a Menegilda la cinta de ganadora, pero ella simplemente continuó bailando. Todos aplaudieron de nuevo, pero ella no mostró signos de querer detenerse. \\q¡Creo que eso es suficiente, querida!\\q alguien llamó, pero ahora había lágrimas corriendo por la cara de Menegilda y la asamblea llegó a entender que quería detenerse, pero no podía.\
\
'La gente se apresuró al escenario y trató de quitarle los zapatos violetas, pero no se los pudieron quitar. Los pies de Menegilda volaban de izquierda a derecha, aquí y allá, pero incluso cuando cayó en un estupor el baile continuó. Por fin se detuvo, pero los días de baile de Menegilda habían terminado. Los zapatos fueron empacados en una caja y sellados, escondidos en un rincón polvoriento de una madriguera olvidada. Los hobbits hablaron por un tiempo de Menegilda y los zapatos malditos, pero eventualmente la historia pasó a ser leyenda, y la gente dudaba si realmente había sucedido alguna vez, incluso mientras temían hablar de ello.'","'Todos saben que me encanta echarme una siesta, y a lo largo de los años ha sido motivo de algunas bromas. ¡Pero les digo esto! Mamá nos contó esta historia cuando éramos muy pequeños, y si algunos de ustedes la olvidaron, bueno, ¡yo no! Una vez que la hayan escuchado de nuevo, estarán celosos de mis siestas por la tarde y mis madrugadas, ¡no lo dudo!\
\
'Hace muchos años, un hobbit llamado Hamson Broadbeam vivía en el pueblo de Sobrecolina. Era un carpintero de gran renombre, y la gente venía de toda la Comarca para comprar sus productos artesanales. Todavía se pueden encontrar cofres de roble con su marca en los agujeros de hobbit por todas las Cuatro Cuadernas, aunque Hamson mismo solo se recuerda en esta historia.\
\
'Fue víctima de su propio éxito. Había tantos pedidos de tantos clientes que tenía que quedarse despierto hasta tarde para terminar cada producto artesanal, tambaleándose hacia la cama cuando los primeros rayos de luz comenzaban a brillar a través de los árboles sobre Sobrecolina. Su trabajo comenzó a sufrir, y temía que su reputación se viera empañada a menos que algo cambiara, y rápido.\
\
'Un día, Hamson caminaba somnoliento por el Bosque del Fardo hacia un área donde solía talar árboles para su banco de trabajo. Al acercarse al lugar, sintió que el pelo de sus dedos se erizaba; algo lo estaba observando desde el dosel del árbol.\
\
'\\q¿Hola? ¿Hay alguien ahí?\\q llamó.\
\
'\\qVivo aquí,\\q respondió una voz delgada y aguda. Hamson entrecerró los ojos hacia las ramas, pero no pudo ver al hablante.\
\
'\\qNo te veo,\\q dijo Hamson. \\q¿Estoy dormido? Debo haberme quedado dormido en algún lugar del camino, y ahora estoy soñando. ¡Espero que ningún animal encuentre mi cuerpo mientras duermo!\\q\
\
'\\qMe pareces bastante despierto para mí,\\q respondió la misteriosa voz. \\qAl menos, no estás dormido, pero quizás deberías estarlo. Tus extremidades cuelgan flojamente, tus párpados caen, y veo agotamiento en cada parte de ti.\\q\
\
'Hamson estaba impresionado de que este extraño nuevo conocido pudiera leer la situación con tanta claridad, y describió las muchas demandas de su tiempo que le impedían dormir. \\q¡Si tan solo no necesitara dormir!\\q exclamó, \\q¡No tendría que preocuparme por nada!\\q\
\
'Al principio, la voz del dosel del árbol no respondió. Luego, una pequeña rama con bayas rojas cayó desde lo alto, aterrizando en la tierra junto a los pies de Hamson. \\q¿Qué es esto?\\q preguntó.\
\
'\\qNo necesito dormir,\\q respondió la voz. \\qCome esas bayas y tú tampoco necesitarás dormir.\\q Normalmente, Hamson no habría confiado en un regalo así de un extraño, especialmente de uno tan extraño como este, pero quería desesperadamente que las bayas hicieran lo que la voz prometía que harían, así que no lo pensó dos veces. Las comió con avidez, pero no se sintió diferente. Preguntó cuánto tiempo tomaría para notar su efecto, pero la voz no respondió. Enojado, Hamson se fue a casa. Ni siquiera le importaba recoger la madera que lo había llevado al bosque en primer lugar, tan decepcionado y molesto estaba.\
\
'Esa noche, Hamson fabricó un juego de sillas solicitadas por un rico cliente, y el trabajo era lo suficientemente delicado como para mantenerlo bastante ocupado y aún despierto hasta el amanecer. De hecho, su somnolencia había desaparecido, y trabajó todo el resto del día y hasta la siguiente noche. \\q¿Puede ser?\\q le preguntó a su agujero vacío. \\q¿Esas bayas me quitaron mi necesidad de dormir?\\q Parecía ser así, y Hamson nunca había estado tan feliz.\
\
'Las semanas siguientes fueron un deleite para el carpintero, y terminó cada pedido que se le presentó. Cuando ya no hubo más pedidos que cumplir, leyó su pequeña colección de libros, y sintió que se había convertido en un hobbit mucho más inteligente y culto. Cuando ya no hubo más libros que leer, dio largos paseos por la Comarca por la noche, y se maravilló de la belleza nocturna del campo. Cuando eso finalmente perdió su lustre, regresó a su hogar y se acostó despierto en su cama. Había agotado todo lo que quería hacer, y ahora estaba aburrido. Todo lo que quería hacer era cerrar los ojos y dormir, pero por más que lo intentaba, nunca volvería a dormir. Tan mal como se había sentido antes, ahora se sentía peor. Cada día se sentía como una eternidad, y cada noche se sentía como dos.\
\
'Hamson caminó por cada pulgada del Bosque del Fardo, llamando a la misteriosa voz para que regresara y le diera otras bayas, pero hasta donde yo sé nunca la encontró. Podría estar caminando allí todavía, justo por ahí, buscando un fin a su interminable vigilia...'","Busca otro Boffin para que cuente una historia de miedo","Elige a uno de los Boffins para que cuente una historia de miedo","Bingo y su ribera de primos se han reunido a la orilla de los Campos Verdes para compartir historias espeluznantes y celebrar el espíritu del Festival de la Cosecha.","Instancia: Una noche de historias de fantasmas","'Escuché esta historia cuando era muy pequeño, ¡y me impresionó mucho! Juré no dejar que el miedo me dominara, y hasta ahora no lo ha hecho, ¡y no lo hará! ¡Algunos hobbits aún podrían aprender esa lección, diría yo!\
\
'Hace mucho tiempo, un rico hobbit llamado Longo Ganapié vivía solo en una elegante mansión en Cavada Grande. Le gustaban las cosas caras y tenía muchos sirvientes, y no era ningún secreto que no los trataba bien. Disfrutaba de la comida que le preparaban, pero estaba consumido por la desconfianza, y temía que se colaran en la despensa y robaran los ingredientes para sus propias familias.\
\
'Así fue como Longo instaló fuertes cerraduras y pesadas barras en su despensa, y llevaba las únicas llaves. Cuando era hora de que sus sirvientes prepararan sus cenas, los llevaba a la puerta, desbloqueaba todo cuidadosamente y se quedaba allí observando mientras retiraban lo que necesitaban. Marcaba cuidadosamente las cantidades de cada alimento, y si parecía que se retiraba más de lo necesario, tenía palabras fuertes listas para usar.\
\
'Esto continuó durante algún tiempo, pero aún así Longo estaba seguro de que sus sirvientes le estaban robando su comida. No puedo decirlo con certeza, pero me parece que las medidas extremas que usó para prevenirlo deben haber inflamado el deseo de los sirvientes de perpetrar algún robo, ¡pero eso podría ser solo mi perspectiva como un hobbit rebelde!\
\
'En cualquier caso, llegó un día en que las sospechas de Longo estaban en su nivel más alto y llamó a todos sus sirvientes a la sala de estar. \\q¡Ya no necesito sus servicios!\\q proclamó, y los despidió a todos. \\q¡Vayan a robar del almacén de otra persona!\\q gritó mientras salían corriendo de la mansión.\
\
'Esa noche, mientras Longo estaba acostado en su cama, descubrió que sus sospechas no se habían aliviado al despedir a todos sus sirvientes. Por el contrario, ahora temía que no estuvieran atados por la lealtad y podrían irrumpir en la mansión para acceder a su despensa. ¿Dónde estaban sus llaves? Ah, aquí están. Aún así, podrían haber realizado la hazaña y reemplazado las llaves cuando terminaron.\
\
'Longo se apresuró a la despensa y encontró las muchas cerraduras como las había dejado más temprano ese día. Desbloqueó cada una y abrió la puerta, revelando estante tras estante de ingredientes útiles y alimentos. Mientras entraba para echar un vistazo más de cerca, rozó la puerta por accidente y se cerró detrás de él. Si no hubiera estado tan concentrado en contar los sacos de harina e inventariar los frascos de encurtidos, podría haber escuchado la pesada barra caer en su lugar fuera de la puerta, pero no lo hizo.\
\
'Nadie sabe cuánto tiempo pasó antes de que alguien notara que no habían visto a Longo Ganapié salir de su mansión durante algún tiempo, ya que les había dicho a sus sirvientes que no regresaran y no tenía amigos ni familiares que lo revisaran. Podría haber durado bastante tiempo en esa despensa bien abastecida, pero al final, después de todo, ¿realmente importa si fueron días o meses?\
\
'Pero los hobbits en la Comarca han reportado sentimientos de incomodidad en sus propias despensas tarde por la noche, como si estuvieran siendo observados desde detrás de los estantes, y algunas personas han afirmado haber visto ojos mirándolos entre los sacos y cajas, ojos llenos de celos y desconfianza.'","'Mi historia es una especie de... advertencia, pero escúchenla bien, porque es tan verdadera como cualquier otra. Los eventos que se narran en ella tuvieron lugar no hace mucho tiempo, poco después de que las nuevas residencias de la Comarca estuvieran disponibles.\
\
'Una hobbit muy vieja y, según se dice, bastante desagradable, la viuda Hilandera, estaba enamorada de una de las casas de la calle de los Arrayanes, y deseaba con todas sus fuerzas comprarla. No era la única persona interesada, por supuesto, pero tenía más dinero para gastar y pudo superar a su principal rival, un joven hobbit llamado Bob Gamonuevo. Compró la casa más deseable de la calle de los Arrayanes y vivió allí durante varios meses, para gran consternación de Bob.\
\
'Bob no era alguien que se rindiera fácilmente, incluso cuando perdía un concurso, y se aseguró de pasar por la calle de los Arrayanes tan a menudo como podía, frunciendo el ceño en dirección a la casa de la viuda Hilandera cada vez que tenía oportunidad. Una noche, mientras pasaba por el camino, escuchó una voz extraña que llamaba en la oscuridad. Miró más de cerca y vio a la viuda Hilandera parada en el patio junto a su madriguera, vistiendo una larga camisa de dormir y un gorro de noche.\
\
'\\q¡Vieja loca!\\q pensó Bob para sí mismo mientras continuaba por el camino hacia su propia madriguera, igualmente decepcionante y estrecha.\
\
'Pensando en esa curiosa visión algún tiempo después, Bob decidió que podría haber sido la última persona en ver a la viuda Hilandera antes de que desapareciera. De hecho, nadie más pudo decirle a los oficiales lo que le había pasado ni dónde había ido. Bob fue tan útil como pudo serlo y les dijo lo poco que sabía, pero no pasó mucho tiempo antes de que se declarara muerta a la viuda Hilandera y el número 6 de la calle de los Arrayanes estuviera nuevamente disponible para comprar.\
\
'Bob no perdió tiempo y compró la casa, y era todo lo que esperaba que fuera. La decoró a su gusto y vivió allí felizmente durante varios meses. Estaba acostado en la cama una noche, poco después de la medianoche, cuando escuchó una voz. \\qAyúdame,\\q llamó desde algún lugar fuera del acogedor dormitorio de Bob.\
\
'\\q¿Qué es eso?\\q se preguntó Bob para sí mismo, y se tapó con las mantas hasta la barbilla. \\qAyúdame,\\q volvió a llamar la voz. Bob apretó los ojos con fuerza, pero luego decidió que la mañana estaba demasiado lejos y que no habría forma de escapar de esa voz lastimera. Siguió su llamado fuera de su dormitorio, por el pasillo, y finalmente afuera.\
\
'El aire era frío y la noche oscura, pero pudo escuchar la voz lo suficientemente claro como para seguirla hasta el patio lateral, donde estaba el pozo. Seguro que sí, la voz resonaba desde el oscuro agujero en el suelo. \\qAyúdame,\\q volvió a preguntar. Bob se inclinó sobre el agujero y frunció el ceño. \\qHilandera, si eres tú ahí abajo...\\q comenzó, pero no pudo terminar su pensamiento antes de que algo le golpeara la espalda y resbalara sobre el césped húmedo. Bob cayó por el pozo y todo se volvió oscuro.\
\
'Cuando despertó, estaba medio dentro y medio fuera del agua, profundamente dentro del pozo. Una grieta en la pared se abría hacia una cámara excavada en la tierra, y estaba dolorosamente atrapado en esa grieta. Se sentía mareado y le costaba enfocar los ojos. Gradualmente lo logró y vio a la viuda Hilandera sentada en el suelo, apoyada contra la pared de tierra de la cámara, con una tetera y varios platos dispuestos a su alrededor.\
\
'\\qAyúdame,\\q dijo la voz una vez más, y Bob se dio cuenta de que no provenía de la viuda Hilandera, sino de algún lugar mucho más cercano, justo al lado de su oído. \\qAyúdame a preparar el té,\\q continuó. \\qEstará tan feliz de tener a alguien con quien tomar el té.\\q Algo tiró bruscamente de su brazo y Bob desapareció dentro de la cámara de tierra. Nunca más se le volvió a ver...\
\
'He oído que el número 6 de la calle de los Arrayanes está disponible para comprar de nuevo... si no te importa el té a medianoche.'","Mantente alerta para encontrar una cura a las malditas botas","'¡No estoy contando una historia! Elijan a alguien más, ${PLAYER}. ¡En serio!'","¡Esmeralda no puede dejar de bailar! ¿Serán los zapatos mágicos?","Escucha las historias espeluznantes con los Boffin","Los numerosos primos de Bingo tienen historias a hacer miedo para compartir, y es tu turno de elegir quién va a contar la siguiente.","¿Qué está pasando? ¡Con todas estas historias, la noche se vuelve realmente aterradora!","Bingo está de pie cerca de la hoguera, al borde de los Campos Verdes, con sus muchos primos.","Los muchos primos de Bingo quieren contar historias a hacer miedo, y es a ti a quien le toca elegir quién empezará.","'Odo Cavada fue el mejor pescador que la Comarca haya visto jamás, y ninguno de los que hoy lanzan sus líneas puede esperar igualar su habilidad. Ni deberían, si creen en la historia que estoy a punto de contar. Yo creo en ella, porque seguramente es verdad.\
\
'El nombre de Odo era conocido por toda la Comarca en su época, y parecía que podía encontrar peces en cualquier cuerpo de agua; no solo peces, sino peces de un tamaño que apenas se podría esperar. Donde la mayoría de los hobbits sacaban pececillos de tamaño medio de sus anzuelos, Odo podía lanzar al río y sacar peces de una belleza increíble, con escamas de arcoíris brillando, criaturas de un tamaño que ningún hobbit había sacado antes.\
\
'Tan hábil era que se atrevió a subirse a un bote hecho por él mismo y pescar lejos de las orillas, lo cual era muy inusual para los hobbits de su época, ¡y sigue siendo así! Sin embargo, también resultó ser una mala idea, porque llegó un día en que un gran pez monstruoso agarró su línea y tiró su bote rápidamente con la corriente. La mayoría de los hobbits habrían soltado su caña y remado a salvo, pero Odo tenía una reputación que mantener; se apoyó contra los lados y se aferró a la caña como si su vida dependiera de ello.\
\
'\\q¡Te haré mía!\\q proclamó al gran pez mientras lo arrastraba. \\q¡Seré el vencedor en este concurso, o mi nombre no es Odo Cavada, Maestro Pescador!\\q\
\
'La batalla duró días, y el poderoso pez llevó el bote de Odo lejos de la Comarca y hacia tierras desconocidas para todos los hobbits. Finalmente, consumido por el hambre y el cansancio, Odo soltó su agarre en la caña de pescar y esta salió volando del bote hacia el agua. \\qMe rindo,\\q dijo a nadie mientras su bote desaceleraba después de la rápida persecución. Tomó los remos y se preparó para comenzar el largo viaje hacia casa.\
\
'Entonces algo golpeó la parte inferior de su bote y los remos se rompieron en sus soportes y cayeron al agua; pero su rápido viaje hacia el sur continuó. \\q¿Qué está pasando?\\q gritó en voz alta, y miró por encima del costado hacia el agua debajo. El gran pez no lo había dejado, sino que permanecía, empujando el bote en su curso hacia el sur. \\q¿A dónde me llevas?\\q preguntó Odo, pero el pez no respondió.\
\
'Esto continuó durante muchos días, hasta que Odo estaba débil por el hambre. Se desplomó en la base de su bote, y una vez más se preguntó cuándo el gran pez lo dejaría ir. \\q¿Me trajiste aquí solo para dejarme morir?\\q gritó en voz alta, demasiado débil para siquiera sacudir su puño hacia los cielos crueles. Entonces escuchó un chapoteo, y otro: pequeños peces estaban saltando del agua y aterrizando en el bote. \\q¡Qué... qué suerte!\\q jadeó, y los agarró con ambas manos. Los comió crudos, lo que habría encontrado desagradable en casa, pero en este terrible día estaba agradecido por el regalo inesperado.\
\
'Con su vigor renovado, Odo ahora era lo suficientemente fuerte como para mantener la vigilancia desde la parte delantera de su bote, y así fue como vio acercarse el Gran Mar, y el fin del río. El bote desaceleró, y el gran pez detuvo su empuje. Levantó su gran cabeza del agua, y Odo vio que la criatura no estaba sola: había peces de todas las formas y tamaños imaginables rodeando su bote. \\q¿Qué quieres?\\q preguntó.\
\
'Mientras Odo examinaba la gran variedad de las diversas especies que lo rodeaban, se dio cuenta de que reconocía cada tipo de pez. En algún momento de su estimada carrera, había atrapado al menos uno de cada uno de estos tipos, y en algunos casos muchos. \\q¿Me consideras responsable?\\q susurró. \\qViniste por mí. Viniste por mí... ¿para vengarte?\\q\
\
'Los peces lo miraron con ojos globulosos, sus branquias trabajando silenciosamente justo debajo de la superficie del agua.\
\
'\\qPero... pero me alimentaste. ¿Por qué mantenerme con vida?\\q\
\
'No hubo respuesta de los silenciosos reunidos, pero de repente se movieron como uno solo. Cientos de peces presionaron contra los lados y el fondo del bote de Odo, y la multitud plateada y multicolor forzó el bote desde el agua dulce del río hacia la sal del Gran Mar, muriendo en el proceso.\
\
'Y así Odo Cavada pagó el precio de su éxito. Piensen en él esta noche, flotando en el Gran Mar lejos de aquí, para nunca regresar.'","Bingo tiene una historia espeluznante que contar.","Ayuda a Esmeralda a quitarse los zapatos malditos","'Cuando llegamos aquí para ver a nuestro primo Bingo y celebrar el Festival de la Cosecha con él, cruzamos el Puente del Brandivino y tomamos el camino por Cepeda. ¿Recuerdan todos mirar al otro lado del agua y ver las granjas de Bolgovado? Mi historia tuvo lugar en una de esas granjas, y los eventos que se cuentan allí sucedieron no hace mucho tiempo. Sé que estos eventos son verdaderos, aunque suenen increíbles. La historia me la contó alguien que sabría la verdad del asunto.\
\
'La granja estaba justo al borde del río, y pertenecía a un hobbit llamado Everard. Era un Bolger, como muchos de los habitantes de Bolgovado, pero mientras que la mayoría de los Bolger son buenos agricultores, Everard luchaba diariamente para mantener su cosecha. O era arruinada por la plaga, o saqueada por los cuervos, o comida por los conejos, y en muchas ocasiones tuvo que depender de la caridad de sus vecinos para que su familia sobreviviera.\
\
'Everard culpaba sobre todo a su espantapájaros. Por más que lo intentara, no podía hacer un espantapájaros lo suficientemente aterrador; cada día, los pájaros venían a darse un festín con sus cultivos, sin inmutarse. Estaba desesperado un martes, y mientras miraba con furia a su espantapájaros fallido, un cuervo voló desde el cielo y se posó sobre él.\
\
'\\q¡Oh, te enseñaré lo que mereces!\\q gruñó Everard mientras lanzaba su azadón al pájaro. El cuervo voló justo fuera de alcance, y luego aterrizó una vez más sobre el sombrero de paja del espantapájaros.\
\
'\\qParece que estás molesto, amigo,\\q dijo el cuervo. Esto sorprendió a Everard un poco, porque aunque había oído historias de pájaros parlantes nunca había encontrado uno él mismo. \\q¿Molesto?\\q logró decir. \\q¡Por supuesto! ¡Ustedes los pájaros no dejan mis cultivos en paz, cosas viles!\\q\
\
'\\qParece que mereces algo mejor,\\q respondió el cuervo. \\qSi quieres, puedo hablar con los míos y ver si quizás podríamos llegar a un acuerdo. Estaría dispuesto a hacer esto por ti si me dejas probar algunos de estos granos.\\q Everard lo pensó y no vio muchos inconvenientes en la propuesta del cuervo. Después de todo, el apetito de un pájaro sería menor que el de toda una bandada, y al renunciar a parte de la cosecha podría asegurar la seguridad del resto. \\qDe acuerdo,\\q le dijo al pájaro, y lo vio devorar parte de la cosecha antes de volar lejos.\
\
'El día siguiente no mostró mucha mejoría, y los pájaros continuaron acosando sus cultivos. Estaba seguro de que no volvería a ver al cuervo, pero para su sorpresa el pájaro apareció y habló. \\qDijeron que quieren ayudarte, pero simplemente no pueden resistir el sabor de los cultivos que estás cultivando aquí. Dijeron que lo que necesitas es un mejor espantapájaros. Eso haría mucho más difícil para ellos volar cerca.\\q\
\
'\\qHe intentado hacer este más aterrador,\\q le dijo Everard, \\qpero simplemente no funciona.\\q\
\
'\\qVeamos qué podemos hacer,\\q respondió el cuervo.\
\
'El sol del miércoles cruzó el cielo, y cuando se acercaba el anochecer, la esposa de Everard envió a su hija Holly a buscar a Everard para cenar. Mientras Holly se acercaba al campo, se maravilló de lo realista que parecía el segundo espantapájaros que su padre había hecho. Debió haber pasado todo el día confeccionándolo; parecía un hobbit de verdad. Mientras lo observaba, un cuervo saltando entre los granos graznó y voló lejos.'","'Hace muchos, muchos años, mucho antes de que nuestros árboles genealógicos hubieran siquiera brotado, había un pequeño pueblo a orillas del Brandivino, no muy lejos de donde se encuentra Cepeda hoy en día. Una de las figuras prominentes de este pueblo era un tipo llamado Gerd Buenaltura; tenía el respeto de sus vecinos y era consultado sobre muchos de los asuntos que enfrentaba la ciudad. Se creía ampliamente que cuando llegara el momento de que el alcalde renunciara, Gerd sería fácilmente elegido para tomar su lugar.\
\
'Un día, Gerd estaba caminando entre los juncos al borde del río cuando escuchó una pequeña voz entre las cañas. \\q¡Qué curioso!\\q pensó para sí mismo, y se agachó en el barro para encontrar al dueño de la voz. Al no encontrar nada, se preparó para levantarse nuevamente, pero antes de que pudiera hacerlo, un gran gato negro salió de los juncos. \\qBueno, hola,\\q saludó al gato, y se dio la vuelta para irse.\
\
'\\qHola a ti también,\\q le dijo el gato.\
\
'Gerd se sorprendió mucho, ya que era la primera vez que un gato le hablaba. Una vez que se recuperó, descubrió que el gato no solo era hablador, sino también bastante amigable. Se presentó como Ojosverdes, y dijo que venía de una tierra lejana en busca de un hogar. Gerd estuvo encantado de ofrecerle a Ojosverdes un lugar en su humilde madriguera, y Ojosverdes contribuyó a su manera: manteniendo a las ratas y otros indeseables alejados de la despensa de Gerd.\
\
'Con el tiempo, Ojosverdes demostró ser capaz de encontrar mucho más que ratones. Se paseaba por todo el pueblo, entrando sigilosamente por ventanas entreabiertas y empujando puertas sin pestillo. Aprendió muchos rumores interesantes y escuchó muchos chismes sobre los hobbits del pueblo, y contó cada bocado jugoso a Gerd con deleite.\
\
'Gerd comenzó a mirar a sus vecinos con desagrado y desconfianza, y descubrió que ya no podía soportar conversar con ellos. Se volvió frío y distante, y otros hobbits lo evitaban cuando lo veían en la carretera, cruzando al otro lado en lugar de hablar con él. Cuando regresaban a sus hogares, Ojosverdes los seguía y escuchaba mientras los llamaban desagradables, extraños e inhóspitos. El gato contaba estas historias a Gerd con pesar, pero su cola se movía felizmente de un lado a otro.\
\
'\\qDe todos modos no necesito a estos mentirosos como amigos,\\q le dijo Gerd un día. \\qTe tengo a ti, Ojosverdes, y eres el único amigo que este hobbit necesita.\\q Ojosverdes asintió con la cabeza, moviendo la cola.\
\
'No mucho después, llegó un día en que Gerd no pudo encontrar a Ojosverdes en ningún lado. Desesperado y seguro de que uno de sus vecinos había hecho daño a su amigo, corrió gritando hacia el centro del pueblo. La gente observó su progreso a través del pueblo, y sus susurros ya no eran silenciosos ni ocultos. Loco demente, Gerd corrió hacia las orillas del río, y allí finalmente encontró a su amigo.\
\
'Ojosverdes estaba entre los juncos, y con sus dos patas delanteras empujó un pequeño bote hacia el río. Se subió a bordo, y se volvió para mirar a Gerd mientras flotaba con la corriente.\
\
'\\q¿Por qué, Ojosverdes? ¿Por qué debes irte?\\q le gritó Gerd. Ojosverdes no respondió, sino que solo lo miró en silencio hasta que la corriente lo llevó lejos y fuera de vista.\
\
'No se sabe qué pasó con Gerd Buenaltura después de eso, pero nunca volvió al pueblo, y nunca se convirtió en alcalde. Pero hay algunos que dicen que si la luna está alta en el cielo, como lo está esta noche, podrías echar un vistazo a Ojosverdes en su bote, flotando río abajo, moviendo la cola, moviendo la cola, moviendo la cola.'","'¡Esta es la noche perfecta para compartir historias espeluznantes, ${PLAYER}, incluso mejor de lo que esperaba! Muchos de los hijos de mi prima Prisca me han dicho que tienen sus propias historias listas para compartir, y yo también tengo una.\
\
'¡Fortalece tu coraje, amigo mío, y celebremos el espíritu aterrador de la temporada!'","'¡Qué divertido! ¿Qué te parece, ${PLAYER}? Me parece que Esmeralda debería probar suerte en el teatro del Risco Invernal... ¡fue una actuación convincente!\
\
'Diría que ciertamente le dimos a Dino un buen sabor de lo que es esta temporada, ¿no crees?\
\
'Oh, todo es en buena diversión. Él estará bien. Solo necesitaba un buen susto. No habríamos llevado a cabo esta broma si Prisca no hubiera dado su permiso, y ella pensó que podría hacerle algo de bien, al igual que nosotros. ¡Después de todo, es la temporada de los sustos!'","'No tengo una historia preparada, pero estoy feliz de escuchar.'","Bingo se encuentra cerca de la hoguera, a la orilla de los Campos Verdes.","¡Las llamas danzantes de la hoguera iluminan los rostros de los Boffin, y un silencio espeluznante se apodera del lugar!","'Creo que he sido muy claro, ${PLAYER}. ¡No voy a contar una historia! ¡Elige a alguien más!'","Habla con Bingo junto a la hoguera","Escucha las historias a hacer miedo con los Boffin","'Me encantaría ir primero, pero no tengo una historia preparada. Por ahora, prefiero escuchar.'","Habla con Bingo para escuchar su historia espeluznante","Las llamas danzantes de la hoguera iluminan los rostros de los Boffin, y un silencio siniestro se apodera del lugar.","¡Las botas no se quitan!","'No conozco muchas historias de miedo, pero sé que otro de mis hijos estaría encantado de contar la siguiente. No Dinodas, quizás, pero alguien más sí'","'Hace muchos, muchos años, mucho antes de que nuestros árboles genealógicos hubieran siquiera brotado, había un pequeño pueblo a orillas del Brandivino, no muy lejos de donde se encuentra Cepeda hoy en día. Una de las figuras prominentes de este pueblo era un tipo llamado Gerd Buenaltura; tenía el respeto de sus vecinos y era consultado sobre muchos de los asuntos que enfrentaba el pueblo. Se decía ampliamente que cuando llegara el momento de que el alcalde se retirara, Gerd sería fácilmente elegido para tomar su lugar.\
\
'Un día, Gerd estaba caminando entre los juncos al borde del río cuando escuchó una pequeña voz entre las cañas. \\q¡Qué curioso!\\q pensó para sí mismo, y se agachó en el barro para encontrar al dueño de la voz. Al no encontrar nada, se preparó para levantarse una vez más, pero antes de que pudiera hacerlo, un gran gato negro salió de los juncos. \\qBueno, hola,\\q saludó al gato, y se dio la vuelta para irse.\
\
'\\qHola a ti también,\\q le dijo el gato.\
\
'Gerd se sorprendió mucho, porque era la primera vez que un gato le hablaba. Una vez que se recuperó, descubrió que el gato no solo era hablador, sino también bastante amigable. Se presentó como Ojosverdes, y dijo que venía de una tierra lejana en busca de un hogar. Gerd estuvo feliz de ofrecerle a Ojosverdes un lugar en su humilde madriguera, y Ojosverdes contribuyó a su manera: manteniendo a los ratones y otros indeseables alejados de la despensa de Gerd.\
\
'Con el tiempo, Ojosverdes demostró ser capaz de encontrar mucho más que ratones. Acechaba por todo el pueblo, entrando por ventanas entreabiertas y empujando puertas sin pestillo. Aprendió muchos rumores interesantes y escuchó muchos chismes sobre los hobbits del pueblo, y contó cada bocado picante a Gerd con deleite.\
\
'Gerd comenzó a mirar a sus vecinos con disgusto y desconfianza, y descubrió que ya no podía soportar entablar conversación con ellos. Se volvió frío y distante, y otros hobbits lo evitaban cuando lo veían en el camino, cruzando al otro lado en lugar de hablar con él. Cuando regresaban a sus hogares, Ojosverdes los seguía detrás y escuchaba mientras llamaban a Gerd desagradable, extraño e inhóspito. El gato contaba estas historias a Gerd con pesar, pero su cola se movía felizmente de un lado a otro.\
\
'\\qDe todos modos no necesito a estos mentirosos como amigos,\\q le dijo Gerd un día. \\qTe tengo a ti, Ojosverdes, y eres el único amigo que este hobbit necesita.\\q Ojosverdes asintió, su cola se movía.\
\
'No mucho después, llegó un día en que Gerd no pudo encontrar a Ojosverdes en ningún lado. Desesperado y seguro de que uno de sus vecinos había hecho algún daño a su amigo, corrió gritando hacia el centro del pueblo. La gente observaba su progreso por el pueblo, y sus susurros ya no eran susurrados ni ocultos. Loco, Gerd corrió hacia las orillas del río, y allí finalmente encontró a su amigo.\
\
'Ojosverdes estaba entre los juncos, y con sus dos patas delanteras empujó un pequeño bote hacia el río. Se subió a bordo y se volvió para mirar a Gerd mientras flotaba en la corriente.\
\
'\\q¿Por qué, Ojosverdes? ¿Por qué debes irte?\\q le gritó Gerd. Ojosverdes no respondió, pero solo lo miró en silencio hasta que la corriente lo llevó lejos y fuera de vista.\
\
'Nadie sabe qué pasó con Gerd Buenaltura después de eso, pero nunca regresó al pueblo, y nunca se convirtió en alcalde. Pero hay algunos que dicen que si la luna está alta en el cielo, como lo está esta noche, podrías echar un vistazo a Ojosverdes en su bote, flotando río abajo, su cola moviéndose, moviéndose, moviéndose.'"},
[6741]={"Habla con Ravaedron frente a la Cabaña del Helechal","Acompaña a Ravaedron mientras se despide","'¿Conoces a Ravaedron desde hace mucho? Nosotros lo conocimos hace poco, pero le tenemos mucho cariño, ¡y las historias que nos ha contado de tiempos antiguos y lugares lejanos nos han cautivado! ¿Llegó a encontrar la presa que buscaba, esos villanos de oscuros ropajes que lo atrajeron al Ángulo?\
\
'Hemos jurado guardar el secreto y no hablaremos de ello con nadie más. ¡Pero confieso que las sombras de la noche me parecieron más profundas después de que nos hablara de jinetes sin montura sueltos por el bosque!\
\
'Aun así, no los tememos. Mi marido y yo somos de una estirpe dura; ¡nadie podría sobrevivir mucho tiempo en esta tierra de otro modo!'","Habla con Maddoc Astaciervo dentro de la Cabaña del Helechal","Maddoc Astaciervo te ha dado la bienvenida a la Cabaña del Helechal.","Glenys Astaciervo te ha dado la bienvenida a su hogar.","'Verás que los Astaciervo son muy agradables, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Son una pareja encantadora, y su hijo Bran es un muchacho muy vivaz.\
\
'Avisaré de que estamos aquí.'","Visita a los Astaciervo mientras Ravaedron se despide","Ravaedron se encuentra frente a la Cabaña del Helechal, el hogar de sus amigos los Astaciervo.","Instancia: Una separación","'¡Pasad, pasad! Hay pocos caminos en estas tierras, ¡y debéis de estar agotados de vuestros viajes!'","'Siento que hayas tenido que presenciar esto, ${PLAYER}. Me duele decirlo, pero quizá Ravaedron no era un amigo tan cercano como pensábamos. Su pueblo y el nuestro deben de ser simplemente demasiado diferentes.\
\
'¿Se hizo amigo nuestro... por pena? ¿Acaso todos los Inmortales ven a los hombres y mujeres del Ángulo como meras flores, tan frágiles y efímeras que hay que protegerlas y compadecerlas? Pensaba que nuestra amistad con Ravaedron era diferente, pero supongo que me equivocaba.'","Ravaedron te ha pedido que lo acompañes a despedirse de sus amigos, los Astaciervo, antes de abandonar la Tierra Media para siempre.","Habla con Maddoc Astaciervo","Habla con Glenys Astaciervo dentro de la Cabaña del Helechal","Quédate junto a Ravaedron y ofrécele el consuelo que necesita mientras se despide.","El ambiente se ha enfriado dentro de la Cabaña del Helechal.\
\
Maddoc Astaciervo te hace un gesto para que hables con él."},
[6742]={"Nabatínu has asked you for the personal favour of checking on the welfare of his wife, Kugâna, a Jatsakóri still under the thrall of the Bokhóri sorceresses.","Another group is arriving at Gebarakór. You should move closer to hear what they are saying.","You spot her, alive, but not well","This is close enough","Instancia: Un asunto personal","'We have seen what we came to, and should make our way back to Gadim-ûn. Are you ready to leave?'","You have travelled with Faeron to Gebarakór, the Ordâkhai open-pit mine. You should talk to Faeron.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> for Kugâna among the workers","Observe the conversation","Move closer to the Ordâkhai","Talk to Faeron","'Look around, do you see anyone meeting Kugâna's description?'","Another group has arrived at Gebarakór. You should listen in on what they are saying.","'Quietly now, ${PLAYER}. Their own torches should blind their eyes to our presence, but they could still hear us.\
\
'Look there, someone approaches. Let's move closer to listen.'","You witnessed the arrival of Ombátha, the leader of the Bokhóri, sorcerers with the ability to ensnare Men's will. You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for Kugâna, Nabatínu's wife, among the assembled workers."},
[6743]={"Enjoy the meal","'You scrounge up some light, a bit of straw for a seat, and a few plates will help, ${PLAYER}. Merry and I will find what else we need and meet back around this table.'","These rooms would make handsome quarters for a Hobbit, if restored","Join Merry and Pippin in enjoying the makeshift meal.","Instancia: Un lugar para los hobbits","Collected a useable candlestick (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Help Pippin and Merry gather the things needed for a makeshift meal.","Habla con Merry","Collected some straw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Is this considered a common home by the Big Folk around here? It is bigger than any house we ever saw in Breeland, and I dare say the whole of the Smials would fit in this one main hall!'","Habla con Gandalf","You should bring the things you collected to the table.","Habla con Pippin","'All this running about and scrounging has got my stomach rumbling right and proper.'","Explore the kitchens","Explore the side quarters","Collect provisions crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well I suppose we really ought to have a look around, and see what we can see, hadn't we?'","Little remains of ovens or cookery, but the kitchens must have been fine and well-provisioned, once","Pippin and Merry have come running back with their own findings.","'This place, Bâr Thorenion, is yours by royal decree of the kingdom of Gondor. You might think this is some jest of our old friend Aragorn, but in truth it was the soldiery and the rangers of Ithilien who petitioned him that it be so.\
\
'I have brought you here prematurely, I confess. I know not how many men will be here tomorrow to make the place somewhat more habitable. I thought, however, you should like to see it sooner, so you could make your own plans.\
\
'It will serve as a fine residence, indeed, for the time that you dwell here in Gondor before heading back Shireward. And, with any luck, it will keep you out of trouble and away from some of your more foolish notions -- for a few days, at least, if we are lucky.\
\
'Well, come on then. Let us step inside!'","Collect some plates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect some straw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What a remarkable place Gandalf found for us. Amazing to think that it is ours! Can you imagine what it will look like after the Gondorians have tidied it up? I should like to chat with them and make sure some of our things are placed in some of the rooms and that the kitchens in particular are restored, if anything.\
\
'My, but listen to me! A meal, some good company, and something to do and think about is welcome in this odd, free time after we won. But I hope old Gandalf doesn't think he's fooled us into forgetting about Mordor. We should still very much like to go. '","There are spaces that might have been dining areas and studies off here... is that an overgrown garden beyond?","Explore Bâr Thorenion with Merry and Pippin.","Gandalf has invited everyone to step in and see Bâr Thorenion. You should talk to Merry and Pippin and hear what they think of it all.","Talk to Pippin in the central courtyard, now that you have all explored Bâr Thorenion.","After the question of whether they should go into Mordor, Gandalf announced he had something - or rather some-place - to show Pippin and Merry.","Little but the kitchens lead off of this way","Explore the north passage","'I don't know if either of you observed the fact, but it so happens that we have everything we need for a simple makeshift meal - beginning with this old table someone happened to leave right here.\
\
'I know that I could use a bite to eat. What about you two?\
\
'There are crates of food and some bottles of old wine with the seals intact. Some light, a bit of straw for a seat, and a few plates will help. If you gather those, ${PLAYER}, Merry and I will work on cups, knives, and anything else we can muster up.'","Collected Ithilien Wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There we are. A meal, all laid out. Fine work, friends! \
\
'Well, don't just stand about. Let us eat!'","Collected a plate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explore the central courtyard","Gandalf has led you to Bâr Thorenion in North Ithilien, cut into a high place above Cormallen. \
\
You should talk to Gandalf to hear more about Bâr Thorenion.","Collect some kind of light (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect Ithilien Wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explore the southern passage","Collected a provisions crate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The central pool must have been lovely when it was clean and clear","Lay the things about the table","'Go on, see what you can see. As I said, some Men of Gondor will be by tomorrow to make the place a bit more livable.'"},
[6744]={"'This is madness! Where is the justice in letting our enemies just walk away freely?\
\
'This Uruk-hai has seen the layout of our city, our lack of supplies, and the conflicts in our leadership! We only show further weakness by letting him go.'","Sithric stands beside Stanric in the Stangard Mead Hall.\
\
Sithric wishes to discuss the capture of the Uruk and respond to Stanric's judgement.","Talk to Gadda about the Uruk's fate","Talk to Stanric about the Uruk's fate","Stanric stands at the head of the Stangard mead hall.\
\
Stanric wishes to discuss the capture of Dargum, and decide an appropriate course of action.","Talk to Sithric about the Uruk's fate","'What foolishness is this? You would have me believe that the White Wizard himself is now our enemy...?'","Talk to Odda","Dargum has been bound and brought before the leaders of Stangard. They will decide his fate and what should be done about this new-found threat.","'You have done well to capture the Uruk and to expose the betrayal that besets us. I wish to stay and hear Stanric's judgement, but I must depart with haste.\
\
'I have been granted leave of my company and will join another band of men in the Wailing Hills. Perhaps my eagerness for action will not be considered such a burden, as it was at the Cuthstan.'","Stanric and Sithric are preparing to discuss the matters at hand","Gadda stands before Stanric and Sithric in the Mead Hall.\
\
Gadda wishes to discuss the result of Stanric and Sithric's council.","'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I must commend you for subduing the one responsible for damage to the Cuthstan and for bringing him before us.'","'I will deal with escorting this Uruk out of Stangard. You should leave this hall before irritating Sithric further.'","Odda is waiting to speak with you inside the Stangard Mead Hall.","Instance: A Prisoner to Stangard"},
[6745]={"Make your way through the tunnel to the Skarháld throne room","Karazgar has cut a swath of destruction through the Dwarves of Skarháld, but you may still have a chance to stop him.","Gandalf awaits the mask of Karazgar.","Karazgar has come to Skarháld in fulfilment of his second promise.","A pitched battle was fought in the throne room only recently","'Karazgar is wounded, but still... he overmatched us....\
\
'He left... the keep....'","Pick up the mask of Karazgar","Kámat breathes his last","Karazgar has escaped, but he left his mask behind.","The Dwarves of Skarháld are in danger! You must hurry through the escape tunnel carved behind the fortress if you are to reach them before it is too late!","Karazgar has left the keep. If you hurry you might still be able to save some of the Dwarves of Skarháld.","Stand with Gandalf in defence of the Dwarves of Skarháld","Bring the mask of Karazgar to Gandalf","Instancia: Una promesa cumplida","Find and confront Karazgar","Talk to Kámat in the throne room","'This mask is a relic of power, an artifact of great evil. It is not safe for any others to hold it for long. In my care, however, it will be safe.\
\
'Karazgar has been defeated, for now. We must discuss what should be done next, for he has revealed to us something most peculiar: his desire to possess the Black Book of Mordor.'","The tunnel behind Skarháld has been cleared by an unknown interloper. Can it be that Karazgar has come to fulfil his promise?","The mask is cold to the touch","Kámat has been seriously wounded and is near death.","Hurry to the exit of the keep and you may still save some lives"},
[6747]={"'Will you please speak with Limril for me, and learn what has so upset her?'","Overcome with emotion, Limril has become upset and Gladion is concerned for her.","Instancia: Una comida tranquila","Gather dishes from the hutch","Help Limril by setting the table","Limril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should offer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Gladion.","Set the table for six (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have helped prepare for dinner, and should now wait for the meal to begin.","'Thank you for the help, ${PLAYER}. Gladion should be home any moment now.'","'I am so embarrassed, ${PLAYER}. I asked you to set the table for six... because when last you were here, we were expecting Fuirion...'\
\
She falls silent. After a moment she sighs unhappily and wrings her hands.\
\
'But he will never join us for a meal again, will he? It will take some time to become used to that idea, if such a thing is even possible. I do not know if it is, but... we will try.\
\
'I will talk to Gladion. For now, let us try to enjoy our meal.'","Talk to Gladion","Limril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should see what else Limril needs.","You should set the table for Limril","The peace is broken by the sound of the door opening","Offer to help Limril with dinner","Limril has asked you to help with dinner.","'I am glad you would share a meal with us once again, ${PLAYER}. I know you will insist on helping, so I will not try to dissuade you.\
\
'You recall where we keep the dishes? The hutch in the corner -- would you set the table for six, if you please?'","The hutch is in the corner.\
\
Gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.","'Let us try and enjoy a quiet meal. I cannot pretend it will be easy... but we must do what we can to keep living, to keep surviving, no matter the family and the friends we have lost.'","The table is in Gladion and Limril's home.\
\
Gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.","Wait for the meal to begin","Talk to Limril"},
[6748]={"Wynmar followed you to Haldirith and seeks a final word with Noriel.\
\
You should escort Wynmar to Haldirith.","Wynmar has followed you to Haldirith and stands beside you now.\
\
You should talk to Wynmar.","Tell the Elves why you have brought a trespasser to the Elf-keep","Ninil is outside of Haldirith, waiting to speak with you.","Noriel is at Haldirith.","Tell Ninil why Wynmar begged to come","Wynmar has begged you to let him see Noriel one last time to make a gift of flowers.","Ah! Hidden Dwimordene-ruins! My men and I have surely walked by this spot a score of times and never saw this place.\
\
'What sorcery conceals the lovely Noriel and her folk from our eyes? Thank you for leading me to this place before our banishment from Thinglad, ${PLAYER}.'","Observe the meeting of Wynmar and Noriel","Noriel sighs and shakes her head slightly","Instancia: Una solicitud razonable","'You do not...think I was too hard on him, do you? But I had to be firm -- under no circumstances would an Elf of this age choose to love a mortal Man...would she? His life will be as fleeting as a single breath.'","You tell Ninil that Wynmar wishes more than anything to speak with Noriel before leading his people from Thinglad for good.","Escort Wynmar to Haldirith","Talk to Noriel","Show Wynmar the ruins of Haldirith on the path ahead","'How infuriating, ${PLAYER}! I did not ask for this foolishness. Bah, let him return to his home. I am sure he will forget all of this soon enough, the foolish Man.'","Noriel and Wynmar are at Haldirith.","You explain to Noriel that Wynmar has been intent on seeing her again since their first meeting.\
\
'This is folly, ${PLAYER}! I do not think you were right to bring this stranger to our hidden keep, no matter what the reason.'","Wynmar cannot believe his eyes at the sight of Haldirith, home of the Elven sentinels of Thinglad"},
[6750]={"Agelwyn, the young wife of Thane Gladsúnu of Marton, is reluctant to lead her people in her husband's absence.","Agelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.\
\
You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.","Agelwyn is distraught under the pressure of responsibility that has settled on her shoulders","'I have never been so sad in my life, ${PLAYER}. I remember our last conversation like it was yesterday.'","'And here is my predicament: Should I really urge these people to make for Helm's Deep?\
\
'How do I know when that dire time is here? What if I wait too long, or go when I should stay and fight?'\
\
You assure Agelwyn that King Théoden himself has retreated to Helm's Deep, and urges everyone he sees to do the same.","'I miss my husband, ${PLAYER}. Would that he were here! I would give anything for news of Gladsúnu.'","Instancia: Un joven líder reacio","Speak with Agelwyn","Listen to Agelwyn","'Now what do I do, ${PLAYER}? I have not the experience to see what is right. In my heart, though, I wish to do as my beloved Gladsúnu bade me.'","Agelwyn's memory unfolds....","If Agelwyn wishes to heed her husband's advice and make for Helm's Deep, now is the time.","Talk to Agelwyn"},
[6751]={"'I have come with much of my household across the mountains, by way of the High Pass, for the marriage of my daughter awaits us in Gondor. Aragorn Elessar has claimed the crown of that land, and it is Arwen's wish, and his, that they marry. She will remain by his side forever. I know the way of hard choices, and this is hers to make.\
\
'Glorfindel accompanies us, as do many others of my folk. Some will attend Arwen at the wedding, and others there are who desired to see the lands beyond Imladris one last time before departing this Middle-earth. All are welcome, for such an occasion should be made as happy as can be, and more hearts make for merrier times. We travel light, but not without goods and gifts. I myself bring the Sceptre of Annúminas. It will be a gift for King Elessar, for it is his by right.\
\
'It is my own desire that this journey be full of cheer, for my daughter's benefit, but this land holds only sorrow for me; I will be happy to leave it. I understand there is a pleasant house nearby at which we might find lodging. It was the home of Beorn the Skin-changer, and is kept now by his son, is it not?'","Ask Karazgar the questions you wish","Instancia: Una solicitud","Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has declared a truce and desires to speak with you.","Karazgar has fled from the new arrivals on the road.","Karazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you.\
\
He has given you the chance to ask the questions you wish.","Approach Karazgar and hear what he has to say","Listen to what Karazgar has to say","Give Karazgar your response to his request","Elrond and much of his household have made the passage of the mountains.","'Lead on, ${PLAYER}. I trust we will find the son of Beorn a hospitable host.'","Remain alert for the reaction of Karazgar, and stay on your guard.","Karazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you.\
\
He waits for you to respond.","Wait for the newcomers to arrive","Karazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you.","Karazgar has made his request of you: he wants you to give him the Black Book of Mordor.","Mantente en guardia","Talk to Elrond on the road near the Old Ford","Give your response to Karazgar"},
[6752]={"Bingo ya debe haber elegido un buen lugar para que hagas una hoguera.","'Ah, estoy respuesto, y he tenido un sueño muy bonito. Volvía a ser un joven muchacho de nuevo, y el aroma del desayuno se colaba en mi dormitorio. Escuchaba a mucha gente haciendo ruido fuera de mi habitación, y el chocar de cacerolas y sartenes en la cocina.\
\
'¿Tú has tenido algún sueño placentero, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}?'","Instance: Una noche apacible","Habla con Bingo junto a la hoguera","Habéis dejado el camino y ahora Bingo quiere acampar para pasar la noche.","Yesca adecuada para el fuego recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las horas de la nochen han pasado... con muchos incidentes... y Bingo por fin se levanta.","Habla con Bingo","Bingo se ha dormido, pero alguien tiene que quedarse despierto y alerta por si surge algún peligro. ¡Y ese alguien eres tú!","Recoge yesca adecuada para el fuego (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bingo te ha pedido que busques yesca adecuada para hacer una hoguera.","'Está oscureciendo. ¡Encontraré un buen lugar para encender un fuego, si tú recoges algo de madera!","'¡Siéntate! Quizá ahora seamos aventureros, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero no hay razón para estar siempre de pie! El descanso es el descanso, y a estas alturas nos lo merecemos, ¿no crees? Hemos cubierto una buena distancia hoy, y ya hemos dejado atrás las Tierras Solitarias. ¡El Bosque de los Trolls espera!'","Bingo está sentado junto al fuego que habéis encendido en el Bosque de los Trolls, listo para irse a dormir.","Bingo está listo para descansar por hoy, y quiere acampar justo a la entrada del Bosque de los Trolls.","Haz una hoguera en el lugar que ha elegido Bingo","Monta guardia en el campamento mientras Bingo duerme","'Es una pena haberme despertado tan pronto. ¡Me hubiera gustado disfrutar más de ese agradable sueño! El desayuno estaba casi listo para servir, y un desayuno de la Comarca es mejor que en ninguna otra parte... ¡nada que ver con el Bosque de los Trolls!'"},
[6753]={"Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:visto[m]|vista[f]} por Ardhun.","Llega Ardhun","<rgb=#FF0000>No te acerques demasiado a la conversación entre Eluna y Ardhun</rgb>","Espera a que Ardhun llegue","¡Los Draig-lûth atacan!","Más guerreros Draig-lûth aparecen con fuerza","Defiende a Eluna","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Eluna ha sido derrotada!</rgb>","'Regresamos a Lhan Garan sin demora. Ardhun vendrá con nosotros. Yo asumiré la responsabilidad por ella.'","Partes junto a Eluna y sus estudiantes hacia una negociación de alto riesgo.","'Entonces, sigamos adelante.'","Habla con Eluna","Espera a que Ardhun llegue.","Habla con Eluna antes que cominencen las negociaciones.","La lucha ha terminado.\
\
Reagrúpate con los demás.","Eluna ha sobrevivido al intento contra su vida, en gran parte gracias a tu valentía.\
\
Deberías hablar con Eluna.","Deberías defender a Eluna","Permanece alerta.","Reagrúpate con Eluna y sus estudiantes","Escucha la conversación entre Eluna y Ardhun.","Instancia: Un Reencuentro Agridulce","Permanece en guardia mientras llegan más Draig-lûth","'Espero que podamos resolver esto solo con palabras, pero si no, contaré contigo para luchar. Mantente ocultandote a menos que sea necesaria tu intervención.'"},
[6754]={"Habla con el Frontero Boffin.","'Tu entrenamiento tendrá que bastar por ahora. Toma las armas del bolso. No son gran cosa, pero con suerte te ayudarán si te encuentras con algún peligro.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Para abrir la caja, usa el ratón y haz doble clic sobre ella o clic derecho una vez.</rgb>","Después de demostrar tu habilidad, háblale al Frontero Boffin para saber a dónde desea llevarte.","En la puerta de la Granja de Odo, habla con el Frontero Boffin.","<rgb=#00FF00>¡Has entrenado bien y has impresionado al Frontero Boffin!</rgb>","Libera a los otros hobbits.","Sigue al Frontero Boffin.","Toma las armas del bolso del Frontero Boffin <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre el bolso)</rgb>","'Bien hecho. Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un Frontero[m]|una Frontera[f]} en todo menos en ceremonia. Nos ocuparemos de eso cuando regresemos a Cavada Grande. Explora el camino mientras cierro esta puerta y asegúrate de que esté despejado. Vuelve a mí cuando hayas despejado el paso.'","Escapa del campamento Montebruno con Trancos.","El Frontero Boffin ha mencionado que necesitas un arma antes de adentrarte más en la granja. Te ha llevado a un bolso con un par de armas.","Después de demostrar tu habilidad, habla con el Frontero Boffin para saber a dónde desea llevarte.","'Me alegra haberte encontrado. Estos Montebruno han encarcelado a demasiados. Debemos rescatar a los otros hobbits. Es demasiado tarde para el Frontero Boffin, pero debemos lamentarlo después. ¡Rápido, sígueme!'","Mientras el Frontero Boffin intenta cortar las telarañas, defiéndelo de las arañas que seguramente intentarán detenerlo.\
\
Al avanzar por la granja del viejo Odo, encontraste tu camino bloqueado por telarañas.","'¡Ayúdanos! ¡Ella volverá en cualquier momento! ¡Está dormida!'","Mientras entrenas para convertirte en Vigilante, tu instructor, el Frontero Boffin, ha conocido a tres hobbits viajeros en el camino. Los tres hobbits están viajando a Bree, pero se han detenido para tomar un refrigerio.","Deberías informarle al Frontero Boffin que el camino hacia la siguiente puerta ya está despejado.\
\
El Vigilante Boffin te pidió que despejaras el camino hacia la siguiente puerta mientras él vigilaba por si regresaba el Jinete Negro.","'No te quedes ahí ${PLAYERNAME:parado[m]|parada[f]}. Despeja el camino hacia la siguiente puerta. Yo vigilaré que ese Jinete no regrese. Te dije que las arañas crecen grandes por aquí.'","Despiertas dentro del campamento Montebruno.","'Una vez que abra esta puerta, necesitarás despejar el camino hacia la siguiente entrada. Mientras haces eso, vigilaré por si regresa ese jinete.'","Tras ahuyentar al Nazgûl, habla con Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón.","'¡Ya era hora de que nos salvaras! Es momento de salir de aquí antes de que aparezcan más gente grande. ¡Tengo hambre!'","Un Jinete Negro ha asustado al Frontero Boffin fuera del camino. ¡Síguelo!","El Frontero Boffin cree que lo mejor es esconderse hasta que el Jinete Negro pase, y piensa que el granero de hojas del viejo Odo podría ser un buen lugar para ocultarse.","'Ya casi salimos de esta granja infestada de arañas. Sin duda elegí un mal lugar para esconderme. Había olvidado que Odo la abandonó hace ya bastante tiempo.\
\
'¿Qué crees que quería ese jinete con esos buenos hobbits? En fin... ¡sigamos!'","Los hobbits parecen estar pasándola muy bien. Los tres viajeros se dirigen a Bree, lo cual es algo inusual para un hobbit, pero pronto la charla sobre hongos te distrae de esa preocupación.","<rgb=#00FF00>¡Has escapado con la ayuda de Trancos!</rgb>","Libérate de los Montebruno de Archet.","Ahora que has sido ${PLAYERNAME:liberado[m]|liberada[f]}, sigue a Trancos para ayudar a su compañero montaraz, Amdir. Ellos te guiarán fuera de este campamento maligno.","'Bien, despejaste el camino. No ha habido señales de ese Jinete, pero estoy seguro de que aún ronda por aquí.\
\
'Corramos hacia la siguiente entrada. ¡Cuanto antes entremos en la casa del viejo Odo, mejor!'","Sigue al Frontero Boffin en busca de un lugar seguro.\
\
El Vigilante Boffin encontró la llave de la casa del viejo Odo, pero en su apuro por abrir la puerta, la rompió dentro de la cerradura.","Habla con el Frontero Boffin <rgb=#00FF00>(Camina hacia adelante presionando W)</rgb>","Siéntate y escucha a los hobbits.","Al regresar de tu encargo, ves que el Frontero Boffin ha invitado a tres hobbits a compartir su fuego. Los hobbits están viajando a Bree, lo cual ya es curioso por sí mismo.","'Ah, bien, has regresado. Estos buenos amigos estaban caminando por el camino y se detuvieron para cenar, merendar y cantar en la fiesta.\
\
'Son gente muy alegre. ¡Ojalá tuviéramos más viajeros por los Límites!'","Te encuentras ${PLAYERNAME:prisionero[m]|prisionera[f]} en el campamento de los Montebruno en Archet. Te tienen en su campamento. Debes encontrar la forma de escapar.","Derrota arañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La Reina Araña ha despertado. Libera al Frontero Boffin y a los otros hobbits de la malvada criatura.","'Un último paso en tu entrenamiento y serás ${PLAYERNAME:un Frontero[m]|una Frontera[f]} en todo menos en nombre. Tendremos que esperar hasta regresar a Cavada Grande para la ceremonia oficial.\
\
'Muéstrame lo que puedes hacer con esas armas tuyas.'","Habla con Trancos","El Frontero Boffin te ha pedido que entrenes con él para asegurarse de que puedes emprender tus viajes.","'No te quedes ahí ${PLAYERNAME:parado[m]|parada[f]}... ¡sácame de aquí! ¡Soy un Sacovilla-Bolsón!'","Arañas vencidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Con el camino despejado, sigue al Frontero Boffin mientras abre la puerta.","Habla con el hobbit prisionero, Mundo, e intenta ayudarlo a salir de allí.","Instancia: Un camino a través de la oscuridad","¡Has encontrado a dos hobbits atrapados!"},
[6755]={"Has demostrado que puedes luchar; ahora es más seguro continuar con la patrulla.","'¡Eres un hobbit más audaz de lo que pensaba! Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. ¡Sigamos adelante!'","Habla con el Frontero Boffin.","Sigue a Trancos mientras te ayuda a escapar","Arañas atacantes derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durante un paseo nocturno, te encuentras con el Frontero Boffin en un camino especialmente oscuro de la Comarca.","Derrota a las arañas atacantes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Frontero Boffin te espera en el sendero.\
\
Debes hablar con el Frontero Boffin antes de continuar tu huida a través de la granja.","'¡Ya estamos cerca, ${PLAYER}! La granja de Odo nos llevará a salvo hasta el camino, y desde allí podremos llegar al pueblo más cercano... con suerte sin encontrarnos con arañas, o algo peor.'","Has salido a dar un paseo y parece que hay alguien más en el camino.","Sigue al Frontero Boffin.","El Frontero Boffin necesitará protección de las arañas mientras corta sus resistentes telarañas.\
\
Debes derrotar a las arañas y proteger al Frontero Boffin mientras intenta llevarte a un lugar seguro.","Te encuentras en una celda de prisión, rodeado por los bandidos que te secuestraron a ti y a tus compañeros hobbits.","Instancia: Un camino a través de la oscuridad","'¿Ya has equipado tu arma, ${PLAYER}? ¡Practiquemos entre nosotros ahora!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>ACCESO AL INVENTARIO: Presiona ‘i’ para abrir tu inventario y ver el arma, o haz clic izquierdo en los Íconos de bolsas en la parte inferior de la pantalla.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPAR TU ARMA: Haz clic derecho en el arma de tu inventario para equiparla. Esto reemplazará el arma endeble que tienes equipada actualmente.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>CONSEJO: Debes equipar tu mejor arma antes de intentar entablar combate.</rgb>","El saco está cerca del Frontero Boffin en el camino.\
\
Debes mirar dentro del saco para ver si contiene algo que pueda serte útil en una noche oscura como esta.","Las arañas están en la Granja de Hojas de Odo.\
\
El Frontero Boffin teme a las arañas y desea que despejes el camino antes de aventurarse adelante.","Hay un arma en el saco. Ahora debes saquearla y equiparla antes de intentar luchar.","Habla con el Frontero Boffin para comenzar el combate de práctica <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre el arma en tu inventario para equiparla.)</rgb>","Has despertado dentro de una prisión, rodeado de bandidos.","Amdir ha ayudado a rescatar a tus amigos de los crueles bandidos.\
\
Ahora debes reunirte con el compañero de Trancos, un Montaraz llamado Amdir","Debes hablar con el hobbit que te llama.","Avanza por el camino <rgb=#00FF00>(Muévete hacia delante presionando W)</rgb>","Trancos ahora se arrodilla junto a su amigo gravemente herido, Amdir.\
\
Debes hablar con Trancos, pues él sabrá mejor qué hacer a continuación.","Intenta salir de tu celda","La puerta que te saca de la prisión está al final del pasillo, saliendo de tu celda.\
\
Debes seguir a Trancos fuera de la puerta de la prisión.","El Frontero Boffin quiere ver si eres capaz de empuñar una hoja para defenderte.\
\
Debes practicar un duelo de entrenamiento con el Frontero Boffin para que ambos se sientan más confiados en el oscuro camino.","Sigue a Trancos","El Frontero Boffin está intentando llegar a un lugar seguro a través de la Granja de Hojas de Odo.\
\
Debes seguir al Frontero Boffin hasta un camino más seguro, que los conducirá a ambos a una aldea cercana.","Arañas amenazantes bloquean tu camino.","'¿Quién va ahí? ¿Cuál es su asunto en el camino? ¡Soy un Frontero, respóndanme de inmediato!'\
\
El hobbit se sobresalta, pero la alarma en su rostro se transforma en alivio cuando ve tu cara.\
\
'¡Oh, gracias al cielo! — ¡un hobbit! Lo siento muchísimo; me llevé un buen susto. Algo no se siente bien esta noche.'","Debes hablar con tu rescatador de aspecto severo","El Jinete Negro se ha ido, pero el compañero Montaraz de Trancos está gravemente herido","Un Hombre misterioso y curtido por el clima te espera en la prisión de los bandidos.\
\
Debes hablar con tu rescatador para que pueda guiarte fuera del peligro.","'Permanece cerca de mí esta noche, ${PLAYER}... debemos llevar a Amdir a un lugar seguro. ¡Debemos huir hacia Archet!\
\
'Frontero Boffin, deberías regresar a la Comarca. Sus lindes deben mantenerse a salvo. Celandine, Mundo — vengan conmigo. Me preocupa la seguridad de Mundo cuando toda la gente malvada al oeste del Camino Verde está buscando a \\qBolsón\\q. ¡Ay de que mi verdadera misión deba esperar!'","Abandona la prisión <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre las puertas para abrirlas. Camina hacia las puertas abiertas para ser transportado a tu destino.)</rgb>","El Frontero Boffin desea patrullar el camino, pues tiene una inquietante sensación sobre esta noche.\
\
Debes patrullar el camino junto al Frontero Boffin.","Derrota arañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}) <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre una araña para seleccionarla en combate. Haz clic izquierdo en los Íconos de habilidades en la parte inferior de la pantalla para usarlas.)</rgb>","Has salido a dar un paseo, pero parece que hay alguien en el camino delante (algo poco común en estos parajes tranquilos.)\
\
Debes hablar con el individuo que está en el camino frente a ti. <rgb=#00ff00>Haz clic derecho sobre los personajes para interactuar</rgb>.","El Frontero Boffin te espera en el sendero.\
\
Debes seguir al Frontero Boffin para escapar de la amenaza en el camino.","Habla con el sujeto del camino <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre el hobbit para interactuar)</rgb>","Habla con Trancos","Las arañas están en la Granja de Hojas de Odo.\
\
El Frontero Boffin teme a las arañas y desea que despejes el camino antes de aventurarse más adelante.","Has salido a dar un paseo, pero parece que hay alguien en el camino delante (algo poco común en estos parajes tranquilos.)\
\
Debes hablar con el individuo que está en el camino frente a ti.","Derrota arañas (0/2) <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre una araña para seleccionarla en combate. Haz clic izquierdo en los Íconos de habilidades en la parte inferior de la pantalla para usarlas.)</rgb>","Examina el saco al costado del camino <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre el saco para recoger lo que hay dentro)</rgb>","Arañas vencidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Te has encontrado con un Frontero sobresaltado en el camino del País de las Colinas Verdes.\
\
Debes hablar con el Frontero Boffin para escuchar lo que tiene que decir.","'¡Ven, ${PLAYER}! Veo que tienes un espíritu valiente, pero es hora de huir. El Bolsón que capturaron no es el Bolsón que están cazando.\
\
'Los bandidos no nos seguirán cuando descubran su error, pero sería prudente estar muy lejos de aquí.\
\
'Mi compañero está afuera, ayudando a rescatar a tus amigos. ¡Unámonos a ellos!'"},
[6756]={"Drugât and Nerzus can be found in the innermost chamber of Nimrond.\
\
Defeat Drugât and Nerzus, leaders of the ruthless dead and Orkish forces.","You should speak with Arvaethor.","Arvaethor asks for you to follow him to the very heart of the caverns, deep inside the mountain.","'Come, let us return to Ethring.'","'The Ruthless Dead have begun to amass their forces, for what purpose, I know not. Many will die if they march out of the Vale, under cover of these darkened skies. We have made it this far. Perhaps we stand a chance of slaying their leader and leaving their forces without command.\
\
'Come, let us brave the darkness together.'","Drugât has been defeated","Delve to the deepest chamber of the caverns of Nimrond","Arvaethor has fallen in battle!","<rgb=#FF0000>Arvaethor must survive</rgb>","Speak with Arvaethor","Speak with Arvaethor.","Delve to the deepest chamber of the caverns of Nimrond.","The Hall of Nimrond stands before you, crawling with the Dead","Destroy the dark stones to gain entrance to the inner hall of Nimrond.","Defeat Drugât and Nerzus","Instancia: Un Final Despiadado","Destroy the dark stones to gain entrance to the inner hall of Nimrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed dark stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Drugât had strayed far from redemption. I doubt we shall see him wander among the living again.'"},
[6757]={"'What in Durin's name have we found here? There are no records of this place! I had thought the only thing we might find down this far was the Stair itself, but... perhaps I was wrong! Let us look around!'","Are you... imagining this?","Talk to Frethi","Instancia: Una cámara secreta","Frethi is ready to begin exploring the chamber.\
\
You should talk to Frethi.","You have found an ancient chamber deep beneath Moria. What secrets lie within?","Look around with Frethi","You ask if Frethi saw the strange figure.\
\
'No, I saw nothing. Are you feeling all right, friend?'"},
[6758]={"'Lo lograste, ${PLAYER}. ¡Haremos de ti ${PLAYER:un Experto Cazador[m]|un Experta Cazadora[f]} de Tesoros! ¡Debes contarme los detalles de la recuperación mientras regresamos a Avenal!'","Instancia: Un Club Secreto","Has venido a Dwaling con Ponto Avena para ocuparte de los bandidos que han tomado el pueblo.","La porra que buscas está en el suelo junto a los bandidos dormidos cerca de la casa de Perlina Gamyi en Dwaling.\
\
Ponto espera que recuperes la porra de entre los bandidos dormidos en Dwaling.","Encuentra la porra","'Muchos de los bandidos duermen junto a las hogueras cerca de la casa de Perlina Gamyi, cuesta abajo en Dwaling. Acércate sigilosamente y busca la porra; tómala y tráemela, pero no entres en combate. Si te ven, nuestra tarea fracasa.'","¡Un rufián te ha visto!","Evita ser detectado por los rufianes","Ponto Avena está de pie en el camino que baja hacia Dwaling.\
\
Ponto espera hablar contigo sobre tu próxima \\qrecuperación\\q.","'¡Partamos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} ! ¡Espero con ansias el relato de tus hazañas esta noche!'","Robas silenciosamente la porra del bandido dormido","'La aldea de Dwaling está justo cuesta abajo, ${PLAYER}, y está llena de bandidos. Uno de los Hombres del Jefe empuña una porra mortal; sin esa arma, aseguro que no sería rival ni siquiera para un solo ${RACE}.\
\
'Algunos de los bandidos permanecen de guardia, pero muchos de los villanos duermen junto a las hogueras cerca de la casa de Perlina Gamyi. Acércate sigilosamente a los que duermen; la porra de su líder seguramente estará en el suelo, junto a su lugar de descanso.\
\
'¡Toma la porra y vuelve conmigo, ${PLAYER}! Pero no entres en combate. Si te ve siquiera uno de los Hombres del Jefe, nuestra tarea fracasa.'","Ponto Avena está en la ladera del borde norte de Dwaling.\
\
Ponto espera oír cómo te fue en la recuperación de la porra."},
[6759]={"Grímyr is waiting to speak with you.","A dwarf named Grímyr has asked to speak with you privately about some urgent matter.","Defend yourself","Grímyr has suddenly attacked you!\
\
You should defend yourself!","Grímyr has asked that you follow him to a more discreet location.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. What I must say is very important. Come, let us move somewhere more private.'","Instancia: Una reunión secreta","Talk to Grímyr","Follow Grímyr","'I do not want to hear your excuses! You must stand before the King! Now!'","Grímyr suddenly attacks!"},
[6760]={"Glorfindel is in Sul Madásh.","Cúridwan is in Sul Madásh.","Cúridwan has returned from her wandering in the blighted forest and Inkanûsh is eager to speak with her in Sul Madásh.","'Earlier I was amused because Cúridwan reminded me of Inkanûsh... but I did not expect such similarities as these!'\
\
Glorfindel suddenly falls silent, listening.\
\
'Enemies approach, ${PLAYER}. I fear Sul Madásh is under attack!'","Inkanûsh and Cúridwan are in Sul Madásh.","Listen to Glorfindel","'The number of Wizards sent to the northern lands may have been five, but I assure you these southern lands are vast. Do you think the Shoghór nomads would welcome you among them in the body you now wear? The Ghursâti, the \\qPowers,\\q as you name them, they sent their servants in form appropriate to the people they sought to aid. How might \\qthe Golden Maiden\\q or \\qthe Sorceress in Green\\q be received in the cold northern lands, I wonder?  \
\
'The Wizards of the northern line and the Wizards of the southern line must be different, or they must each fail in their purposes. In this I see the wisdom of the Powers that gave to us our missions, separate though shared they may be.\
\
'It is not for an individual to see the entire breadth of the tapestry. That is reserved for those who sent us, is it not?'","Listen to the conversation between Inkanûsh and Cúridwan","Check Baharúd for signs of life","Inkanûsh is in Sul Madásh.","'But how can this be?'\
\
The Wizard's brow furrows.\
\
'It is true that some things were left unknown to me by the Powers that sent me to Middle-earth, that I might best accomplish my purpose... but the number of my Order is five. Far have I travelled across Middle-earth to oppose the evils of Sauron and his servants, and Radagast too has played his part. Saruman was the highest of my Order, until he succumbed, but even in that I see the role Saruman played in the defeat of Sauron.\
\
'Two others of the five travelled east into distant lands, and their fate is unknown to me. They serve the Powers, as I do. I am certain of it.'","'Thórvilon is dear to me, as are all of the Kintai. I have sought for many years to cure the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight that holds Imhûlar in its grip, but while my salves have proven beneficial here and there, something has of late revealed itself to me. The Pale Blight is itself a symptom only, and not the source of the evil. A greater corruption emerged in Adagím, moving throughout the Emerald Wood, and my salves have proven less effective at dealing with this root cause of the blight.\
\
'But I will not give up.'","Talk to Cúridwan in Sul Madásh","'Let us see what this woman Cúridwan has to say in answer to my questions, ${PLAYER}.'","Alas, Baharúd is slain","Talk to Inkanûsh in Sul Madásh","'Ísman rules above them all, the Sky-master. In his lordly form he observed the comings and goings of the Shoghór as they crossed the great desert; it was in feminine aspect that Ísman lit the stars to show them the way.\
\
'Jarângar the Water-friend brings healing and wards away the much-feared drought, and Shin-samêt the All-Shaper fashions the plants that grow beside the rivers and the animals that drink from the oases.\
\
'Zangûr the Walker of the Wilds knows all the paths of the mountains and valleys, as well as the wild flowers of the hillside and the secrets of the blossoming forests.\
\
'Bâkhlas the Doom-hand is feared and respected by the Shoghór nomads, for the domain of Bâkhlas is death. Better-loved are Arâmkal the Soothing Word, who brings rest and dreams to the Shoghór, as well as Garândi the Swift One, who endures all hardship to emerge triumphant and laughing at the end of suffering.\
\
'The seven Ghursâti who gave me my purpose and sent me to aid the people of this land are opposed by the demonic figure Makhâl, but I will not speak of him. The Shoghór speak his name only in whispers, and then unwillingly.'","Talk to Glorfindel in Sul Madásh","Instancia: Una miniaventura compartida","The Utûgi have been driven away, but they leave sorrow in their wake."},
[6761]={"Imák and Venko wait for you on the hill upon which the Drearspire stands.","Eavesdrop on the discussion between the cultists in the Drearspire","Loud mechanisms operate noisily inside Tûr Fúar, but the halls are empty","Talk to Imák outside the Drearspire","'I hear the voices of Angmarim from just ahead, ${PLAYER}. Let us advance, slowly, and see if we can eavesdrop on their conversation. Let us remain out of sight and we may learn what they seek to do here in Câr Bronach, and elsewhere.'\
\
He turns to address your Stout-axe companion.\
\
'Imák, you stay here and guard the path of our escape, in the event we need it. But we will try to avoid being seen by these villains.\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}, and make as little noise as possible!'","Venko stands before a side entrance to the Drearspire, considering its suitability for your purpose.","Follow Imák and Venko toward the Drearspire","Enter the Drearspire with Imák and Venko","You have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko and should search the tower for answers.","You have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko, and now you have the opportunity to eavesdrop on some of the Angmarim who remain in the tower. Perhaps you will learn what these evil folk seek to accomplish within Câr Bronach, and elsewhere.\
\
You must not be seen by the Angmarim cultists.","Inside the Drearspire, Venko has called for you to halt.","Talk to Imák inside the Drearspire","Explore the Drearspire with Imák and Venko","Instancia: Una presencia silenciosa","'The snow has begun. It is not yet very heavy, but if it gets worse perhaps it will mask our approach.\
\
'Let us try to do this without fighting, if we can. I wager the answers we seek will be on an upper level of the tower, and the further we can get without making noise, the more we will learn.\
\
'Will this be a problem, Brawler?'","<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid being seen by the Angmarim cultists</rgb>","Talk to Venko inside the Drearspire","Imák and Venko hope your presence in the Drearspire will go unnoticed as you investigate the Angmarim interest in the tower.","'A tower of this size could hold a battalion of Angmarim, ${PLAYER}, and our prior scouting revealed that recently it did! Where then have the cultists gone?\
\
'Let us proceed, and let caution be the watch-word.'","'The snow has begun. It is not yet very heavy, but if it gets worse perhaps it will mask our approach.\
\
'Let us try to do this without fighting, if we can. I wager the answers we seek will be on an upper level of the tower, and the further we can get without making noise, the more we will learn.\
\
'Agreed? Good.'","You have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko, in search of answers: what villainy have the Angmarim conducted within Câr Bronach?","'Still we have seen no guards, and it seems to me we might have walked right up to the front door of the tower, if that was our wish! We have either been very fortunate to this point... or it is a trap.\
\
'Let us use this side entrance. It may allow us to surprise any Angmarim that might lie in ambush for us within the Drearspire.'","Talk to Venko beside the side entrance to Drearspire","'Our investigation has borne fruit, ${PLAYER}: it seems the strange occurrences within Câr Bronach are not entirely understood by the Angmarim cultists themselves.\
\
'But there is reason for us to leave this tower, and with haste! The Angmarim leader Rúvaran now possesses an artifact with which he hopes to break the runes on Gloomingtarn, where stand the still waters of the sacred lake of Durin!\
\
'We will set aside the mysteries of Câr Bronach for now. Rúvaran and his Angmarim must be opposed!'","You have come with Imák and Venko to Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, to learn if an Angmarim ritual is behind the curious happenings within Câr Bronach."},
[6762]={"Leland Sotomonte está dentro de la cueva, escondite de los bandidos que le robaron el almuerzo.\
\
Leland Sotomonte espera para hablar contigo.","'Déjame cortar el asado y luego partiremos. ¡Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ir!'","Habla con Leland Sotomonte","Instancia: Una canción para la compañía","'El hombre a cargo de estos bandidos se llama Holt Viperino, ¡y no puede salirse con la suya! ¡La gente decente no debería preocuparse de que le roben sus cosas!\
\
'Sigue de cerca lo que ocurra, ${PLAYER}, y tal vez puedas crear una canción que conmueva los corazones de la buena gente y advierta a villanos como estos bandidos que no recurran al crimen.'","Protege a Leland Sotomonte","Leland Sotomonte busca recuperar algo que le fue robado por los bandidos.\
\
Leland Sotomonte te ha pedido que lo ayudes.","Leland Sotomonte ha encontrado el escondite de los bandidos que le robaron algo valioso.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ir? ¡Te acompañaré, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} cantante! ¡Gracias de nuevo, y espero que esta historia sirva para una buena canción!'"},
[6763]={"'¡Valientemente hecho, ${PLAYER}! Has prestado un gran servicio a todos nosotros y mereces la más alta alabanza por tu papel al mantener la línea.\
\
'Me gustaría ver a esos bandidos intentar esto otra vez; ¿creyeron que saber blandir una espada sería suficiente para desafiar una línea de Vigilantes? ¿Están locos? ¡Deben estarlo!'","Habla con Toby Thorndyke","Andrew Roblebosque está detrás de la línea de Vigilantes al sur de Bree.\
\
El ataque ha sido repelido con éxito, y ahora deberías hablar con el Vigilante Roblebosque.","Toby Thorndyke está en tu lugar dentro de la línea de Vigilantes que defienden Bree del ataque desde el sur.","'Regresemos a Bree, ${PLAYER}, y hablaremos de algunos puntos finos de tu desempeño durante el ataque.'","Te has alejado de tu posición, y la defensa ha sufrido por ello","El ataque ha sido repelido","Instancia: Una Lanza en la Marca del Sur","Habla con Andrew Roblebosque","'Me alegra que hayas accedido a ayudarnos, ${PLAYER}, pues hay un hueco en nuestra línea y quiero verlo cubierto.\
\
'Habla con Toby Thorndyke, justo adelante, y él te mostrará tu lugar en la línea.\
\
'¡Es muy importante que no abandones tu puesto en la línea cuando comience el ataque! Una defensa organizada es nuestra mejor arma contra bandas de bandidos como la que se aproxima.'","Has aceptado unirte a la línea de Vigilantes defendiendo el acceso a Bree contra una banda de bandidos que se aproxima desde el sur.","'¿Nos aliaremos en la defensa, ${PLAYER}? ¡Me alegra oírlo!\
\
'Te mostraré los límites de nuestra posición. ¡No debes alejarte de estos límites durante el ataque! ¡La línea no debe romperse!'","Andrew Roblebosque está detrás de la línea de Vigilantes al sur de Bree.\
\
El Vigilante Roblebosque está esperando hablar contigo.","No abandones tu puesto en la línea"},
[6765]={"Answer Glúrkub's question: can the goblin trust Prince Durin?","Listen to Glúrkub","Glúrkub stands in the hiding spot near the path to the mountain's summit.","Watch Glúrkub carry out the plan","Talk to Glúrkub in the Welkin-lofts","'I am sorry about that, ${PLAYER}... I forgot the password!\
\
'But all is well now.'","Glúrkub stands in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.","Instancia: Un robo de libertad","Talk to Prince Durin","You have come with Glúrkub to the Welkin-lofts to steal the mithril hammer wielded by Gorgar the Ruthless, and perhaps earn the goblin captive his freedom.","You have safely escorted Glúrkub past the dwarf-lines and out of Gundabad.","Return to Prince Durin with Glúrkub and the mithril hammer","Answer Glúrkub's question: what password should he use to call you from hiding if he gets into trouble?","'I not know what to say, ${PLAYER}. I did not think dwarf-prince would honour agreement. Glúrkub happy to be wrong!\
\
'Lead the way, friend ${RACE}. Sooner Glúrkub far from here, the better!'","'Now is my turn, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Remember! Do not leave hiding spot until you hear me say password!'","Talk to Glúrkub","Glúrkub is in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>","You were seen too early, and the plan has failed!","You and Glúrkub successfully carried out the plan to steal the mithril hammer and should now return to Prince Durin.","'I will not lie to you, ${PLAYER}: I am glad to see him go. Glúrkub was of some help to the Gabil'akkâ, but it could very easily have gone otherwise.'\
\
You ask Glóin if he feels eyes upon the two of you, and he shakes his head.\
\
'I cannot say I do, my friend, but that means little. As the years pass I find more and more things similarly passing my notice! It would not surprise me to learn that Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ watch us from afar, pondering our escort of Glúrkub to safety.'\
\
You give Glóin a nod but keep your silence; the watchful presence has already departed, and you do not wish to worry the old dwarf unnecessarily.","Talk to Glúrkub outside Gundabad","Listen to Glúrkub explain the plan","Glúrkub has asked you if he can trust Prince Durin, and if you think the prince will let him go.","Escort Glúrkub from Gundabad","Glúrkub has delivered the mithril hammer to Prince Durin, as he promised. The goblin now waits to speak with you.","Talk to Glúrkub in the hiding spot","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot until Glúrkub shouts the password!</rgb>","Glúrkub has gone to execute his part of the plan: stealing the mithril hammer from the guards Gorgar left behind. You should remain in the hiding spot and not emerge unless Glúrkub gets into trouble and shouts the password.","'Thank you for bringing me this far, ${PLAYER}. I will go rest of the way from here.\
\
'Glúrkub look forward to life far from Gorgar, Hrímil, and Gundabad!'","Glúrkub stands among the trees not far from the hiding place you scouted.","Listen to Glúrkub and wait for Gorgar to climb to the peak","'You have done well, ${PLAYER}... you and the goblin both.'\
\
Durin studies the clean, angular lines worked in the mithril of the hammer, marvelling at the ease with which he hefts the weapon.\
\
'Remarkable, my friend, truly remarkable. Gorgar will not be pleased to lose this! Let him howl his anger to the skies, while he can, for with this he will be undone, and every dwarf that suffered at his hands will be avenged!'\
\
Durin looks up from his study of the mithril hammer and considers the goblin standing before him.\
\
'Now to the matter of the goblin. Your kind are enemies of me and mine, Glúrkub, and you served our hated foe; you would have seen us all slain, if you could.\
\
'But you did not, and through your efforts you have aided the cause of the Gabil'akkâ. So too have you performed a great service to me personally, for the delivery of this mithril hammer has lifted my spirit and given to me a weapon unrivalled. For your service on my behalf I will grant you what you have said you sought: safe passage through the lines of war, and the freedom to establish your own dwelling far from Gorgar and his people, somewhere beyond the lands of my folk.\
\
'${PLAYER} will see you brought through the lines, and where you go afterward is up to you. These are my thanks, and they are all you will receive, for I am unaccustomed to speaking words such as these to goblins.'","Glúrkub has asked you what password he should use to call you forth from hiding if he gets into trouble.","'This where we wait. Gorgar will be along soon, and after he leaves the shiny hammer behind, that is when Glúrkub earns his keep, and won't be kept any longer!'","Glúrkub has seized the mithril hammer and raced back to the hiding spot, where he waits to speak with you.","'We almost there, ${PLAYER}. You will see how helpful Glúrkub can be, and then your prince will let him go.\
\
'How funny: Glúrkub must steal a thing to earn his freedom!'","Prince Durin has commanded that Glúrkub be given safe passage away from Gundabad, and asked you to escort the goblin from Elderslade.","Glúrkub has delivered the mithril hammer to Prince Durin, as he promised to do. How will the prince now respond?"},
[6766]={"'¡Lo has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}! Veo que te desenvuelves bien entre sombras y luz de luna, ¡como debe ser un buen saqueador!\
\
'¿Escuchas eso? ¿Son perros ladrando?'","Atherol Tuk está agachado en la cerca al borde de la propiedad de Maggot, junto al camino.\
\
Atherol espera hablar contigo sobre el plan para evitar que los bandidos roben los hongos de Maggot.","Algunos bandidos han venido a Bamfurlargo y pueden estar escondidos en cualquier parte de la granja.\
\
Atherol Tuk espera que elimines a los bandidos que planean robar los hongos de Maggot... ¡y quiere que tú también robes algunos!","Tú y Atherol Tuk habéis venido a Bamfurlargo para evitar que los bandidos Montebruno se lleven los deliciosos hongos de Maggot.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar al Campamento de Adso? ¡Los hongos están a salvo!'","'Hay varios bandidos por ahí, escondidos en alguna parte de la granja del granjero Maggot, . ¡Ve y enséñales una lección! Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un saqueador[m]|una saqueadora[f]}, ¿verdad? No deberías tener problemas para acercarte a ellos sigilosamente.\
\
'¡Y aprovecha para recoger algunos hongos! Ningún saqueador que se respete dejaría la granja sin unos cuantos de los deliciosos hongos de Maggot. Ten cuidado con sus perros, sin embargo: si te acercas demasiado, te olfatearán, sin importar cuán ${PLAYERNAME:sigiloso[m]|sigilosa[f]} creas que eres.'","Has recogido algunos de los hongos de Maggot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Según mi información, el proveedor de los Montebruno iba a enviar a algunos de sus compinches aquí esta noche para robar tantos hongos como puedan llevar.\
\
'Yo vigilaré aquí. Busca a los bandidos en la granja y usa tu habilidad para acabar con ellos en silencio. Te esperaré aquí cuando los hayas eliminado a todos.\
\
'¡Mantente alerta! Es una noche oscura y los bandidos pueden estar escondidos en cualquier parte de la granja. Ah, y recoge algunos hongos mientras estás aquí. Ningún saqueador que se respete se iría de la granja sin unos cuantos de los deliciosos hongos de Maggot. Ten cuidado con sus perros: si te acercas demasiado, te olfatearán, por muy sigiloso que creas ser.'","Recoge algunos de los hongos de Maggot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Atherol Tuk está esperando junto a la cerca, al lado del camino, fuera de Bamfurlargo.\
\
Atherol Tuk espera saber que te has deshecho de los bandidos que planeaban robar los hongos de Maggot.","Instancia: Un ladrón en la noche"},
[6767]={"Defeat Zakrif, the troll-commander of the Orc-company.","'Ah, my friends, you have arrived. I have told Reeve Fastred of the Easterlings coming from the north, but he will not relent....'","Instancia: Sed de sangre","Hutha has perished","'Alas, we have failed here. Let us return to Snowbourn.'","Talk to Reeve Fastred","'Well-fought, ${CLASS}! That was a dire fight, but we proved victorious.\
\
'I do not doubt the accuracy of Burnoth's report, but this battle only proves my will. The people of the Sutcrofts shall stand and defend their lands.'","Listen to the discussion between the Riders Four and Reeve Fastred.","Listen to the discussion between the Riders Four and Reeve Fastred","You have accompanied the Riders Four to the camp of Reeve Fastred in the Sutcrofts in the hope of discussing the Khundolar invasion with him.","Talk to Burnoth.","Léofdag has perished","Defeat Zakrif","Fastred has perished","Ulf has perished","Burnoth has perished","Talk to Burnoth","Defeat the Orcs attacking Fastred's camp","Defeat the Orcs attacking Fastred's camp.","Defeated Zakrif","Fastred and the Riders Four must survive","Talk to Fastred."},
[6768]={"You have driven off the Shadow-wolves","Speak with Amarion and return to Echad Dagoras in Fordirith.","'I would say that we should move quickly before the wolves notice us....\
\
'Wait, no, it is too late...they come!'","Help Amarion escape from the Black Dens.","Talk to Amarion","'Enough! You have fought well, ${PLAYER}, and at last we have a moment's respite.\
\
'I have found something of import here, but this is neither the place nor time to speak of it, as we should leave this place swiftly.'","'Let us be off then!'","Instance: A Timely Rescue","Amarion left camp to search the Black Dens, where he believed he might find some way to destroy the Shadow-wolves -- but he has been gone too long. Braigiar has asked you to search for him among the Dens in the hope that he might be found unharmed."},
[6769]={"You appear to have come upon a trail of vengeance, left by a mysterious warrior whose deeds strongly resemble Thrymm's....","Listen to Cyneberg","'I cannot wait to see Gárwig's face when he sees that Thrymm is alive!\
\
'Let us leave at once. We must prepare for battle.'","Listen to Thrymm and Cyneberg","Cyneberg se encuentra en el norte de las Altas Cumbres.\
\
Deberías seguir a Cyneberg.","A look of relief passes over Thrymm's face","Reassure Thrymm that Cyneberg is all right","'I am well now, ${PLAYER}. The joy overwhelmed me, for I thought all hope was lost.\
\
'Thrymm, why did you not return to us? I knew you were alive, but no one believed me!\
\
'I searched everywhere for you.'","Instancia: Un rastro de venganza","You should listen to Thrymm and Cyneberg.","'Do we continue to follow this trail, or do we admit our defeat and return to Forlaw?'\
\
You tell Cyneberg that you have a strange feeling about the trail of felled Orcs. Cyneberg shrugs in reply.\
\
'If you wish to live in denial of our doom a little longer, I am not one to criticize.'","Follow Cyneberg","See if Cyneberg is feeling better","Thrymm is in the northern High Knolls.\
\
You should speak with Thrymm.","Thrymm and Cyneberg are in Thrymm's cave in the northern High Knolls.","Talk to Cyneberg","'Is she ill? I cannot bear to lose her now that I have found her again. I thought everyone dead!'\
\
You assure Thrymm that Cyneberg is as healthy as can be.\
\
The shock of seeing Thrymm alive when she had given up hope seems to have overwhelmed her.","'Now... now we can defeat Núrzum, or die trying. We have Thrymm, and we have so much more knowledge of our foe.'"},
[6770]={"La criatura sigilosa está escapando por Tâl Bruinen, y debes seguirla si puedes.","Coloca el pescado bajo la ventana","Instancia: Una Trampa para la Criatura","Habla con Garbert","Tú y Garbert están listos para poner en marcha el plan del pescador para atrapar a la criatura sigilosa que ronda Tâl Bruinen.","Adwold logró alcanzarte a pesar de sufrir una herida en la pierna durante la persecución.\
\
Está esperando saber el resultado.","Adwold está escondido detrás del refugio improvisado que Garbert construyó cerca de su cabaña.\
\
¿Qué fue ese sonido? Adwold está seguro de haber oído algo. ¿Será la criatura?","La criatura sigilosa ha regresado a la cabaña de Garbert, y tú y Adwold están listos para activar la trampa.\
\
Adwold te indicó esperar su señal antes de saltar sobre la criatura para intentar capturarla.","'Hay algo ahí fuera, ${PLAYER}... creo que nuestra criatura está cerca.\
\
'Ahí está otra vez: un chapoteo suave. ¡Viene desde el agua!\
\
'Yo te daré la señal para saltar y tratar de atraparlo: queremos que esté en medio de comer el pescado, así que espera mi señal antes de revelarte.'","Udulug derrotado","Habla con Adwold","Garbert ya ha preparado parte del plan, pero aún necesita tu ayuda.","Persigue a la criatura sigilosa por Tâl Bruinen","'Este será un lugar perfecto para esperar, ${PLAYER}. Mantén los ojos abiertos: la criatura volverá en algún momento esta noche, ¡o eso cree Garbert!'","Atrapá a la criatura cuando Adwold dé la señal","Adwold está esperando que coloques el pescado bajo la ventana.\
\
Adwold te mostró el lugar perfecto para dejar el cebo: bajo la ventana grande en el costado de la cabaña de Garbert.","Derrota a Udulug","'Es una lástima que lo perdieras, pero no tienes mi experiencia como rastreador, así que era de esperarse. Hiciste lo mejor que pudiste, ${PLAYER}, y lo aprecio.\
\
'Creo que asustamos lo suficiente a esa criatura como para que no vuelva a molestar a Garbert, a Afanen o a su hijo, ¿y no es eso lo que importa, después de todo?\
\
'¡Buen trabajo con el orco, por cierto! Si no fuera por mi pierna, te habría ayudado sin duda alguna. Me pregunto qué hacía ese tal Udulug aquí y qué relación tendría con la criatura. Muy extraño. Probablemente nada importante.'","Adwold está listo para aguardar escondido a que aparezca la criatura.\
\
Debes prepararte para activar la trampa.","'Vamos a atrapar a esta criatura, ${PLAYER}, ¡lo presiento! Seguro volverá a la cabaña esta noche, ¡y estaremos esperándola!\
\
'Ya hice la mayoría de los preparativos. ¡Solo falta que llegue Adwold!'","Has perdido a la criatura, pero encontraste a un orco que parece haber sido encargado de seguirle el rastro: se trata de Udulug, de quien la criatura habló.\
\
Udulug debe ser derrotado.","'¿Estás listo para ir?'"},
[6771]={"Anborn recalls bringing Gollum forth to be questioned by Faramir shortly after his capture, and his fears for the journey of the Halflings and the gangrel-creature.","Anborn can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
Anborn is telling you what he recalls of the night he brought the gangrel-creature to be questioned.","'At my lord's request, I goaded the gangrel-creature forth to answer for his intrusion...'","'I led the creature away, and he rested, but never did my eyes leave him...'","Listen to Anborn's tale","'That is all I recall of that night, my friend.'","Instancia: Un Camino Problemático"},
[6772]={"'Using the re-animated bodies of fallen dwarves as mere tokens of favour? Despicable... the hobgoblins and Angmarim then left, heading South. I did not come out of hiding for a long while, for fear of the drakes seeing me from above!'","Talk to Molkha","Molkha is ready to describe what she saw earlier.\
\
You should talk to Molkha.","Listen to the conversation","Instancia: Un informe preocupante","Molkha is describing what she saw transpire between the drakes, hobgoblins, and Angmarim.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Molkha has a troubling report to share: the Frost-bound Hobgoblins, the Angmarim, and the Drakes of the Frost-horde are negotiating alliances and using fallen dwarves as bargaining chips.","'Not long ago, I witnessed the hobgoblins and Angmarim passing through. When they reached this frozen lake, they stopped and looked toward the sky....'"},
[6773]={"'We will not need to fight side by side on this day, ${PLAYER}, as we did before. This is a day for celebration!'","Talk to Hrostyr","'I could have told the king you were worthy of praise when you first arrived and saved you some time... but no one asked me, after all! Ha ha ha!\
\
'Well-done, ${PLAYER}! You have done much for my people!'","King Thorin III has called for the folk of the Lonely Mountain to assemble and hear his words.","Hrostyr stands before the throne of King Thorin III.","Instancia: Un verdadero amigo del pueblo de Durin","Listen to the words of Thorin III, King Under the Mountain","Thorin III, King Under the Mountain, addresses the folk of the Lonely Mountain."},
[6774]={"Listen further to the words of King Elessar in the Court of the Fountain","King Elessar is in the Court of the Fountain, atop the city.","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, true friend of Gondor!'","Instancia: Un verdadero amigo de Gondor","'I am glad you have come, ${PLAYER}. You beheld the sapling growing on the side of Mindolluin, and rumour of its discovery has spread throughout Minas Tirith, but it is important for the folk of the city to see it with their own eyes. Elessar believes that one group needs to see it above all others, and I believe he is right.                               \
\
'This ceremony is for them. I hope they hear its message clearly.\
\
'The old tree has been removed with care. It will not be burned. It will instead be laid to rest within Rath Dínen, there to remain in dignity and in peace.'","'There is one more thing, ${PLAYER}. The king requested your presence for more than just that! Attend him now, and hear his words.'","Talk to Malthengil in the Court of the Fountain","King Elessar has invited the folk of the city to a ceremony in the Court of the Fountain.","Listen to the words of King Elessar in the Court of the Fountain","Malthengil, the guard of King Elessar, is in the Court of the Fountain.","Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain, high atop the city.","Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain"},
[6775]={"Ugrukhôr is ready to face you in single combat.","Ugrukhôr does not have the capacity for mercy. He toys with you and with the lives of your friends. He must pay for his cruelty.","Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit, has captured the Ranger Annoth. He comes now to Barad Cúron to challenge Gothmog for supremacy of Imlad Morgul.","The Ranger Culang is in the throne room inside Barad Cúron.","Lûrkh has been swiftly defeated! Now you can descend the tower","Gothmog has been defeated, but he is not the only Master of Mordor who has come to Barad Cúron.","Instancia: Un corazón vengativo","Lûrkh has given all his attention to the Oath-stone in the centre of the chamber. Now is your chance to overpower him!","'Be on your guard, my friend. We have few friends in this dark city, and fewer still who might gain access to this tower!'","Lûrkh is focused on the Oath-stone. Now is your chance to overpower him!","'You are alone, ${PLAYER}. You came to this tower with allies, but they have abandoned you.\
\
'Your Rangers may find success in the woods, but in towers of stone they die the same as any others. They cannot save you.\
\
'The Thandrim crossed me, long ago, and they are all dead. The only man who remembered them will have no vengeance. I gave him death instead, and none now will wield his sad sword or bear his broken shield.\
\
'And Karazgar? Long have I thought to test my might against the Weeping Warrior, but he is a sneaking coward. When I have secured my position here, he will be the next to fall. But of this I am now convinced: he is no friend to you. Perhaps he and I will strike a bargain, for we each may have information of use to the other.\
\
'${CLASS}! Do you dare test your will against Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit? Did I say we were equal? I see now I was wrong! You are no equal of mine, for I am Gúrzyul... and I am your ending!'","The time has come to face Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit, and avenge the lives he has taken.","Defeat Lûrkh, and do it quickly","Talk to Ugrukhôr","Wait for Culang's signal to attack","Permanece alerta","Descend Barad Cúron and return to the throne room without alerting Ugrukhôr to your presence","Talk to Lûrkh","Defeat Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit","Ugrukhôr does not have the capacity for mercy. He toys with you and with the lives of your friends.","'You'd better come with me, slime! You're going to show me where your friend Karazgar is hiding, and if you so much as look at me strangely I'll kill you first!'","With the advantage of surprise on your side, you should descend the tower of Barad Cúron and return to the throne room.","Clear the room atop Barad Cúron of merrevail","Culang has noticed your return, and now you must wait for his signal to attack. Do not let Ugrukhôr see you before that time!","'${PLAYER}... I am all right...\
\
'I will survive... and Ugrukhôr will not!'","Talk to Culang inside the throne room of Barad Cúron","Culang catches your eye. Be ready for his signal!","'Ah, now you speak swiftly. It is a good lesson, ${RACE}.\
\
'But you will still not tell me if Karazgar remains in the tower? This defiance does not suit you, and it will avail you nothing. Indeed, it may cost you your life, or the lives of more friends. Is that what you want?'","Ugrukhôr has asked you a question.","Ugrukhôr has commanded one of his guards, an Orc named Lûrkh, to take you on a search of the tower for Karazgar.","Lûrkh wants you to clear the room of merrevail while he studies the Oath-stone, pondering if some valuable piece of it might be chipped away and kept as treasure."},
[6776]={"Search for Vaskorn","The Ungoledain have begun to retreat, but left behind a vicious spider shade to fight you.","Defeat the spider shade","Threkmóth and his folk have taken the poison-protecting potion in preparation for the assault on the Ungoledain... and possible rescue of Vaskorn.","Instancia: Un Golpe Venenoso","Protect Vaskorn from Ungoledain attackers","Vaskorn appears to be unconscious, but alive.","The Ungoledain appear to be ready for an attack. Fight them off as you continue to search for Vaskorn.","'We have accomplished what we set out to do, now honey cakes await!'"},
[6777]={"Todos los hijos Boffin han vuelto a Nobotella y ahora la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de Angélica puede comenzar sin más retrasos.","Comprueba que los Boffin estén en el almacén","Justo cuando terminas de decirle a Angélica (algo sorprendida) que sus hermanos están todos todavía aquí en vez de a saber dónde, alguien llama a la puerta.\
\
'Creía que me habías dicho que estábamos todos aquí, ¿no?' te pregunta la muchacha hobbit.","Angélica no cabe en sí de gozo.","Comprueba que los Boffin estén en el salón","Angélica está esperando tu informe en su nueva casa.","Comprueba que los Boffin estén en la cocina","'Muchas gracias por venir a la Comarca Allenda para darme la bienvenida a mi nueva casa, ${PLAYER}. Significa mucho para mí que te hayas tomado la molestia, ¡y que ayudaras a reunir a mis hermanos de nuevo después de que se dispersaran a los cuatro vientos!'\
\
Una expresión preocupada de repente invade la cara de Angélica.\
\
'Están todavía todos aquí, ¿no? Será mejor que lo compruebes.'","Angélica está en su nueva casa: el nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel, Nobotella.","'¡Esta debe ser Magetha Cavada!' dice Bingo alegremente.\
\
'Justo después de volver de Campotieso, me topé con la nueva vecina de Angélica. Todo eran buenas palabras de la visita que le hicisteis Camelia y tú, ${PLAYER}, y creí que era un gesto amable invitarla a la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de Angélica, junto con toda su familia.'","Berilac ha encontrado un lugar para su siesta","Sobrevive a la fiesta de inauguración de la casa sin pasar vergüenza","Los co-conspiradores Camelia y Dinodas están aquí, por supuesto","Habla con Prisca","'¡Qué fiesta más agradable! Todo el mundo ha disfrutado, diría yo.\
\
'¿Podría hablar contigo, ${PLAYER}? Fuera mejor, diría yo.'","'¡Debiste haberme dicho qué estabais planeando Bingo y tú, ${PLAYER}! Siento haber sospechado antes... claramente todos mis hijos tenían sus recados que atender para preparar esta sorpresa para Angélica.\
\
'De cualqueir manera, ahora todo está bien. ¡De todos mis hijos, solo Angélica toleraría tantos animales sueltos en su nueva casa! Recuerda eso para cuando el siguiente se mude, ${PLAYER}: Fosco no estaría tan feliz con ese regalo. Quizá algo para la decoración sería más adecuado: un cuadro de un bote, por ejemplo.\
\
'¡Gracias por todo lo que has hecho! ¡Después de todo, ha sido un día encantador!'","Un visitante ha llegado al nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel durante la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de Angélica.","'¿Habéis preparado mis hermanos y tú esto, ${PLAYER}? ¡Seguro que sí! Imagínate: puedo pasar todo el día cuidando de los animales de Magetha... ¡me encanta haberme mudado aquí!\
\
'¡Este es el mejor regalo de inauguración para la casa que podría haber imaginado! ¡Muchas gracias!'","Habla con Angélica","Angélica piensa que deberías comprobar que sus hermanos están todos todavía aquí, y que ninguno ha desaparecido de nuevo.","Caléndula y Griffo están en el salón","Fosco y Esmeralda están en el salón","Instancia: Una inaguración muy Boffin","Habla con Bingo","Prisca está contenta de que todo haya salido bien.","Bingo está en el pasillo de la nueva casa de Angélica, con una sonrisa de felicidad."},
[6778]={"Follow Dolenthol","After the wards surrounding Barad Cúron were destroyed, the fell magic sealing Uialrond, the Dome of Evening has been undone.","Instancia: Una luna creciente","Find a good spot to look down at the council table of Uialrond","This table is covered in a thick layer of dust, but conceals no secrets","You find nothing of note buried within this old dust and debris","Examine the source of the curious glimmer","You should search Uialrond and try to discern why it was sealed.","Search for anything that might explain why Uialrond was sealed","You should witness the vision of Galadriel.","A small lamp-fragment of Lórien glimmers in the darkness and you feel a sudden presence","'I supposed the time had come, ${PLAYER}.'","A curious glimmer catches your eye!","Talk to Faramir","This shelf holds many dusty books of Gondorian make","You should follow Dolenthol into Uialrond, the Dome of Evening.","Bear witness to the echo of Galadriel","You think you spy something in the centre of the council table below","<rgb=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> down at the council table of Uialrond","Only the plated gold on this chair is tarnished","Uialrond appears to be curiously untouched by the evil in Minas Morgul","The echo of Galadriel fades back into the darkness of Uialrond","Dolenthol is standing inside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening.\
\
You should talk to Dolenthol.","You have a clear view from here","'I did not wish for you to come to this place, Éowyn, but here in the darkness, I can think only of how much I have missed you. You are a woman of duty - none may turn you from your charge and indeed, none should dare to!'\
\
Faramir embraces Éowyn.\
\
'These are hopeful tidings from the Lady of Light, though it seems they were spoken long ago.\
\
'Let us hope that they still speak of days to come!'","You should find a good spot to look down at the council table of Uialrond.","'I do not see any sign of evil in this place, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It seems as if it were sealed and forgotten, but why?\
\
'I wonder...'","You should examine the source of the curious glimmer.","You have witnessed the hopeful words of Galadriel, and Dolenthol has revealed himself to be the Lady Éowyn before Prince Faramir in Uialrond.\
\
You should talk to Faramir.","Talk to Dolenthol"},
[6779]={"The time has come for King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel to exchange their vows, in view of the assembled masses.","Mithrandir has called for a moment of silence to remember those who did not live to see this day.","Mithrandir's fireworks are as impressive as ever, and the celebration will continue long into the night.","Some honoured guests have asked to speak some words at the ceremony.","Instancia: Una boda en el Solsticio de Verano","Midsummer's Day has arrived, and with it the Great Wedding of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel.","The procession is underway, and King Aragorn Elessar II is waiting for you to walk down the aisle to him, where he has a few words for you.","Listen to Mithrandir's additional words of remembrance","Your place, from where you will have a fine view of the ceremony, is next to Meriadoc Brandybuck on the southern side of the aisle.","<rgb=#00FF00>Mourn</rgb> to remember those who did not live to see this day","You take your place next to Merry and the procession continues","<rgb=#00FF00>Cheer</rgb> for Sam","Mithrandir's fireworks signal an end to the ceremony, but only the start of the celebration","Listen to the speeches by honoured guests","The speeches concluded, Mithrandir continues the wedding ceremony.","The processional continues while the Elves take their places atop the prow.","Mithrandir wishes to speak some additional words of remembrance.","'Mithrandir never fails to impress, does he not?\
\
'But I understand the ceremony is merely the beginning of the festivities this night? I hope to see you later, my friend.'","Witness the marriage of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel","Wait for the Elves to take their places as the processional continues","Watch as Mithrandir continues the ceremony","Sam has finished reciting his poem, and the assembled crowd cheers for the embarrassed hobbit.","Listen to Mithrandir's words of welcome","Walk down the aisle and speak to Aragorn","Stand next to Merry on the southern side of the aisle","Mithrandir has some words of welcome for the folk assembled atop the pier.","Aragorn smiles at you.\
\
'I am pleased you could be here, ${PLAYER}, on this day of joy. Take your place beside Merry, my friend.'"},
[6780]={"Hear the stranger speak","'The spell has lifted! Perhaps the river will improve as well! Now let us return to Radagast and tell him what we have learned on our journey to Caras Tilion.'","Defend yourself.","Talk to Oroniel","Someone - or something - has come to dwell in Caras Tilion.","Oroniel is able to walk again and calls for a retreat","Defeat Agânuzir.","Defend yourself!","Defeat Agânuzir","Oroniel is able to defend herself, though she cannot move","'Fear not. I have my sword and mastery of my arms. I am ready. Make yourself ready too.'","Talk to Oroniel.","Silence descends upon the hilltop as a figure steps out from behind the ruins","Hear what the stranger has to say.","Instance: Acolyte of the Necromancer"},
[6782]={"'I think that we have discussed this quite enough for one night, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Arcil","Arcil, Éothain, and others have gathered to discuss the next course of action for Aldburg.\
\
You should speak with Arcil.","'I am afraid that nothing was settled. We each presented our cases, but both of these groups pose a potentially great threat. We need to see that they are both dealt with swiftly.'","Instancia: Aldburg se reúne","A small assembly from Aldburg have gathered to discuss how to handle the Orc problems that have plagued the Eastfold of late.","Both Arcil and Éothain stated their case about which Orc-tribe poses the greatest threat.\
\
You speak with Arcil once again.","The people of Aldburg have come together to decide how best to deal with the two Orc-tribes that have been causing trouble of late.\
\
You should observe the discussion.","'I am pleased  that you could join us, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We are about to decide how we should proceed with our new-found Orc problem. Since you have encountered both of these Orc-tribes, I wanted you present for this conversation.'","Observa la discusión"},
[6783]={"The sons of Isildur weigh what should be done with Urudanî Stonemaiden. She has been defeated, but while she lives she remains a threat to the Great Alliance.","Vëamacil and Ornaher are outside the walls of Amon Fuin.","Vëamacil and Ornaher, two of the sons of Isildur, are eager to conduct a dangerous rescue mission into the enemy-held fortress of Amon Fuin.","Defeat the guards that defend Urudanî Stonemaiden","'I saw you from afar, my friend, and came to lend you any assistance you might require. And this too: a warning 'gainst this course! Was this excursion to Amon Fuin your idea, or that of these sons of Isildur?\
\
'It is true that there is less activity here than there was of late, but Amon Fuin is still a place of evil and will not be undefended. This seems to me an unwise course, and I beg you convince these two to turn back, for the Great Alliance will be the worse for it should something befall them.'","Magoldir wants you to advise Vëamacil and Ornaher to abandon their mission to Amon Fuin.","You and the sons of Isildur have encountered Magoldir the Elf outside Amon Fuin.","'A pox on them!\
\
'I did not need those cowards before, and I do not need them now! I will slay you myself, and exult in your demise!'","Instancia: Todo está en calma","Urudanî's cultists have been defeated, and her contingent of Orcs has abandoned her, but she still intends to stand and fight.","Talk to Vëamacil","Talk to Vëamacil and Ornaher and convince them not to proceed into Amon Fuin","The sons of Isildur have charged forward into Amon Fuin, dismissing the warnings of Magoldir.","Talk to Urudanî Stonemaiden in Amon Fuin","'Magoldir's warning is well-intentioned, but you must understand that we cannot allow good soldiers of the Alliance to remain in torment within Amon Fuin. We have no choice! It is up to Isildur's sons to save them, and we will not shrink from that purpose!'","Urudanî Stonemaiden commands the Mordorrim cultists within Amon Fuin.","'That was... unexpected.'\
\
Magoldir hefts his sword.\
\
'I suppose we need to follow them. Their father will not look kindly upon us were we to abandon them now, although it seems to this observer that they were the ones who abandoned us. Even so, this is our duty.'","'I hate to leave without the success for which we hoped, but I see no other choice. There is no sign of our missing soldiers, and from the words of Urudanî Stonemaiden I fear we are not likely to see them again.\
\
'Magoldir should not have had us spare her. If she works some mischief upon the works of the Great Alliance it will be upon his head, and no other.\
\
'Bah! Let us leave this place, friend. It is not safe to remain here, no matter its unusual quiet.'","'All is quiet, but do not trust the stillness! There will be look-outs up ahead, and we should dispatch them quickly before they can raise the alarm. Are you ready?'","Stand alongside Magoldir and the sons of Isildur in Amon Fuin","You failed to protect your allies!","<rgb=#FF0000>All of your allies must survive</rgb>","Talk to Magoldir outside Amon Fuin","'Yes, I hear Magoldir's warning, but the evil of the Mordorrim must be opposed, and who better to do so than the sons of Isildur? Good soldiers have been spirited away by some evil ruse, and we must find them if we can!'"},
[6784]={"Talk to Randgar","Inhild has travelled to Randgar's farm, in order to say a final farewell to the man she loved so dearly.","'Thank you for bringing me here, ${PLAYER}. I hope that I have not been overly troublesome to you. You have been a greater friend to Randgar and myself than you know.\
\
'Please excuse me for a moment.'","Inhild begins to call out for Randgar","'My father cares for me, but he shares not my views of love. He would never allow for me to spend my life with a farmer, no matter how good that man might be. \
\
'Randgar and I must depart together for safer lands. You have been so helpful, but I must ask of you one final request. Please, tell my father that I have gone off with a rich and handsome Rider from Edoras, whom we encountered on our return. In this way, he will miss me, but be all together happy for my good fortune.'","Randgar has returned and is awaiting outside his farm.\
\
Randgar has appeared, alive and well, and would like to explain things to you.","'Greetings again, ${PLAYER}. I understand your surprise. Please, allow me to explain.'","Talk to Inhild","Inhild can be found along the road to Randgar's farm.\
\
Inhild wishes to speak with you about Randgar.","Inhild can be found near Randgar's farm.\
\
Inhild wishes to discuss one final matter with you.","Instancia: Todo lo que queda","'Good fortune to you, ${PLAYER}. We owe you our happiness together.'"},
[6785]={"Aragorn has slowed beyond the Fords. He wishes to speak with you.","Éomer has heard a horseman approaching, and wants to speak with you.","'We are well-met once again, ${PLAYER}, but in hardship. I sought the treacherous leader of the Falcon Clan, but he gave me the slip and escaped into the mountains. He lives still the life of a coward.'\
\
You tell Golodir that Lheu Brenin's flight brought him into your path, and he has been slain.\
\
'You tell me true? Then he has paid for his crimes. He abandoned some of his own people when he fled, and we left them in a place of peace, where they should be safe. I worried that their former chieftain might seek them out and visit upon them further harm, but even Saruman's magic cannot help Lheu Brenin now. I am satisfied, ${PLAYER}. Thank you, on behalf of my fallen kinsmen and also for those of his own people he betrayed.'","Habla con Calenglad","'I never believed I would see such things, ${PLAYER}. Ents! I am filled with wonder at the sight, wonder of a kind I thought was the sole reserve of children. I am an old man, a white-beard of many winters, and still I have seen things this day I would not have believed yesterday.\
\
'They tower above mortal men, and cover such a span with each stride! What damage they could do to the homes of my people, if that was their thought! But I do not believe that is their desire.'","Habla con Aragorn","Habla con Halbarad","'It seems you found Aragorn before we did, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps we should have gone with you.'","Talk to Théoden on the road through the mysterious wood","Talk to Legolas on the road through the mysterious wood","Habla con Golodir","Halbarad and the Grey Company have accomplished their mission, and Halbarad wants to speak with you.","'I hope you found rest before we set out, ${PLAYER}. I tried to do so, but I could not quiet my roving mind, and I am still greatly fatigued. What will we find in Isengard?'\
\
Aragorn looks from side to side at the towering trunks of the forest.\
\
'These trees were not here when we arrived at Helm's Deep yesterday. I think we both know what brought them here, to the foot of the Dike, but that makes it no less frightening a sight, does it?'","'This is truly an unexpected encounter, ${PLAYER}! I am glad to see you are well, and in the company of Aragorn, no less! Our errand has not ended, though its first goal be now accomplished. Now we must lend what aid we can to Aragorn.\
\
'Is it true you take the road to Isengard? Whatever other objective Aragorn has with Saruman, we must add this one as well: the rescue of Lothrandir my kinsman, if he yet lives!'","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I knew in my heart we would see you once more, but I did not think to find you in the company of my chieftain Aragorn! Much has happened since we parted, and little of it good, but we will need to speak of our respective deeds when there is time to breathe.\
\
'We have found Aragorn between perils, it seems. He had your help for the first, and he has all of us for the second. May it be enough!'","Instancia: Aliados Inesperados","'${PLAYER}, wait! Do you hear that? I hear a great sound of creaking timbers and rustling branches. It comes this way!'","Aragorn is speaking with Halbarad past the Fords of Isen.","The Fords of Isen are a sad reminder of the good folk who fell in defence of Rohan","Journey with the company beyond the Fords of Isen","'These Ents are herdsmen, not warriors. The people of Rohan need not fear them, as long as they cause no harm to their flock. There is one in this land that would have done well to heed the Ents before now; if he had heeded them the battle that is lately ended might have come to a different conclusion.\
\
'It is good for Rohan, and for all free folk, that he did not take them into account. Let us proceed, ${PLAYER}. There are still many miles to go before we reach Isengard.'","Talk to Éomer on the road","Many of your friends among the Grey Company wish to speak with you before continuing on.","Gandalf is on the road, waiting to proceed.","Talk to Aragorn beyond the Fords of Isen","The company continues toward Isengard.","'I feel confident that we can accomplish anything, ${PLAYER}, now that my kinsmen are here. Can it be that the tides turn in our favour this day?'","'I hear the sound of swift hoof-beats approaching from behind us. Let us confront this rider before he overtakes us and offers some harm to the King!'","'Many good men fell at the Fords, but their kingdom still stands. We are almost to Isengard, and will bring report of their valiant sacrifice to the Wizard who forced its need.\
\
'Let us rejoin our companions, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Radanir","'It was not a long good-bye after all, ${PLAYER}, though the intervening days have been eventful. I think Halbarad keenly felt the burden of his duty after you left us, for he was not sure how best to proceed. But it seems he chose a-right, for we have found Aragorn as the words of Galadriel bade us.\
\
'The sons of Elrond bear messages for him from their father, and Halbarad carries the gift of Arwen. I trust that Aragorn will know what to do with each of these gifts.'","Habla con Corunir","Théoden is on the road through the mysterious wood. He has never seen Ents before, and the sight has filled him with wonder.","Talk to Gandalf on the road through the mysterious wood","Legolas has dismounted and is staring into the trees.","Talk to Aragorn on the road through the mysterious wood","'Halbarad has given me much to think about, ${PLAYER}. We have more reasons to converse with Saruman than I believed.'","Aragorn has turned back to hear your opinion of the mysterious wood through which the company now travels.","Gandalf has unsettled business with Saruman, and the company rides with him to Isengard."},
[6786]={"'Debemos regresar a Tinnudir, ${PLAYER}. Temo que Amarthiel haya vencido en esta hora. Debemos planear nuestro próximo movimiento, y con rapidez, ¡para que su victoria sea breve!'","Encuentra a Amarthiel y descubre sus planes.","Debes derrotar al Númenóreano Negro.","Instancia: La esperanza de Amarthiel","Calenglad te ha pedido que encuentres a Amarthiel y descubras sus planes. Te ha enviado a Annúminas con cinco Montaraces para ayudar a rechazar a los angmarim.","Encuentra y detén a Amarthiel.","Habla con el montaraz protector que está frente a ti.","Habla con el montaraz protector antes de buscar a Amarthiel.","'¡Deprisa, estaban preparados para nosotros! ¡Debemos abrirnos paso si queremos encontrar a Amarthiel antes de que sea demasiado tarde! ¡Seguidnos!'"},
[6787]={"Rûkhor and his forces depart","The uruks have fallen back, but a strange man has appeared above the camp.\
\
You should listen to Rûkhor.","The camp is under attack!","Travel to Echad Taerdim with Legolas and Atli","Talk to Mablung","'Come, ${PLAYER}, let us deliver Atli to the care of the Rangers.'","The attack has been repelled.\
\
You should talk to Mablung.","Listen to Rûkhor","The uruks fall back!","Strange uruks are attacking the Ranger camp.\
\
Defend the camp!","Habla con Legolas.","'Come, we must tend to the wounded and assess the damage to the camp.'","Legolas would like to return to Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should travel with Legolas and Atli to the Ranger camp.","Defend the camp","Instancia: Emboscada en Echad Taerdim","Legolas would like to return to Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","You return to Mablung's camp with Legolas and Atli, but something is wrong.","'A few of my Rangers are wounded, but no deaths. Rûkhor surely could have taken us all out if he wished. Is he toying with us?'"},
[6788]={"Instancia: Emboscada en las alturas","'Here they are now, just over the hill behind us. We will split and engage the caravan from both sides. Faeron and Mêshaget, you charge the front. Rhadrog and I will strike from the rear. ${PLAYER}, choose your direction of attack, but remain alert and assist whoever is most in need.\
\
'Are we prepared?'\
\
The others nod.\
\
'Then we begin!'","'Good work, everyone. Hopefully, that is all of them. My sword arm tires! I no longer have the endurance I had in my youth, when I was a soldier.\
\
'Faeron and Rhadrog, keep watch for more reinforcements. Mêshaget, will you join me in searching for anything of use? Missives, orders, keys, anything of that sort. ${PLAYER}, collect what crates of supplies you are able. Swiftly, now. The longer we tarry, the more likely it is that the entire army will descend upon us.'","You should talk to Nabatínu when you are ready to begin the assault.","Talk to Nabatínu","Talk to Rhadrog","Supply crates collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge las cajas de suministros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have collected the supply crates. You should talk to Rhadrog about what to do next.","'Yes, it looks like we have everything we will get from this adventure. Let us return to Gadim-ûn.'","'You have the supplies? Excellent, we should be on our way, then. Ask Mêshaget if he and Nabatínu are satisfied with their search.'","Nabatínu has given orders to everyone in your company. You should collect the supply crates.","Rhadrog, Faeron, and Nabatínu have devised a plan to acquire supplies needed by the Jatsakóri by attacking an Ordâkhai supply caravan.","<rgb=#FF0000>Nabatínu must survive</rgb>","Your company has defeated the Ordâkhai defending the supply caravan. You should talk to Nabatínu about what to do next."},
[6789]={"Listen to Balakhâd's account","'Nakási removed from her garment a small glass phial containing an oily substance that glittered even in the dim light of the chamber. I knew it for its terrible reputation: Narghâk, the Hungry Fire, longest-burning and deadliest of the alchemic weapons ever used in war throughout Shagâna and in Umbar.\
\
'My father searched for stores of Narghâk that might have evaded destruction over the centuries, but he never found any. The last sages who knew the secret of its making were put to the sword a hundred years ago.\
\
'Even so small a quantity of Narghâk as Nakási possessed has not been seen in Umbar for many years. I believed the Hungry Fire had left the world.'","'Even through the haze of my fear, one thing was clear to me: Azagath and Nakási might have possessed a shared purpose, but their tolerance for each other began already to wear thin. Whatever they hoped to accomplish, every day that passed wore upon their alliance.\
\
'In my desperation I hoped to take advantage of their eroding trust for each other, but I could think of no effective means of accomplishing it.'","Listen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.","Talk to Balakhâd","Instancia: Entre enemigos","Balakhâd has agreed to tell you what befell him after he fled from Jirush and hid within the tombs of Nirgambâr.","Balakhâd has more to tell you.","'Even through the haze of my fear, the realization dawned upon me: not only do Azagath and Nakási not trust each other, every member of their ruling Kindred fears and distrusts the others.\
\
'I did not believe I would live long enough to take advantage of this knowledge, but it brought to me a calm I never thought to feel again. The Kindred of the Coins that displaced the Heirs of Castamir will not much longer survive to rule Umbar. The seeds of their undoing are already planted, and they have done it themselves.\
\
'The knowledge brought me peace, even as my new captors discussed the manner of my death.'","'Memories of my frightening escape from Jirush flashed before my eyes: the Ordâkhai barring Azagath's approach to my cell, the intruder raising his arms, the soldiers falling to the floor as his dark sorcery stole the very life from their bodies.\
\
'I knew he would follow me, but I sought to get as far from his dreadful presence as I could.'"},
[6790]={"Enfréntate a la espía en el exterior","Habla con Cariad","Observa el interrogatorio de Igrain","Igrain ha ofrecido dejarte marchar para poder espiar libremente a los refugiados Cuan-lûth.\
\
Deberías esperar y no ceder.","Igrain se ha rendido.\
\
Deberías observar su interrogatorio.","Deberías hablar con Cariad sobre la opinión que tiene Erlys de los montaraces.","Derrota a Igrain","Han visto a una espía de Saruman fuera de la cueva.\
\
Erlys te ha ordenado que te enfrentes a la espía y la derrotes.","Cariad desea hablar de unos asuntos con Erlys.","Cariad te ha llevado a conocer al resto de su pueblo, los Cuan-lûth de las Tierras Brunas.","Instancia: Una audiencia con los Cuan-lûth","'Siento que hayas tenido que desarmarte antes de entrar. Mi pueblo no confía en ti y, si te soy sincero, tendrás que demostrarme un poco más tu valía antes de que pueda confiar plenamente en ti. Espero que lo entiendas.\
\
'No te preocupes. No te pasará nada malo mientras no hagas ninguna imprudencia. Tienes mi palabra.'","Deberías hablar con Cariad antes de acercarte a Erlys.","'No importa. Por ahora hay cosas más importantes que atender.'","Derrotar a Igrain puede ayudar a que los Cuan-lûth confíen más en ti.","'¿Por qué Erlys no se da cuenta de que tenemos todo en contra? Su terquedad acabará matándola algún día.\
\
'Perdóname; ha sido un comentario muy feo. Quiere lo mejor para nosotros, pero a veces no ve con claridad en los peores momentos.'","Espera y mantén tu posición","Observa la discusión"},
[6791]={"Speak with Mizâdi inside the Shorakhúna.","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards.","The Doorwards have requested Mizâdi's presence in Zajâna. Go with Shâra Mizâdi to show the Doorwards she mean them no harm, and rally their support in her hunt for Bârshud.","Instancia: Una audiencia con los porteros","Listen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi.","Join Mizâdi and Numûru outside the council chambers","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the Doorwards","'I believe we should accept these terms. They are the best for which we could hope.'","Place the sword on the table in front of Sarâgh, Master of Spears","Speak with Numûru inside the Shorakhúna.","Speak with Mizâdi inside the Shorakhúna","Enter the council chamber with Mizâdi within the Shorakhúna.","Speak with Numûru inside the Shorakhúna","Listen to the conversation between the Doorwards and Mizâdi","Join Mizâdi and Numûru outside the council chambers.","Place the sword on the table in front of Sarâgh, Master of Spears.","'I agree with Numûru. We will show them via our actions that we mean them no ill will.'","Pick up the sword from the table in the Shorakhúna","Enter the council chamber with Mizâdi within the Shorakhúna","Pick up the sword from the table in the Shorakhúna."},
[6792]={"'I am not sure why I must address this petition with the likes of you, but if I must, I will begin.'","Speak to Rothog regarding Zarzíra Dawn-star's petition","Members of the Kindred of the Coins take petitions from nobles throughout Umbar. Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear one specific complaint.","Speak to Zarzíra and witness the proceedings","Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear a specific complaint from one of his nobles regarding one of the gladiators.","Instancia: Una audiencia con la tormenta","Speak to Rothog the Storm","Talk to Rothog","'Let us see what she is to say regarding this situation. It should be most interesting.\
\
'Tell her she may begin.'","'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER} for witnessing the petition. Let us leave these chambers and return to Dâr Laja.'","Approach Zarzíra Dawn-star to begin her petition.","'These accusations are most troubling. While I do not doubt that these incidents have transpired, I do feel that she may not be telling us everything. It would be good to investigate this further.\
\
'Would you be willing to do so?'","Rothog requests that you call forth the petitioner"},
[6793]={"Durin stares into the sheet of ice at Winterstith, muttering quietly.","'Can you not feel the power in the air, ${PLAYER}? My warriors will not know defeat, and soon, yes... soon we will walk in Gundabad once more, and cast out the Orcs that fill it!'","You have managed to break Durin's reverie at the Anvil of Winterstith, but he still speaks slowly, as if waking from a deep sleep.","Durin stares deeply into the ice, muttering quietly","Mírkuz has listened to the words of Durin with growing displeasure and worry, and now he wishes to voice his concerns to you.","Carefully approach Durin","Listen to Heilar's account","'I followed this great array of Longbeards here from Skarháld, for I do not like it and did not trust it. I like what I am hearing from their prince even less!\
\
'You need use no force, ${PLAYER}. I am of the Zhélruka and fear nothing, neither ${RACE} or dwarf. Nor do I fear kings or princes such as he.'","Listen to the questions of the Longbeards","Talk to Mírkuz","'I do not like it, ${PLAYER}. I fear the prince's words on this day will echo throughout the mountains until they reach unfriendly ears.\
\
'Who can say what evil might be done as a result of this Longbeard's newfound course?'","Listen to Durin as he addresses the great force of Longbeards","Gently break Durin's reverie, if you can","Glóin stands among the warriors of the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.","Habla con Glóin","Instancia: Un eco en las montañas","'This is... Winterstith? What am I doing here?'\
\
Durin shakes his head to clear it. His eyes refocus upon you, and he no longer speaks as if he were submerged in the deep water of sleep.\
\
'I remember leaving Skarháld, and calling for Heilar to accompany me, but my purpose for doing so has fled. It seemed so clear to me, like the great sheet of ice before us, but now it is clouded over and hazy. It is lost to me. There was a voice; that much I do remember. It drew me here. If you had not disturbed me I might have learned what it wanted!'\
\
You remind Durin of the need for caution: Hrímil Frost-heart dwells somewhere behind the ice, sealed within the Anvil of Winterstith, and the speech of dragons is known to have a strange power.\
\
'Do you take me for a fool? I would have known if this was dragon-speech. It cannot have been the voice of Hrímil, ${PLAYER}. No, I think this was something else. Many are the dwarves, Longbeard and Zhélruka alike, who have reported a fascination with the Anvil throughout the years. Many of them were kings. Can it be that it is now my turn to accept this kingly aspect?'\
\
Durin nods to himself, and his face shines as he sees the Longbeard army behind you.","Glóin is worried for the prince of the Longbeards, and has asked you to slowly approach Durin and learn why he came to Winterstith.","The Zhélruka Mírkuz followed on the heels of the Longbeard army during its march from Skarháld, and now he has interrupted Durin's speech.","Habla con Durin","Durin was last seen travelling north-east with a single companion. Do they journey to the Anvil of Winterstith? And for what purpose?","Glóin and the warriors of the Longbeard army marvel at Durin's secret departure from Skarháld.","'Do you see him down the hill there? At least he is not unguarded, for Heilar stands with him. But what purpose brought them hither with no word to anyone?'","Newly-resolved, Durin addresses the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.","Durin has managed to shake free of his reverie, seeing for the first time the Longbeard army from the Lonely Mountain."},
[6794]={"'Are you ready to go to the mines below this hall? Very good. I am ready to show you the way.'","'How can Nár know of the errand of the Grey Company, ${PLAYER}? And more than that: how can he know of my father's words to my brother and me? How can he know we were considering taking the Paths of the Dead once we meet with Aragorn?\
\
'I must tell Halbarad and the other Rangers of this. I think things may have just become more complicated.'","'We are far beneath the earth now, ${PLAYER}, and a feeling has been growing on my mind for some time now. I think someone, or something, has watched as we descended. I cannot pinpoint it, but I believe some intelligence has observed our passage from Zudrugund.\
\
'Something else has made me uneasy. How much of Frithgeir's brew has Nár already consumed? And how much remains? The dwarf has been alert for our descent, but what happens when the steaming brew has been exhausted?'","The lever squeals with disuse, then slides into place","You have travelled deep into the mine beneath Zudrugund with Nár, Elladan, and Nona. Elladan has had a curious feeling that you have been watched for some time now.","Nár seems to be more aware of his surroundings, thanks to the brew supplied by Frithgeir, and may now tell you what he said to Wadu.","'We are a long way from Evendim, ${PLAYER}. I wonder how our friends are managing in our absence?'\
\
Calenglad sighs and looks suspiciously at Nár.\
\
'I understand why we have taken this brief excursion into the hills, for if Nona is satisfied by what we learn here, our dealings with the Uch-lûth should be made easier. But what can we really learn from this dwarf? He does not seem even to notice us!'","Frithgeir has prepared the brew for Nár, and you should now see if it has the promised effect.","'Is it the smell of the brew that has kept the bats from attacking Nár? We should hope that it was not, for he seems to have exhausted it. A few drops may remain, but the odour is much less than it was, and he seems to be falling once more out of awareness.'\
\
Elladan shakes his head.\
\
'There is a gate ahead, and if I have learned anything of dwarves, it is that such a gate certainly has a lever somewhere to open it. Find the lever and return to us, ${PLAYER}, and we will proceed. I fear that this journey will soon end in failure, for without a guide that can speak to us in ways we understand, what can we hope to learn here?'","Nona has asked you to get to the bottom of the mystery concerning her brother Wadu and the dwarves of Zudrugund.","Nár looks around in an interested fashion, but you cannot tell if he even sees you at the moment.","Nona listens impatiently as you explain what the situation in Zudrugund seems to be.\
\
'I want answers for myself. My brother was changed after he came here, and this Nár knows why. He will tell me why, or it will go badly for him!'","You have pulled the lever to open the gate and should now rejoin your friends below.","'There must be a lever somewhere around here that will open the locked gate. You must find it, ${PLAYER}.'","'My brother...even after the terrible things my father said to him, and even after what I said to him, in my frustration....'\
\
Nona trails off, staring at the body of the enormous gwiber.\
\
'He mastered his fear, ${PLAYER}, and achieved a victory that even the bravest and strongest warriors of the Uch-lûth could not hope to match.\
\
'And now he is gone, slain by enemies who waited in hiding for him to pass. The cowards! They were nothing compared to this great beast, but they laid him low where even it could not! My Wadu....'","Nár has offered to take you to the mines below Zudrugund, where he last remembers seeing Wadu. Perhaps the mystery of what happened to Nona's brother here remains below.","'I have been listening to Nár's ramblings, ${PLAYER}, and I have managed to piece together some of his history. I believe he was once the servant or friend of Thrór, grandfather of Thorin Oakenshield, and that this was one of their homes in exile.\
\
'Thrór did not return to Erebor, but it seems to me he made another journey, and Nár accompanied him. From his words, I believe they came into danger, and....'","Find and use the lever that unlocks the gate","Nona has learned the truth: that her brother Wadu found his courage far below Zudrugund and defeated a mighty gwiber in the depths.","Talk to Frithgeir","Habla con Elladan.","'There must be a lever somewhere that opens the gate. Perhaps high above us? Are not the ways of dwarves strange?'","'Please, I need to concentrate. Speak with your friends here while I prepare the brew.'","Frithgeir is working to prepare the brew for Nár so you may speak to him without difficulty.","Nona has demanded an explanation from you.","Elladan is thinking, pondering what to do next, now that you are deep beneath Zudrugund and Nár is passing out of awareness again.","Your friends are missing. Have they already gone on past the gate that blocked passage deeper into the mine?","Your friends are deep within the mine, seeking the truth of what befell Wadu in the depths when he came here with Nár.","Learn what Nona wants from the dwarves","Nona has burst into the dwarf-hall, intending to confront the dwarves about the fate of her brother Wadu.","'I do not like this. Why do the bats of this cavern not attack the dwarf? Why does he walk among them without danger?\
\
'Wadu came into this mine full of fear and uncertainty. What happened here that he emerged from it with courage, courage that would lead him to his death?\
\
'The longer this journey takes, the more questions it poses, ${PLAYER}! I want to be above-ground again, in the sunlight!'","A locked gate blocks further progress into the mine, and Elladan has asked you to find the lever that should open it.","'So many books, ${PLAYER}, and none of them taken when Nár's people left him. It puzzles me. It is clear that many dwarves once lived here, but where they have gone and why is a mystery. I suspect that even Frithgeir's brew will not clear Nár's mind sufficiently for him to provide us the answers we seek.'","'I do not know what to make of this dwarf, ${PLAYER}. Where did all of his people go? Why would they leave him behind? And what could he have seen that might leave him so...addled?\
\
'Frithgeir seems to be kind-hearted, and it seems to me that Nár would be hard-pressed to survive here for any period of time without him, but there is something not quite right about these two.'","Halbarad wishes to speak with you while Frithgeir prepares the brew for Nár.","'The water is boiling already, and now I will add the ingredients you collected. The odour will be quite pungent, so perhaps you should speak with the rest of your friends that have come to Zudrugund while it steeps.\
\
'The odour is rather unpleasant, though I find that it does clear the cobwebs away when I am feeling under the weather.'","Nona wears a puzzled expression. She seems dissatisfied with the journey and wishes to speak with you.","Follow Elladan to Nár and listen to the dwarf's tale","Frithgeir is preparing the brew for Nár and has recommended that while you wait you speak with the members of the Grey Company who have come to Zudrugund.","Elladan is waiting to speak with you about Nár's mysterious and sudden change.","'We must all return to Zudrugund. I do not know what this means, but I fear for every answer we obtained in this place we have received twice as many questions.'","Listen to the exchange between Nona and Nár","Nár shakes his head, breathing deeply of the steam billowing out of the mug.\
\
'Wadu...I know that name. We went to the father-lode, where rang the sound of hundreds of dwarf-hammers, far below Zudrugund.\
\
'It is curious. I remember walking with Wadu among the great turning water-wheels of the Old Father, but I have not seen him since. He is not still down there, is he?'\
\
You tell Nár that Wadu has been slain, and his beard creases into a frown.\
\
'Ah, that is a shame. He was most brave. Wasn't he? I can take you to the mine, if you'd like.'","Instancia: Un eco de días pasados","'I am sorry we did not wait, ${PLAYER}, but Nár gave a shout and ran forward when the gate opened, and we did not want to lose him.\
\
'He is just ahead, with Nona.'","The gate stands open, but your friends are gone. Are they below?","Rejoin Elladan, Nona, and Nár below"},
[6795]={"Deberías recoger las piedras rúnicas ahora que han sido alcanzadas por los rayos","Instancia: Un Ojo en la Tormenta","Habla con Techeryn","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para irte, ${PLAYER}? Alejémonos de la tormenta.'","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}: no solo al cumplir mis instrucciones, ¡sino también al encargarte de los orcos!\
\
'¡Mira esto! Aunque cada una de estas runas fue alcanzada directamente por un rayo del cielo, la única marca visible en las piedras sigue siendo la runa que grabé en cada una antes de dártelas: la runa de \\qrelámpago\\q.\
\
'¿Necesitas más pruebas de que hay poder en la forma en que describimos el mundo natural? Regresemos a la posada, ${PLAYER}, y podremos seguir hablando de lo que esto significa mientras descendemos.'","En la cima de Amon Sûl pueden encontrarse tres piedras planas.\
\
Techeryn te ha pedido colocar tres piedras rúnicas sobre las piedras planas de la cima y esperar a que cada una sea alcanzada por un rayo.","Has venido con Techeryn a Amon Sûl, donde una tremenda tormenta envuelve la cima, para desentrañar parte del misterio que rodea a las runas y su conexión con el mundo natural.","'Te he dado tres piedras, , en las que he inscrito una runa. Quiero que asciendas hasta la cima de la colina y las coloques sobre las tres piedras planas que encontrarás allí. Luego debes esperar, ${PLAYERNAME:Maestro Rúnico[m]|Maestra Rúnica[f]}, a que un rayo alcance cada una de las piedras rúnicas.\
\
'¿A qué se debe esa expresión de sorpresa, ? ¿Dudas que esto pueda ocurrir? Yo estoy seguro de que sucederá.\
\
'Pero ten cuidado, pues he visto indicios de orcos merodeando por esta zona últimamente.'","Techeryn está en el sendero que asciende hacia la cima de Amon Sûl.\
\
Techeryn está esperando para hablar contigo.","La piedra aún humea tras el impacto del rayo, pero la runa permanece como la única marca","Piedras rúnicas colocadas sobre las piedras planas en la cima de Amon Sûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge las piedras rúnicas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Coloca las piedras rúnicas sobre las piedras planas de la cima de Amon Sûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Techeryn ha llegado a la cima de Amon Sûl y está esperando para hablar contigo.","Lleva las piedras rúnicas a Techeryn","Techeryn te ha asegurado que la foudre golpeará las tres piedras rúnicas que colocaste en la cima de Amon Sûl, y no debes regresar con ella hasta que eso ocurra.","Espera a que los rayos golpeen las tres piedras rúnicas","'Coloca las tres piedras rúnicas que te he dado sobre las piedras planas en la cima de Amon Sûl. Una vez colocadas las tres, debes esperar a que cada una sea alcanzada por un rayo.\
\
'¿Por qué dudas de que esto sea posible, ${PLAYER}? ¿Niega tu corazón que las runas tienen alguna conexión con el mundo natural?'","'¿No me has traído las piedras rúnicas?'","Los rayos han alcanzado cada una de las tres piedras rúnicas que colocaste en la cima; ahora deberías recogerlas todas de nuevo."},
[6797]={"Talk to Doron","Defeat Maraz","You have uncovered a room decorated with strange banners and trinkets that fill you with dread. While you do not see the Easterling, you believe him to be nearby.","The Easterling, Maraz, has revealed that he drove the brigands into serving his brotherhood, and that he and his people seek to crush Rohan beginning with Parth Celebrant. He must be defeated before his plans can come to fruition.","'The day is ours. Let us leave this foul place.'","Suddenly, a voice rises through the air behind you","Doron hopes to find the Easterling invader among the crumbling tunnels of Ost Celebrant. Explore the ruins and try to uncover his whereabouts.","Search the ruins for the Easterling","Instancia: Un presagio del este","Doron can be called to your side with the horn you carry.","Explore the ruins under Ost Celebrant","You notice strange banners adorning this hall, but there is no sign of the Easterling","'The Easterling is vanquished and our search is at an end, but this man brings grim tidings for the days to come. If his people are truly as strong as he claims, the Horse-lords have much to fear. \
\
'Come, let us depart. You must bring word to your allies immediately.'","With Doron's guidance, you have discovered a passageway under Ost Celebrant. Doron bids you to enter and confront the Easterling invader."},
[6798]={"Dís seems unusually wary of speaking in your presence, but gestures for you to approach...","King Thorin III is speaking with Arcah, Daughter of Croär, chief of the ravens of Ravenhill.","Talk to King Thorin III","King Thorin III is at Ravenhill.\
\
You have spoken to Arcah and told her much of your adventures, and you should now speak to King Thorin III.","As the North awaits the coming of Vethúg Wintermind, King Thorin III has received an urgent and unexpected summons from Ravenhill.","Talk to Dís at Ravenhill","Dís can be found in the chambers of Ravenhill.\
\
You have come to Ravenhill seeking to answer an urgent summons. You should talk to Dís.","'It is time we returned to Erebor, ${PLAYER}.'","King Thorin III is at Ravenhill.\
\
Hoping to answer an urgent summons, King Thorin III has travelled to Ravenhill. You should follow him.","'Now... who are you, ${RACE}?'\
\
You introduce yourself and tell Arcah of the many adventures that led you to the North.\
\
'An interesting tale. It seems you have been an ally to many others before you came to serve the King under the Mountain. Curious....\
\
'If next I summon you, you would be wise to answer my call.'","'I did not expect to see you, ${PLAYER}. Am I to understand you have some business with the King under the Mountain this day?'\
\
You explain to Dís that Erebor will soon be under siege by the great cold-drake, Vethúg Wintermind, and that you have served as something of an ambassador to King Thorin III.\
\
'These tidings are known to me. You may remain, but do not interrupt. This is a matter between the King under the Mountain and the ravens of the North.'","Arcah, Daughter of Croär, is at Ravenhill.\
\
After speaking with the King under the Mountain, Arcah desires to learn more of you.","Talk to Arcah, Daughter of Croär","Instancia: Una convocatoria inesperada","Listen to King Thorin III and Arcah","Follow King Thorin III into Ravenhill","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'For many long years, even by the reckoning of Durin's Folk, Dís has been the Keeper of Ravenhill. Had Fíli and Kíli not met with their tragic fates, I do not know if she would have come to tend the peoples of Roäc. Such questions are best left unanswered, I think. Dís would not summon me without cause, and so I am curious to learn what matter could be so pressing. And perhaps of use to my kinsfolk upon the eve of battle!\
\
'Shall we enter Ravenhill, friend?'","Arcah hops in your direction and looks at you curiously...","'These are good tidings, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The ravens of the line of Roäc, son of Carc, were of great wisdom, and I believe that Arcah shall prove no different. Her ravens shall spy the hidden foes and dangers of the North, and if all goes as I hope, we will learn precisely when Vethúg intends to come to Erebor. We shall know the truths beyond our sight, and be the better prepared for it!\
\
'I must honour the promise I have made to Arcah, and so, I wish to return to Erebor. Let us go!'","King Thorin III is at Ravenhill.\
\
You have come to Ravenhill with King Thorin III and should now seek an audience with Dís."},
[6799]={"Fonn ha aprendido que se han visto gorthorogs viajando hacia Ologfil en Malenhad. Ha enviado a un explorador para investigar, pero el explorador no ha regresado.","Con la muerte de Ulkrank, deberías poder liberar a Bethad de su prisión y escapar de la oscura guarida de Ologfil.","Bethad ha sido encarcelado por el líder de guerra gorthorog, Ulkrank, quien debe ser asesinado para poder liberar al explorador de forma segura.","Libera a Bethad de su encarcelamiento","El montañés Bethad debe estar en algún lugar de esta cueva fétida, aunque si es posible que esté vivo o no es una incógnita.","Has liberado a Bethad.","Has descubierto la prisión de Bethad.","'¡Qué valor has demostrado al venir tan lejos para salvarme! Mi familia y yo estaremos eternamente en deuda contigo. Ahora, rápidamente, salgamos de este horrible lugar.'","Encuentra a Bethad en Ologfil","Has derrotado a Ulkrank.","Instancia: Antigua guarida","Derrota a Ulkrank"},
[6800]={"Escucha mientras Crannog se dirige a los Trév Gállorg y a los Trév Duvárdain","Crannog se encuentra en Fail-á-Khro.\
\
La negociación ha concluido. Debes hablar con Crannog.","Mientras algunos de los Trév Duvárdain se adelantan para hablar, la negociación comienza en serio","Instancia: Angmar Renacido","Al concluir la negociación, Crannog te hace señas para que hables con él","Asiste a la negociación en Fail-á-Khro","Crannog se encuentra en Fail-á-Khro.\
\
Has seguido a Crannog y a los Trév Gállorg hasta Fail-á-Khro para negociar con los Trév Duvárdain. Debes hablar con Crannog.","Los Trév Gállorg se han reunido en Fail-á-Khro para negociar con los Trév Duvárdain.\
\
Debes presenciar la negociación entre los Trév Gállorg y los Trév Duvárdain.","Los Trév Gállorg se han reunido en Fail-á-Khro para negociar con los Trév Duvárdain.\
\
Debes escuchar mientras Crannog se dirige a los Trév Gállorg y a los Trév Duvárdain.","Con el fragmento de Tauressar destruido, los siervos del juramento liberados y los últimos vestigios de la Corona de Hierro llevados a la ruina, un nuevo día incierto, pero esperanzador, amanece en Angmar.","Habla con Crannog","'Ha terminado, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Duró más de lo que esperaba, pero eso no es desagradable. Mucho queda por resolver en los días venideros, pero nos reuniremos y superaremos esos desafíos. Los Trév Duvárdain se han dividido, pero no les reprocho su uso de ese nombre. Les pertenece, y no se lo quitaría. Si nuestras tribus se unirán en parentesco como lo hicimos hace mucho tiempo sigue siendo incierto, pero esa es una pregunta para otro día.\
\
¡Regocijémonos en nuestra libertad!'","'Ven, regresemos a Aughaire. Me alegrará el corazón verlo una vez más.'","'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} entre nosotros, , pero este es un asunto que debemos resolver por nosotros mismos.\
\
'No ha habido tal negociación entre los Trév Gállorg y los Trév Duvárdain en muchos años, y no sé lo que significará para nuestros pueblos. No he olvidado las fechorías de los Trév Duvárdain bajo el mandato de Domongart, pero Soltakh estaba entre ellos, y ha cambiado. Aunque ahora es un Trév Gállorg, en verdad, es de ambas tribus, y eso me da esperanza de que algún día podamos unirnos nuevamente.\
\
'Ha durado lo suficiente. Es hora, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'"},
[6801]={"'Elrohir did not say why he wished to speak with you, but he did seem concerned about something. I wonder what is troubling him? Something about the road ahead?'","Habla con Candaith","Talk to the exhausted Ranger","Halbarad is waiting to speak with you outside the ring-forges.","Treasure-coffers from Minas Elendúr can be found in the corner of the ruins.\
\
Fúsi Gem-cutter has asked you to bring him more gold from the coffers you retrieved from Minas Elendúr.","Instance: As Near as May Be","'According to Fúsi Gem-cutter, his father's work is going well and smoothly. With no more interruptions, I feel that we will soon see an end to this delay.'\
\
Halbarad laughs softly, a sound that has been missing from the journey of the Grey Company, unnoticed until now.\
\
'I say delay, but I feel better for having a secret held in reserve. Let our foes mill about in confusion, while the true heir of Isildur makes stealth his ally! It is good to be doing something.'","Fúsi receives the gold with an appraising look","'A party of...uruks! They have...climbed the path.... And there are others...in the distance. It will not be long...before they arrive....'\
\
Radanir seeks to catch his breath, but the exertion has been too much and the urgency of his message cannot be restrained.\
\
'Golodir...is at the entrance.... He hopes to...hold them back. Help him...help him quickly....'","Golodir has remained at the entrance courtyard of the ring-forges in order to delay the attacking uruks. He needs your help.","Fúsi Gem-cutter has emerged from the ring-forges with a request for you.","The uruks have been defeated","Habla con Halbarad","Investigate the distant shout","What danger has come to the ring-forges, and what does it signify for the Grey Company?","Habla con Elrohir","An exhausted Ranger stands before you, his breath ragged and uneven","'The work goes well, ${PLAYER}! Already some of the rings have been made, and they are identical to the description with which my father was provided. But the gold is running low! Very little gold is needed for each ring, of course, but my father can use only small quantities of the material when it is melted, or imperfections will arise.\
\
'Bring more coffers of gold to me from where they are being stored!'","Habla con Golodir","'The crafting of the rings sought by Halbarad goes well, ${PLAYER}? Good. If these preparations give our enemies even the slightest pause, the time they take will be counted five and seven times in value.'\
\
Elrohir pauses for a moment, thinking, and then takes you into his confidence.\
\
'Before we left Imladris, my father gave to me messages for Aragorn, confident that he would understand them. But I too understand their meaning, and that understanding fills me with worry. He bade me to remind Aragorn of the words of the seer Malbeth, and of the Paths of the Dead. I will tell you of...'\
\
Suddenly, a shout breaks the silence, and Elrohir leaps to his feet!","The uruks have been defeated and the plans of the Grey Company remain intact.","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter","Halbarad's plan is set into motion: for Fúni Gem-cutter to fashion imitations of Aragorn's ring of Barahir, based on Candaith's description.","Candaith has asked to speak with you, if you have a moment to spare.","A distant shout has broken the stillness. What has happened?","'I hope there is enough gold for the rings your friends require. It takes more than ordinary gold, you see. Only the highest quality gold can be used if these are to be sufficiently realistic, and when melted, only very small amounts of this gold is suitable.'","'Despair not, ${PLAYER}. We will defeat these uruks, or we will delay them for as long as is necessary for the remainder of our Company to complete the task for which we have come to these forges.'","'We have done well this day, ${PLAYER}. May Fúni Gem-cutter's work go as well!'","'Fúni Gem-cutter has been working hard within, melting gold with which to fashion quality imitations of the ring borne by Aragorn our chieftain. Candaith, learned in lore as he is, described the ring to Fúni, and the dwarf has pledged that his reproductions will deceive all but the most studious observer.'","Elrohir is waiting for you in the courtyard north of Candaith and Halbarad.","'${PLAYER}...a party of warring uruks...has climbed the path to this place. And I have seen others...in the distance. It will not be long...before they arrive....'\
\
Halros grabs your arm, desperate to tell you something else.\
\
'Golodir...stayed behind...to hold them back. Help...help him....'","'We have victory! The uruks will not again underestimate the Dúnedain! It is good to stand against our foes with true allies behind and beside us, is it not? I had forgotten what it felt like, ${PLAYER}. I have been bowed beneath too many shadows of late. It is good to cast them off!'","Pick up a treasure-coffer from the corner of the room where they are stored","'Where are you keeping the coffers of gold you brought out of those ruins, ${PLAYER}? Go get one! My father needs more high-quality gold if he is to continue making these imitations.'","'The ring-making is going well? Good. I gave the jewel-smith a description of the ring of Barahir as I remembered it, and if he has the skill he claims to have, his imitations should be suitable.\
\
'Elrohir wanted me to send you to him, if you had a moment. He was contemplating our plans beneath a tree in the courtyard to the north of here, if you would speak with him.'","'His father Fúni must still be working to fashion recreations of the ring borne by Aragorn. What must Fúsi Gem-cutter require of us?'"},
[6802]={"Speak with Ashâmi to continue the hunt for Kanagir","Speak with Ashâmi","'We are not the hunters here, ${PLAYER}. This serval is cunning beyond normal measure. We must be cautious.\
\
'We will not become prey.'","You survived the attack by Kanagir","She scans the woods and speaks softly.\
\
'I kissed him. It was spontaneous, something I never expected do.\
\
'I have not often allowed anyone to get close to me.\
\
'My mother's disposition, love of life, and attitude of defiance in the face of great oppression shaped me. I am who am I because of her. Her marriage to my father was arranged. I never understood how she came to care for him.\
\
'But, Raphûz,-'\
\
She stops, alerted to a sound.\
\
'What was that?'","Ashâmi appears a bit shaken as she looks over the woods. You, too, have an uneasy feeling in these woods.","There has been no sign of the serval Numûru described to Ashâmi. The woods are eerily still and quiet.","In order to prove their mettle Raphûz and Ashâmi were tasked by Numûru to prove their abilities while confronting their fears. Ashâmi must face a fearsome serval in Imhûlar.","Speak with Ashâmi to begin the hunt","Speak with Ashâmi about how to proceed","Ashâmi slows to a stop peering through the woods","Ashâmi looks eager to speak after surviving the ambush","'${PLAYER}, Raphûz speaks highly of your skill and how you helped him along his path to find me and his fate. I have seen how capable you are when you helped me with the Alad.\
\
'Still, something here makes me uneasy. Do you feel it too?'\
\
She breathes in deeply and sighs.\
\
'Perhaps I should be more eager, like Raphûz. Come, let us hunt this creature.'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You're a capable warrior. Raphûz is a good judge of character.'\
\
She manages a smile.\
\
'I confess, while we were fighting just now, I was thinking of how I must survive so I can return to him. It is a strange feeling to me. One with which I am not entirely comfortable.\
\
'I am glad we had time to travel together. I understand why he sees you as such a trusted companion. Let us return to Urmâkh.'","Instance: Ashâmi's Challenge","'Something is not right. Can you feel it?'\
\
She looks around, listening intently and peering into the woods.\
\
'If Raphûz were here, he would say, 'Is this another Shagâni superstition?''\
\
She chuckles softly.\
\
'I find his questions very amusing. He does not understand how much our superstitions kept us safe in the darkest of times. Our lives coming together as they have does seem to be something different.\
\
'I never expected -'\
\
She stops and points.\
\
'Look, there. Let's go.'","Ashâmi stopped her search and looked back into the woods. Something still feels off.","There is still no sign of Kanagir","Kanagir proved a true hunter. You and Ashâmi survived and should discuss a return to Urmâkh.","Ashâmi looks shaken, but resolute. The serval pack attacked without warning. The serval Kanagir, as described, was not among them. You feel like you are being stalked."},
[6803]={"Instance: Assault on Bardh-dorám","You should speak with Reeve Fríthild before starting your attack.","Defeat the gate-guard and its minions.","'So we have come to it, ${PLAYER}. The enemy is great, but they shall soon know the courage and strength of the Riddermark!\
\
'Yon gate is guarded by a great troll. We will need to slay the beast ere we can enter the encampment.'","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","Escape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate.","Defeat Mabaj and his minions","Defeated Mabaj and his minions","Defeat the gate-guard and its minions","You have accompanied Reeve Fríthild, Thane Ordlac, and Dudsig to the enemy encampment of Bardh-dorám.","Escape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate","<rgb=#FF0000>Reeve Fríthild has been defeated</rgb>","Defeat Mabaj and his minions.","<rgb=#FF0000>Reeve Fríthild must survive</rgb>","Defeat Ushatar and his minions.","Defeated Ushatar and his minions","Defeat Ushatar and his minions","Defeat Illska and his minions.","Defeat Illska and his minions","Defeated Illska and his minions","Defeated the gate-guard and its minions"},
[6804]={"You and the dwarves have followed the trail of the Angmarim into Clovengap, where you hope you will find some sign of the Black Stone Anvil's passage.","'Remain alert, ${PLAYER}. None of us must be blinded by the beauty of Akrakír, for we are here to learn where the Angmarim have stolen the Black Stone Anvil of my people!'","'We should make camp before another warg-pack finds us. They will not have forgotten the death of Ránulur upon the very threshold of the Mountain-home. That was the doing of dwarves, but it was Gorgar that commanded the warg-chieftain to battle. Until we have a better foothold in Gundabad, this is their territory... not ours.\
\
'But one day it will be ours again.'","Talk to Bósi near the entrance to Clovengap","Talk to Bori by the warg corpse in Clovengap","Listen to the dwarves discuss the situation in Clovengap","'You too, ${PLAYER}. Wargs are as smart as they are ferocious, and I expect this hunting-pack to attempt to encircle us.\
\
'They may attack from any direction, and we must be prepared to defend ourselves!'","The dwarves have discovered the corpse of an Angmarim cultist not far from the first body you encountered in Clovengap.","'This warg was not slain by dwarf-axes or swords, then? Aye, I see the scorch marks. Fire it was that killed this beast.'\
\
He faces Bósi and raises his voice.\
\
'I will lead us from here, father! Follow me!'","You have fended off the wargs... for now.","Bori and the other dwarves gather around the warg corpse you found near the entrance to Clovengap.","The dwarves have discovered the corpse of a warg among the mist-laden grasses of Clovengap.","Bósi stands by the entrance to Clovengap.","The dwarves discuss the violence that has been done here in Clovengap; what does it mean for the safety of your travelling party?","This corpse has been torn by the sharp claws of wargs","Examine the warg corpse","Instancia: Asalto a Pasohendido","The corpse of this warg is marked by fire, and smells of sorcery","There are wolf-voices on the wind, and it seems the dwarves do not have long to prepare before the wargs attack!","Talk to Bósi in Clovengap","Examine the corpse of the Angmarim cultist","Remain alert for the return of the wargs"},
[6805]={"Habla con Avorthal","'Estoy listo, ${PLAYER}. Encontraremos a Skorgrim Duramano y expulsaremos a esa criatura malvada no solo de Rath Teraig, sino de todo Ered Luin.'","Avorthal busca a Skorgrim Duramano en el valle de Rath Teraig, infestado de trasgos.\
\
Avorthal ha prometido la fuerza de su brazo a tu causa y busca vengarse de Skorgrim por el daño que ha causado a los pueblos de Ered Luin.","'Skorgrim ha escapado, ${PLAYER}, pero creo que Ered Luin estará a salvo de él ahora... al menos por un tiempo. Por eso, siento que el asalto combinado de enanos y Elfos fue un éxito.\
\
'Tardaremos mucho en conocer el coste total de nuestras acciones aquí. Muchas buenas personas han caído en Rath Teraig este día.\
\
'Voy a atender las heridas de mi padre, y luego juntos podremos informar a Langlas y contarle lo que ha sucedido aquí hoy.'","'Deberíamos ir a ver a Langlas.'","Skorgrim Duramano ha escapado. Avorthal te espera para hablar sobre el curso que debes tomar a continuación.","Instancia: Asalto a Rath Teraig","Avorthal busca a Skorgrim Duramano en el valle de Rath Teraig, infestado de trasgos.\
\
Un ataque sorpresa de los trasgos ha diezmado las filas de los Pueblos Libres en Rath Teraig, y ahora Avorthal lidera un contraataque contra los trasgos que acechan en las alturas.","Avorthal busca a Skorgrim Duramano en el valle de Rath Teraig, infestado de trasgos.\
\
Avorthal ha jurado rescatar a Sara Roblecorazón, que está cautiva de los trasgos en Rath Teraig, y dejar de preocuparse por el destino de su padre hasta que ella esté libre.","'Estoy listo para continuar, ${PLAYER}. Debemos encontrar y rescatar a esta Sara Roblecorazón. Una vez que ella esté a salvo, podemos continuar nuestra búsqueda de Skorgrim.\
\
'Quizá encontremos a mi padre más adelante y podamos prestarle nuestra ayuda, aunque estoy seguro de que no necesita mucho nuestras armas.'","Los enanos y los Elfos de Ered Luin han comenzado su asalto contra el ejército trasgo en el desfiladero de Rath Teraig, y Langlas te ha enviado tras las líneas enemigas para reunirte con Avorthal.","'Me siento lo suficientemente descansado como para continuar. Continuemos nuestra búsqueda de Skorgrim Duramano.'"},
[6807]={"Escucha a escondidas a Lagordal y a la espía","Espera a que Erlys interrogue a Lagordal","Todavía queda la cuestión del destino de Lagordal.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Igrain ha sido derrotada!</rgb>","Instancia: En una encrucijada","${PLAYERNAME:Acompañado[m]|Acompañada[f]} por Erlys e Igrain, partes hacia Tornhad para salvar a Cariad.","Habla con la montaraz","Te has alejado demasiado de Erlys e Igrain","Deberías hablar con Erlys antes de acercarte a Tornhad.","La espía se ha percatado de tu presencia.\
\
Deberías enfrentarte a ella y a Lagordal junto con tus aliados.","Deberías esperar nuevas órdenes de Erlys.","Espera nuevas órdenes de Erlys","La espía ha sido derrotada, pero Lagordal sobrevive.","El enfrentamiento ha terminado de forma violenta.\
\
Deberías defender a Erlys e Igrain.","'Entonces, sigamos adelante.'","'Debo confesar que, si no fuera por tu presencia, habría pensado que los dunlendinos venían en busca de venganza.\
\
'Estas acusaciones contra Lagordal son muy graves. Ver a uno de los nuestros ayudar de tan buen grado a los espías del Mago Blanco... es perturbador, cuanto menos.'","Habla con Erlys","Sigue a Erlys","Libera a Cariad de sus ataduras","'Puede que no confíe en los montaraces, pero me gustaría que esto se resolviera con el menor derramamiento de sangre posible, si es que se puede. Sígueme.'","Deberías mantenerte ${PLAYERNAME:oculto[m]|oculta[f]} con Erlys e Igrain para escuchar a escondidas.","Defiende a Erlys e Igrain","Erlys te ha ordenado que liberes a Cariad.","'Me alegra que me hayas demostrado que me equivocaba, duvodiad.\
\
'Antes de que vuelvas a partir, regresa y comparte una comida con nosotros.'","Espera la sentencia de Lagordal","Enfréntate a Lagordal y a la espía","Una montaraz ha exigido saber el motivo de la presencia de los dunlendinos aquí.\
\
Deberías contarle lo que ha pasado.","Has ayudado a liberar a Cariad y a poner fin a las intrigas de Lagordal.\
\
Deberías hablar con Erlys.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Erlys ha sido derrotada!</rgb>","Deberías seguir a Erlys.","<rgb=#FF0000>No te alejes demasiado de Erlys e Igrain</rgb>"},
[6808]={"Talk to Britou","'King Rioc has led us for these many years, and his word is hewn from stone like that of the Mountain itself, with roots as deep. Let Sauron show himself again, at his peril! He would dare it not, when confronted with we Men of the Mountain and you, the sons of Númenor and now Gondor!'","Examine the disturbing idol erected by the Orcs in Garth Lotheg","Talk to Isildur","Instancia: En la Piedra de Erech","'We know what this means, Beriadar. It means that these Orcs are not leaderless, but were given purpose by Sauron their master.'","You are Iarvund, a soldier of the young Kingdom of Gondor, come to the Hill of Erech with your friend Urcheneb to serve your master Isildur.","Wait for the Men of the Mountain to arrive","'Examine that idol, Beriadar. It fills me with unease, for I know what it portends.'","Isildur is in the centre of Garth Lotheg, waiting to speak with you about the disturbing idol of Sauron the Orcs erected there.","The Orcs have erected a disturbing idol in the centre of Garth Lotheg.","Isildur is standing by the Stone of Erech, waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Dorwë","The Men of the Mountain have arrived. Will they now swear the oath of allegiance to Isildur?","Talk to King Rioc","'I did not believe the whispers, Beriadar. I thought Rioc's people would be as good as their word, but it seems the rumours were true: they worshipped Sauron in secret during the Dark Years, and now he has returned they cast their lot in with his.\
\
'Standing here upon Erech, I look from the height and see for a great distance, even into the years ahead. Know this: my words to Rioc were not empty. This war will last for countless years, and if Gondor defies Sauron, Rioc's people will be summoned once more before the end.\
\
'They will never know peace until they have fulfilled their oath. This I vow and let all bear witness to it!'","Support Isildur as he curses the Men of the Mountain for their refusal","'Beriadar, this is terrible! Look what has happened to Garth Lotheg! This is the reason we have heard naught from its defenders...they are slain and the fort taken!\
\
'How could such evil have come to Gondor without our knowledge?'","'There is a great deal we can learn from you and from the Kingdom of Gondor. We are now as brothers, are we not? The bond of our oath will tie us together, and let our shared enemies tremble! Gondor and the Mountain!'","Candaith is telling you the tale of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead.","'Our wait has ended, Beriadar. King Rioc and some of his people now climb to the summit. They are late, but their support against Sauron will excuse them their tardiness.'","'This is the place, Iarvund: the Hill of Erech. You stayed behind at the encampment when our lord was last here, but I was in the party that wrestled the Stone to the summit. Several days of toil, true, but I can think of no better way to mark the escape of Númenor's sons from the deluge.\
\
'Seeing the forest we came through from this height gives me a greater appreciation for its beauty, and I forgive its branches the many scratches we sustained! This new Kingdom of Gondor is a beautiful land indeed; may it stand evermore!\
\
'This way, Iarvund! Isildur has gone ahead, and we must not let our lord wait on our arrival!'","'At this moment, there are none in this land more proud than I, King Rioc of the Mountain. There is so much our people can learn from each other, and by sharing our strength, we will be the stronger for it. Your lord Isildur was wise to reach out to us, and we are honoured to have been called to this place.\
\
'Should Sauron return, he will face our combined might and be fearful!'","Many years passed, and a shadow fell upon the Kingdom of Gondor.","Candaith is continuing the story of Isildur and the oath of the Men of the Mountain.","'Look at the Stone up there, Iarvund. It will stand here long after we are gone. I feel it in my bones.\
\
'Or perhaps I feel the aching memory of the countless men and horses used to haul it to the summit!'","King Rioc and the Men of the Mountain have come to Erech, summoned by Isildur to fulfill their oath.","'This is the work of Orcs, Beriadar. You and Dorwë come with me. We will fight our way into the fort while the rest of our band approaches Garth Lotheg from the flank. They will rue the day they spilled Gondorian blood on our soil!'","It is as Isildur feared. Garth Lotheg has been besieged by Orcs, and its defenders slain.","Talk to Urcheneb","The Men of the Mountain have arrived, but they refuse to honour the terms of their oath.","Urcheneb and Isildur are on the summit of Erech.","Talk to Bodúan","Isildur has asked you to look for the Men of the Mountain to arrive from the north slope of the hill of Erech.\
\
Isildur and his trusted soldiers have come to Erech and now wait for the arrival of the Men of the Mountain.","Witness the meeting between Isildur and the Men of the Mountain","'It is a good day, Iarvund. Gondor will be strong, but she will be stronger with allies, and this night, she will have more than she had this morning.'","Isildur is at the summit by the Stone of Erech, waiting for the Men of the Mountain to arrive and fulfill their oath.","Isildur is at the summit of Erech.","Listen to Candaith continue the telling of the tale","Listen to Candaith's story continue","'Iarvund, is it? Yes, I thought so.'\
\
Isildur looks about expansively, admiring the view from the summit.\
\
'This has been a year of toil, Iarvund. But in moments like this, breathing the clean air and looking out over the forests of this Middle-earth, I can almost believe that this is home.'","'I have called the Men of the Mountain to this place. Will they come? Gondor is young and needs her allies.\
\
'Look for them to arrive from the north side of the Stone, Iarvund.'","The King of the Mountain has sworn to fight against Sauron should he return to Middle-earth, and in return, his people will have the aid of Gondor.","'What a day this has been, Iarvund! We must learn from Isildur's example: do not undervalue the worth of our alliances! It would be easy to look upon the wonders of Gondor, even this early in its life, and think we can conquer any enemy.\
\
'But Sauron is conniving, and if he does somehow return, as Isildur fears, we will be glad for the strong warriors of the Mountain.'","Isildur has returned to the Stone of Erech to summon the Men of the Mountain to fulfill their oath, but they have not yet arrived.","'It does not look good, Beriadar. The Men of the Mountain should have been here by now, but they have sent no word and made no appearance.\
\
'I have never seen our lord Isildur like this. It may be best for King Rioc if he does not come here at all.'"},
[6809]={"Instancia: En la Cima de la Isla","Balakhâd has expressed a desire to speak with you instead of fighting.","Sigileth has tracked Balakhâd and Nakási to the island of Kasukhín, in the middle of the Fearwater.","Sigileth is eager to end the threat posed by Balakhâd and Nakási.","Corudan has been grievously injured by Nakási's deadly blade.","Talk to Sigileth on the island of Kasukhín","Stand your ground against Balakhâd","'My childhood was one of tumult, ${PLAYER}. My mother and my father spoke often to me of Castamir, instructing me that it was our duty to follow his example. Often I wondered if they were right. Was it true that Elves would always seek to keep our people underfoot, subject to their laws and their shadowy rule?\
\
'Could my parents have been wrong? From time to time I saw Elves of the Oasis, the Kintai, in the markets of Umbar Baharbêl, and they seemed otherworldly to me but never sinister. In truth, much of the evil I saw came at the hands of Men! Did not the Kindred of the Coins hold me captive and chase my mother into hiding at the conclusion of their uprising? Was I not threatened with torture by Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper?\
\
'But then I beheld the terrible battle where the waterfalls ran red, and I saw the monstrous Orcs that emerged from Utug-bûr. I heard the battle-cries of the ferocious Utûgi, and I saw the corpses piled at their feet. I perceived the name of their masters, ${PLAYER}, and they were called the Thardúth. From afar I heard the Wizard Inkanûsh speak of them as he strove against their powers, and I knew them for what they were.\
\
'They are Elves, ${PLAYER}. A terrible evil of the ancient world has awoken to endanger the lands of Men, and it is in form and nature precisely what my father believed it would be. Castamir was right, and my parents were right, and in their names I have gathered those who would fight to save our world from Elf-kind. Nakási and I have set aside our quarrel. With her ships and my loyal Heirsworn, we will free all of Middle-earth from the grasp of the Elves, and those who aid them.\
\
'If you will stand with me, I would welcome your prowess. You know how dangerous the Thardúth can be.'","'Balakhâd and Nakási must be somewhere within the ruins of Kasukhín that sit atop the island; from that high place they can survey the fleet. It will not be long until they begin to see the effects of Cúridwan's interference. We must hurry.\
\
'They will have defenders posted on the bridge that leads to the ruins, ${PLAYER}. Prepare for a fight!'","Examine Corudan's wound","Balakhâd has attempted to convince you of the rightness of his position.","Nakási has discovered your attempt to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind!","Defeat Balakhâd on the island of Kasukhín","'${PLAYER}... don't worry about me...\
\
'You have to stop them...'","Delay Nakási long enough for Cúridwan to finish her mission","Talk to Balakhâd on the island of Kasukhín","Words will not appease Balakhâd. Only combat will suffice!","Nakási and Balakhâd escape to the surviving ships of the fleet!"},
[6810]={"'Continue upwards to Zudrugund, ${PLAYER}! Find Candaith along the path further ahead and help him fight the uruks!'","Núrzumgrat has left a mighty troll to defend the span below Zudrugund. It must be defeated if you are to reach the top.","'Ha ha ha ha! That is how you slay an uruk! But where is Thráin? He would want the honour of defeating the leader of this band, and it was wrong of us to deprive him of it!'","'There are uruks further up the mountain! I have heard some of their talk, and they call themselves the Grishgúk. Their leader is called Núrzumgrat, and it sounds like he has come to the summit! We must fight through these uruks, ${PLAYER}!'","You have repelled the attack","'We have to do something about this troll, ${PLAYER}! The Defender of the Span keeps us from Zudrugund, where Nár and Frithgeir must be in mortal danger!'","You have defeated the Defender of the Span","Fight your way further up the path and talk to Candaith","Now that the Defender of the Span is defeated, you can approach Zudrugund, where the leader of the uruks confronts the dwarves.","'You must defeat the Defender of the Span if we are to come to Zudrugund!'","Instancia: Ataque a Zudrugund","Talk to Nár outside Zudrugund","Defeat the Defender of the Span","'We are here and not much behind the uruks, if that is their foul stench I sense on the air! The other Rangers who came with us will approach from the other slope, and we will rejoin them when they have scouted the heights.\
\
'For now let us continue and defeat whatever uruks have stayed behind to defend their way back down the mountain!'","Candaith is further up the path to Zudrugund.","Talk to Radanir on the path up to Zudrugund","'${PLAYER}! This way! The uruks are at the summit! We have to do something, and quickly!'","If Ergothorn can be trusted, a warband of uruks marches on Zudrugund from the south, with orders involving Nár that could endanger the errand of the Grey Company.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","'I will be well enough after a short rest, ${PLAYER}. Help me to my feet and inside Zudrugund. I have something I need to tell you about Nár. He was acting peculiarly before the attack.'","Nár is outside Zudrugund, and you should speak to him now that the uruks are defeated.","You have come with Radanir to Zudrugund in pursuit of the uruk-band.","Fight your way up the path to Zudrugund and talk to Calenglad"},
[6811]={"The Ent stares down at the bird's lifeless body. A strange expression plays across his eyes.\
\
'I see....'","You have found Oldheart's little bird-friend...dead, suffocated by the pollutants of the Orcs and Uruks crossing Fangorn from Isengard to Rohan.","You have picked up Oldheart's fallen friend","'You have done enough, little ${CLASS}. The Ents will take over from here. We cannot slumber while our forest is corrupted by the filth of Saruman....'","Bring the bird to Oldheart","Oldheart stops at the edge of the polluted pond","You should follow Oldheart.","Instancia: Despierto por fin","Oldheart is in Fangorn.","Follow Oldheart and defend yourself from enemies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Oldheart is at the pond's edge in Fangorn.","Oldheart stops at the edge of the pond and turns around expectantly","'They are coming. There will be revenge. There will be justice. Orcs will pollute the Eaves of Fangorn no more.'\
\
The Ent's eyes now burn with a fire that fills you with fear...fear, admiration, and awe. It is good to be a friend of the Ents, and not an enemy.","Oldheart speaks, his voice slow from disuse, but the tone of sadness is unmistakeable","Speak with Oldheart, for the other Ents approach","Tell Oldheart of the little bird's fate","The dead bird can be found in the middle of the murky, foul pond.","Talk to Oldheart","Oldheart stands at the edge of his meadow in Fangorn.\
\
You should speak with Oldheart.","You awakened the Ents of Fangorn's eaves","You are tempted to lie to Oldheart to spare the Ent his feelings, but it will not do. Those keen eyes will see through it at once.\
\
You gently relay your tale to Oldheart, of the Orcs of Saruman, the sullied water, and the little victim -- a bird that did nothing but pass unwitting through the cloud of death that creeps upon all the lands of Middle-earth.","The Ent rumbles softly as he searches for a voice that has not oft been used for many years.\
\
'Hrum. Where is my little friend? Please bring him to me.'","Has derrotado a un enemigo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Follow Oldheart","You should talk to Oldheart.","Pick up the little bird","The Ents are awake...."},
[6812]={"Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
You have fought your way to the White Stone Forge, but Allaban the Collector and his forces will soon arrive at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Spall and Thrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
Despite all peril, Spall and Thrástan have accompanied you to Abkân'aban to confront the Iron Crown. You should talk to Spall and Thrástan.","Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown have arrived at Abkân'aban. You should confront them and prevent them from laying claim to the White Stone Forge.","As the last of the Angmarim of the Iron Crown falls defeated, Hermáth calls you over","'Something stirs within me, ${PLAYER}, but I know not what it is...\
\
'All I know is that the Shaper's hearth beckons to me! It is as if I were a stray ember returning to the forge...\
\
'Will you accompany me up the old stairs, friend?","'These stones... are familiar to me, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'My memories seem clearer the nearer we draw to the Shaper's hearth. I came here once... I came with Durin...'\
\
Thrástan trails off and begins mumbling to himself for a moment. After a moment, he grips his smithing hammer tightly.\
\
'I must return....'","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
You have accompanied Hermáth Stormhammer and his warriors to confront the Iron Crown at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Talk to Spall","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. I am the Forge-servant, Tamindur, wrought anew by the will of the Shaper... the First Crafter.... He Who Made The Dwarves!\
\
'Invaders run rampant upon the Stone of Wakening, but no longer. By some lesser magic, they have come here unhindered, but they cannot oppose me nor my lord in the Uttermost West.\
\
'Though you be not of the Eldest House, you shall be spared my wrath.'","Thrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
After escorting Thrástan to the White Stone Forge, it has sprung to life. You should talk to Thrástan.","Thrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
Thrástan has thanked you for your aid and asked you to bear witness to his \\qawakening\\q. You should honour Thrástan's wishes.","As Tamindur descends, you see Allaban and the Iron Crown preparing to attack!","Without hesitation, the Forge-servant strides forth","'I do not believe the Angmarim are the sort to make empty threats. But we have claimed the White Stone Forge... at least for the moment!\
\
'If we have truly been led into a trap, it will not be long before it is sprung. In the meantime, escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge. Even if our doom is soon to follow, I would do right by him and honour an old dwarf's last request.\
\
'I and the others will prepare to make our stand—as hopeless as it may be!'","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
The Forge-servant has used his ancient power to defeat Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Witness the wrath of the Forge-servant","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
You have spoken to Spall and Thrástan and they intend to do what they can to repel the Iron Crown. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","'By Durin's beard! What have we witnessed this day?!'","The Iron Crown can be found at Abkân'aban.\
\
You should follow Hermáth Stormhammer and do what you can to repel the Iron Crown from the Stone of Wakening.","'Everyone is prepared then? Good.\
\
'There is little time to waste!'","Witness Thrástan's awakening","Talk to the Forge-servant","The Forge-servant can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
The Forge-servant is confronting Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown. You should bear witness to the Forge-servant's wrath.","Confront Allaban the Collector and the Iron Crown","'Lord Stormhammer need not concern himself with my safety, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'As soon as I passed beyond the warding-runes at Zâram-mekhem, I understood what peril might await me in Gloomingtarn. And to be quite honest, I would sooner die than allow the Iron Crown to defile the Stone of Wakening.\
\
'I will wield my axe as best I can, my friend. Let us hope it is enough!'","All that remains where Allaban the Collector once stood is a pillar of basalt!","At Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening, the Angmarim of the Iron Crown seek to master the white forge of Durin the Deathless, forever defiling the hallowed caverns of Gloomingtarn.","As if in answer, the ancient forge springs to life at your approach!","Instancia: El Despertar","The Forge-servant can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
By some ancient magic, Thrástan has been returned to his true form: the Forge-servant. You should talk to the Forge-servant.","The White Stone Forge can be found atop Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
With sudden clarity, Thrástan wishes to return to the White Stone Forge. You should escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge.","Talk to Thrástan","'By Durin's beard! What have we witnessed this day?!\
\
'${PLAYER}, this is beyond all belief!'","'At last we come to Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening... but it appears the Angmarim of the Iron Crown arrived sooner than we supposed!\
\
'We have broken their numbers upon the span, but I fear that is not the last of them. Others of their order must have gone ahead in search of the White Stone Forge, but we cannot allow them to lay claim to it!\
\
'I have my misgivings that Spall and Thrástan are prepared for the coming battle, but it seems there is little choice for us now but to press onward.\
\
'When they are prepared, we shall strike against the Iron Crown!'","Fight through the Iron Crown to the White Stone Forge atop Abkân'aban","Escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge","As the flames fade around you, an imposing figure appears where Thrástan stood","'I understand, ${PLAYER}. I see all that the Shaper wished of me!\
\
'That I laboured as a servant of the great forge long before Durin laid dreaming beneath Mount Gundabad. And when my task was finished, so too did I rest for many years of the world.\
\
'The time of my awakening has come—and my long slumber is at its end!'","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer","Thrástan can be found at Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.\
\
Although Allaban the Collector and the forces of the Iron Crown will soon arrive, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge. You should talk to Thrástan."},
[6813]={"'The guardsmen are in disarray. They speak of two groups: those loyal to Azagath and those who now question him. We should remain alert for the first, and learn what information we can from the second.'\
\
Nauriel turns her gaze to the great hall, lingering briefly on the fountain in its centre.\
\
'I wish you had waited for me to accompany you before you came here the first time, ${PLAYER}. Had you done so, we would not now need to make this venture... for Azagath's head would already be shorn from his body and I would be half of the way back to Pinnath Gelin!\
\
'But what is done is done, and that undone remains undone. Let us speak to these women and learn if they support Azagath or oppose him.'","Nauriel has not forgotten the injuries done to her family by the Kindred of the Coins, and she wants to pursue Azagath and his fleeing allies as they attempt to escape the Citadel of Winds.","Follow Azagath's trail through the door and outside the Citadel of Winds","'Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}? We will likely face opposition from those still loyal to Azagath, and they will seek to keep us from reaching their master and his allies in the Kindred.\
\
'Once we pass through this door, we must let none keep us from finding the treacherous leader of the Kindred of the Coins! Others of your crew will follow behind to keep Azagath from circling around us and escaping. Now let us fight!'","'I beg you! Have mercy upon me and my fellows! We had no choice! Nakási Wave-reaper threatened to skin us alive if we did not help them cast off with utmost haste! There was a terrible light in her eyes, and I think she would have done it!\
\
'Belondor's crew is fiercely loyal, and they manned the oars without argument. Even when Azagath told them their destination, they did not balk at it as I would have done!'\
\
You ask the dock-worker where the leaders of the Kindred intended to row, and he shudders.\
\
'Across the water, stranger. They made for the Temple of the All-Seeing. They made for the Mâkhda Khorbo.'","Nauriel is within the great hall of the Citadel of Winds, ready to pursue Azagath and his allies.","Azagath and his allies fled outside the Citadel of Winds by making use of the door at the bottom of the stairs.","'For now they have escaped us, but not for long.'","'Those warriors were guarding the north-east corridor, ${PLAYER}. That must be the way Azagath, Nakási, and Belondor fled.\
\
'It is curious, but I see no one guarding the passage. Still, we must remain alert!'","Talk to Nauriel outside the Citadel of Winds","Ushu wants to speak to you in the Citadel of Winds.","Follow Nauriel to the docks outside the Citadel of Winds","'The corridor to the south-east descends a long flight of stairs. Azagath and his allies must have gone that way!'","Follow Ushu and Enât","Azagath and his allies have escaped from the island on which stands the Citadel of Winds.","'I do not have a good feeling about this. That door leads outside!\
\
'${PLAYER}, we must hurry. We cannot allow Azagath to escape us!'","Nauriel is waiting to speak with you within the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to the observant dock-worker outside the Citadel of Winds","'When we aided you we did not think you intended to bring Gondorian sorcery to bear against the Kindred! We fled when the Corsair made your presence known to Azagath, but from the far side of the hall we witnessed the terrible creatures as they rose from the fountain. Where have they now gone? Do you plan to unleash them upon the city?'\
\
You assure Ushu that the Five Sisters would not have harmed either her or her friends in any way, and now that Thorongil has been rescued they will not trouble the folk of the city. She considers your words.\
\
'That is a comfort, but something yet confuses me. If these water-spirits answered to the call of Gondor, why were they dressed in Umbari garb? To my eye they were dressed as nobles of the city, and Enât told me the same.'\
\
You tell Ushu that the Five Sisters did not appear that way to you, and she furrows her brow but does not seem surprised.\
\
'For one thing to appear many ways is not unusual in these times. The Kindred of the Coins seemed to be one thing to us, and yet Azagath's words of late have cast another light upon it, a light fell and sickly.'","Nauriel has come with you outside the Citadel of Winds in pursuit of Azagath.","'No... no...\
\
'This cannot be! Azagath and his allies cannot have escaped us!'","Nauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to Ushu in the Citadel of Winds","Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of Winds","Instancia: Azagath Perseguido","Ushu has agreed to show you and Nauriel the passage through which Azagath and his allies fled.","The nearby dock-worker may know where Azagath and his allies fled."},
[6814]={"Balakhôr has offered you a drink from his collection of wines.","Talk to Lothíriel and prepare to depart for the Night-jewel","'What advice would you give to me, ${PLAYER}?'","'This is the Nûluzimir, the jewel of Umbar and flagship of Balakhôr the Scourge. You are here under a flag of peace, but if it were otherwise you would never leave it, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will bring you to Balakhôr. He will not be pleased that you have come instead of Imrahil's daughter, but that is not my concern. That must be yours.'","'But you must already have known this, ${PLAYER}. Most of Gondor's warriors have been called to battles elsewhere. Even were they here, there is little they could do against the fleet of Umbar.\
\
'But I have been a poor host. You must be quite parched, and I have done naught but tell you things you already know.'","Instancia: Balakhôr el Azote","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
Balakhôr has sent a summons to Lothíriel to treat with him on his flagship, the Night-jewel.","'Look around you, ${PLAYER}. What do you see? You see the sea-faring power of Umbar, rebuilt from nothing!\
\
'Thirty years ago, a hero of Gondor sailed to Umbar at the head of a fleet. He burned the ships he found at the port and took the city. The Corsairs have spent the time nursing their hurts and rebuilding their power. No hero will save Gondor from them this time.\
\
'Where is that hero now, ${PLAYER}? He is gone, and now I have come to return that overdue favour. I will burn his fleet as he did that of Umbar. But there will be nothing left to rebuild when I am finished with it.'","Talk to Lothíriel","'The Corsairs range far and wide upon the seas, ${PLAYER}, and have taken bottles of wine for my collection from every land lapped by the waves. You are welcome to sample any of my finest.'","Balakhôr stands on the deck of the Night-jewel, waiting to hear why Lothíriel did not answer his summons.","Dorthaneth has come to the Great Hall of Dol Amroth to advise her friend Lothíriel.","Talk to Dorthaneth","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. She has asked for your advice concerning Balakhôr's proposal that she treat with him on the deck of his flagship.","Accept or refuse Balakhôr's offer","Step off the side of the Night-jewel","'It does not matter to me what Prince Imrahil might have done if he were in his daughter's place, for he is not. I do not think Balakhôr would have made this request of Imrahil.\
\
'She must not trust him. He is a snake, like the others who call themselves Heirs of Castamir, and his flagship will not be a place of safety for her, or for anyone.\
\
'You must urge her to reject this proposal.'","Umer, the Corsair emissary, has rowed you to the Night-jewel and is now ready to bring you to Balakhôr.","'Well, you have heard my demands. You are not devising a counter-proposal, are you? You are in no position for this, my foolish ${CLASS}!'","Dorthaneth is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. She has asked if you are willing to go to the Night-jewel in Lothíriel's stead.","The corsair rowed you to the Night-jewel in awkward and unpleasant silence","Balakhôr has done enough talking. Now it is time for you to make your own demands of the Corsair leader.","Talk to Balakhôr","Balakhôr has summoned Lothíriel to treat with him on his flagship, the Night-jewel.","'So Umer delivered the message, but Lothíriel elected to send you in her stead? How am I to interpret this response? It reveals that she does not respect my wishes, and distrusts my word. It is a cowardly response, for it shows she values her own life and safety above those of others.'","'That seems to me a wiser course, ${PLAYER}, if you are willing to risk the adventure. Balakhôr cannot be trusted, but you may be better-prepared to deal with any treachery he might think to enact.\
\
'Walk with me and I will do my best to prepare you for this errand.'","The wine is among the best you have ever tasted","'I am the ruler of Dol Amroth while my father is away, and it is my duty to do what is best for its people. How am I to know what that is, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Would my father treat with Balakhôr? Would he have gone to his enemy's flagship under a banner of peace?'","Balakhôr's eyes flash angrily at your refusal","Balakhôr is on the deck of the Night-jewel, and has more to say to you.","'I thank you, ${PLAYER}. Stay watchful in the company of Balakhôr. I know he is not to be trusted, and you should watch him carefully.\
\
'Do what you can for the people of Dol Amroth! I would have gone myself, but if this plan eases Dorthaneth's mind....'","Make your own demands of Balakhôr","Balakhôr has refused your demands, and instead has made you an offer: to step off the side of the Night-jewel and swim to shore.","You are walking with Balakhôr on the deck of the Night-jewel, remaining alert for any sign of treachery.","Give Lothíriel your advice on her course of action","You have come to the Night-jewel to treat with Balakhôr about the war.","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
You have agreed to meet with Balakhôr on his flagship, the Night-jewel, in Lothíriel's stead.","Talk to Umer on the deck of the Night-jewel","Go to the Night-jewel and meet with Balakhôr"},
[6815]={"King Thranduil is at Torech Emel.\
\
After threatening King Thranduil, the bloated and sickly Iphantemel welcomed her own end. You should talk to King Thranduil.","Talk to King Thranduil","'My long hunt for vengeance is finally ended, but it rings hollow.\
\
'Iphantemel was once a great foe of my people... and it was she who first darkened the eaves of the Greenwood. Yet now, she merely awaited her death... almost welcoming it.'\
\
Thranduil pauses for a moment and seems uneasy.\
\
'She spoke a name I have not heard in over an Age, but I sensed that you knew it well. Ungwetári, the Spider-queen....\
\
'In truth, Iphantemel was but one of her children. If Ungwetári has summoned all the spiders of her brood back to the shadowed caverns of the Ephel Dúath, we have much still to fear.\
\
'Let us go from this place, ${PLAYER}.'","Despite uncovering evidence that the Weeping Warrior still lurks within Eryn Lasgalen, King Thranduil has turned his attention to his hated foe of old: Iphantemel.","<rgb=#FF0000>King Thranduil has been defeated!</rgb>","King Thranduil is standing in the webbed hollow in Torech Emel.\
\
You have repelled an attack by the children of Iphantemel, but it seems the Old Mother may have called off her children.","Confront Iphantemel","King Thranduil is at Torech Emel.\
\
You have come to a webbed hollow in Torech Emel and learned that Iphantemel dwells in the nearby cavern. You should talk to King Thranduil.","Instancia: La perdición del Rey Elfo","You are being attacked by Iphantemel's spiders in Torech Emel.","King Thranduil's scout is speaking to him.","<rgb=#FF0000>King Thranduil must not be defeated</rgb>","'I do not understand, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'Has Iphantemel called off her own children? She must know her doom comes, so why does she surrender?\
\
'I must see her with my own eyes. Let us press on!'","'It is quiet here, ${PLAYER}, and I take no comfort in it.\
\
'Iphantemel's brood has lessened in size of late, but it is still enough to overcome the unwary. My scouts have pressed onward deeper into Torech Emel, and I warned them to tread softly in Iphantemel's lair. Let us hope they have done as I have bidden, or we may soon find ourselves outnumbered.\
\
'Let us move to join them, but remain on guard. Iphantemel's children lurk in their hiding places, and we may rouse them with careless steps....'","Iphantemel's massive form falls lifeless to the ground...","Repel the spider ambush in Torech Emel","King Thranduil beckons you over...","King Thranduil is standing in Torech Emel.\
\
You have come to Torech Emel to confront and defeat the Great Spider, Iphantemel. You should talk to King Thranduil.","Follow King Thranduil into Torech Emel","One of King Thranduil's scouts stands watch at the edge of a thickly-webbed hollow...","Iphantemel can be found in a small cavern in Torech Emel.\
\
Iphantemel has called off her children and awaits King Thranduil.","Listen to King Thranduil and his scout","'Iphantemel's brood once spread through all of Mirkwood, blighting the lands from here to the distant Scuttledells. And now, it seems they have left it in silence.\
\
'How can this be? What has happened?'","'While Ungwetári still lives, Iphantemel's death shall bring me little comfort. Let us go.'","King Thranduil is at Torech Emel.\
\
King Thranduil intends to confront the Old Mother, but he is unnerved by the lack of spiders at Torech Emel. You should follow him and remain on guard."},
[6816]={"Encuentra a Laerdan","Entra en Barad Tironn y habla con Forchon.","'Debemos marcharnos rápido antes de que nuestra presencia sea descubierta, ${PLAYER}.'","Has descubierto que Laerdan no fue asesinado y que fue retenido en Barad Tironn para ser interrogado.","Éin derrotado","Instancia: Barad Tironn","Entra en Barad Tironn y encuentra a Laerdan.","Espera a Forchon","Espera a Forchon en Barad Tironn","'Hemos llegado a salvo, pero temo que el Enemigo pueda estar pisándonos los talones.'"},
[6818]={"'Acercate,","'We need to hide. Quickly, behind the large mirror!'","Defeat the remaining hobgoblins.","Defeat the remaining hobgoblins","Talk to Gazathrug.","Find a good location to spy on the Orcs.","Find a good location to spy on the Orcs","Listen to the Orc factions","A group of Orcs led by Gazathrug has converged with a group of hobgoblins","Defeat Gazathrug.","Talk to Hetbrúda","Gazathrug picks himself up, sword in hand, to die in battle","A large group of Orcs gathers close to here!","Talk to Gazathrug","'Come, ${PLAYER}, let us continue to the Steepset. While at Imrêkh-guthlu I overheard that dwarves had secured Zidir-nesad.'","Instancia: Batalla por los Confines Superiores","Gazathrug, still breathing, beckons you closer","Gazathrug falls in combat","Now is the time to take on the last few remaining hobgoblins!","Defeat Gazathrug","Talk to Hetbrúda.","Listen to the Orc factions.","Gazathrug's fear of losing the Upper Reaches of Máttugard are quite warranted."},
[6819]={"Take the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces.","Set up barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Mizâdi on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma","Take the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces","Defend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive!","Defend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive","Defeat Ekhamati forces and destroy Ekhamâti tar pots as you move toward the hilltop.","Set up camp on the hilltop outside of Khud Zagin.","Mizâdi has faltered!","Set up barricades around the hilltop encampment.","Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun Shûma","Defeat Ekhamâti at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun Shûma.","Mizâdi has tracked Bârshud to the fortress of Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin. The time has come to meet Bârshud in pitched battle and defeat him for good.","'Now is the time for us to charge into battle and end the threat of Bârshud! Meet me on the hilltop!'","'Now that this hilltop has been won in hard-fought battle, we need to make our camp here and fortify it. Can you help set up the tents, tables and barricades we'll need to make this camp safe for everyone?'","Set up camp on the hilltop (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Set up barricades around the hilltop encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>","Speak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma.","Destroy tar pots on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: Batalla por Hamât, Parte 2","Destroyed tar pots on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Ekhamâti at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[6820]={"Push into Dun Shûma and end the threat of Bârshud!","Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma.","Treat the wounded Subuzûri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat the Ekhamâti forces!","Defeat the Mûmak!","Enter the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma","Instancia: Batalla por Hamât, Parte 3","Treated the wounded Subuzûri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Ekhamâti forces at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Make your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi","Make your way down the hilltop and toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.","Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud II.","Defeat the Mûmak","Make your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.","Mizâdi has faltered!","Defeat Ekhamâti forces and treat the wounded Subuzûri at Dun Shûma.","Defeat Ekhamâti forces at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enter the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma.","Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma","'Bârshud has escaped! No! He was right here, and he slipped through my grasp!\
\
'At least that monster was defeated. Thank you for that. I know not how many Subuzûri would have fallen had you not been here to slay the beast.'","Defeat the Ekhamâti forces","<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>","Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud II"},
[6822]={"'La caja para los picos está justo al sur, junto al señor Brogur. Puedes dejarlos allí.'","Dile a los enanos que dejen de perturbar el agua (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Wárr está supervisando los trabajos en la Puerta de Acebeda, al este del pequeño puesto avanzado y alrededor del lago.\
\
Mientras Bósi ayuda con los preparativos en el pequeño puesto avanzado, quiere que lleves los picos reparados a Wárr en la Puerta de Acebeda.","'Encontrarás a Wárr en los escombros que bloquean la Puerta de Acebeda. Llévale los picos reparados y dile que llegaré en breve.'","'No me gusta esto, ${PLAYER}; algo está mal. El aire está demasiado quieto y silencioso.'","Enanos que arrojan piedras al agua se pueden encontrar a lo largo de las orillas del lago.\
\
Brogur tiene un mal presentimiento sobre el lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda y te ha pedido que hagas que los enanos dejen de perturbar el agua.","Espera a que lleguen más enanos.","'Nos detendremos un momento en este puesto avanzado antes de continuar hacia las puertas, ${PLAYER}. Necesitaremos establecer un campamento una vez que estemos dentro de las minas, y quiero asegurarme de que todo esté preparado.\
\
'¿Todavía tienes los picos, verdad? Bien. Sígueme.'","¡Algo, o muchas cosas, se esconden en las aguas del lago!","'Esos picos nos van a ayudar mucho, ${PLAYER}, aunque te hayas tomado tu tiempo para traérnoslos. ¡Nuestros trabajadores ya casi han despejado los escombros!\
\
'No te preocupes por eso; lo hecho, hecho está. Me preocupa más este lago: hay algo en él que no me gusta. Me pone nervioso.\
\
'Algunos de mis enanos han estado lanzando piedras al agua, y agradecería que les dijeras que paren. Me pone nervioso.'","El pequeño puesto avanzado se encuentra al otro lado del lago, donde defendiste a Bósi de los lobos de sombra que atacaban.\
\
Los enanos están intentando luchar contra la misteriosa criatura que ahora acecha fuera de los Muros de Moria. Bósi te ha ordenado que te apresures al pequeño puesto avanzado para buscar ayuda para los enanos desesperados.","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Aprecio tu ayuda. Entiendo que muchos de mis enanos están inquietos, pero hay algo en esa agua que no me gusta. Me sentiré aliviado cuando los trabajadores hayan terminado de retirar los escombros frente a la puerta y podamos abandonar esta orilla desagradable.'","Retira los escombros de la Puerta de Acebeda (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'¡Todavía estamos esperando esos picos!'","Brogur está frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Brogur está esperando para hablar contigo sobre cómo ayudar a la expedición en la Puerta de Acebeda.","'¿Qué pasa, ${PLAYER}? ¿Dices que viste algo moverse en el agua? ¿Qué era?\
\
'No veo nada ahora. ¿Estás ${PLAYER:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que no lo imaginaste?'","Bósi está fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Bósi ha llegado y te espera para hablar contigo.","La caja se encuentra al sur de Wárr y junto a Brogur, frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Wárr te ha pedido que dejes los picos reparados en una caja para su uso futuro.","'¿Viste cómo la carne de esa criatura desvió nuestros golpes, ${PLAYER}? ¡Necesitamos más que armas ordinarias si queremos enfrentarnos al Guardián del Lago Negro!\
\
'Esperó en las profundidades, observando mientras nos esforzábamos por abrir las puertas, y atacó justo cuando éramos más vulnerables. ¡Maldita sea su piel por haber matado a Bróin, y a muchos otros buenos enanos además de él!\
\
'Serán vengados, pero por ahora debemos retirarnos. No podemos esperar entrar por las puertas mientras esa criatura merodea frente a ellas.'","Habla con Brogur.","El pequeño puesto avanzado que está a lo largo del camino que serpentea hasta el lago tranquilo frente a la Puerta de Acebeda está siendo atacado.\
\
Bósi y los enanos necesitan tu ayuda para defender el puesto avanzado de los lobos de las sombras.","Bósi está en el pequeño puesto avanzado donde luchaste contra los lobos de sombra, al otro lado del lago amenazante.\
\
Los enanos están en plena retirada ante la misteriosa criatura en el lago, y deberías hablar con Bósi antes de que la expedición se convierta en una derrota.","Algunas piedras grandes han bloqueado las Puertas de Durin, que se encuentran en los Muros de Moria, a orillas del Lago Negro.\
\
Bósi cree que sería un honor para ti ayudar a despejar algunos de los escombros de la Puerta de Acebeda.","'Algunos de los trabajadores están arrojando piedras al lago, y quiero que les digas que no perturben el agua. Hay algo en este lago que me pone nervioso.\
\
¿Crees que estoy exagerando? Esperemos que no.'","'Nos has sido de gran ayuda en nuestro trabajo aquí en Acebeda, ${PLAYER}, y sé que serás de gran beneficio una vez que estemos dentro de Khazad-dûm propiamente dicho.\
\
'Sería un honor para mí que tomaras una piqueta y nos ayudaras a despejar los restos de escombros que bloquean las Puertas de Durin. Esta es una oportunidad histórica, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} , y es un placer para mí ofrecértela en agradecimiento por los muchos servicios que ya nos has brindado.'","'Debemos retirarnos con los supervivientes que queden. ¡Volveremos para vengarnos del Guardián del Lago Negro!'","Habla con Bósi","Lleva los picos reparados a Wárr","Mantente en guardia","'Muy bien. Estas picas parecen estar en buen estado y serán un gran recurso mientras terminamos de desenterrar los últimos escombros.\
\
'Puedes dejarlas en esa caja al sur, justo al lado del Señor Brogur.'","Dijiste a los enanos que dejaran de perturbar el agua (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Regresa al pequeño puesto avanzado y busca ayuda","Los trabajadores de la expedición de Bósi y Brogur casi han desenterrado los escombros que bloquean la Puerta de Acebeda, y ha llegado el momento de entrar en Khazad-dûm.","'Este es un trabajo duro, sin duda, pero dentro de unos años te alegrará recordar la mano que tuviste en abrir el camino hacia Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Ayúdanos a despejar algunos de los escombros que bloquean la Puerta, y nunca olvidarás tu parte en las grandes hazañas que están por venir.'","Bósi está con el resto de los enanos de la expedición al borde del lago, fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
La Puerta de Acebeda está casi abierta y los enanos se preparan para entrar en las minas, pero algo te ha hecho sentir ${PLAYERNAME:incómodo[m]|incómoda[f]}.","Brogur está fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Has logrado que los enanos dejen de perturbar las aguas del lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, y ahora deberías regresar con Brogur.","Instancia: Ante las Puertas de Durin","Los enanos están reunidos al borde del lago, fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
La Puerta de Acebeda está casi abierta y los enanos se preparan para entrar en las minas.","Bósi está de pie en la pendiente que serpentea más allá del pequeño puesto avanzado enano, con vista al lago tranquilo.\
\
Has venido con Bósi por el camino sinuoso que conduce a la Puerta de Acebeda, y él está esperando para hablar contigo.","Habla con Bósi.","Coloca los picos reparados en la caja","Escombros de la Puerta de Acebeda retirados (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[6823]={"Instance: Behind Bars","Find the key to Dagoras' cell in the jailor's quarters.","Braigiar believes that his captain, Dagoras, has been captured by the Dunlending deserters after going to negotiate an agreement with them. He has asked you to try to find and rescue Dagoras from Lhe Lhechu.","'Listen carefully now: the guard who carries the key to this cell usually sleeps in the next room.\
\
'You should be able to sneak in there and find the key -- or if necessary just relieve him of it personally.\
\
'Try not to make too much noise though: this cell is small, and I do not have room for a lot of company here.'","Find the key to Dagoras' cell","'Let us return to Echad Dagoras. I would not want to deny Braigiar his chance to ridicule me for allowing myself to be captured.'","You have rescued Dagoras","Release Dagoras from his cell","'There is no time to waste! Let us depart.'","Dagoras has made it to the cave exit","Speak with Dagoras and find a way to release him from his cell.","Jailor's effects searched (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found the key","Help Dagoras escape","Talk to Dagoras","Release Dagoras from his cell.","'Ah! It is good to be out in the open air again, but let us not tarry. The others will soon realize that something is wrong.'","'Good, they seem to have given up their pursuit. I think we are finally safe...for now.'","Speak with Dagoras again.","Escape from Lhe Lhechu with Dagoras."},
[6824]={"La historia de Finrúth continúa en las profundidades de Tûr Fúar...","'Avanzamos hacia Agal Dûn, y durante un tiempo pareció que los Angmarim de la Corona de Hierro tenían la intención de habitar la antigua fortaleza.\
\
'Había llegado a ser como otro Carn Dûm, y comencé a preguntarme por qué estaban tan empeñados en regresar a Angmar. ¿No habíamos dejado a nuestros enemigos atrás?\
\
'Pero nunca era suficiente para los Angmarim, y su trabajo debía continuar...'","Finrúth está preparada para contar la historia de su tiempo con la Corona de Hierro en el Monte Gundabad.\
\
Debes hablar con Finrúth.","Habla con Finrúth","Escucha la historia de Finrúth","'Ninguno de nosotros será perdonado... ni los Trév Duvárdain, ¡ni el resto de la Corona de Hierro!'","Después de la caída de Mordirith y el abandono de Carn Dûm, los miembros de las tribus Trév Duvárdain se dividieron cada vez más, lo que llevó a muchos a abandonar la Corona de Hierro. Sin embargo, muchos todavía permanecieron entre los Trév Duvárdain y, ya sea por ignorancia o por ceguera voluntaria ante la verdadera maldad de la Corona de Hierro, la siguieron hasta el Monte Gundabad.","Instancia: Bajo el Agujalúgubre","'Mi historia comienza en Balach Iaran, el Paso de Hierro...\
\
Se decía que el alcance del Rey Brujo de Angmar se extendía hacia el este durante su reinado. Allí se encontraba una fortaleza conocida como Agal Dûn, y los Angmarim tenían la intención de reclamar los secretos olvidados que yacían dentro de ella. Sobre la fortaleza, la leyenda hablaba de una aguja rota que perforaba el cielo: Tûr Fúar, la Agujalúgubre, y se creía que poderosas herramientas de hechicería podrían encontrarse dentro de ella.\
\
Todos entre los Angmarim tenían planes para encontrar el poder que buscaban. Con una herramienta robada de Barad Gularan, uno de ellos pensó en ascender al ahora vacante trono de Angmar. La herramienta que portaba se llamaba Maltagar, el Infame Excavador, y poseía una magia sobrenatural. Susurros y visiones de los Muertos llegaban a todos los que se acercaban demasiado a Maltagar, y su maldad parecía crecer como si se alimentara de nosotros.\
\
Fue llevado a través de Balach Iaran y nosotros, los Trév Duvárdain, seguimos a la Corona de Hierro hasta Câr Bronach...'","Finrúth está relatando la historia de su tiempo con la Corona de Hierro en el Monte Gundabad.","'En secreto, la Corona de Hierro buscaba algo mucho más poderoso.\
\
Bajo Tûr Fúar, un terrible artefacto había quedado casi olvidado, pero no para la Suma Sacerdotisa Ásachal. En sus estudios, había aprendido muchas cosas sobre Angmar en el momento de su caída y sobre las muchas maldades del Rey Brujo que nunca salieron a la luz. Aunque nada hablaba tan claramente de lo que encontraría, sospecho que conocía su naturaleza. Y lo quería, para tener éxito donde el Rey Brujo de Angmar había fracasado.\
\
Uno de los suyos, Rúvaran, fue el hombre que robó Máltagar y con él, tenían la intención de arrebatar el poder del Rey Brujo en sus propias manos. Su trabajo la llevó a menudo a las profundidades de Tûr Fúar, pero nadie parecía saber dónde trabajaba.\
\
Decidí que lo descubriría...'","La historia de Finrúth continúa en Agal Dûn...","Finrúth está lista para continuar el relato de su tiempo entre la Corona de Hierro en el Monte Gundabad.\
\
Debes hablar con Finrúth."},
[6825]={"Has encontrado al Frontero Piedraprima","Habla con Halros","Encuentra al Frontero Piedraprima","El Frontero Piedraprima se ha herido en las cuevas situadas bajo los Campos Verdes.\
\
Has encontrado al Frontero Piedraprima, pero los trasgos lo han herido.","Instancia: Bajo los Campos Verdes","Halros ha encontrado al fin un camino que lleva a la \\qsala del trono\\q de Lubach y te espera para hablar de tu victoria.","La red de cuevas bajo los Campos Verdes parece ser extensa y se ha convertido en el hogar de una peligrosa tribu de trasgos.","'Te pido disculpas, ${PLAYER}. Esperaba llegar antes de que te unieras a la batalla contra Lubach, pero vi algo que desvió mi atención y ralentizó mi progreso por la cueva. Uno de los trasgos, una criatura ruin de poca destreza, había puesto sus manos en la porra del Toro Bramador. Intentaba escapar de las cuevas con ella, y no tengo ninguna duda de que la ira de Lubach habría sido grande al descubrir que había desaparecido.\
\
'Le ahorramos el disgusto de su ira, aunque eso ya no le servirá de mucho. He recuperado la porra y se la devolveré a Piedraprima cuando lo haya llevado sano y salvo a la Casa de vigilancia de Tejonera.\
\
'Has hecho bien en detener esta amenaza, ${PLAYER}, pero hay algo en este asunto que me inquieta. Ven a mi campamento dentro de un rato y podremos hablar de estos asuntos al aire libre.'","'Has hecho bien, pero vámonos de aquí. ¡El hedor de los trasgos es realmente insoportable!'","El Frontero Piedraprima se encuentra en algún lugar de las cuevas de los trasgos y puede estar en peligro.\
\
Halros te ha enviado a buscar al Frontero Piedraprima bajo los Campos Verdes para salvarlo.","'Yo... encontré a los trasgos, ${PLAYER}. A ellos no les importó mucho la porra del Toro Bramador... y me lo quitaron sin... mucha dificultad. Su líder es un trasgo... llamado Lubach. Tenemos que... deshacernos de este tal Lubach. Puede que no sea... Golfimbul... pero creo que es... igual de malo.\
\
'¡Mis heridas parecen peores de lo que son! Iré contigo. Solo... dame medio momento.'","Habla con el Frontero Piedraprima"},
[6826]={"The dream feels so real to you.","Maintain focus as your dream continues","Enter the tower room in your dream","Your dreaming mind conjures unusual images before you, with familiar voices emerging from unexpected places.","Balakhôr the Scourge glares at you from across the chamber","A feeling of disorientation clouds your mind: this is not the grove of Arwáth","Witness the strange images conjured by your dreaming mind","Listen to unfamiliar voices conjured by your dreaming mind","Even seen through the haze of unreality conjured by your dreaming mind, you can see lines of care and worry on the Wizard's face. Some great effort has left its mark upon him, and his exhaustion is apparent in every movement.","You suffer a feeling of unreality as Corudan's voice emerges from the body of the scorpion.\
\
'She cautioned us that the creatures possess great reserves of patience,' he says.\
\
'They might lie in wait for hours, hidden from careless observation, and strike without any warning.'","Talk to Corudan in your dream","Though he has been dead for months, the image of Balakhôr the Scourge glowers at you from the other side of the tower room.","'For many days Megorlam whispered to me from the stone and I came to understand he was a prisoner. I know not the precise reason for which Sauron imprisoned him, though I might make a guess. The chains that bind him within this statue remain unbroken; the Dark Lord must have drawn upon another source to fashion those bonds. They survived his own defeat, to the sorrow of Megorlam.\
\
'My struggle with the captive spirit has revealed this much, Taurdir: he possessed knowledge of some secret that even Sauron knew not. He taunted the Dark Lord with this secret, claiming that this power was beyond Sauron, impossible for even that terrible sorcerer to harness. \\qThis power is beyond all living memory!\\q he said to Sauron, and great was the Dark Lord's anger. As I strove against Megorlam, he repeated these three words over and over again: \\qbeyond living memory,\\q he cried, \\qbeyond living memory!\\q\
\
'I believe Megorlam thought to ensnare me with the promise of knowledge, attempting to steal my powers and use them to break from his prison. I proved more capable than he expected, Taurdir, and he has relented in that effort, but I dare not speak to him again lest he overcome my defences.\
\
'But his words trouble me, my Ranger friend. A power beyond Sauron...'","Balakhôr appears as you remember him.\
\
Months ago, before the end of the War of the Ring, the leader of the Heirs of Castamir stood on the deck of the Night-jewel, defying Aragorn and the Army of the Dead in what proved to be his final moments.","Mithrandir stands within Thuringwath, Valley of the Secret Shadow","Examine the image of Balakhôr the Scourge conjured by your dreaming mind","Familiar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind.","Despite the comfortable accommodations given to you by Girhâzi, your sleep has been disturbed by strange dreams.","In your dream the Wizard Mithrandir stands before an unpleasant statue in the Valley of the Secret Shadow.","You are gripped with a sense of unreality as an unfamiliar land coalesces before your sleeping eyes.","The tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.","Talk to Mithrandir in your dream","'Where might Sigileth have gone, ${PLAYER}? She spoke of wishing to meet the Kinta Elves. Do you think she has gone to see Shanthar, the Elf-warden of Arwáth?'","An image from the darkest corner of the Morgul Vale swims from the recesses of your mind.","You expected your dreaming mind to bring you a vision of the grove of Arwáth, but it is not so. It seems the course of your dream is not so easily-controlled.","The unnatural flames barring the way into the tower room high within the Citadel of Winds have disappeared, granting you passage.","The hallway outside the tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.","Somehow, your unconscious mind knows this wraith to be the Nazgûl known in the annals of Gondor as the Grim Southron... but he and the others of his kind perished with Sauron.\
\
Is this a vision of the distant past, when the Nazgûl still lived?","'${PLAYER}! Have you seen Sigileth? I have been calling for her ever since she came this way, but she has not responded!\
\
'She will not turn back from this course!'","Examine the image of Mithrandir conjured by your dreaming mind","Examine the image of the Grim Southron conjured by your dreaming mind","Thuringwath swims hazily before your dreaming eyes.","Instancia: Más allá de la memoria viva","Listen to familiar voices conjured by your dreaming mind","Examine the scorpion conjured by your dreaming mind","Unfamiliar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind, of events you never could have seen."},
[6827]={"Willem está al sur del puente, en el reino de Rohan.","Bingo ha decidido cruzar el reino de Rohan a pie para evitar tener que montar un caballo.","'Soy Egwylf, y estoy en una misión urgente, pues el mensaje que llevo debe llegar a Stangard lo antes posible; no me detendré mucho, aunque parece que los cuatro compartimos el odio hacia los orcos y podríamos pasar un tiempo contando historias.'\
\
Te presentas a ti y a tus compañeros, y Egwylf examina a Bingo con atención.","Habla con Willem al otro lado del puente","Bingo está listo para cruzar al reino de Rohan.","'Egwylf dijo que había pueblos no muy lejos de aquí. ¡Encontrémos uno y continuemos nuestro viaje... a pie!'","Habla con Bingo junto al puente hacia Rohan","Willem te mira con indiferencia, como diciendo: '¿Qué te tomó tanto tiempo?'\
\
De pronto, sus orejas se mueven y tú también oyes voces guturales. ¡Orcos se acercan desde el sur!","Habla con Egwylf","Habla con Bingo","Has conocido a una mujer llamada Egwylf justo dentro de los límites de Rohan, y está muy interesada en las aventuras de tu pequeño grupo.","'¡Un paseo nos hará bien a ambos, ! No necesitamos montar caballos en Rohan. Nuestros pies servirán perfectamente. Si no me crees, ¡camina conmigo y verás!\
\
'¡Te sorprenderá lo rápido que pasa el tiempo una vez que volvamos a movernos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! ¿Quién necesita caballos?'","'Parecía muy agradable, pero creo que Egwylf está equivocada sobre la necesidad de montar un caballo en Rohan. Me las he arreglado bastante bien hasta ahora, ¿no es así? Y no habríamos apreciado tanto ese puente si hubiéramos pasado al galope o al trote, ¿verdad?\
\
'No, no lo habríamos hecho.'","Escucha lo que Egwylf tiene que decir sobre Rohan","Bingo está al sur del puente, en el reino de Rohan.","Una mujer de Rohan ha llegado galopando por el camino, impresionada por tu victoria sobre la partida de saqueo orca.","Instancia: La carga de Bingo"},
[6828]={"El bandido moribundo reveló que los Montebruno estaban siendo pagados tanto por alguien del sur como por agentes de Angmar. Cuando intentó reformar la banda sin lealtad a ninguno de los dos, el Enano Pálido lo abatió. Deberías hablar con el Condestable Sotomonte sobre esto.","'No podrías haber llegado un momento antes, ¿podrías? ¿Antes de que ese Enano me atravesara? Bueno, supongo que así es la vida.\
\
'Primero fue ese Éogan, diciendo que si jurábamos lealtad a Angmar, nos harían ricos. Bueno, cuando todo eso se vino abajo, algunos de nosotros decidimos que no queríamos nada que ver con Angmar. Empezamos a hablar con unos nuevos tipos, hombres que venían del sur. Eran un grupo feo, pero al menos no parecían propensos a invocar espíritus malignos o algo así sobre nosotros.\
\
'Parece que Angmar no le gustó la perspectiva... de que los dejáramos. Ese... ese Enano apareció, y ya ves cómo terminó eso. Ahora, supongo que los Montebruno están en... su final....'","Habla con el Condestable Sotomonte","Habla con el bandido","En una de las cámaras más profundas del escondite de los Montebruno, encontraste al misterioso Enano amenazando a un bandido. El Enano hirió gravemente al bandido, luego huyó, ordenando a sus enanos que te atacaran.\
\
Condestable Sotomonte te ha pedido que hables con el bandido herido.","'¡Santo cielo, este lugar es silencioso como una tumba! Ojalá pudiéramos decir que todo está en paz y marcharnos, pero supongo que tenemos que hacerlo mejor que eso.\
\
'De acuerdo, no sirve de nada posponer lo que hay que hacer. ¡Vamos! Y asegúrate de tener tu espada preparada, por si nos encontramos con algún problema.'","Instancia: Montebruno Debilitados","'Es mejor que abandonemos este lugar'","El Condestable Sotomonte viajó contigo hasta el escondite en una cueva de William Zorrillero, el antiguo líder de los Montebruno en la zona de Combe. Zorrillero está muerto, al igual que muchos otros bandidos, pero debes estar seguro de que no han empezado a reunir sus fuerzas de nuevo.","Has protegido al Condestable Sotomonte","'Bueno, parece que ese extraño Enano escapó. ¡Cómo salió de aquí es un misterio para mí! Y por lo que dijiste de la historia de ese bandido, ese Enano era el que debería preocuparnos, ¡no estos Montebruno!\
\
'Bueno, supongo que los Montebruno están realmente rotos ahora... ¡pero por alguna razón aún no me siento seguro! Bueno, no hay mucho más que podamos hacer aquí. Será mejor que lleves noticias a tu amigo Montaraz en Bree'","Has viajado con el Condestable Sotomonte de Combe a la cueva que los Montebruno utilizaron una vez como escondite."},
[6834]={"Talk to Herion","Erchar can be found in Linhir.\
\
Erchar is fighting against the invaders in Linhir. You should aid him.","Garvir can be found on the ledge above the Gilrain.\
\
You have found Garvir and should aid him before defeating the invaders.","<rgb=#FF0000>Herion must not be defeated</rgb>","Listen to the captain's report","Defend Linhir with Erchar","Aid Erchar in searching for Herion in Linhir","Defeat the Haradrim war-master and his men","Erchar can be found in Linhir.\
\
Erchar is searching for Herion in Linhir. You should follow him.","'They are upon us, ${PLAYER}. We have held them thus far, but our lines are weakening.\
\
'Swiftly now, we must defend the gates!'","The Corsairs and Haradrim make ready once more for battle at Linhir as the Heirs of Castamir seek to avenge their fallen.","'Curse that man! Curse him and all of his inbred men!\
\
'I shall see him slain, ${PLAYER}. I swear this above all else!'","The Haradrim war-master can be found near the ledge overlooking the Gilrain.\
\
Garvir has been killed by one of the Heirs of Castamir, who called his forces away. You should defeat the remaining men.","Instancia: Sangre por Sangre","'Brother! I am glad you both have come.\
\
'Garvir and I were separated by a sudden rush of Haradrim through the east-gate. I was pushed back, and now all my men have fallen.\
\
'I will not see him fight alone - we must reach him!'","DNT","Aid Garvir and defeat the invaders from Lebennin","You have prevailed, but at great cost...","Fight through Linhir with Erchar and Herion to aid Garvir","'It is a sorry day, ${PLAYER}. Let us tend to those we lost...'","<rgb=#FF0000>Herion has been defeated!</rgb>","Erchar can be found in Linhir.\
\
You have broken the first assault and should now speak to Erchar.","Erchar can be found in central Linhir.\
\
You have defeated the invaders and beaten back the attack, but at great cost. You should speak to Erchar.","Erchar and Herion can be found in central Linhir.\
\
Erchar and Herion are fighting their way through Linhir to reach Garvir.","<rgb=#FF0000>Erchar has been defeated!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Erchar must not be defeated</rgb>","'I think we have halted their assault, at least for the moment. My men here shall hold the line should they return.\
\
'We must go to Herion's aid at once.'","Erchar can be found in Linhir.\
\
The Corsairs and Haradrim are attacking Linhir. You should speak to Erchar and defend the city.","The captain can be found in Linhir.\
\
Erchar is speaking with one of his captains. You should listen to the captain's report.","Herion can be found in central Linhir, overlooking the Gilrain.\
\
You have found Herion amidst the battle and should now speak to him.","Talk to Erchar"},
[6835]={"Thromur and Shálun can be found at Amdân.\
\
Shálun has told his tale of the defeat of Urro at Mount Gundabad, but Thromur has suddenly interjected. You should listen to Thromur and Shálun.","Sputtering with rage, Urro falls defeated and succumbs to Thorin's blows with the oaken shield!","Fight through the forest and search for Frerin","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have accompanied Thromur to confront Shálun. You should talk to Thromur.","After a tense moment, Shálun lets out a sorrowful sigh","Felled by Orkish arrows, Fundin seemingly met his end defending the vanguard's retreat","You discover Fundin slain in the woods beside Kheled-zâram","Follow Shálun and deliver Urro's hand to Frerin","Follow Thorin and aid Shálun in defeating Urro One-hand","After a long moment, Shálun produces Urro's hand from a small bag on his belt","Investigate the source of the glint","Follow Thromur and confront Shálun","Shálun points toward where he caught sight of the glint","Instancia: Lazos de Roble y Hierro","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should offer your reassurance to Thromur by agreeing about the symbolic importance of Urro's hand to Frerin and Durin's Folk.","Follow Shálun and aid Thorin","Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You should follow Thorin and aid Shálun in defeating Urro One-hand.","Shálun can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You should follow Shálun and aid Thorin.","Talk to Shálun","Urro turns to challenge Thorin!","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should follow Thromur and confront Shálun.","Defeat Urro One-hand","Shálun can be found at Azanulbizar.\
\
You have arrived to discover King Thráin's vanguard beset by Orcs. You should talk to Shálun.","'We have done it... but I don't even know your names, my friends.'\
\
You introduce yourself and Shálun. Amidst the battle around you, Thorin smiles slightly.\
\
'You have my thanks, Hermáth... and you also, Shálun. Your deeds this day will not be forgotten among the Zhélruka, nor shall they be among the Longbeards—that I promise to you!\
\
'Stay with Shálun, Hermáth. His eyes grow dark, and the comfort of a friend would do his spirit well.\
\
'As for me, I....'","'What has happened?! The vanguard is in retreat!\
\
'Come, we must find Frerin!'","As you approach, Shálun raises a single eyebrow appraisingly","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
Shálun insists that he played a vital role in Frerin's defeat of Urro at Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Thromur.","'Stay with... me... a moment, won't you?'","'You have... my thanks, but I did not... see you in the vanguard. Did my father send for you?'\
\
As Thorin tries to catch his breath, you explain that you came on another errand, but chose to aid the vanguard when you discovered what had befallen them.\
\
'If you and your Zhélruka friend had not arrived when you did, I... things may have gone differently. I am not defeated yet, though.\
\
'And Urro must pay for slaying my brother!'","<rgb=#FF00FF>Agree</rgb> with Thromur and try to convince Shálun to relinquish Urro's hand","Shálun can be found at Amdân.\
\
Shálun insists that he played a vital role in Frerin's defeat of Urro at Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Shálun.","Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have aided Thorin in defeating Urro One-hand. You should talk to Thorin quickly before tending to Shálun.","Pausing to look around for a moment, Thromur beckons you over","Examine the corpse of Fundin","You should search for what remains of King Thráin's vanguard.","Thromur can be found in the woods to the north-west of Durin's Stone.\
\
After pondering what to do next, Thromur has beckoned you over. You should talk to Thromur.","'I know not of what he speaks.\
\
'If there is more to this tale, I would hear it. And preferably before we come to blows!'","'Hermáth... is that you?'\
\
Shálun coughs and blood dribbles from his lip.\
\
'Is... Urro... slain? What... of the Longbeard... prince?'\
\
You tell Shálun that Thorin slew Urro and survived. Shálun smiles weakly.\
\
'I... told Thromur... I would... make it right. Didn't... I?'","'I... I did not mean for that. Nor did I wish for Frerin's death. I only wanted... no matter.\
\
'I will make this right, Thromur. I must!'","Stunned at Shálun's assertion, Thromur looks to you","Listen to Thromur and Shálun","Thorin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
Thorin has been wounded by Urro One-hand and lays injured. You should talk to Thorin and aid him if you might.","Talk to Thorin","Despite his injuries, Thorin has risen and hewn an oak branch from a nearby tree","Agree with Thromur and try to convince Shálun to relinquish Urro's hand","'Fundin was a friend of my master's....\
\
'From the looks of it, he was far from the only dwarf who fell in the vanguard's retreat. I fear for master Frerin, but I also fear for King Thráin and what remains of his vanguard.'\
\
Thromur glances at the ground, his eye pausing at a few spots.\
\
'There are many tracks leading to the south-east, and not all of them were made by dwarves. If the Orcs are in pursuit, we must aid the King and our kinsfolk before it is too late!'","'There he is, Hermáth.\
\
'Let us see what Shálun has to say for himself!'","Talk to Thromur","'No. I... we are too late. What have I done?'\
\
Shálun steadies himself.\
\
'To lose a son is a pain no father should bear... not once, and certainly not twice.'","Shálun can be found at Amdân.\
\
To your surprise, Shálun has produced Urro's hand. You should talk to Shálun.","Shálun can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have arrived to find King Thráin's vanguard in dire need of aid. The King is wounded and Frerin was slain by Urro One-hand.","Follow Thromur and find what remains of King Thráin's vanguard","After finding the corpse of Fundin, Thromur and Shálun are discussing what is to be done.","The glint can be found in the woods to the north-west of Durin's Stone.\
\
Shálun noticed a glint in the dark of the woods of Azanulbizar. You should investigate its source.","Thromur looks to you for reassurance","Shálun can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
Shálun aided Thorin, but was dealt a fatal blow by Urro One-hand. You should talk to Shálun.","Shálun can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should try to convince Shálun of the symbolic importance of Urro's hand to Frerin and Durin's Folk.","Thromur and Shálun have arrived at the woods to the north-west of Durin's Stone to aid the vanguard, but they are in retreat! You should fight through the forest and aid the vanguard as you continue the search for Frerin.","After King Thráin and his vanguard set out to assault the gates of Khazad-dûm, a sudden revelation threatens to raise tensions between the Longbeards and the Zhélruka at Amdân.","Shálun can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should travel with Shálun to deliver Urro's hand to Frerin.","Urro One-hand can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
Urro has mortally wounded Shálun. You should aid Thorin in defeating Urro One-hand.","'Oh, so now you want to hear what I have to say?'\
\
Shálun glances derisively at Thromur.\
\
'So long as you keep that one away from me, I'll tell you whatever you want.\
\
'I am no thief! Will you hear my tale?'"},
[6836]={"Make your way towards Borangos' inner sanctum in Nargroth.","Find a suitable place to hide","Stay hidden and let events transpire.","With the knowledge you now hold, you must speak to Isnír at once!","Borangos approaches!","Upon receiving the remnants of the ancient ward originally used to keep Borangos at bay, Isnír wishes for you to return to Nargroth in the hopes of learning more about the domain of Great Rogmul.","Find a suitable place to hide.","¡Te han descubierto!","Borangos will not notice you here","Make your way towards Borangos' inner sanctum in Nargroth","Instancia: Borangos el Horror","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave your hiding place!</rgb>","Stay hidden and let events transpire"},
[6837]={"Talk to Bósi, former leader of the Iron Garrison","Rúvaran's forces have been routed, and now Durin is eager to return to the work of breaking through the ice before Gundabad.","Durin, Prince of the Longbeards, and Ingór, Prince of the Zhélruka, have commanded their forces to break through the ice that blocks passage into Gundabad.","Talk to Durin on the landing outside Gundabad","Durin is eager to pass beyond the ice and into Gundabad.","'Prince Ingór ordered that I help break through the ice alongside these Longbeards, but even without that command I would do it. Let them see the Zhélruka hold true to their word.\
\
'Even now cracks begin to form deep in the ice! We will soon be through!'","'Put your back into it, fellows! This unnatural ice cannot keep us from our goal, and it will not!\
\
'Already I hear the ice cracking, ${PLAYER}! It will not be long before we are through!'","'This is it, ${PLAYER}. Nothing stands in our way.\
\
'Let us climb the rest of the way and pass into Gundabad, the Mountain-home of my people!'","Talk to Prince Ingór at the ice outside Gundabad","Talk to Durin inside Gundabad","Talk to Durin outside the gates of Gundabad","Talk to Venko of the Zhélruka","'I ordered some of my own fellows to bring up torches, and with their help we will weaken this ice. Have I not personally seen strong metal bend and twist in the forges of the Heart of Fire? I have, ${PLAYER}. So too will it be here.\
\
'This may be a dragon's ice, but it is ice all the same.'","Prince Ingór desires to wield a sword, not a pick-axe, in service of the effort to gain entrance to Gundabad.","Durin stands on the landing before the gates of Gundabad, eager to pass into the Mountain-home.","'I daresay we won't see him again, but if we do he will regret it. Let Ingór keep watch for him. You and I will return to the ice and help as we may.'","Follow Durin","The gates of Gundabad lie before you, atop the stairs.","Climb the stairs and pass through the gates into Gundabad","At long last, Durin has entered the Mountain-home.","'This way, my friend. See how my dwarves labour at the ice? Nothing stands long before my people when they set their minds and muscles to overcoming it!'","Habla con Durin","Talk to Stóthkell, forge-master of the Iron Garrison","<rgb=#FF0000>Durin and Ingór must not be defeated!</rgb>","Durin wishes to observe the progress made by the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ outside the gates of Gundabad.","Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ work to break through the ice that blocks passage into Gundabad.","Talk to Imák the Stout-axe","'I can hardly believe it, ${PLAYER}, and yet here we stand.\
\
'Gundabad at last!'","'I toiled long in Mordor, ${PLAYER}, but this is not the same.\
\
'It is much colder up here.'","'My folk toil no less than Durin's Longbeards, and I beam with pride to hear no complaint! But my skill is with the sword and not with the pick-axe. There must be another way I can aid this effort.'\
\
The Zhélruka prince falls silent, listening closely.\
\
'Do you hear that, ${PLAYER}? Our foes deliver just such a use for my talents!'","'There is much to be done.'","Instancia: Abriéndose paso","Durin has fallen!"},
[6839]={"Examine the corpse of Bregmor","'Blast! Someone was here before us?! The look on your face tells me much. You seek the one who beat you here.'","Experience the vision","Another vision presents itself","Experience the vision.","Examine the rust spot.","Examine the corpse of Bregmor.","Fotri will lead you to the dragon Bregmor's corpse.","The strange vision disperses","There can be no doubt: some of the dragon's bones are not here","Examine the rust spot","Instancia: El legado de Bregmor"},
[6840]={"Instancia: La alianza rota","Bandidos derrotados en la cueva de los bandidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los bandidos y Orcos en la cueva.","Derrota a los bandidos en la cueva de los bandidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has encontrado la cueva. Ahora solo queda entrar, dispersar a los bandidos y Orcos, y derrotar a sus líderes."},
[6841]={"'What is this, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Robbo told you to do this? Bah, he should know better! Thank you, but we simply do not have time for outfit changes now!\
\
'In fact, we have only moments before we are expected on stage!\
\
'${PLAYER}, I know this would be asking a great deal, but would you go on stage and keep the crowd entertained while we finish preparing?\
\
'You could tell a story, dance a bit if you're feeling daring, or figure out something else! Hurry on!'","Habla con Robbo Moliespalda","Stand at the front of the stage in the Blue Theatre","This does not appear to be the outfit Robbo described...","Deliver the outfit to Polla Stoutley","'That was wonderful! Let us talk more off-stage.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Dance</rgb> for the audience","'Do not worry, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Even if they grew tired of your act, which I am certain they did not, you gave us more than enough time to prepare!\
\
'Make your way out to a seat in the audience, and we'll start our show!\
\
'Thank you again!'","Watch the Cloudyheads perform in the Blue Theatre","You have found the outfit and should now show it to Polla!","The Cloudyheads have negotiated a performance in the legendary Blue Theatre of Minas Tirith, but now they must think on how best to utilise the theatre's grand scale.","Talk to Polla Stoutley","The Cloudyheads are on stage in the Blue Theatre.\
\
The Cloudyheads are performing, so you should enjoy the show!","Search for the ornate outfit that Robbo described","The stage can be reached by passing through the short halls behind the stage in the Blue Theatre.\
\
Polla has asked you to stall for time as the Cloudyheads finish preparing for their performance. You should try the things she suggested to keep the audience entertained.","Polla Stoutley can be found behind the stage inside the Blue Theatre.\
\
You have tried to keep the audience entertained with varying degrees of success and should now return to Polla.","The audience seems enthralled by your tale!","Robbo Gristback can be found behind the stage in the Blue Theatre.\
\
You have arrived at the Blue Theatre and should now help the Cloudyheads prepare for their performance.","Various outfits can be found in the halls behind the stage inside the Blue Theatre.\
\
Robbo mentioned seeing an outfit in the halls behind the stage. You should search for the most ornate one you can find.","You have reached the front of the stage and should now entertain the audience!","Tell a <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> to the audience","Polla Stoutley can be found on the stage in the Blue Theatre.\
\
You have watched the Cloudyheads' performance and should now congratulate Polla and the others.","The audience seems to be tiring of your act...","'I am beyond words, ${PLAYER}! They loved us!\
\
'Góthrik was even in the audience... did you see?\
\
'Allow me a few moments to gather myself and then we can talk further! Oh, thank you!'","The audience applauds softly...","Perform a <rgb=#FF0000>handstand</rgb> for the audience","'Hallo again, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'We do not have much time now, but I saw a lovely outfit in the halls back here that Polla might love. Would you mind looking for it?\
\
'It's a very ornate dress! You'll know it right away, I swear it.\
\
'Bring it to her if you find it, and then we can get on stage!'","Polla Stoutley can be found behind the stage in the Blue Theatre.\
\
You have found the outfit Robbo described and should now bring it to Polla.","Instancia: Ajetreo en el Teatro Azul"},
[6842]={"Make your way to the upper levels of Narchost.\
<rgb=#FF0000>Do not be seen by any of your foes!</rgb>","The Rangers move quickly, eager to be done with this evil place","Eager to learn the Enemy's secrets to help Aragorn and the Host of the West, Faeron wants to enter Narchost.","Talk to Faeron inside Narchost","Faeron has returned from scouting the ridge.","Talk to Mincham on the rocky slope","Talk to Mincham inside Narchost","Sounds below you in the tower signal the return of the Orcs","The smell of the burning herbs is most foul","'I would not have been able to forgive myself if we let this chance pass untaken, ${PLAYER}, but now that we are inside my resolve wavers. Let us learn what we can and then depart!\
\
'If there are any secrets to be found that will be of value to Aragorn, they will be on the upper levels of the tower. We must make our way upwards, but do not be seen by any of the guards that still lurk within! It is important that our passage remains unnoticed!\
\
'Mincham and I will follow in the shadows. You must find a way to reach the upper levels of the tower without being seen! Do not approach the guards or we will all be imperiled!'","Eavesdrop on the conversation without being seen","'We have picked our way across the tumbled stones and parched dust of Dagorlad, but all we have found is an inhospitable land. None live here, for what man could? The Orcs keep watch on this place, for it lies on the border of their master's fell country.\
\
'Faeron has gone ahead to see what lies beyond the ridge. When he returns, we will turn back and tell Aragorn what we have seen: a dead land, watched by his enemies, through which we must pass nonetheless.'","'We have to get out of here!'","An acrid stench fills the air, offending your senses","You have crossed the noxious plains of Dagorlad with the Rangers Faeron and Mincham, scouting the lands through which Aragorn's host must pass.","You have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.","Follow Faeron to Narchost","The entrance to Narchost is temporarily unguarded.","You have overheard a conversation between Khôgath the Render and his minion Fulak, but it is not safe to linger within Narchost.","Talk to Faeron on the rocky slope","Mincham is ahead of you on the rocky slope.","The herbs burn with a terrible smell","'I hear foul mutterings ahead, ${PLAYER}, and know them for what they must be: the vile Black Speech used by the creatures of Mordor. It is a language I have learned to understand, though the study pained my ears and my heart both.\
\
'Let us move closer and I will try to translate the words for you and Faeron. Remain still out of sight! We must not be noticed, or I fear we will not leave this tower alive!'","Enter Narchost and remain alert","Instancia: Por pasos secretos","'Mincham's study of that foul language has borne fruit, ${PLAYER}, and we have learned what we can: the armies of Mordor have orders to allow Aragorn to come to the gate! What terrible fate does the Enemy have in mind for the Host of the West?\
\
'I hope Aragorn finds this knowledge useful, but now we need to escape from this place and return to his camp. We can no longer stay here!'","'From the top of the ridge I could see a good distance, and I marked the movement of many Orcs crawling hither and yon across the plain. But near at hand, a great tower rises from the rocks and spies the approach. I know the place from Aragorn's maps: it is Narchost, one of the Towers of the Teeth.\
\
'As I watched, a door in the tower opened and a great patrol of Orcs marched out on some mission. They made for Mordor, but if we hurry we might be able to enter the tower before they return. We might learn something of value for Aragorn, but we must seize this chance while we have it!\
\
'Once the Orcs return the opportunity will be lost! Hurry!'"},
[6843]={"Glorfindel has spotted enemies ahead.","Inkanûsh and Glorfindel have come to speak with Cúridwan, but as the sun sets upon Imhûlar they are not the only visitors to Kûgrun.","Instancia: Llamando a Cúridwan","You hear someone moving around behind the house!","Listen to the conversation between the Wizard, the Elf, and the hermit in Kûgrun.","Pass through the vines and enter Kûgrun","Talk to Glorfindel on the slope that rises to Kûgrun","Learn from Usakâr what has happened to Cúridwan","The disturbed vines reveal that some of the Orcs have already entered Kûgrun.","Someone hid from the Orcs behind Cúridwan's dwelling.","'It is true. That was my favourite hat, but Luhum-gêna kept stealing it right off my head. Not only that, but no matter how often I think she is slain, Luhum-gêna somehow keeps coming back. Eventually I decided to just let her keep it.'","Inkanûsh stands outside the entrance to Cúridwan's home of Kûgrun.","Usakâr the Hermit may know what happened to Cúridwan.","'I fear some of the Orcs may have already passed into Kûgrun. Even now the life of Cúridwan may be in jeopardy!\
\
'Glorfindel and I will ensure it is safe out here, and we will join you within when we can. Go now, and hurry!'","Orcs and jackals have come to threaten Cúridwan, and must be cleared from Kûgrun.","Listen to the conversation in Kûgrun","Talk to the one who hid from the Orcs behind Cúridwan's dwelling","'There are Orcs on the slope above us. I think they remain unaware of our presence, which grants to us the advantage. Shall we put an end to their menace?'","Talk to Inkanûsh outside the entrance to Cúridwan's home of Kûgrun","'I cannot say for certain, but when last we spoke Cúridwan had crafted a salve that could help fight against the Lâg Dávrit, the blight tainting the woods hereabout. She expressed a desire to bring it not only to the grove here in Imhûlar, but also to those further east, in Adagím. \\qI must do this, Usakâr,\\q she said to me. \\qWhat is the hurry?\\q I responded, but there must have been some need for haste after all.\
\
'She has always been a friend to the Kintai, and if she possesses a means of curing their dying forest, she would share it without question. She has a big heart, our Cúridwan. Often she speaks of her purpose in these lands: to heal them, and to fortify them against evil.\
\
'She would not appreciate these Orcs in her home, I know that! She must have gone already to Adagím, and missed their arrival entirely!'","Talk to Usakâr the Hermit in Kûgrun","'You are not an Orc, are you? No, you are not. That is a relief to me! It must be a relief to you as well, yes?\
\
'If you are here to dine with Cúridwan, as I am, I must tell you that she is no longer here. Luhum-gêna was quite disappointed to learn of our friend's absence, as was I, but perhaps it is just as well. Neither of us expected the Orcs to find the hidden way into Kûgrun! Someone with more in the way of brains must have helped them find it, but they are not welcome.'","Orcs and jackals have come to threaten Cúridwan, and must be cleared from Kûgrun!","Inkanûsh and Glorfindel have come to Kûgrun in search of Cúridwan.","Defeat all the Orcs and jackals threatening Kûgrun"},
[6845]={"Observe the feast in the Mead Hall of Stoke.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}...go fetch some water from the table over there.'","You should speak with Reeve Fríthild.","Thane Ordlac is kneeling beside Reeve Fríthild.\
\
You should bring the water to Thane Ordlac.","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","You should speak with Thane Ordlac.","Collected mug of water","Reeve Fríthild has collapsed","Talk to Thane Ordlac","A mug of water sits on one of the tables below the dais.\
\
Thane Ordlac instructed you to fetch a cup of water.","Collect mug of water","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I am pleased that you were able to join us for this feast. While I remain uneasy about the outcome, I find that I am able to -- for the moment -- put aside my worries. You and Ordlac have my gratitude for this respite.\
\
'Please, join the festivities!'","'Take the children from here and summon someone to care for Fríthild's body.'","'Alas, my friend, it is too late. Fríthild has gone from us. Fríthbert is now Reeve of the Broadacres....'","Instance: Celebration of Victory","Observe the festivities in the Mead Hall of Stoke","You have joined Reeve Fríthild and her guests in the Mead Hall of Stoke for a feast celebrating the victory at Bardh-dorám.","Bring the water to Thane Ordlac"},
[6846]={"One of the Nine known to mortals as The Gloom of Nurn has emerged to answer your challenge at the gates of Dol Guldur. You and your allies must gather all of your strength if you have any hope of defeating him and his forces.","'You have completed the battle at the gate!'","Instance: Challenge at the Gate","Defeat the Gloom of Nurn and his forces before the gates of Dol Guldur.","Defeated the Gloom of Nurn","Derrota a la Languidez de Nurn","Are you prepared to leave the field of battle?","Return to the Stone of Challenge"},
[6847]={"Defeated wights in Plas-maru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated the wight-captain","Defeat the wight-captain","Naeglanc has sent you to uncover what is happening in Plas-maru.","Defeat wights in Plas-maru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat the wights that have arisen within the great cairn of Plas-maru.","Instance: Clear the Path"},
[6848]={"The Weeping Warrior has arrived at last","Wait by the flat stone for Karazgar to arrive and claim his prize","Instancia: Cerrando el libro","Karazgar has come to meet with you at the Old Ford.","Answer Karazgar","You have decided to deliver the Black Book of Mordor to Karazgar, as he requested.","Place the Black Book of Mordor on the flat stone","'I see you have brought the tome with you, ${PLAYER}. Do you intend to honour our agreement?'\
\
You tell Karazgar that you will give him the Black Book of Mordor, and he smiles.\
\
'I am pleased you were willing to listen to reason, ${RACE}.'","Karazgar has agreed to your conditions, and waits for you to set the Black Book on the flat stone.","Give Karazgar your conditions","Karazgar has taken the Black Book of Mordor.","You have chosen to deliver the Black Book of Mordor to Karazgar, and should wait by the flat stone in the Old Ford until he arrives to claim his prize.","Karazgar waits to hear your conditions.","Talk to Karazgar at the Old Ford","Mantente en guardia","'Give to me this artifact and I will leave you be.'\
\
Karazgar holds out his hand, and when you do not immediately give him the Black Book he scowls.\
\
'Why do you hesitate? You risk the wrath of Karazgar, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You tell him the Book is not without cost, and there are conditions attached to this gift.","Karazgar has asked you a question, and awaits your response."},
[6849]={"Talk to Gléowine outside Meduseld","Instancia: Órdenes del Rey","'Do you hear how desperately he wishes to be relieved of this charge? If that plea does not excuse Gríma from war, I can think of no other that will. I would not trust him to carry a sack of grain into the mountains, for fear he would steal either the sack or its contents, whichever he thought we would desire more!\
\
'My uncle is no fool. He will not humour this request.'","'Théoden King has gone ahead with Gandalf, ${PLAYER}. Do you think he has forgiven us? I know in my heart we returned for the good of the kingdom, but it is a serious crime to disobey the word of a king!\
\
'My heart is a-flutter, friend.'","Talk to Gríma outside Meduseld","Gandalf is outside Meduseld, speaking words of wisdom to Théoden.","'Gléowine still believes we will be punished, but my mind is not troubled. We returned to Théoden at the right moment for forgiveness. Was Gandalf not sent away with equal force? And yet now he has the ear of the king, and speaks wisdom to him.\
\
'We return without the insight of the Wizard, but we bring something valuable all the same: warning of Saruman's reach and power. That warning too has value to the king, and when he chooses his course he will weigh what we have to say alongside the words of his advisors.'","'The air is fresh and clean, ${PLAYER}, and the tall grasses sway in the breeze. From here we can look out over the fields of Rohan. See how the sunlight dances upon that distant river?\
\
'It has been some days since Théoden beheld his own lands, I warrant. Gríma gave him report of them, but always in such a way as to advance his own ends, and those of Saruman his master.'","'Now we will hear the commands of Théoden, and learn if we have truly come to him in time. Rohan stands at a crossroad, and it is up to her King to choose the correct course. We will help him choose aright, to the sorrow of Saruman!\
\
'It is not magic that Gandalf uses to cure Théoden of the hurts that Saruman and his agent Gríma have wrought. No, our wise friend seeks to cure Théoden with words: words of friendship and hope. Already I see it working.'","Talk to Gandalf outside Meduseld","Horn is outside Meduseld, waiting to speak with you.","Gríma has been brought out of Meduseld and awaits the King's judgement.","Stand with Théoden and hear the commands of the king","Gríma has asked to be named steward of Meduseld in Théoden's absence.","'I have long known there was strength still in this land, and in its king. Théoden's decisions on this day are not a surprise to me, and they should not have been surprising to you either, ${PLAYER}.'","Gríma hisses at you, his eyes narrowed unpleasantly.\
\
'Do not disturb my lord more than you have already! He is weary, and needs his rest. Only when you and your irksome friends leave his lands will he be once again at peace.'","Gríma's eyes dart back and forth from face to face, sizing up the assemblage.\
\
'My lord, can you not see what this Wizard and his ragged band seek to achieve? They do not care for your health or for your safety, and seek to lead you into danger. Your death would grieve them little, but there are those close to you who would mourn even the smallest hurt to your person.\
\
'Listen to Gríma, and come back inside. Abandon the madness these cruel ones have instilled in your mind. Let me send them away. Speak not of war! That is a young man's endeavor, and you have ruled the Mark for many seasons. Will you not listen to your faithful Gríma? Send me not away!'","Talk to Aragorn outside Meduseld","Gléowine is outside Meduseld, worrying.","Théoden has emerged from the Golden Hall to look out over his kingdom, and to issue the commands necessary for its survival.","'Enough! Gríma succeeds again, if not at his truest goal then still at one of value to his master. For Saruman is his master, and every hour we delay plays into his hands. We can spare no more time on him.'","Talk to Éomer outside Meduseld","Aragorn is outside Meduseld, waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Horn outside Meduseld","Théoden stands atop the steps outside Meduseld, gazing out upon his lands."},
[6850]={"Defeat Dravron and his brigands.","Talk to Dervorin","You set out with Dervorin to confront Dravron.","Approach Dravron","Instancia: Enfrentando a Dravron","Regroup with Dervorin and the workers","Listen to Dervorin and Dravron's conversation.","Listen to Dervorin and Dravron","Dravron attacks!","La lucha ha terminado.\
\
Reagrúpate con los demás.","'Once we acquire Dravron's ledger, we will be able to prove his misdoings. As acting Lord of the Vale, it is my right to demand it, so I do not anticipate any trouble, but if he should choose to make trouble, I hope you are prepared to fight.\
\
'Are you ready to go?'","Talk to Dervorin before the negotiation begins.","<rgb=#FF0000>Dervorin has been defeated!</rgb>","Dervorin sighs.\
\
'I have a long day ahead of me.'","'${PLAYER}, I did not think I would be fighting alongside you so soon. As dire as our situation was during the war, I preferred crossing blades with vicious Orcs than my own countrymen twisted by greed and delusions of grandeur, but there is no time to dwell on these things.\
\
'We must summon the guard and the healers, and I must determine how to proceed with the operation of this lumber camp.\
\
'Given Dravron's outrageous actions, I have all the justification I need to strip the land from his possession.'","Approach Dravron."},
[6852]={"Defeated Head Servant Sintáhi","Thothril the Entangler has begun to take over the minds of the servants in the palace.\
\
You should talk to Razâl.","Defeat maddening illusions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated maddening illusions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have arrived inside the servant's living quarters of the palace.\
\
You should investigate the area.","'That seems to be everyone who is still sane. We must now deal with the head servant. She seemed practically fanatical in her devotion to Thothril, and will only drive others to madness if she is left alive. Let's end this and get out of here.'","You have arrived inside the servant's living quarters of the palace.\
\
You should talk to Razâl.","Instancia: Locura devoradora","'Thothril the Entangler has already begun driving these people mad! We need to save who we can, and fast! However, I fear some of them may be too far gone to save....'","As the palace of Emax Dûl succumbs to the control of Thothril the Entangler, many civilians have become trapped. It is our duty to free them before they are driven to madness.","You have defeated Thothril's illusions and saved who you can.\
\
You should talk to Razâl.","'We have arrived unseen! Now, we need to assess the servants' condition here. I just hope we are not too late!'","'It is done. Let's get back to Nashûbu.'","All that is left to do is to defeat the head servant before she can convert others to Thothril's cause.\
\
You should defeat Head Servant Sintáhi.","Investigate the servants' quarters","Talk to Razâl","Defeat Head Servant Sintáhi","Thothril the Entangler has begun to take over the minds of the servants in the palace.\
\
You should defeat the maddening illusions to save those whose minds are still intact."},
[6853]={"'See yonder waterfall? The mad man's journal says that behind it lies the entrance to a cave. It is from here that the sarrowstones are harvested. This is the source of the corruption, friend! I would come to help you, but as you know, I am useless with weapons. I shall be right behind you, however! Good luck!\
\
'Ah, I nearly forgot! Take the candle with you! The journal says that by its light, the way shall be revealed.'","'Well done, friend! And these bones! Amazing! Ancient and seemingly the source of the corruption.\
\
'I shall stay on a while longer to study these bones. Go now, and tell Mother Amma that Praushod and Bruidalg have been defeated.'","La cascada está en el este de Clovengap.\
\
Rúni el Sabio cree que hay una cueva oculta tras la cascada cercana. Debes encontrar la cueva.","The source of the corruption is deep in the Min Návaid cave in Clovengap.\
\
You should uncover the source of the corrupted sarrowstones and put an end for good to the terrible experiments of Bruidalg the Bloodletter.","'Do not worry about me. I shall stay on a while longer to study these bones. Go now, and tell Mother Amma that Praushod and Bruidalg have been defeated.'","Instancia: La fuente de la corrupción","Investigate the dragon bones","Talk to Rúni","Find the secret tunnel","The secret tunnel is within the crystal cave, Min Návaid.\
\
The journal spoke of a secret tunnel whose entrance can be revealed by the light of the candle. With the Angmarim High Priest defeated, you should look for the secret tunnel.","Lore-master Rúni is in the crystal cave.\
\
You should tell Lore-master Rúni that the deed is done.","Defeated Praushod the Foetid","There is a cave behind the waterfall!","Praushod the Foetid lies deeper within Min Návaid.\
\
You should summon Praushod the Foetid by striking the corrupted crystals.","The dragon bones are in Min Návaid.\
\
Lore-master Rúni has asked you to investigate the cave for dragon bones.","Lore-master Rúni waits for you by the falls in western Clovengap.\
\
You should talk to Rúni.","Defeat Bruidalg the Bloodletter","The tunnel is revealed!","Deep in the ground, in crystal-laden, foetid pools, an ancient evil spreads corruption.","Defeated Bruidalg the Bloodletter","Find the crystal cave","'I shall be right behind you, friend! Well, probably more at a distance, really.'","Summon Praushod the Foetid"},
[6854]={"'Rest well, Hermáth. I shall see you in the morn!'","Dáin can be found at Amdân.\
\
After listening to Thráin's council with the Kings of the Seven Houses, Dáin has beckoned you. You should talk to Dáin.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Cheer</rgb> for Thráin","'I hope my father did not think me imprudent in my concern, Hermáth.\
\
'I could tell he, too, was displeased that the Iron-folk would be held in reserve, but a dwarf of his station would not dare say as much. At the very least, I seem to have amused our elders and some of the Kings!\
\
'I fear we have a long day ahead of us on the morrow, my friend. Let us sleep while we might!'","As you take your place beside Dáin, Thráin begins to speak","Such a rousing speech is worthy of a cheer!","Dáin can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should talk to Dáin.","Listen as Thrain addresses the Kings of the Seven Houses at Amdân","Dáin can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should accompany Dáin and join the gathering at Amdân.","'I think we're in luck, Hermáth.\
\
'It doesn't sound like it's started yet, but we'd better hurry over!'","Instancia: Concilio de los Siete","As Thráin and the others prepare to take rest, Dáin beckons you over","As the cheers fall quiet, Thráin begins the ordering of the Haban’akkâ","After coming to Azanulbizar at long last, King Thráin has called the Kings of the Seven Houses to council at Amdân.","Thrain is addressing the Kings of the Seven Houses at Amdân.","Talk to Dáin","Follow Dáin and join the gathering at Amdân","Thráin can be found at Amdân.\
\
You should cheer for Thráin."},
[6857]={"Habla con Elrond","Baradal needs to talk to you.\
\
You should talk to Baradal.","Talk to Baradal","Listen to the conversation","Ránulur has come to finish what he started.\
\
You should defeat Ránulur!","Despite our efforts, evil still lingers in the world. It has crawled into dark corners and deep places to hide from the light. I will not allow it to threaten one of our own. It will not hide from me anymore.","Elrond would like to speak with you about what has transpired.\
\
You should talk to Elrond.","Galadriel and Arwen are conversing.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","'Come, let us be on our way.'","'He is coming! I am injured, but I will do what I can. Stand behind me!'","Defeat Ránulur","'Being in this place rekindles the pain I felt at my wife's departure. But I will see Celebrían again in the Undying Lands; Arwen will not. I hope this has brought her some peace. She follows in my brother's footsteps, for the love of one of his line. My heart breaks and wells with pride all at once.\
\
'I must thank you for the part you played in this, ${PLAYER}. We were unaware such a powerful foe resided in these ruins, and Baradal might have perished had you not been here. Arwen would have blamed herself had that happened.\
\
'Baradal has been eager to prove herself. I fear she will consider this incident a failure and lose faith in her abilities. Many of those in her position would have seen their valour fail; reassure her of that, if you can. She is dear to our family, and I do not wish her to be mired in self-doubt.\
\
'I believe we are done here. Let us find a place to heal Baradal's injuries.'","Instancia: La llegada del alba"},
[6858]={"Listen to Barallas' tale at Enting Hollow","Instancia: Días pasados","'Hoom. And so, little one, my tale ends. \
\
'Let us speak of other things...'","Barallas wishes to tell you of times before the siege of Fangorn Forest and the scattering of the Ents.","Barallas' tale comes to a close","Barallas is recounting his tale of the Ents at the Enting Hollow in the Balewood.\
\
Barallas and the other Ents of the Balewood once stood united at the Enting Hollow before Núrzum came to Fangorn.","Talk to Barallas","'And so, little ${CLASS}, you have heard all I wish to say on these matters.\
\
'Let us return to Stonecliff... such an open space is a perilous place to remain....'","Barallas is standing at the Enting Hollow in the Balewood.\
\
Barallas has finished his tale of the Ents. You should speak with him before setting off.","Barallas is standing at the Enting Hollow in eastern Balewood.\
\
Barallas has chosen to tell you of times long past in Fangorn Forest, when the Ents still stood united.","'We have made it, ${PLAYER}. Hoom... this forest has become so unfamiliar to me since Núrzum returned.\
\
'Ah yes, he was here once before, little one, but then... he was different. What he gained in might, he lost in compassion for the creatures of this realm.\
\
'Let us walk, and I shall tell you more of Núrzum and the Men of these lands.'"},
[6859]={"Pick up the fallen banner where it fell from Guthláf's hand","Give the banner to Éomer, as Théoden requested","Théoden nods at you weakly, desiring to speak","'For glory and honour! Let us ride to Théoden King and make safe the fields before the city!'","Death has come to the Pelennor, and even kings cannot stand against it forever.","Théoden has asked you to give the banner to Éomer.","Permanece alerta","'I have come to the end... of my road... ${PLAYER}. But Rohan will go on...'\
\
Théoden nods weakly.\
\
'Pick up the banner... where it fell... and give it to Éomer. He must lead now...'","Talk to Théoden","Guthláf is on the fields of the Pelennor, ready to ride as his king commands.","Guard Théoden during his last moments","Éomer silently takes the banner from you and lifts it to the sky.","The Riders of Rohan have joined the battle, but on the fields of the Pelennor, great deeds go hand in hand with death.","Talk to Guthláf on the field of battle","Instancia: La muerte llega para todos","Théoden has come to the end of his road, but he has a final request of you.","Remain on guard as Éomer remembers the fallen.","The battle rages before the White City.","Théoden requested that you pick up the banner of Rohan where it fell, and give it to Éomer.","Ride with Guthláf and stand with the king"},
[6860]={"Instance: Death From Below","Speak with Vatnar and begin your counterattack against the goblin-sappers!","'Right then, let us hie ourselves from this stinking tunnel. We wouldn't want Rodelleth and her Elves getting lonesome for lack of our company, would we?'","Vatnar has detected a band of goblin-sappers digging a tunnel below the cellars of Thangúlhad. He and his brother Thyrnir intend to invade the goblin-tunnel and collapse it before they can undermine the tower's foundation.\
\
<rgb=#00ff00>WARNING: Death From Below is a high difficulty solo challenge quest. Beware, all who enter therein.</rgb>","¡Victoria!","Talk to Vatnar to return to the surface.","Talk to Vatnar","'Let us be upon our task, shall we?'","'Aye! That did it! Well fought, ${PLAYER}! The goblins' works are broken, and the remaining sappers seem to have run off.\
\
'It must have been that scowl of yours that did it....'"},
[6861]={"Sterkist is under attack!\
\
You should defeat Borzagor the Grisly!","Instance: Deep in the Darkening Wood","Deep within Mirkwood, an ancient enemy has returned. A Beorning trader is lost within a maze of trees and thorns, predators closing in around him. Find a way through, and save him before it is too late.","With Sterkist recovered, it is time to escape.\
\
You should talk to Thorlind.","'This place is like a maze! How do we proceed?'\
\
Langhár sniffs the air.\
\
'Ah, a familiar scent on the wind! Follow me, and stay close, lest you find yourself lost in these woods!'","Borzagor the Grisly is defeated","Habla con Langhár","Langhár went this way","'We have the Beorning. Now, we need to retreat, quickly! We will soon be swarmed by Taurogrim! I will have to return later with a stronger force.'","Langhár becomes a bear and follows the scent!","'Quickly, we must retreat!'","Langhár collapses!","Sterkist is somewhere within these woods.\
\
You should follow Langhár and find Sterkist.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Langhár must survive!</rgb>","Talk to Thorlind","You have arrived at the edge of a section of deep woods.\
\
You should talk to Langhár.","Find Sterkist","Defeat Borzagor the Grisly","Sterkist is in danger!","Langhár must survive!"},
[6862]={"You should talk to Pippin and find out what he thinks he has seen.","'Just look what I've found. Over there, between those rocks. Boot marks -- and they're too soft and narrow to be Orc-feet, by my reckoning.\
\
'Come, let us see where they lead!'","With that, the half-orc expires","Instancia: Más adentro","'If they have a bone of decency among the three of them, they will be standing upon a high rock again, talking loudly enough to hear and find them by.'","Habla con Merry","You should begin searching the area for signs of the three half-orcs.","Confront the half-orcs","Habla con Pippin","Talk to the dying half-orc","'This is near to the place Golodhon thought they should be. They are not standing out in plain view, at any rate! I suppose the only thing is to begin looking around for them, or signs of where they have gone.'","The half-orc who was struck by the troll has some life yet in him. You should speak to him now and see what you can learn.","Defeated enraged troll","Begin searching","'Poor fellow. He will not be dearly missed by anyone, I suppose, not even his craven comrades. I cannot say that I am satisfied, but I think we have done all we could this day. It is time we headed back.'","Stop to get your bearings","Defeat the enraged troll","Merry has brought your expedition to a stop. You should hear what he has to say.","You should follow the footprints that Pippin discovered and see where they lead.","An enraged troll has stumbled into the confrontation, knocking down one of the half-orcs and sending the other two fleeing. You must defend yourself against the troll!","You should resume searching the area for signs of the three half-orcs.","'Merry is right, of course. We are done with Mordor for now. Perhaps for good. Let us get going then, before anything else unpleasant can happen!'","'Bah! That's done me in, I know it. And you lot.  So you found some barrels in Isengard, did you? That isn't half of it. Ha ha. Ha ha ha ha....'\
\
He devolves into pained coughing for several moments.\
\
'There's plenty more where that came from, in your precious Shire. That land is good undefended, it is. Ripe for the plucking.'","You should talk to Pippin and Merry.","You have found the three half-orcs again!","You have returned with Merry and Pippin to Mordor, with the sole intent of finding the three suspicious half-orcs. The Ranger Golodhon has pointed you on the way to where he believes they ought to be.","Continue searching","Follow the footprints","You have found the three half-orcs again. Join Merry and Pippin and try to get some answers out of them.","'Those - those weren't answers. Those were riddles. Riddles that would drive even old Bilbo mad!'","The prints lead ever onward and upward","'¿Qué pasa, Pippin?'","You should continue searching the area for signs of the three half-orcs."},
[6863]={"Find Varthmath","Defeat Ormoth, the drake assault leader.","Protect the Carrock and defeat the attacking drakes.","The leader of the drake assault has arrived!","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. Luck would have it that I decided to enter Beorn's cave at the Carrock's base, precisely before these drakes attacked. A group entered the cave, but I fought them off. It would seem they tried to desecrate this sacred cave and the Carrock!'","The Carrock is under attack!","'We must tell Grimbeorn at once. He will be grateful to know that the Eagles gave you warning of this attack.'","Ormoth has fallen!","Talk to Anórohir","Find Varthmath.","Protect the Carrock and defeat the attacking drakes","'The drakes, they approach. I must take leave, for Lord Gwaihir has bade me not to interfere. I have faith in your skills, ${CLASS}. Farewell!'","Instancia: Defensa en la Carroca","Talk to Anórohir."},
[6864]={"Speak with Thrymm in the centre of Scylfig","Speak with Grimgar in the centre of Scylfig","Speak with Thrymm in front of the Mead Hall","'${PLAYER}, we must hurry! The Orcs have penetrated the wall and are now attacking villagers. Follow me up to the northern stables!'","'I don't know what I'll do without them...'","Follow Thrymm to the northern stables to fend off the White Hand attackers.","Help Thrymm fend off the White Hand attackers along the path leading to the Mead Hall.","A giant has breached the gate to Scylfig and is charging forth into the centre of town.","'Good work so far, ${PLAYER}. Our work is far from done though. Let's head to the centre of town to cut off the Orcs before they head towards the Mead Hall.'","'My brother and I have this area well defended. We will not allow anything to get past us. Wait... do you hear that sound? What is that? The gate, the sound is coming from the front gate!'","Follow Thrymm to the Mead Hall","Speak with Cyneberg","'This is not good. Grimgar and Humbald were defeated rather soundly by the giant. We must not let their defeat be in vain. You and I need to go protect the Mead Hall at once!'","Fend off the White Hand attackers at the northern stables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The giant, Núrzum has breached the gate and is now heading towards the Mead Hall. It needs to be defended at all costs.","Stand beside Thrymm and guard the Mead Hall","'${PLAYER}, whatever happens, you and Cyneberg must protect the Mead Hall. \
\
'Your assistance has proven valuable. Myself and all of Scylfig are thankful for your efforts.\
\
'I must do this myself. You and Cyneberg must not intervene.'","The southern stables have been secured, but the giant Núrzum has breached the gate. Speak with Thrymm to find out what to do next.","Garsig and Cynegar are now trying to head Núrzum off at the road before he gets to the Mead Hall.","The White Hand have already penetrated the perimeter of Scylfig and are attacking. Speak with Thrymm to find out the plan to defend Scylfig.","Follow Thrymm to the northern stables","Go to the Mead Hall and stand guard","The strange giant felled Grimgar and Humbald in a single blow","Cynegar and Garsig were the latest to perish at the hands of Núrzum.","The northern stables have been secured. Speak with Thrymm to find out where to head next.","Fend off the White Hand attackers along the path up to the Mead Hall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The giant, Núrzum, has hurled a gravely-wounded Thrymm far into the desolate lands of Wildermore, smothering hope and Scylfig beneath a harsh winter","More White Hand attackers rush forth to oppose you!","The giant, Núrzum charges forth towards the Mead Hall and is met there by Thrymm Red-beard. Observe the battle between the two warriors and ensure that no one gets into the Mead Hall.","Help Thrymm fend off the White Hand attackers!","Follow Thrymm to the centre of town","Speak with Thrymm","Follow Thrymm to the centre of Scylfig to defend against the White Hand attackers.","After defeating Thrymm, Núrzum turns and departs Scylfig. The women and children inside the Mead Hall appear to be safe.","Stand with Cyneberg and observe the battle between Thrymm and Núrzum","Gárwig's grandson, Grimgar, has been holding his own along with his brother, Humbald in the centre of town. Speak with him.","Núrzum's might easily overcomes Garsig and Cynegar","Speak with Thrymm at the northern stables","Fend off the White Hand attackers near the northern stables.","Fended off a White Hand attacker (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: Defensa de Scylfig","The attack the people of Scylfig feared is now upon the town. Villagers throughout Scylfig need protection from the White Hand, but ultimately, the Mead Hall must not be breached. Therein are the women and children of the town.","Grimgar and Humbald met an unfortunate fate while dealing with Núrzum. Speak with Thrymm to find out the next course of action.","'We've experienced much grief today, ${PLAYER}.'","Speak with Thrymm on the road leading up to the Mead Hall","Follow Thrymm up towards the Mead Hall to make sure nothing gets past.","Grimgar and his brother, Humbald have kept this area of Scylfig well-defended","'${PLAYER}, we must protect the Mead Hall at all costs! Come with me!'","Assist Thrymm in defeating any remaining Orcs in the centre of Scylfig"},
[6865]={"Ides can be found at the mill, north of the training grounds.\
\
Ides wishes to discuss her thoughts with you.","'I am eager to learn more from you, ${PLAYER}. I know it will not come easily, but I will become a shield-maiden, no matter the cost.\
\
'I am fortunate to have met someone with the same determination and will to do good that I see in myself... and in my father.'","Talk to Ides about Edwulf","'We have defeated the invaders! It is most fortunate that we were nearby... Edwulf's wounds are not fatal, and the damage to the camp will be quickly repaired.\
\
'These men owe us their lives, ${PLAYER}. We arrived just in time.'","Ides can be found along the road, west of the training grounds.\
\
Ides has spotted an Uruk, and will need your help to defeat it.","The Uruk-hai have been routed","The grunts of Uruks can be heard coming from the training grounds","Do not allow Ides to become defeated","'Edwulf has been wounded! It is not a fatal blow, but he will need someone to protect him.\
\
'This must be the work of the Uruks, ${PLAYER}! No doubt they are assailing the training grounds. Go and assail the Uruk-intruders, while I stay and watch over Edwulf.'","Talk to Ides","'I hear the faint roar of fighting coming from the training grounds. We had better investigate with haste.'","Ides can be found along the road, west of the training grounds.\
\
After defeating the Uruk-hai invaders, Ides awaits your return.","Ides can be found at the mill, north of the training grounds.\
\
Ides seems to have heard a noise and wishes to inquire about it.","Defeat the Uruk-hai warrior","Uruks have assaulted the Rohirrim training grounds.\
\
Ides has asked you to help deal with the attacking Uruk-hai.","Ides has asked you to walk with her and to listen as she expresses her thoughts.","Ides has been defeated","Defeated the Uruk-hai at the training grounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We must allow time for the men to recover and restore the camp.\
\
'Once again, I am honoured to be your student.'","Talk to Ides along the roadway","Defeat the Uruk-hai at the training grounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Ides along the road","Instance: Desire Above Strength","The sounds of combat can be heard to the south","Ides can be found at the forked path along the road, west of the training grounds.\
\
Ides has found Edwulf, injured in battle, and would like to discuss what should be done."},
[6866]={"Rescue the miners trapped by the collapsed shafts throughout the mine.","You have reached the mine exit in time!","¡Escapa de la mina antes de que se derrumbe!","Escape before the mine collapses","Hûzo asked that you enter the mine to free the workers trapped within.","Instancia: Cavar profundo","Your rescued the miners, but the mine is shaking violently. Make your way out of the mine.","Rescata a todos los mineros atrapados en Jid Phêsi (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","La mina se derrumbó","Rescued a miner at Jid Phêsi"},
[6867]={"Approach and listen to Shadowfax and his companion","Shadowfax awaits you on the border of the eastern fields of Rohan.","For centuries the Mearas have freely roamed the plains of Rohan, bowing only before the kings and princes of the Rohirrim.","'Welcome back, my brother. He who rides me, Gandalf, is right to say that you are a descendant of the Mearas. I summoned you here to remind you of your true home.\
\
'A darkness spreads over the lands. Soon, a time shall come when the herd will need to ride again. Return to us, when you are ready.'","Instancia: Descubriendo al Descendiente","Shadowfax is waiting for you here in the fields of Rohan. Shadowfax has led his companion here to wait for you, though the companion is not yet aware of why he came to this place."},
[6868]={"'¿Ninguna cueva? Oh, ${PLAYER}, creo que no tenemos opción después de todo. Esta tormenta antinatural es demasiado intensa, ¡y no podemos quedarnos aquí para seguir buscando! ¡Si queremos encontar a la montaña, tendremos que seguir a la Guarnición de Hierro! ¡No deseaba hacerlo, pero parece que será la única manera!\
\
'¡Tendríamos que bajar la montaña y poner en orden nuestras ideas antes de que podamos recuperar a nuestro hobbit!'","Spalvi está en lo alto del Paso del Cuerno Rojo, en medio de una terrible ventisca.","'Parece que tendremos que luchar, ${PLAYER}. Thóvarg no va a rendirse, ¡y no podremos luchar contra sus guerreros y la ventisca!'\
\
'¡Espero que puedas aguantar! ¡Sabe usar muy bien ese hacha que lleva!'","Escuchas voces traídas con el viento una vez más","Spalvi te ha pedido que te adentres en la ventisca y <rgb=#FF0000>mires</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>eches un vistazo</rgb> alrededor en busca de entradas a cuevas.","Spalvi y tú habéis subido a lo alto del Paso del Cuerno Rojo buscando algún acceso al interior de la montaña.","Sobrevive al enfrentamiento con el grupo de asalto Duramano","Spalvi y tú habéis sobrevivido al ataque de un grupo de asaltantes Duramano.","Habla con Spalvi en la ventisca","'Bueno, ¿a qué estás esperando? ¡Descendamos de esta gélida ladera antes de que termine con nosotros!'","Has subido a las montañas con Spalvi en busca de alguna cueva.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> o echa un <rgb=#FF0000>vistazo</rgb> en busca de entradas a cuevas en medio de la fuerte ventisca","Spalvi y tú habéis subido a lo alto del Paso del Cuerno Rojo buscando alguna forma de llegar a Bingo, pero ha aparecido un nuevo peligro: ¡un grupo de asalto de los Duramano!","'¡Mientras más alto subimos más difícil es, ${PLAYER}! ¡Intenta mantener los ojos abiertos para encontrar alguna cueva!\
\
'Creía que podríamos encontrar un camino hacia el interior de la montaña para buscar a Bingo, ¡pero si esto sigue así tendremos que encontrar una cueva para refugiarnos y sobrevivir!'","Thóvarg no va a retirarse, y Spalvi está deseando pelear.","La cara de Willem es inescrutable, pero crees que está bastante satisfecho consigo mismo.","'¡Thóvarg ya no me atormentará más, y tengo que darte las gracias por ello, ${PLAYER}! No solo a ti, supongo, ¡sino también a Willem Bigotes!\
\
'¡Ahora bajemos de esta montaña! Debemos tomar el único camino que tenemos ante nosotros. No quiero congelarme aquí arriba, ¡y esto seguro de que si no nos movemos pronto será así!'","No encuentras cuevas, pero escuchas voces traídas por el viento","Instancia: Caras Hurañas"},
[6869]={"Frithbéorth neglected to mention the rat infestation in the manor that he just sold to Cíllan for a hefty sum.\
\
You should defeat the rats that reside in the manor.","Instancia: Pago inicial","Cíllan just arrived in the new manor you just purchased for her in Harwick.\
\
You should hasten to Cíllan to hand her the keys and tell her of the deal with Frithbéorth...and it would be wise to mention the rats as well.","Return to Cíllan at the door of her new manor","Defeat rats in the refugees' new home (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The house in harwick you purchased for Cíllan has unwanted occupants...","'We have a bit of tidying up to do here, and a few things to move in from the refugee-camp. Please come back to visit us soon.'","Investigate the old manor to ensure that the refugees may move in","The old home of Frithbald, father to Frithbéorth, is located in the north-east corner of Harwick.\
\
You should investigate the house before the refugees begin to move in.","Defeated rats in the refugees' new home (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You hand Cíllan the keys to the manor","The old manor is infested with rats","'Oh, my... this manor is not in the condition I was expecting, but it will do just fine, with a little work.'"},
[6870]={"Bori ha sido escoltado a un lugar seguro","'Hemos logrado entrar en las mazmorras, ${PLAYER}, y ahora depende de ti encontrar y rescatar a Bori. Creemos que lo tienen en una celda del ala este.\
\
'Hemos conseguido mantener nuestra infiltración en silencio hasta ahora, y algunos de los guardias del ala este pueden estar dormidos en su trabajo. ¡Déjalos dormir y rescata a Bori!'","'¡Liberémonos de estas mazmorras! Estoy listo para ver el sol de nuevo, o al menos tanto del sol como se pueda ver bajo los árboles del Bosque Negro.'","Encuentra a Bori y habla con él","Has entrado en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur en busca del prisionero Bori con un pequeño grupo de Elfos.","Ningloril ha tenido problemas en la antesala de las mazmorras.\
\
Habla con Ningloril cuando haya sido liberada de la celda.","'¡Estoy listo para liberarme de este lugar, ${PLAYER}! ¡Dejemos estas mazmorras atrás!\
\
'Mantente cerca de mí, porque no conozco el camino de salida, y esta oscuridad me causa gran temor.'","Bori está siendo retenido en algún lugar del Ala Este de las mazmorras.\
\
Encuentra a Bori en el Ala Este de las mazmorras y libéralo.","Ningloril se encuentra en la antesala de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur.\
\
Los Elfos han tomado las mazmorras por asalto, y Ningloril te espera para hablar contigo en la antesala principal.","Habla con Bori","'¡${PLAYER}, ¡Por fin has venido a buscarme! No me atrevía a esperar que me rescataran, ¡pero no puedo negar que me alegro de verte!\
\
'Tienes que prepararte para nuestra huida: coge algunos de estos barriles de belladona y llévalos al pasillo. Si se acercan más guardias, ¡los vapores de la belladona deberían dejarlos inconscientes!\
\
'¡Avísame cuando hayas preparado todo adecuadamente, amigo mío! ¡En ese momento podremos escapar!'","Habla con Ningloril","Bori se encuentra en una celda en el Ala Este de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur.\
\
Bori espera que dejes barriles de belladona en el pasillo para noquear a cualquier guardia que llegue, luego que lo escoltes fuera de las mazmorras.","'Tuvimos algunos problemas sin ti, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero la victoria es nuestra en este día! ¡Salgamos de esta sombría mazmorra!'","Instancia: Mazmorras de Dol Guldur"},
[6871]={"Talk to Lothrandir","'I believe we have a lead! Let us consider our next steps.'","The Angmarim have launched an ambush!\
\
You should defeat the Angmarim attackers!","Listen to the conversation","You have arrived at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.\
\
You should talk to Lothrandir.","Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present","Lothrandir, a Ranger of the North, has joined you in your quest to find a lost Arnorian treasure in Forochel. Your only hope of finding it may lie with the shade of Arvedui, last King of Arthedain.","'We have arrived. It is time to speak with King Arvedui.'","Defeated the Angmarim","Defeat the Angmarim","Lothrandir is speaking with Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.\
\
You should listen to the conversation."},
[6872]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Ulf has perished</rgb>","'You should find Léofdag and learn the state of his company.\
\
'I believe he is posted near the southern gate.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Léofdag has perished</rgb>","'Now all we must do is... wait! What is that? I think I see Hutha approaching!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Burnoth has perished</rgb>","Defend Eaworth and spring the trap","You have defeated the Orc-assault","'All is in readiness here, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Stay a moment, though. I once told you that I would not speak of my past. It is rare indeed that I do so, and only with those I trust. You have earned my trust.\
\
'You deserve to know a little, at least, of what drives me onward....'","Reeve Ingbert is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Reeve Ingbert.","Hear Léofdag's tale.","'We have again made a good showing against our enemies, ${PLAYER}! Come, we will speak again when the Reeve's men have cleared away this rabble.'","'I believe we are nearly ready, ${PLAYER}; however, would you stay and speak with me a moment before checking in with the others?'","Hear Burnoth's tale.","Talk to Ulf the Reaver in the southern end of Eaworth.","Talk to Léofdag","Speak with Ulf the Reaver.","Talk to Ulf the Reaver","Talk to Burnoth.","Hear Ulf's tale.","'${PLAYER}, go down into the southern end of the village and speak with Ulf and Léofdag. Make certain they are ready, then go to the gate to watch for Hutha's return.'","'You and Burnoth's Riders have done my people a great service, ${PLAYER}. We will consider the captain's warnings.'","Hear Ulf's tale","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have come to check on our readiness? Indeed, all is prepared here.\
\
'However, do you have a moment to speak with me?'","<rgb=#FF0000>Ingbert has perished</rgb>","Talk to Burnoth","Talk to Reeve Ingbert","The trap has been set, soon to be sprung against the Orcs besieging Eaworth.","Hear Léofdag's tale","Hear Burnoth's tale","<rgb=#FF0000>Hutha has perished</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Ingbert and the Riders Four must survive</rgb>","Instancia: Eaworth bajo asedio","Speak with Léofdag near the southern gate of Eaworth.","Defend Eaworth and spring the trap.","Speak with Léofdag."},
[6873]={"Instancia: Ecos de Los Muertos","'Stay on your guard, ${PLAYER}. These Men are without honour. We are here to listen to their words, but we must remain cautious.'","Habla con Candaith","'This is an evil place, ${PLAYER}, and the dread of it lies like a cloud upon my limbs! And so cold...I should think I would never be warm again.\
\
'This is a place of the Dead, kept by them throughout the long years. Will they rally to Aragorn's cause? We must learn if it be so.'","'This seems to me a good sign, ${PLAYER}! If the Oath-breakers will fulfill their oath to Isildur, we will command an army the like of which has never been seen in Middle-earth. Surely victory will not be far behind!'","You have not ventured far along the Forsaken Road and have already encountered one of the Oath-breakers cursed by Isildur.","Radanir stands within the Forsaken Road, wishing to speak with you about the grim place.","Run back through the Forsaken Road and talk to Radanir to escape!","Maonir has given in, at last, and seems to wish to speak with you.","'You fight passing well, for a child. Britou will want to speak with you. Britou always wants to speak with those who brave this road. Keep the chasm on your right, and you will find him.'","Habla con Halbarad","'We will stay here, but you should find Britou on the other side of the chasm. We must learn what we may along the Forsaken Road and cover as much ground as we can.'","Find and talk to Britou","'It was unwise of you to come here, warm-bloods. This place belongs to the Dead Who Do Not Rest, and all your kind who stray here perish.'","'What has happened? All of a sudden, the Oath-breakers fell upon us, and we have only driven them off for the moment! We have to get out of here!'","Halbarad has confronted Maonir along the Forsaken Road.","You are betrayed! You must escape the Forsaken Road","Maonir told you that Britou wants to speak with you, and that you could find him by keeping the chasm on your right.","'You are correct...we must get out of here! Hurry, before it is too late for us!'","Candaith is in the depths of the Forsaken Road, confronting the Oath-breaker Britou.","'We will explore this side of the chasm, ${PLAYER}. You must go on ahead and search the other side of the great rift in the earth for Britou, he of whom Maonir spoke.'","You have come to walk the Forsaken Road beneath the Lich Bluffs, where it is said a number of Oath-breakers from the time of Isildur still dwell, suffering from their curse.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","'Who dares disturb this place? Who dares venture where only the Dead may walk?\
\
'The living may not pass. This road is not for you. Turn back! Turn back while you still have the power to do so!'","Talk to Maonir","Talk to Radanir","You have been betrayed. You must escape from the Forsaken Road."},
[6878]={"Speak with Blaire before continuing.","End the nightmare of the Abominations","You have saved the Abominations, ending the nightmare","You have stepped inside Knotfist's hut","Blaire has been defeated!","You have accompanied Blaire to Lhan Colvarn to put and end to the Abomination threat and their leader, Knotfist.","Instance: Ending the Nightmare","The time to end the nightmare of the Abominations has come. Finish what has been started.","'You have done well to clear out a large portion of this village.\
\
'We must end this menace now. The Abominations must cease to exist.'","Talk to Blaire","You have killed Knotfist, ending the nightmare","'The deed is done. For better or for worse, we have dealt with these Abominations. Let us leave here and return to camp. We will talk at greater length there.'","Enter Knotfist's hut","Enter Knotfist's hut."},
[6879]={"'¡Esa beórnida realmente es impresionante! ¿Viste cómo luchó? ¡Qué fuerza, qué ferocidad! Debo admitir que dejó en ridículo mis propias habilidades.'","Bingo está justo dentro de la entrada del puesto avanzado de Stangard.","'No voy a ocuparme de ninguna de esas cosas, ${PLAYER}.'","'¡Qué criatura, ${PLAYER}! ¡Nunca he visto nada comparable! Pensar que una criatura tan majestuosa podría acudir en ayuda de mi pueblo... ¡es increíble!\
\
'Y esta mujer, esta beórnida... ¿ella también lucha por el Rohan? Lucharemos juntos, ${PLAYER}, y rechazaremos a nuestros enemigos. ¡A partir de ahora somos amigos y aliados!'","Tú y Bingo han descubierto un plan oriental para atacar el puesto avanzado de Stangard.","'¡No puedo dejar de pensar en esa beórnida! Abrió una brecha entre los invasores orientales como si fueran simples espigas de trigo. ¡Qué fuerza, qué ferocidad!'","Sabert ha quedado mudo por la aparición de Landroval, pero necesitas que esté listo para la batalla: ¡los orientales han comenzado su ataque sobre Stangard!","Habla con Bingo y averigua de qué tareas se encargará","Langhár está justo dentro de la entrada de Stangard.","Habla con Bingo en Stangard","Bingo ha regresado de sus encargos y está listo para participar en la batalla... ¡que ya ha concluido!","'Puede que no tengamos mucho tiempo antes de que la partida de saqueo oriental ataque Stangard. ¡Debemos aprovechar al máximo el tiempo que tenemos para estar preparados!'","Instancia: Entran los Orientales","Habla con Sabert en Stangard","Investiga el alboroto al suroeste","'¿Qué? ¿La batalla ya ocurrió? Me pareció oír algo más allá del chapoteo de la espuma, pero pensé que era mi imaginación.\
\
'Al menos los platos están limpios. ¡Aun así, habría sido emocionante ver a Landroval y Langhár en acción! No quiero restar valor a tu contribución, ${PLAYER}... ¡sé que también eres impresionante en combate!'","Sabert está en la entrada de Stangard, listo para prepararse para el ataque oriental.","Habla con Langhár y averigua de qué tareas se encargará","'¡Por fin una tarea adecuada para mí, ${PLAYER}! Yo me encargaré de los platos, y tú puedes ocuparte de las tareas que requieren levantar peso.\
\
'¡Te buscaré cuando haya terminado!'","Habla con Sabert en la entrada de Stangard","'Si la batalla ya ha ocurrido, supongo que logramos lo que vinimos a hacer, ${PLAYER}!'","Ha habido un fuerte alboroto hacia el suroeste. ¿Ha comenzado el ataque oriental?"},
[6880]={"Follow Akhrûn and escape Naerband","Defend yourself!","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! Quickly, we must escape. There is not much time. Follow me!'","You notice a loose brick","Confront Thraknûl.","Escape the cell","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso.","Talk to Akhrûn","Thraknûl and Urudanî have returned to Naerband and there is little hope that you will be able to escape the prison fortress alive.","Instancia: Escape de Naerband","That almost worked! One more try should do it!","Confront Thraknûl","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso","Behind the loose brick you find an old scrap of metal","You hear the lock unlatch!","'Let us not stay here another moment. The passage to outside is not far!'","Akhrûn can be found in her cell, in the south-western end of Naerband.\
\
You should free Akhrûn.","Talk to Akhrûn.","Follow Akhrûn and escape Naerband.","Escape the cell using the what information you remember from Akhrûn's own daring escape.","Enemies guard the stairs ahead.\
\
You must approach them and prepare to defend yourself!","Free Akhrûn","'This passage leads through an old culvert. No one seems to know it exists!'"},
[6881]={"Baldgar has been defeated!","You are hiding with Baldgar, still awaiting Acca's signal.","Acca has been defeated!","Wait with Baldgar for Acca's signal: an enormous blast of flame and smoke","It is time to carry out Baldgar's plan to escape from Isengard.","'You have got the keys there, do you not? You must let us out! You cannot leave us to die here, friend! We can help you!'","Acca is ready to speak with you.","Baldgar wants to speak with you before you leave the dungeons.","'You have my word: I will help you to save your Ranger friends from their captivity at the hands of the Falcon-clan. I am sorry that we can do nothing for the Ranger that was sent here with you. Lothrandir, he was called?\
\
'If Lothrandir lives still, Saruman has kept him very close. We cannot hope to gain entrance to Orthanc.\
\
'What is taking Acca so long?'","Run up the slope to the entrance to the dungeons with Acca and Baldgar","'What... what is that noise?'","'There is a gap in the wall between the buildings on the western side. Once the black powder does its work, you should be able to make it there in the confusion.\
\
'But first we need to get to the surface. It will not be easy with so many of us.'","Talk to Baldgar","'We are almost out! Now we just need to light the black powder ${PLAYER} set up ahead of time, and we will have all the chaos we need to make it to the other side of the Ring... and freedom!'","Morflak has killed Acca, and now Baldgar wants you to keep Morflak busy so that he can light the black powder.","You need to walk slowly through the large, open room with Baldgar and Acca so as not to attract undue attention.","Talk to Morflak and keep him busy","Walk slowly through the large room with Baldgar and Acca so as not to attract attention","One of the Dunlending prisoners has tried to attract your attention.","Baldgar is in his cell. He wants to speak with you one last time before you begin.","Talk to Acca","You defeat the Uruk-hai key-master and retrieve his keys!","'You would be nothing without me, ${PLAYER}. I gave you the run of Isengard. It was the fear of me that kept you from being thrown in the cells alongside these vermin.\
\
'But now we will see. Oh, yes, we will see whose time it is to die. See how I repay treachery!'","You, Baldgar, and Acca will go before the rest of the prisoners, running up the slope to the entrance to the dungeons.","Acca has volunteered to light the black powder to provide you with the distraction which you need to escape.","You have made it to the surface of Isengard. You are almost there!","'Here is what we need to do, ${PLAYER}. The key-master is an Uruk-hai who carries a ring of keys that can open these cell doors. He tends to come down into the dungeons several times a day... or what passes for a day here in the lightless reaches.\
\
'Look for him somewhere in the dungeon and see if you can catch him unaware. He is likely to be down the other wing of the dungeons. Climb the slope and turn right when you can. Once you have the keys, come back here and release me! We can then open the door for Acca, and we will make our way to the surface.\
\
'The Uruk-hai must have seen you walking about Isengard. They may believe that you are bringing us to see Saruman, by order of the Wizard. They may let us pass.'","Return to Baldgar","Instancia: Escape de Isengard","'We do not want to attract attention, ${PLAYER}. We should walk slowly from here, so as not to attract undue attention.\
\
'Let us go!'","Find the Uruk-hai key-master","'I am ready for what comes, ${PLAYER}. I will set the black powder aflame, and it will draw all of Isengard to this side of the Ring.\
\
'When that happens, the western side should be empty, and you will be able to slip through the gap in the Ring-wall.\
\
'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. May you live past tonight and help put an end to my master's evil.'","'This is not what I meant, ${PLAYER}.'","Acca has gone to light the black powder, and you should hide with Baldgar until you see the signal: a giant plume of smoke and flame!","'What are you doing down here? Fâsh didn't tell me you had any business here today.\
\
'I don't like the smell of you. Get out of here!'","Talk to the Dunlending prisoner","The key-master is somewhere in the dungeons. Baldgar wants you to take him by surprise, and told you to climb the slope, turning right into the other wing of the dungeons when you have the opportunity.","Talk to Baldgar just inside the entrance to the dungeons","You have recovered the keys from the Uruk-hai key-master.","You have freed Baldgar and Acca from their cells, and now Baldgar wants to speak with you."},
[6882]={"Protege a Bróin de los orcos que atacan","Habla con Bróin","Los Elfos y los enanos están discutiendo el destino de Mazog.","A petición de Issuriel, relatas la historia de tu escape de Rushdurinul con Mazog a cuestas.","'Es demasiado pronto para celebrar en exceso, ${PLAYER}, lo sé; ¡pero haber llegado hasta aquí ya es algo extraordinario!\
\
'Y sin embargo, me pregunto: Mazog es de gran valor para las fuerzas del Enemigo. ¿Puede ser que consideren un intercambio? Si lleváramos a Mazog ante las puertas de Dol Guldur, ¿aceptaría Gorothúl la vida de Mazog a cambio de la de mi primo Bori?\
\
'He jurado que mi hacha pondrá fin a la vida de Mazog, pero si un bien mayor pudiera lograrse con su supervivencia... se convierte en una pregunta más difícil, ${PLAYER}. ¡No podemos abandonar a Bori ahora!'","Bróin está en las profundidades de Rushdurinul, esperando escuchar lo que tienes que decir sobre el destino de Mazog.","'¡Eso estuvo cerca, , pero hemos logrado controlar a Mazog una vez más! ¡Debí haber sabido que aún le quedaba algo de fuerza para luchar!\
\
'Una cosa es segura, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} : ¡necesitaremos hacer cadenas más fuertes para mantener a nuestro prisionero en el futuro!'","Has obligado a Mazog a someterse","A pesar de su intento de escapar, has logrado que Mazog se someta. Ahora deberías hablar con Bróin.","Bróin está esperando para hablar contigo en Rushdurinul.","Da tu opinión a Bróin sobre su decisión respecto al destino de Mazog","'¿Gobernar aquí? ¿Crees que quiero gobernar aquí? ¡No tengo ningún deseo de gobernar este miserable reino! ¿No tienes idea de lo que está pasando, verdad?\
\
'El maestro de Gorothúl es generoso con sus amigos. Se preocupa por ellos. Les dice cosas. ¡El mío tendrá el ejército más grande de todos!\
\
'\\q¿Qué recompensa deseas?\\q me preguntó Gorothúl. \\qSolo el reino que debería ser mío,\\q le respondí. \\qEse lugar no servirá,\\q dijo. \\qMi maestro me ha ordenado sacar los grandes terrores del abismo. Ese reino nunca estará libre de ellos,\\q dijo, y solo los tontos no creerían sus palabras!'","'Toma estas cadenas, ${PLAYER}, y úsalas para atar las muñecas de Mazog. Están hechas de hierro y deberían ser lo suficientemente fuertes para mantenerlo seguro mientras luchamos para salir de este lugar.'","Has llegado a la entrada de Zurr-thurkh y ahora debes asegurarte de que las palabras de Mazog no sean más que fanfarronadas antes de irte.","Escucha la discusión sobre el destino de Mazog","'¡Rápido ahora, antes de que más Orcos ataquen, llevemos a Mazog con nosotros y dejemos este lugar atrás!'","Bróin te ha explicado cómo modificar el rol de apoyo de tus aliados, utilizando la bandera que ha colocado, y está esperando a que lo hagas.","Los Elfos y los enanos dentro de Rushdurinul están considerando las diversas implicaciones de lo que debe hacerse con Mazog.","Mazog está en Rushdurinul. Debes atarlo con las cadenas que Bróin te ha dado.","'¿Crees que estas cadenas pueden atar a Mazog en su propio dominio? ¡Eres un tonto si crees que no puedo romperlas con el más mínimo esfuerzo!\
\
'¡Pero esperaré hasta que estés más vulnerable, ${RACE}, y entonces sentirás mis manos alrededor de tu cuello!'","'Ahora necesitamos salir de Rushdurinul, ${PLAYER}, pero me temo que ya hemos tardado demasiado: este lugar pronto estará lleno de Orcos. Si esperamos escapar de aquí con vida y con la de nuestro cautivo, necesitamos a alguien que gestione el flujo de la batalla.\
\
'Te sugiero que aceptes ese papel. Deberás decirnos cuál debe ser nuestro rol de apoyo a medida que la batalla avanza y retrocede. ¿Deberíamos centrarnos en mejorar tu moral, tu poder, la fuerza de tus ataques o la fortaleza de tu defensa?'","¡Bróin ha sido derrotado!","Bróin está en Rushdurinul, esperando para hablar contigo ahora que Mazog está encadenado.","Habla con Mazog","Instancia: Escapar de Rushdurinul","Usa el estandarte para cambiar el rol de apoyo de tus aliados","Esclaviza a Mazog","La fuga de Rushdurinul ha comenzado -- ¡debes defender a Bróin del ataque de los Orcos!","Bróin está esperando para hablar contigo en las profundidades de Rushdurinul."},
[6883]={"You and Trausti have discovered where Eskil Bloodthumb is held captive within Vatug-ronk.","Talk to Trausti in Vatug-ronk","'I will break the lock on Eskil's cell and release him. I do not think we will have much time before Gorgar's reinforcements get here, ${PLAYER}. Remain on guard!'","Talk to Eskil beside the cage","'If you are here to slay Orcs, you have come too late! Ever since that cursed dragon arrived, raiding parties of hobgoblins have come through from time to time, but this last one was even worse than usual. It was all we could do to fight them off, and we paid for it!\
\
'Garn! We sent for reinforcements from Gorgar, but they have still not arrived! We should have killed that goblin of his when we had the chance, and paid the consequence! But he is gone, and my boys all slain.\
\
'The dwarf-prisoner? Glúrkub wouldn't let us eat him. Should have slain him anyway, and the goblin too. So what if Glúrkub had orders to keep him alive? He's still locked up, I expect. I don't think the hobgoblins were looking for him; they found me and the boys instead, and did us in. This injury could well be my last....'","'Thank you for rescuing me, ${PLAYER}! I knew I should not have come to Deepscrave... but what choice did I have?\
\
'My jailor was a goblin. Glúrkub he was called, I think, and the Orcs were afraid of him; it seemed to me that he must be high up in Gorgar's counsels. He forbade them from harming me. The last I saw of Glúrkub, he had Trausti's axe in his hand, but where he is now I do not know. After the hobgoblins attacked there was no more sign of him.\
\
'Thank you both for coming to save me! I know I do not deserve it... I am no warrior, and can be of little help to the Gabil'akkâ!'","Instancia: La huida de Eskil","Trausti wants to search Vatug-ronk for Eskil Bloodthumb.","Talk to Trausti by the camp-fire","'Well, I am glad we rescued Eskil. But if we are to find my axe we will need to track down this Glúrkub, it seems. Fear not, Lofrík! He will not keep it for long!'","Trausti has come with you to search Vatug-ronk for Eskil Bloodthumb and his stolen axe.","Talk to the weary Orc by the camp-fire and learn what befell the camp","Something passed through the encampment of Vatug-ronk and slew the Orcs within. Those who remain are too weary or injured to offer much resistance.","'It's quiet here, ${PLAYER}, except for the sound of the wood creaking and the groaning of the support beams above, overtaxed by their heavy loads.\
\
'Where are the guards? Where are Eskil's captors?'","Trausti has vowed to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb from imprisonment in the depths of Vatug-ronk... and to find his stolen axe as well, if such a thing might be arranged.","Talk to Trausti outside Vatug-ronk","'I think our fortune may hold true, ${PLAYER}, for it sounds to me that Eskil may still be alive. I cannot imagine why this goblin Glúrkub might have had orders to keep him alive, but I will not trouble about it for now. It is enough that Eskil may yet live!\
\
'Follow me, friend. We will find him somewhere in Vatug-ronk. Perhaps these Orcs are too weary from battle with their supposed hobgoblin allies to stand against us!'","You have defeated the reinforcements Gorgar sent to Vatug-ronk to deal with the hobgoblins. You should speak with Eskil to ensure he is safe and will recover from his ordeal."},
[6884]={"Umer has come out onto the deck of the Night-jewel, ready to face you at last.","'So we have the victory. We will need many more if we are to have lasting peace for Gondor!'","Aragorn is on the docks of Pelargir, waiting to storm the Night-jewel in search of Balakhôr.","'I was unable to find Balakhôr below-decks, ${PLAYER}. Have you seen him? We cannot let this so-called Heir of Castamir escape! I fear the harm he might still work upon the people of Gondor.'","Instancia: Incluso en la Oscuridad","Talk to Aragorn on the docks of Pelargir","Legolas, Aragorn, and Gimli have fought through the city to the docks.\
\
Legolas is waiting to speak with you concerning the number of allies you might have ready at hand.","'What a strange day this has been, ${PLAYER}. To think we would be grateful for the aid of the Dead against the Living! Aragorn believes he must count the oath of these Men fulfilled, and certainly they proved most valuable, but why not retain their loyalty for a few more days?\
\
'Perhaps it is good that it not be my decision to make.'","'The Corsairs are routed, ${PLAYER}! They flee before the Army of the Dead and Aragorn's grim countenance! They flee before you and me, and before stout-hearted Gimli as well!\
\
'But Balakhôr remains, my good ${CLASS}, and until he is defeated we cannot trust that this victory will last. He is surely aboard the Night-jewel.\
\
'Before you storm the flagship in search of him, tell me this: do you have further allies to aid with this, or will you stand alone with Aragorn and Gimli?'","Talk to Gimli at Aragorn's camp","'You should not have come back, ${PLAYER}! I thought it was a mistake for Balakhôr to let you go, but it seems you will die on the deck of the Night-jewel after all!\
\
'The Heirs of Castamir will triumph, and Umbar will be great again!'","'Do you plan to take on Balakhôr by yourself, or do you have a Fellowship near at hand? Give me your answer, ${PLAYER}, and quickly, before the battle is ended!'","The Corsair attack on Pelargir has been turned back, in large part, but Balakhôr himself must still be defeated if their threat is to be ended.","Talk to Aragorn at his camp","'I am glad that is behind us, ${PLAYER}! I confess I was not certain the Dead would follow me, and I am relieved they did so.'\
\
Aragorn laughs, and you realize what an uncommon sound that has become.\
\
'I am more relieved they have now departed, my friend. I would be a braggart indeed to pretend otherwise!'","Free slaves on the deck of the Night-jewel (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Aragorn on the deck of the Night-jewel","'Balakhôr will no longer trouble the people of Gondor, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to the Grey Host and see how our other companions fared during the battle. There is one more matter to which we must attend.'","Aragorn has returned to the deck of the Night-jewel, unable to find Balakhôr below-decks.","Legolas has asked if you plan to take on Balakhôr by yourself or if you have a Fellowship near at hand.","Talk to Legolas on the docks","Talk to Legolas and declare your intentions","The Corsairs have been defeated and Pelargir retaken. One task remains.\
\
Gimli wishes to speak with you about the next step Aragorn plans to take.","The Corsairs have enslaved the people of Gondor as they moved up the coast toward Pelargir. Now it is time to free these slaves from the benches to which they are chained.","The Dead Men have departed, and now Aragorn wishes to speak with you.","Balakhôr has been defeated, and now Aragorn wishes to speak with you on the deck of the Night-jewel.","Stay on guard while Aragorn speaks to the King of the Dead","Talk to Aragorn on the Night-jewel","Aragorn speaks now to the Dead Men of Dunharrow, who have fulfilled their oath to fight against Sauron's forces.","'Most of the Corsairs have been routed, ${PLAYER}, but Balakhôr remains. Any Corsairs that remain by his side will have the utmost loyalty and will fight to the very end.\
\
'Let us storm the Night-jewel and bring that end about, ${PLAYER}!'","Talk to Umer on the deck of the Night-jewel"},
[6885]={"'I will help you with anything I can, ${PLAYER}, if it will help the Lady Éowyn catch this man. Ask me what you will, and I will tell you what I remember of the man I saw.'","Céolflad saw a suspicious figure in Edoras, and now you should ask her questions to learn what you can of his appearance.","Éowyn is on the steps outside Meduseld.","Elfburg's recollection of the man she saw is very similar to that of Céolflad","Nona has been confronted by a number of children in Edoras, and she does not seem happy about it.","'This way, ${PLAYER}. We will find the Lady Éowyn and see how her efforts have progressed while we saw to the will of her brother in Aldburg.'","Talk to Éowyn outside Céolflad's house","Corudan is in the market in Edoras, amused by the recent turn of events concerning Nona and the Rohirrim children.","'Let us go to Éowyn together, and tell her what we have learned of this man.'","Elfburg is in Edoras, north of Céolflad's home. She too has seen a suspicious figure in Edoras, and Éowyn would like you to ask her questions as well.","Horn is waiting to speak with you on the road through the market, in Edoras.","Talk to Horn in Edoras","Nona's hands are clenched, and her eyes are ablaze.\
\
'Step aside, ${PLAYER}. I will not listen to these children speak ill of my people.'","Talk to Éowyn on the steps outside Meduseld","Horn listens to your account, and nods.\
\
'There are many men with blond hair and beards in Rohan, ${PLAYER}, but this brooch sounds distinctive. A red gemstone in the shape of an eye is not a common adornment among my people. This is how we will find this treacherous snake, and keep him from doing further hurt to Éowyn or her people.'","Éowyn listens to the description you obtained from Céolflad and nods excitedly.\
\
'Very good, ${PLAYER}, but we need confirmation and may now be able to obtain it. Another citizen of Edoras is claiming to have seen this man. Follow the road to the north and speak to Elfburg. If her description matches that of Céolflad, we should be able to trust their memory of this man.'","Find Elfburg and question her about the suspicious man she saw in Edoras","You have returned to Edoras with Horn, and Nona has set foot within the city for the first time.","Ask Céolflad questions about the suspicious man she saw in Edoras","Talk to Céolflad in Edoras, north-east of the Meduseld steps","Éowyn listens to your report of your visits to Underharrow and Aldburg, but you can tell from her guarded expression that something troubles her.\
\
'I fear we did not root out all of Gríma's allies when last you were in Edoras, ${PLAYER}. I believe someone interferes with my efforts to empty the city. Someone cut holes in the sacks of grain we set by, and damaged the wheels of one waggon I did not think needed guarding. Céolflad saw a suspicious figure flee the city to the north.\
\
'Speak to her and see if she can provide you with a description of this man. If we do not know his appearance, we will not be able to prevent him from doing more damage, should he return. Find her outside her home, to the north-east.'","Céolflad is north-east of the Meduseld steps, outside her home.\
\
Éowyn has asked you to speak to Céolflad and obtain a description of the suspicious figure that interfered with her duty to empty the city.","Talk to Nona in Edoras","Instancia: Ojos de Edoras","'Ha! I did not expect this turn, ${PLAYER}! It seems our Nona has an effect even on the children of Rohan! If Horn is not cautious, he may find she has little time for him, so busy will she be instructing these children in sword-play!\
\
'You should go on ahead, my friend, and find Éowyn outside Meduseld. It may take us some time to get there.'","Éowyn has hurried up to you near Céolflad with news.","Horn has come to your position near Elfburg, and you should tell him what you have learned.","Talk to Corudan in Edoras"},
[6886]={"Lady Tóla asked you to speak with her husband's grandmother, Lady Góda, and obtain her assistance in convincing Reeve Ingbert to deny Lord Ingmar's wishes.","You tell the Reeve that you must know more of the situation before you can provide him with adequate advice","'I do not deny that under ordinary circumstances, great glory might be won by attacking the foe, and perhaps the siege might be averted, but we are forbidden to attack the Orcs by Théoden King himself.\
\
'Under such circumstances, would it not be treason to attack the Orcs? Would it not be wiser counsel to fortify the city and prepare for a siege? It cannot be denied that we may defend ourselves against attack, for then we are not the hunters.\
\
'What say you?'","Talk to Lord Ingmar","'You there, what is your name? ${PLAYER}, you say? You are a stranger here, so perhaps you might provide my father wiser counsel than either myself or my grandmother.\
\
'I believe the best defence for Eaworth against the coming siege is to attack the Orcs directly and subvert the siege before it has begun. Do you not believe this to be wise counsel?'","Speak with Lady Góda.","'I am more at odds with myself than ever. Arguments have been made for both causes, but I am still uncertain.\
\
'Can you see no other options?'","Watch the discourse between Reeve Ingbert, Lady Góda, and Lord Ingmar.","You agree that there is wisdom in taking the Enemy unaware","Instancia: Enfrentando miedos","'My grandson is headstrong and will not listen to reason. I believe Tóla's fears to be justified... let us speak of this later.'","Speak with Lord Ingmar.","You admit that it is a difficult decision. King Théoden's edict is, in truth, law","Speak with Reeve Ingbert.","Talk to Lady Góda"},
[6888]={"'The information you provided suggests that this is where we will find my brother. I shan't take joy in facing him, but will rest better knowing that justice was served this day.\
\
'Here is where our search ends, but tread lightly. He has fallen in with an unsavoury sort, and is undoubtedly using them for protection until the coast is clear.'","'I do not intend to be put up on display for the whole city to marvel at how the great Faltharan overcame a personal struggle and brought his little brother to justice. I would sooner perish!\
\
'Defend yourself, for you crossed the wrong person!'","Faltharan can be located at the stairs near the east gate.\
\
You should speak with Faltharan.","DNT - Not Used","Confront Lorvegil","You have discovered the location of the traitor Lorvegil, and must help Faltharan bring him to justice.","Instancia: La Confrontación de Faltharan","Faltharan can be found to the west of the eastern gate.\
\
You should speak with Faltharan.","'It is done.\
\
'He may deserve death for what he did, but I will not stand in judgement of him, so long as our father remains missing. I am no longer an impartial subject with this matter.\
\
'We shall take him back with us, and I would have him rot in private with all the time to consider his treachery. Maybe the true Lord of Pelargir will return to stand in judgement....\
\
'I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for helping me to close this dark chapter.'","Aid Faltharan as he confronts Lorvegil","Talk to Faltharan","<rgb=#FF0000>Faltharan has fallen!</rgb>","Aided Faltharan","Confronted Lorvegil","<rgb=#FF0000>Faltharan must not be defeated</rgb>","Faltharan can be located at the stairs near the east gate.\
\
You should aid Faltharan as he attempts to confront Lorvegil.","Lorvegil can be found to the west of the eastern gate.\
\
Speak with Lorvegil in order to confront him about his crimes.","'Let us make our way back to Tol Ciryarani.'","Talked to Faltharan"},
[6890]={"Wait until Calenglad is satisfied that he can join the Grey Company","The robbers have put their gathered plunder into a strongbox located within the crypt.","Habla con Calenglad","You have defeated the tomb-robbers and should now examine their plunder","'Let us leave this place, ${PLAYER}. The air has grown chill of a sudden, and I am ready to return to Tinnudir.'","Talk to Calenglad at Tinnudir","Calenglad is speaking with Gwindeth, the Blue Lady of Nenuial.","Calenglad is standing in front of a tomb-entrance in the Flooded Ward.","'You must think me an old fool, ${PLAYER}. There is no protection I can offer Gwindeth that she cannot manage for herself. Still it is difficult to leave behind people and places we hold dear.\
\
'I did not want to leave without saying good-bye. I have now done so, but it does not make the leaving any easier.'","Instancia: Despedida de Evendim","Calenglad is inside the crypt in the Flooded Ward, waiting to speak with you.","'There are more robbers inside this tomb, ${PLAYER}. Clear them out and recover whatever relics they have already stolen. While you see to that, I will investigate some of these other buildings. I will meet up with you again once the tomb is clear of these villains.'","Inside the chest you see many relics stolen from Annúminas","Gwindeth favours you with a distant smile, brought on by some fond memory","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. This section of the city suffered greatly in the battle against Amarthiel's forces, and robbers have come from the surrounding lands in order to plunder it of goods.\
\
'The tree-lined streets of this ward were quite beautiful before the fighting, deserted though they were. Now the walls are cracked and many of the buildings and tombs that are found here have been flooded, or are flooding.\
\
'Let us save what relics we may from the undeserving pockets of robbers, ${PLAYER}.'","Calenglad is in the Flooded Ward of Annúminas.","'Search the crypt for the robbers' plunder, ${PLAYER}. They will have gathered it into a strongbox.'","You have come with Calenglad to the Flooded Ward to clear it of robbers so that his heart may rest easy as he travels with the Grey Company.","Investigate the tomb-robbers' plunder"},
[6891]={"Instancia: Adiós a Pelargir","'I wonder what will come of this.... Will people return to the city some day, or will they try to make new lives elsewhere? Many of us are too old to begin anew....\
\
'The guards seem to have everything in order. I think we can depart from here, ${PLAYER}.'","Faltharan has asked you to accompany him as his family departs for more safe lands.","Talk to Faltharan","'Let us return to Tol Ciryarani, and discuss what is next.'","Observed the farewell","DNT - Not Used","Faltharan is located at the shipyard.\
\
You should accompany Faltharan as he says his good-byes.","Faltharan is located at the shipyard.\
\
You should speak with Faltharan.","Observe the farewell","'Here we stand, ${PLAYER}. The sky grows bleak every day, but these ships represent symbols of hope for our city.\
\
'I intend to have my mother and siblings aboard those ships before they depart, and will see to that matter personally. Like yourself, they have been valuable allies in maintaining the stability over the city as we played host.\
\
'I only wish that some day the fighting will end, and we can return to rebuild this place.'"},
[6892]={"Speak with Irsinith","'The trees here are covered in this rot. I can watch as they twist to the infection inside them.\
\
'The foul fungus that grows on them is spreading quickly.\
\
'It seems almost unbelievable how fast they are consumed by the blight. But that is why I know in my heart that Amûma herself is succumbing to it.'","Listen to Irsinith","Irsinith wishes to tell you more about Amûma and her duty as her warden.","'As you can see with your own eyes, this Pale Blight is rotting these lands.\
\
'The bark of Amûma herself is festering with fungal blooms and weeping poison from her boughs.\
\
'As I have said, her roots now feed the blight as it ravages all life here. My duty as her warden is to commune with her and bring her words to my people as well as speak with the forest.'\
\
Irsinith sighs.\
\
'Even if a cure or defence against this blight is found. I fear Amûma may be past saving. Her words to me are weak and filled with anger.'","Instance: Fate of the Mother Tree","'Look out over this land, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The ground is covered in a blanket of poison and fungus. Our waters turned murky and vile.'\
\
Irsinith pauses a moment as tears form in her eyes.\
\
'My duty... to this land.. and to Amûma. Is to protect them and hear their words. I have failed.\
\
'This blight has taken so much from me and I feel myself sickly as a result. I feel powerless as I watch my lands wither and die.\
\
'I am sorry. Give me but a moment to compose myself.'"},
[6893]={"The tracks continue here. Long toes with claw marks are visible in the rotten dirt","These tracks are fresh. The source of this blight must be nearby","You have defeated the morroval that you encountered at the ruins of Nagakhêdi. Return to Sul Madásh with the scout to report to Dáthlil.","Scouts in Sul Madásh believe they have discovered the source of the Pale Blight with an unknown enemy being spotted near the ruins of Nagakhêdi to the south. Follow the tracks the scouts discovered to the east of the camp.","There are more tracks continuing east. Faded talon-marks are visible in the earth","Speak with the scout and return to Sul Madásh","Instancia: El destino del Bosque muerto, parte 10","'The monster is dead. I have never seen such a creature in these lands before.\
\
'You have done well this day ${CLASS}. We should return to Sul Madásh.'","Follow the tracks to the source of the Pale Blight","Kill the morroval","The tracks led you to the ruins of Nagakhêdi and a morroval has appeared to stop you. Defeat her!","Scouts in Sul Madásh believe they have discovered the source of the Pale Blight with an unknown enemy being spotted near the ruins of Nagakhêdi to the south.","The tracks are much newer and lead south towards the ruins","You found faint tracks that you can't identify. They continue to the east"},
[6894]={"You drink the serum. It leaves an earthy and burning taste in your mouth.","Eat the <rgb=#FF0000>red</rgb> mushroom","Eat the <rgb=#00FF00>green</rgb> mushroom","You drank the serum, now it is time to eat the blighted mushrooms and see what happens!","Eat the <rgb=#0000FF>blue</rgb> mushroom","Despite the foul taste, your body feels more resilient","It is suspiciously chewy, but you feel more focused","It tastes worse than the last and almost makes you sick","<rgb=#00FF00>Drink</rgb> the Pale Blight serum","It burns more than the others, but you somehow feel invigorated","Speak with Viznak","Instancia: El destino del Bosque muerto, parte 9","You drank the serum and ate the mushrooms. Speak with Viznak again to see what is next.","Eat the <rgb=#FFFF00>yellow</rgb> mushroom","Test the Pale Blight serum that the Viznak and the Rangers made to ensure it protects the imbiber from the rot.","'Good job!\
\
'That was everything for now!'"},
[6895]={"'I am ready. Let us continue on the path to Ered Mithrin.'","Grimbeorn seeks word of the situation in the Wells of Langflood.","Náth has fallen!","Talk to Rúzat.","<rgb=#FF0000>Rúzat must survive</rgb>","Journey to Ered Mithrin with the dwarves","'I am grateful that you decided to accompany us!\
\
'Now then, let us make for Skarháld. I do not think I would fare well in any further ambushes today!'","Defeat the ambushers.","<rgb=#FF0000>Agátur must survive</rgb>","Talk to Rúzat","Defeat the ambushers","Agátur has fallen!","Journey to Ered Mithrin with the dwarves.","Instancia: El destino del Norte","Rúzat has fallen!","<rgb=#FF0000>Náth must survive</rgb>"},
[6904]={"The giant Núrzum is heading to Forlaw in an attempt to extinguish the last bastion of hope for the people of Wildermore. Run towards Núrzum until you're close enough for him to hear the sound of the Winter's Horn.","The frost grims have been defeated. Sound the Winter's Horn","Núrzum has been defeated","Sound the Winter's Horn to damage Núrzum.","Get close enough for Núrzum to hear the Winter's Horn","'This nightmare is now over, ${PLAYER}. Our losses were great, but this giant will terrorize us no longer.'","'We should leave this place now and  head back to Forlaw.'","The frost grims have been defeated. Quickly sound the Winter's Horn","Infuriated by the sound of the Winter's Horn, the giant Núrzum turns his attention to you","Clear the area of all threats before using the Winter's Horn again.","Núrzum is making his way towards Forlaw. He must be stopped before he is able to complete his path of destruction.","The Stone of Thangorodrim has been separated from Núrzum, creating a flash freeze encapsulating him in a tomb of ice","You are within range. Now blow the Winter's Horn to get Núrzum's attention","Núrzum has been weakened. It should take one more sounding of the horn to finish him off.","Defeat frost grims","Instancia: Última batalla","Thrymm, Cyneberg, and Gárwig are prepared to defeat Núrzum. Speak with Thrymm along the ice bridge.","Sound the Winter's Horn to defeat Núrzum","Sound the Winter's Horn to further damage Núrzum.","'This is it, ${PLAYER}. We must make a final stand here and stop Núrzum. We mustn't fail, or we risk losing Forlaw.\
\
'Once we get within range of the giant, you must blow the Winter's Horn. Once we have his attention, I will hold him off.\
\
'Here, take the Winter's Horn. It will take some time to recharge its power, but you may need to blow it several times until Núrzum falls.'","Blow the Winter's Horn to get Núrzum's attention","The Huorn fused with Núrzum appears to be retracting, weakening his physical form and causing him to break apart","Speak with Thrymm","You are close enough to Núrzum for him to hear the sound of the Winter's Horn. Blow the horn to get the giant's attention.","Núrzum is infuriated by the sound of the Winter's Horn. He appears to be weakening each time it sounds","The Winter's Horn caused massive damage to Núrzum, but he struggles through the pain. Make sure that Gárwig remains protected.","Núrzum has been defeated. The people of Wildermore will be terrorized no longer. Speak with Thrymm.","Sound the Winter's Horn","The frost grims have been defeated. Sound the Winter's Horn one last time to defeat Núrzum!","Protect Gárwig"},
[6905]={"Meneldor has escaped the webbing and wishes to depart from the cave at once.","'Be careful, friend! We are not alone here....\
\
'Hurry, she moves ever closer to me!'","Landroval has directed you to the entrance of a large hill-cave, which is home to a dangerous breed of spiders. If Meneldor has entered this cave, he may be in great peril.","Talk to Meneldor and release him from the webbing","Landroval has asked you to search for signs of Meneldor in the cave and to lend him aid if you happen upon him.","Meneldor has warned you of the presence of a dangerous creature in the cave. This threat must be dealt with quickly before attempting to free the Great Eagle.","'I cannot thank you enough for freeing me. I am most fortunate that Landroval sent such a hardy liberator. You fared well against that dreadful spider!'","Talk to the Great Eagle, Meneldor","'Let us leave this dreadful place at once. I was foolish to have come here at all.\
\
'Enough of my strength remains to bear us both safely back to Landroval. You may climb upon my back, but hold on tightly!'","Defeat the spider, Meneghen","Instancia: Encontrando a Meneldor","Meneldor remains entagled in the spider's webbing. He may safely break free now that the spider-queen has been defeated","Talk to Meneldor to leave the spider-cave","Meneghen has been defeated and Meneldor is now safe","You hear a large creature moving among the webs","'With the swiftness of the northern winds, I will break free from this cursed webbing. Just a moment.'"},
[6906]={"Talk to Mithrandir","'Let us return, my friend. We have done what we could, and should tarry no longer.'","Habla con Aragorn","Talk to Mithrandir.","'We must not tarry here. That dark citadel was once Minas Ithil, the Tower of the Moon, but it has not been called by that name for a terrible span of years. It is the fortress of the Nazgûl now, and none dare go that way.\
\
'Thanks to the power and wisdom of Mithrandir, our work this day will make it more difficult for our foes to assail Gondor by this road, and that is a work done well.'","'That is the city of Minas Morgul. Once it was Minas Ithil, the Tower of the Moon, but no longer. Do you see the arched structure that crosses the river to the east? That is the bridge we must destroy if we are to keep the foes from the Morgul Vale from crossing into Ithilien.\
\
'Let us rejoin Aragorn, ${PLAYER}.'","Set fire to noisome flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Mithrandir at the overlook.","'The smoke of their burning is foul, ${PLAYER}, but it will pose less harm than leaving those evil blooms would have done. Let us press forward!'","Instancia: Fuego bajo la Sombra","Angbor has spoken to Aragorn and Mithrandir about an important matter concerning the Morgul Vale.","Let Mithrandir execute his plan","'Our destination lies further ahead, ${PLAYER}, but I ask that you take a moment to hear my counsel.\
\
'The flowers that line the road have fallen to some corruption, prey for some dark force. I suggest that we burn these evil blooms in order to prevent their spread beyond the vale into Ithilien and Gondor.'","Let Mithrandir execute his plan.","Set fire to the noisome flowers.","Talk to Aragorn."},
[6907]={"Busca los obeliscos y abre el camino hacia el centro de la tesorería.\
\
El examen del obelisco hallado en la entrada de la tesorería reveló que la única forma de acceder al centro es invocar el nombre de Elbereth en los obeliscos dispersos por toda la tesorería.","Invoca el nombre de Elbereth en los obeliscos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Invocaste el nombre de Elbereth en los obeliscos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: Fuego y Hielo","Busca al Nazgûl y pon fin a sus planes.\
\
Ahora que has invocado el nombre de Elbereth en tres de los obeliscos de la tesorería, el camino hacia el centro está abierto.","Examina el obelisco","Por petición del Maestro Elrond de Imladris, has entrado en la tesorería abandonada de Helegrod para poner fin al plan del Nazgûl de restaurar al dragón Thorog.","Busca al Nazgûl y pon fin a sus planes.","Examina el obelisco\
\
Has encontrado un obelisco que brillaba tenuemente.","Una placa en el lateral de este obelisco está escrita en varias lenguas. Dice:\
\
'Yo, Durin, señor de Khazad-dûm, he excavado esta cámara con la ayuda de los Gwaith-i-Mírdain. Para proteger las grandes riquezas halladas aquí, se erigieron obeliscos forjados con las artes de los Elfos como símbolo de amistad.\
\
Sólo aquellos que invoquen el nombre de la Encendedora de Estrellas podrán pasar. Tres veces tres son los obeliscos, y tres veces debes hablar.'","Detén los planes del Nazgûl"},
[6908]={"Tu esposo Tumúldo se reúne con los demás miembros de la Hermandad de la Moneda dentro de la Ciudadela de los Vientos.","Nakási Segadora de Olas navega por las aguas de la memoria, desconocida para todos salvo para ella.","'You know I have eyes everywhere. Sometimes they see things of interest to me... and to those of my friends I can trust.\
\
'Know you of the vast lake at the head of the Ikorbân? I thought not, for it appears on few maps, and none in Umbar. Any who stray too near this lake, Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, are slain before they can report of its existence. What deserves such secrecy? I have learned the answer, my friends, and I ask that you hear me out complete before you disregard my words.\
\
'Decades ago, following the destruction of Umbar and the burning of its fleet at the hands of the hated Thorongil, the Dark Lord of Mordor commanded the creation of a new fleet to replace the one that was lost. Barkhûsh ordered the creation of this new armada at Sûg Nidar, far from the prying eyes of Dúnadan and Gondorian spies. \\qThe Song of Waves and Wind\\q it was named by its builders, and in number it would far exceed even the most grand of the Corsair fleets of history. The work continued for many years, but for reasons unknown to me Barkhûsh began his war without waiting for the Song to be ready; only now does it near completion.\
\
'Let me forestall your objection, my friends! This Kindred exists to oppose the Church of Barkhûsh, and allies with none who worship that Dark Lord, though he be gone. But the Song of Waves and Wind is not of itself evil. It is a tool, a weapon to be used, and just because Barkhûsh set it down does not mean others might not pick it up and use it for their own defence, and for their own aims. This fleet could be a gift to Umbar, and to those who must now lead it through dangerous days.'","Los demás miembros de la Hermandad se retiran de la reunión, pero tú y Tumúldo se quedan.","Tu miedo, tu ira y tu soledad se disuelven en la oscuridad.","Whatever Nakási may have experienced during her final moments, you hope she is now at peace.","Tatháta stands upon the deck of Tumuldo-râba, Nakási's flagship.","Azagath desea hablar contigo y con Tumúldo sobre un asunto secreto.","Uno de los guardias dentro de la Ciudadela de los Vientos intenta impedir tu paso a la sala donde se reúne la Hermandad de la Moneda.","Quédate junto a Tumúldo mientras la Hermandad de la Moneda debate tu presencia","Tumúldo siempre fue tu roca firme, incluso cuando los días eran aterradores y las noches largas y terribles.","Había algo que querías decirle a tu esposo, pero ahora no puedes recordar qué era.","Talk to Tatháta on the deck of Tumuldo-râba","Instancia: Primer Verso, Último Verso","'She is gone, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'With its leaders dispatched and the Narghâk weapons damaged, the Song of Waves and Wind has reached the end of its campaign against Gondor. Already the fighting turns against them.\
\
'The battle will soon be over. Now the healing must begin.'","La Hermandad de la Moneda debate tu presencia en la Ciudadela de los Vientos.","Tu miedo, tu ira y tu soledad finalmente han desaparecido.","Habla con el guardia dentro de la Ciudadela de los Vientos","Entra en la sala donde tu esposo Tumúldo se reúne con los demás miembros de la Hermandad","'I am sorry, Captain. The Kindred of the Coins meets within.\
\
'I cannot let you pass.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Reflexiona</rgb> sobre esta pregunta: ¿cumplió la Hermandad de la Moneda con sus intenciones?","Permanece con Tumúldo tanto tiempo como puedas","Habla con Azagath sobre un asunto secreto","Toma su mano y enfrenta lo que venga","Nakási Wave-reaper is gone","Debes <rgb=#00FF00>reflexionar</rgb> sobre esta pregunta: ¿cumplió la Hermandad de la Moneda con su propósito?","Quédate con Tumúldo mientras el resto de la Hermandad se retira"},
[6910]={"Instancia: Cinco contra el Páramo","<rgb=#FF0000>Ulf has been defeated</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>HUtha has been defeated</rgb>","'Our task is done, and victory is ours! Neither Orc nor the East will overshadow Rohan!'","Defeat the Khundolar riders.","<rgb=#FF0000>Léofdag has been defeated</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Burnoth has been defeated</rgb>","'Let us return now to Harwick....'","<rgb=#FF0000>All of the Riders Four must survive</rgb>","Talk to Burnoth and return to Harwick.","Speak with Burnoth.","Defeated the Khundolar riders","'Here, we will show Fate for the fraud it is! For honour and glory, let us ride!'","Talk to Burnoth","Defeat the Khundolar riders","You have accompanied the Riders Four to an encampment of Easterlings, where Burnoth hopes to prove to Aldor Harding that Men make their own fates."},
[6912]={"'${PLAYER}, there is nothing we can do! We must retreat! Everyone, make for the East-gate!'","Brogur fell behind during the retreat, and Bósi asked you to find his cousin.","You have entered Khazad-dûm from the East-gate, and the situation appears worse than you feared.","'Brogur, my cousin! How can it be? How can it be?\
\
'We have to leave, ${PLAYER}! We have to get out of here! The Iron Garrison has failed!'","Talk to Solsi inside the First Hall","Find Brogur in the First Hall","'Khazad-dûm is lost!'","Bósi and Brogur have not yet made it back to the East-gate. Solsi asked you to find them, if they still live.","Instancia: Huida de Khazad-dûm","Talk to Bósi in the First Hall","Brogur is on the western side of the First Hall.","Find Bósi and Brogur and escape from Khazad-dûm","You have found Brogur, but he is dead","'${PLAYER}, Brogur has fallen behind! Can you find him?'","Bósi has finally made it to the First Hall!","Bósi is in the First Hall, near the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.","If the rumours are true, the Iron Garrison is in danger and their foothold in Khazad-dûm is threatened.","You have found Brogur, but there is no sign of Bósi","Bósi has made it to the First Hall.","'${PLAYER}! The Iron Garrison is in disarray! Great tremors shook the city to its very foundations, and Orcs and goblins boiled from every crevice and chasm in the deep! I have never seen so many!\
\
'We were overcome! We have no choice but to escape, but Bósi and Brogur have not made it back yet! You have to find them!'","'${PLAYER}! We have to fight them off for as long as we can! We need to give my cousin time to catch up to us!'","Talk to Brogur in the First Hall"},
[6913]={"Jaith has entered Dâr Laja with information about what transpires in the city.","The catacombs of Umbar-môkh may allow you to flee the uprising and escape to safety!","Talk to Gadâr within Dâr Laja","Guard-captain Gadâr stands prepared to defend you within Dâr Laja.","The fate of some members of the Kindred of the Coins remain a mystery, and for now can only be guessed at by wondering minds.","Follow Khôltekh through Umbar-môkh to safety","Your guards have left Dâr Laja to prevent the uprising from entering the Meeting-hall and doing you some harm. You should return to the main hall and stay away from the entrance!","Temámir soldiers bar your passage.","Walk to the northern waggons or defy Khôltekh by standing your ground","Talk to Jaith inside Dâr Laja","'You are too valuable to kill,' Khôltekh says. 'Carry her, boys.'","Khôltekh motions for you to speak to him.","Instance: Flight of the Golden Queen","Khôltekh had better have an explanation for this insult!","'Most of the crowd has not yet thought to look for us in Umbar-môkh. We can follow these passages to safety!'","'Hold it right there, Hármelak.'\
\
The Temámir meaningfully grips the haft of his spear and nods in the direction of Khôltekh.\
\
'I will not use this unless I am commanded to do so... but I will obey the order if it is given.'","Khôltekh nods in the direction of the waggons to the north.","Return to the safety of the main hall of Dâr Laja","Follow Gadâr and remain under his protection","Temámir soldiers bar your passage","'Dâr Laja is not safe for us, Hármelak. I know you trust in your guardsmen to keep the unruly throng at bay... but I have not that faith in them.\
\
'The city has come alive with anger, and that fury is directed at you... at us. If we remain here, I believe we will be slain.'","'Spare me your indignation, Hármelak: you know what happens to those who gamble with the lives of others without taking care to slant the odds sufficiently in their favour. The Song of Waves and Wind proved very useful, and it may be that Gondor lies in ruin even now, but you failed to manage the people of the city, and they have turned upon you. That they think to also hold me accountable for your blunder is... unfortunate.\
\
'But the memories of the people are short. You will be kept safe and unharmed until such time as it is politically advantageous for the Temámir to produce you.\
\
'The waggons to the north will transport you safely out of the city and beyond reach of the crowd that calls for your head. This is much finer treatment than you would receive from anyone else; let us say it is in remembrance of the tyrants we overthrew, and the Kindred we led together, if only for a short time.'","'You have nothing to fear, my Lady. The doors of Dâr Laja are strong, and the men who guard them are even stronger! None of the shouting throng will get inside.'","Khôltekh has led you into Umbar-môkh, through which you must find safety!","Gadâr has sworn to protect you. You should stay close to him.","'The area from Dâr Laja to Bith Gabâr is packed with residents of the city, a shouting throng. Many in the crowd carry weapons, but for now they have not wielded them against us. I think that will not change, but I cannot say that with certainty.\
\
'You must stay inside, my Lady. It is not safe for you out there. I fear we cannot protect you if you leave the safety of the Meeting-hall!'","Talk to the Temámir guardsman barring your passage","Talk to Khôltekh and demand an explanation","Talk to Khôltekh in the main hall of Dâr Laja","You demand to know the meaning of this insult","Flee through Umbar-môkh to safety!","Khôltekh hopes to lead you through Umbar-môkh to safety!","Talk to Khôltekh in Umbar-môkh","Khôltekh beckons you to the safety of the main hall"},
[6914]={"'You were a blur of blade and hoof.  Your prowess will be recorded this day!  Floodwend is in your debt. You have the gratitude of all of Middle-earth!'","Objective 2: Ride out and trample the unmounted forces.","Speak with Elfhelm again.","You have defeated the remaining forces. Ride on! <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (4/6)</rgb>","You have defeated the Uruks at the gate.  Ride on! <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (2/6)</rgb>","Continue through the valley. You must chase down the Nazgul rider.","Objective 6: Speak with Elfhelm","The town of Floodwend has been besieged. You must do everything in your power to drive back the evil forces of Isengard and Mordor and save the town from imminent doom!","'Grimbold told us he would send help.  You are it?  Where are the Riders of Rohan? Is there no one else who will come to our aid?  \
\
'You must succeed where othere could not, then.  You must drive back the evil of Mordor itself.  These forces are driven by a dark rider.  Come with me to the gates.  Then we ride from there!'","Objective 1: Speak to Elfhelm","Objective 3: Defeat the enemies on the road","Objective 4: Defeat the remaining enemies on the road","Instance: Floodwend Besieged","Time is up! Please try again later.","Objective 5: Defeat the Nazgûl","Floodwend is saved! <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (5/6)</rgb>","Congratulations! You are the hero of Rohan! <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (6/6)</rgb>","Elfhelm has asked you to ride and push back the enemy forces.  The horses are dead, reinforcements are ariving late, and only you can stop the threat.","At the end of the valley, waits the Nazgul rider.  Defeat him and reclaim Floodwend for Rohan!","Follow Elfhelm to the town gates. <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (1/6)</rgb>","Speak with Elfhelm before you. He will lead the way to the gates of Floodwend!","You have defeated some ambushers. Ride on! <rgb=#00FF00>Objective Completed (3/6)</rgb>"},
[6915]={"Speak with Radwig","Listen to Radwig","Floodwend's peril has come to a boil. The Orcs and Easterlings have advanced on Floodwend, lead by the Nazgûl: the Grim Southron.","You let Radwig die!","The Mead Hall is safe at last","You let Etta die!","The town of Floodwend is besieged by the forces of Jóshkhin Orda, led by the Grim Southron who re-grouped the routed army.\
\
You must protect the Mead Hall, and the young Thane of Floodwend!","The Mead Hall of Floodwend has been defended, and Radwig is excited to congratulate you, and thank you for your help.","Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.","The sounds of battle grow louder. The forces of Mordor are not far!","Radwig shows great courage for one so young. You must ready yourself for an attack on the Mead Hall.","Speak with the young Thane","Instance: Floodwend Besieged","'Look, ${PLAYER}! Floodwend still stands!\
\
'The Easterlings are truly driven off. I cannot thank you enough for helping us here, my friend. Look at my people, whole and hale.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Radwig cannot be defeated</rgb>","'We could not have managed this without you, ${PLAYER}. I owe you so much. I do not think I would have embraced my responsibilities with such confidence if you had not been here to show me the way a true leader, a true warrior, must be.'","Protect the Mead Hall from the forces of Mordor","'It is time to brace for battle, ${PLAYER}. I can already hear the sounds of war outside. We must take a stand here, in this very Mead Hall, and ensure that it does not fall as Langhold did, not many days ago.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Etta cannot be defeated</rgb>","Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend, awaiting the approach of the forces of Mordor, let by the Grim Southron."},
[6916]={"Listen to Mizâdi","Speak with Mizâdi by Eshtali's tomb","'Thank you. Come, we should return to Kûr Anzar before dusk floods Esh-kimâkhi.'","Instancia: Flores para Eshtali","Offer comfort to Mizâdi.","Join Mizâdi at Eshtali's tomb.","Place the flowers on Eshtali's tomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Please, place the flowers on the centre of his sarcophagus.'","Eshtali lies in the tombs of Esh-kimâkhi. In the fight to liberate Kûr Anzar, there was scarcely enough time to think, let alone mourn the dead. Now that the immediate threat is over, we mourn our fallen and remind ourselves why they still take such firm residence in our hearts.","Join Mizâdi at Eshtali's tomb","Offer comfort to Mizâdi","Place the flowers on Eshtali's tomb.","Listen to Mizâdi.","Speak with Mizâdi by Eshtali's tomb."},
[6917]={"Wait for the Ents to arrive outside Drû Vádokan","Nindorn has fallen!","The glow of flames can be seen as an Uruk rushes forth in the distance","With Voskor's death, a sense of peace has returned to Balewood","Talk to Barallas","Barallas and the other Ents are outside Drû Vádokan.\
\
The Ents are ready to assault Drû Vádokan. You should speak to Barallas and begin the assault.","'Hooom. We have travelled far, little one... and the time has come for us to reclaim our forest.\
\
'The others have journeyed here, and should be arriving soon...\
\
'Of course, if Tithenolf has fallen asleep again.... Hum, I could not speak to where he might be.'\
\
Barallas appears to become lost in thought for a moment before remembering he is speaking to you.\
\
'Hoom, I think I hear their approach.... Let us hope it is them, ${PLAYER}.'","As Tithenolf slowly strides forth, it is clear the last Ent has arrived","Voskor can be found inside Drû Vádokan.\
\
Barallas and the Ents have discovered a vile Uruk leading the Orc forces in Balewood, but he appears to be wounded.","Fight your way through Drû Vádokan","Strongroot has fallen!","'The Orcs will trouble us no longer, my bold friend. Hoom. Let us return to Stonecliff and enjoy this peace.'","Voskor is standing in the middle of Drû Vádokan.\
\
You should approach Voskor and confront him with the Ents of Balewood.","Barallas and the Ents are attacking Drû Vádokan.\
\
You should follow them into battle to ensure their success.","Barallas is standing outside Drû Vádokan.\
\
Barallas and the others have travelled to Drû Vádokan and now stand ready to raze what remains of the Orc forces in Balewood. You should speak to him while you wait for the others to arrive.","Barallas has fallen!","<rgb=#FF0000>Barallas and the Ents must survive</rgb>","Instancia: Bosque por los árboles","Barallas is outside Drû Vádokan.\
\
You should wait for the other Ents to arrive before beginning the assault.","Follow Barallas and the Ents to the gate","Barallas and the Ents have decided to assault Drû Vádokan and put an end to the White Hand presence in Fangorn Forest.","Mossbeard has fallen!","'Hoom, I see the first of their kind just outside their camp up the road.\
\
'Let us bring our branches crashing down upon them....'","Defeat Voskor","Approach Voskor","Tithenolf has fallen!","Barallas and the Ents are marching to assault Drû Vádokan.\
\
You should follow Barallas and the other Ents as they march to the gate of Drû Vádokan."},
[6920]={"'The bodies of the dwarves were nothing more than another misdirection by the devious Karazgar. He wanted nothing more than to stoke the fires of mistrust in the north.'","'Fram set out towards Scatha's hoard, as he often did. On this journey he had no intention of taking riches, however. His only goal was to confront Karazgar....'","Léothred and Fróthi have finally uncovered the truth of how Fram died and who killed him.","Talk to Fróthi","Talk to Léothred","Listen to Fróthi and Léothred's tale.","Instancia: La locura de Fram","Listen to Fróthi and Léothred's tale","'If only we had known then what we know now. To think of the added prosperity that both our peoples unknowingly abandoned.'","Talk to Léothred.","Talk to Fróthi."},
[6921]={"Listen to the words of Bozhéna","'For twelve years he remained in Mordor, and when he finally returned he was not the same. The time he spent among such wickedness in the Black Land and the citadel of Minas Morgul took its toll upon him.\
\
'No one could have survived such an experience unchanged, but by my beard I say none could have done better than my Vóin.'","Listen to the words of Bozhéna in the Halls of Memory","'And then he was gone.'","Listen to the words of Vóin, as remembered by Bozhéna","Bozhéna will pick up the tale on the slopes of Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.","Bozhéna has made her own contributions to the Halls of Memory.","'He spent years in Minas Morgul, trying to free his friend from a cruel fate.'","It was Vóin's wife Bozhéna who completed the Black Book of Mordor, hiding her contributions among the illustrations in the margins towards the end of the tome.","Delve deeper into the Halls of Memory","'He did not stay in Mordor. After twelve years, my husband returned to me.'\
\
Even hidden among the margin illustrations in the Black Book, the tone of Bozhéna's writing is as clear as the crystal surface of a mountain lake.\
\
'I had some questions,' she writes.","'The chamber took many years to finish. It was his life's work, and into its construction he poured every part of himself. On the walls he carved the song of Thafar-gathol, for that was the dream he set aside for the love of his friends and the memory of their struggles, but it still captured his imagination. Often I would enter the hidden chamber unnoticed and find him staring at the song, humming to himself. More than once I would interrupt his musings and hear him speaking softly in the dim light. \\qOne day,\\q he would say from time to time. \\qOne day.\\q\
\
'Our son Tázko was born in the years following his father's return from Mordor, and he delighted to play in the hidden room, but eventually Vóin grew cross and forbade his son from entering. \\qIt is disrespectful, Tázko!\\q he chided the boy. \\qThis room is a crypt. It is a tomb for the dwarf I was, and for my friends who have died, and worse than died.\\q\
\
'\\qWhat could be worse than death?\\q Tázko asked him once, but that was the end of the discussion. Vóin would no longer speak openly of the hidden chamber or the tome within.\
\
'In time, my husband felt the onset of his years, and knew his end approached. There was one last journey for us to make, and then he would be satisfied with the life he had lived.'","'We returned to Járnfast. My husband was right: Tázko grew to be a fine, strong dwarf, and as the years passed he proved an able help to his mother and to the rulers of the Iron Hills. He spoke often of the great deeds of Zhélruka past and present; Vóin would have been very proud of his son.\
\
'I placed the tome my husband had written in the hidden chamber, and sealed the door. I entered that secret room less and less often as the years went on, and in time I stopped going inside at all. Tázko does not remember the journey we took to the Grey Mountains with his father, but every now and then he asks what I think happened to him. \\qHe found the lost city of Thafar-gathol,\\q I tell him, and he smiles. And why should he not? Vóin survived Mordor, and Minas Morgul, and defied the edicts of the Witch-king himself. I think if anyone could find that lost city, it would be my husband.\
\
'Now I feel the passing of the years, as Vóin did, and I know my time is nearly ended. I have come into the hidden chamber one last time, and I will write the conclusion of my husband's story in the manner he wanted. \\qMy friends defied evil,\\q he said to me, \\qand I do not want them forgotten.\\q I promised to conclude the tale, and now that I have done so I will set this book down upon its table, and sing the song my husband carved upon the walls. I will leave the hidden chamber and seal the door, and then I think I will sit for a time and think of Vóin.\
\
'If any should find this book after a year, or two, or ten, know that Vóin and Bozhéna and their son Tázko were happy with their lot, and despite the difficulties of their time they knew that even a hopeless night must come to an end, and there would always be good-hearted folk ready and eager to greet the dawn.'","Talk to Bozhéna on the slopes of Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Listen to the words of Bozhéna on the slopes of Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","'Vóin returned home, walking through Mordor as if he were the master of that land. He had no more to fear from it.'","'Vóin wanted to build a secret chamber in which to hide the book he had written.'","'The three of us journeyed westward, to the Grey Mountains.'","'But it was not to be. The torments of the Witch-king proved too severe, and in time Eärnur's resistances fell, as he knew they would. He had told Vóin this day would come, but my husband refused to believe it.\
\
'Alas, the depth of the evil in that place overmastered Vóin's hopeful heart, and the words of his friend proved true.'","'It has been a long journey, but I have a few steps more to take. I trust you both know you have all my love? Good, good!\
\
'Keep the deeds of the Zhélruka close to your heart, Tázko, and live by their example! You will be a strong dwarf and brave, stronger and braver than I have been, I expect! I am proud of you, my son. Take care of your mother, and see that she wants for nothing.\
\
'Bozhéna, you are more dear to me than you know, and these years have been better than I deserve. Take care of Tázko, and know that I will bear the memories of our time together wherever these steps take me.'","Instancia: Liberado de la carga","'Vóin left Minas Morgul then, walking as if he were its master and could not be harmed.'","'Farewell, unknown friend, farewell!'","As the end of his years approached, Vóin took one last journey to the Grey Mountains.","Hear the conclusion of Bozhéna's account, secretly recorded in the Black Book","'Vóin knew the time had come. He ascended the stairs in the tower and came to the very highest chamber, where resided the great beacon. He broke a shard from its reflective surface, and using the secret arts of our kind he trapped a ray of the moon's light in that glass.\
\
'Sitting in that high place, my husband took from his satchel an empty tome he had taken from an archive in the city; the accursed sage that governed it never knew the book to be missing. In the light of that moon, Vóin wrote the tale of his years, and he left nothing out. He wrote of Magoldir the Elf, into whose life my husband came only near the end, and wept to not have known him longer. He wrote of the knights of Gondor with whom he adventured in Gundabad and elsewhere: hopeful Silmahtar, courageous Calatúr, swift Macilnis, and loyal Orolang, whose death grieved him for all the rest of his days.\
\
'But most of all, he wrote of Eärnur, the lost king of Gondor and his dearest friend. It would be the only record of the man Eärnur had been before he fell into the net of the Witch-king. When Vóin could find no more words to write, he found a plain coffer in the city and fashioned two keys to open it. One of the keys he kept; the other he set beneath hammer, and broke the end.'","Hear the words of Vóin, as recorded by Bozhéna","'I am named Bozhéna, and I am of the Zhélruka. I met Vóin who would be my husband when I was young and my beard was but a shadow of what it is today, and I did not count him much of a dwarf. It was only with the passage of years that he earned my love, and now we have a son. Tázko is his name, and already I have filled his ears with the stories of his father's adventures. But he is young, and to him tales are just tales; ask an old dwarf the tales of her youth, and she may not remember them.\
\
'So I do not entrust this story to Tázko, though he is dearest to me in all this world and I will raise him to be all a Zhélruka should be. It was Vóin's wish that I record the end of his tale in the tome he brought out of Mordor, and this I now do.'"},
[6922]={"Frodo está en los senderos fuera de La Última Morada, tomando el aire nocturno.\
\
Gandalf el Gris te pidió que caminaras con Frodo Bolsón y evaluaras su estado de ánimo.","'Gracias nuevamente por el paseo, ${PLAYER}. Tal vez las cosas no sean tan sombrías después de todo.'","'Siempre he dicho que un buen paseo al aire libre por la noche hace maravillas para despejar la mente, y parece que tenía razón — me siento mucho mejor ahora, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Disfruté nuestra conversación. Si vuelvo a verte, tendremos que tener otra.\
\
'Cuando te vuelva a ver, quiero decir.'","Frodo está en una bifurcación de caminos no muy lejos de La Última Morada.\
\
Tu paseo con Frodo parece haber aliviado algunas de sus preocupaciones.","'Un paseo es justo lo que necesito, ${PLAYER}. Puedes contarme tus aventuras. No hay nada que me guste tanto como una buena historia de aventuras.\
\
'Las aventuras reales no son lo mismo, ¿verdad?'","Gandalf el Gris te ha pedido que hables con Frodo Bolsón sobre sus preocupaciones.","Instancia: La carga de Frodo","Camina con Frodo","Frodo está fuera de La Última Morada, tomando el aire nocturno.\
\
Gandalf el Gris te pidió que caminaras con Frodo Bolsón y evaluaras su estado de ánimo.","Habla con Frodo"},
[6923]={"Defend the Hornburg against the White Hand","'Hurry, my friend...the wall is breached, and we must defend the Hornburg! Enemies are making for the Glittering Caves of Aglarond!'","You have defeated the first wave","'Alas, my good friend and retainer has fallen...but with his sacrifice, he proved that any accusations against his honour were without base. Let us take his body from this place, lest it be forgotten upon the field....'","The forces of the White Hand are attacking the Hornburg. Aid the Rohirrim against their enemy.","You have joined with Burnoth in remembering Léofdag's valour at the Battle of the Hornburg.","You have defeated the third wave, but Léefdag has fallen....","You should speak with Burnoth at once.","Instance: Funeral for a Friend","Talk to Burnoth","You have defeated the second wave","The armies of the White Hand are attacking the Hornburg. You should speak at once with Burnoth."},
[6924]={"Estás ${PLAYERNAME:dormido[m]|dormida[f]} y experimentas un sueño muy extraño...","Estás atrapado en un sueño.","Estás atrapado en un sueño peculiar.","Instancia: El Sueño de Galadriel","Estás teniendo un sueño muy peculiar.","Estás ${PLAYERNAME:dormido[m]|dormida[f]} y soñando."},
[6925]={"Ratúlko the Bloody has discovered your true identity!\
\
You should fight for your life!","Armed imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Ebuzâm","You have found Ratúlko the Bloody and his 'important guest'","Enter the execution chamber","Collected Ordâkhai weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have cleared the torture chamber.\
\
You should continue to the next cell block.","Ratúlko has noticed you!","You have found several prisoners being tortured in the torture chamber.\
\
You should defeat the torturers and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.","You have collected enough weapons to arm the prisoners and stage a riot.\
\
You should free and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.","'You there, state your name! Wait. I know you....\
\
'You are the one who attacked us outside Ahâba! Did that traitor Mizâdi send you here to kill me?'","Broken binding chains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ratúlko the Bloody is busy having a conversation with Góramul Sai.\
\
You should quietly free and arm the prisoners in the execution chamber while they are talking.","You have travelled to the prison of Esh Mêkag with Ebuzâm.\
\
You should talk to Ebuzâm.","You hear prisoners screaming","Defeated Esh Mêkag torturers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Esh Mêkag torturers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Break binding chains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enter the torture chamber","Instancia: Fuga de la cárcel","Talk to the Ordâkhai guard","You have cleared the torture chamber, but have yet to find Ratúlko the Bloody.\
\
You should continue forward and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.","You have made it past the first gate.\
\
You should discreetly collect any Ordâkhai weapons you find.","Arm imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Eavesdrop on the conversation","Collect Ordâkhai weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We have done it! Ratúlko the Bloody has fled with his tail between his legs! Now these dogs of Ordâkh will pay!\
\
'Let's get out of here for now and regroup at the ruins.'","The prisoners erupt in cheers! They have pushed back the Ordâkhai!","'They still believe you are a guard. That should allow us to remain undetected. If anyone asks, you have captured me and are taking me to directly to Ratúlko for punishment.\
\
'Once we're past the first gate, we need to find some weapons. We arm every prisoner we come across, and then we attack! This will only work if we can get everyone armed and ready quietly, and catch the Ordâkhai off-guard. Let's go.'","You explain to the guard that you have captured Ebuzâm and are taking him to Ratúlko the Bloody personally. He smirks.\
\
'Good! This one has been a thorn in our side for quite some time. Did you really think you could get away, Ebuzâm? I hope the warden finally puts you in the dirt where you belong.'","Ebuzâm wants to enter the torture chamber to free anyone inside.\
\
You should enter the torture chamber.","Talk to Ratúlko the Bloody","Survive Ratúlko's attack","Enter the next cell block","The door deeper into the prison is locked and guarded.\
\
You should talk to the Ordâkhai guard and convince him to let you pass.","Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth, grinds Men to dust year after year. Now, when we few have finally found the strength to escape, they threaten to execute the rest. This will not stand... not while I draw breath!","There is one chamber left.\
\
You should enter the execution chamber.","Ratúlko the Bloody is having a conversation with Góramul Sai.\
\
You should listen to their conversation. What they say might be valuable information to Mizâdi's cause.","Ratúlko the Bloody has noticed you.\
\
You should talk to Ratúlko the Bloody and try to convince him you are just a guard."},
[6926]={"Defeat the Dheghûn in the glade.","Defeat the Dheghûn","A strange howling sound emanates from the Púkel-men statues","Let Rhûd-pulo-Drât perform his ritual.","Ghân-buri-Ghân believes Rhûd-pulo-Drât may need the newly constructed ward more than the entire village of Drû Bhûta to protect the Drúadan Wood.","Follow Rhûd-pulo-Drât","This hidden glade must be a very sacred place to the Woses. Rhûd-pulo-Drât seems nervous","'The Okwô-kuryô here are awake again. Their hearts beat like sap through a Dhûrghud.  Balance has come to Luk Khakát. Let us return to Drû Bhûta.'","Let Rhûd-pulo-Drât perform his ritual","'Drû Bhûta must hear this new tale.'","You should speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât.","Instancia: Claro de los Tres Alegres","Follow Rhûd-pulo-Drât to Luk Khakát.","The last of the Dheghûn falls and calm is restored to the glade","Speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât"},
[6927]={"Fish up a glinting Relic of Inner Fire","Elhudan circle the pools in this area of the Dunbog, casting their fell light upon your wary faces.\
\
You should defeat all of the elhudan in this area.","The turtles roam the pool that Franis led you to.\
\
You should defeat the turtles that romp in this area so that you may fish in peace when all is done.","Slugs slither around the pools to which Franis has led you.\
\
You should defeat all of the slugs of this area before you attempt to fish here.","'I can help you pick a path to the best fishing pools, ${PLAYER}. Just stay close and do not stray. I might not be able to help you fight, but I do have a knack for finding relics.'","Defeat each of the turtles","Defeat all of the elhudan around this pool","Follow Franis to the turtle-guarded pools","Fish up a muddy Seal of Patience","You have collected a muddy Seal of Patience","Collected a glinting Relic of Inner Fire","'I hope you are not tired! There are still more pools to fish from tonight. Follow me, and keep up!","Collected a dripping Relic of Cunning","The avanc have been slain; it is now safe to fish","A muddy Seal of Patience can likely be found in the nearby pools.\
\
You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.","Collected a worn Relic of Time","Fish up a soggy Relic of Strength","'You are quite the fisher-${RACE}, ${PLAYER}! And a warrior also -- I would be happy to scout these parts with you any time you want it. You have quite a talent for hooking the lost valuables. I hope your catch will be of great use to you.'","The bog-lurkers have been cleared away, and you may now fish in peace","Talk to Franis","You have defeated the slugs; you may now fish in peace","The turtles are gone, and it is now safe to fish","Defeat all of the slugs","Franis is waiting for you to speak with him again.\
\
You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog has steered you successfully to the most promising pools.","A soggy Relic of Strength can likely be found in the nearby pools.\
\
You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.","'Are you ready to move to the next pool? Follow me closely, and I will lead you there now.'","Avanc circle the pools in which a soggy Relic of Strength might be found.\
\
You should defeat the avanc so that you can fish in peace in the pools.","'Come along, ${PLAYER} -- there is no time to waste! The next pool is this way. Oftentimes, there are rather menacing turtles in that area, but hopefully they will not be there.'","Franis is waiting for you to speak with him again.\
\
You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog will steer you to the most promising pools.","A dripping Relic of Cunning can likely be found in the nearby pools.\
\
You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.","Many valuable relics of old were lost in a battle that took place long ago in the Dunbog. It is often said that night-time fishing excursions will produce ancient and wonderful gems that enhance powerful items.","Fish up a worn Relic of Time","Instance: Glinting in Forgotten Pools","Franis has led you to a pool that is surrounded by menacing bog-lurkers.\
\
You should defeat all of the bog-lurkers so that you may fish in peace.","Defeat all of the bog-lurkers in this area","Fish up a dripping Relic of Cunning","Collected a soggy Relic of Strength","'Let us keep moving, my friend. The night is not growing any younger, and I would like to dry my feet before the sun comes up.'","Talk to Franis to continue through the bog","Defeat the avanc at the first pool","Franis is waiting for you in the Dunbog.\
\
You should speak with Franis.","A glinting Relic of Inner Fire can likely be found in the nearby pools.\
\
You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.","'Are you ready to travel back to Galtrev? I will have you there before you can snap your fingers. Come, follow me.'","A worn Relic of Time can likely be found in the nearby pools.\
\
You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic."},
[6928]={"Find a path through the Tower of Cirith Ungol","You are searching for a path to the tower-gate with Legolas. Remain on guard.","Shelob's children flee back beyond the Under-gate toward the tunnels of Torech Ungol!","You have come to the Under-gate, and a path out of the tower lies open before it!","Talk to Legolas in the Tower of Cirith Ungol","'We must go at once!'","Legolas is standing near the shattered remains of the Under-gate.\
\
Saernaston appears to have been devoured by Shelob herself. Belzagar has fled the tower, and now you and Legolas should as well.","You have come to the Under-gate and should now guard Belzagar's escape from Cirith Ungol.","Stand against Shelob's children at the Under-gate","Instancia: Mosquitos en su red","Defeat Saernaston","You suddenly notice green eyes leering at you in the shadows above!","'Belzagar has gone, and our hope now lies with him! We can do no more here!\
\
'Shelob comes! We must leave this place at once!'","'${PLAYER}, we have nearly made it to the Under-gate, but I fear the worst lies ahead of us. The tremors now shake the entire tower, and I fear it might crash down upon us at any moment.\
\
'We must move swiftly, but carefully. Webs choke the door and tunnels of the tower, and we could easily fall into a spider's trap!'\
\
Legolas turns to look at Belzagar.\
\
'Do not dare to deceive us, Man. Both of us are skilled enough to defeat you on our own! Send word to your masters as we bid, and you may still survive Shelob's wrath!'\
\
Legolas turns back to you.\
\
'No matter the danger, Belzagar must reach the gate. Are you prepared, my friend?'","Legolas is standing in the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\
\
You and Legolas plan to distract the spiders of Shelob's brood at the Under-gate to allow Belzagar to send word to Ugrukhôr and Rûkhor the Pale Herald. You should speak to Legolas when you are prepared.","You have been cornered in the depths of Cirith Ungol by the ancient spider, Saernaston. You must defeat him if you hope to escape!","In an attempt to warn the Gúrzyul of Shelob's growing wrath and secure Cirith Ungol, Legolas has decided to allow an emissary of Rûkhor the Pale Herald the opportunity to escape by distracting Shelob's brood at the Under-gate.","Pursue Shelob's children into Torech Ungol","Talk to Legolas at the Under-gate","Shelob's children have fled back beyond the Under-gate toward the tunnels of Torech Ungol. You should pursue them and prevent more from entering the Tower of Cirith Ungol.","You hear the cracking of Saernaston's carapace and terrible screeches echoing from the tunnels of Torech Ungol!"},
[6929]={"Sirgon waits below the stairs that climb to the Hungry Deep Tavern.","'I know my words are just words, Belondor, and I have given you little reason to believe them. But I speak this from my heart: King Elessar is a good man, and he desires only what is best for his people and for yours. He wants peace between Gondor and Umbar, and prosperity for both.\
\
'I know this is so. He is not the same as the Steward Denethor. Can the Kindred of the Coins come to see this, if Azagath no longer controls them? Can you, and they, work alongside the kingdom of Gondor, and not against it? Can you join hands with King Elessar, if it means setting aside war and conflict?'","Stand by Sirgon while he meets with Belondor","Belondor's wife Mêshka has arrived at the Hungry Deep Tavern, and she is not pleased to see that Sirgon has violated her ban upon returning to the Upper Ward.","Climb up to the Hungry Deep Tavern with Sirgon","Talk to Mêshka at the Hungry Deep Tavern","'I warned your friend Sirgon not to return to the Upper Ward! Does he think he remains out of reach and free from justice?\
\
'Rothog has slain many such men who believed themselves to be untouchable, and for less reason that this. Belondor has not forgotten how easily Sirgon cast aside his long friendship and was rewarded for it! He followed the Steward Denethor's commands, and questioned them not!'","Talk to Rothog at the Hungry Deep Tavern","Talk to Sirgon below the Hungry Deep Tavern","Belondor has suggested that Sirgon meet with him at the Hungry Deep Tavern, but it will be best if you and your crew attend the meeting as well... for the safety of all involved.","'What kind of bird was that?'\
\
You tell Rothog that the bird's name is Gwallang, and he is a Limlinn from across the Bay of Belfalas.\
\
'Gwallang. Limlinn. I have not heard these names before. He is brave for one so small.\
\
'But I came here for two purposes: to fight, and to fetch. I am disappointed there was no fight, but now you will come with me.\
\
'Hármelak wants to see you again.'","Remain alert to see what Rothog will do","Instancia: Gondor y Umbar","Talk to Sirgon at the Hungry Deep Tavern","Belondor wishes to speak with you at the Hungry Deep Tavern.","Rothog the Storm has questions for Belondor.","Sirgon is compelled to speak on behalf of King Elessar.","Talk to Belondor at the Hungry Deep Tavern","'I hope we have repaired something of the friendship we once possessed, Sirgon, but I am not ready to say the same of that between Gondor and Umbar. Your King has much to prove to us, for we have heard sweet words before, and were deceived. It will not happen again.\
\
'The Kindred of the Coins will survive without Azagath and Nakási. It was larger than both of them. It is larger than all of us, for it is Umbar. Your King will need to realize that if he believes there can be peace between our lands.'","Belondor wants to speak with you about the events that transpired beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo.","'Beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo he worked cruel magic, tearing the life from dear members of my crew, friends I have known for years. They died trusting me, Sirgon. They trusted I would bring them to safety, and trusted that their families would know they did not die for nothing.\
\
'But Azagath spent their lives for no purpose! Their deaths were needless, and provided only the smallest of delays so the Sea-shadow could make his escape! He did not know those men, and he discarded them without thought... only I am left to suffer the grief of their loss.'","Rothog the Storm has something to say to you.","You have agreed to stand by Sirgon with much of your crew while he meets with Belondor.","'Gondorians and Umbari are both alike in this: each of them uses too many words.\
\
'I came here for two purposes: to fight, and to fetch. I am disappointed there was no fight, but now you will come with me.\
\
'Hármelak wants to see you again.'","'I appreciate you and the crew of the Wave-hunter agreeing to accompany me to this meeting with Belondor, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Hungry Deep, and my fate, awaits me atop these steps.'"},
[6930]={"Por petición de Dwalin, has entrado en la Mansión de Thorin para confrontar a Gormr por su participación en el robo de Hen-heledh.","Dwalin informa a Mathi Manofirme, quien acaba de entrar, que tú le contarás la historia de tu batalla contra Marrec.","Con Marrec muerto y Hen-heledh a salvo, deberías atender a Dwalin.","Confronta a Marrec.","'¡Bah!'","Has encontrado a Gormr.","Mientras hablabas con Mathi, la dama Arwen entró y comenzó a atender las heridas de Dwalin. Deberías hablar con ella para saber cómo está.","Instancia: La Codicia de Gormr","En lugar de confrontar a Gormr, lo encontraste rodeado de trasgos. Con la distracción que provocaste, logró escapar, pero Marrec envió trasgos a atacarte. Debes defenderte.","Has derrotado a los trasgos, pero Dwalin ha caído. Deberías atenderlo.","Marrec ha derribado a Dwalin, dejándote solo para evitar su huida.","Has acompañado a Dwalin a la sala del trono de la Mansión de Thorin. Deberías hablar con él antes de confrontar a Gormr.","Has encontrado a Gormr, mortalmente herido por Marrec. Deberías hablar con él mientras aún vive.","Marrec ha robado el Espejo de Visión a Gormr. No debe escapar de la Mansión de Thorin con Hen-heledh.","Dwalin te ordena seguir a Marrec y detenerlo antes de que robe Hen-heledh a Gormr.","Sigue a Marrec."},
[6931]={"Can it be? How did Golodir come to Osgiliath before you, and what evil befell him here?","Talk to Derufin by the mighty ram Grond","You have found the broken body of the Ranger Golodir","Derufin has asked you to travel north through Osgiliath while he searches to the east for his brother Duilin and for Grond.","A flash of colour to the north-east! Can it be?","A feeling of dread falls upon you, and hazy images swim before your eyes","You have made your way with Derufin into enemy-occupied Osgiliath in search of the mighty ram Grond.","The enemy has brought a great weapon to Osgiliath, and you have volunteered to damage or destroy the mighty ram Grond before it can be used against Minas Tirith.","Talk to Derufin and ask him about the dreadful, ghostly images","Travel north through Osgiliath in search of Grond","Your heart is gripped by a sudden chill","You are drawn to the north-east... is that where Grond may be found?","Give your last respects to Golodir","'Before we left the culverts, I asked Damrod how we will know this ram called Grond, and he responded with laughter. When I pressed him on the matter, he said we would simply know, so it must be obvious, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us make our way through the city and see if he speaks the truth!'","Talk to Derufin within Osgiliath","Instancia: Gothmog Aparece","A terrifying foe has come to Osgiliath.","Your eyes must be playing tricks on you","Grond resists your efforts, but you do not give up (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Derufin and Duilin have caught up with you and marvel at the sheer size of the mighty ram Grond.","You have found Grond, and the mighty ram is undefended. Now is the time for you to damage its great wheels.","Derufin is within the city of Osgiliath, helping you search for Grond, the mighty weapon of the enemy.\
\
You experienced an overpowering feeling of dread within the city of Osgiliath, and felt the presence of ghostly images, but Derufin does not seem to have noticed any of the strange occurrences.","Talk to Duilin by the mighty ram Grond","Damage the great ram Grond (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have found Grond, great weapon of the Enemy","Stand with Duilin and Derufin within Osgiliath","'I stand in awe of your deeds, ${PLAYER}! You have managed to inflict some damage on the great weapon of the Enemy! It seems clear that the destruction of Grond itself is beyond our means, but you have inflicted enough damage to the structure that bears it, and that may slow its progress toward the gates of Minas Tirith!\
\
'My brother fought a number of Orcs within the city, well more than we encountered. He thinks they are preparing for a renewed assault.'","'What is wrong, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You ask Derufin what he makes of the ghostly images and the feeling of dread that accompanied them, and he looks at you with confusion.\
\
'I do not know of what you speak, friend. I see nothing but an absence of Orcs and the crumbling ruins of once-proud Osgiliath. You say that you saw more than that? Do you see it still?'","'I can tell by your face that something has you in its grip, ${PLAYER}, and it is frustrating to see you experience this devilry and be unable to help in any way! All I can say to you is to master your eyes, and distrust even convincing visions of horror, for they surely seek to lead you astray!\
\
'Duilin and I grew up in the Blackroot Vale, and we are no strangers to feelings of dread. But why do you feel this presence so keenly and I feel nothing?\
\
'The sooner we find Grond and destroy it, the sooner we will leave this place. If you are well enough to continue, you should search to the north and I will search to the east. Stand strong against whatever evil you find, my friend, and know that you are its better!'","Find Grond somewhere within Osgiliath","As you approach the fallen Ranger, your mind rebels at the thought that Golodir might have somehow gotten ahead of you and come to Osgiliath against Aragorn's command. How could he have come more swiftly than the Corsair ships, more swiftly than your own tread?\
\
The merest flickering doubt is enough to dispel your wondering mind, and you see now that the body lying on the cold stones of war-torn Osgiliath is not that of Golodir after all, but another soldier fallen in the defence.","Derufin is within Osgiliath, and has expressed concern over the increasingly potent visions you have experienced within the city.","'What a terrible weapon, ${PLAYER}. My brother and I took solemn vows when we were children to always look upon the bright side of a situation, but I must tell you that I am finding it difficult to maintain this outlook while confronted with the terrible Grond!\
\
'And yet, you managed to disable it, at least for a time. Even a weapon as frightful as this can be slowed! Hope springs in my breast even as I worry, and the worry passes!'"},
[6932]={"Gothmog has not yet exhausted his powers. With his illusions defeated he redoubles his attack!","Go with the disguised Ayorzén to Barad Cúron, pretending to be his prisoner","Survive the further assaults of Gothmog","Culang has succumbed to his wounds!","The watchful presence that guards the entrance to Barad Cúron has given you leave to enter the tower.","Draw upon the memory of Isildur for inspiration","Both weakened and enraged by your defiance, Gothmog presses the attack!","Ayorzén has disguised himself as Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and plans to bring you inside Barad Cúron as his prisoner.","Draw upon the memory of Elendil for inspiration","Gothmog stumbles in pain, cursing his mortality","Draw upon the memory of Narmeleth for inspiration","Culang believes you should use Gothmog's own weapons against him, reminding the wraith of those heroes who stood against darkness despite the evils arrayed against them. It is Culang's hope that the light of their inspiration will serve to weaken the wraith, sapping him of his strength.","Defeat Gothmog","Enter Barad Cúron and confront Gothmog","Talk to Ayorzén outside Barad Cúron","Draw upon the memory of Anárion for inspiration","Defeat the illusions of Mordirith","Inside Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon, the villain Gothmog awaits.","<rgb=#FF0000>Culang must survive</rgb>","Instancia: La ira de Gothmog","Ayorzén has disguised himself as Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and now he attempts to bring you and the Ranger Culang into Barad Cúron as his prisoners.","Draw upon the memory of Golodir for inspiration","'I hope you are ready for this, ${PLAYER}. Remember what I said! I will not die for you!'","Inside Barad Cúron, the wraith Gothmog attempts to demoralize you with painful memories of the past."},
[6933]={"Habla con un enano al borde del Lago Espejo","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a Mekhem-bizru! Me alegra ver que has salido de Moria con tu piel intacta. Debes ser ${PLAYERNAME:un guerrero[m]|una guerrera[f]} valiente.\
\
'Puedes descansar aquí y contemplar la belleza de Kheled-zâram.'","Sigue a Svanr hasta el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío","Svanr se encuentra en la Primera Sala de Nud-melek.","Vuelve con Svanr","El enano te invita a contemplar Kheled-zâram","Instancia: Saluda al cielo","Habla con Svanr","Habla con alguien en Mekhem-bizru","Svanr se encuentra fuera de Moria, en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Debes hablar con Svanr.","'Aquí estamos. Si no te importa, ${PLAYER}, me gustaría un momento a solas.'","Mekhem-bizru se encuentra al final del camino que parte de la Puerta Este de Moria.","'¡Qué justo y fresco es el Valle! Me alegra haber vivido para verlo.'","Las aguas de Kheled-zâram parecen frescas y claras, las estrellas brillando sobre la superficie como joyas relucientes.","'Hermoso, ¿no es así? Es cierto que las estrellas del Lago Espejo siempre brillan en la superficie del agua, ya sea de día o de noche. ¡Mira por ti mismo!'","Este es un buen punto de vista","'Me siento renovado y listo para regresar a las profundidades de Khazad-dûm para seguir ayudando a la expedición a establecerse.\
\
'¿Qué planeas hacer?'","'¡No puedo esperar para ver el sol, la luna, las nubes y las estrellas una vez más! Esta travesía ha sido larga y triste. Hemos sufrido muchas pérdidas.\
\
'No puedo estar más agradecido de volver a contemplar el hermoso sol, ${PLAYER}.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> el Lago Espejo desde Mekhem-bizru","El Lago Espejo, también llamado Kheled-zâram, es el lago que se encuentra junto a Mekhem-bizru en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Debes <rgb=#FF0000>mirar</rgb> el Lago Espejo desde Mekhem-bizru.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión requiere emotes.</rgb>","Es hora de dejar Moria por fin y disfrutar del aire fresco nuevamente.","Svanr se encuentra en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Debes hablar con Svanr.","Kheled-zâram es el gran lago que se encuentra en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Debes hablar con un enano que contemple Kheled-zâram."},
[6934]={"'The king ruled in my favour. Why then do I feel as if he also ruled against me? Did I win or did I lose?'","Instancia: Agravios","Accompany Authi as he presents his case before King Thorin","Talk to Authi","Talk to Hrostyr, King Thorin's personal guard","King Thorin has chosen to hear Authi Gem-cutter's grievance, but he will not do so at his throne.","'Khîl seeks to flatter me, but I am too wise a king to fall prey to such a tactic. I named my son Durin for my own reasons, and I do not feel the need to share them with Longbeards or with Zhélruka. He stays now in Járnfast with my brother Náin, Lord of the Iron Hills, and he will be king after me. If he is to be anything else is certainly beyond the sight of this Zhélruka.'\
\
King Thorin strokes his beard, and you might detect a slight upturn among his whiskers. Does he smile in spite of Khîl's flattery or because of it?\
\
'Durin the Deathless come again? Hmm. Imagine that!'","Listen to the judgement of King Thorin","'I suppose we should be going, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to my home and perhaps we can make sense of this.'","King Thorin has chosen to go among his people for the hearing of Authi's complaint.","Authi has heard the king's judgement and now wishes to speak with you.","'This is highly irregular. Why does the king choose not to hear this grievance at his throne? Would he not be more comfortable at his high seat?'","Talk to King Thorin","Authi Gem-cutter has asked for your help with bringing his grievance against Khîl Tale-spinner before the king.","Listen to Khîl's response before the king"},
[6935]={"An unwelcome smell fills the air....","Hildith has chosen to free the prisoner in hope that he will stop the attack","Hildith has asked you to watch and wait....","Elfhelm is with Hildith at the gate of Grimslade.","Talk to Hildith","Instancia: Bosque Oscuro arderá","'I see. It would seem we have all abandoned him....\
\
'Erkenbrand's host torn asunder by the Uruks, Prince Théodred's death in his arms....\
\
'His home closed to him, his soldiers dead....\
\
'And I, his fellow, leaving him alone where he stood.'\
\
Elfhelm's face is grave as he meets Hildith's eyes. 'I must take my leave, my lady, for Gandalf bade me to protect Edoras for the King.'","Hildith is in the jail of Grimslade.","Speak with Hildith once more","Hildith is in the jail of Grimslade.\
\
You should speak with Hildith.","Hildith is at the front gate of Grimslade.","Hildith has gone to the front gate of Grimslade.\
\
You should speak with Hildith.","Grimslade must be saved from the Half-orcs bringing fire.","Speak with Elfhelm","The half-orc who was moments ago a prisoner of Grimslade now stands before the gates of town.","'My poor husband. What have I done?!'\
\
Hildith sighs deeply as she turns to Elfhelm.\
\
'Good luck to you, Elfhelm. I will not forget what you have done for us this day. If I ever see Grimbold again, I will tell him of how your valour saved us all.'","Assist Hildith at the front gate","'Such a soft, foolish, trusting lot can have no place in the new Rohan -- a Rohan governed by Saruman the Wise!'","'I like not that Grimslade's fate hangs by the honour of a half-orc's oath....'","'Let us convene at the gate. I want to see to his safe departure myself.'","Grimslade is being attacked! Defend the city gate....","Stand your ground to defend Grimslade","Speak with Hildith","Defend Grimslade","'And now we wait, I suppose....\
\
'We have bolstered our defences somewhat, in case our friend decides not to keep his word. I cannot bring myself to go back inside just yet, and I'll feel much safer if you remain here with us, ${PLAYER}.'","Wait alongside Hildith and the guards of Grimslade","Speak with the prisoner","Follow Hildith","Listen to Hildith's decision","'Do we let the prisoner go free to keep his word, and call off the attack? Or do we hold him here, punish him, fight, and if we die, let him die with us?'","The half-orc who was moments ago a prisoner of Grimslade now stands before the gates of town.\
\
You should speak with the prisoner."},
[6937]={"Has recuperado una mitad de Narchuil y debes asistir al consejo convocado por Elrond para discutir el destino del anillo y analizar las acciones de Laerdan.","'No permaneceré inactivo en Imladris. Pronto buscaré los caminos que llevan al norte...'","Instancia: Medias verdades","Asiste al Consejo de Narchuil","'El consejo no puede continuar sin Laerdan. Hablaré contigo en privado en mi biblioteca, ${PLAYER}.'","'Temo lo que pueda suceder ahora que Laerdan ha regresado.'","Asiste al Consejo de Narchuil."},
[6940]={"Listen to Mizâdi speak to the other leaders","Continue listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders","'A real Subuzûri blade! This is quite the weapon! I shall not always use it, but when I do, know that I will think of you. My thanks.'","Give Mizâdi's gift to Rahâzi","Bow out of respect to Mizâdi","Speak with Mizâdi at Dun Shûma.","Bow out of respect to Mizâdi.","Mizâdi, Girhâzi, Rahâzi, Amalíbi, and Numûru have gathered outside Dun Shûma to discuss their victory and what is next for Shagâna.","Cheer with Mizâdi","Instancia: Hamât Renovado","Listen to the conversation between the leaders","'A saddle? Oh I see. Thank you. It has not been easy to come together with everything that has happened these past few weeks, but I thank you for this gift, and accept it in the spirit in which it is offered.'","'We accept this horn in the spirit in which it is given. If Hamât ever needs our aid, know that we shall remain at the ready to offer our Dumûri to aid her as well.","Continue listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.","Speak with Mizâdi at Dun Shûma","Give Mizâdi's gift to Amalíbi","Finish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders","Give Mizâdi's gift to Girhâzi","Gather gifts Mizâdi pointed out (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Cheer with Mizâdi!","Continue listening to the conversation","Give gifts to each of the leaders.","Gathered gifts (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Gather pile of gifts Mizâdi brought.","'Now that we are all gathered here, and the day has been won, I would have words and express my gratitude to each of you.'","Finish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders","Give Mizâdi's gift to Numûru","'I am grateful. This axe has a fine balance, and look at that blade! The skulls we shall split with her!'"},
[6941]={"Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld","Thane Edric can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
Thane Edric has argued with Éowyn and has now drawn his blade against her. You must defeat him.","Instancia: Negociaciones difíciles","DNT -- Players will not see","'If he spoke true, I grieve for his wife and people...\
\
'These are dark times in Rohan, and it pains me to see our people faced with such brutality. I know not when his madness will leave him, but I shall speak of the good he and Léoflad have done for our people and she shall live on in our songs.\
\
'I know not why he forced you to follow him here, but I am thankful that you fought alongside me.'","Listen to Edric and Éowyn's conversation","The glow of torches in the distance signals Éowyn's arrival","Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
You have defeated Edric, subduing him before his madness could inflict any harm on Éowyn. You should now speak to Éowyn.","Thane Edric can be found on the stairs to Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
You have arrived in Edoras and should now follow Edric as he seeks Éowyn.","Thane Edric is standing outside the doors to Meduseld.\
\
Thane Edric is clearly overcome by his recent loss. You should speak to him.","Following the tragic deaths of his wife and people, Thane Edric journeys to Edoras to confront Éowyn.","Thane Edric is outside Meduseld.\
\
Éowyn has arrived in response to Edric's shouts. You should wait until Edric demands your account of the events on the road to Aldburg.","Wait with Thane Edric","Knowing he is beaten, Edric yields and tears stream down his face","Edric's face betrays a seething rage","''Come, we have more to speak of.'","'Where is she? Where?!'\
\
Edric seems oblivious to your attempts to speak to him.","Follow Thane Edric to Meduseld","Talk to Thane Edric","Thane Edric is outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
Edric seeks an audience with Éowyn. You should wait at his side.","'It was a long ride, ${PLAYER}. I hope your wits are still about you. Now, let us seek Éowyn...'","DNT -- Player will not see","Thane Edric can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
You have ridden to Edoras with Thane Edric in search of Éowyn. You should follow Edric.","Defeat Thane Edric"},
[6942]={"Ofolmóth te ha revelado sus intenciones. No acatará las leyes de los Hombres.\
\
Langhár desea hablar contigo antes de que comience el combate.","Habla con Langhár en las ruinas","Has encontrado a Ofolmóth, y se pregunta si has venido a unirte a él.","'Sabía a qué veníamos, pero aun así me resistía a herir a Ofolmóth. Él no mostró tal reparo, y sus garras cortaron hondo.\
\
Langhár se estremece por el dolor de su herida.\
\
'No sé mucho acerca de Skorgrím, pero lo poco que he aprendido es inquietante. Me queda claro que manipuló de algún modo a nuestro antiguo pariente, aprovechándose de sus debilidades.\
\
'Hemos hecho lo que Grimbeorn nos pidió y puesto fin a la amenaza que Ofolmóth representaba para la gente inocente. Eso debe ser suficiente por hoy. Quizá mañana hagamos algo respecto a Skorgrím Duramano, pues su peligro aún persiste.'","Habla con Ofolmóth","Has llegado con Langhár a las Ciénagas del Sur en busca de Ofolmóth. Ella espera hablar contigo antes de continuar hacia las ruinas donde se vio por última vez a tu pariente.","'Regresemos a Ost Guruth. Estoy herida, pero puedo caminar.'","Sobrevive a tu encuentro con Ofolmóth","Instancia: El odio al oso y al Hombre","Has encontrado a Ofolmóth, pero ya no es de tu sangre. Ahora es tu enemigo.","Habla con Langhár en las Ciénagas del Sur","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ? Ofolmóth no vendrá con nosotros, pero no podemos dejarlo libre, pues es un peligro para la gente inocente de la Tierra Media. No sé mucho sobre estos enanos, pero puedo decir que este Skorgrím corrompe a cualquiera que entra en contacto con él.\
\
'¡Yo me encargaré de Ofolmóth si tú puedes ocuparte de estos enanos, ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}!'","Langhár ha sido herida de gravedad, pero sigue con vida.","¡Langhár está en dificultades!","'Tu expresión me da la respuesta, ${PLAYER}. Ya lo suponía. Fue una vana esperanza creer que honrarías la memoria de nuestro pueblo y la sangre de Beorn. En cambio, te pones del lado de quienes no son dignos de ti.\
\
'Creí que podía hacerte fuerte, ${PLAYER}. Fracasé en eso, y lo lamento.'","Ofolmóth ha herido gravemente a Langhár y debe ser derrotado.","Has llegado con tu hermana Langhár a las Ciénagas del Sur de las Tierras Solitarias en una misión triste: poner fin a los males cometidos por tu pariente Ofolmóth.","Derrota a Ofolmóth por sus crímenes contra la gente inocente","'Ofolmóth fue visto por última vez entre las ruinas que tenemos delante. Avancemos con cautela, ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}.'"},
[6943]={"Burn the carcass of the fell-beast","Wrap the head of the fell-beast in the heavy cloth given to you by Mithrandir.","Talk to Éomer on the Pelennor.","Talk to Mithrandir near the corpse of the fell-beast.","Mithrandir greets the scholars of the Houses of Lore","'Thank you for your help with this unpleasant burden, ${PLAYER}. Such creatures are bred in the darkness of Mordor, and little is known of them, save that they are raised in corruption and used for evil. They are fed vile meats and treated unkindly, and have proved fitting steeds for the Enemy's most powerful lieutenants.\
\
'Can they teach us anything more? Perhaps our friends here will learn something valuable from this study, and perhaps not. But I am glad to have given them the opportunity for such learning, if there is a chance it might be had.'","The corpse burns with eerie flames","Mithrandir takes the wrapped fell-beast head from you","'You should return to Aragorn's Pavilion, if you are finished here.'","Mithrandir gives you a heavy cloth in which to wrap the head of the fell-beast","Talk to Éomer by the burning carcass of the fell-beast","Now that you have wrapped the head of the foul steed in heavy cloth, Mithrandir asked that you burn the corpse of the fell-beast.","Stand by as Mithrandir speaks with the scholars of the Houses of Lore.","Mithrandir has taken an interest in the slain fell-beast that once served as the steed of the Witch-king of Angmar, Lord of the Nazgûl.","Remain alert while Mithrandir speaks with the scholars at the Houses of Lore","'The dead beast and its foul master have both been cleansed from the Pelennor, and for that you have my thanks, but the memory of them lingers.\
\
'I would have seen both head and body burned, but if it is Gandalf's wish that the head be preserved for scholarly study, I will not gainsay him.'","Talk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Lore.","Wrap the fell-beast head in the cloth","Talk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Lore","'Let us away to the Houses of Lore, ${PLAYER}, and we will bring with us our freshly-wrapped burden. May the cloth shroud the eyes of any who see us pass, for such a burden will work fear in the hearts of folk of the city, even if its days of rending and tearing are done.\
\
'The greatest evil it poses now is against the nose, ${PLAYER}. Let us deliver it to the scholars with this advice: keep it not in an enclosed space; rather, let the place of its study be an airy one, and dispose of the foul-smelling relic when you have learned all you can of it!'","Travel to the Houses of Lore with Mithrandir","Instancia: Cabeza de la Bestia Caída","Talk to Mithrandir by the carcass of the fell-beast","'The carcass of the fell-beast still mars the field at which it breathed its last, and it remains a foul reminder of the villain it bore. It must be removed.\
\
'I had thought to do so quickly and without ceremony, but a number of scholars from the city beseeched me, wishing to preserve some part of the creature for their study. Take this heavy cloth and wrap the head in it, so it may be safely transported to these scholars.\
\
'We will then burn the body, for it cannot be allowed to fester here at the site of Théoden King's ending.'","Travel to the Houses of Lore with Mithrandir and deliver the head of the fell-beast to the scholars there.","Talk to Mithrandir by the burning carcass of the fell-beast"},
[6944]={"More Ungoledain are approaching!","'Good work, ${PLAYER}. We have secured Rhosgobel, for now.\
\
'I fear our time to rest will be cut short, my friend. More of the Ungoledain approach as we speak! Prepare yourself, ${RACE}. I will do what I can to assist you.'","Defeat Ungoledain at Rhosgobel","Defend Rhosgobel from the Ungoledain.","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso.","Instancia: Atendiendo a la llamada","Defeat Mengris Tásakh.","Defeat Ungoledain at Rhosgobel.","Talk to Radagast outside his cottage.","'It is done. The Ungoledain will no longer linger here.'","Listen to Radagast","Radagast is concerned that the Ungoledain may have come to Laerlad because they are searching for Rhosgobel.","The Ungoledain retreat","Defend Rhosgobel from the Ungoledain","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso","Defeat Mengris Tásakh","Talk to Radagast outside his cottage"},
[6945]={"Your head is pounding.","You have encountered a daring hobbit lass while searching for a way to cleanse the corruption from the sceptre that came out of Mordor.","Examine the tomb in Haudh Nogbenn","'I will return to my home, and you will go on your way. Where are you going? Rivendell? My goodness, that sounds exciting!'","There is a hobbit girl in Haudh Nogbenn! What is she doing here?","Instancia: Reliquia de Cardolan","'What happened to you? You were standing there and staring at the tomb for a really long time. I tried to snap you out of it, but you didn't answer until just now!'\
\
The sceptre has been cleansed of its corruption, and you thank Marigold for her assistance. When you ask her what she thought of the shade of the Cardolan prince, she looks at you with complete and utter disbelief.\
\
'Are you telling me the truth? I cannot BELIEVE this! There was a mysterious shade here and I MISSED it? What a disaster! It sounds as if you accomplished what you set out to do, which is good, but I am not very happy that I missed out on seeing any shades or princes.'","You found a fallen shield outside Haudh Nogbenn. Has someone been taken inside the barrow, and now needs your help?","'Hullo there, are you an adventurer? My name is Marigold, and I have been stomping all over the barrow-downs in search of excitement. I thought I heard the barking of a dog or a hound, and came to this barrow to search for it, but there is no sign of the curious beast. I hope it is all right! What brought you to this place? I can see that you are a Guardian, so is it a general desire to face danger or is there something more to it?'\
\
You tell the unusual hobbit lass that a sceptre infused with corruption came into your possession, and you believe bringing it to this barrow may help cleanse it of its evil.\
\
'Well, it is worth a try! I see you have my shield there, so I will take it back, and let's go see if we can fix this sceptre!'","Marigold Boffin is in Haudh Nogbenn.","Listen to the words of the slain prince","'What happened to you, ${PLAYER}? You were standing there and staring at the tomb for a really long time. I tried to snap you out of it, but you didn't answer until just now!'\
\
The sceptre has been cleansed of its corruption, and you thank Marigold for her assistance. When you ask her what she thought of the shade of the Cardolan prince, she looks at you with complete and utter disbelief.\
\
'Are you telling me the truth? I cannot BELIEVE this! There was a mysterious shade here and I MISSED it? What a disaster! It sounds as if you accomplished what you set out to do, which is good, but I am not very happy that I missed out on seeing any shades or princes. Next time, ${PLAYER}! Next time.'","Talk to the owner of the shield and protect them from harm","Talk to Marigold Boffin","Has someone fallen into danger in Haudh Nogbenn?","Search for someone in danger inside Haudh Nogbenn","There is a tomb in Haudh Nogbenn. Is this the final resting place of the sceptre's owner?","It's Marigold Boffin!","'I say, if it isn't ${PLAYER}! It is good to see that you have not abandoned the adventuring life! Is cousin Bingo with you? What a pity that he is not!\
\
'I have been stomping all over the barrow-downs in search of excitement. I thought I heard the barking of a dog or a hound, and came to this barrow to search for it, but there is no sign of the curious beast. I hope it is all right! What brought you to this place, other than a Guardian's general desire to face danger?'\
\
You tell Marigold that a sceptre infused with corruption came into your possession, and you believe that bringing it to this barrow may help cleanse it of its evil.\
\
'Well, it is worth a try, ${PLAYER}! I see you have my shield there, so I will take it back, and let's go see if we can fix this sceptre!'"},
[6946]={"'Thrótrun and the rune-keepers could not leave the Chamber of Machurful, but I wonder if something managed to get in: an ancestor of the great beast that attacked us?'\
\
Greith sighs heavily, and strokes his beard.\
\
'Perhaps it would give them some joy, if they could see it, to know that the door was eventually opened. Would they be glad to know they are remembered, even too late? I hope so, ${PLAYER}. I hope so.'","Dwarves died here, but there is no sign of Orc-kind in these rooms","Greith is in the central chamber, just east of the geode.","Talk to Greith in the central chamber, just north of the geode","Greith has asked you to search the room to the east of the Chamber of Machurful.","'I found a tablet of stone by the geode, ${PLAYER}, and it bears writing on its face. It appears to be a list of rune-keepers who served in the Chamber of Machurful. None of the names are familiar to me, save one: Thrótrun.\
\
'She was a rune-keeper of great renown, and many lessons of the art can be traced to her teachings. Thrótrun lived in Khazad-dûm during the time of Durin, but none knew of her fate. It was believed she perished during the fall of Moria, and it seems that is the case after all.'\
\
Greith scratches at his beard.\
\
'This list of rune-keepers has a solemn feel about it. The carving of runes takes time, even for a skilled artisan. I think this list was made to mark their deaths.'","The Key of the Forgotten has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!","<rgb=#FF0000>Greith must not be defeated</rgb>","Greith has asked you to search the room to the north of the Chamber of Machurful.","Greith is in the central chamber, by the tremendous geode.","Defeat Grotcleaver","Greith survived the battle with Grotcleaver, and wishes to speak with you.","Grotcleaver falls, last resident of Machurful","Talk to Greith","You have unlocked a door in Khazad-dûm that has remained sealed for more than a thousand years.","'The key no longer bears the corruption of Mordor! You are welcome to keep it, ${PLAYER}, as a memento of Thrótrun and her rune-keepers. The Chamber of Machurful will be locked no longer, in memory of the wrong that was done to them. Bring the key where you will, and may it serve you well!'","Search the northern chamber","Search the southern chamber and return to Greith","Talk to Greith in the central chamber","Grotcleaver, a tremendous deep-claw, has made its home in the Chamber of Machurful.","Greith has been defeated!","Search the rooms to the east","Greith is in the central chamber, just north of the geode.","Talk to Greith in the central chamber, just east of the geode","'You found the skeletons of dwarves, but no Orc or goblin remains? I begin to worry that the rune-keepers fought among themselves, ${PLAYER}. By Durin's name I hope it is not so.\
\
'I have found more of Thrótrun's writing, and it may help us to understand what happened here. It seems that the rune-keepers were sealed away in the Chamber for their own protection. None knew the extent of what was happening. They believed that the shaking in the earth would not last; they did not know Moria would fall into darkness for a thousand years.\
\
'She writes of a dwarf named Orthvord, who took the key to Machurful and swore to keep it safe. He vowed he would return when the trouble had passed and let the rune-keepers out. But he never came back. Thrótrun writes that some of the others despaired, but she never told them what she believed in her heart: that Orthvord was slain, the key taken.\
\
'She was right, and eventually the key came into evil hands, but the one who took it did not know the door it unlocked. The key was taken into Mordor, and the rune-keepers were forgotten.'","Greith has asked you to search the room to the south of the Chamber of Machurful.","Instancia: Reliquia de Khazad-dûm","Bodies lie in the northern chamber, but the shelves are undisturbed","'I cannot believe what we have found, ${PLAYER}. This must be the Chamber of Machurful, long believed forever lost! It was a place for the keeping of powerful rune-stones and the secrets of their use, but none still living knew where to find it! Before Moria fell into ruin, the most talented of rune-keepers might have known its location, but they are all long dead.\
\
'Ah, I understand. The door locks from the outside, for the secrets contained within the Chamber might be put to deadly use. Machurful must have been sealed when Durin died, and the key lost.'"},
[6947]={"Listen to the words of Nathlad","Nathlad has ended his patrol and now stands before you, deep in thought.","'I have also given up the free-booter's life, if you must know. Shortly after my captain left, I changed the name of the ship to Valatëa, and we are now mostly honest men. Mostly.\
\
'Thank you for hearing me out, stranger. I think it did me some good to remember my former captain, and to speak of his choice. You are welcome to keep that rigging-hook, if you would desire it. It was named Anchor of the Past by my friend Dírharn, but it need not be such a weight for you. May it be a help to you in the journeys that lie ahead.'","Nathlad has brought you down to the bridges that now cross the Anduin, above which stands the city of Osgiliath.","Talk to Nathlad by the bridges that cross the River Anduin","'When those soldiers of Gondor passed over the great bridge, heading east, they did not come down here to the water's edge. I am not surprised: their eyes are ever on the horizon, dreaming about the great things they plan to accomplish for the lord that gave them their orders. It falls to common folk like me and my fellows to take care of everything else.\
\
'In this case, that means the Orcs that hid down here when the army passed by. We are going to take care of these stragglers. Come! I will tell you about that rigging-hook while we work, and you can tell me how you came by it.'","Nathlad has agreed to tell you what he knows about the rigging-hook you recovered from Mordor, but he wants you to help him with his work along the river.","'Goodbye, stranger. I will count you from this day forward a friend of mine, and of Dírharn.'","Talk to Nathlad","Instancia: Reliquia de Osgiliath","'It is now your turn, stranger. How did you come to find Dírharn's rigging hook?'\
\
You tell Nathlad that it was found within a stronghold in Mordor, and you hoped to cleanse it of the corruption that ensnared it.\
\
'In the depths of Mordor, you say? There is a story here, to be certain, for I watched him cast that rigging-hook into the Anduin not far from this very spot. Did an Orc or some other fell creature fish it from the river and bring it on dark paths into the Black Land? That is a better answer than the one I suspected, the one for which I led you down here.\
\
'I thought to test your loyalties, and if you proved a friend to the Orcs I would have buried my sword in your back for the murder of my friend. But I think now you are what you claim to be.'","Nathlad has come to a conclusion."},
[6948]={"Instancia: Reliquia de Rhudaur","The coffer contains only dust. What a waste!","'You have betrayed the Corcur! You are not who you claimed to be!\
\
'I don't know what you did, but you have spoiled a priceless artifact of Rhudaur; it can no longer be used in sacrifice. You have ruined it forever! For that you will die, betrayer!'","You have entered the Rhudauran Lost Temple in an attempt to cleanse the evil from the corrupted cup that came to you out of Mordor.","Fithákh falls. She will not see the Corcur rise, after all","The cultist has mistaken you for a friend","An enterprising soul has already looted this coffin","Talk to Fithákh in the inner chamber","Fithákh asked you to set the cup on the tomb in the middle of the inner chamber, saying that it will serve as an altar for a sacrifice.","You feel light-headed. Suddenly, a cool breeze rushes through the chamber!","'There you are! I must confess, you are not what I expected, but the Corcur need every ally they can get if we are to recover from such defeats as we have suffered. Do you have the artifact?'\
\
Unsure what she might be expecting, you withdraw the corrupted cup from your pack and show it to her. She gasps.\
\
'A cup of sacrifice! I did not dare to dream I would ever see one in the flesh! I was told you had one of Ferndúr's totems, but I never expected this! Set it on the tomb. It will serve as an altar, and perhaps I can find a beast with blood to serve. It has been so long since these walls have seen a proper sacrifice, and that is worth far more to me than a gaunt-lord's totem!'","You hastily leave the Lost Temple. Fithákh is not your concern","Set the corrupted cup on the central tomb","Explore the Lost Temple and find a way into the innermost chamber","There must be some way to get into the innermost chamber of the Lost Temple, where Elrond believes the corrupted cup might be redeemed.","Either leave the inner chamber or put an end to Fithákh's villainy","Sadly, the brazier contains nothing of value","Fithákh, a cultist of the Corcur, has gained entrance to the innermost chamber of the Lost Temple. She seems to be expecting someone.","You have done what you set out to do, and now you can either leave the chamber with haste or put an end to Fithákh's villainy."},
[6949]={"'This was not long ago, by the counting of Ents, but you would feel otherwise. Years? Perhaps, yes, you would say years, but it feels much shorter to me.'","Talk to Rattleleaf and get him back on track","'The earthborn and the earth-kin were given similar instructions, little ${RACE}. We may not be kindred, but we tend to the same concerns and our purposes are not opposed. The divide between us is a small one only.\
\
'The divide between the earth-kin I witnessed was much wider, and it was caused by Angmar. Ah, that is a name malignant. Hrumty bum, hroomty boom! The seed-bag went to Angmar, but it did not stay there. They could not open it. Somehow it came to you, and it was sealed tight, and there was evil all around it.\
\
'But now the pouch has been freed from the corruption that ensnared it. It is a gift from he who remained. Go now where you can best make use of his gift. I will stay here, and remember. Hroom, broom, toom!'","Rhothlas has begun to tell you the tale of what he saw by the still pool.","Rattleleaf has agreed to tell you the story of what he saw by the pool beneath Kar Lak. Will hearing his tale help you to cleanse the Earth-kin pouch of its corruption?","'Hoom, oh yes, you wanted to hear the tale of the one who remained behind. I am sorry. For an Ent, every detail is important to convey, but you smaller races do not drink deeply of every flavour in the same way.'","Rattleleaf is by the still pool beneath Kar Lak, waiting to tell you his tale.","Listen to Rattleleaf's tale","Rattleleaf is by the pool beneath Kar Lak.","Instancia: Reliquia de los Hijos de la tierra","Rattleleaf seems to have distracted himself, and needs reminding of the story he was going to tell.","'He who remained could have given up his task, and lived. He did not, and did not, and now it has come to you. Hrum, hoom.'","Talk to Rattleleaf and hear his tale","Talk to Rattleleaf","Rattleleaf has told you the story of Trotsiv, unhappy though it was.","'The other creatures went away, but the first remained behind, and returned to the earth. Hoom, boom, toom.'\
\
'I saw it all, but it is not the place of the Ents to interfere in the lives of other creatures. My own charge is to tend to the trees; I am not a shepherd of anything else. She who made the earth-kin would understand, hoom, boom, toom.'\
\
Rattleleaf's eyes are deep pools, and you cannot be certain, but they seem to hold a deep sorrow.\
\
'I know that this is so, root and branch... but... I also know that I have done wrong, little ${RACE}.'"},
[6950]={"Darothild's shade stands before you at the Spring of the Red-maid, where she lost her final battle.\
\
Walgar has asked you to show the corrupted sculpture to Darothild's shade.","You know beyond any doubt: this is the shade of Darothild, who fell at the Spring of the Red-maid.","'These ruins are curiously empty, ${PLAYER}. It feels to me as if some presence waits for us, holding its breath! Does the Red-maid live again, thinking to seize us and pull us beneath the foetid water?\
\
'We all listened to the Stone-speaker's tale, and in the mid-day light of Ost Guruth this seemed like an idea with merit. If the sculpture you carry is truly a carving of the warrior-woman Darothild, bringing it to the site of her last battle might cure it of the corrupting ailment that surrounds it. But now that we are at the place, I am not as certain!\
\
'Let us finish this, then, but stay on your guard! This place ended Darothild. I do not wish for it to signal our ends as well!'","Walgar is at the Spring of the Red-maid.","Darothild's shade stands before you at the Spring of the Red-maid, where she lost her final battle.","'Where next will you go? To Rivendell? I wish you good fortune, my friend.'","You have survived the onslaught of enemies at the Spring of the Red-maid, but now a mysterious figure has revealed herself.","Talk to Walgar at the Spring of the Red-maid","'Stay back! I will not hesitate to put you in the ground! My spear has tasted the blood of so many, and for the defence of my people and my land it will drink deeply of yours, villain!'\
\
Darothild falls silent as you begin to speak. You speak calmly, with quiet words, but each one cuts deeper than the one before it, deadlier than any of your other weapons. You tell of the stories that were passed down among the Eglain, stories about Darothild, the mighty champion who faced the Red-maid in defence of her people and never returned.","Talk to Darothild's shade","Aric the Stone-speaker told you that the carving seems to be of Darothild, a champion who defied the Red-maid long ago, and was lost.","Defend Walgar from the Woman at the Spring","Show the corrupted sculpture to Darothild's shade","Instancia: Reliquia de los Eglain","Ease Darothild's pain","There can be no doubt. This is the shade of Darothild","'Where did you find this? I would know this carving anywhere, for it was a gift from my love. He begged me not to go. He gave me presents and gifts he carved from wood and stone and bone and tusk, but I refused them all. I carried my love for him to this place, and my spear, and nothing else.\
\
'All else is clouded to me, but I can see his face more clearly than anything else in this shadowed world. He must be long dead now, my Bemwin.'\
\
You tell Darothild that the Eglain have found many similar sculptures in the swamp-lands; Bemwin must have lived long enough to make many such carvings. She smiles sadly at you.","'The story of Darothild was a sad one, ${PLAYER}, but it was told to children of the Eglain to impress upon them the importance of standing and fighting against evil, even if it is not easy. Especially if it is not easy.\
\
'The carving has been cleansed of its corruption, and the shade of Darothild has escaped from her long captivity. Those are both worthy goals to have accomplished this day! I think she will be glad for you to hold onto her carved image, ${PLAYER}, especially if it will help you combat evils such as the Red-maid.\
\
'Let us leave this place, and then I will bid you farewell. May the Image of the Champion serve you well!'","You have come with some Eglain warriors to the Spring of the Red-maid. Here it may be that you can remove the corruption that encircles the carving of Darothild."},
[6951]={"Talk to Techeron at the Bridge of Ariant","Talk to Techeron","'The badge has been cleansed of its corruption? We have made proud whatever forgotten warden wore this badge in defence of his king, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I have thought of something as well. The guards of the city in days of old wore these badges to signify their posts, but I am grateful that we have not maintained that tradition. If the Steadfast Sisters were consigned to their own posts, they would not have come here to Ariant when they did, and Olcránnag might have escaped to work further evil. Truthfully, there is no man save Elessar alone who might be able to command the Sisters and have them heed it, but still I am glad that wardens and Rangers go where they are needed, not where they are assigned to be.\
\
'Where next will you go? To Rivendell, to speak with Elrond? Give him my regards, for I must stay here and hold the line against Angmar.'","The Ranger Techeron is near the Bridge of Ariant.","Instancia: Reliquia del Gran Rey","The Badge of Ariant has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!","'Safe journey to Rivendell, my friend.'","The Ranger Techeron is at the Bridge of Ariant, in Annúminas.","'Let us cross the bridge, and remain vigilant! The forces of Angmar crept back into the city while we were in the South-lands, and they may seek to surprise us.'","You have come with Techeron to the Bridge of Ariant with the hope that the corrupted badge might be cleansed of its evil."},
[6952]={"Habla con Umín","Umín stands outside the docked ship, waiting to speak with you.","'Where next will you go? To Rivendell? I wish you good fortune, my friend.'","Umín has collected the necklace from where it lay, and he wishes to speak with you about it.","Habla con Mal Juntahierbas","Investigate the forsaken ship","'I'll think about it, but I make no promise that you will not see me again, Brawler.'","Others have come to the lost ship for some unknown purpose, and you should learn what they intend.","Umín's words have had an effect on Mal Stackwort, but whether they will last remains to be seen.","'I know not how this necklace came to the land of Mordor, ${PLAYER}, but I am certain now that this is the very same artifact that caused me so much trouble and grief on the deck of this very ship. What servant of evil could have brought it to that place, and for what purpose? I cannot say, but this I know: the Spirit of the Necklace is well and truly gone. I feel its absence as strongly as I feel the wooden deck beneath my feet.\
\
'Gone too is the corruption that enveloped this necklace as a result of its stay in the Black Land. I think it is fitting that you take it now, and make whatever use of it you deem right. It no longer has any hold upon me, and I am left in peace at last. I hope Mal Stackwort and his fellows will find freedom from their own controlling spirit, Man though he be.'\
\
You thank Umín for the gift of the necklace, and tell him you believe Elrond of Rivendell will be able to imbue it with some force for Good.\
\
'I hope so, my friend. Go to Rivendell with my good wishes.'","Mal Stackwort has no idea of the meaning behind Umín's words, and has asked you to explain them.","Mal Stackwort, former minion of Bill Ferny, leads a crew of cutthroats intending to free the forsaken ship from its trapped berth.","Instancia: Reliquia de lo Ordinario","Umín has returned with you to the forsaken ship where the Spirit of the Necklace was defeated, hoping to aid you in cleansing the corruption from the necklace you found in Mordor, and perhaps to find some measure of peace for himself.","'Well? Why does this fellow say I shouldn't take this ship and go a-pirating?'\
\
You briefly describe Umín's experience with the Spirit of the Necklace, which culminated with the shade seizing control of the poor adventurer's body and turning him against his allies on this very ship's deck, before the spirit was finally defeated and Umín freed from its influence.\
\
'He can't have been completely freed, can he?' Mal muses wryly. 'He came back here, didn't he? Are you certain this spirit was truly defeated? It sounds powerful.'","Mantente en guardia","'See? It is just as I said: whatever force gave life to the traps within these caverns has fled. Was it the Spirit of the Necklace, or some other power? Whatever it might have been, it is gone now.\
\
'But I hear voices ahead. Who else has come to this forsaken ship?'","Defeat Mal Stackwort's crew of cutthroats"},
[6953]={"The Orcs that captured Eldmath belong to the Boar-tribe and are led by Tharbag.","Remain alert and look for an opportunity to free Eldmath","Instancia: Reliquia de la Marca de los Jinetes","Eldmath was taken eastward to Gris-shâtroful","Talk to Tharbag","Talk to Eldmath","Tharbag's Orcs have captured Eldmath, and you really should free him... he was holding onto the corrupted tusk-shard when he was taken!","Sneak into Gris-shâtroful from the back","Skámash has been left in charge of dealing with you. This will likely prove to be a mistake!","Tharbag has foolishly left a single Orc to deal with you","The Vengeance of Folca has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!","Talk to Skámash","Eldmath has run into some trouble while out in the field, and now he has been captured by Orcs. Even worse, he was holding onto the corrupted tusk-shard when he was taken!","'Well-done, ${PLAYER}! I would say both of us have proven to be heroes this day, wouldn't you? To think that this shard came from the tusk which gave King Folca his mortal wound... and in its own way it proved the undoing of the Boar-tribe Orcs who worshipped it! I think Folca would be very pleased about that, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It is an heirloom of Rohan, but you are welcome to keep it. I have had enough of adventuring, for now, and will return to Aldburg. Perhaps I will add this verse to the songs I sing about King Folca and his campaign against the Orcs. Yes, I will do just that!'","'Curse that Tharbag, leaving me to deal with you! He is afraid to fight you, I can tell! Pah!'\
\
A cunning light creeps into Skámash's eyes.\
\
'But if I slay you, that will prove I am stronger than Tharbag, and that lot will see I am fit to be the boss, and he is not! Ah, Tharbag, you fool! You have given me just what I need to take your place as leader of the Boar-tribe!'","Gris-shâtroful is to the east, and you might be able to drop down from above and surprise the Orcs that captured Eldmath.","Eldmath is in Gris-shâtroful, waiting to speak with you.","'The Boar-tribe has lurked in the shadows for too long! With you two as captives, we will at last be seen as the power we deserve!'","You have found Eldmath, but the Orcs were alerted to your presence.","'I will return to the tavern, there to add my new verse. Where will you go? Rivendell? I have never heard of it, is it far from here? Safe travels, ${PLAYER}!'","Survive the encounter with Tharbag"},
[6954]={"Lothrandir is in the village of Sûri-kylä.","Pinja has been defeated!","'I have, and she has never been better! Her husband Oiva has returned! All thought him dead, but he lives still and has come back to the village! I was just going to spread the glad news!\
\
'Pinja is no longer a widow, for her Oiva is alive!'","Talk to Pinja in front of her home","You never met Oiva, but this does appear to be a warrior of the Lossoth. As you study the still form, you feel a sharp pain behind your eyes and a throbbing in your head.","A Lossoth warrior claims that Pinja's dead husband Oiva has returned to life. How can this be?","The widow Pinja is outside her home, in Sûri-kylä.","The Brooch of Bone has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!","Remain alert for any further treachery by Hamaito","Lothrandir has been defeated","Something is afoot in the the village of the Lossoth, and Lothrandir fears that the corruption that infuses the brooch may have done some harm to the widow to whom he returned it.","Habla con Pinja","'I should have known that Hamaito was clouding my mind, ${PLAYER}. In the dungeons of Isengard I resisted Saruman's torments, but there I knew of the Wizard's tricks. I knew to resist them! The corruption that affixed to the brooch in Mordor drew Hamaito to it, and he hid his lesser evil in that greater one, and was masked therein.\
\
'That the corruption went with Hamaito when he was cast out is useful to us; in that way he did us a good turn! Perhaps that is the greatest jest of all.\
\
'Farewell for now, my friend! Give my regards to Elrond in Rivendell, and I hope he is able to infuse the brooch with a force for Good, as Mithrandir believes. Until we meet again!'","Find Pinja and learn what has happened","Hamaito has been defeated, and the corruption of Oiva's bone brooch has been cleansed.","'Do you think I would not know my own husband? Oiva was mine, and when the ice claimed him it was as if a piece of me was taken too. I do not know what thing has taken his shape and pretends to be him, but it is not my husband. It is not my Oiva.\
\
'I clubbed it over the head and left it behind my home. You can see it if you like.'","Lothrandir is in Sûri-kylä.","Talk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä","Pinja told you that whatever has taken her husband Oiva's shape is currently unconscious behind her home.","'Quickly, ${PLAYER}! The widow Pinja lives to the south-west, and if the brooch has worked some evil upon her that is where we must go!'","Instancia: Reliquia de los Hombres de las Nieves","'Farewell for now, my friend!'","A spirit has masqueraded as Pinja's slain husband for its own cruel jest, but you have now revealed it.","Defeat Hamaito","Hamaito has revealed himself and seeks to avenge the spoiling of his jest.","Examine the unconscious body behind Pinja's home","The cold air shimmers as if beheld through a haze of heat","A Lossoth warrior has news of Pinja's whereabouts in Sûri-kylä.","'The spirit Hamaito was to blame for the deaths of our missing warriors, and he would have done injury to all of the Lossoth if he could. I am glad that you and Lothrandir aided me in casting him back to nothing.\
\
'For the aid you rendered to me, I give to you Oiva's brooch. I do not need it to remember my husband. I deem that the evil with which it attracted Hamaito attached itself to him as he carried out his jest. It went with him into the far reaches when we cast him out.\
\
'May Oiva's brooch of bone help you as you adventure, and render your aid on behalf of those who need it. Not all people are Lossoth, and will have more need of you than we!'","Talk to the Lossoth warrior in Sûri-kylä"},
[6955]={"'I give the needle to you. Bear it with you on your journey, and remember Deilur!'","'And now you have come to my village, and you bear a needle so like those used by Deilur those many years ago. You say that it came from a place of evil, and the feeling of it is so corrupt that I do not question it. I can tell you the story of that needle, for now I know its ending.\
\
'Maushkán was made weak by Deilur's needle, and it caused him a great deal of pain, but it was sunk deep into his flesh and he could not remove it. He returned in time to his own land, but every day was a torment, for the needle pained him so. He must have learned to live with the pain, but every sharp twinge was a reminder of Deilur's defiance. There was no day he did not think of Deilur, and in that way he was very like me.\
\
'But while I am now grown old, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, I think Maushkán did not reach such an age. There came a day when he succumbed, at last, to the pain of Deilur's needle, and when his body was gone only the needle remained. Perhaps some villain picked it up, never knowing what it signified, or any of its history, and it came by long roads to you, and then to me.\
\
'This needle travelled many leagues to have its vengeance upon Maushkán, but now its task is done. Farewell, Deilur! You have been avenged, and this old woman remembers you and what you did, and always will. And now ${PLAYER} will as well.'","'Yes, I am ready to continue. Sometimes words must travel through darkness to reach the light. We are quite in the darkness now.'","Raiglud is telling you a tale from her childhood.","Raiglud is ready to continue her tale.","Talk to Raiglud and listen to the rest of her story","Raiglud has told you she needs to rest a moment, for the telling of this tale is taking a lot out of her.","Raiglud has a story to tell, and perhaps hearing it will help you to cleanse the needle of the corruption that surrounds it.","Raiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has begun to tell you a tale from her childhood.","'Before the Uch-lûth came to be Algraig, our home was in the south, in Dunland. I was very young then, and I spent my days climbing the hills and scaring the birds with my shouting. I was a fiery child, and the elders ran out of ways to discipline me. Then they sought to beseech my better nature, hoping I might calm somewhat and learn the art of the tailor.\
\
'That did not work either, so they gave it up, and let me do as I would. That was the smartest thing they might have done! Ha! Ha!'","Consider Raiglud's description of Maushkán","Maushkán has already slain many members of Raiglud's tribe this day, but he is eager to kill even more. You can almost see the rage and hatred in his eyes, and smell his foul stench. He leads a raiding party of Orcs, and they follow him out of fear and a desire for treasure.","Listen to Raiglud's story","Raiglud has told her story.","It is hard to believe that Raiglud could ever have been young, but you know that it must have been true, as it is for all people. You can almost see her, hidden by a mound of grass and hay, as her fear of Maushkán and his band wars with her anger at what they have done to her people.","Consider Raiglud's description of Deilur","Consider Raiglud's description of herself as a child","Talk to Raiglud","You can almost see Deilur standing defiantly before the Orc raiding party, surrounded by the bodies of her friends and her family among the Uch-lûth. She has little chance of surviving this encounter, but Raiglud's description of her is so vivid that she seems almost to be standing before you, hale and hearty.\
\
She has nothing that might be called a weapon, but she does grip a needle of bone in one hidden fist.","Instancia: Reliquia de las Tribus","The Needle of Many Leagues has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!"},
[6956]={"Instancia: Reliquia de los Hombres Salvajes","'What a relief! It's just a ${RACE}! There are rumours about these statues. They say they come to life when you aren't looking at them, and have slain whole encampments!\
\
'The war hasn't gone as the bosses wanted, and I thought I'd slip away and find my own place to hide out until everything blows over. And this cave would be perfect if it wasn't for these horrible statues! I think I'll do what I can to smash them to pieces, and then this will be a perfect hideout for Turkalb.'","'This cave favourite place of Bhai-buri-Ghân? Do not know why. Too damp for Khôr-buri-Ghân.\
\
'What special about cave?'","Khôr-buri-Ghân is inside the cave that was his brother's favourite place.","Descend to the lower chamber of the cave and confront the Orc","An Orc has found Bhai-buri-Ghân's cave.","Confront Turkalb","You have come with Khôr-buri-Ghân to the cave that was his brother Bhai-buri-Ghân's favourite place.","'Statue carved by Bhai-buri-Ghân no longer have feel of gorgûn. Khôr-buri-Ghân give memento of brother to you, ${PLAYER}. Maybe will help on road you walk, when evil about. Khôr-buri-Ghân not need memento to remember Bhai-buri-Ghân. Will remember whenever come to favourite place.\
\
'Always be friend to Wild Men. Always be foe to gorgûn. Wind in the trees, water in the lake. Now you take memento far away, use for good. Remember Bhai-buri-Ghân, remember Khôr-buri-Ghân.'","Khôr-buri-Ghân is in his brother's favourite cave.","'Always be friend to Wild Men. Always be friend to Khôr-buri-Ghân.'","Help protect Khôr-buri-Ghân","'This more statues than in village or in forest. So many different sizes. Bhai-buri-Ghân come here often. This carving place? Brother Bhai-buri-Ghân carve sculpture here? Maybe help carve some of these, too?'\
\
Khôr-buri-Ghân suddenly freezes, and points silently down towards the lower chamber.\
\
'Gorgûn,' he whispers.","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân inside the cave","The Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân has been cleansed of Mordor's corruption!","Khôr-buri-Ghân motions for you to descend and confront the Orc, and he will follow","The Orc Turkalb has found Bhai-buri-Ghân's favourite cave."},
[6957]={"Talk to Durin atop the stairs near the Steepset","Talk to Durin in the court below the Steepset","The stairs leading to the Steepset have been made safe","Durin stands with his personal guard Hrostyr not far from the Steepset, and he waits to speak with you.","Clear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foes","Hear the words of Durin before the Steepset","Instancia: Alto Asiento de los Enanos","Durin stands by the Steepset, mourning for what has been lost.","'The reclamation of Gundabad has begun. That will have to be enough... for now.'","Durin stands before the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad.","Durin desires to see with his own eyes the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad.","'The stairs to the Steepset are just to the south of us, ${PLAYER}. Before we ascend, Hrostyr and I will make safe this court. I do not ask you to follow us! With the Red Axe I will make short work of the creatures here, and with Hrostyr to guard my flank I will fear no injury.\
\
'This is the task I have for you, my capable friend: I ask that you clear the stairs of our foes. Once you have accomplished that, Hrostyr and I will join you at the top and we will approach the Steepset together.'","Talk to Durin by the Steepset","Durin asked you to clear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foes. Once you have accomplished this, he will rejoin you at the top of the stairs.","'The Steepset is just ahead, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We will stand together, and show that none can oppose us!'","'Glóin mourns for the Zabad'ibîn, and he is not alone. Seven sacred jewels they were, brilliant and scintillating even in the dark, and they were housed in the very stone of this throne for centuries. But that was long ago, and the Zabad'ibîn have been stolen away during the years of our absence by persons unknown.\
\
'I did not truly expect to find otherwise, but the sight of this plain stone is like a dagger in my heart, ${PLAYER}, and it would be the same for any Longbeard. Recovering the gems and returning them to their pride of place in the Steepset would mean a great deal to me, for it would signal that treasures long thought lost could come back to us.'","Now that you have cleared the stairs of his foes, Durin can climb to the Steepset.\
\
He waits to speak with you at the top of the stairs."},
[6958]={"Hildith's council is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.","Hildith is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.","Hildith is in Grimslade's Mead Hall.","Hildith is in the Grimslade Mead Hall.","'Good, everyone is here. Let us begin at once.\
\
'Pay attention, everyone. Your Thane is speaking!'","Listen to the council","Hildith gives you a look as hard as stone as you depart","Hildith has offended everyone with her harsh words...","Bow to Hildith and take your leave","Speak with Hildith","Walk to the door","'Do you wish to help us, ${PLAYER}? You look to be a seasoned warrior. Grimbold took the bulk of our soldiers to fight with him at the Fords, and we need all the strength we can muster if we are to survive this war.'\
\
You ask Hildith why she asks for help when she turns it away when offered by her counsellor. Her face turns to stone.\
\
'Of course, you are not obligated to stay. Help yourself to whatever hospitality Grimslade has to offer, and then I wish you safe travels.'","Ask Hildith why she was so harsh to Dunward","Utterly alone in the Thane's seat, Hildith's angry demeanor has dissolved into one of deep sadness now that she thinks no one is near.","You feel compelled to take one last look at Hildith","Instancia: El Consejo de Hildith","Hildith decides to sit and hear council from you and from Dunward.","Éomer's tale is done. You should now return your thoughts to the men gathered at Helm's Gate, waiting for Gandalf and hoping that Erkenbrand will return soon.","You should head towards the door of the Mead Hall.","Look back at Hildith from across the Mead Hall"},
[6959]={"Habla con Fuirgam y comienza el asalto a la fortaleza orca.","Fuirgam debe sobrevivir","'¡Este fuerte es nuestro ahora y los Orcos han sido enviados a retroceder para acobardarse a los pies de sus amos en Dol Guldur!\
\
'Ahora debemos apresurarnos para reclamar las rutas que se encuentran entre los Lindes Oscuros y la oscura morada del Nigromante. Planeo establecer mi base entre las antiguas ruinas de Emyn Lum, ${PLAYER}. Que el destino nos reúna allí de nuevo, porque los días que tenemos por delante se consumirán con tumulto y dolor, antes de alcanzar nuestro objetivo final.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Has completado la invasión del desembarco del Bosque Negro. Ahora eres libre de explorar más a fondo el Bosque Negro.</rgb>","Instancia: Asalto a la colina","'¡Es hora de atacar! El comandante uruk en la cima de la fortaleza es nuestro objetivo, si cae, la fortaleza será nuestra!\
\
'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} en cuerpo y mente, entonces comenzaré el asalto!'","Habla con Fuirgam para poner fin a la batalla y reclamar la fortaleza para los Malledhrim.","¡Victoria!","'¡Tu valiente fuerza nos ha comprado este día, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Con la caída de este canalla, los orcos están derrotados y ninguna de sus fuerzas puede detener nuestro avance hasta que estemos frente a las puertas de Dol Guldur!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completar esta misión pondrá fin al asalto a los Lindes Oscuros. \
\
Cualquier misión que no hayas completado en esta área será cancelada y ya no estará accesible después.</rgb>","Habla con Fuirgam","Fuirgam está preparado para lanzar su asalto a la fortaleza orca que domina los Lindes Oscuros. Te ha pedido que te unas a sus fuerzas para el ataque, que, si tiene éxito, debería romper la columna vertebral de las fuerzas orcas que defienden el bosque, permitiendo a los Malledhrim avanzar hacia la torre de Dol Guldur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completar esta misión pondrá fin al asalto a los Lindes Oscuros. \
\
Cualquier misión que no hayas completado en esta área será cancelada y ya no estará accesible después.</rgb>"},
[6960]={"Instancia: El hijo de su padre","Talk to Gurnákh","'So be it. I will give you these three things for which you have asked. My Crow-feeders will get first crack at your marching men, but I will send word to the other raiding-parties within range of us. Bloody Moon and Twisted Neck will want to be included, but my Crow-feeders deserve the greatest share of the treasure, and they will get it.\
\
'But I warn you, traitor. Cross me, and you will keep your life, but only so you will know torments the like of which you have never dreamed.'","Once again, the shade of Tárandil falls silent","'That was when I saw the Orcs.'","Vágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.","The shade that came to be called Vágari the Wanderer desires to confess to you the misdeeds of his past.","'I am glad of their service to you, Tárandil, son-of-no-blood, but their betrayal remains beyond pardon. This treachery cannot now be redeemed, no matter how dear to me the subject of their aid.\
\
'But let us not dwell upon the oath-breakers! It brings me no happiness to speak of such faithless traitors, not on such a joyful occasion as this, your return from the wild, and from the dead!\
\
'I understand if you do not wish to take the western road again so soon. The change of heart that brought you hither to Minas Ithil is understandable, and if it is your wish I will not push for you to return to Belfalas. Come with us instead on the northern road, if you are hale and hearty enough for the journey.'","'I resolved to stay as near to Isildur as I could without arousing suspicion. When he fell beneath the blades of the Orcs, I needed to ensure I could take the Ring from his body before the Orcs seized it for themselves. A traitor sees treachery everywhere, and I did not trust Gurnákh.\
\
'One hour after meeting with the Crow-feeders, I was back at the camp with my sword sheathed at my side. No one had missed me. My treason remained a secret.'","Hear the words of Isildur as recounted by Vágari","'I remember little of the days and weeks that followed. I wandered in the wilderness, mad with grief for my wife and son, lamenting their doom: an eternity of pitiless unrest. I never came to the halls that awaited me; Belfalas was not to be mine, and I cared not. I dreamt my family called to me, their voices drawing me deeper into the wild lands. I know not where trod my feet; uncaring, I grew gaunt and hungry.\
\
'Somewhere in the wilderness, not far from the site of a past victory that was now wholly meaningless, I found a creature that was known to me, one of Nine. It was a Nazgûl of Sauron, and I could not escape it. Do I say \\qcould not?\\q That is not the right of it.\
\
'I did not try to escape. Aye, perhaps this Nazgûl could give me the only escape I wanted. I welcomed the cold touch of death, and feared it not.'","'They delighted to see me again, for they feared my death in the wilderness.'","'The falsehoods came more easily to me than they once did. I told Isildur and my brothers that I had been waylaid and wounded by Orcs on the road, left to die by one of their raiding-parties. \\qThat would have been the end,\\q I said to them, \\qbut for the Orodhoth, the Men of the Mountain. They rescued me and nursed me back to health; for that they have my gratitude. I tell you true, I would count their broken oaths repaired for this deed.\\q'","'You are more reckless than others of your kind I have slain, but there is something else, too. A shadow lies upon you, deeper and darker than that on any Orc. Is that why you have given us the marching orders for your band, and suggested this plan of attack? It is more detailed than any Orkish plan of battle: a feint and a retreat, followed by a finishing attack when their guard is down. I like it.\
\
'I could kill you right now, foolish one. You have given us the perfect location to surprise your band, trapped between the marshes to their left and the forest to their right. What need do I still have for you?\
\
'Ah, I can name the reason you still live, and it is this only: my curiosity. I want to know why you do this.'","Listen to Vágari's account","'And so I became my father's son, after all.\
\
'By how many twisting paths had Adûnzagar, son of Ûrizagar, come to this place? The name Tárandil no longer suited me, but I knew I needs must wear it a little longer if I was to fulfil my bargain with the Blade of Lebennin and his master.\
\
'I returned from the wilderness gaunt and haggard, but with new-found purpose. I returned to Minas Ithil just as my foster-father Isildur prepared to depart for Annúminas to claim his father Elendil's throne.'","The shade of Tárandil says nothing.","Talk to Vágari the Wanderer"},
[6961]={"Talk to Horn outside the Mead Hall in Eaworth","Listen to the conversation around the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Corudan at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'So what did you make of my father, ${PLAYER}? That went about as well as I expected. No, it actually went better. Our last meeting, before I left for Stangard, was an icy one. My time away seems to have thawed him somewhat, if only slightly.\
\
'I hadn't thought to keep Prince Théodred's death from my sister Ingyth until it became clear my father had not told her, but I think it is best this way. She was very much in love with him, and his loss... well, it will not be an easy thing.'","'I would like to apologize for my father's words, ${PLAYER}. He speaks harshly because the troubles of the Entwash Vale weigh heavily upon him, and he cares so much about his people. He wants to do what is right, but he worries that it is not enough.\
\
'If only the will of the King were not so... confused. It is hard to know what is best for Rohan. Ha! Will you listen to me? I am no shield-maiden. What would Prince Théodred say if he could hear me talk this way?'","You have attended a feast at Horn's home of Eaworth. The food was good, but your reception by Horn's father Ingbert was frosty.","Talk to Nona in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Horn is outside the Mead Hall, in Eaworth.","Horn is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","Instancia: Regreso a casa","Ingbert, Ingyth, and Nona have gotten up from the table and are each in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should speak with each of them.","'We will speak later, ${PLAYER}, but I thank you for holding your tongue. I have kept the sad tidings from the Fords of Isen from my daughter, until now. She is not yet ready to hear them.'","'Let us return to the Mead Hall, ${PLAYER}. Relaxing with you and Corudan and Nona in time of peace is more home-like now than anything Eaworth can provide to me.'","'Yes, that is enough. We will speak of the Prince... later. No need for that talk now.'\
\
Reeve Ingbert thumps the table with his fist.\
\
'There is another matter of which to speak, a very serious matter indeed.'","Horn interrupts before you can speak to Ingyth","Nona looks at you darkly.\
\
'Why did I come to this place, ${PLAYER}? My journey with you was to be one of vengeance and victory, and instead I encounter a complicated web of distrust and confusion!'\
\
Nona lowers her voice and speaks to you in a harsh whisper.\
\
'That girl does not know her beloved is dead, and none here wish her to know! Is that because they fear the truth would kill her, that her grief would be too much for her to bear? She should take the sadness and turn it to anger, and wield a sword against the Orcs that slew her love! That is what I have done, in memory of Wadu, and what I would do to avenge my love... to avenge...'\
\
Nona halts suddenly, out of breath.\
\
'But his people and mine are enemies, ${PLAYER}. It is wrong to... to feel this way. You heard that old man! He will never accept that Nona, daughter of Suvulch, could be anything but a foe. Has my fondness for Horn changed me? Has it made me weaker, more unsuspecting? Why can I no longer bring myself to hate the horse-lords in the same way they hate my people?\
\
'I do not want to die in ambush, ${PLAYER}, as my brother did. But I fear I have been blinded. My heart has done it. I... need some time to think.'","Corudan's seat is just to your right, at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","Talk to Ingyth in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Horn inside the Mead Hall of Eaworth","The feast is over, but the conversation continues.","'No, you are right, ${PLAYER}. I am being unfair. Eaworth has suffered greatly at the hands of Orcs, and it is to regain the glory of Rohan that its people fight!'\
\
Horn shakes his head to clear it.\
\
'Yes, my songs were not lies. Rohan was great, and will be again. It's just... I have become fond of Nona, and I wanted my family to accept her for the same reasons I have. And I wanted her to feel less out-of-place here. I did not think she would have as much trouble fitting in here in Eaworth, though perhaps I should have known better.\
\
'Neither of us belong in Rohan, it seems. She and I are both outcasts. It does not seem to bother her the way it bothers me. Perhaps she can help me come to accept it.\
\
'Thank you for the walk, ${PLAYER}. The fresh air has done me some good.'","Talk to Reeve Ingbert at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'I know the Reeve promised a meagre feast, but this seemed like a bounty to me. Eaworth is besieged by troubles, as are the other villages we have visited in the Eastemnet, but still its lord and his guests eat well.'","Reeve Ingbert is at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","'I think I could use some air, ${PLAYER}. Let us walk outside for a short while.'","Horn is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","Talk to Ingyth at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Ingyth is at the table just to the right of her father, Ingbert, in the Mead Hall of Eaworth."},
[6963]={"Follow Fastred as he seeks Crúmgam","Burnoth is standing on the field near Kings' End.\
\
You have arrived at the last location where Fastred sighted Crúmgam, and should now talk to Burnoth.","Instancia: Honor y traición","Crúmgam's flames are upon one of the charred fields outside Kings' End.\
\
Vile flames have sprung to life and must now be quenched.","The ambushing foes can be found just ahead.\
\
You have begun your search for Crúmgam, but foes now harry your advance. You must defeat them!","Confront Crúmgam","Burnoth is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End.\
\
You have defeated the traitor, Brodwulf, and should now speak to Burnoth.","'Crúmgam is nowhere to be found, my friend, but fear not! It is difficult to move unnoticed through such a battle and he cannot have gone far.\
\
'Fastred spoke of the sorcerer's mastery of flame - we must proceed carefully or he shall too soon sense our approach and send whichever magics he commands against us.\
\
'Let us go now before these fiends slip away!'","Fastred and the Riders Three are searching the fields outside Kings' End.\
\
You have survived an ambush and should now resume your search for Crúmgam.","Talk to Burnoth","Search the charred fields for signs of Crúmgam","Defeat the ambushing foes","'The traitor is slain, but Crúmgam has escaped with his vile sorcery.\
\
'In his wake, he has left the Reeve slain and Ulf wounded. We must retreat to safer ground, and heal what we may. The body of the Reeve must be borne to the gates of the city - I shall not leave him here among the dead!\
\
'Come!'","Fastred is running through the charred fields outside Kings' End.\
\
You have witnessed Crúmgam's sorcery and should now search the nearby area for Crúmgam.","Defeat Brodwulf and avenge Léofdag","The paths of the Riders Three and Reeve Fastred align as they move against Crúmgam and his traitorous agent.","Defeat the seeking flames","'No victory comes easy this day, my friend.'","Brodwulf is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End.\
\
Crúmgam has fled, leaving the traitor to his fate. You should defeat Brodwulf and avenge Léofdag.","Crúmgam is standing before the pyre outside Kings' End.\
\
You have found Crúmgam and beside him stands a man bearing the armour of the King's knights - a traitor deep within the heart of Rohan."},
[6964]={"El hombre está vestido de manera extraña, pero parece amistoso, y cualquier enemigo de los trasgos o de los orcos es amigo de los Holbytlan.","Protege a tus amigos y familia de los trasgos","Rebusca en el saco del trasgo para conseguir un arma y equípala, y luego habla con Fanglind","Habla con Odger Túcca más adelante por el sendero hacia el sureste","El Águila Fanglind ha protegido durante mucho tiempo a los Holbytlan de cualquiera que encuentre su valle oculto, y hoy no ha sido diferente.","'¡No puedo creer que realmente hayas decidido dejarnos, ! Sé que hablamos de esta posibilidad durante muchos años, pero... bueno, debo admitir que siempre pensé que sería yo el primero de los Holbytlan en la memoria viva en dejar este valle oculto, y el primero en regresar.'\
\
Le dices a Valaric que es bienvenido a acompañarte, y para su crédito —y su sorpresa— casi lo considera. Luego niega con la cabeza.\
\
'Oh, no —balbucea por fin—. Dicen que es un mundo muy grande ahí afuera, y no creo estar listo para verlo. Pero tú eres ${PLAYERNAME:el más alto[m]|la más alta[f]} de nosotros, y creciste por más tiempo. Si alguno de los nuestros tiene el valor para dejar Misthallow, creo que eres tú.'","Habla con tu amigo Valaric Túcca entre los pacíficos hogares de los Holbytlan","Habla con Meneldir y completa la misión 'Un Mundo Más Grande'","Habla con la Abuela Madelgard Túcca","'No te pediré que te quedes, ${PLAYER}. Veo que tu decisión está tomada.'\
\
La Abuela Maddy te sonríe y te tira suavemente de la oreja con cariño.\
\
'Ahora escúchame, querido, porque esto es importante y no lo repetiré. Debes mantener tus ojos en el camino delante de ti, y no preocuparte por nosotros; tenemos a Fanglind y a las otras Águilas para vigilarnos, y Lyndelby estará bien mientras estés lejos. Pero recuerda esto: solo te dejamos ir para que puedas traer ayuda a la gente que encuentres en ese mundo ancho y peligroso. Debes hacerte útil, ${PLAYER}. ¡Hay gente ahí fuera que necesitará tu ayuda, y debes ayudarles! Creo que ese es el llamado que te aleja de nosotros, y solo para que lo sigas es que te permito marcharte.\
\
'¿Estamos de acuerdo? Entonces <rgb=#00FF00>saluda</rgb> hacia nosotros y parte en tu gran aventura, ${PLAYER}. ¡Y recuerda lo que dije!'","'¿Entonces hoy es el gran día? Ogiva me ha estado diciendo que pronto te embarcarías en alguna aventura, pero pensé que no era asunto nuestro. No puedo imaginar dejar Lyndelby, pero supongo que cada uno de nosotros es distinto, al fin y al cabo.\
\
'Debes cuidarte allá fuera, más allá de Misthallow, ${PLAYER}. ¿Quién sabe qué peligros podrías encontrar? Las musarañas siempre se meten en mis huertos y echan a perder mi lechuga, ¡y supongo que hay criaturas mayores y más peligrosas en el mundo amplio! ¡Musarañas GIGANTES, no lo dudaría!'","Has visto a Odger Túcca más abajo por el sendero hacia el sureste, y deberías contarle tus planes.","Durante incontables siglos, la humilde gente que se conoce a sí misma como los Holbytlan ha vivido vidas pacíficas entre las cañadas ocultas de Misthallow. Ahora, ${PLAYERNAME:uno[m]|una[f]} de ellos busca abandonar la seguridad de Lyndelby en busca de aventura...","'No olvides equipar tu nueva arma, . No podré protegerte cuando salgas de Misthallow, y necesitarás confiar en tus habilidades y en el equipo que encuentres si quieres sobrevivir a los desafíos que se aproximan.\
\
'El mundo ahí fuera es peligroso. ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que esta es la vida que has elegido? La mayoría de los tuyos no dejan su hogar, prefiriendo permanecer cerca de la tierra de su nacimiento.'","Le dices a Oggy que la extrañarás","¡Los trasgos se han colado en la aldea de Lyndelby y ahora amenazan a tus amigos y familia!","Habla con Ogiva Túcca cuesta abajo","Le prometes a Erma que volverás, algún día.","Habla con la Abuela Maddy","La Abuela Maddy te ha pedido que <rgb=#00FF00>saludes</rgb> a tus amigos y familia, y luego comiences tu gran aventura.","Reúnete con Heldric Túcca fuera de su hogar en Lyndelby cuando el sol se levante en el día que has decidido partir.","Tu buen amigo Valaric Túcca apenas puede creer que hayas tomado la decisión de marcharte.","'¿Te marchas de Lyndelby en busca de aventura? Adiós entonces, ${PLAYER}. Te veré cuando regreses, y...\
\
'¡Oh! ¡También deberías despedirte de Croaker! Es la mejor rana-amiga que alguien haya tenido nunca, ¡y lo sabes! Definitivamente debes despedirte de Croaker también. Será un tiempo antes de que vuelvas, después de todo.'","Habla con Fanglind, uno de los Grandes Águilas que protegen a tu gente","Tu aventura comienza, y juras hacer lo que pidió la Abuela Maddy: ayudar a cualquiera que necesite ayuda.","Habla con Erma Túcca cerca de la base de la colina","El mejor amigo de Odger Túcca, su rana Croaker, ha desaparecido.","Vilíhad nunca ha tenido demasiada imaginación.","'Vi a los trasgos desde lo alto, ${PLAYER}, pero también vi algo más: te vi despidiéndote de tu gente, y supe tu determinación. Sé lo que planeabas desde hace semanas, y he vigilado tus pasos. Espero que no te moleste.\
\
'Seguiré protegiendo a tu gente, como lo he hecho todos los años que te he conocido. Pero necesitarás estar bien equipado si quieres sobrevivir a las aventuras que te aguardan. No posees las poderosas garras de mi especie, aunque eres inusualmente alto y fuerte... para alguien de tu pueblo. Sigues siendo muy pequeño comparado con las Grandes Águilas y con las otras gentes que encontrarás más allá de las crestas que rodean tu aldea.\
\
'Estos trasgos eran ladrones, y su líder poseía un saco de armas. Quizá deberías hacer uso de este equipo; el trasgo no tiene derecho alguno sobre él, y su antiguo dueño ya no podrá usarlo, pero en tus manos podría servir de mucho.'","Habla con Vilihad en el sendero hacia el sur","Instancia: Comienzos Humildes","Reúnete con Heldric Túcca cuando salga el sol","La Abuela Maddy te pidió que te despidieras de algunos de los madrugadores de Lyndelby.","'Entonces, ¿qué tiene tan alterado a mi Heldric, ? Y no he visto a Valaric tan emocionado desde... bueno, desde que Gísla duplicó por accidente la receta de su famoso relleno de tartas, y para ser sincera ese fue un gran día para todos nosotros.'\
\
Le dices a la Abuela Maddy que por fin ha llegado el momento de dejar Lyndelby, ver el mundo más amplio y vivir una aventura. Ella asiente en silencio y te da un golpecito en la nariz.\
\
'Era inevitable tarde o temprano, ${PLAYERNAME:querido[m]|querida[f]} . Siempre has sido diferente, a tu manera: ${PLAYERNAME:más extrovertido[m]|más extrovertida[f]} que el resto de nosotros y ${PLAYERNAME:más curioso[m]|más curiosa[f]} por lo que yace más allá de las cañadas cubiertas de niebla. ¡Y más ${PLAYERNAME:alto[m]|alta[f]}, también! La sangre de los antiguos Holbytlan es muy fuerte en ti, ¡siempre lo he dicho! ¿Verdad, Heldric? Oh, ha dejado de escucharme. ¡Ese viejo cabra!'","Encontraste a Croaker... ¡pero también encontraste una tropa de trasgos husmeando!","El mejor amigo de Odger Túcca, su rana Croaker, ha desaparecido, pero oíste su croar cerca de las rocas al suroeste.","Fanglind te ha recomendado que busques en el saco que dejaron los trasgos y equipes una de las armas que encuentres dentro. Después, quiere hablar contigo un poco más.","Oyes el croar preocupado de Croaker proveniente del suroeste","'Despertaste temprano hoy, ${PLAYER}. ¿Estás planeando...?'\
\
Las alegres palabras de Ogiva se desvanecen, y su expresión afable se transforma en una de sorpresa.\
\
'¡Este es el día! ¡Lo sabía! Le dije a Vilihad que por fin ibas a irte a iniciar tus andanzas, ¡y acerté! No sabía que sería esta mañana, quizá no exactamente, pero sabía desde hace tiempo que estabas planeando un viaje así. Eso es tremendamente emocionante, ${PLAYER}. ¡Ve y haznos sentir orgullosos, ya verás!'","'¡Simplemente no puedo creer que nos dejes, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
Erma se seca una lágrima y te hace prometer que volverás después de haber tenido tu ración de aventura. Le dices que sin duda regresarás a Lyndelby cuando puedas, después de ver lo que yace más allá de las distantes cumbres del horizonte.\
\
'Las montañas son terriblemente altas para ser escaladas por uno de los Holbytlan —dice—. Sé que Valaric dice que nuestra gente fue por allí, una vez, pero él dice muchas cosas. ¡Quizá seas el primero de nosotros en ver lo que hay al otro lado! Si eso es verdad, ¡asegúrate de volver y contarnos todo!'","<rgb=#00FF00>Saluda</rgb> a tus amigos y familia, los buenos Holbytlan de Lyndelby, y comienza tu gran aventura","Le dices a Fanglind que tu corazón te llama a partir, y él agita sus plumas.","La Abuela Madelgard Túcca está esperando hablar contigo mientras el sol se eleva sobre un hermoso día en la aldea oculta de Lyndelby.","Tu viaje exige que ayudes a la gente que lo necesite","Espera a que Croaker revele a dónde ha ido","Busca a Croaker cerca de las rocas al suroeste","La Abuela Maddy te mira con tristeza, pero también con esperanza en sus ojos."},
[6965]={"Talk to Shaidal","'You are truly a worthy candidate, ${PLAYER}. I have heard your name whispered within these halls. There is rumour that Rothog has sent you to speak with me regarding an incident, and I would hope you would be willing to assist me.\
\
'I will tell you that I am innocent of the crimes that have damned me to this place. You see, I worked for Zarzíra, and noticed there were some ill deeds happening within the house. I approached the captain of the guards regarding the deeds, and shortly afterwards, I was being accused of the brutal slaying of one of Zarzíra's competitors. I was saved from death by Rothog, only to be sentenced to  fight in the sands of Dahâl Huliz.\
\
'While working for her, it was rumoured in her house that she kept excellent records of her business dealings and her exploits both legal and less than legal.\
\
'While it is true that I did work with someone to recover those records, it was to prove my innocence and free me from here. Not for any other nefarious purpose....\
\
'I think I hear something!'","The sounds of footsteps fill the halls, you are ambushed by attackers.","Rothog has asked that you travel into the gladiator's residences and question Shaidal regarding the petition.","With the ambush survived, Shaidal calls you over","'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. Please tell Rothog of the attack and that I may have access to the evidence that would prove my innocence.\
\
'Please convince him to allow you to look into the matter further, for I fear for my life and that of those whom I hold dear.'","Instancia: Cazador cazado","Speak to Shaidal about the attack and what he will need of you.","'As you can see, Zarzíra has become most desperate. She has even sent her people in an attempt to silence me. I beg of you to speak to Rothog on my behalf, and ask if you could gather proof of my innocence.'","Within the halls of Dahâl Huliz, the gladiators make their home. Rothog has asked that you question Shaidal.","Speak to Shaidal about the attack","Defeat ambushers"},
[6966]={"Ondor has collapsed the cave-entrance","You have come upon a cave-entrance in the northern Heathfells, on the border of Nan Curunir, where you have encountered a rather unusual dwarf. Without heed to his own safety, he has set about collapsing the cave-entrance, which he claims leads to a warren of Orcs below.","Instance: Imminent Collapse","Ondor is at the Orc-cave.\
\
You should speak with Ondor the Dwarf once more.","'Well, I suppose that's the last of the Orcs. It will take them weeks to dig out that mess... lazy curs.\
\
'If it were dwarves trapped in there, they would be out in a day!'","Defend Ondor as he works to collapse the cave-entrance.","'All right, here we go. Keep an eye on that cave, and if any Orcs come running... well, you know what to do.'","Talk to Ondor","'It has been a pleasure working with you, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Ondor at the Orc-cave"},
[6967]={"Camina junto a Boromir y cuéntale lo sucedido desde que os separasteis.","Habla con Boromir","Instancia: En un Valle del Norte","Bregoleth te dijo que un amigo te espera más adelante, por el sendero que desciende hacia Rivendel.","Encuentra al amigo del que habló Bregoleth más adelante en el sendero","Al parecer, el propio viaje de Boromir llegó a buen puerto, y el soldado de Gondor se alegra de verte.","Le contaste a Boromir parte de lo que te ocurrió junto a Meneldir después de que los tres se separaron, y el soldado de Gondor ha pasado gran parte del trayecto en silencio.","Habla con Galasebdir en el camino a través de las Tierras Solitarias.","Elrond, el señor de la casa, desea escuchar tu historia.","Habla con Bregoleth","Galasebdir, un montaraz conocido tuyo, te ha alcanzado en el camino a través de las Tierras Solitarias.","Elrond de Rivendel debe ser advertido de la sombra que se alza en Angmar.","Habla con Boromir junto a La Última Morada.","Semiorcos acosan a los viajeros en el camino a través de las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Candaith tenía razón: el camino a Rivendel es peligroso.","Derrota a los semiorcos en el camino (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Boromir desea saber qué ocurrió después de que los tres tomaron caminos distintos.","'Ahí está otra vez, ${PLAYER}, entre los árboles junto al camino. ¿Oyes ese crujido? A mí me suena como algo grande... fingiendo ser pequeño.\
\
'Un troll, sin duda. ¿Es demasiado esperar que podamos pasar sin que nos note?'","'Parece que tu propio viaje llega a su fin en el mismo valle septentrional que el mío, ${PLAYER}. Cuando oí a los elfos decir entre ellos que un ${RACE} se acercaba a Rivendel en compañía de un montaraz, supe que tú y Meneldir os aproximabais. Pero... ¿dónde está él? ¿Por qué se retrasa?'\
\
Boromir ve algo en tu expresión y guarda silencio.\
\
'¿Su viaje también ha llegado a su fin, verdad? Cuéntame qué le ocurrió mientras caminamos, ${PLAYER}. Aún queda un buen trecho hasta la casa de Elrond.'","Habla con Gandalf el Gris fuera de La Última Morada.","'Sí, sé algo del camino que tomaste para llegar hasta aquí, ${PLAYER}, y de algunas de las noticias que traes. ¡No todas, no! Pero sí algunas. Gentes de tierras muy distintas han llegado a Rivendel en los últimos días, y veo en ello una señal esperanzadora. En los días que vienen se celebrarán consejos, y deberán tomarse decisiones de gran importancia.\
\
'Pero esta no es mi casa. Debes hablar con Elrond, su señor, y entregarle el mensaje que has traído a lo largo de tantas millas.\
\
'Volveremos a vernos, ${PLAYER}.'","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[m]} a Rivendel, . Este es un lugar de seguridad y refugio, y eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[m]} a tomar todo el descanso que puedas en el valle. Pero antes, ¿estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[m]} a decirme qué te trae aquí? Son muchos los peligros que has enfrentado para llegar hasta aquí, y si tu historia es como otras que he oído últimamente, creo que anuncian problemas para los pueblos de la Tierra Media.'\
\
Le dices a Elrond que tienes mucho que contarle, y él asiente, con una expresión reflexiva en el rostro.","Habla con Elrond fuera de La Última Morada.","Habla con Galasebdir en el camino a través del Bosque de los Trolls","Gandalf el Gris te ha saludado fuera de La Última Morada y desea hablar contigo.","Habla con Galasebdir en el camino a través del Páramo Alto","En la entrada de Rivendel, el guerrero elfo Bregoleth se alegra al verte.","Semiorcos derrotados en el camino (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Galasebdir en el camino a través del Bosque de los Trolls.","'Solo he visitado Rivendel una vez, en compañía de mi capitán Aragorn, pero creo que ya estamos cerca. Pronto veremos a los elfos que custodian el paso, y tú llevarás a Elrond tu advertencia sobre la sombra que se alza en Angmar.'","Has viajado con Galasebdir hacia los bosques del Bosque de los Trolls.","'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} a Imladris, , y mi corazón se alegra al verte a salvo. Los exploradores os vieron a ti y a Galasebdir de los Dúnedain mientras ascendíais al Páramo Alto, y me trajeron noticias a mí y a otros en el valle cuando os acercabais al paso. Pedí permiso al señor Elrond para ser yo quien te diera la bienvenida.\
\
'Confío en que no hayas hecho este viaje solo para traerle las noticias de Saruman que yo ya entregué. No... veo en tus ojos que hay algo más. Te dije una vez que estábamos al borde mismo del peligro, ¡y los acontecimientos de los últimos días me han demostrado que tenía más razón de la que creía!\
\
'Otros esperan tu llegada a Imladris. Uno de esos amigos se apresuró a darte la bienvenida en la entrada, pero parece que aún no ha llegado. Búscalo más adelante en el sendero.'","'Era un buen hombre y valiente, ${PLAYER}, y murió luchando contra el mal. Que cada uno de nosotros haga lo mismo, si ese es el destino al que deben llevarnos nuestros caminos.\
\
'Elrond te espera.'","Boromir de Gondor levanta la vista hacia ti, con una sonrisa satisfecha en el rostro.","'Los trolls no son conocidos por ser inteligentes, ${PLAYER}, y por lo general no cazan en grupo. Puede haber sido simple mala suerte que tuviéramos que enfrentar a dos seguidos, o quizás los días se están volviendo más oscuros y la amenaza creciente de la Sombra vuelve a las criaturas más audaces.\
\
'Debemos seguir adelante. Pronto tendremos que iniciar el ascenso, y el terreno puede volverse peligroso.'","Has ascendido por el Páramo Alto junto a Galasebdir y ahora estás cerca del valle oculto de Rivendel.","'¡No te he visto desde que partiste del Vado de Sarn en compañía de Halbarad, ${PLAYER}! Cuando regresó nos contó lo que ocurrió con Meneldir bajo Dol Ernil, y lloramos por él, a pesar de su pasado. Pero el mal se agita en la tierra y hay poco tiempo para el duelo. ¿Qué te trae a las Tierras Solitarias?'\
\
Le dices a Galasebdir que buscas llevar noticias a Elrond de Rivendel sobre los planes malignos del Rey Brujo y de sus servidores en el reino de Angmar. El montaraz reflexiona por un momento.\
\
'Había planeado regresar a Tornhad, en el Ángulo del Mitheithel, ${PLAYER}, pero tu viaje me parece de gran importancia. Te acompañaría en esta misión, si aceptas mi ayuda. El camino a Rivendel seguramente será peligroso.'\
\
Le dices a Galasebdir que su compañía será bienvenida mientras te diriges a Rivendel.\
\
'Entonces estamos de acuerdo. Guía el camino.'"},
[6968]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Lord Ingmar perished</rgb>","'Ha! You think that you have won? Fools!'","'Ah... what glory I may... have earned has been overshadowed... by grief. To know that... Saruman the White has betrayed us is terrible... enough, but to know that he used... my grandmother as the tool is a... deathly blow.'","Listen to the conversation","You have broken through the mounted defences of Maustazg","Listen to what Hoital has to say.","Confront Hoital, leader of the Orcs at Maustazg.","'You have decided to join us in defending my people....'","You have broken through to the central camp of Maustazg","Fight your way to the centre of Maustazg.","Lord Ingmar has launched an assault upon the Orcs at Maustazg.","Ingmar lies wounded in the central camp of Maustazg.\
\
You should speak with Ingmar and leave Maustazg behind.","You lift Ingmar and carry him away.","Fight your way through the mounted defences of Maustazg.","Defeat Hoital.","Fight through the mounted defences of Maustazg","Talk to Ingmar","Fight your way to the centre of Maustazg","'Come! We have broken through their lines... let us continue!'","Confront Hoital","<rgb=#FF0000>Lord Ingmar must survive</rgb>","Defeat Hoital and his minions","Defeated Hoital","Speak with Lord Ingmar.","Instancia: En defensa de Eaworth"},
[6969]={"Éowyn has agreed to bring you along","Éowyn is in Edoras.\
\
You should speak with Éowyn.","Instancia: Necesitado de Ánimos","'Come, let us talk while we walk. What is it you wished to say to me?'\
\
You tell Éowyn that you know of the sadness she hides beneath her cool, brave exterior, and that some people are grown deeply worried for her.","Éowyn is in Edoras.\
\
You should follow Éowyn.","Fight alongside Éowyn","Éowyn has fallen","Éowyn is in Edoras.\
\
You should listen to Éowyn.","Éowyn's eyes are far away as you look at her, a bitterness upon her fair features that is sad to look upon.\
\
You gently speak her name, and she looks at you once more, her reverie broken.","Éowyn is ready to face the foe that threatens Edoras.","Listen to Éowyn","Fight alongside Éowyn.","Follow Éowyn","Éowyn looks at you once more, startled","'That was the most fun I've had in...I cannot even remember! Was that not a wonderful rush, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I have half a mind to ride out and find another enemy to slay...but I must return, I know. The women and children and elderly must get to Dunharrow safely, and it is my duty to make it so.\
\
'Come, let us return to Edoras.'","'There they are. Look at them! My blade thirsts for their blood, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We ride!'","Speak with Éowyn","'All right, all right! You may come with me, if you wish. I would not deny the wishes of such a worthy ${RACE}.\
\
'Let us leave at once! I long for battle.'","'We have done it!'","Speak with Éowyn.","You have defeated the warband that threatened the refugees of Edoras!","Rouse Éowyn from her unhappy reverie","Join Éowyn in battle","Éowyn is in need of cheering up, though she hides her dire mood well for the sake of her people."},
[6970]={"Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is almost ready to begin. You should talk to Mêshka.","'Thank you for your assistance with making this all come together, ${PLAYER}. When I first asked for your help, I was unsure of your intentions, or if you would even show. I must tell you though that I am glad you did. Belondor has told me that you have been aiding him, and I am glad for him to have a friend.\
\
'It is my hope that this memorial will help him move past his current unease. He has not been kind to himself. He will not be able to do what he needs to in such a state.'","You see a painting of Belondor valiantly attempting to defend his doomed crew from Azagath","Talk to Mêshka","Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. The families of the deceased mariners have tried to absolve Belondor of his feelings of guilt. Belondor wants to talk to you.","Talk to Belondor","Attend the memorial","Admire the mural","Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is ready to begin. You should take a moment to look at the mural.","As you approach Belondor, he looks haggard, older than you remember him being and is clearly troubled.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I have a few things to take care of before I leave here, but I would like to speak with you later. Meet me back in Dâr Laja when it's convenient for you.'","Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is ready to begin.","'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. It was difficult to watch, but I think this has done exactly what I had hoped.'","Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is beginning.","Instancia: En recuerdo"},
[6971]={"Roamingstar has appeared in the Palace of the Swan.","King Elessar and Queen Arwen wait to discuss important matters with Imrahil, Prince of Dol Amroth.","'And so concludes my Queen's greatest purpose in this journey, ${PLAYER}. She desired to ease Roamingstar's burden, and I believed we would need to visit the Cave of the Avorrim to make the attempt. But we were fortunate that Nimrodel was here in the Palace of the Swan, and now we have saved some time.\
\
'I said Arwen's purpose on this journey was ended, but of course mine is only beginning! We must speak with Prince Imrahil about the continued presence of the Corsairs that threaten Gondor's shoreline, and also about the rise of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar, across the Bay of Belfalas! But we have already achieved some good today, for Roamingstar and Nimrodel each deserve the peace and the happiness that their sorrows stole from them. I hope we have helped lighten their burdens today. I think we have.'","Dorthaneth stands in the Palace of the Swan.","Queen Arwen has indicated a place on the floor where she wants you to set down the bowl of water.","Wait until Queen Arwen explains her peculiar words and deeds.","'Just one moment,' the Queen says to you seriously, retrieving a finely-crafted bowl and a glass jar from the recesses of her cloak. She removes the corked stopper from the mouth of the jar and slowly pours the crystal-clear water contained within into the bowl, spilling not a drop.\
\
'Will you set this down on the floor just there?' she asks you.","'I know what cruelty is, Maiden of the Gilrain. The world is cruel, and has always been. Can you know my story and say it is not so?\
\
'Amroth was a king among Elves, but to me he was more; he was my love, and the brightest star of my night sky. \\qWe must depart, Nimrodel,\\q he said to me, \\qfor the dwarves have awoken terrible evil, and if we stay it will endanger our folk too,\\q and I believed his words. I believe them still, for I know what befell in the centuries since, as he cannot.\
\
'Amroth went ahead to make ready the ship. I travelled with a small company to join him at that distant harbour, but the passage of the mountains was hard. The high crags filled me with unease; the rocky way troubled my heart. When at last we descended to the low-lands, I danced in the woods and became separated from my folk, so grateful was I to leave the mountains behind. The sound of the River Gilrain was beautiful, and its music had magic in it, and whatever else befell I can still remember how it was, and know that I loved it. I slept in peace for too long, and by the time I awoke a fell wind had come from the north and driven my love's ship from the shore, never to return. It is said Amroth leapt from the ship and braved the waves that he might wait for me... but never again was he seen by Elf or by Man, though I walked the shore for uncounted days and innumerable nights.\
\
'I dwelled in sorrow from that day forth, never far from the Bay where I lost my love, and I have worn this mourning veil for so long I cannot remember the sight of the sun without it. I have held my grief close, but so too has it held me. Until now I believed the weight of those heavy chains was only mine to carry. I did not know you sorrowed too, Maiden of the Gilrain. It was not for you to feel this way. Do not burden yourself with the grief that is mine. I spoke of cruelty? The greatest cruelty is that this sadness must snare more than one heart, and for so many years!'","'This hall is so cold... but the Queen wants me to speak, so I shall speak.\
\
'Long ago, and for always, I dwelt within and beside the River Gilrain, and my music was the song of sunlight on the water, and of wind in the leaves. But it was a lonely song, for my sisters had gone away and I did not think I would see them again. Animals came to the stream to drink, and birds to bathe, but except for such creatures I was alone and felt the pain of it... until one day.\
\
'An Elf-maid tarried by the river as she journeyed southward from a distant land. She was more beautiful and radiant than anyone I had ever seen. I sang to her and she delighted in my song, for it reminded her of home. She danced beside my stream, and I was so gladdened by her presence that the music I made held more enchantment than ever it had before. She slept on the bank of Gilrain, comfortable and safe, and I was no longer alone. I dreamt that once she awoke she would fashion a home for herself in my wood, and I would teach her my song and she would call me sister. She would have children of her own, Elf-children of merry eyes and high voices, and I would show them the flower-fields and the secret springs, and they would fashion brightly-coloured petal-crowns to wear, and their mother would delight in them.\
\
'It was a happy dream, but it lasted too long, and when she at last awoke many seasons had passed. The Elf-ship that waited in distant harbour for her to arrive could wait no longer. With selfish hands I stole that life from her, and I grieve every day at the sorrow I caused her. I did not intend such sadness to befall, and I would take it back if I could! And yet it is my doing, and the guilt weighs heavily upon my every moment.'","Listen to the words of Dorthaneth","'Many of the Prince's court and the greatest part of his swan-knights went with Imrahil to Minas Tirith for the waging of the war, but his daughter Lothíriel managed the rule of the city while he was away. That Dol Amroth still stands is a testament to her ability, and tells me she has learned much from her father!'","Talk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan","Set the bowl of water down on the floor where Queen Arwen indicated","Queen Arwen has asked to speak with you.","Talk to Roamingstar in the Palace of the Swan","Talk to Rossaran in the Palace of the Swan","You have come to the Palace of the Swan, where Imrahil, Prince of Dol Amroth, considers how to deal with the threats that still endanger Gondor in the aftermath of the War of the Ring.","Wait for your audience with the Prince of Dol Amroth","Wait for Queen Arwen to explain herself","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Palace of the Swan","Instancia: En el Palacio del Cisne","Talk to Dorthaneth in the Palace of the Swan","King Elessar waits patiently for his audience with Prince Imrahil to begin.","The Swan-knight Rossaran has brought you before the Prince of Dol Amroth, as King Elessar desired."},
[6972]={"You have not seen this Angmarim woman since you left the north-lands. When last you saw her, she had been cast out by her clan for dishonouring them. Her name was taken from her, and she became known as Gun Ain: without name.\
\
She survived in the wastes of Forochel by stealing food from the Lossoth hunters once their prey was felled. Lothrandir gave her a bag of food to last until she could rebuild the wreckage of her life.\
\
What is she doing here?","Listen to Saruman within Orthanc","You have been called to Orthanc to appear before the Wizard Saruman.","Explore the tower of Orthanc","Talk to Saruman in the tower of Orthanc","Instancia: En presencia de Saruman","The power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement.\
\
You must <rgb=#FF0000>resist</rgb>. You must not succumb.","Talk to Fâsh inside Orthanc","'Why do you reject this course? Can you not see that it is futile to continue this fools' charade?'","<rgb=#FF0000>Resist</rgb> the power of Saruman's voice (use <rgb=#FF0000>/resist</rgb>)","You have been summoned inside Orthanc to present yourself to Saruman and have been ordered not to stray from the path.","Saruman has brought you to a library within his tower of Orthanc.","'Well, you're here. This is as far as I go. Follow the stairs straight up and don't wander. The Old Man will know if you do!'","You have not seen the Angmarim once known as Avair since you were in Forochel. Her name was taken from her, and now she serves Saruman as Gun Ain, 'Without Name.'","Fâsh has brought you inside Orthanc and is waiting to speak with you.","'We have much to discuss, ${PLAYER}. I am Saruman the Wise, and I know much that might surprise you, but still there are mysteries. I need your help.\
\
'Together, we can learn much that would otherwise remain hidden. There is much we could accomplish.'","'I will bring you to Morflak. But soon I will kill you, and I will kill your friend Lothrandir, and I will earn my new name. My master has promised.'","Talk to Gun Ain"},
[6973]={"No has encontrado a Thelaron ni al Gwatharan, pero un elfo familiar se alza ante ti...","Los barriles de polvora negra pueden encontrarse al este del destacamento avanzado en el Dagorlad.\
\
Slégar el Artero te ha pedido encontrar lo que queda de la polvora negra del Enemigo y prenderle fuego. Espera que eso proporcione una distracción para que la Alianza avance hacia la Puerta Negra.","El príncipe Amroth está entre la compañía de Harthalín.\
\
Has llegado y encuentras a Harthalín y su compañía atendiendo las heridas del príncipe Amroth. Amroth afirma haber visto a uno de los Gwetherain pasar con un elfo sobre su corcel.","Las Lanzas de Lindon han resistido a las fuerzas de Sauron, pero luchan una batalla desesperada","Habla con el Alto Rey Gil-galad en el destacamento avanzado","Harthalín puede encontrarse junto a tu lecho en Tham Send, en La Última Morada.\
\
Has despertado de tu encuentro con el Rey Brujo dentro del refugio de Imladris. Harthalín ahora está sentada a tu lado. Debes intentar hablar con ella.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Selecciona a Harthalín y escribe '/murmurar' para avanzar la misión.</rgb>","Enfrenta a los Gwetherain","Debes permanecer junto al Alto Rey y los demás comandantes de la Alianza.\
\
Los Gwetherain se aproximan al cuartel trasero de la Alianza.","¡Has rescatado a Thranduil del Jinete Maldito y rechazado a los engendros de Ungwetári!","'¡Así que Padre por fin te ha dado permiso para viajar desde Imladris, ${PLAYER}! Debo decir que estoy emocionado por aprender más de las batallas de las Edades pasadas de parte tuya. Padre nos dijo que no te molestáramos con tantas preguntas, pero esta es seguramente nuestra última oportunidad. ¿No es así?\
\
'Estoy seguro de que Padre te ha contado todo acerca del viaje que tienes por delante, pero no te preocupes — ¡el asunto de su sueño no debe inquietarte!\
\
'Además, el viaje a Celondim nos dará tiempo suficiente para hablar de otras cosas. ¡Imaginaría que los acontecimientos de los últimos tres mil años serían de algún interés para ti!\
\
'Mi hermano y yo estamos listos para partir hacia Ered Luin. Cuando tu quieras, ¡partiremos de inmediato!'","Dernaith y Megoril pueden encontrarse en el destacamento avanzado en Dagorlad.\
\
Has encontrado a dos de las Lanzas de Lindon, pero no has encontrado a Thelaron. Debes hablar con Dernaith y Megoril.","El campamento de los Hombres del Este se encuentra muy al este del destacamento avanzado.\
\
Harthalín te ha llevado al extremo más lejano del campamento de los Hombres del Este, y ahora debes buscar cualquier señal de Thelaron o del Rey Brujo.","'Cuando mi compañía acudió en ayuda del príncipe Amroth, oí un gran grito y un estruendo como alas batiéndose desde arriba. Sonaba como una criatura terrible y voladora, tan grande como las Águilas. No pude verla entre el humo, pero estoy segura de que acechaba fuera de mi vista. No sé si esta criatura sirve a Sauron, pero su presencia me hace temer aún más por Thelaron.\
\
'Si el Rey Brujo lo ha llevado al mirador, debemos pasar por el campamento de los Hombres de los Orientales más adelante. Los orientales se han vuelto arrogantes con el poder de Sauron y han dejado un pequeño paso abierto desde su campamento hacia el bosque.\
\
'¡Sígueme, e infiltrémonos para evitar los peligros de acercarnos a su puerta desde el camino!'","El destacamento avanzado se encuentra al otro lado de las zanjas en llamas del Enemigo, al sur del cuartel trasero.\
\
El Alto Rey te ha pedido que explores el destacamento avanzado y transmitas un mensaje a sus allegados: las Lanzas de Lindon.","Habla con Elrond, recoge tus pertenencias y parte de viaje con sus hijos","'Me alegra verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Dernaith y Megoril me han hablado de la captura de Thelaron, y estoy preocupado por tan sombrías noticias. El Señor Oscuro no habría olvidado pronto las heridas que sufrió a nuestras manos, y temo la forma que pueda tomar su venganza. Incluso ahora que deseo abandonar mi deber, no puedo apartar mis ojos de la Puerta Negra en una hora tan crucial. Por ello, te doy esta misión de importancia extrema. Debes encontrar a Thelaron, y debes salvarlo de los Gwetherain.\
\
'En cuanto a la Alianza, uno del Pueblo de Durin ha ideado un plan astuto para llamar la atención de las fuerzas del Señor Oscuro y permitir un golpe rápido contra la Puerta Negra. En verdad, no sé si este plan dará fruto, pero debemos conquistar la Puerta si Sauron ha de ser derrotado.\
\
'Te pediría que hables con Slégar el Artero. Es un enano lo bastante honorable, pese a su título. Una vez cumplas lo que te pida, ¡persigue al Gwatharan y rescata a Thelaron!\
\
'Nuestros caminos se separan ahora, pero esperemos que ambos lleven a la victoria. ¡Que la luz de los Valar brille sobre nosotros!'","Has sufrido enormemente a causa de la herida que te infligió el Rey Brujo. Debes seguir descansando hasta sanar por completo.","Debes buscar cualquier señal del paso del Gwatharan y seguir su camino.\
\
Has proporcionado la distracción que la Alianza necesitaba. Ahora debes buscar a Thelaron y seguir la senda del Gwatharan que lo llevó.","Harthalín puede encontrarse con su compañía más allá de las zanjas orientales en el Dagorlad.\
\
Has sabido que el propio Rey Brujo tomó a Thelaron, y ahora debes hablar con Harthalín y planear un rescate.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Murmura</rgb> a Harthalín e intenta moverte\
<rgb=#FF0000>(Selecciona a Harthalín y escribe /murmurar)</rgb>","'¡${PLAYER}! Parecías ${PLAYER:perdido[m]|perdida[f]} en un trance, y no pude despertarte hasta este momento. Mi ${PLAYER:queridísimo amigo[m]|queridísima amiga[f]}, ¡no permitas que el Enemigo nuble tus pensamientos con visiones de derrota! Como Sauron bien sabe, ¡el dominio es nuestro en esta batalla!\
\
'¡Ay! Un enemigo acorralado es el más mortífero, y ninguno es más traicionero que el Enemigo en este reino. Debemos dejar de lado nuestras preocupaciones por ahora y aprovechar nuestra ventaja.'","El Alto Rey Gil-galad y Elendil el Alto están hablando a la Alianza.","Hithgol puede encontrarse en una de las camas de Tham Send en La Última Morada.\
\
Hithgol, el guerrero y herborista que una vez ayudó al príncipe Amroth, recibió un golpe del Señor Oscuro. Debes saber cuál es su condición y ver si pronto sanará también.","Pezuñas familiares conducen más profundo en el campamento oriental...","Rescata al príncipe Thranduil al oeste del destacamento avanzado","Harthalín se prepara para rechazar a los Hombres del Este. ¡Debes seguir adelante!","Elrond puede encontrarse en el valle cubierto de telarañas al oeste del destacamento avanzado.\
\
Tú, Elrond y Glorfindel habéis rechazado a los terribles engendros de Ungwetári que amenazaban tanto al Jinete Maldito como a Thranduil. Ahora debes hablar con Elrond.","Habla con Slégar el Artero","Averigua el estado de Hithgol en Tham Send","Conoce el destino de Thelaron por boca del príncipe Amroth","Elrond el Medio Elfo puede encontrarse dentro de Tham Send en La Última Morada.\
\
Elrond te habla de la gran batalla contra Sauron y del destino de tus allegados.","'Me trae gran alegría verte de pie una vez más, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Después de que caíste, intentamos sanarte en la llanura de batalla, pero el Rey Brujo de Angmar te había infligido una grave herida — una como ninguna que nuestras gentes hayan sufrido antes por mano del Señor Oscuro. Se tomó la decisión de llevarte a Imladris, lejos de las tierras del Enemigo. Sufriste durante años en una agonía inquieta mientras mis sanadores trabajaban para librarte de los males que persistían en tu herida. Cuando terminó la Guerra, regresé para ayudarlos y aprendí mucho sobre sanar las viles heridas del acero de Morgul. Cuando por fin pudiste descansar, lo hiciste durante muchos años. A pesar de mis esfuerzos, tu fuerza se ha debilitado mucho. Puede llevar tiempo, pero creo que volverás a conocer el poder que yace en tu interior.\
\
'En cuanto a la tarea que te dio Gil-galad, no la consideres un fracaso, . Nadie podría haber previsto la malicia del Enemigo al enviar a sus Nazgûl a capturar a Thelaron. Trágicamente, nunca fue encontrado — ni siquiera después de que Barad-dûr fuera reducida a ruinas. Dolió profundamente a Gil-galad perderos a ambos en la Guerra, y se dice que su luz se apagó durante todas las batallas que siguieron. ¡Aun así, no flaqueó ante el Enemigo!\
\
'No, no caíste en vano, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Nuestra victoria en la llanura de batalla aquel día dio fruto, sin duda. Sauron resistió nuestros asaltos durante siete años en la Torre Oscura, pero al final fue derrotado por Gil-galad y Elendil. El hijo de Elendil, Isildur, cortó el Anillo del dedo de Sauron, destruyendo al Señor Oscuro y expulsándolo de este reino.\
\
'Hay más que decir sobre estos asuntos...'","Escucha al Alto Rey Gil-galad y a Elendil el Alto","Soldados heridos rescatados de los orcos al oeste del destacamento avanzado (${VALUE}/5)","'¡Habla rápido, pues nuestros enemigos avanzan desde el este!'\
\
Le cuentas a Dernaith tu encuentro con los Gwetherain y entregas el mensaje del Alto Rey.\
\
'¡Los Gwetherain... dos de ellos pasaron por nuestras posiciones desde el norte! ¡Uno cabalgó hacia el oeste y dispersó a nuestros hombres, pero el otro... se llevó a Thelaron!\
\
'En medio de la batalla, atrapó el brazo de la espada de Thelaron con un cruel lazo de cuerda y lo arrastró hacia el este con su corcel funesto! No pude seguirlo entre la masa de orcos... Le fallé...\
\
'¡Fallé al Alto Rey... pero aún debo seguir luchando!'","Se pueden encontrar soldados heridos al oeste del destacamento avanzado en el Dagorlad.\
\
Dernaith y Megoril te han alertado del reciente paso de uno de los Gwetherain, el Jinete Maldito, que dispersó sus fuerzas y dejó a muchos heridos en la llanura de batalla.","DNT","Camina con Elrond","Encuentra y sigue el camino del Gwatharan","Conoce el destino de las Lanzas de Lindon y su cuartel","Las inconfundibles huellas del corcel del Gwatharan conducen hacia el noreste.","Elrond Medio Elfo se encuentra en algún lugar dentro de Tham Send en La Última Morada.\
\
Has despertado de tu largo letargo y ahora debes buscar a Elrond.","Descansa hasta que tu herida sane","Habla con Elrond","El Alto Rey Gil-galad puede encontrarse en el destacamento avanzado en el Dagorlad.\
\
Has llegado para encontrar a la Alianza reunida en el destacamento avanzado. Ahora debes hablar con el Alto Rey Gil-galad como él solicitó.","El Alto Rey Gil-galad y los comandantes de la Alianza están de pie al frente del cuartel trasero.\
\
Harthalín te ha pedido que te unas a ella en el discurso del Alto Rey a la Alianza en vísperas de una gran batalla.","Debes hablar con Harthalín.\
\
Tú y tu compañera, Harthalín, habéis marchado en la Última Alianza durante años bajo el mando del Alto Rey Gil-galad.","La Alianza ha llegado al destacamento avanzado en Dagorlad.\
\
Elrond el Medio Elfo ha traído noticias del avance de la Alianza, y el Alto Rey Gil-galad ha solicitado tu presencia en el destacamento avanzado.","Elrond el Medio Elfo puede encontrarse dentro de Tham Send en La Última Morada.\
\
Has encontrado a Elrond y ahora debes hablar con él.","'¡${PLAYER}! Me alegra este reencuentro, pero hay poco más que celebrar...\
\
'El Alto Rey me envió con mi compañía hacia el este para saber qué había sido de los Elfos de Lórien, pero, por desgracia, solo el príncipe Amroth permanece en el campo. Su padre y los demás fueron expulsados hacia el norte, pero adonde hayan ido no podemos seguirlos. El príncipe está herido, pero sanará con el tiempo.\
\
'Debo preguntar, sin embargo... ¿por qué has venido?'\
\
Le cuentas a Harthalín la tarea que te dio el propio Alto Rey, y sobre Thelaron, la Lanza de Lindon perdida, tomado por uno de los Gwetherain.\
\
'Tu relato me inquieta... pues Amroth habló de una figura terrible que pasó con un elfo colgado sobre su corcel.\
\
'Puede que el tiempo se agote para Thelaron. Creo que es hora de que sepamos más de lo que el príncipe vio...'","El corcel del Rey Brujo se agita salvajemente a tu llegada — ¡él y Thelaron deben de estar cerca!","A pesar de parecer curado por fuera, Hithgol parece estar en un sueño profundo e inquieto","Es el año 3434 de la Segunda Edad, y Sauron ha regresado. Tú y tu compañera, Harthalín, os habéis unido a los Elfos y Hombres de la Última Alianza en la llanura de la batalla para desafiar al Señor Oscuro de Mordor.","Rescata soldados heridos de los orcos al oeste del destacamento avanzado (${VALUE}/5)","Encuentra a Elrond en La Última Morada","Habla con Harthalín","Slégar el Artero puede encontrarse en el destacamento avanzado en Dagorlad.\
\
El Alto Rey Gil-galad te ha enviado en una misión doble: proporcionar una distracción para la Alianza y rescatar a la Lanza de Lindon, Thelaron. Antes de partir, debes hablar con Slégar el Artero del Pueblo de Durin.","Harthalín puede encontrarse con su compañía más allá de las zanjas orientales en el Dagorlad.\
\
Has encontrado a Harthalín y su compañía mientras buscabas a Thelaron. Debes hablar con ella para ver si alguno en su compañía puede ayudarte.","Busca en el campamento cualquier señal de Thelaron o del Rey Brujo","Entrega el mensaje del Alto Rey a las Lanzas de Lindon","Instancia: Una estrella cae en las tinieblas","'A tu servicio, ${PLAYER}, ¡o quizás tú al mío!'\
\
'¿Has pensado en cómo las zanjas del Enemigo nunca dejan de arder? Pues yo sí.'\
\
Slégar señala la pila de barriles a su lado.\
\
'Estos barriles están llenos de polvora negra y tosco que explota al contacto con la llama. No solo eso, ¡sino que seguirá ardiendo horas después! Sí, si fuera más útil para la piedra, ¡creo que el propio Durin nos haría robar un poco!\
\
'Los Jinetes Negros del Señor Oscuro... los malditos Espectros del Anillo como los llaman los Hombres, son astutos, pero estos trasgos no son muy brillantes. ¡Han dejado los barriles justo al lado de sus propias ballestas y catapultas!\
\
'¿Por qué no haces estallar algunos? Eso debería poner fin a su asedio y desviar su atención el tiempo suficiente para que la Alianza llegue a la Puerta Negra.\
\
'¡Solo asegúrate de no quedarte cerca una vez los enciendas!'","Reúnete con la Alianza en el destacamento avanzado","Elrond te ha dado permiso para viajar a Celondim en preparación para zarpar hacia los Puertos de Mithlond, pero necesitarás provisiones para tu viaje.","'El príncipe ha tenido suerte de sobrevivir al ataque de su padre en la Puerta Negra, pero las palabras del Gwatharan me inquietan...\
\
'El Jinete pronunció un nombre en quenya antes de partir: ¡Ungwetári! ¡La reina-araña!\
\
'Ungoliant ha desaparecido de este mundo y no volverá a atormentarlo, pero Sus hijas permanecen, depredando todo lo que puedan devorar y extendiendo Su oscuridad por la Tierra Media. Uno de ellos debe ahora sentir el mismo hambre que Ella... sin preocuparse por los poderes del Señor Oscuro y sin propósito alguno excepto consumir.\
\
'Son malas noticias, ha sido afortunado que las Grandes Arañas se volvieran contra el Jinete. Si no hacemos frente a esta hija de Ungoliant en la guerra, es seguro que llegará el día en que su hambre busque saciarse más allá de las sombras de Mordor.\
\
'El Alto Rey me dio permiso para seguirte por petición de las Lanzas de Lindon, pero pide tu regreso de inmediato. La Alianza ha llegado por fin al destacamento avanzado. Reúnete con ellos allí, ${PLAYER}, y prepárate para nuestro asalto a la Puerta Negra!'","El príncipe Thranduil puede encontrarse muy al oeste del destacamento avanzado, en un valle cubierto de telarañas.\
\
Uno de los Gwetherain, el Jinete Maldito, ha desviado al príncipe Thranduil a un valle cercano donde ahora está atrapado. Debes ayudar a Thranduil a rechazar al Jinete Maldito.","El Alto Rey Gil-galad está de pie fuera del cuartel trasero en el Dagorlad.\
\
Has resistido ante los Gwetherain, y el Alto Rey ahora desea hablar contigo.","Habla con el Alto Rey Gil-galad","Asiste al discurso del Alto Rey ante la Alianza","El Rey Brujo puede encontrarse en lo alto del mirador más allá del campamento de los Hombres del Este.\
\
Has seguido al corcel del Rey Brujo hasta el extremo del campamento de los Hombres del Este y ahora debes subir las largas escaleras hasta el mirador. Debes enfrentar al Rey Brujo y rescatar a Thelaron.","¡Elrond dijo la verdad! ¡El Alto Rey y Elendil han llegado al fin!","Prende fuego a los barriles de polvora negra del Enemigo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}, antes de que llegaran los Nueve envié a las Lanzas de Lindon con un destacamento de elfos y hombres. Con las demandas de Sauron rechazadas, ya no podemos confiar en que los Gwetherain detengan su mano en esta batalla.\
\
'Conoces a las Lanzas como Thelaron, Megoril y Dernaith, y han permanecido a mi lado en muchas grandes batallas contra Sauron y los más terribles de sus siervos.\
\
'Antes de partir, juraron cruzar las zanjas del Enemigo y desmantelar su maquinaria de asedio. Es cierto que los disparos de catapultas no han alcanzado nuestra posición desde hace un tiempo, pero el frente más amplio ha sido reducido a ruinas por esas máquinas.\
\
'Ahora debes ir en misión de reconocimiento y con un mensaje. Averigua qué ha sido de su destacamento y, si alguno de ellos aún vive, entrégales un mensaje de esperanza.\
\
'La Alianza marcha hacia la Puerta Negra, ¡y ningún Hombre malvado u orco se interpondrá en nuestro camino hacia la victoria sobre Sauron!'","Enfrenta al Rey Brujo y rescata a Thelaron","¡Has despertado al fin!","'¡Salve, ${PLAYER}! Soy Megoril de Lindon. ¿Cómo van las batallas al norte?'\
\
Le cuentas a Megoril tu encuentro con los Gwetherain y entregas el mensaje del Alto Rey Gil-galad.\
\
'Si realmente atacaremos la Puerta Negra hoy, la Alianza debe llegar aquí pronto. Cumplimos lo que mandó el Alto Rey y destruimos las armas del Enemigo, pero cuando aparecieron los Gwetherain, mataron a muchos de los nuestros y dividieron nuestras fuerzas en la Dagorlad. Los rostros por los que alguna vez reconocí a los Gwetherain cuando tomaron los Anillos han desaparecido hace mucho, pero a este lo reconocí por su hoja. Lo llaman el Jinete Maldito, y espoleó a su corcel sobre las espaldas de Elfos, Hombres y orcos por igual!\
\
'Por desgracia, nos vimos obligados a retirarnos antes de poder ayudar a muchos en el campo de batalla. Ahora luchamos por mantener el único camino sobre las grandes zanjas, y las fuerzas del Enemigo han traído más trabuquetes y ballestas al Dagorlad.\
\
'¡Ayuda a los heridos en el campo, y esperemos que la Alianza llegue pronto para expulsar a las fuerzas del Enemigo!'"},
[6974]={"'The Kindred of the Coins have fled deeper into their citadel, but our purpose is fulfilled, and Thorongil rescued. The power of the Five Sisters frightens Azagath; he was right to flee from them, and his allies beside him.\
\
'And yet Roamingstar and her sisters cannot long remain this far from their homes. They have helped buy us a reprieve, and freedom for the Kindred's hostage, but that is all. If Azagath and his Kindred remain a threat, we cannot rely upon the Five Sisters to face it.'","The other water-bearers stand to the south-east of the fountain inside the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to Jajax's captive","Instancia: En la Ciudadela","The Kindred of the Coins has obtained a new, more valuable hostage: you!","Survive the attention of the Kindred of the Coins in the Citadel of Winds","The bubbling fountain in the Citadel of Winds heralds the arrival of an unexpected presence.","Pick up the bowl of sea-water on the bridge to the Citadel of Winds","The Kindred of the Coins escape into the Citadel's depths, leaving their captive behind","Eavesdrop upon the confrontation of the Kindred of the Coins with Jajax and his captive","Jajax has revealed your identity to the Kindred of the Coins!","Talk to Water-bearer Ushu south-east of the fountain","Several members of the Kindred of the Coins guard their captive inside the Citadel of Winds.","The jar falls to the floor and shatters, water soaking into the carpet","Witness the confrontation","Jajax's captive is in the Citadel of Winds.","You pour the sea-water into the fountain, and should now take up your place alongside the other water-bearers","You should pick up the bowl of sea-water and carry it across the bridge to the island, bringing it past the defences and up the hill into the Citadel of Winds. Do not drop the bowl or spill any of the water!","At the suggestion of Hármelak, the Golden Queen, you have uncovered a means of gaining access to the Citadel of Winds, where Azagath Sea-shadow must be holding Thorongil captive.","Azagath has noticed you within the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to Azagath Sea-shadow in the Citadel of Winds","Several members of the Kindred of the Coins meet with Jajax inside the Citadel of Winds.","'Now we must wait until we are dismissed. It is best to not attract any attention.\
\
'Remain within these steps with the rest of us, and we will stay beneath the notice of anyone who might take offence at our listening.'","Jajax is in the Citadel of Winds.","Eavesdrop upon the conversation of the Kindred of the Coins inside the Citadel of Winds","'I thought something was out of place. I see now that it was you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You have come a long distance to be here. It is curious that none of my fellows thought to mention your presence to me. I do not believe you could have escaped Khôltekh's notice, or Hármelak's spies. Perhaps they tire of our continued association? I have experienced such disillusion before; some went willingly to the knife, but only later learned what it meant.\
\
'Do you think to battle me now? Do you think you could best me in my own palace?'","'You are lucky I came along when I did, ${PLAYER}, for the Kindred of the Coins were only moments away from discovering you. I deem that I saved you from imprisonment at least, and death at most, and you would do well to reward my friendship with whatever valuables you might have at hand.'\
\
You remind Jajax that the Kindred was quite oblivious to your presence until he called their attention to you, and he waves a dismissive hand.\
\
'Ah, who can remember now? The important thing is that great deeds were done, and prisoners rescued, and the legend of Jajax has increased.'","Talk to Jajax in the Citadel of Winds"},
[6975]={"Instancia: En el abismo","Gimli can be found in the Chamber of the Watchers in Barad-dûr.\
\
You have repelled the attacks of a glamour, one of the remnants of the Dark Lord himself, which warned of an insidious trap laid for the Firehorns and King Váskmun Greytooth. You should now speak to Gimli.","Confront the glamour in the Chamber of the Watchers","Gimli can be found in the depths of Barad-dûr.\
\
You are searching the depths of Barad-dûr for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns. You should follow Gimli and keep a keen eye on the shadowed tunnels of the Dark Tower.","'What is all this?\
\
'Váskmun and the Firehorns must have come through here... for the trail of dead has led us to this chamber. Hmm....\
\
'Look, the passage descends even further! Oh no, ${PLAYER}, don't you dare think I've become jealous! Whatever this place might be, it is no Khazad-dûm!\
\
'Ah, but something here leaves me uneasy, my friend. Does it seem to you that that statue is looking at us?\
\
'Because it sure seems so to me!'","The caverns suddenly grow wider, and you come to a room dwarfed by statues of Sauron and his servants...","Search the depths of Barad-dûr for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns","Talk to Gimli in the Chamber of the Watchers","'Some kind of trap? I don't like the sound of this at all!\
\
'We're going to need more than you or I if Váskmun and the Firehorns went down there, and if you ask me, we shouldn't wait around for those Eye-mad cultists to find us either!\
\
'Let us return to the ruins of Díngarth, and tell Legolas and the Stout-axes of what we have learned!'","'I think we've seen enough, ${PLAYER}!'","Gimli is standing in the Chamber of the Watchers in the depths of Barad-dûr.\
\
You and Gimli have found a grisly trail of slain followers of the Order of the Eye leading to the Chamber of the Watchers. A statue of Sauron looms ahead and its gaze is fixed upon you. You should speak to Gimli.","'It is quiet here, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'If Váskmun and the Firehorns came to this place, they did so by another way. Knowing Váskmun, he probably marched his army right up to the gates of Barad-dûr!\
\
'Hah! There will be no tales of proud dwarves this day, my friend. Váskmun's pride does his folk no good at all!\
\
'Now, we must find some sign of him or his folk before we are discovered!\
\
'Let us go!'","The glamour, one of the malevolent remnants of the Dark Lord, fades into the shadows...","Habla con Gimli","Deep in the depths of Barad-dûr, there lies a passage into the Mordath, the Black Pits of Mordor, through which Váskmun Greytooth intends to lead the Firehorns in his quest to reclaim the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","Gimli can be found on the precipice within the abyss of Mordath.\
\
You descended into the abyss of Mordath and have come to a ledge within depths of Barad-dûr. You should speak to Gimli and begin your search for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns.","The glamour can be found in the Chamber of the Watchers in Barad-dûr.\
\
A glamour has risen from the statue of Sauron in the Chamber of the Watchers. You and Gimli must stand fast!"},
[6976]={"The tower is secure!","Secure the tower","¡Has asegurado el segundo piso de Barad Arthir!","Secure the tower.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended to have the quest The Circle of Madness underway.</rgb>","The tower of Barad Arthir, otherwise known as the Lofty Watch-fort, must be captured in order to enter the Circle of Despair and reclaim Minas Morgul.","A foothold has been established in the tower","Talk to one of the Rangers.","Talk to one of the Rangers","Instancia: En el Círculo de la Desesperación","'We have secured the tower!'","¡Has asegurado el primer piso de Barad Arthir!"},
[6977]={"Instancia: En el Círculo de la Locura","The tower is secure!","Secure the tower","¡Has asegurado el segundo piso de Barad Elenath!","Secure the tower.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended to have the quest The Circle of Sorrow underway.</rgb>","¡Has asegurado el primer piso de Barad Elenath!","A foothold has been established in the tower","The tower of Barad Elenath, otherwise known as the Star-gazers' Spire, must be captured in order to enter the Circle of Madness and reclaim Minas Morgul.","Talk to one of the Rangers.","Talk to one of the Rangers","'We have secured the tower!'"},
[6978]={"The tower is secure!","Secure the tower","Barad Orhant, otherwise known as the Tower of the Treegarth, must be captured in order to enter the Circle of Sorrow and reclaim Minas Morgul.","¡Has asegurado el segundo piso de Barad Orhant!","A foothold has been established in the tower","Secure the tower.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended to have the quest The Circle of Wrath underway.</rgb>","Instancia: En el Círculo de la Pena","Talk to one of the Rangers.","Talk to one of the Rangers","'We have secured the tower!'","¡Has asegurado el primer piso de Barad Orhant!"},
[6979]={"The tower of Barad Angarth, otherwise known as the Gate-wardens' Keep, must be claimed in order to enter the Circle of Wrath and reclaim Minas Morgul.","The tower is secure!","¡Has asegurado el segundo piso de Barad Angarth!","Secure the tower","¡Has asegurado el primer piso de Barad Angarth!","Secure the tower.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended to have the quest Into the Dead City underway.</rgb>","A foothold has been established in the tower","Talk to one of the Rangers.","Talk to one of the Rangers","'We have secured the tower!'","Instancia: En el Círculo de la Ira"},
[6980]={"You helped Mêshaget and defeated the dwarf-wight he was fighting. You should talk to him.","Mêshaget is being attacked by a dwarf-wight! You should help him defeat his foe.","Search the tomb with Mêshaget","Talk to Mêshaget","Save Mêshaget","You have the journal!","You have the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding, the famous engineer from Lâkindar of old. You should talk to Mêshaget.","Help Mêshaget search the tomb for the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding.","You have found the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding, the famous engineer from Lâkindar of old. You should take the journal out of her stone resting place.","You have what you came for and should now leave the Quelling-house.","Open the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding","Escape the Quelling-house with Mêshaget","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, I thought I was soon to join the dead. I felt I would be haunting the Quelling-house myself by the morrow!\
\
'I am certain this is where Semayâti the Unyielding was laid to rest. Hopefully she rests still! Come, let's look at the tomb!'","Instancia: Hacia la Casa de la Represión","Take the journal","'The journal! This will change everything, ${PLAYER}, you will see. May I carry it?\
\
'Come, let us leave this cursed place and return to Jiret-menêsh.'","As you approached what you thought was the entrance to the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding, you heard a frightened scream from inside. It must be Mêshaget! You should enter the tomb and help him.","This prominent stone grave must belong to Semayâti the Unyielding. You should open it and see what awaits inside.","'I... I have never killed a fellow dwarf before. Nor someone I recently thought of as a dear friend. My heart hurts more than this cut on my leg.'\
\
The young dwarf is clearly trying to blink back tears.\
\
'Something in my eye. Worry not, I will be fine. We have done what we came to do. We will give the journal to Châmelek Gêta, and Jiret-menêsh will be protected from outside threats while also freeing us from being prisoners in our own home. It will be a long walk. Best to get started.'"},
[6981]={"Has entrenado con Gimli. Ahora debes adentrarte en la mina...","Hay algo extraño en este lugar...","'Muy bien, joven... ya has holgazaneado bastante. Deberías volver al trabajo. ¿Acaso tu capataz no te ha dado suficiente tarea?'","'¿Ya has equipado tu arma, ${PLAYER}? ¡Rápido! Practica conmigo antes de entrar a la mina. Nunca se sabe qué males pueden surgir cuando las montañas tiemblan.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>ACCEDER A TU INVENTARIO: Presiona 'i' para abrir tu inventario y ver el arma, o haz clic izquierdo en los íconos de bolsa en la parte inferior de tu pantalla.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPAR TU ARMA: Haz clic derecho sobre el arma en tu inventario para equiparla. Esto reemplazará el arma endeble que tienes equipada actualmente.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>CONSEJO: Deberías equipar tu mejor arma antes de entrar en combate.</rgb>","Deberías hablar con los mineros para evacuarlos","Un saco lleno de equipo yace cerca de la entrada a la Mina del Abismo de Plata.\
\
Deberías saquear el saco para equiparte con lo que necesitarás para la jornada.","Has recogido un arma, pero algo no está bien...","Acércate al anciano que está cerca <rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza presionando W)</rgb>","Habla con Gandalf","Deberías caminar junto a Gandalf","Habla con el mago <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre Gandalf para interactuar)</rgb>","Gandalf el Gris, un mago que acompaña a la Compañía de Thorin, salvó a Gimli del troll.","El nuevo túnel excavado por Tvistur se abre ante ti.\
\
Deberías adentrarte en el túnel para intentar interceptar al troll mientras persigue a Gimli.","Sigue al capataz Otur para conseguir ayuda para Gimli.\
\
Mientras intentabas llamar a Tvistur para la ceremonia de Thorin, él rompió una pared y liberó a un troll. El troll lo mató, y luego fue tras Gimli. Deberías seguir a Otur y ver cómo puedes ayudar a Gimli.","Este enano está perfectamente conservado, y yace entre las ruinas de una antigua estructura élfica...","'Espero que esto no sea un mal presagio para el viaje de mi padre con Thorin.'","Busca a Gimli","Entrena con Gimli para practicar tus habilidades en combate <rgb=#00FF00>(Asegúrate de equipar tu arma)</rgb>","Un anciano encorvado se encuentra frente a ti mientras te diriges a la Mina del Abismo de Plata.\
\
Deberías acercarte a él.","Thorin parte, dejando su mansión al cuidado de Gormr Forjadura","Habla con Gimli para saber qué hacer","Examina el cadáver en las ruinas élficas","Camina junto a Gandalf mientras desea tenerte cerca.","Deberías acompañar a Gandalf, pues es un consejero respetado de Thorin.","Camina junto a Gandalf y escúchalo un momento <rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza presionando W; gira con A y D)</rgb>","Has llegado hasta Gimli. ¡Ayúdalo, si puedes!","Ábrete paso hacia el interior del Abismo de Plata para ayudar a Gimli.\
\
Mientras seguías a Otur, descubrió que la puerta que llevaba al puente había sido dañada por los ataques del troll. Te pidió que fueras a ayudar a Gimli mientras él iba a buscar más ayuda.","El Hombre de gris es Gandalf, consejero de tu señor Thorin Escudo de Roble","Gimli quiere que demuestres tu fuerza antes de permitirte seguirlo a la mina para rescatar a los trabajadores. Nunca se sabe qué males pueden surgir cuando las montañas tiemblan.","'¡Tú! Trabajas en la mina aquí, ¿verdad? Dime tu nombre entonces, por favor.\
\
'${PLAYER}... un buen nombre. Soy Gandalf, si no me conoces. También soy Gandalf si sí me conoces... Gandalf el Gris.\
\
'Ahora, ¿le harías compañía a un viejo por un rato? Estoy bastante cansado y me vendría bien alguien con quien caminar.'","Parece que has descubierto unas ruinas antiguas, aparentemente de estructuras élficas. Un cuerpo yace entre ellas.","'No escucha, así que tendré que darle un pequeño empujón a las cosas. Verás, necesitamos otro miembro para la compañía que parte hacia la Montaña Solitaria. Trece no bastan.'","Gormr no está de humor para entretenerte, joven. Deberías recoger tu equipo y ponerte a trabajar","El mago Gandalf el Gris, consejero de Thorin Escudo de Roble, desea hablar contigo. Como Thorin es el señor de estos salones, crees que lo mejor es escuchar.","<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Los archivos que necesitas para continuar tus aventuras en la Tierra Media deberían terminar de descargarse en breve. ¡Gracias por tu paciencia!</rgb>","Recoge tu equipo del saco junto a la puerta <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre los objetos brillantes para recogerlos)</rgb>","'Tenemos que evacuar a todos estos mineros. Un túnel que tiembla nunca es buena señal, ¡y hasta lo sentimos desde afuera!\
\
'¡Rápido, ${PLAYER}! Toma este pasaje hacia adelante, yo iré por el pasaje lateral.'","'Debemos darnos prisa. No sé cuánto tiempo podrá Gimli mantener ocupado a ese troll antes de que la bestia lo supere.\
\
'¡Sígueme!'","Thorin y su Compañía se preparan para partir desde las Montañas Azules hacia el hogar ancestral de su pueblo, la Montaña Solitaria. Eres solo ${PLAYERNAME:un minero sencillo[m]|una minera sencilla[f]}, pero el mago Gandalf ha solicitado tu ayuda.","Has derrotado a un Rascacueva (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Gormr, el nuevo Senescal de la Mansión de Thorin","Gormr Forjadura ha sido nombrado Senescal de la Mansión de Thorin mientras Thorin está ausente. Ahora que Thorin y Gandalf han partido, deberías hablar con Gormr para escuchar sus instrucciones.","Sigue a Gandalf y escucha sus reflexiones","La entrada a la Mina del Abismo de Plata se alza ante ti.\
\
Gimli quiere encontrarse contigo dentro de la mina inestable, donde lo ayudarás a evacuar a los mineros. Deberías entrar por la puerta.","Pregunta a Gimli qué hacer a continuación","Sigue el túnel que abrió Tvistur para intentar alcanzar a Gimli","Un saco lleno de equipo yace cerca de la entrada a la Mina del Abismo de Plata. Deberías saquear el saco para equiparte con lo que necesitarás para la jornada.","'¿Encontraste el cuerpo de un enano? ¿Oíste eso, Gormr? Me pregunto si ${PLAYER} ha dado con Skorgrím, tendido bajo las ruinas derrumbadas donde fue abatido por un guerrero Elfo llamado Talagan.\
\
'Pero eso es asunto de tiempos ya pasados. Hoy mi preocupación es Thorin. Gormr puede investigar la tumba de su ancestro mientras sea el Senescal de estas tierras en ausencia de Thorin.'","Los mineros están repartidos por toda la mina, trabajando arduamente.\
\
Un temblor de tierra ha inquietado a Gormr, el nuevo líder. Él y Gimli quieren despejar esta mina para que nadie salga herido.","Recoge tu equipo del saco junto a la puerta de la mina","Convence a los mineros de que se retiren","Tienes trabajo que hacer, pero Gandalf aún tiene más que decir","Derrota a los Rascacueva mientras avanzas hacia Gimli y el troll (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prepárate para demostrar tu valentía ante Gimli","Habla con el Capataz Otur","Tras recoger tu arma, un gran temblor sacudió la montaña sobre ti. Gimli, hijo de Glóin, y Gormr se sobresaltaron.","Instancia: Hacia el Abismo de Plata","'¿Así que tenemos la orden de evacuar? Bien — si no supiera más, pensaría que hay un troll suelto por la montaña.\
\
'Queda un minero más por este camino. Vamos a buscarlo.'"},
[6989]={"You should speak with Céolflad.","Talk to Edhild again.","'Leave us be, meddler! Ye'd rather talk to the nobility than to us, anyhow, eh?'","'They do not accept me. Do you see how they will not stand near me? Without Céolstan or the Thane nearby, they will be openly unfriendly.\
\
'I have always been kind to them, ${PLAYER}! I must get used to being alone, until the child comes.'","Ránmald is clearly isolated from the other women, a dangerous problem for a pregnant woman who must survive a harsh winter","Listen to Frithwyn.","Talk to Edhild at Céolstan's grave.","The women of Byre Tor can be found at Aldstan's grave.\
\
You should speak with the women.","See if Edhild needs comfort","You should speak with Edhild at Aldstan's grave.","'What now, hm? Are ye telling us how we should grieve for our own Thane? Aldstan is our loss, not yours.'","You ask Céolflad of what squabbles she speaks. What is the women's problem with Ránmald?\
\
'It is no longer my concern. Now leave me be, meddler. Ye have struck me hard with grief, bringing me here to see my dear Thane in the ground.\
\
'I'll be kind to the girl from now on. For him.'","Ask Edhild why the women do not like Ránmald","Talk to Frithwyn at Céolstan's grave.","Talk to Céolflad.","Meet the women of Byre Tor at Aldstan's grave","Instance: Isolation Amongst Survivors","'Ye heard right, ${PLAYER}. I thought Céolstan would be mine forever, and he let me think so, until he brought Ránmald here.\
\
'I'll never like her, no matter how hard ye try to stir pity in my heart. When I look at her...\
\
'...I see that I was not good enough for him.'","'You see? There is no hope to reconcile us.'\
\
You ask Ránmald for a few moments to speak alone with the women outside.\
\
'Yes, I will be fine by myself. Take as much time as you need.'","Listen to Céolflad's speech","'I shall miss ye, Céolstan.'\
\
Edhild bows her head, and when she looks up again, her eyes are sharp and clear.\
\
'I'll help Ránmald and see that the son of Céolstan, my future Thane, will survive this fell winter. I swear it on this grave.'","Edhild will not explain, despite the Thane's dying wish that Ránmald should be accepted","You should express your frustration and <rgb=#FF0000>roar</rgb> at the women.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This objective requires an emote.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the unkind women","You should speak with Ránmald.","Talk to Céolflad","'I've seen enough, ye troublesome meddler. Let us return to the Steaping Cave.\
\
'I'll not give Ránmald any more trouble.'","Talk to Ránmald","Céolflad is indignant towards you for associating with Ránmald","Frithwyn resents that Ránmald is an outsider","Ask Frithwyn why she does not like Ránmald","You should speak with Edhild.","You should speak with Frithwyn.","The women are unconcerned by your frustration","'Why did ye have to bring me here, ${PLAYER}? I did not want to see him like this, buried, surrounded by wicked Orcs!\
\
'This was a cruel trick. Ah! It is a stab of pain to see Céolstan this way!'","Ask Ránmald if she will excuse you while you talk to the others","Talk to Frithwyn at Céolstan's grave","'She thinks she's better than us, that's why! Has ever since she came to our little town from the south, from some fancy city.'","Listen to Frithwyn","Talk to Edhild at Céolstan's grave","Ránmald feels isolated from the other women, and you do not wish to leave her alone with them in her vulnerable condition.","Listen to Céolflad's speech.","Speak with Edhild","Ask Céolflad why she is cold to Ránmald","'Don't ye involve me in it, stranger. I've no love for the girl either, even if the Thane wished things different.'"},
[6990]={"Sal de tu celda y acércate a tu rescatador <rgb=#00FF00>(Usa W para avanzar)</rgb>","Derrota al captor de Mundo","Despiertas en un calabozo de un campamento de bandidos. Un hombre de aspecto sombrío -- un Montaraz, Trancos -- está delante de ti. Mientras te pones de pie con dificultad, su voz urgente llega a tus oídos.","Amdir se encuentra justo más allá de la puerta principal.\
\
El Montaraz Amdir fue derribado por el Jinete Negro antes de que Trancos pudiera ahuyentarlo. Deberías preguntarle a Trancos qué hacer, porque la situación es ahora muy grave.","'Bien... los hobbits están... están fuera de peligro. Me alegra.\
\
'No... te preocupes por mí. El mayor peligro... ha pasado. Los Nazgûl temen a quienes manejan el fuego...'","'No eres ${PLAYERNAME:el único[m]|la única[f]} prisionero aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Mi compañero Amdir y yo hemos venido a rescatar a un hobbit, pero resulta que no es el hobbit que estábamos buscando.\
\
'Esta fuga será peligrosa para todos nosotros, porque sé que un gran mal acecha aquí. Me han llegado noticias de sus movimientos y puedo sentir su presencia. ¿Sabes luchar? Practica conmigo para familiarizarte con esa arma.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>ACCESO A TU INVENTARIO: Pulsa 'i' para abrir tu inventario y ver el arma (o haz clic izquierdo en los Íconos de la bolsa en la parte inferior de la pantalla).</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPAR TU ARMA: Haz clic derecho en el arma de tu inventario para equiparla. Esto reemplazará el arma endeble que tienes equipada actualmente.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>CONSEJO: Deberías equipar tu mejor arma antes de entablar combate.</rgb>'","Trancos ha vencido a los guardias bandidos, pero te advierte de que hay más enemigos por delante.\
\
El Montaraz quiere que practiques el combate luchando con él para asegurarse de que eres capaz de defenderte durante la fuga.","'¡Ya era hora! ¿Esperabais que... que me rescatara yo solo?\
\
'¡Vamos, tú, grandullón! Sácame de aquí antes de que vuelvan esos bribones. ¡Quieren venderme como si fuera un saco de patatas!'","Trancos espera cerca a la puerta principal.\
\
Amdir está gravemente herido. Trancos sabrá mejor qué hacer para ayudar a su amigo.","Sigue a Trancos al exterior","Encuentra a Trancos y Amdir","Captores de Celandine derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón","<rgb=#00FF00>Has demostrado adecuadamente tu destreza en el combate</rgb>","'Bien hecho. ¡Tu destreza en el combate es impresionante! Ahora, escucha con atención: necesitaré tu ayuda para salir de aquí. La verdadera batalla comenzará cuando salgamos de esta prisión.'","'Aquí nos separamos por un tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Debes liberar a los dos hobbits inocentes que también están siendo retenidos como prisioneros aquí: Celandine Brandigamo y Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón.\
\
'Debo buscar señales del sirviente de Mordor y aprender lo que pueda sobre su conexión con los Montebruno. Amdir, mi compañero Montaraz, está allanando un camino seguro para nosotros; nos estará esperando en la puerta principal.\
\
'Libera primero a Celandine. Es a Mundo a quien quieren con vida, porque lo han confundido con alguien más valioso. Cuando tengas a ambos hobbits a salvo, busca a Amdir cerca de la puerta principal. Luego nos dirigimos a Archet, donde encontraremos seguridad.'","Celandine Brandigamo está retenida en el campamento de bandidos.\
\
Trancos quiere que rescates a los hobbits, empezando por Celandine, mientras él va en busca de señales de Mordor (que se encuentra sorprendentemente cerca). Tendrás que derrotar a todos los bandidos que encuentres mientras buscas a los hobbits.","Derrota a los captores de Celandine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón está retenido en la zona de la prisión, más allá de la puerta de la jaula donde estaba Celandine.\
\
La distracción de Celandine fue un éxito. Solo queda un bandido para vigilar a Mundo. Deberías deshacerte de él rápidamente.","Instancia: Fuga de la prisión","'¡Consigue un arma para luchar mientras yo me ocupo de estos bandidos!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>INTERACCIÓN CON OBJETOS: Para saquear el bolso, haz doble clic izquierdo en el objeto o haz clic derecho una vez.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Los archivos que necesitas para continuar tus aventuras en la Tierra Media deberían terminar de descargarse en breve. ¡Gracias por tu paciencia!</rgb>","Un bolso está en el suelo, cerca de tu rescatador.\
\
Trancos te ha dicho que busques armas en el bolso y recojas su contenido, porque necesitarás defenderte durante esta atrevida fuga.","Ahora que has practicado el combate, habla con Trancos para saber qué hacer a continuación.","Celandine está retenida en una jaula, junto a la pared del recinto.\
\
Has vencido a los captores de Celandine, pero no has encontrado a Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón. Celandine puede que sepa dónde está retenido Mundo.","Ahora que has salido de la prisión, habla con Trancos para saber cuál es el siguiente paso.","Has derrotado al captor de Mundo","'Por desgracia, llego demasiado tarde. Amdir ha sido herido con una hoja de Morgul; esto no es una buena señal. Necesitamos salir de este lugar de inmediato. Archet está cerca y servirá como un buen lugar para descansar mientras Amdir se recupera. ¡Rápido, sígueme!'","Habla con Trancos <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en Trancos para hablar)</rgb>","Trancos ha salido de la prisión y ha entrado en el patio. Te está esperando allí.","Habla con Trancos","Trancos y Amdir os esperan a ti y a los hobbits en la puerta principal.\
\
Has liberado a ambos hobbits que habían desaparecido, pero aún no has escapado del campamento.","Mundo está atado a un poste en el patio.\
\
A pesar de la derrota de su captor, Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón parece estar especialmente disgustado. Deberías animarle a que se una a ti.","'¡Gracias, gracias, gracias! ¡Empezaba a preocuparme de que esta pequeña aventura fuera mi fin! Estos bandidos son gente horrible.'\
\
'Creo que mi amigo Mundo está cerca. ¡También debemos salvarlo! ¡Los bandidos han estado diciendo cosas terribles!\
\
'¡Necesitaremos una distracción... y sé exactamente qué hacer!'","Busca armas en la mochila <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en la mochila para abrirla)</rgb>","Mientras viajabas por el bosque de Chet, unos bandidos te asaltaron y te hicieron prisionero. Ahora te encuentras en una celda, buscando la manera de escapar."},
[6991]={"Beregond is in the hall, and has not heard that it is his time for judgement.","King Elessar must weigh the issues facing Gondor and make his pronouncements.","'${PLAYER}? Yes, I am ready.\
\
'I left my post without permission; three men of Minas Tirith I slew in my haste to come to Faramir's aid. I will rue the deed evermore, but I did not know what else to do!'","'There are several matters upon which the king must rule, and then he will hear your report of Mordor, ${PLAYER}. It will not be long.'","Wait until the king calls for your report","'Tell me what has transpired in Mordor since your last report, my friend.'","Instancia: Juicios del Rey","Talk to Malthengil","Find Beregond in the Hall of the King and tell him it is his time for judgement","There are many issues facing Gondor which require the pronouncements of King Elessar.","Malthengil has asked you to deliver your report of Mordor to King Elessar, but first there are some matters on which the king must rule."},
[6992]={"Keep close to Dolenthol and remain alert","Defeat Thargaun and the Morroval.","'They are nearby. We must be careful so as not to alert Thargaun to our presence.'","Talk to Dolenthol.","Instancia: Guardián de los Muertos","Defeat the Morroval","Keep close to Dolenthol and remain alert.","<rgb=#FF0000>Dolenthol must survive</rgb>","'Thargaun is not truly defeated. I saw a true death on Pelennor with the defeat of the Witch King. No, something else keeps Thargaun bound here. It is a deeply fell sorcery.'","Defeat Thargaun","Dolenthol needs your help to find and confront the vile wraith who commands the Dead in Minas Morgul.","Now is the time to attack!","Talk to Dolenthol","Defeated Thargaun!","<rgb=#FF0000>Dolenthol has fallen in battle!</rgb>"},
[6993]={"You have infiltrated a meeting of supporters of the Heirs of Castamir, and should learn what you can of their operation and their plans to undermine the rule of King Elessar.","'We have friends across the kingdom, hidden in plain sight. If we can rally the people of Gondor to our side....\
\
'Aye, it could be done, ${PLAYER}. The folk of Gondor do not wish to be ruled by Elessar and his Elf-queen; nor do they wish to be made subservient to Umbar! If the Kindred of the Coins thinks to challenge us for the rule of Gondor once our plans bear fruit and King Elessar is slain, perhaps they will find we are not so easily conquered. I have to believe this is the way it will be.'","Instancia: Espíritus afines","Observe the meeting of the Castamir supporters","Maethon is within one of the abandoned homes of Linhir now used by supporters of the Heirs of Castamir.","'Ah, do not trouble yourself overmuch. They will warm up to you when they learn how useful you will be to us.\
\
'I hope Elessar has enjoyed his kingship, for it nears its end!'","Nakási Wave-reaper desires vengeance upon the Heirs of Castamir, and has challenged you to stand with her against them.","A supporter of Castamir stands inside an abandoned home and bars your passage.","Tumúldo Fierce-water lies dying, attacked by the supporters of Castamir.","Maethon is in the cellar of an abandoned home in Linhir.","Talk to Nakási","'Nakási, my love... you were right...\
\
'Gondor... must die...\
\
'The Song...'","Hear what transpired","Maethon excitedly waves you over","'None of these vermin remain alive in this place, Tumúldo. You are avenged upon them.'\
\
Nakási turns her eyes to you.\
\
'Let us leave this place. Go ahead of me; I will carry the body of my husband. He deserves to rest forever in the Sea, and not in these vile houses of stone.'","Tumúldo Fierce-water is on the very precipice of death.","'No, there is something about you that is different. You are not with this rabble, even as they seek to court you. Tumúldo and I know well that achieving a goal can at times mean you must ally with your enemies.\
\
'Are you willing to die with these folk? Or will you stand with me to repay their treachery? The next one they stab in the back might be you, or it might be a friend, or it might be a lover. Tumúldo was all of these to me.'","Observe the meeting of the Castamir supporters and the emissaries from Umbar","Introduce yourself to Castamir supporters in the cellar of the abandoned home (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Maethon asked you to introduce yourself to some of the supporters of Castamir in the cellar of the abandoned home.","'I have nothing to say to you. Count yourself fortunate I do not cut you down where you stand. You may have deceived Maethon, but I am not fooled by this part you play, ${RACE}.'","Examine Tumúldo Fierce-water","Find Maethon somewhere within the abandoned homes of Linhir","'Do not think you are one of us just because Maethon invited you to this meeting, ${PLAYER}. You have not yet proven yourself to me.\
\
'I spoke with a gossipmonger in town who says that King Elessar has already departed Minas Tirith, and he travels this way! Perhaps you will soon have a chance to prove yourself to me after all.'","Tumúldo Fierce-water, emissary from Umbar, is interested to speak with you.","'Is it true you are close to the King? That will be useful indeed.'\
\
You tell him that Maethon mentioned another member of Elessar's court is a supporter of the Heirs of Castamir. He studies you carefully.\
\
'Aye. But you have yet to earn my trust, and until you do I will speak no more of those who should remain secret, for now. It should bring you joy to hear that the King is not as safe as he believes himself to be, and we may soon have the victory we seek.'","Maethon is somewhere within the abandoned homes taken over by supporters of the Heirs of Castamir.","'Introduce yourself to my friends, ${PLAYER}, and then we will begin.'","'Maethon vouches for you, but you had better be on your finest behaviour while you are with us, ${PLAYER}. If you put a single toe out of line you will wish you hadn't.\
\
'Praise the memory of Castamir, and all his heirs.'","'I don't understand how this could have happened! We heard no word from the Heirs of Castamir who remained in Umbar, but I believed they would send messages as soon as they could. From where sprang this Kindred of the Coins, and how could they so easily overthrow our folk? The Heirs of Castamir were so established in the city... I cannot understand it....\
\
'What has become of Saklaphêl, the widow of Balakhôr, or of Balakhâd his son? What are we now to do?'","Talk to the Castamir supporter inside the abandoned home","Hear the final words of Tumúldo Fierce-water","'You found the right place! I am delighted for you to join us, my friend. To have another member of Elessar's court among our number seems almost too great a gift to be believed, but I will not turn it down!\
\
'The meeting is soon to begin.'","Tumúldo Fierce-water lies on the cold stone floor in a pool of his own blood, a Gondorian blade buried in his back. His wife Nakási kneels by him, her eyes burning with fury and with unshed tears.","Tumúldo Fierce-water has been grievously wounded, a deadly blade buried in his back.","Talk to Maethon","'It is said that when Balakhôr the Scourge met his end, it was at the hands of Dead Men that he met it. They say it was the King Elessar who commanded the killing blow, but others stood nearby: an Elf... a dwarf... a hero who bore the name ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I had no love for Balakhôr, ${PLAYER}. Nakási and I preyed upon the ships he sent forth from Umbar before he came to power, but afterward, when we did not cease our roguery, he took one hand from each of us. They were ours to keep, and so we did, though we replaced them with these made of metal.'\
\
Tumúldo raises his left hand, and it shines in the dim light of the cellar.\
\
'The hands he cut from us were preserved, and now they decorate the cabin of our ship, each forever clasping the other, a sign of our love... and also of our desire for vengeance. Your part in the death of Balakhôr has robbed us of that vengeance.'","Supporters of the Heirs of Castamir secretly meet in a cellar in Linhir.","Talk to Tumúldo Fierce-water","Follow Maethon upstairs and learn what has happened","Tumúldo stirs. He is alive, but has only moments","Something has happened upstairs!"},
[6994]={"Éowyn stands in Meduseld as she presides over Edoras in King Théoden's absence.\
\
You should speak with Éowyn.","Listen to Éowyn","'I...I must leave. I have much to do to prepare for our departure. I beg your pardon, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You are welcome in Edoras, so you may feel free to go wherever you wish.'","Instancia: La Carga de la Dama Éowyn","Witwyn, Éowyn's serving-woman, can be found in Meduseld.\
\
Witwyn wishes to speak with you.","A shadow seems to fall upon the lady's bright features, and she looks troubled....","'I will gladly hear your concerns, my good stewards.\
\
'Pray tell me what goes on in Edoras on the eve of our departure to Dunharrow, so that I may make this passage easier for our people.'","Éowyn stands in Meduseld as she presides over Edoras in King Théoden's absence.\
\
You should listen to Éowyn.","Speak with Witwyn, the serving-woman","Éowyn leaves in haste, her face a mask fair and cold....","'Did you chance to notice my lady's face, ${PLAYER}? Perhaps you did not see it; some sadness or gloom has taken her.\
\
'Those who love her well see it settled on her shoulders like a rain-cloud mantle. I grow more worried for her with every day that passes....'","'I do not know why I suddenly spilled my fears to you, ${PLAYER}. There is something trustworthy about you.\
\
'Will you help my lady? Perhaps we can think of something that will cheer her, now that her uncle is recovered from his stupour.'","Speak with Éowyn","Éowyn sits proudly in Meduseld, hearing the concerns of her people before their departure to Dunharrow."},
[6996]={"Cruel Dancer engages Tatháta the Beast in conversation aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour.","Cruel Dancer has chased after Tatháta the Beast, but your priority must be to rescue Corudan.","Someone emerges from below deck: the ship's captain","Wait for the ship's captain to arrive","Corsairs loyal to the Kindred of the Coins have learned of your presence in the hidden harbour!","Instancia: Guarida de la Bestia","Witness the confrontation between Cruel Dancer and Tatháta the Beast","Talk to Tatháta the Beast aboard her ship","'You should follow the walkway to the west and investigate the first of the ships docked within this hidden harbour. I will circle around and come to it from the water, so we will have the advantage of surprise upon any members of the Kindred onboard the ship.'","'${PLAYER}... is that you? I cannot believe it!\
\
'But you must be careful! I hear Tatháta coming back!'","Having found no one within the first ship, Cruel Dancer believes the hostages you seek may be aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour.","You have boarded the first ship and should wait for Cruel Dancer to join you.","'I still cannot believe you came to rescue me, ${PLAYER}... are our friends here too?'\
\
You tell Corudan that you will recount your adventures to him just as soon as you untie him and bring him safely from Tatháta's hidden harbour. With a grin, you say that Sigileth will be very pleased to see him alive and unharmed. He blinks at you with surprise.","Tatháta the Beast stands upon the deck of her ship.","Board the nearest ship to the west in the hidden harbour","You have found Corudan aboard the second ship, and he is still alive!","Cruel Dancer has returned from her search of the first ship's interior.","'I hear folk inside the ship, and even now we have attracted their notice. They approach from within.\
\
'I will search below deck while you keep them busy up here.'","The deck of the ship is free of enemies","Cruel Dancer arrives aboard the second ship","Defeat Tatháta and her crew","Talk to Cruel Dancer in the hidden harbour","'Who are you to stand so boldly upon the deck of my ship? There are few indeed who would dare such a thing, for I have sent most of those to watery graves.\
\
'${PLAYER}? I have heard this name before now; Nakási has spoken of you to me. I am surprised you are still alive. Were she still here, instead of in the Citadel of Winds with the hostage from Pinnath Gelin, she would no doubt skin you alive. She will be disappointed to learn she missed you.\
\
'But why are you here? You cannot have come all the way to Umbar Baharbêl to take Nestinanessornë from us. It amused Nakási to take him aboard our ships, but he says little enough to us, and when he does speak his talk is mostly nonsense and riddles. The lions like him, which has kept him alive this long, but if they should get hungry I believe they will like him both less and more.'\
\
Tatháta smiles languidly.\
\
'I can speak in riddles too, you see?'","Cruel Dancer stands aboard the deck of one of the ships moored within the hidden harbour.","You have found the hidden harbour used by two members of the Kindred of the Coins, and hope to rescue the hostages contained within.","Wait for the captain of the ship to arrive.","Corudan is a captive aboard the second ship, but he is still alive.","The conversation has become a violent conflict!","Talk to Corudan aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour","Wait for Cruel Dancer to join you aboard the ship","Talk to Cruel Dancer aboard the ship","The nearest of the ships you should investigate is to the west.","Talk to Cruel Dancer aboard the first ship in the hidden harbour","Defeat the Corsair defenders aboard the ship while Cruel Dancer searches below deck","'There were no prisoners within this ship, ${PLAYER}. If your mission is to succeed, and if I am to claim the bounties I seek, we must hope the prisoners and their captors are aboard the second of the ships docked within this harbour.\
\
'Follow the walkways to the second ship. I will approach that vessel by water as I did this one, and maintain the element of surprise.'","Follow the walkways to the second ship moored within the hidden harbour","Cruel Dancer emerges from below deck","Cruel Dancer has come with you to the hidden harbour."},
[6997]={"'Thank you for your part in this, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to have heard Golasgil's wishes, for now we can see that they will be carried out. He was a good friend and a worthy soldier, and I want to honour his directives.\
\
'There is still a question I want answered, but it is of a sensitive nature and I will first allow the audience to disperse. We will speak with the Lady Marra about this last question when we can do so without too many ears nearby to hear.'","King Elessar has called for the final testament of Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas, to be read aloud and his wishes carried out.","King Elessar is in the study of Lond Cirion.","'We are here to witness the last wishes of Lord Golasgil, as written in his final testament? That is a relief, ${PLAYER}! I was afraid I had done something wrong!'\
\
Caebar turns a bright shade of pink at the realization that he has spoken loudly in the quiet room.\
\
'O hush now, Caebar!' he chides himself under his breath. 'This is a solemn occasion.'","'You found something written in Golasgil's hand? Aye, these notes are extensive, and see where he signed them, here at the bottom? He must have been very interested in the movement of the currents to have written so much! Let me compare the handwriting of these pages with his purported testament...'","Caebar is in the study of Lond Cirion, seeking to prove that Golasgil's testament was truly written by the Lord of Anfalas before his death in battle.","Listen to the reading of Golasgil's final wishes","Caebar is in the study of Lond Cirion, where Golasgil's testament will be read.","The study of Lond Cirion may contain samples of Lord Golasgil's writing that can be used to prove he wrote the testament, and its provenance made secure.","Talk to King Elessar","You and Caebar have proven that both the testament and Golasgil's notes on the currents were written by the same person, and now the Lord of Anfalas's last wishes can be read aloud and carried out.","A paper used as a bookmark has the notation 'Remember to buy fish,' but is unsigned","Examine the papers that contain Golasgil's final wishes","Instancia: Últimos deseos del Señor de Playa Larga","The seal on these papers has indeed been broken, which is unusual for such a document","This parchment contains notes on the migratory patterns of sea-birds, but it is unsigned","Pages with the heading 'Notes on the Currents' is signed by Golasgil and contains musings on the subject","Search the chamber for papers written in Golasgil's hand","Give Golasgil's notes on the currents to Caebar","Stand ready in the event you will be of some use","This page lists coins earned and spent, but could have been written by anyone","King Elessar has suggested that his scribe Caebar may be able to ascertain the provenance of the handwriting contained in Golasgil's purported testament.","Lady Marra has produced her husband's final wishes and set them on the table.","King Elessar has commanded that Lord Golasgil's testament be read aloud and his wishes carried out.","Talk to Caebar in Lond Cirion"},
[6998]={"'Es tal como temía... Ferndúr ha escapado, ${PLAYER}. Regresemos a Rivendel.'","Derrota a Ferndúr el Virulento y a sus hombres demacrados","<rgb=#FF0000>Glorfindel no debe ser derrotado</rgb>","Nuestro enemigo nos espera, ${PLAYER}... eso está claro.\
\
'La vil influencia de Ferndúr ha reclamado demasiadas vidas de mi pueblo y ha enfermado nuestras tierras. Su corrupción debe ser purgada del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
'Solo veo aquí a sus siervos repugnantes, pero el Señor Demacrado debe estar cerca. Avancemos con cautela...'","Habla con Glorfindel","Ábrete paso hasta el altar junto a Glorfindel","Instancia: Dando Descanso a los Muertos Malvados","DNT -- Will not be seen","Ferndúr el Virulento se encuentra en la cima del altar en Ost Brandras.\
\
Ya te has enfrentado a Ferndúr y ahora debes derrotarlo.","Debes hablar con Glorfindel antes de enfrentarte al enemigo.\
\
Glorfindel está afuera de Ost Brandras y espera tu ayuda para confrontar a Ferndúr el Virulento.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Glorfindel ha caído!</rgb>","Acércate a los hombres demacrados en lo alto del altar","Has acompañado al señor Glorfindel a Ost Brandras para enfrentar al Señor Demacrado, Ferndúr el Virulento.","'Ha llegado el momento, ${PLAYER}. Si los funestos poderes de este Señor Demacrado son realmente la causa del mal en el Bosque de los Trolls, debemos enfrentarlo.\
\
'No podemos permitir que reúna más muertos para fortalecer su poder.\
\
'Prepárate, ${PLAYER}. ¡Nada impedirá que cumplamos con esta tarea!'","Glorfindel está al pie del altar en Ost Brandras.\
\
Te has abierto paso entre numerosos espíritus malignos y ahora debes enfrentar a Ferndúr cuando estés preparado.","Sigue a Glorfindel dentro de Ost Brandras","Glorfindel está en Ost Brandras.\
\
Debes seguir a Glorfindel dentro de las ruinas y enfrentar a Ferndúr el Virulento.","Los hombres demacrados se encuentran en la cima del altar en Ost Brandras.\
\
Has llegado a la base del altar y ahora debes enfrentarte a los hombres demacrados."},
}
